gement. And two weeks ago, there were reports that another top Icahn deputy, Alex Denner, might be leaving to start his own fund.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Icahn Locks In a Deputy With a New Contract', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T00:22:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Leder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c364c055-03ed-52ff-96c7-6ae9ee69d889', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c364c055-03ed-52ff-96c7-6ae9ee69d889'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in the Hudson Valley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/nyregion/events-in-westchester.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in the Hudson Valley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in the Hudson Valley. Items for the calendar should be sent at least three weeks in advance to westweek@nytimes.com.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Events in Westchester', 'kicker': 'Calendar', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Westchester', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T00:23:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/992d0676-c342-5eee-ab88-5f3ea4e307a1', 'word_count': 4341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/992d0676-c342-5eee-ab88-5f3ea4e307a1'}, {'abstract': 'An effort to close the only center in North America where addicts may legally inject drugs was thwarted by Canada’s Supreme Court in a unanimous decision released Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/world/americas/canada-court-saves-drug-injection-center-from-shutdown.html', 'snippet': 'An effort to close the only center in North America where addicts may legally inject drugs was thwarted by Canada’s Supreme Court in a unanimous decision released Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An effort by the Conservative government to close the only center in North America where addicts may legally inject drugs was thwarted by the country’s Supreme Court in a unanimous decision released Friday. In 2008, the government said it would not extend the center’s exemption from federal narcotics laws, a position endorsed by the Royal Canadian Mounted Police. The Insite center in Vancouver, British Columbia, does not supply drugs, but allows addicts to inject them without fear of arrest under medical supervision on the condition that they undergo treatment. The court ruled that denying that permit and closing the clinic violated its users’ constitutional rights by “threatening their health and indeed their lives.” The justices also said that “during its eight years of operation, Insite has been proven to save lives with no discernible negative impact on the public safety and health objectives of Canada.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Court Saves Drug Injection Center from Shutdown', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | THE AMERICAS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Court Saves Drug Injection Center from Shutdown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservative Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Canadian Mounted Police', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T00:25:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a8f1648-df15-5cab-864b-a2371b212561', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a8f1648-df15-5cab-864b-a2371b212561'}, {'abstract': 'A minor character in “Camelot,” Mordred, steals the show in a production at the John W. Engeman Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/nyregion/camelot-at-the-john-w-engeman-theater-review.html', 'snippet': 'A minor character in “Camelot,” Mordred, steals the show in a production at the John W. Engeman Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In most productions of “Camelot,” the character of Mordred, the evil spawn of King Arthur and a sorceress who seduced him in his youth, is a footnote. Usually, he’s barely remembered by theatergoers and mentioned only briefly in reviews; in the movie version, he was stripped of his two big numbers. In the stage musical, he doesn’t even appear until the second act. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': 