58-56bf-95d8-909d2b41b79b'}, {'abstract': 'The social history of a section of Long Island can be traced by the evolution of the Nathaniel Rogers House, which started as a farmhouse around 1824.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/nyregion/the-evolution-of-the-nathaniel-rogers-house-reflects-long-islands-history.html', 'snippet': 'The social history of a section of Long Island can be traced by the evolution of the Nathaniel Rogers House, which started as a farmhouse around 1824.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE house at Montauk Highway and Ocean Road in Bridgehampton started out as a simple farmhouse around 1824, before being transformed in 1840 by a noted portrait artist into a handsome example of Greek Revival architecture, complete with four tall columns in front. In the 1880s, it became a boardinghouse for visitors to the “summer colony” that had taken root in the Hamptons. By 1894, it had been altered again, this time into an elegant inn, and then reverted to a private residence in the 1950s. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/nyregion/02SPOTLI/02SPOTLI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/02/nyregion/02SPOTLI/02SPOTLI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/nyregion/02SPOTLI/02SPOTLI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/nyregion/02SPOTLI/02SPOTLI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/02/nyregion/02