ents bearing the logo of a favorite team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mildred Ryan never missed a Yankee game. She was watching when Reggie Jackson swatted three home runs in Game 6 of the 1977 World Series. She was watching as Don Mattingly toiled for years to keep his team from plunging to the bottom of the standings. She was watching when Derek Jeter — “her boy,” her son, Ed, said — helped return the World Series trophy to the Bronx in 1996.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/01/nyregion/flowers2/flowers2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1017, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/01/nyregion/flowers2/flowers2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/01/nyregion/flowers2/flowers2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Devoted Fans Go to the Grave With Team Spirit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Increasingly, Devoted Sports Fans Go to the Grave With Team Spirit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T00:32:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'N