n': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/540f8d1c-ff29-50f9-bba2-250a8553c482', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/540f8d1c-ff29-50f9-bba2-250a8553c482'}, {'abstract': 'On Friday, Admiral Mike Mullen stepped down as the head of the Joints Chiefs of Staff, a position he had held since the Bush administration.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/09/30/a-look-back-at-mullens-tenure/', 'snippet': 'On Friday, Admiral Mike Mullen stepped down as the head of the Joints Chiefs of Staff, a position he had held since the Bush administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After fours years of serving as the nation’s highest-ranking military officer in the administrations of Presidents Obama and George W. Bush, the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, Adm. Mike Mullen, retired on Friday at a ceremony in Arlington, Va. His last day on the job also saw the death of Anwar al-Awlaki, an American-born leader of Al Qaeda’s branch in Yemen who was killed by an American drone strike.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Look Back at Mullen’s Tenure', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Awlaki, Anwar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joint Chiefs of Staff', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T01:26:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vijai Singh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vijai', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bd2c9