orm.html', 'snippet': 'We are certain that health care reform is in the country’s interest. If the Supreme Court takes on the issue, it must not let politics influence its decision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the Supreme Court decides to take up the constitutionality of health care reform in its current term, which begins on Monday, a ruling could come by the end of June, well before the November elections. Pundits are already speculating over which party would gain the most traction from a decision that goes one way or another. The court must not let politics influence its decision. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Supreme Court and Health Care Reform', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Supreme Court and Health Care Reform', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T01:46:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b31b8e7e-597c-585f-8fd9-30e6e01b90c8', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b31b8e7e-597c-585f-8fd9-30e6e01b90c8'}, {'abstract': 'Ten owners and more than 20 players met for nearly five hours on Friday as the parties began a last-minute push to broker a deal before endangering regular-season games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/sports/basketball/another-day-passes-without-nba-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Ten owners and more than 20 players met for nearly five hours on Friday as the parties began a last-minute push to broker a deal before endangering regular-season games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.B.A. did not cancel the season on Friday, but it inched ever closer to deleting games from the calendar after another day passed without a labor deal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Day Passes Without N.B.A. Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Day Passes Without N.B.A. Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Derek', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter, Billy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T01:47:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/963178b2-d6fc-5b32-9a10-29b00eff4def', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/963178b2-d6fc-5b32-9a10-29b00eff4def'}, {'abstract': 'A special United Nations court convicted two men on Friday of helping mastermind the 1994 Rwandan genocide, and it acquitted two others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/world/africa/rwanda-two-convicted-in-genocide.html', 'snippet': 'A special United Nations court convicted two men on Friday of helping mastermind the 1994 Rwandan genocide, and it acquitted two others.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A special United Nations court convicted two men on Friday of helping mastermind the 1994 Rwandan genocide, and it acquitted two others. The International Criminal Tribunal for Rwanda, based in Arusha, Tanzania, convicted Justin Mugenzi and Prosper Mugiraneza, the former ministers of trade and civil service, sentencing them to 30 years each. The tribunal acquitted two other senior members of Rwanda’s former government, Casimir Bizimungu, the former health minister, and Jerome-Clement Bicamumpaka, the former foreign minister. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rwanda: Two Convicted in Genocide', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | AFRICA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rwanda: 2 Convicted in Genocide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rwanda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Tribunal for Rwanda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T01:48:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9bfe3d9-26b5-52f4-8477-7d4f4445a4b9', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9bfe3d9-26b5-52f4-8477-7d4f4445a4b9'}, {'abstract': 'X-rays of art objects from the J. Paul Getty Museum connect the contemporary viewer to the art impulse at the core of the ancient works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/01/opinion/20111001_OPINION_XRAY.html', 'snippet': 'X-rays of art objects from the J. Paul Getty Museum connect the contemporary viewer to the art impulse at the core of the ancient works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'X-rays of art objects from the J. Paul Getty Museum connect the contemporary viewer to the art impulse at the core of the ancient works.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/01/opinion/20111001_OPINION_XRAY-slide-ERD5/20111001_OPINION_XRAY-slide-ERD5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Heart of the Art', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Getty, J Paul, Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T01:50:50+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Opinion', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/338769ee-5e28-57bf-8068-a1c8904fdcff', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/338769ee-5e28-57bf-8068-a1c8904fdcff'}, {'abstract': 'The deaths caused by listeria bacteria on cantaloupe are a warning that both the food industry and the government need to do more to protect the public.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/opinion/lessons-of-the-listeria-outbreak.html', 'snippet': 'The deaths caused by listeria bacteria on cantaloupe are a warning that both the food industry and the government need to do more to protect the public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The deaths caused by listeria bacteria on cantaloupe is a warning that both the food industry and the government need to do more to protect the public. The outbreak has already sickened more than 70 people in 18 states and killed at least 15 of them, mostly elderly, in eight states. This is the deadliest outbreak of food-borne disease in the United States in more than a decade.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons of the Listeria Outbreak', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lessons of the Listeria Outbreak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Listeria Monocytogenes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cantaloupes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T01:51:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/526e2149-fb02-5201-9057-fe8dd4430a46', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/526e2149-fb02-5201-9057-fe8dd4430a46'}, {'abstract': 'The Bloomberg administration expressed support for a City Council bill that would hamper federal authorities’ ability to detain and deport foreign-born inmates on Rikers Island about to be released.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/nyregion/law-expected-in-new-york-city-would-hamper-inmate-deportations.html', 'snippet': 'The Bloomberg administration expressed support for a City Council bill that would hamper federal authorities’ ability to detain and deport foreign-born inmates on Rikers Island about to be released.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a significant reversal, the Bloomberg administration said Friday that it would support a City Council bill that would hamper federal authorities’ ability to detain, and eventually deport, foreign-born inmates on Rikers Is