 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinian Request Sent to Experts', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | UNITED NATIONS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Palestinian Request Sent to Experts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T02:58:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c0f5709-06f9-50fa-82ec-34736a95bf84', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c0f5709-06f9-50fa-82ec-34736a95bf84'}, {'abstract': 'From the earliest hand-tinted postcards to kinetic, digital images, the sidewalks of New York have been muse and model to countless color photographers.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/09/30/rediscovering-the-urban-palette/', 'snippet': 'From the earliest hand-tinted postcards to kinetic, digital images, the sidewalks of New York have been muse and model to countless color photographers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The images depicting the city of shadow-cloaked smokestacks and sun-drenched skyscrapers are tucked away in our minds. Manhattan streetscapes bursting with odd angles and odder people. Pastoral landscapes of misty Central Park mornings. Ragamuffins and ruffians, dandies and dowagers, all strutting across the city’s stage — and all frozen in black and white.', 'source': 'The