rmer Soviet neighbors, complaining of “discrimination.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' Belarus withdrew Friday from a diplomatic summit meeting aimed at improving ties between the European Union and its former Soviet neighbors, complaining of “discrimination.” Western leaders have criticized the country’s authoritarian president for jailing and harassing his opponents, and the European Union has called for people it deems political prisoners to be released before talks on financial aid and economic ties can be resumed. Belarus’s Foreign Ministry said President Aleksandr G. Lukashenko had not been invited to attend the so-called Eastern Partnership summit meeting and that its delegation had been excluded from several events. Because of European Union sanctions against Belarus, Mr. Lukashenko is banned from entering the bloc. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Belarus Withdraws from European Summit Meeting', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Belarus Withdraws from European Summit Meeting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lukashenko, Aleksandr G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T03:27:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fb9f043-7efb-593c-bb24-227d37662ed9', 'word_count'