d that serious forest damage would not set in before the middle of the 21st century. Some of them have been shocked in recent years by what they are seeing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Justin Gillis reports on climatic threats to forests and the implications for the earth’s future. Please post your questions for him in the comment field below. He will respond next week on the Green blog.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Forests and Climate Change: Ask the Reporter a Question', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T09:51:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba42c0e3-bc1e-53a4-9289-9efa3ff0c6fe', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba42c0e3-bc1e-53a4-9289-9efa3ff0c6fe'}, {'abstract': 'It’s impossible to put any one Giant pass defender in the matchup with wide receiver Larry Fitzgerald.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/giants-cardinals-matchup-to-watch/', 'snippet': 'It’s impossible to put any one Giant pass defender in the matchup with wide receiver Larry Fitzgerald.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Giants (2-1) at Cardinals (1-2), Sunday at 4:05 p.m. Eastern, Fox', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants-Cardinals: Matchup to Watch', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA CARDINALS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T10:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c31b243-b42f-5dca-8b2b-57591e0e0c10', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c31b243-b42f-5dca-8b2b-57591e0e0c10'}, {'abstract': 'Rick Santorum has struggled to stand out in the race for the Republican presidential nomination,  but despite weak poll numbers and a small war chest, he’s still around.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/the-weekend-word-in-it-to-win-it/', 'snippet': 'Rick Santorum has struggled to stand out in the race for the Republican presidential nomination,  but despite weak poll numbers and a small war chest, he’s still around.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s Times:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Weekend Word: In It  to Win It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T10:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3f8078e-f6a5-54c4-8703-b30ee8097f6c', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3f8078e-f6a5-54c4-8703-b30ee8097f6c'}, {'abstract': 'Yes, the rates are going up — but it’s even worse for large companies.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/for-small-business-the-bad-news-about-health-care-costs-is-not-as-bad/', 'snippet': 'Yes, the rates are going up — but it’s even worse for large companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s bad news from the workplace: as The New York Times reported on Tuesday, the cost of health insurance rose sharply in 2011 after several years of relatively slow growth. According to the Kaiser Family Foundation‘s annual survey on employer health benefits, the average premium to insure a family of four grew 9 percent, to just over $15,073. For single coverage, premiums rose 8 percent, to $5,429.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Small Business,  Bad News on Health Care Costs Isn’t as Bad', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kaiser Family Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T11:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c914e43-815d-5226-a8cf-f5c4a247ea62', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c914e43-815d-5226-a8cf-f5c4a247ea62'}, {'abstract': 'The Barcelona-born Cristian Zuzunaga trained as a type designer, and his love for letterpress squares evolved into a fixation on the pixel, “the icon of our time.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/styled-to-a-t-cristian-zuzunaga/', 'snippet': 'The Barcelona-born Cristian Zuzunaga trained as a type designer, and his love for letterpress squares evolved into a fixation on the pixel, “the icon of our time.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Designer', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Styled to a T | Cristian Zuzunaga', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T11:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58cf8d57-37bc-58b3-93da-ad3a48557e8b', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58cf8d57-37bc-58b3-93da-ad3a48557e8b'}, {'abstract': 'Malik Mumtaz Hussain Qadri killed a prominent secular politician, sending shockwaves throughout Pakistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/world/asia/guard-sentenced-to-death-in-slaying-of-pakistani-governor.html', 'snippet': 'Malik Mumtaz Hussain Qadri killed a prominent secular politician, sending shockwaves throughout Pakistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — A court on Saturday sentenced to death an elite police guard who assassinated a leading secular politician he had been charged with protecting, a killing that sent shockwaves throughout Pakistan and was seen as a clear marker of growing religious intolerance and extremism in the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistani Is Sentenced in Killing of Governor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistani Is Sentenced In Killing Of Governor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taseer, Salman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qadri, Malik Mumtaz Hussain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T11:36:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b24d4a8-406a-5e7a-a62b-2b73985abb9b', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b24d4a8-406a-5e7a-a62b-2b73985abb9b'}, {'abstract': 'Designs that pack a punch.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/out-of-the-box/', 'snippet': 'Designs that pack a punch.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#714", 592, 490, true, chameleonData);', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out of the Box', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T12:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andreas Kokkino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andreas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kokkino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a59e628-628d-57d4-8c38-a9fee556ed19', 'word_count': 17, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a59e628-628d-57d4-8c38-a9fee556ed19'}, {'abstract': 'Boston Dynamics, a robotics company, showed off its latest battlefield robot, called AlphaDog. It’s scary.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/large-alphadog-robot-runs-like-a-horse-scares-people/', 'snippet': 'Boston Dynamics, a robotics company, showed off its latest battlefield robot, called AlphaDog. It’s scary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2007 Boston Dynamics, a robotics company, posted a video online of a robot called the BigDog that could run on any type of terrain like a dog. The video quickly went viral, partly because\xa0people\xa0were in awe of the robot’s agility and also because it was so scary to watch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unleash the Robot Dogs of War', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robots and Robotics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T12:25:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/215cfd27-7bb0-5ee7-adcf-f4dfffd7bf42', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/215cfd27-7bb0-5ee7-adcf-f4dfffd7bf42'}, {'abstract': 'The reading list from our fall design issue: “The Scrapbook of Frankie Pratt,” David Rothenberg’s treatise on art and a visual history of the 1968 Paris uprisings.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/bookshelf-10/', 'snippet': 'The reading list from our fall design issue: “The Scrapbook of Frankie Pratt,” David Rothenberg’s treatise on art and a visual history of the 1968 Paris uprisings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “The Scrapbook of Frankie Pratt” (Ecco, $26), Caroline Preston, a former archivist, pastes vintage postcards, Jazz Age ephemera and typewritten snippets into a sweetly beguiling novel about a New England girl who trades Vassar College for Greenwich Village on the advice of Edna St. Vincent Millay. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bookshelf', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T13:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c33ea13-b2b4-566e-8c21-4ac737b133d3', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c33ea13-b2b4-566e-8c21-4ac737b133d3'}, {'abstract': 'The synth-pop duo known as Bubbles recently performed at the Agnès B. flagship store in Soho.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/notes-from-the-underground-bubbles/', 'snippet': 'The synth-pop duo known as Bubbles recently performed at the Agnès B. flagship store in Soho.', 'lead_paragraph': "The synth-pop duo known as Bubbles recently performed at the Agnès B. flagship store in Soho. A crowd of forty or so looked on as Alain Levitt banged on his machines, and Jason P. Grisell flailed around the small stage area. Endearingly low-maintenance, the group wins hearts with their unpretentious slacks, sneakers, and baseball hats. Bubbles has played most of the better underground venues in New York, and is steadily gaining steam. And yet, while Levitt’s music was danceable and solidly interesting, Grisell’s vocals left the audience pondering whether or not we are in for a revival of that No-Wave school of “Can’t sing? Start a hit band!'” ", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes from the Underground | Bubbles', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T13:30:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By IO Tillett Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Io', 'middlename': 'Tillett', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d799b11b-17a9-5a62-a7b2-ab0ab86e0f72', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d799b11b-17a9-5a62-a7b2-ab0ab86e0f72'}, {'abstract': 'NATO forces said Haji Mali Khan was a “revered elder” in the brutal Pakistan-based clan and an uncle of two of its top leaders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/world/asia/nato-says-key-haqqani-leader-captured-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'NATO forces said Haji Mali Khan was a “revered elder” in the brutal Pakistan-based clan and an uncle of two of its top leaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — NATO forces said Saturday that they had captured a man they described as a high-ranking member of the Haqqani network, the brutal Pakistan-based clan the United States considers one of the biggest threats to bringing stability to Afghanistan. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NATO Says It Caught a Haqqani Clan Leader', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'NATO Says It Caught A Haqqani Clan Leader', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haqqani, Sirajuddin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haqqani, Jala