tly, I found a lovely maitake mushroom cluster that weighed over two pounds growing at the base of a giant pin oak near where I was staying just outside New Paltz. The maitake had grown over and around a fallen branch, and there were a few acorns attached to the bottom. I took the whole thing home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Urban Forager | Maitake Mushrooms', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mushrooms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Paltz (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T14:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ava Chin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ava', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e9ee10b-3a79-515f-8606-9d9976f85547', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e9ee10b-3a79-515f-8606-9d9976f85547'}, {'abstract': 'In “New York From the Air: A Story of Architecture,” Yann Arthus-Bertrand transforms street-level scenes into abstract cityscapes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/02/nyregion/20111002VISUALss.html', 'snippet': 'In “New York From the Air: A Story of Architecture,” Yann Arthus-Bertrand transforms street-level scenes into abstract cityscapes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “New York From the Air: A Story of Architecture,” Yann Arthus-Bertrand transforms street-level scenes into abstract cityscapes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/nyregion/20111002VISUALss-slide-TU8Q/20111002VISUALss-slide-TU8Q-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'cr