league play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The difference between the game in the United States and Europe is easy to illustrate by comparing two team competitions currently under way. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Europe, Players Profit From Team Efforts', 'kicker': 'Chess', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Europe, Players Profit From Team Efforts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ponomariov, Ruslan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gelfand, Boris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Radjabov, Teimour', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T15:36:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cee62738-46bc-50bd-802e-6ffa20745edc', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cee62738-46bc-50bd-802e-6ffa20745edc'}, {'abstract': 'The reviews are in! The critics weigh in on Friday’s shows in Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/runway-in-review-23/', 'snippet': 'The reviews are in! The critics weigh in on Friday’s shows in Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christian DiorDesigner: Bill GayttenDate and Location: Friday, Sept. 30, Musée Rodin, 77 Rue de Varenne, 7ePhotos: slide show', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Runway In Review', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T15:49:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison S. Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dfde776-7550-5945-920e-0718aaa277c5', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dfde776-7550-5945-920e-0718aaa277c5'}, {'abstract': 'Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon crack me up.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/brilliant-cryptic/', 'snippet': 'Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon crack me up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Administrivial Notepad Alert:  In the Sunday puzzle, there will be a notepad that reads: Ten famous people are attending a costume party in this crossword. After the grid is filled, change the two shaded letters in each theme answer to “unmask” a celebrity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: A Brilliant Cryptic', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T16:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb7762e9-77b3-51a6-9d53-b87bcdc8cbce', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb7762e9-77b3-51a6-9d53-b87bcdc8cbce'}, {'abstract': 'The wine writer Mark Oldman spends a day in court for an open container violation.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/bordeaux-sediment-tell-it-to-the-judge/', 'snippet': 'The wine writer Mark Oldman spends a day in court for an open container violation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent evening at Colicchio & Sons, in the Meatpacking District, the wine writer Mark Oldman attended an engagement dinner during which several bottles of 1970 Chateau Palmer were drunk. “I still remember the plums-and-truffle perfume and enduringly silky, savory finish,” Oldman said. He was so enamored, in fact, that before leaving, he snuck out an empty bottle with him as a souvenir. (Oenophiles, Oldman noted, refer to empties as “dead soldiers.”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bordeaux? Sediment? Tell It to the Judge', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T16:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a74d7445-d46a-546c-a474-fbe06619d07f', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a74d7445-d46a-546c-a474-fbe06619d07f'}, {'abstract': 'A group apparently dragged a wheelchair-bound French woman out of bed before speeding away in their boat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/world/africa/somali-gunmen-grab-wheelchair-bound-french-tourist-in-kenya.html', 'snippet': 'A group apparently dragged a wheelchair-bound French woman out of bed before speeding away in their boat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — Somali gunmen staged another brazen attack inside Kenya on Saturday morning, snatching a French tourist from a beachside bungalow and escaping to Somalia three weeks after a similar assault.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'r