, and that no doubleheaders will be permitted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 5:22 p.m. In his pregame comments, Manager Joe Girardi was asked if he would be hesitant to start the game if there was rain in the forecast for 9:30 or 10 p.m., and he said, “Unfortunately, I don’t get to make that decision. That’s in MLB’s hands. I would highly recommend that we don’t start if it’s going to rain half an hour, 45 minutes, an hour. But I’m not making the decisions.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Different Rules for Rainy Weather in Playoffs', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AccuWeather', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T17:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2cdf449-4a17-50e2-92fd-1e95ddfa5167', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2cdf449-4a17-50e2-92fd-1e95ddfa5167'}, {'abstract': 'The mayor of El Paso and two City Council members are the subjects of a recall election because they support health benefits for the domestic partners of gay city employees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/us/in