that the actual playing Diamondbacks bounced back from a 97-loss season to outdistance the defending World Series champion San Francisco Giants and win the National League West.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/sports/YARIZONA1/YARIZONA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/02/sports/YARIZONA1/YARIZONA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/sports/YARIZONA1/YARIZONA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/sports/YARIZONA1/YARIZONA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/02/sports/YARIZONA1/YARIZONA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Revived Diamondbacks Follow Their Leaders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Revived Diamondbacks Follow Their Leaders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA DIAMONDBACKS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibson, Kirk', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T18:12:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33c22b21-e59e-5edf-a825-6629536f83a5', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33c22b21-e59e-5edf-a825-6629536f83a5'}, {'abstract': 'The All Tomorrow’s Parties, the festival that pays lovingly microscopic attention to olden tastes in underground pop from around the world,  has relocated its New York-area edition from the Catskills.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/festival-starts-a-3-day-run-in-asbury-park/', 'snippet': 'The All Tomorrow’s Parties, the festival that pays lovingly microscopic attention to olden tastes in underground pop from around the world,  has relocated its New York-area edition from the Catskills.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ASBURY PARK, N.J. — All Tomorrow’s Parties, the festival that pays lovingly microscopic attention to olden tastes in underground pop from around the world, started its three-day run last night. It has relocated its New York-area edition to Asbury Park from the Catskills, and this was a life-affirming move. The old place, Kutshers Country Club, is a down-at-heels resort — the enclosed and remote feeling there made the event feel like a quarantined zone for those afflicted with obscure interests. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Festival Starts a 3-Day Run in Asbury Park', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Asbury Park (NJ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Catskills (NYS Area)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T18:13:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'ti