n': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c0a56a3-6c53-545f-b954-f9c5f2b71630', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c0a56a3-6c53-545f-b954-f9c5f2b71630'}, {'abstract': 'After Friday’s aborted start, C.C. Sabathia said he might be able to pitch on Sunday. His manager begs to differ.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/girardi-makes-it-clear-sabathia-wont-pitch-until-monday/', 'snippet': 'After Friday’s aborted start, C.C. Sabathia said he might be able to pitch on Sunday. His manager begs to differ.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joe Girardi made clear Saturday afternoon that he will not allow C.C. Sabathia to persuade him that he should pitch Sunday in Game 2 instead of Game 3 on Monday in Detroit. Girardi confirmed what he said after Friday’s game was suspended due to rain — Freddy Garcia will pitch Game 2 on Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Girardi Makes It Clear: Sabathia Won’t Pitch Until Monday', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burnett, A J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T21:56:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/943a3301-35c6-510e-8e0d-cf54fa7686e2', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/943a3301-35c6-510e-8e0d-cf54fa7686e2'}, {'abstract': 'Kent Matlock, chairman of Matlock Advertising and Public Relations, says he learned to treasure the help and inspiration of his mentors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/jobs/02boss.html', 'snippet': 'Kent Matlock, chairman of Matlock Advertising and Public Relations, says he learned to treasure the help and inspiration of his mentors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I\u2002 WAS born in Chicago and am a middle child. My parents had 14 brothers and sisters between them, so my siblings and I grew up in a large extended family. During the summers, we spent time in Brownsville, Tenn., where my mother grew up. That grounded us in our family values — faith, family and freedom, or the ability to choose your path.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/business/02-BOSS/02-BOSS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 789, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/business/02-BOSS/02-BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/02/business/02-BOSS/02-BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pay the Grace Forward', 'kicker': 'The Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pay the Grace Forward', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T21:56:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kent Matlock', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Matlock', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89c03ad9-bf07-5479-9dcf-bede0b7596be', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89c03ad9-bf07-5479-9dcf-bede0b7596be'}, {'abstract': 'You’ve been invited to a masquerade party hosted by Eric Berlin. Please don’t forget to RSVP.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/masquerade/', 'snippet': 'You’ve been invited to a masquerade party hosted by Eric Berlin. Please don’t forget to RSVP.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — After reading the Notepad for this puzzle, I jumped to what turned out to be a false conclusion. I assumed (and you should never assume) that I would find this puzzle frustrating. First, you have to figure out the theme clues and their corresponding entries, which are not necessarily “in the language.” Then you have to “unmask” the hidden celebrities in each entry. O.K., so I was wrong. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday: Masquerade', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T22:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/224f0db2-f01c-53bb-b437-397d8cf7266f', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/224f0db2-f01c-53bb-b437-397d8cf7266f'}, {'abstract': 'Readers offer their comments on my “Occupy Wall Street” column.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/suggestions-for-that-er-tahrir-on-the-hudson/', 'snippet': 'Readers offer their comments on my “Occupy Wall Street” column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column is about the Occupy Wall Street movement — and in particular suggestions for financial reforms that the movement should take up. My Twitter comparison of the occupied park with Tahrir Square already raised eyebrows — and caused me to rush to clarify — so I’d welcome comments on that, or on any specific steps you recommend to reform the financial system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suggestions for that, er, Tahrir on the Hudson?', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T22:12:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/742024b4-07e0-55cf-89d4-4432eb22398a', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/742024b4-07e0-55cf-89d4-4432eb22398a'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers at the University of Texas hope that a new project there will lead to the commercial use of algae as a source of vehicle fuel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/us/ut-making-a-big-bet-on-the-future-of-algae.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers at the University of Texas hope that a new project there will lead to the commercial use of algae as a source of vehicle fuel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just off a dirt road in northwest Austin stand hundreds of 12-foot-tall tubes filled with green liquid. Nearly 15,000 gallons of algae grow inside the tubes, which are housed in a massive structure called a shadehouse. Lab workers have to climb ladders to peek inside and tend to the tiny organisms. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/us/02TTALGAE1/02TTALGAE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/us/02TTALGAE1/02TTALGAE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/02/us/02TTALGAE1/02TTALGAE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.T. Making a Big Bet on the Future of Algae', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.T. Making a Big Bet On the Future of Algae', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALGAE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biofuels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T22:16:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lara Lapin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e264e1df-e1e8-508e-a729-8b1d146b13cc', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e264e1df-e1e8-508e-a729-8b1d146b13cc'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Rick Perry’s point of view on tuition for illegal immigrants may not have gone well at a recent debate, but a lot of Texans understand his thinking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/us/on-immigrant-tuition-texans-see-it-perrys-way.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Rick Perry’s point of view on tuition for illegal immigrants may not have gone well at a recent debate, but a lot of Texans understand his thinking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ross Ramsey, the managing editor at The Texas Tribune, writes a column for The Tribune.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Immigrant Tuition, Texans See It Perry’s Way', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Immigrant Tuition, Texans See It Perry’s Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T22:17:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85ed069a-e197-5236-9dae-e9d3881427df', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85ed069a-e197-5236-9dae-e9d3881427df'}, {'abstract': 'Marfa may be a small, remote town (a seven-hour drive from Austin), but the recent Trans-Pecos Festival shows that it is well on its way to becoming an important music town.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/us/tiny-remote-marfa-poised-to-be-a-rock-star-magnet.html', 'snippet': 'Marfa may be a small, remote town (a seven-hour drive from Austin), but the recent Trans-Pecos Festival shows that it is well on its way to becoming an important music town.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Something strange happened at last weekend’s Trans-Pecos Festival of Music and Love at El Cosmico in Marfa. Five hundred concertgoers — most staying in one of a hundred tents, six trailers, four safari tents and four yurts — three security guards, four sound men and one lighting specialist heard the voice of Led Zeppelin perform onstage. It seemed random and a little surreal, but somehow there was Robert Plant, live in the middle of nowhere. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiny, Remote Marfa Poised to Be a Rock-Star Magnet', 'kicker': 'Texas Monthly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tiny, Remote Marfa Poised to Be a Rock-Star Magnet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marfa (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffin, Patty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lambert, Liz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plant, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-01T22:25:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Langer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Langer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_mat