unnel.html', 'snippet': 'In the early 1900s, a tunnel through a hill linked Oakland and Lafayette. The tunnel closed in the 1940s, but a flagpole marks the entrance to this once-bustling locale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just off Old Tunnel Road in Oakland, a stone and brass-plated marker attests to the former use of a nearby hillside. In the early 1900s, a tunnel through the hill linked Oakland and Lafayette, allowing horse-drawn and pedestrian traffic between the two growing communities. Cars used it, too. The tunnel closed in the 1940s, but a flagpole marks the entrance to this once-bustling locale. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/us/02BCINTEL2/02BCINTEL2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/02/us/02BCINTEL2/02BCINTEL2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/us/02BCINTEL2/02BCINTEL2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/02/us/02BCINTEL2/02BCINTEL2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/02/us/02BCINTEL2/02BCINTEL2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Kennedy Tunnel', 'kicker': 'Local Intelligence', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Kennedy Tunnel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oakland (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'maj