ason very much in jeopardy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The longest bargaining session of the N.B.A. lockout ended on Saturday without a deal and without much progress, but so far without the “enormous consequences” that Commissioner David Stern threatened before the weekend.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bargaining Session Is Greater in Length Than in Productivity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bargaining Session Is Greater In Length Than in Productivity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter, Billy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Players Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T00:35:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ff08317-91d8-541f-a258-3d95d9bcc024', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ff08317-91d8-541f-a258-3d95d9bcc024'}, {'abstract': 'Herman Cain, Ron Paul and Gov. Haley Barbour talk about the presidential race.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/01/sunday-breakfast-menu-oct-2/', 'snippet': 'Herman Cain, Ron Paul and Gov. Haley Barbour talk about the presidential race.', 'lead_