rrested if they crossed the Brooklyn Bridge’s roadway.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/police-gave-warnings-at-bridge-videos-show/', 'snippet': 'Two videos show the police warning protesters that they would be arrested if they crossed the Brooklyn Bridge’s roadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 12:33 p.m. | With the Internet bursting with videos showing various interactions between the police and protesters from Occupy Wall Street, the New York Police Department decided to add two more. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Gave Warnings at Bridge, Videos Show', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brooklyn Bridge (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T15:10:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b390d39c-01e2-5a65-af6d-4eb4957904e1', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b390d39c-01e2-5a65-af6d-4eb4957904e1'}, {'abstract': 'Schohaja’s Paris fashion week photo diary.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/photos-of-the-moment-sonia-rykiel-2/', 'snippet': 'Schohaja’s Paris fashion week photo diary.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#597", 592, 400, true, chameleonData);Schohaja’s Paris fashion week photo diary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of the Moment | Sonia Rykiel', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T15:15:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Schohaja', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Schohaja', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a341b792-7ae6-53d5-ac07-90a6c5cef3f8', 'word_count': 34, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a341b792-7ae6-53d5-ac07-90a6c5cef3f8'}, {'abstract': 'The model Frida Gustavsson transforms with makeup by Stephane Marais and hair by Guido Palau.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/model-morphosis-frida-gustavsson-at-jean-paul-gaultier/', 'snippet': 'The model Frida Gustavsson transforms with makeup by Stephane Marais and hair by Guido Palau.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Greg Kessler captures the transformations of Paris Fashion Week. Here, the model Frida Gustavsson from IMG before (left) and after (right) transforms, with makeup by Stephane Marais and hair by Guido Palau for Redken. (Drag the orange bar left to reveal the full transformation.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Model-Morphosis | Frida Gustavsson at Jean Paul Gaultier', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T16:03:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Kessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73bf01a0-b6ff-5b74-a1f8-d79e2e269c5e', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73bf01a0-b6ff-5b74-a1f8-d79e2e269c5e'}, {'abstract': 'Gen. Martin E. Dempsey, the new chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, will have to work with drastically fewer Defense Department dollars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/world/americas/new-military-chief-faces-economic-challenges.html', 'snippet': 'Gen. Martin E. Dempsey, the new chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, will have to work with drastically fewer Defense Department dollars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — After his Senate confirmation as chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, Gen. Martin E. Dempsey knew he had some catching up to do before being sworn in last Friday as the nation’s highest-ranking officer and the principal military adviser to the president and secretary of defense.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/world/dempsey/dempsey-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/world/dempsey/dempsey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/03/world/dempsey/dempsey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Economy to Be a Challenge for New Military Chief', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Economics Crash Course For New Military Chief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Martin E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joint Chiefs of Staff', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T16:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86f2e399-f929-520d-b146-6d1e0dc0d420', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86f2e399-f929-520d-b146-6d1e0dc0d420'}, {'abstract': 'Another survey of major employers shows that workers may shoulder an even larger burden of health care premiums in 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/new-survey-projects-higher-employee-health-premiums/', 'snippet': 'Another survey of major employers shows that workers may shoulder an even larger burden of health care premiums in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Companies next year will push more health care costs onto their workers, who may see an increase of nearly 11 percent in what they have deducted from their paychecks for health insurance, according to a new annual study by Aon Hewitt, a large Chicago benefits consultancy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Survey Projects Higher Employee Health Premiums', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AON CORP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T16:32:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Japsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Japsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcf8e04d-d5b1-5f06-9f2d-54da4bed130d', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcf8e04d-d5b1-5f06-9f2d-54da4bed130d'}, {'abstract': 'The creators of the hit series are looking for further success with their new show, “American Horror Story.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/arts/television/american-horror-story-to-begin-on-fx.html', 'snippet': 'The creators of the hit series are looking for further success with their new show, “American Horror Story.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Growing up, the television producer Brad Falchuk said, he practiced to see if he was prepared for a possible home invasion by wriggling on the ground, as if he were hogtied, from his bedroom to the kitchen and extracting a knife from a drawer with his mouth. “You’re 8 or 9, this is what you do,” Mr. Falchuk explained. “Could I escape?”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/arts/Horror-1/Horror-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 685, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/arts/Horror-1/Horror-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/03/arts/Horror-1/Horror-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Songs of ‘Glee’ Give Way to Terror', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Songs Of ‘Glee’ Give Way To Terror', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Ryan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T16:34:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c693b5f2-32cf-5375-8bfe-8dfd8b9b03f8', 'word_count': 1301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c693b5f2-32cf-5375-8bfe-8dfd8b9b03f8'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Murphy and Brad Falchuk talk about a creative partnership that has taken them from “Nip/Tuck” to “Glee” to their new FX series, “American Horror Story,” and why they’re equally drawn to dark and light material.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/dont-stop-the-screamin-the-glee-guys-introduce-their-american-horror-story/', 'snippet': 'Ryan Murphy and Brad Falchuk talk about a creative partnership that has taken them from “Nip/Tuck” to “Glee” to their new FX series, “American Horror Story,” and why they’re equally drawn to dark and light material.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of years spent with the sunny kids of “Glee” could send anyone over to the dark side, and that’s exactly where the “Glee” co-creators Ryan Murphy and Brad Falchuk turned for their latest television series, “American Horror Story,” which makes its debut on Wednesday on FX. The new show begins with a husband and wife (Dylan McDermott of “The Practice” and Connie Britton of “Friday Night Lights”) and their teenage daughter (Taissa Farmiga) moving to Los Angeles to start their lives fresh. But their new Gothic fixer-up was a steal for a reason: it’s haunted by a history of murder and visited by creepy neighbors, housekeepers and unwelcome guests (including Jessica Lange, Frances Conroy and Denis O’Hare) as well as a mysterious figure in a full-body S&M costume, whom the “American Horror Story” producers have affectionately dubbed “Rubber Man.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Stop Screaming: The ‘Glee’ Guys Introduce Their ‘American Horror Story’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Glee (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Ryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T16:34:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/616684d6-ff8b-587c-9f7b-23ded4ca3300', 'word_count': 1613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/616684d6-ff8b-587c-9f7b-23ded4ca3300'}, {'abstract': 'Real rates are higher here than in America.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/the-yen-and-the-low-inflation-trap/', 'snippet': 'Real rates are higher here than in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m in Japan for a conference tomorrow. Here’s how I expect it to go:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Yen And The Low-Inflation Trap', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T16:54:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5af2a5a5-3345-5f74-bb9f-851df9ea84c3', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5af2a5a5-3345-5f74-bb9f-851df9ea84c3'}, {'abstract': 'Yes, it matters.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/the-renminbi-and-us-manufacturing/', 'snippet': 'Yes, it matters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate will be taking up Chinese currency this coming week. So I though I should offer a brief note about one of the arguments people make against focusing on Chinese currency manipulation — namely, the claim that China doesn’t really compete head to head with US manufacturing, so that a rise in the renminbi wouldn’t help.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Renminbi and US Manufacturing', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T17:05:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d72bec05-ce08-5951-9063-b98449fc5037', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d72bec05-ce08-5951-9063-b98449fc5037'}, {'abstract': 'AEI economic analysis.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/sos-your-mother-also-reagan/', 'snippet': 'AEI economic analysis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Larry Mishel points us to the American Enterprise Institute response to his paper debunking the regulatory uncertainty meme. It’s quite something, because there’s nothing there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'So’s Your Mother. Also, Reagan.', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T17:09:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd9facb5-d778-5b22-a655-25c5877bb916', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd9facb5-d778-5b22-a655-25c5877bb916'}, {'abstract': 'T plucks the best shoes right off the runway. Today’s pick: a hefty heel that referenced the 1940s.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/the-daily-shoe-celine/', 'snippet': 'T plucks the best shoes right off the runway. Today’s pick: a hefty heel that referenced the 1940s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T plucks the best shoes right off the runway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Daily Shoe | Celine', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T17:12:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27183725-e6cb-579f-9695-40e676ac73c7', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27183725-e6cb-579f-9695-40e676ac73c7'}, {'abstract': 'Jim Leyland’s decision to put Ryan Raburn, a right fielder, at second base may well have cost Detroit in Game 1.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/did-the-tigers-have-the-right-man-at-second-base/', 'snippet': 'Jim Leyland’s decision to put Ryan Raburn, a right fielder, at second base may well have cost Detroit in Game 1.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:48 p.m. | Updated Ryan Raburn is a useful spare part on a major league baseball club. He’s been a slightly above-average hitter over his career and plays a fine outfield. He can also fill in at second or third base, although not particularly well. According to the defensive statistics compiled from video records at Fangraphs.com, Raburn’s fielding has cost the Tigers 14 runs compared to an average second baseman over the 778 innings he has manned the keystone in his major league career. (He has performed even worse at third.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Did the Tigers Have the Right Man at Second Base?', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T17:24:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Rosenheck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenheck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38a866a3-3e9a-5651-8966-6f9b41813407', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38a866a3-3e9a-5651-8966-6f9b41813407'}, {'abstract': 'The campaign of Gov. Rick Perry  found itself on the defensive on Sunday over a report that he once hunted at a West Texas camp with a racially charged name.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/texas-hunting-camps-name-causes-trouble-for-perry/', 'snippet': 'The campaign of Gov. Rick Perry  found itself on the defensive on Sunday over a report that he once hunted at a West Texas camp with a racially charged name.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The campaign of Gov. Rick Perry of Texas found itself on the defensive on Sunday over a report that he once hunted at a West Texas camp with a racially charged name.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas Hunting Camp’s Name Causes Trouble for Perry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T17:42:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rich Oppel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rich', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/757da4af-ab00-5fae-a53d-68f2000e9c4b', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/757da4af-ab00-5fae-a53d-68f2000e9c4b'}, {'abstract': 'That 3-D family film from Alcon Entertainment and Warner Brothers took in an estimated $14.2 million in its second weekend at North American theaters.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/dolphin-tale-leads-in-slow-weekend-for-movies/', 'snippet': 'That 3-D family film from Alcon Entertainment and Warner Brothers took in an estimated $14.2 million in its second weekend at North American theaters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Movie theaters were quiet over the weekend as a hold-over from last week — “Dolphin Tale” — overcame weak competition from several newcomers to take the No. 1 position. “Dolphin Tale,” a 3-D family film from Alcon Entertainment and Warner Brothers, took in an estimated $14.2 million in its second weekend, lifting its total to $37.5 million, according to Hollywood.com, which compiles ticketing statistics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Dolphin Tale’ Leads in Slow Weekend for Movies', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pitt, Brad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T17:52:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/248e32d0-ea0c-5e39-8612-445fe4afac07', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/248e32d0-ea0c-5e39-8612-445fe4afac07'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bloomberg will testify on Monday in a trial over accusations that $1 million in campaign funds were stolen by a political consultant. When mayors appear in court the drama can begin at the swearing in.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/when-hizzoner-takes-the-stand-things-can-get-testy/', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bloomberg will testify on Monday in a trial over accusations that $1 million in campaign funds were stolen by a political consultant. When mayors appear in court the drama can begin at the swearing in.', 'lead_paragraph': '“State your full name,” the Federal District Court clerk in Manhattan asked.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Hizzoner Takes the Stand, Things Can Get Testy', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Witnesses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giuliani, Rudolph W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, Edward I', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Myerson, Bess', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T17:57:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6e282e9-b30a-52a7-8ac1-6a960493e69d', 'word_count': 1085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6e282e9-b30a-52a7-8ac1-6a960493e69d'}, {'abstract': 'Neither C.C. Sabathia nor Justin Verlander had much success in efforts to persuade their respective managers to allow them to pitch Game 2 on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/for-sabathia-and-verlander-monday-is-final-answer/', 'snippet': 'Neither C.C. Sabathia nor Justin Verlander had much success in efforts to persuade their respective managers to allow them to pitch Game 2 on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Neither C.C. Sabathia nor Justin Verlander had much success in efforts to persuade their respective managers to allow them to pitch Game 2 on Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Sabathia and Verlander, Monday Is Final Answer', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verlander, Justin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T18:13:08+0000', 'document_type':