 apiece.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Analysis: Yankees-Tigers, A.L.D.S. Game 2', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Freddy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T18:33:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3fef9b1-d964-53d7-aab8-14ea2c9de444', 'word_count': 3629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3fef9b1-d964-53d7-aab8-14ea2c9de444'}, {'abstract': 'Whether or not he won a job with the Devils, the N.H.L. veteran Petr Sykora definitely made an impression.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/after-giving-his-all-sykora-waits-on-answer-from-devils/', 'snippet': 'Whether or not he won a job with the Devils, the N.H.L. veteran Petr Sykora definitely made an impression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — Petr Sykora, a training camp tryout with a Stanley Cup ring, surveyed the Devils’ spacious locker room at Prudential Center. He glanced at some of his younger counterparts. After 935 regular-season and 115 playoff games in the N.H.L., the 35-year-old Sykora offered some perspective.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Giving His All, Sykora Waits for Answer From Devils', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sykora, Petr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T18:44:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Botta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efb8dd64-5a85-5ced-b663-16775fc83db6', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efb8dd64-5a85-5ced-b663-16775fc83db6'}, {'abstract': 'Alan Gilbert conducts the mezzo-soprano Stephanie Blythe in a new Sept. 11 song cycle by John Corigliano at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/arts/music/stephanie-blythe-and-philharmonic-at-avery-fisher-review.html', 'snippet': 'Alan Gilbert conducts the mezzo-soprano Stephanie Blythe in a new Sept. 11 song cycle by John Corigliano at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a free preseason concert last month to commemorate the 10th anniversary of the Sept. 11 attacks Alan Gilbert conducted the New York Philharmonic in Mahler’s “Resurrection” Symphony at Avery Fisher Hall, with the performance relayed to Lincoln Center Plaza. That great, tumultuous and, finally, exhilarating work was a fitting choice for the solemn occasion. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/arts/Phil/Phil-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 757, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Song Cycle Places One Indelible Day Along History’s Bleak Continuum', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Song Cycle Places One Indelible Day Along History’s Bleak Continuum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blythe, Stephanie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corigliano, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Alan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T18:49:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/22c23ef7-04e6-5566-b1c7-aafde8d5f1fc', 'word_count': 853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22c23ef7-04e6-5566-b1c7-aafde8d5f1fc'}, {'abstract': 'A 24-year-old right-hander, the hot-hitting Daniel Hudson is so high-strung that he concedes he is probably his own worst enemy on the mound.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/arizona-hoping-hudson-can-keep-his-cool/', 'snippet': 'A 24-year-old right-hander, the hot-hitting Daniel Hudson is so high-strung that he concedes he is probably his own worst enemy on the mound.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILWAUKEE — Daniel Hudson, Arizona’s Game 2 starter in the National League division series Sunday, is a one-man argument for keeping the designated hitter out of the N.L. Hudson led all N.L. pitchers with a .277 average and 14 runs batted in in 65 at-bats. He’s no slouch on the mound, either, winning 16 games after an 0-4 start in his first full season in the majors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona Hoping Hudson Can Keep His Cool', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greinke, Zack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hudson, Daniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Brewers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T19:29:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/742b4531-5342-5c11-9acb-70a08b7104d8', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/742b4531-5342-5c11-9acb-70a08b7104d8'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the death of Anwar al-Awlaki, the infamous Yemeni-American cleric and propagandist for aspiring jihadists, Yemen’s battle against Al Qaeda is far from complete.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/world/middleeast/in-yemen-one-islamist-dead-many-more-in-arms.html', 'snippet': 'Despite the death of Anwar al-Awlaki, the infamous Yemeni-American cleric and propagandist for aspiring jihadists, Yemen’s battle against Al Qaeda is far from complete.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANA, Yemen — Despite the death of Anwar al-Awlaki, the infamous Yemeni-American cleric who was a propagandist for aspiring jihadists around the globe, Yemen’s battle against Al Qaeda is far from complete, as security forces fought over the weekend against Islamic militants who control large areas of territory in the country’s restive south.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/03/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Yemen, One Islamist Is Dead, but the Battle Goes On', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Yemen, Unrest Is Persistent Despite Death of a Top Militant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Awlaki, Anwar al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T19:31:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Kasinof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kasinof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e11e106-6640-5193-b17b-68ea1e81d3d2', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e11e106-6640-5193-b17b-68ea1e81d3d2'}, {'abstract': 'Any immediate resumption of peace negotiations with the Palestinians appeared unlikely as the Israelis and Palestinians differed sharply over the terms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/world/middleeast/israel-supports-proposal-to-restart-mideast-talks.html', 'snippet': 'Any immediate resumption of peace negotiations with the Palestinians appeared unlikely as the Israelis and Palestinians differed sharply over the terms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Israel on Sunday formally accepted an international proposal to return to peace negotiations with the Palestinians, but any immediate resumption of talks appeared unlikely as the Israelis and Palestinians differed sharply over the letter and spirit of the proposal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/world/mideast/mideast-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/03/world/mideast/mideast-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/world/mideast/mideast-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/world/mideast/mideast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/03/world/mideast/mideast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Supports Proposal to Restart Mideast Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Accepts New Peace Talks, but Impasse Remains on Terms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T19:42:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e7024bf-169f-563a-958d-71d1a7304a52', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e7024bf-169f-563a-958d-71d1a7304a52'}, {'abstract': 'A map of efforts to amplify doubt on risks from greenhouse gases.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/a-map-of-organized-climate-change-denial/', 'snippet': 'A map of efforts to amplify doubt on risks from greenhouse gases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oct. 3, 9:00 p.m. | Updated A chart of “key components of the climate change denial machine” has been produced by Riley E. Dunlap, regents professor of sociology at Oklahoma State University, and Aaron M. McCright, an associate professor of sociology at Michigan State University. The diagram below (reproduced here with permission) is from a chapter the two researchers wrote on organized opposition to efforts to curb greenhouse gases for the new Oxford Handbook of Climate Change and Society. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Map of Organized Climate Change Denial', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libertarianism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Think Tanks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T19:51:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2693e996-b8ec-5ef9-9ade-f314e551ea82', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2693e996-b8ec-5ef9-9ade-f314e551ea82'}, {'abstract': 'New York police commanders have been observed grabbing protesters or initiating arrests at Wall Street protests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/nyregion/nypds-white-shirts-take-on-enforcer-role.html', 'snippet': 'New York police commanders have been observed grabbing protesters or initiating arrests at Wall Street protests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Police Department puts an endless list of tasks on the shoulders of its so-called white shirts — the commanders atop an army of lesser-ranking officers in dark blue.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/nyregion/white1/white1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/03/nyregion/white1/white1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/nyregion/white1/white1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'w