ing-charges.html', 'snippet': 'The European Commission will try to determine whether telecommunications operators are unduly profiting from outdated networks and thus have no incentive to invest in broadband.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — The European commissioner for digital technology was expected to begin an in-depth review Monday of the charges that the Continent’s largest telecommunications operators impose for leasing access to their national landline networks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe to Study Telecommunications Leasing Charges', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'European Inquiry Looks at Access Fees to Landline Networks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'France Telecom S.A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Telecom Italia S.p.A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Telekom A.G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kroes, Neelie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T20:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Internet', 'byline': {'original': "By Kevin J. O'Brien", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': "O'Brien", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17749870-0fc2-53d7-85c6-c569aaf9301c', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17749870-0fc2-53d7-8