ri': 'nyt://article/8ed1c8b2-5436-5f81-aaf5-056802826fb8'}, {'abstract': 'After their summer concert in Central Park was canceled because of a storm, the Black Eyed Peas tried again, and this time rapped cheerfully in the rain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/arts/music/black-eyed-peas-play-central-park-benefit-concert-review.html', 'snippet': 'After their summer concert in Central Park was canceled because of a storm, the Black Eyed Peas tried again, and this time rapped cheerfully in the rain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Often will.i.am, the frontman and behind-the-boards maestro of the Black Eyed Peas, will appear in public wearing what seems to be a plastic mold, or sheath, covering his head, giving him the air of an Afro-futurist cybernaut or a character from a William Gibson novel. It turns out he’s just planning for rain.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/arts/peas1/peas1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/arts/peas1/peas1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/03/arts/peas1/peas1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rapping in the Rain, All Smiles', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rapping in the Rain, All Smiles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Black Eyed Peas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T21:57:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a86f4f1e-88db-5d92-ab40-9943f3105a8d', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a86f4f1e-88db-5d92-ab40-9943f3105a8d'}, {'abstract': 'Garth Fagan brings his dance troupe to the Joyce Theater this week with a premiere of a work about Nelson Mandela.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/arts/dance/garth-fagan-finds-inspiration-in-nelson-mandela.html', 'snippet': 'Garth Fagan brings his dance troupe to the Joyce Theater this week with a premiere of a work about Nelson Mandela.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROCHESTER — Garth Fagan does not simply walk into a room. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/arts/sub-fagan/sub-fagan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 890, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/arts/sub-fagan/sub-fagan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/03/arts/sub-fagan/sub-fagan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Innovator of Dance Celebrates 40 Years', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Innovator Of Dance Celebrates 40 Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fagan, Garth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Garth Fagan Dance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T21:59:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27488ba0-7104-5881-b622-6310fe85aa9a', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27488ba0-7104-5881-b622-6310fe85aa9a'}, {'abstract': 'A plaintive tribute to an ex-President by Stanley Newman. Or is it?', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/02/stories/', 'snippet': 'A plaintive tribute to an ex-President by Stanley Newman. Or is it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — If you’re keeping track, another one of the unwritten rules of mainstream crossword theme development is: “Thou shalt not drag thy political leanings into the daily puzzle.” The daily crossword is placed squarely (sorry) in the entertainment section as a respite from the rest of the day’s news. Today, however, Stanley Newman, editor of the Newsday crossword puzzle, hitches his vowels to our 43rd president in what appears to be a tribute to George “DUBYA” Bush.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday: Sob Stories', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-02T22:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82af910d-ed34-56ea-98a2-e70aa31c011f', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82af910d-ed34-56ea-98a2-e70aa31c011f'}, {'abstract': 'Topspin Media and other companies are offering bands sophisticated tools to run all aspects of their online business, including direct-to-fan ticket sales.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/business/media/high-tech-tools-help-bands-market-directly-to-fans.html', 'snippet': 'Topspin Media and other companies are offering bands sophisticated tools to run all aspects of their online business, including direct-to-fan ticket sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Pixies, the reunited stars of 1980s alt-rock, decided recently to play a special show in Los Angeles, they wanted to make sure their biggest local followers were invited first. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/business/SUB-jpTOPSPIN-1/SUB-jpTOPSPIN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/03/business/SUB-jpTOPSPIN-1/SUB-jpTOPSPIN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/business/SUB-jpTOPSPIN-1/SUB-jpTOPSPIN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/business/SUB-jpTOPSPIN-1/SUB-jpTOPSPIN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/03/business/SUB-jpTOPSPIN-1/SUB-jpTOPSPIN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Tools Help Bands Do Business', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker':