and the need for more scrutiny.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/opinion/harmful-practices-by-the-new-york-police-dept.html', 'snippet': 'A reader responds to an editorial regarding questionable practices by the New York City Police Department and the need for more scrutiny.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harmful Practices by the New York Police Dept.', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Harmful Practices by the New York Police Dept.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T00:03:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbee1eb3-b4a6-5435-8071-534c31428a82', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbee1eb3-b4a6-5435-8071-534c31428a82'}, {'abstract': 'The talk after the Giants’ comeback victory centered on Victor Cruz’s actions after his 19-yard catch that set up the winning pass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/sports/football/mannings-late-touchdown-passes-rally-giants-past-cardinals.html', 'snippet': 'The talk after the Giants’ comeback victory centered on Victor Cruz’s actions after his 19-yard catch that set up the winning pass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GLENDALE, Ariz. — It was a fumble. Of course it was a fumble. Arizona Cardinals safety Kerry Rhodes was sure. Defensive end Calais Campbell was sure. Even Eli Manning, standing 25 yards back upfield with his hands clasped to the sides of his head, was sure that Victor Cruz had just inexplicably, incomprehensibly, laid the game at the Cardinals’ collective feet.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/sports/JPGIANTS/JPGIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/03/sports/JPGIANTS/JPGIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/sports/JPGIANTS/JPGIANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/sports/JPGIANTS/JPGIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/03/sports/JPGIANTS/JPGIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Victory for the Taking, Almost Left on the Ground', 'kicker': 'Giants 31, Cardinals 27', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Victory for the Taking, Almost Left on the Ground', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ballard, Jake', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicks, Hakeem', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wells, Beanie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA CARDINALS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T00:05:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ba842ce-2403-55ec-825c-84ac9c7cb995', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ba842ce-2403-55ec-825c-84ac9c7cb995'}, {'abstract': 'The case of Live Nation Entertainment shows that aborting deals is not always necessary to foster competition. Extracting concessions can work instead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/business/altering-a-deal-without-blocking-it.html', 'snippet': 'The case of Live Nation Entertainment shows that aborting deals is not always necessary to foster competition. Extracting concessions can work instead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blocking mergers is the bluntest tool in an antitrust watchdog’s armory. That is what the Justice Department is trying with AT&T’s ambition to acquire T-Mobile USA.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/business/VIEWS/VIEWS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 708, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Altering a Deal Without Blocking it', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Altering a Deal Without Blocking it', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T00:12:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Cox and Agnes T. Crane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Agnes', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Crane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/987eca43-5411-5eca-9a93-830120eb1e68', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/987eca43-5411-5eca-9a93-830120eb1e68'}, {'abstract': 'The “Annoying Orange” has embarked on the road to television, a path littered with the carcasses of other Internet standouts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/business/media/annoying-orange-tries-for-a-tv-career.html', 'snippet': 'The “Annoying Orange” has embarked on the road to television, a path littered with the carcasses of other Internet standouts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — There is little doubt that Dane Boedigheimer has created an online sensation that struck a pop cultural nerve. The “Annoying Orange” Web videos that he’s been rolling out for the last two years have racked up more than 800 million views on You Tube, where the threshold for a runaway hit is about 50 million. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/business/03orange/03orange-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/03/business/03orange/03orange-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/business/03orange/03orange-