endangering the environment by constructing a tar sands oil pipeline.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/opinion/say-no-to-the-keystone-xl.html', 'snippet': 'There are better ways to create jobs, without endangering the environment by constructing a tar sands oil pipeline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unless good sense intervenes, it looks increasingly likely that the State Department will approve the Keystone XL pipeline, which would carry a coarse, acidic crude oil from northern Alberta in Canada to refineries on the Gulf Coast of Texas. That would be a mistake.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Say No to the Keystone XL', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Say No to the Keystone XL: There are better ways to create jobs, without endangering the environment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Sands', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TransCanada Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T01:05:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8537d958-feee-5401-81dc-fb9cc2d85d6d', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8537d958-feee-5401-81dc-fb9cc2d85d6d'}, {'abstract': 'The Greek government also finalized a draft budget for 2012 and conceded that it would miss a deficit-reduction target.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/world/europe/greeks-move-to-slash-state-jobs-for-30000.html', 'snippet': 'The Greek government also finalized a draft budget for 2012 and conceded that it would miss a deficit-reduction target.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — After marathon talks with foreign auditors, the Greek government said Sunday that it had reached a deal on how to slash its unwieldy public sector by putting 30,000 workers on a scheme that would lead to early retirement for some and dismissal for others, in a bid to meet conditions set by foreign lenders for the release of crucial emergency loans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/world/03greece-jobs-inline1/03greece-jobs-inline1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greeks Move to Slash State Jobs for 30,000', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greeks Move To Slash State Jobs For 30,000', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T01:06:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type