ion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecd5ba6f-8ec1-5808-9347-57ca39ca4529', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecd5ba6f-8ec1-5808-9347-57ca39ca4529'}, {'abstract': 'Migrant shelters along the Mexican border are filled with seasoned crossers braving ever-greater risks to get back to their families in the United States — the country they consider home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/world/americas/mexican-immigrants-repeatedly-brave-risks-to-resume-lives-in-united-states.html', 'snippet': 'Migrant shelters along the Mexican border are filled with seasoned crossers braving ever-greater risks to get back to their families in the United States — the country they consider home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AGUA PRIETA, Mexico — "My wife, my son — I have to get back to them," Daniel kept telling himself, from the moment he was arrested in Seattle for driving with an expired license, all the way through the deportation proceeding that delivered him to Mexico in June.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/world/americas/03immigration/03immigration-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/world/americas/03immigration/03immigration-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/03/world/americas/03immigration/03immigration-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crossing Over, and Over', 'kicker': 'Immigration Upended | The Yo-Yo Effect', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crossing Over, and Over', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub':