classes/', 'snippet': 'As Sam Dillon reports in Monday’s Times, a national program adopted at some high schools in the U.S. has tied success on A.P. exams to financial rewards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Monday’s Times, Sam Dillon reports on the National Math and Science Initiative, a program that allows all interested students at participating high schools to enroll in Advanced Placement courses, regardless of their past academic performance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Advanced Placement Classes for All, and $100 for a Passing Score', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T15:39:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9a15922-de90-56c8-b664-998a9c4f1bc3', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9a15922-de90-56c8-b664-998a9c4f1bc3'}, {'abstract': 'Dario Franchitti capitalized on Will Power’s misfortune to reclaim the IndyCar series lead, but it was Carpenter who stole the spotlight.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/monday-motorsports-franchitti-regains-indycar-lead-at-kentucky-while-carpenter-logs-first-career-win/', 'snippet': 'Dario Franchitti capitalized on Will Power’s misfortune to reclaim the IndyCar series lead, but it was Carpenter who stole the spotlight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'His famous wife may call the Bluegrass State home, but Kentucky has not been so welcoming to Dario Franchitti. Entering Sunday’s Indy 300 at Kentucky Speedway, the three-time IndyCar champion had not finished higher than fifth at the oval track and had wrecked spectacularly in 2007. While Franchitti did not come away with a victory on Sunday, he did leave with the overall IndyCar series lead.', 'source': 'The New York 