s-at-hackny-fall-hackathon/', 'snippet': 'College students from across the Northeast U.S. and Canada descended on NYU for hackNY’s Fall Hackathon. The New York Times APIs were one of 14 official event APIs, all of which came from a New York City startup or, in the Times’s case, institutio...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times was one of fourteen official API-providers, along with groups like Foursquare, Etsy, NYCPlatform (the City of New York’s data site), and tumblr, (plus unofficial API-providers like Google and Twilio) at the hackNY Fall hackathon, held over the weekend at NYU.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Students hack The New York Times at hackNY Fall Hackathon', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T16:16:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Stenger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2de97a14-fa7f-5f67-b478-c8879fb1ae51', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2de97a14-fa7f-5f67-b478-c8879fb1ae51'}, {'abstract': 'Free, it seems, has its costs. Microsoft’s chief counsel explains its patent strategy toward Google’s Android.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/microsofts-patent-strategy-against-android/', 'snippet': 'Free, it seems, has its costs. Microsoft’s chief counsel explains its patent strategy toward Google’s Android.', 'lead_paragraph': ' When Samsung Electronics blinked last week, Microsoft scored another win in its campaign to strike patent-licensing deals with the makers of smartphones and tablets using Google’s Android software. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Microsoft’s Patent Strategy Against Android', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Brad', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T16:20:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49238b83-fff1-589b-ba51-0b135db1ff7b', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49238b83-fff1-589b-ba51-0b135db1ff7b'}, {'abstract': 'In the third quarter, five venture-backed companies went public — a 77 percent plunge from the second quarter, and a 64 percent drop from the same period last year.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/dealbook-venture-backed-i-p-o-s-slow-in-third-quarter/', 'snippet': 'In the third quarter, five venture-backed companies went public — a 77 percent plunge from the second quarter, and a 64 percent drop from the same period last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For initial public offerings, market volatility has been poison.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DealBook: Venture-Backed I.P.O.’s Slow in Third Quarter', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Venture Capital Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T16:31:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/225126ec-8498-544f-999a-74e2c9645916', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/225126ec-8498-544f-999a-74e2c9645916'}, {'abstract': 'Last night, Tod’s had a cocktail party at the Italian Embassy for its new signature collection, followed by a dinner that attracted a lot of editors in chief, along with Lee Radziwill, Marissa Berenson, Rachel Zoe and assorted Casiraghis and Courtin-Clarinses.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/an-evening-with-the-swells/', 'snippet': 'Last night, Tod’s had a cocktail party at the Italian Embassy for its new signature collection, followed by a dinner that attracted a lot of editors in chief, along with Lee Radziwill, Marissa Berenson, Rachel Zoe and assorted Casiraghis and Court...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last night, Tod’s had a cocktail party at the Italian Embassy for its new signature collection, followed by a dinner that attracted a lot of editors in chief, along with Lee Radziwill, Marisa Berenson, Rachel Zoe and assorted Casiraghis and Courtin-Clarinses. It was a little fancy for me, and I found myself going over the hits and misses of the week with Hal Rubenstein and Nina Garcia, who both liked Riccardo Tisci’s strong tailoring this season for Givenchy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Evening With the Swells', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T16:45:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c68f067a-df11-5691-9e0b-3c7fbff24fdb', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c68f067a-df11-5691-9e0b-3c7fbff24fdb'}, {'abstract': 'Zuzanna Bijoch is transformed with makeup by Pat McGrath and hair by Luigi Murenu.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/model-morphosis-zuzanna-bijoch-at-givenchy/', 'snippet': 'Zuzanna Bijoch is transformed with makeup by Pat McGrath and hair by Luigi Murenu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Greg Kessler captures the transformations of Paris Fashion Week. Here, the model Zuzanna Bijoch from Next Model Management before (left) and after (right) transforms, with makeup by Pat McGrath and hair by Luigi Murenu for John Frieda. (Drag the orange bar left to reveal the full transformation.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Model-Morphosis | Zuzanna Bijoch at Givenchy', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T16:45:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Kessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/357b6d49-77c7-53ec-8997-2ecd9a55dfd1', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/357b6d49-77c7-53ec-8997-2ecd9a55dfd1'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Tom Sachs will present “SPACE PROGRAM 2.0: Mars.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/park-avenue-armory-will-be-setting-for-trip-to-mars/', 'snippet': 'The artist Tom Sachs will present “SPACE PROGRAM 2.0: Mars.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the years the Park Avenue Armory has transformed its cavernous drill hall into everything including a science-fiction fun house and a landscape created from 30 tons of discarded clothing. For its next act the New York artist Tom Sachs will offer “SPACE PROGRAM 2.0: Mars,’’ his fictional mission to the planet. The project is a presentation of the Armory and Creative Time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Park Avenue Armory Will be Setting for Trip to Mars', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prada, Miuccia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sachs, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gagosian Gallery', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Avenue (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T16:45:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c75bf89-54ee-582f-a506-b6b6fd61860d', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c75bf89-54ee-582f-a506-b6b6fd61860d'}, {'abstract': 'Once the N.F.L. laughingstock, Detroit has turned its fortunes around under Coach Jim Schwartz, who has given the Lions reason to believe in themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/sports/football/lions-rebuild-team-psyche-in-4-0-start.html', 'snippet': 'Once the N.F.L. laughingstock, Detroit has turned its fortunes around under Coach Jim Schwartz, who has given the Lions reason to believe in themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It figures that the Detroit Lions would be the first team in N.F.L. history to win consecutive games after trailing by at least 20 points in each. After all, once a team has resurrected itself from a 0-16 season, come-from-behind victories are just microcosms of a much bigger rebuilding job.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/sports/football/04forward_lions/04forward_lions-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/04/sports/football/04forward_lions/04forward_lions-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/sports/football/04forward_lions/04forward_lions-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 786, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/sports/football/04forward_lions/04forward_lions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/04/sports/football/04forward_lions/04forward_lions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lions Rebuilt Team, Psyche and Record', 'kicker': 'N.F.L. Fast Forward', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '4-0 Lions Rebuilt Team and Psyche', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Jim (1966- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stafford, Matthew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hasselbeck, Matt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tennessee Titans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Vikings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fox, John', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Lions', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T16:48:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34a35cf0-0f1d-5bd6-99e5-8847ca3a42c1', 'word_count': 1293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34a35cf0-0f1d-5bd6-99e5-8847ca3a42c1'}, {'abstract': 'To one attaché, the August attack on a British agency in Kabul is a reminder that while Afghanistan’s future relies on many things, its culture may be its most inspirational asset.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/they-heard-the-word-culture-and-they-reached-for-their-gun/', 'snippet': 'To one attaché, the August attack on a British agency in Kabul is a reminder that while Afghanistan’s future relies on many things, its culture may be its most inspirational asset.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Funnily enough, I was in New York when it happened. It was a short breather after several months in Kabul — a treat for my children, whom I hadn’t seen for so long. We’d been out all day — MoMA, Harlem for lunch, Yankees tickets, a cruise past the Statue of Liberty. There was a reflection on the water of the development at ground zero as we steered by. “That’s why you’re in Kabul?” my kids asked.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'They Heard the Word Culture, and They Reached for Their Gun', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Council', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T16:58:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a4faa37-f9ef-58e9-90df-ac97fc30f997', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a4faa37-f9ef-58e9-90df-ac97fc30f997'}, {'abstract': '“The Web-Savvy Patient,” a book co-written by a cancer patient, is a guide to using the Web to one’s advantage, and avoiding its potential pitfalls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/health/04brody.html', 'snippet': '“The Web-Savvy Patient,” a book co-written by a cancer patient, is a guide to using the Web to one’s advantage, and avoiding its potential pitfalls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrew Schorr, a specialist in health communications, is convinced that the Internet saved his life. Now, through a book he wrote with Mary Adam Thomas, “The Web-Savvy Patient,” he is trying to help others facing a medical crisis use the Internet to their advantage and avoid its potential pitfalls.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/science/04BROD/04BROD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 658, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/science/04BROD/04BROD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/04/science/04BROD/04BROD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Navigating the Net Wisely in a Health Crisis', 'kicker': 'Personal Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Navigating the Net Wisely in a Health Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T16:59:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane E. Brody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Brody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea6185ed-8382-5808-82eb-9969ebc3571c', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea6185ed-8382-5808-82eb-9969ebc3571c'}, {'abstract': 'Taking the fight to the court of public opinion can pay off for the smaller company.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/defending-david-against-goliath/', 'snippet': 'Taking the fight to the court of public opinion can pay off for the smaller company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may have seen a fascinating New York Times article about the lawsuit Procter & Gamble has filed against a start-up called Willa, which produces a line of cosmetics that is sold in Target and in small boutiques. It turns out that P.&G. has a line of cosmetics called Wella, a German hair care brand that the conglomerate acquired in 2003 for $7 billion. P.&G. sued Willa over the name, claiming that it was confusingly similar to Wella.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Defending David Against Goliath', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trademarks and Trade Names', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TerraCycle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T17:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Szaky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szaky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b34f4332-cf25-5a5f-9a11-fadb287dadac', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b34f4332-cf25-5a5f-9a11-fadb287dadac'}, {'abstract': 'The announcement would clear the way for a new interim government that would run the country until elections can be held.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/world/africa/libya-leaders-promise-new-government-after-qaddafi-hometown-captured.html', 'snippet': 'The announcement would clear the way for a new interim government that would run the country until elections can be held.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TRIPOLI, Libya — Libya’s provisional leaders said Monday that they would resign once the former rebels defeat the vestiges of armed support for Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi in his home city of Surt, a move that would clear the way for a new interim government that would run the country until elections can be held.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/world/04libya-span/04libya-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/04/world/04libya-span/04libya-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/world/04libya-span/LIBYA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/world/04libya-span/04libya-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/04/world/04libya-span/04libya-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Libyan Rebels Clarify Steps to New Rule', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Libyan Rebels Clarify Steps To New Rule', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transitional National Council (Libya)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jibril, Mahmoud', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 's