011/10/03/diamondback-beset-with-redemptions-summer-losses/', 'snippet': 'In August alone, Diamondback’s main hedge fund lost 7 percent, leaving it down about 5 percent for the year, according to an investor in the fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since federal agents stormed into its office late last year, Diamondback Capital Management has been working to stay afloat. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Diamondback Beset With Redemptions, Summer Losses', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Diamondback Capital Management', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Level Global Investors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T19:54:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25ca4071-de85-5126-be8d-85ede7b73869', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25ca4071-de85-5126-be8d-85ede7b73869'}, {'abstract': 'Rhapsody said on Monday that it has signed an agreement to acquire Napster from Best Buy, uniting two cloud music players amid escalating competition in a growing market.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/rhapsody-to-acquire-napster-in-deal-with-best-buy/', 'snippet': 'Rhapsody said on Monday that it has signed an agreement to acquire Napster from Best Buy, uniting two cloud music players amid escalating competition in a growing market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rhapsody, the subscription digital music service, said on Monday that it had signed an agreement to acquire Napster from Best Buy, uniting two cloud music players amid escalating competition in a growing market.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rhapsody to Acquire Napster in Deal With Best Buy', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Best Buy Company Incorporated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Napster', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rhapsody.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T19:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25788d7a-cbeb-5ecc-a22c-b757b0cde899', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25788d7a-cbeb-5ecc-a22c-b757b0cde899'}, {'abstract': 'An entrepreneur finding markets for sustainably caught fish presents a nuanced view of subsidies.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/on-subsidies-fish-and-fishing/', 'snippet': 'An entrepreneur finding markets for sustainably caught fish presents a nuanced view of subsidies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A report examining the roughly $8 billion in subsidies that have flowed from the European Union or Spanish taxpayers to Spain’s fishing fleet since 2000 was published over the weekend by the International Consortium of Investigative Journalists. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Subsidies, Fish and Fishing', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crop Controls and Subsidies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlantic Ocean', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Trinidad and Tobago', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T19:58:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efd90750-0cb4-5086-8193-b37681d24de6', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efd90750-0cb4-5086-8193-b37681d24de6'}, {'abstract': 'The Broadway musical “Billy Elliot,” the winner of 10 Tony Awards in 2009 and a hot ticket for much of its run, will close on Jan. 8.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/billy-elliot-to-close-in-january/', 'snippet': 'The Broadway musical “Billy Elliot,” the winner of 10 Tony Awards in 2009 and a hot ticket for much of its run, will close on Jan. 8.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Time to hang up the ballet shoes. The Broadway musical “Billy Elliot,” the winner of 10 Tony Awards in 2009 and a hot ticket for much of its run, will close on Jan. 8, 2012, after 3 years and 3 months of performances, the producers announced on Monday. The decision to close “Billy Elliot” came after a somewhat precipitous decline in ticket sales that accelerated through the late spring and summer amid competition from new musicals like “The Book of Mormon” and “Priscilla Queen of the Desert,” hit revivals like “Anything Goes” and “How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying,” and “Memphis,” the durable recipient of the 2010 Tony for best musical. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Billy Elliot’ to Close in January', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Billy Elliot (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T20:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f5c56da-def8-57a2-891f-e95e42f3d2c0', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f5c56da-def8-57a2-891f-e95e42f3d2c0'}, {'abstract': 'A new study showed patients can learn to become more active, social and employable by engaging in a type of talk therapy that was invented to treat depression.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/health/research/04schiz.html', 'snippet': 'A new study showed patients can learn to become more active, social and employable by engaging in a type of talk therapy that was invented to treat depression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People with severe schizophrenia who have been isolated, withdrawn and considered beyond help can learn to become more active, social and employable by engaging in a type of talk therapy that was invented to treat depression, scientists reported on Monday.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talk Therapy Lifts Severe Schizophrenics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talk Therapy Lifts Severe Schizophrenics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Schizophrenia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T20:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benedict Carey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benedict', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34bdab42-0ea9-5b16-878c-c022ca498f97', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34bdab42-0ea9-5b16-878c-c022ca498f97'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers report that throat cancers caused by the human papillomavirus, transmitted during oral sex, have increased significantly in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/health/research/04hpv.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers report that throat cancers caused by the human papillomavirus, transmitted during oral sex, have increased significantly in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Throat cancers caused by a virus transmitted during oral sex have increased significantly in the United States in recent years, researchers reported on Monday. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Cites Increase in Cancers From HPV', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Cites Increase In Cancers From HPV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Papilloma Virus (HPV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Head and Neck Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oral Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexually Transmitted Diseases', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T20:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denise Grady', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2978a8c4-5915-5594-9641-86d391a44087', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2978a8c4-5915-5594-9641-86d391a44087'}, {'abstract': 'Eugene Souleiman and Pat McGrath discuss the hair and makeup for the Spring 2012 collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/backstage-beauty-report-stella-mccartney/', 'snippet': 'Eugene Souleiman and Pat McGrath discuss the hair and makeup for the Spring 2012 collection.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s a bit of a battle,” said Pat McGrath backstage at Stella McCartney of making sure that models’ tan bodies match their often paler faces. “We’re warming up with the foundation.” There wasn’t much else required in the way of makeup, save for Covergirl’s Lushberry creme blush, Lash Perfect mascara and some lip balm. “Fresh, beautiful, gorgeous, glowing, young and alive,” is how McGrath sees the Stella girl. “Spontaneous and real,” was Eugene Souleiman’s description of the designer, which he translated as a bun slicked back at the sides with texture on top. To create this look, he separated a horseshoe of hair all around the head, pulling it back tightly into a ponytail polished with a makeup brush coated in Wella hair spray. The crown was then roughed up with a little of Wella’s Refined Texture product. Souleiman explained that sometimes it’s more difficult to come up with a simple look than, say, one that is high concept. That wasn’t an issue today. “With Stella, it just kind of happens,” he said. “You’re never trying too hard.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backstage Beauty Report | Stella McCartney', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T20:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Lacava', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lacava', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01b87594-ee25-53f9-a205-4494aef8fa11', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01b87594-ee25-53f9-a205-4494aef8fa11'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Bloomberg entered and exited court through an unusual entrance, managing to give the slip to reporters waiting to follow up on his testimony on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/bloomberg-uses-furtive-means-to-access-courthouse/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bloomberg entered and exited court through an unusual entrance, managing to give the slip to reporters waiting to follow up on his testimony on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All along the sidewalk at the Manhattan Criminal Courthouse and lining the hallways outside the 11th-floor courtroom, the news media horde stood waiting: cameras rolling, flashes poised to pop, shoutable questions on the tips of tongues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Furtive Steps, Bloomberg Made His Way to Court', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Correction Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T20:20:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman and John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dcd4408-7827-5acd-bdfd-2b0ae9f8bb31', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dcd4408-7827-5acd-bdfd-2b0ae9f8bb31'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets lost to the Ravens, but their game on NBC made the network a ratings winner. CBS was second on the night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/n-f-l-carries-nbc-in-sunday-night-ratings/', 'snippet': 'The Jets lost to the Ravens, but their game on NBC made the network a ratings winner. CBS was second on the night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For one night of the week at least, NBC has little to worry about regarding its broadcast schedule: the National Football League continues to save the network from what has so far been a dismal fall season. The Baltimore Ravens defeated the Jets, 34-17, on “Sunday Night Football” to give NBC a ratings win in all viewership categories. Final audience numbers were not available on Monday afternoon. CBS finished second over all with new episodes of “The Amazing Race” and “The Good Wife,” though the numbers were skewed higher because of N.F.L. coverage overruns across the country. On ABC, “Pan Am” quickly lost altitude; it averaged 7.75 million total viewers in its second week, down more than 3 million from the series premiere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Carries NBC in Sunday Night Ratings', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T20:30:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/942d7fc8-0755-5847-9507-41e3c3804fac', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/942d7fc8-0755-5847-9507-41e3c3804fac'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists say that ostensibly generous behavior, taken to extremes, can become unhelpful, unproductive and even destructive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/science/04angier.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists say that ostensibly generous behavior, taken to extremes, can become unhelpful, unproductive and even destructive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some years ago, Dr. Robert A. Burton was the neurologist on call at a San Francisco hospital when a high-profile colleague from the oncology department asked him to perform a spinal tap on an elderly patient with advanced metastatic cancer. The patient had seemed a little fuzzy-headed that morning, and the oncologist wanted to check for meningitis or another infection that might be treatable with antibiotics. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/science/04ANGI/04ANGI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 886, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/science/04ANGI/04ANGI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/04/science/04ANGI/04ANGI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pathological Altruist Gives Till Someone Hurts', 'kicker': 'Basics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Pathological Altruist Gives Till Someone Hurts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Altruism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eating Disorders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hoarding', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T20:32:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Angier'