m after 23 years, presents three works including the premieres of “B-Sides” and “Kafka’s Cotillion” and the restaging of “Bound.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/arts/dance/bound-slideshow-slide-UN5O/bound-slideshow-slide-UN5O-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/03/arts/dance/bound-slideshow-slide-UN5O/bound-slideshow-slide-UN5O-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/arts/dance/bound-slideshow-slide-UN5O/bound-slideshow-slide-UN5O-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Isabel Gotzkowsky’s New York Finale', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gotzkowsky, Isabel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dance New Amsterdam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T22:48:34+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/fb44c44d-31d8-5ae8-a2cf-616067da2825', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/fb44c44d-31d8-5ae8-a2cf-616067da2825'}, {'abstract': 'A new study suggests that an injectable, hormonal contraceptive popular with African women has biological properties that may make women and men more vulnerable to H.I.V. infection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/health/04hiv.html', 'snippet': 'A new study suggests that an injectable, hormonal contraceptive popular with African women has biological properties that may make women and men more vulnerable to H.I.V. infection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most popular contraceptive for women in eastern and southern Africa, a hormone shot given every three months, appears to double the risk the women will become infected with H.I.V., according to a large study published Monday. And when it is used by H.I.V.-positive women, their male partners are twice as likely to become infected than if the women had used no contraception. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/health/04hiv-graphic/04hiv-graphic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Contraceptive Used in Africa May Double Risk of H.I.V.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Contraceptive Said to Double Risks of H.I.V.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T22:49:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pam Belluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35a49cd9-b03e-5b8f-b1d4-e7748fd86440', 'word_count': 1285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35a49cd9-b03e-5b8f-b1d4-e7748fd86440'}, {'abstract': 'A new French film by Ismaël Ferroukhi tells a little-known story of how a Paris mosque saved some Jews from the Nazis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/movies/how-a-paris-mosque-sheltered-jews-in-the-holocaust.html', 'snippet': 'A new French film by Ismaël Ferroukhi tells a little-known story of how a Paris mosque saved some Jews from the Nazis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The stories of the Holocaust have been documented, distorted, clarified and filtered through memory. Yet new stories keep coming, occasionally altering the grand, incomplete mosaic of Holocaust history. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/arts/mosque-1/mosque-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/04/arts/mosque-1/mosque-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/arts/mosque-1/mosque-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/arts/mosque-1/mosque-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/04/arts/mosque-1/mosque-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Heroic Tale of Holocaust, With a Twist', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heroic Tale Of Holocaust, With a Twist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosques', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T22:5