nyt://slideshow/a55b17ac-8e89-5338-b630-62e1df2fda15'}, {'abstract': 'An analysis suggests that even if Oracle paid a big premium, it could reap a hefty return from acquiring Hewlett-Packard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/business/a-potential-suitor-for-hewlett-packard.html', 'snippet': 'An analysis suggests that even if Oracle paid a big premium, it could reap a hefty return from acquiring Hewlett-Packard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Investors unimpressed by Hewlett-Packard’s dysfunctional governance have sold off shares, leaving the tech company vulnerable to a bid. And Larry Ellison’s acquisitive Oracle is a credible potential suitor. A Breakingviews analysis suggests that even while paying a big premium, Oracle could reap a hefty return.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Potential Suitor for Hewlett-Packard', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hewlett-Packard’s Potential Suitor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oracle Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hewlett-Packard Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-03T23:19:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By ROBERT CYRAN, RICHARD BEALES and ANTONY CURRIE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CYRAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BEALES', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CURRIE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}]