', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fa358a7-3f98-5d13-85fb-7b6b6bd5c11e', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fa358a7-3f98-5d13-85fb-7b6b6bd5c11e'}, {'abstract': 'A harsh new law in Alabama spreads fear and punishes the vulnerable and makes the state the country’s most hostile territory for immigrants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/opinion/alabamas-shame.html', 'snippet': 'A harsh new law in Alabama spreads fear and punishes the vulnerable and makes the state the country’s most hostile territory for immigrants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Only about 3.5 percent of Alabama’s population is foreign-born, according to the Census Bureau. Undocumented immigrants made up roughly 4.2 percent of its work force in 2010, according to the Pew Hispanic Center. But the drafters of Alabama’s harsh immigration law wanted to turn their state into the country’s most hostile territory for illegal immigrants. They are succeeding, as many of Alabama’s most vulnerable residents can attest. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alabama’s Shame', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alabama’s Shame: A harsh immigration law spreads fear and punishes the vulnerable', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T02:19:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d069f453-cce1-596d-b974-42fcc8a05859', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d069f453-cce1-596d-b974-42fcc8a05859'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t blame health care reform, which offers the best hope for restraint. Look to increased medical care costs and higher profits for insurance companies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/opinion/your-soaring-health-insurance-premiums.html', 'snippet': 'Don’t blame health care reform, which offers the best hope for restraint. Look to increased medical care costs and higher profits for insurance companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Annual premiums for employer-sponsored health coverage soared by 9 percent for families and 8 percent for individuals this year from 2010, far faster than wages or inflation. Republicans, predictably, blamed health care reform for contributing to the rise. In fact, the reforms accounted for only 1.5 percentage points of the increase this year. The value to millions of Americans who are already getting expanded coverage and benefits is undeniable. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Soaring Insurance Premiums', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Your Soaring Insurance Premiums: Don’t blame health care reform, which offers the best hope for restraint', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T02:19:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/15922c7e-e3b5-5339-afba-f3c2a933c97e', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15922c7e-e3b5-5339-afba-f3c2a933c97e'}, {'abstract': 'As lawmakers trim the national debt, Congress has proposed cutting financing for the State Department and its related aid agencies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/10/04/us/politics/us-foreign-aid-since-1977.html', 'snippet': 'As lawmakers trim the national debt, Congress has proposed cutting financing for the State Department and its related aid agencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As lawmakers trim the national debt, Congress has proposed cutting financing for the State Department and its related aid agencies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Foreign Aid Since 1977', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T02:24:36+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/4a3b565b-d1b6-55ca-9260-e038e6e304ea', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/4a3b565b-d1b6-55ca-9260-e038e6e304ea'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney does not fit the exciting mold Republicans think they want, but he may be just what the times require.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/opinion/brooks-in-defense-of-romney.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney does not fit the exciting mold Republicans think they want, but he may be just what the times require.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past several months, Mitt Romney has been an excellent presidential candidate. He has performed superbly in the debates. He has outorganized his rivals. He has relentlessly stayed on his core theme of putting Americans back to work. He has taken Rick Perry apart with a cold ruthlessness that is a wonder to behold.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight'