': 'nyt://article/17717392-45ae-59e9-b6ef-1d200dccab21'}, {'abstract': 'Judges at the International Criminal Court in The Hague have given the prosecutor the go-ahead to investigate war crimes in Ivory Coast after the country’s disputed presidential elections last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/world/europe/the-hague-court-will-investigate-war-crimes-in-ivory-coast-violence.html', 'snippet': 'Judges at the International Criminal Court in The Hague have given the prosecutor the go-ahead to investigate war crimes in Ivory Coast after the country’s disputed presidential elections last year.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Judges at the International Criminal Court in The Hague have given the prosecutor the go-ahead to investigate war crimes in Ivory Coast after the country’s disputed presidential elections last year. The prosecutor has said that both sides in the conflict, the forces backing the ousted leader Laurent Gbagbo and those backing his successor, Alassane Ouattara, had killed civilians and committed other crimes, including rape. Less than a week ago, the new government also formed a Truth and Reconciliation Commission to help establish peace, after the killing of an estimated 3,000 people and the destruction of vast numbers of homes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hague: Court Will Investigate War Crimes in Ivory Coast Violence', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hague: Court Will Investigate War Crimes in Ivory Coast Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gbagbo, Laurent', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ouattara, Alassane D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ivory Coast', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T02:50:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbdf9387-4235-588e-bd1b-3b608534c4ec', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbdf9387-4235-588e-bd1b-3b608534c4ec'}, {'abstract': 'Readers shared their expectations about their job status, the future of the economy and the prospects for the next generation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/business/2011-economy-sentiment.html', 'snippet': 'Readers shared their expectations about their job status, the future of the economy and the prospects for the next generation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers shared their expectations about their job status, the future of the economy and the prospects for the next generation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Your Economic Outlook?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T02:51:06+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/11f94d66-f986-50e9-8078-6e794fc3532d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/11f94d66-f986-50e9-8078-6e794fc3532d'}, {'abstract': 'Two severed heads were found on a busy highway near the Defense Ministry in Mexico City on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/world/americas/mexico-severed-heads-found-in-capital.html', 'snippet': 'Two severed heads were found on a busy highway near the Defense Ministry in Mexico City on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Two severed heads were found on a busy highway near the Defense Ministry in Mexico City on Monday, a reminder that the capital has not entirely escaped the violence sweeping large parts of the country. One head was found on the hood of a sport utility vehicle and the other near it on a sidewalk, along with a message from a criminal gang known as the Hand With Eyes, claiming Mexico City as its territory. It was unclear whether the heads were intended to send a message to the military, which has been deployed to fight the drug cartels. Very little cartel-related mayhem has been reported in Mexico City, but a decapitated body was found in another part of the city in August. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Severed Heads Found in Capital', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | THE AMERICAS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Severed Heads Found in Capital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Cartels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T03:01:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Zabludovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zabludovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb7baf56-a545-55c7-8d62-50ef423db231', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb7baf56-a545-55c7-8d62-50ef423db231'}, {'abstract': 'The Iranian lawyer for two American hikers who were released in September and repatriated after spending more than two years in a Tehran prison has been barred from leaving Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/world/middleeast/lawyer-is-barred-from-leaving-iran.html', 'snippet': 'The Iranian lawyer for two American hikers who were released in September and repatriated after spending more than two years in a Tehran prison has been barred from leaving Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Iranian lawyer for two American hikers who were released in September and repatriated after spending more than two years in a Tehran prison on charges of espionage and trespassing has been barred from leaving Iran, he confirmed in a text message. The lawyer, Masoud Shafiei, said authorities had prevented him from boarding an international flight without explanation. His destination was unclear, but the Iranian Student News Agency said he had intended to go to the United States. Last week, security forces raided his home and interrogated him about the Americans, Joshua F. Fattal and Shane M. Bauer, who denounced Iran after they left the country. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawyer Is Barred From Leaving Iran', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | MIDDLE EAST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawyer Is Barred From Leaving Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shafiei, Masoud', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bauer, Shane Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fattal, Joshua Felix', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T03:01:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 