useums had a more efficient way to organize their holdings than the boxfuls of dog-eared index cards that had served them for generations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/arts/04ellin/04ellin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 873, 'width': 967, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/04/arts/04ellin/04ellin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/04/arts/04ellin/04ellin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Everett Ellin Dies at 82; Helped Computerize Art Catalogs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Everett Ellin, 82, a Pioneer In Computerizing Art Catalogs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T03:50:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/5037f598-ae96-5596-87d6-93660c3e1ef0', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5037f598-ae96-5596-87d6-93660c3e1ef0'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Litvinoff wrote several volumes of poetry and novels, but is best known for criticizing T. S. Eliot as anti-Semitic in a poem he read aloud with Eliot present.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/03/books/emanuel-litvinoff-poet-dies-at-96.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Litvinoff wrote several volumes of poetry and novels, but is best known for criticizing T. S. Eliot as anti-Semitic in a poem he read aloud with Eliot present.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Emanuel Litvinoff, an English-born Jewish poet known for his scathing verse indictment of T. S. Eliot’s anti-Semitism — and for reading it before an audience that happened to include Eliot — died on Sept. 24 at his home in London. He was 96.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/sports/05litnivnoff/05litnivnoff-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 743, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/sports/05litnivnoff/05litnivnoff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/sports/05litnivnoff/05litnivnoff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Emanuel Litvinoff, Poet and Detractor of T. S. Eliot, Dies at 96', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Emanuel Litvinoff, 96, Poet and Detractor of T. S. Eliot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eliot, Thomas Stearns', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T03:50:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdac338b-fa4e-5217-8aa5-a80b86c65aeb', 'word_count': 1090, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdac338b-fa4e-5217-8aa5-a80b86c65aeb'}, {'abstract': 'Male circumcision will remain legal throughout California, after Gov. Jerry Brown signed a bill on Sunday that prevents local governments from banning the practice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/us/governor-of-california-signs-law-to-protect-circumcision.html', 'snippet': 'Male circumcision will remain legal throughout California, after Gov. Jerry Brown signed a bill on Sunday that prevents local governments from banning the practice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Male circumcision will remain legal throughout California, after Gov. Jerry Brown signed a bill on Sunday that prevents local governments from banning the practice. The measure was drafted in response to efforts in San Francisco and Santa Monica to outlaw circumcision for any males under 18 years old. In San Francisco, supporters of the ban gathered enough signatures to get an initiative on the ballot in November. In July, a Superior Court judge struck the initiative from the ballot, citing state law concerning medical procedures. Supporters of the Santa Monica circumcision ban failed to get the measure on the ballot. Two State Assembly members introduced legislation to prevent any potential circumcision bans — which Jews and Muslims argued violated their free expression of religion — in any other municipalities. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Governor Signs Law to Protect Circumcision', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WEST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Governor Signs Law To Protect Circumcision', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circumcision', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T03:51:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d6ee027-3d28-5103-a5df-8b0432d15165', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d6ee027-3d28-5103-a5df-8b0432d15165'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense has identified 4,469 American service members who have died since the start of the Iraq war and 1,783 who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/us/us-military-deaths-in-iraq-and-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense has identified 4,469 American service members who have died since the start of the Iraq war and 1,783 who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 4,469 American service members who have died since the start of the Iraq war and 1,783 who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the deaths of the following Americans recently: ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value'