-caf1-5c29-9a46-8959050aa1fa'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the best synonym for a word used in context?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/test-yourself-english-oct-4-2011/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the best synonym for a word used in context?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the article, “Maine City Casts Off Spurned Sculpture.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Oct. 4, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T08:09:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62506e8b-2e59-55fa-9d4a-9c3cdb76952a', 'word_count': 45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62506e8b-2e59-55fa-9d4a-9c3cdb76952a'}, {'abstract': 'What might happen if Greece defaults on its debt?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/greeces-economic-turmoil/', 'snippet': 'What might happen if Greece defaults on its debt?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHO comprises the “troika” that has kept Greece’s economy afloat?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece’s Economic Turmoil', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T08:27:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/240659b1-46a4-58e0-828f-3d70e55017af', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/240659b1-46a4-58e0-828f-3d70e55017af'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/news-quiz-october-4-2011/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | October 4, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T08:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Frasier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frasier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/968cef69-d882-5b07-b3d5-f873a61af63a', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/968cef69-d882-5b07-b3d5-f873a61af63a'}, {'abstract': 'For the New York Times staff photographer Tyler Hicks, war is no more and no less than who is near and whatever happens. C. J. Chivers reports on Mr. Hicks’s photographs from the Afghan war over the past decade.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/tyler-hicks-a-decade-in-afghanistan/', 'snippet': 'For the New York Times staff photographer Tyler Hicks, war is no more and no less than who is near and whatever happens. C. J. Chivers reports on Mr. Hicks’s photographs from the Afghan war over the past decade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OBSERVATION POST TWINS, Afghanistan — There are places and times where the politics that drive wars fade and then fade more, becoming abstractions to the people who fight or who are in a fight’s way. And there are moments when politics entirely disappear, and more elemental actions and emotions replace them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tyler Hicks: A Decade in Afghanistan', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hicks, Tyler', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T09:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daf2d917-36ca-5cbc-8612-b63d63e9882a', 'word_count': 2193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daf2d917-36ca-5cbc-8612-b63d63e9882a'}, {'abstract': 'Would money motivate you to study and succeed in school?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/should-schools-offer-cash-bonuses-for-good-test-scores/', 'snippet': 'Would money motivate you to study and succeed in school?', 'lead_paragraph': 'As part of the National Math and Science Initiative, some high schools have opened up their Advanced Placement courses to all students, and those who score a 3 or higher on the A.P. exam earn a $100 reward, as do their teachers. What do you think of financial incentives to perform well in school? Would you study harder if there were a cash bonus attached to a good grade?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headl