ist of banks buffeted by the sovereign debt crisis on Tuesday, saying it would not meet its profit target for the year.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/deutsche-bank-to-fall-short-of-profit-goals/', 'snippet': 'Deutsche Bank joined a growing list of banks buffeted by the sovereign debt crisis on Tuesday, saying it would not meet its profit target for the year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — Deutsche Bank, Germany’s biggest lender, joined a growing list of banks buffeted by the sovereign debt crisis on Tuesday, saying it would not meet its 2011 profit target owing to investor uncertainty and a loss from its Greek bond holdings. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deutsche Bank to Miss Profit Goal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T11:25:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7adf9dfa-d1af-55e2-b881-d32b9d08abc9', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7adf9dfa-d1af-55e2-b881-d32b9d08abc9'}, {'abstract': 'Relatives of Meredith Kercher, the 21-year-old murdered in 2007, said Tuesday that the family was still awaiting the “full truth,” which they believe could emerge in the next phase of the case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/world/europe/after-overturned-conviction-of-amanda-knox-slain-students-family-hopes-facts-will-emerge.html', 'snippet': 'Relatives of Meredith Kercher, the 21-year-old murdered in 2007, said Tuesday that the family was still awaiting the “full truth,” which they believe could emerge in the next phase of the case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PERUGIA, Italy — One day after an Italian appeals court overturned the conviction of Amanda Knox, one of three people convicted in the 2007 murder of 21-year-old Meredith Kercher, members of Ms. Kercher’s family said on Tuesday that they still hoped that the facts about her death would emerge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Slain Student’s Family Hopes Facts Will Emerge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slain Student&#8217;s Family Hopes Facts Will Emerge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kercher, Meredith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knox, Amanda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T11:40:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aca68e5a-8b4a-5771-9ae9-46222625284a', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aca68e5a-8b4a-5771-9ae9-46222625284a'}, {'abstract': 'Union workers at Ford will vote over the next two weeks on the agreement, which calls for the company to create 5,750 entry-level jobs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/business/ford-reaches-contract-deal-with-uaw.html', 'snippet': 'Union workers at Ford will vote over the next two weeks on the agreement, which calls for the company to create 5,750 entry-level jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — After winning promises of thousands of new jobs and bonuses for active workers at the Ford Motor Company, the United Automobile Workers union now turns to Chrysler to wrap up its epic contract talks with Detroit’s major automakers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/business/AUTO/AUTO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Deal With Ford, Union Wins Wage Increases and Additional Jobs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Deal With Ford, Union Wins Wage Increases and Additional Jobs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Automobile Workers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T11:53:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Vlasic and Nick Bunkley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vlasic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bunkley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9dff965-91c9-5a2c-9364-09f1dec13a82', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9dff965-91c9-5a2c-9364-09f1dec13a82'}, {'abstract': 'Many Republicans are urging Chris Christie to run for president, but some on the right of the party are less enthusiastic.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/christie-faces-conservative-criticism-as-he-decides-on-run/', 'snippet': 'Many Republicans are urging Chris Christie to run for president, but some on the right of the party are less enthusiastic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Chris Christie makes up his mind about whether to run for president, he is no doubt listening to the effusive praise from donors and activists and leading Republicans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Christie Faces Conservative Criticism as He Decides on Run', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T11:59:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27bba597-1103-5cf8-93ec-840c71677eaf', 'word_count': 988, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27bba597-1103-5cf8-93ec-840c71677eaf'}, {'abstract': 'Each receiver is dominating the league in his own way.  And after four weeks, Johnson and Welker are putting themselves in position to overtake three of the game’s greatest wide receivers.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/different-but-brilliant-wes-welker-and-calvin-johnson/', 'snippet': 'Each receiver is dominating the league in his own way.  And after four weeks, Johnson and Welker are putting themselves in position to overtake three of the game’s greatest wide receivers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There may not be two more distinctly different players in the league, but somehow, they play the same position.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Different but Brilliant: Wes Welker and Calvin Johnson', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welker, Wes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T12:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chase Stuart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chase', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stuart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c15eac3a-32a8-5d99-a7c2-1f9e3f234a0f', 'word_count': 1713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c15eac3a-32a8-5d99-a7c2-1f9e3f234a0f'}, {'abstract': '“Hell and Back Again,” a documentary by Danfung Dennis, follows Sgt. Nathan Harris, a Marine recovering from a shattered hip and leg.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/movies/hell-and-back-again-a-war-documentary-review.html', 'snippet': '“Hell and Back Again,” a documentary by Danfung Dennis, follows Sgt. Nathan Harris, a Marine recovering from a shattered hip and leg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unlike earlier generations of injured veterans, American soldiers who have been wounded in Iraq or Afghanistan have received quite a bit of attention. In print and on television the accounts of their attempts to recover from lost limbs and head trauma have been told and retold, accompanied by images that were startling at first but are less so now. Even “Dolphin Tale,” a film aimed at young children, has a subplot involving wartime injuries.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/movies/back-span/back-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/03/movies/back-span/back-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/movies/back-span/back-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/03/movies/back-span/back-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/03/movies/back-span/back-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Back at Home, a Marine Must Battle His Injuries', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Hell and Back Again'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back at Home, a Marine Must Battle His Injuries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dennis, Danfung', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T12:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbadeedb-bb01-50a4-9b30-7acb0ac99868', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbadeedb-bb01-50a4-9b30-7acb0ac99868'}, {'abstract': 'In all of Stefano Pilati’s collections for Yves Saint Laurent there are characters who, in ruffles and Belle de Jour uptightness, come close to representing the YSL woman.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/yves-saint-laurent-being-a-spectator/', 'snippet': 'In all of Stefano Pilati’s collections for Yves Saint Laurent there are characters who, in ruffles and Belle de Jour uptightness, come close to representing the YSL woman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In all of Stefano Pilati’s collections for Yves Saint Laurent there are characters who, in ruffles and Belle de Jour uptightness, come close to representing the YSL woman, yet never quite nail her. Mr. Pilati has done some interesting collections, one or two genuinely weird ones, and some that qualified as modern. That’s not such a bad track record in seven years, but unfortunately Mr. Pilati is stuck with a label that in public perception is somewhere between a tasty bonbon and a hallowed shrine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yves Saint Laurent: Being a Spectator', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pilati, Stefano', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saint Laurent, Yves', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T12:20:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2659f202-1231-51bb-a9c8-7d9d9548b6e3', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2659f202-1231-51bb-a9c8-7d9d9548b6e3'}, {'abstract': 'In a fresh blow to public confidence, a reactor in southern Japan went into automatic shutdown on Tuesday because of problems with its cooling system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/world/asia/cooling-problem-shuts-nuclear-reactor-in-japan.html', 'snippet': 'In a fresh blow to public confidence, a reactor in southern Japan went into automatic shutdown on Tuesday because of problems with its cooling system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — In a fresh blow to public confidence, a reactor in southern Japan went into automatic shutdown on Tuesday because of problems with its cooling system, clouding the outlook for an imminent restart of the country’s idled nuclear plants. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooling Problem Shuts Nuclear Reactor in Japan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japanese Nuclear Plant Shuts Down After Cooling Problem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T12:22:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/819bfd08-8289-5bb0-8ef8-ef51c1492ac9', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/819bfd08-8289-5bb0-8ef8-ef51c1492ac9'}, {'abstract': 'While immigrants constitute just over a third of the city’s population, they own about 48 percent of the city’s small businesses, according to a study published by the Fiscal Policy Institute.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/immigrants-play-key-role-as-city-entrepreneurs-study-finds/', 'snippet': 'While immigrants constitute just over a third of the city’s population, they own about 48 percent of the city’s small businesses, according to a study published by the Fiscal Policy Institute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Any taxi-riding, bodega-shopping, laundromat-using New Yorker knows that immigrants own many of the businesses that make New York tick. Now a new study shows that while immigrants constitute just over a third of the city’s population, they make up nearly half of the city’s small-business owners.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Immigrants Play Key Role as City Entrepreneurs, Study Finds', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chinatown Manpower Project', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fiscal Policy Institute', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jackson Heights (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T12:28:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Wall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa0357f5-a665-5363-aa8a-bcffaa1e9578', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa0357f5-a665-5363-aa8a-bcffaa1e9578'}, {'abstract': 'Three American-born scientists won the prize for their studies of exploding stars that revealed that the expansion of the universe is accelerating.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/science/space/05nobel.html', 'snippet': 'Three American-born scientists won the prize for their studies of exploding stars that revealed that the expansion of the universe is accelerating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three astronomers won the Nobel Prize in Physics on Tuesday for discovering that the universe is apparently being blown apart by a mysterious force that cosmologists now call dark energy, a finding that has thrown the fate of the universe and indeed the nature of physics into doubt.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/science/05nobel2/05nobel2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/science/05nobel2/05nobel2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/science/05nobel2/05nobel2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Studies of Universe’s Expansion Win Physics Nobel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '3 Win Nobel for Work on Accelerating Universe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons