ression of small fires is a leading cause of the recent huge destructive ones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jim Pitts stood on a Forest Service road near the Arizona town of Nutrioso and surveyed the damage in the valley below. It was July, and only a few weeks earlier the Wallow Fire, the largest in recorded history in Arizona, had swept through this section of steep slopes and tightly packed trees. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chopping Down Trees to Save Forests', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forest and Brush Fires', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Logging Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Forest Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southwestern States (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T15:38:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sean Patrick Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sean', 'middlename': 'Patrick', 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebeb26f9-2277-5303-96d5-e5304e2529c7', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebeb26f9-2277-5303-96d5-e5304e2529c7'}, {'abstract': 'DJ Shadow, a pioneer of hip-hop soundscapes, drops a new album on Tuesday called “The Less You Know the Better.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/dj-shadow-talks-about-his-latest-sonic-collages/', 'snippet': 'DJ Shadow, a pioneer of hip-hop soundscapes, drops a new album on Tuesday called “The Less You Know the Better.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'DJ Shadow has lived for 15 years in the shadow of his own success. The San Francisco disc jockey has put out just three full-length albums since the critically acclaimed “Endtroducing” in 1996, which helped define the then cutting-edge genre of instrumental hip-hop: dance music with symphonic sweep built from scores of samples dug out of eclectic and often obscure recordings. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DJ Shadow Talks About His Latest Sonic Collages', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disc Jockeys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Josh', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grandmaster Flash (1958- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kweli, Talib', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Susan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'De La Soul', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metallica (Music Group)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T15:41:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e0f8e35-d3ea-521b-804c-1e2ee9d1ac51', 