on': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/573ccca7-6b09-5301-8afa-3a9c04488da4', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/573ccca7-6b09-5301-8afa-3a9c04488da4'}, {'abstract': 'Agencies are being asked to cut 2 percent from their budgets for the current fiscal year, which ends in June 2012, and 6 percent from proposed budgets for the following fiscal year.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/city-agencies-to-be-told-to-cut-costs-by-2-billion/', 'snippet': 'Agencies are being asked to cut 2 percent from their budgets for the current fiscal year, which ends in June 2012, and 6 percent from proposed budgets for the following fiscal year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Citing a grim economic outlook and dimming prospects for state and federal aid, the Bloomberg administration on Tuesday asked city agencies to pare $2 billion from their budgets over the next 18 months.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Agencies Are Told to Cut Costs by $2 Billion', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T16:34:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd3a29be-99e8-553b-85b7-1af33d380a2c', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd3a29be-99e8-553b-85b7-1af33d380a2c'}, {'abstract': '“American Horror Story” on FX, from a pair of “Glee” writers and producers, brings a love of excess to the lives of a family moving into a haunted house.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/arts/television/american-horror-story-on-fx-review.html', 'snippet': '“American Horror Story” on FX, from a pair of “Glee” writers and producers, brings a love of excess to the lives of a family moving into a haunted house.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you like the jar with the baby’s leg, wait until you see the jar holding the baby’s head. If one actress with Down syndrome doesn’t provide enough Tod Browning-style otherness for you, don’t worry — there are two. If the line about snorting cocaine off a high school girl’s nipples doesn’t do it for you, maybe the scene of the sobbing naked man masturbating will.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/television/05horrorpic/05horrorpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/television/05horrorpic/05horrorpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/television/05horrorpic/05horrorpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/television/05horrorpic/05horrorpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/television/05horrorpic/05horrorpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbna