_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb3ffb57-d9de-54ec-baa8-b45644546790', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb3ffb57-d9de-54ec-baa8-b45644546790'}, {'abstract': 'The case of Mr. Olson caused a public uproar in the early 1980s after the authorities admitted paying him $100,000 to reveal the locations of his victims’ bodies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/world/americas/clifford-olson-canadian-serial-killer-is-dead-at-71.html', 'snippet': 'The case of Mr. Olson caused a public uproar in the early 1980s after the authorities admitted paying him $100,000 to reveal the locations of his victims’ bodies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Canadian police began connecting the dots in a series of child abductions and torture-murders in the summer of 1981, Clifford Olson, a career criminal with a history of sexual assaults, was placed on a list of potential suspects. It was a good hunch, as it turned out.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/sports/05olson/05olson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 712, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/sports/05olson/05olson-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/sports/05olson/05olson-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clifford Olson, Canadian Serial Killer, Is Dead at 71', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clifford Olson, 71, Canadian Serial Killer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Serial Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T18:26:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Vitello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vitello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/96f4232b-1c89-50ac-8706-be098ef95287', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96f4232b-1c89-50ac-8706-be098ef95287'}, {'abstract': 'The Moment caught up with Katy Perry’s stylist recently in New York to talk about dessert dressing, celebrity and why pop stars have more fun.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/asked-answered-johnny-wujek/', 'snippet': 'The Moment caught up with Katy Perry’s stylist recently in New York to talk about dessert dressing, celebrity and why pop stars have more fun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Johnny Wujek is one of a new breed of stylists who are becoming as well known as their celebrity clients — in his case the pop star Katy Perry. Since the early “I Kissed a Girl” days, Wujek has been pulling the strings behind Perry’s playful and sexually provocative image, including the cupcake bras and whipped cream bikini for the Candy Land-themed “California Gurls” video. “It’s all part of being a pop star,” says Wujek when asked whether he feels Perry’s look is appropriate for a younger audience. “Just look at Madonna, Prince or Michael Jackson, who all have had such emblematic and often controversial styles.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asked & Answered | Johnny Wujek', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T18:27:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marcus Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marcus', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17ab06cb-6591-5da7-97d0-a18330d72338', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17ab06cb-6591-5da7-97d0-a18330d72338'}, {'abstract': 'The Los Angeles Philharmonic, under leadership of the music director Gustavo Dudamel, is setting up a training program based on El Sistema, the Venezuelan-based movement that weds music teaching and social work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/arts/music/los-angeles-philharmonic-to-lead-a-sistema-style-project.html', 'snippet': 'The Los Angeles Philharmonic, under leadership of the music director Gustavo Dudamel, is setting up a training program based on El Sistema, the Venezuelan-based movement that weds music teaching and social work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Los Angeles Philharmonic has seized the initiative in guiding a national teaching program based on El Sistema, the Venezuelan-based movement that weds music teaching and social work. The orchestra announced on Tuesday that it would open an office, host yearly conferences and support a training program to sustain the effort.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/05sistema-span/05sistema-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/05sistema-span/05sistema-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/05sistema-span/05sistema-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 