ber and ends the threat of a government shutdown — for now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — With limited discussion and zero fanfare, the House on Tuesday approved and sent to President Obama a measure to keep the government operating through mid-November, ending for now the threat of any shutdown.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Approves Spending Bill Passed by Senate, and Government Shutdown Is Averted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Approves Spending Bill Passed by Senate, and Government Shutdown Is Averted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T19:23:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdf5c405-2070-5d0a-aa98-d0abffd29f5c', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdf5c405-2070-5d0a-aa98-d0abffd29f5c'}, {'abstract': 'Seven Kosovars are accused of luring victims from Turkey and former Communist countries to Pristina to sell their kidneys with false promises of payments of up to €15,000, or nearly $20,000.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/world/europe/trial-opens-for-7-kosovars-in-organ-trafficking-case.html', 'snippet': 'Seven Kosovars are accused of luring victims from Turkey and former Communist countries to Pristina to sell their kidneys with false promises of payments of up to €15,000, or nearly $20,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRISTINA, KOSOVO — The trial of seven Kosovars