orial Guinea since a 1979 coup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Unesco executive board members voted Tuesday to once again postpone a decision on a proposed scientific award sponsored by a West African leader with a brutal reputation, prolonging what has already been more than a year of negotiations and hand-wringing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unesco Delays Decision on Fate of Prize Sponsored by Dictator', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unesco Vote Will Prolong Prize Dispute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obiang Nguema Mbasogo, Teodoro', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Equatorial Guinea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T20:47:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f44b08ba-0bcf-5ef1-a341-a65d102822f7', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f44b08ba-0bcf-5ef1-a341-a65d102822f7'}, {'abstract': 'Checking in on the new season of “Gene Simmons Family Jewels” and the first of four “Wedding Episodes.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/channel-surfing-gene-simmons-family-jewels/', 'snippet': 'Checking in on the new season of “Gene Simmons Family Jewels” and the first of four “Wedding Episodes.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is there nothing Gene Simmons and Shannon Tweed won’t do to try to keep “Gene Simmons Family Jewels,” the reality show about their lives, interesting? It appears that after two children and almost three decades together, they’re even willing to take the drastic step of getting married.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Channel Surfing: ‘Gene Simmons Family Jewels’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T20:53:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ecdb641-0616-5691-86d9-99e4434a8fd5', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ecdb641-0616-5691-86d9-99e4434a8fd5'}, {'abstract': 'A single-engine helicopter, with five people onboard, went down moments after it took off from a helipad at East 34th Street, the authorities said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/nyregion/helicopter-crashes-in-east-river.html', 'snippet': 'A single-engine helicopter, with five people onboard, went down moments after it took off from a helipad at East 34th Street, the authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A helicopter with a veteran pilot at the controls, and a family of tourists he had known for years aboard, crashed in the East River on Tuesday afternoon, killing a woman despite a frantic rescue effort that involved a flotilla of police and fire vessels and dozens of emergency workers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/nyregion/05copter-span/05copter-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width':