, 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facing Backlash, Syria Revokes Week-Old Ban on Imports of Consumer Goods', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Facing Backlash, Syria Revokes Week-Old Ban on Imports of Consumer Goods', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T21:19:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Bakri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13eafd66-4f5c-5229-bab0-f251491a8856', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13eafd66-4f5c-5229-bab0-f251491a8856'}, {'abstract': 'The avant-garde composer Anthony Braxton will be honored in the Tri-Centric Festival in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/arts/music/the-tri-centric-festival-honors-anthony-braxton.html', 'snippet': 'The avant-garde composer Anthony Braxton will be honored in the Tri-Centric Festival in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anthony Braxton sat perched on a piano bench one recent afternoon, hands folded in his lap, wearing an intent but unreadable expression. Angled away from the piano in a no-frills rehearsal space in Brooklyn, he faced the dozen or so vocalists that currently make up his Syntactical Ghost Trance Music Choir. The singers, arranged in a semicircle, were tackling Mr. Braxton’s “Composition No. 256,” staring hard at their sheet music while trying to keep track of their conductor. It was starting to seem as if the piece, a slippery, scalar proposition, were getting the best of them.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/BRAXTON-2/BRAXTON-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/BRAXTON-2/BRAXTON-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/BRAXTON-2/BRAXTON-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating a Master of the Avant-Garde', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrating a Master Of the Avant-Garde', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Braxton, Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T21:19:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9826e34-4327-53d6-b9fd-4a3a6782dbd4', 'word_count': 1133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9826e34-4327-53d6-b9fd-4a3a6782dbd4'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney praised Chris Christie after the governor of New Jersey announced Tuesday that he would not join the presidential race.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/as-christie-passes-romney-campaigns-on/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney praised Chris Christie after the governor of New Jersey announced Tuesday that he would not join the presidential race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE VILLAGES, Fla. — Though Mitt Romney has always maintained a casual cool on the topic of a possible Chris Christie candidacy — “It’d be fun if he got in,” Mr. Romney said last week in New Hampshire, with a grin plastered on his face that seemed to say it wouldn’t necessarily be that much fun at all — he seemed newly emboldened on the topic Wednesday afternoon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Christie Passes, Romney Campaigns On', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T21:20:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86d531a3-e050-5b77-bf0e-613b6fe41e92', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86d531a3-e050-5b77-bf0e-613b6fe41e92'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Music of Elliott Carter Interpreted,” the ballet choreographers Emery LeCrone and Avi Scher have created different new works to the same music by Mr. Carter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/arts/dance/music-of-elliott-carter-interpreted-at-the-guggenheim.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Music of Elliott Carter Interpreted,” the ballet choreographers Emery LeCrone and Avi Scher have created different new works to the same music by Mr. Carter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Guggenheim Museum’s Works & Process series set a particularly difficult challenge for the young ballet choreographers Emery LeCrone and Avi Scher. Requiring them both to make a dance to the same music was not unusual; comparing and contrasting is habitual at Works & Process. The difficulty arose from the selected music: five unrelated works, atonal and rhythmically irregular compositions by the august and fearsome Elliott Carter, and none of them intended for dance.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/LECRONE/LECRONE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/LECRONE/LECRONE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/LECRONE/LECRONE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/LECRONE/LECRONE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/arts/LECRONE/LECRONE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Youth Meets Aged Master in 2 Dances, One Score', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Youth Meets Aged Master In 2 Dances, One Score', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Elliott', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LeCrone, Emery', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T21:24:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fd401ca-dcb2-5984-8ce6-3de9d401b98c', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fd401ca-dcb2-5984-8ce6-3de9d401b98c'}, {'abstract': 'The heyday of Pierre Cardin and mod fashion finds fresh inspiration in the unaffected Kirsten Dunst.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/16/t-magazine/16well-dunst.html', 'snippet': 'The heyday of Pierre Cardin and mod fashion finds fresh inspiration in the unaffected Kirsten Dunst.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The heyday of Pierre Cardin and mod fashion finds fresh inspiration in the unaffected Kirsten Dunst.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/t-magazine/16well-dunst-slide-1TC7/16well-dunst-slide-1TC7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 667, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/t-magazine/16well-dunst-slide-1TC7/16well-dunst-slide-1TC7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'t