mann-says-staff-changes-were-planned/', 'snippet': 'Michele Bachmann dismissed the perception that her campaign was in disarray because three workers were leaving to return to work at her Congressional office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES, Iowa — Representative Michele Bachmann on Tuesday addressed the perception that her campaign had hit a rocky patch because of dwindling finances after the latest staff shakeup. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann Says Staff Changes Were Planned', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T21:36:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/268a5f34-0e29-59cc-9274-899113165c7a', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/268a5f34-0e29-59cc-9274-899113165c7a'}, {'abstract': 'Touring the South Bronx, and shooting a video, with Amanda M. Burden, the city planning commissioner, and Michael Kimmelman, the New York Times architecture critic.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/a-walk-in-the-south-bronx-with-the-planning-commissioner-and-our-architecture-critic/', 'snippet': 'Touring the South Bronx, and shooting a video, with Amanda M. Burden, the city planning commissioner, and Michael Kimmelman, the New York Times architecture critic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following up on my review last week of Via Verde, a groundbreaking green housing project soon to be completed in the Melrose section of the South Bronx, I took a walk around that neighborhood with Amanda M. Burden, director the Department of City Planning under Mayor Mich