'Gluten', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crackers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T21:46:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2be3a46a-6717-5177-a3e7-49af308cd15c', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2be3a46a-6717-5177-a3e7-49af308cd15c'}, {'abstract': 'Bruno Benzacken and François Athea have graduated from selling their spices and tears at street fairs to opening a store in Grand Central Market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/dining/spices-sugars-teas-a-blast-for-the-senses.html', 'snippet': 'Bruno Benzacken and François Athea have graduated from selling their spices and tears at street fairs to opening a store in Grand Central Market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruno Benzacken and François Athea are cousins from a family that has been in the spice business in Europe since 1933. They came to New York eight years ago and began selling spices and teas at street fairs. Now they have graduated to a store on the Upper West Side, colorful in its array of several dozen spices, teas and blends and just as alluring for the aromas that waft from the displays. Tall canisters hold various sugars (right), and downstairs there are more spices and teas, along with assorted salts, peppers and pepper mixtures; Provençal products, including soaps; and various gadgets for grinding spices and preparing tea. They serve tea and pastries as well. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/dining/05STUFF_SPICE2/05STUFF_SPICE2-jumbo.jpg', 'heig