', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T22:05:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74da82f9-f29e-5d85-9a38-9452c75e4619', 'word_count': 986, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74da82f9-f29e-5d85-9a38-9452c75e4619'}, {'abstract': 'In separate suits, New York’s attorney general and the United States attorney in Manhattan say the bank it overcharged customers almost $2 billion in foreign transactions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/business/new-york-state-says-bank-of-new-york-mellon-cheated-pension-funds.html', 'snippet': 'In separate suits, New York’s attorney general and the United States attorney in Manhattan say the bank it overcharged customers almost $2 billion in foreign transactions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York attorney general and the United States attorney in Manhattan filed separate lawsuits on Tuesday against the Bank of New York Mellon, accusing it of cheating state and other pension funds nationwide out of foreign exchange fees over the last decade.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. and New York Sue Bank of New York Mellon Over Foreign Exchange Fees', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. and New York Sue Bank of New York Mellon Over Exchange Fees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State University of New York', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of New York Mellon Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T22:06:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Dash and Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85d673ed-3608-5d4c-9775-f27e1ef82858', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85d673ed-3608-5d4c-9775-f27e1ef82858'}, {'abstract': 'With the season on the line, Joe Girardi kept his batting order intact against the Tigers’ Rick Porcello.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/besides-burnett-yanks-go-with-same-lineup/', 'snippet': 'With the season on the line, Joe Girardi kept his batting order intact against the Tigers’ Rick Porcello.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — The lineups are in for Game 4 of the Yankees-Tigers American League division series Tuesday night, and Joe Girardi is going with the same lineup he used in the first three games. Detroit’s Jim Leyland made two alterations with the right-hander A.J. Burnett going for the Yankees instead of the left-hander C.C. Sabathia, who started Game 3.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Besides Burnett, Yanks Go With Same Lineup', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burnett, A J', 'rank': 1, 'major':