ecision to finish the fiscal year with no additional funds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The House Appropriations Committee is investigating the Federal Emergency Management Agency’s last-minute decision to finish the 2011 fiscal year with no additional funds, the panel’s chairman said on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Panel Investigates FEMA', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T22:50:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/131fb7e3-a407-5be4-8da8-64d32ad7a737', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/131fb7e3-a407-5be4-8da8-64d32ad7a737'}, {'abstract': 'Gene Monahan, the team’s trainer for 39 years and the man who memorializes baseballs used for Yankees achievements, will become a Nascar volunteer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/sports/baseball/monahan-marker-of-yankees-milestones-is-retiring.html', 'snippet': 'Gene Monahan, the team’s trainer for 39 years and the man who memorializes baseballs used for Yankees achievements, will become a Nascar volunteer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Austin Romine collected his first major league hit Sept. 12 in Seattle, the ball he struck made its way from right field to the Yankees’ dugout and eventually into the hands of the team’s chief athletic trainer, Gene Monahan. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/sports/05monahan-1/05monahan-1-artic