ract': 'Men weren’t the only ones being killed on Civil War battlefields — thousands of boys fought and died alongside them.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/the-boys-of-war/', 'snippet': 'Men weren’t the only ones being killed on Civil War battlefields — thousands of boys fought and died alongside them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With hopes of adventure and glory, tens of thousands of boys under the age of 18 answered the call of the Civil War, many of them rushing to join Union and Confederate troops in the earliest days of battle. Both sides had recruitment rules that barred underage men from enlisting, but that didn’t stop those who wanted to be part of the action: some enlisted without their parents’ permission and lied about their ages or bargained with recruiters for a trial period, while others joined along with their older brothers and fathers whose partisan passions overwhelmed their parental senses. Most of the youngest boys became drummers, messengers and orderlies, but thousands of others fought alongside the men.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Boys of War', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Military)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T23:53:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cate Lineberry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lineberry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2452227-a32a-5db1-9a5e-550d352ad519', 'word_count': 1464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2452227-a32a-5db1-9a5e-550d352ad519'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Hurd of Oracle has been traveling internationally as well as in the United States to take his message to corporations: They need to prepare for a deluge of data.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/mark-hurd-is-still-intense/', 'snippet': 'Mark Hurd of Oracle has been traveling internationally as well as in the United States to take his message to corporations: They need to prepare for a deluge of data.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may have thought Oracle was a hard-charging sales organization even before Mark Hurd showed up. Turns out there was room for more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mark Hurd Is Still Intense', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hurd, Mark V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oracle Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-04T23:57:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17289532-8471-5b46-a730-1b3d6b63288f', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17289532-8471-5b46-a730-1b3d6b63288f'}, {'abstract': 'At a meeting, leaders in Iraq agreed on the need to keep military trainers into 2012 but rebuffed a key American demand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/world/middleeast/iraqis-say-no-to-immunity-for-remaining-american-troops.html', 'snippet': 'At a meeting, leaders in Iraq agreed on the need to keep military trainers into 2012 but rebuffed a key American demand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Iraq’s political leaders announced late Tuesday that they had agreed on the need to keep American military trainers in Iraq next year, but they declared that any remaining troops should not be granted immunity from Iraqi law, a point the United States has said would be a deal breaker.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/world/IRAQ/IRAQ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/05/world/IRAQ/IRAQ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/world/IRAQ/IRAQ-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/world/IRAQ/IRAQ-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/world/IRAQ/IRAQ-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq Denies Legal Immunity to U.S. Troops After 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq Denies Legal Immunity To U.S. Troops After 2011', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immunity from Prosecution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Iraqiya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango and Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arango', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c1bb1f5-0262-5329-9519-c47b8cbf5a5e', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c1bb1f5-0262-5329-9519-c47b8cbf5a5e'}, {'abstract': 'Chelsea Clinton may not have won appointment to the IAC/InterActiveCorp board on her own merits, but it is still within her power to be effective, the Deal Professor says.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/handicapping-iacs-investment-in-chelsea-clinton/', 'snippet': 'Chelsea Clinton may not have won appointment to the IAC/InterActiveCorp board on her own merits, but it is still within her power to be effective, the Deal Professor says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chelsea Clinton as a corporate director? Really?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Handicapping IAC’s Investment in Chelsea Clinton', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Chelsea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diller, Barry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IAC/InterActiveCorp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:20:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eed5830e-9cc1-5697-be65-3210579df28c', 'word_count': 995, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eed5830e-9cc1-5697-be65-3210579df28c'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Porat opposed the removal of Jews from any land in exchange for peace with Israel’s neighbors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/world/middleeast/hanan-porat-jewish-settlement-leader-dies-at-67.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Porat opposed the removal of Jews from any land in exchange for peace with Israel’s neighbors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Hanan Porat, who helped turn Israel’s religious settler movement into a powerful force through the establishment of Jewish communities in the occupied West Bank and Gaza Strip, died on Tuesday at his childhood kibbutz, which he had re-established. He was 67.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/world/obit-porat/obit-porat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/world/obit-porat/obit-porat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/world/obit-porat/obit-porat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hanan Porat, Jewish Settlement Leader, Dies at 67', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hanan Porat, 67, Jewish Settlement Leader', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Porat, Hanan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:20:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe94834a-8e8e-565a-8390-399d615846b2', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe94834a-8e8e-565a-8390-399d615846b2'}, {'abstract': 'Fiona Reid was chief financial officer of the 2009 Bloomberg re-election campaign, from which, prosecutors say, John F. Haggerty Jr. stole $1.1 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/nyregion/bloomberg-aide-tells-jury-of-affair-with-haggerty.html', 'snippet': 'Fiona Reid was chief financial officer of the 2009 Bloomberg re-election campaign, from which, prosecutors say, John F. Haggerty Jr. stole $1.1 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was expected to be a moment of supreme awkwardness for John F. Haggerty Jr., a political consultant accused of stealing money from the mayor of New York.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Trial, Only a Quick Nod to a Bloomberg Aide’s Affair', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Trial, Only a Quick Nod to a Bloomberg Aide&#8217;s Affair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haggerty, John F Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:23:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ea1c054-8d6b-59e5-98e7-9a625a04dbe1', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ea1c054-8d6b-59e5-98e7-9a625a04dbe1'}, {'abstract': 'In person and in a Web video, Mitt Romney keeps jabbing at Gov. Rick Perry and Social Security.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/in-florida-retirement-community-guess-what-romney-talks-about/', 'snippet': 'In person and in a Web video, Mitt Romney keeps jabbing at Gov. Rick Perry and Social Security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE VILLAGES, Fla. — The audience — the aging, the retired and the lively-but-starting-to-show-smile-lines men and women of Florida — could not have telegraphed Social Security concerns more clearly than Mitt Romney himself, who tried a little Social Security humor of his own Tuesday afternoon at The Villages, a retirement community about an hour north of Orlando.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Florida Retirement Community, Guess What Romney Talks About?', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:28:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7180b19-e975-50c0-a290-d023ac56a3b6', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7180b19-e975-50c0-a290-d023ac56a3b6'}, {'abstract': 'As another European country institutes a tax on unhealthful foods, Americans should pay attention.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/how-about-a-little-danish/', 'snippet': 'As another European country institutes a tax on unhealthful foods, Americans should pay attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COPENHAGEN, Denmark — Well lookee here: the inevitable move toward taxing unhealthful foods to raise income and discourage damaging diets has begun. Last month, Hungary, almost unnoticed, began taxing foods with high levels of fat, salt and sugar. And earlier this week, with just a little more fanfare, Denmark instituted an excise tax on foods high in saturated fat. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How About a Little Danish?', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denmark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3e3eb3c-7873-5108-be51-f7f2735e59d8', 'word_count': 942, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3e3eb3c-7873-5108-be51-f7f2735e59d8'}, {'abstract': 'The defendant was captured on a plane bound for Detroit from Amsterdam in 2009 and accused of trying to ignite a bomb hidden in his underwear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/us/abdulmutallab-trial-opens-with-jury-selection.html', 'snippet': 'The defendant was captured on a plane bound for Detroit from Amsterdam in 2009 and accused of trying to ignite a bomb hidden in his underwear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Among the scores of potential jurors for the trial of a man accused of trying to blow up an airliner with a bomb in his underwear, nearly all said they had already heard something about the case, a federal judge here said Tuesday, the first day of jury selection.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jury Sought for Nigerian Held in Bid to Bomb Jet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jury Sought For Nigerian Held in Bid To Bomb Jet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abdulmutallab, Umar Farouk', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d861300e-1f02-541c-93e7-6935bc4c7d4d', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d861300e-1f02-541c-93e7-6935bc4c7d4d'}, {'abstract': 'Many major retailers plan to hire more workers during the lucrative holiday season, a reflection of statistics that show consumers just keep shopping despite the troubled economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/business/with-some-optimism-retailers-to-increase-holiday-hiring.html', 'snippet': 'Many major retailers plan to hire more workers during the lucrative holiday season, a reflection of statistics that show consumers just keep shopping despite the troubled economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even with a turbulent economy, leading retailers say they expect to hire more, or at least as many, holiday workers as last year, when temporary hiring for Christmas grew nearly 50 percent over recession lows.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/business/HIRE/HIRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hope Rising, Stores Hire for Holidays', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hope Rising, Stores Hire For Holidays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8702257-0ad2-5840-b883-d410b6cc4f8d', 'word_count': 909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8702257-0ad2-5840-b883-d410b6cc4f8d'}, {'abstract': 'Insurgents in Afghanistan use tactics like controlling the hours of cellphone use, in addition to selected attacks and some new flexibility on matters like education.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/world/asia/taliban-using-modern-means-to-add-to-sway.html', 'snippet': 'Insurgents in Afghanistan use tactics like controlling the hours of cellphone use, in addition to selected attacks and some new flexibility on matters like education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LASHKAR GAH, Afghanistan — Punctually, at 8 o’clock every evening, the cellphone signals disappear in this provincial capital. Under pressure from the Taliban, the major carriers turn off their signal towers, effectively severing most of the connections to the rest of the world. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/world/middleeast/TALIBAN/TALIBAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/05/world/middleeast/TALIBAN/TALIBAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/world/middleeast/TALIBAN/TALIBAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/world/middleeast/TALIBAN/TALIBAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/world/middleeast/TALIBAN/TALIBAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taliban Using Modern Means to Add to Sway', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taliban Using Modern Means To Add to Sway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Haqqani Network', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:38:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5aa805e-9ff8-5272-beb7-7e4ac7a433c2', 'word_count': 2118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5aa805e-9ff8-5272-beb7-7e4ac7a433c2'}, {'abstract': 'The trial of Barbara Sheehan had accounts of upper-middle-class rituals alternated with stories of hellish brutality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/nyregion/trial-of-woman-who-killed-husband-goes-to-jury.html', 'snippet': 'The trial of Barbara Sheehan had accounts of upper-middle-class rituals alternated with stories of hellish brutality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the morning she shot her husband five times with a revolver, then grabbed a second pistol and pumped six more bullets into him, Barbara Sheehan had proofread an essay on Genesis 22, written by her son for his freshman religion class. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/nyregion/YABOUT/YABOUT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 329, 'subType': 'jumbo',