nter for Architecture in Greenwich Village has expanded again, inspiring other projects across the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the years he has been associated with the New York chapter of the American Institute of Architects, Rick Bell has witnessed some great real estate deals.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/business/AIA/AIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Building Architects’ Centers to Capture Public Attention', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Building Architects’ Centers To Capture Public Attention', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INSTITUTE OF ARCHITECTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:41:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred A. Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f772b79d-d6a0-5d55-a029-b18e3291ce1c', 'word_count': 1011, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f772b79d-d6a0-5d55-a029-b18e3291ce1c'}, {'abstract': 'Why writing off debts may not necessarily increase economic growth; and why investors should be on the lookout for Apple’s new creative/destructive impacts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/business/the-downside-to-a-debt-jubilee-breakingviews.html', 'snippet': 'Why writing off debts may not necessarily increase economic growth; and why investors should be on the lookout for Apple’s new creative/destructive impacts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good ends do not justify bad means. That philosophical observation applies to proposals for a big American debt jubilee that are now doing the rounds. The basic idea is to slash consumer debt, which is an admirable aim for an overleveraged nation. Household debt is still 90 percent of gross domestic product, down only modestly from the 2008 peak of 100 percent. But even bank-haters should recognize that this cure might be worse than the disease.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Downside to a Debt Jubilee', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Downside To a Debt Jubilee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:43:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Hutchinson and Robert Cyran', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hutchinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8179361d-0ceb-5f5f-ad64-aa0dce2d60d3', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8179361d-0ceb-5f5f-ad64-aa0dce2d60d3'}, {'abstract': 'The unusual circumstances under which a convicted killer lost his right to appeal are the subject of a Supreme Court hearing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/us/an-appeal-gone-astray-catches-the-supreme-courts-attention.html', 'snippet': 'The unusual circumstances under which a convicted killer lost his right to appeal are the subject of a Supreme Court hearing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Cory R. Maples, a death row inmate in Alabama, had what turned out to be the bad fortune to be represented by one of the most prominent law firms in the nation. The Supreme Court heard arguments in his case on Tuesday, and Justice Samuel A. Alito Jr. described where matters stood.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Appeal Gone Astray Catches the Supreme Court’s Attention', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Appeal Gone Astray Catches the Supreme Court’s Attention', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maples, Cory R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sullivan & Cromwell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:44:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': No