zation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/910b2d71-49a3-5a40-b7b2-78f1b98ad58d', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/910b2d71-49a3-5a40-b7b2-78f1b98ad58d'}, {'abstract': 'Killing the leader of a terrorist group is not the best way to weaken the organization.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/opinion/awlakis-death-wont-destroy-al-qaeda.html', 'snippet': 'Killing the leader of a terrorist group is not the best way to weaken the organization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE killing of the Yemeni-American cleric Anwar al-Awlaki on Sept. 30 is arguably the most significant attack on Al Qaeda since Osama bin Laden’s death in May.\xa0 ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Leaders Die, Terror Still Thrives', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Leaders Die, Terror Still Thrives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Awlaki, Anwar al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:52:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Jordan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jordan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed603abf-9693-5862-8597-cdbadba93a39', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed603abf-9693-5862-8597-cdbadba93a39'}, {'abstract': 'The buses from World Wide Travel, which operated the one that crashed in March, killing 15 people, were shifted to a new company, state officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/nyregion/bus-company-shut-after-i-95-crash-reappears-under-new-name.html', 'snippet': 'The buses from World Wide Travel, which operated the one that crashed in March, killing 15 people, were shifted to a new company, state officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the months after a bus crash on Interstate 95 killed 15 people in the Bronx, federal officials were so concerned about the operation of the bus company, World Wide Travel, that they revoked its registration. But the disciplinary action seems to have had little practical effect. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/nyregion/BUS/BUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Bronx Crash, a Bus Fleet Stays on the Road', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Bronx Crash, a Bus Fleet Stays on the Road', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Wide Tours', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Interstate 95', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Ophadell', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:55:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Negroni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Negroni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d14a6820-3f8d-567f-b1dd-14d70ae7cb57', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d14a6820-3f8d-567f-b1dd-14d70ae7cb57'}, {'abstract': 'A practice referred to in a criminal case against an aide in Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s 2009 campaign has been associated for decades with efforts to suppress votes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/nyregion/ballot-security-an-issue-in-consultants-trial-has-a-dark-past.html', 'snippet': 'A practice referred to in a criminal case against an aide in Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s 2009 campaign has been associated for decades with efforts to suppress votes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The charge being weighed by a Manhattan jury in the case of the Republican campaign consultant John Haggerty Jr. is whether he took $1.1 million of Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s money to guard against election fraud, and then spent most of it on a house instead. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/nyregion/YBALLOT1/YBALLOT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Roots of ‘Ballot Security’: Dead Voters, Party Fears and Shadowy Tactics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Roots of ‘Ballot Security’: Dead Voters, Party Fears and Shadowy Maneuvers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T00:57:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/086783d7-9f39-5449-8442-62bb09685228', 'word_count': 1010, 'uri': 'nyt://article/086783d7-9f39-5449-8442-62bb09685228'}, {'abstract': 'Russia’s accession to the W.T.O. has been a key goal of the “reset” between Russia and the United States, a reconciliation whose future is uncertain amid political change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/world/europe/russia-says-its-close-to-joining-the-world-trade-organization.html', 'snippet': 'Russia’s accession to the W.T.O. has been a key goal of the “reset” between Russia and the United States, a reconciliation whose future is uncertain amid political change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — After high-level meetings in Washington, Russian officials said Tuesday that they were on the brink of a deal that would allow Russia to become a member of the World Trade Organization after 18 years of halting negotiations, though hostility between Georgia and Russia remains a crucial sticking point.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Declares It Is Close to Joining the World Trade Organization', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia Declares It Is Close to Joining the World Trade Organization', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Trade Organization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia (Georgian Republic)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T01:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0b1fd49-508c-512c-8855-2146fd01b293', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0b1fd49-508c-512c-8855-2146fd01b293'}, {'abstract': 'Delmon Young, traded by the Twins in August, has become a consistent run producer as the Tigers’ No. 3 hitter and finds himself on the verge of eliminating the Yankees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/sports/baseball/with-tigers-delmon-young-gets-new-lease-in-playoffs.html', 'snippet': 'Delmon Young, traded by the Twins in August, has become a consistent run producer as the Tigers’ No. 3 hitter and finds himself on the verge of eliminating the Yankees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — In the three and a half years that Delmon Young played for the Minnesota Twins, facing the Yankees almost always guaranteed a quiet postgame clubhouse. Not only were the Twins swept in back-to-back American League division series, with many of the games close and excruciating, but they also lost 19 of 26 to the Yankees in the regular season.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/sports/yTigers1/yTigers1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/sports/yTigers1/yTigers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/sports/yTigers1/yTigers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Detroit, Young Gets New Lease in the Playoffs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Detroit, Young Gets New Lease in the Playoffs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T01:11:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af9ad6ad-a231-5b65-b355-82a6e6856af6', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af9ad6ad-a231-5b65-b355-82a6e6856af6'}, {'abstract': 'Weeks after rebels took over Libya’s capital, schools there are struggling with politically divided student bodies, attendance problems and outdated textbooks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/world/africa/in-a-changed-libya-schools-face-new-challenges.html', 'snippet': 'Weeks after rebels took over Libya’s capital, schools there are struggling with politically divided student bodies, attendance problems and outdated textbooks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TRIPOLI, Libya — The classrooms at the Dawn of Freedom middle school were empty. Teachers shuffled around aimlessly outside or gossiped in the halls. A small group of bored teenagers sat in the theater and hatched a plan to coax their classmates back.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/world/SCHOOLS-1/SCHOOLS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/world/SCHOOLS-1/SCHOOLS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/world/SCHOOLS-1/SCHOOLS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Back to School in Libya, and Struggling to Adjust', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back to School in Libya, And Struggling to Adjust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tripoli (Libya)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T01:13:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18424708-b966-5c39-9baf-a66ea10b0149', 'word_count': 1201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18424708-b966-5c39-9baf-a66ea10b0149'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court should conclude that Congress went too far in altering the copyright system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/opinion/keep-works-in-the-public-domain-public.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court should conclude that Congress went too far in altering the copyright system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Philadelphia', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/opinion/05OPEDchi/05OPEDchi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/opinion/05OPEDchi/05OPEDchi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/opinion/05OPEDchi/05OPEDchi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Copyright Stifle Hollywood?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Will Copyright Stifle Hollywood?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Motion Picture Assn of America', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T01:16:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Decherney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Decherney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f32f7b90-c42a-5b72-b558-36c396dc36ec', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f32f7b90-c42a-5b72-b558-36c396dc36ec'}, {'abstract': 'We’re waiting for an actual autumn, a season we hope will last as long as it can, not a prognostication of winter or a postponement of summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/opinion/what-kind-of-fall-am-i.html', 'snippet': 'We’re waiting for an actual autumn, a season we hope will last as long as it can, not a prognostication of winter or a postponement of summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no single way to measure the coming of autumn. Gardeners wait for the first hard frost, the one that blackens the basil and pulps the tomatoes still on the vine. For some, it’s the smell of wood smoke or the sight of leaves flaming out one tree species at a time. In New York City, there are different measures. Fall begins when street fashion slips into thermal chaos — down jackets, shawls, bermudas and flip-flops all on the same block. Fall begins, as it did this week, when the residual heat in the subway station feels strangely welcome. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Kind of Fall Am I?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Kind of Fall Am I?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seasons and Months', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T01:17:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a22a3069-a3d6-5734-aaac-6a797dd27600', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a22a3069-a3d6-5734-aaac-6a797dd27600'}, {'abstract': 'Industrial machinery, computers and aircraft bookings climbed, while orders for motor vehicles decreased, a report showed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/business/orders-for-capital-goods-rose-the-most-in-3-months.html', 'snippet': 'Industrial machinery, computers and aircraft bookings climbed, while orders for motor vehicles decreased, a report showed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Orders for capital equipment increased in August by the most in three months, the Commerce Department said Tuesday, a sign that business investment and exports held up in the face of growing concern over the European debt crisis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Capital Goods Orders Rise the Most in 3 Months', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Capital Goods Orders Rise the Most in 3 Months', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T01:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/197e00b2-570b-501c-a33b-6325cc028e1f', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/197e00b2-570b-501c-a33b-6325cc028e1f'}, {'abstract': 'The pilot whose helicopter crashed in the East River was at the helm of a plane that made an emergency landing in a Brooklyn park five years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/nyregion/pilot-in-east-river-crash-made-emergency-landing-in-2006.html', 'snippet': 'The pilot whose helicopter crashed in the East River was at the helm of a plane that made an emergency landing in a Brooklyn park five years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five years ago, Paul Dudley was at the helm of a plane that was forced to make an emergency landing in a Brooklyn park. It was a nonevent, he said, engine trouble that he compared to “getting a blowout with your car on the highway.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Controls of Doomed Aircraft, a Pilot With Experience', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Controls of Doomed Aircraft, a Pilot With Experience', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Helicopters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airplane Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T01:23:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11f6a83c-18da-548a-82b2-b265ba31e8a1', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11f6a83c-18da-548a-82b2-b265ba31e8a1'}, {'abstract': 'The British government plans to tighten anti-squatting laws to make it easier for property owners to evict uninvited tenants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/world/europe/britain-plans-to-tighten-anti-squatter-laws.html', 'snippet': 'The British government plans to tighten anti-squatting laws to make it easier for property owners to evict uninvited tenant