xas “Niggerhead,” using a phrase so commonplace around the South that it was used as a brand name for oysters, soap, tobacco and even golf tees. When Gov. Rick Perry’s family took over the lease for the camp in 1983, it could have demanded that the name be changed. It could have destroyed the rock on which the name was painted. It could have broken with an era when vicious racism was so casual that officials put such a word on maps around the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gov. Perry’s Rock', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gov. Perry’s Rock: The name of a Texas hunting camp is a reminder that casual bigotry is still far too common', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Geographical', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indecency, Obscenity and Profanity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T01:36:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/193a17b4-6e96-59d0-b52f-8058e829c080', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/193a17b4-6e96-59d0-b52f-8058e829c080'}, {'abstract': 'Arthur C. Nielsen Jr. made his father’s company a global leader in market research whose name is synonymous with television ratings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/business/media/ac-nielsen-jr-who-transformed-research-firm-dies-at-92.html', 'snippet': 'Arthur C. Nielsen Jr. made his father’s company a global leader in market research whose name is synonymous with television ratings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arthur C. Nielsen Jr., who transformed the company his father founded in 1923 into an international leader in market research, helping to make its name synonymous with television ratings, died on Monday in Winnetka, Ill., where he lived most of his life. He was 92.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/business/OBIT-NEILSON/OBIT-NEILSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/business/OBIT-NEILSON/OBIT-NEILSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A.C. Nielsen Jr., Who Built Ratings Firm, Dies at 92', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A.C. Nielsen Jr., Who Built Ratings Firm, Dies at 92', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rating Systems (Media and Entertainment)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T01:37:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f716804-1286-5f15-9e68-f46f22ccc953', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f716804-1286-5f15-9e68-f46f22ccc953'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees’ ace left-hander can opt out of his seven-year, $161 million contract after the season and become a free agent.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/sabathias-future-a-question/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees’ ace left-hander can opt out of his seven-year, $161 million contract after the season and become a free agent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — C. C. Sabathia has been a boon to the Yankees since he arrived in New York, going 59-23 with a 3.18 earned run average in three seasons, and leading the team, both on and off the field. In 2009, he repaid his huge contract by leading the Yankees all the way to a World Series championship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sabathia’s Future a Question', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T01:38:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aad035a4-a124-5e34-b0cb-f0dbc8b8a070', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aad035a4-a124-5e34-b0cb-f0dbc8b8a070'}, {'abstract': 'A capital punishment case in Alabama is rife with constitutional defects and should leave no doubt why the death penalty should be abolished.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/opinion/a-missed-deadline-and-a-death-sentence.html', 'snippet': 'A capital punishment case in Alabama is rife with constitutional defects and should leave no doubt why the death penalty should be abolished.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alabama is a step from executing Cory Maples for a reason so grievously wrong that the case argued Tuesday at the Supreme Court should leave no doubt why the death penalty should be abolished. Besides being barbaric, case after case is rife with constitutional defects. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dreadful Missed Deadline', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dreadful Missed Deadline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maples, Cory R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T01:38:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf2adc04-4db4-52bf-816a-c3166ea46153', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf2adc04-4db4-52bf-816a-c3166ea46153'}, {'abstract': 'Adrian Beltre joined a select fraternity when he blasted three home runs in a postseason game Tuesday, putting his name on a list that includes Babe Ruth, Reggie Jackson, George Brett and Adam Kennedy. Wait, Adam Kennedy?!?', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/04/kennedys-big-day-still-an-aberration/', 'snippet': 'Adrian Beltre joined a select fraternity when he blasted three home runs in a postseason game Tuesday, putting his name on a list that includes Babe Ruth, Reggie Jackson, George Brett and Adam Kennedy. Wait, Adam Kennedy?!?', 'le