predicted “The Playboy Club” on NBC would be canceled after three episodes.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/times-readers-predicted-bunnies-demise/', 'snippet': 'In The New York Times TV Ratings Game, 12.3 percent of the participants correctly predicted “The Playboy Club” on NBC would be canceled after three episodes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first casualty of the new television season, “The Playboy Club,” which was canceled by NBC on Tuesday, was also one of the shows considered least likely to make it this season, according to players in The New York Times TV Ratings Game. And 12.3 percent of the participating readers correctly predicted that show would last only three episodes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Times Readers Predicted Bunnies’ Demise', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'APPLEGATE, CHRISTINA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARNETT, WILL', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bello, Maria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cummings, Whitney', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Brian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T12:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da1ca2a1-cf82-56c5-a064-6a50939c9a72', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da1ca2a1-cf82-56c5-a064-6a50939c9a72'}, {'abstract': 'There are still plenty of reasons for Panthers fans to be excited despite a loss. Cam Newton looks like the real deal.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/week-4-film-review-cam-newton-rising/', 'snippet': 'There are still plenty of reasons for Panthers fans to be excited despite a loss. Cam Newton looks like the real deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A closer look at some of the games in Week 4, via film analysis. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week 4 Film Review: Cam Newton Rising', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T12:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6a64059-1252-5eff-a183-7c26a92714a0', 'word_count': 1254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6a64059-1252-5eff-a183-7c26a92714a0'}, {'abstract': 'On Monday night, a raft of Korean culture and tourism groups held a dinner at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, preceded by a pageant in the great hall.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/koreas-master-chef-prepares-a-banquet-at-the-met/', 'snippet': 'On Monday night, a raft of Korean culture and tourism groups held a dinner at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, preceded by a pageant in the great hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday night, a raft of Korean culture and tourism groups held a dinner at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, preceded by a pageant in the great hall (Korean fashion, as well as food, was being celebrated). The banquet reflected the cuisine of the country’s imperial court in the Chosun dynasty, which lasted from about 1400 to 1900. Han Bok-ryeo, the nation’s official “master chef,” was brought in to oversee the serving of kalbi-jjim (braised beef), kimchi, ssam (rolls), mushrooms, and root vegetables like radishes and carrots — enhanced with aromatics like baby ginseng, pine nuts, dried seaweed and dried red chile. Even tarakjuk, soft rice porridge traditionally served to the emperor at dawn, appeared as a first course, sprinkled with chives. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Korea’s ‘Master Chef’ Prepares a Banquet at the Met', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kimchi (South Korean Food)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T12:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5358c52-daf8-5654-be57-16e743120250', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5358c52-daf8-5654-be57-16e743120250'}, {'abstract': 'Afghanistan’s president, Hamid Karzai, calls Pakistan a “twin brother” and India a “great friend.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/world/asia/karzai-tries-to-soothe-pakistan-over-warmer-relations-with-india.html', 'snippet': 'Afghanistan’s president, Hamid Karzai, calls Pakistan a “twin brother” and India a “great friend.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — A day after signing agreements to step up security cooperation with India, Afghanistan’s president, Hamid Karzai, sought to reassure Pakistan that warming ties with India, Pakistan’s archrival, would not sour their relationship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Karzai Tries to Soothe Pakistan Over Warmer Relations With India', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Karzai Tries to Soothe Pakistan Over Warmer Relations With India', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T12:16:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b90d0086-3978-504d-a773-24b6cb790ec9', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b90d0086-3978-504d-a773-24b6cb790ec9'}, {'abstract': 'Dale Carnegie and Emily Post  get updated for the digital age, iPhone gets an upgrade, eye doctors grow wary of Avastin and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/wednesday-reading-dale-carnegie-and-emily-post-for-the-digital-age/', 'snippet': 'Dale Carnegie and Emily Post  get updated for the digital age, iPhone gets an upgrade, eye doctors grow wary of Avastin and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New Yor