-precedent-on-deals/', 'snippet': 'JPMorgan analysts find fault in what they say are a series of expensive acquisitions like the $11.7 billion deal for the British software maker Autonomy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even after Hewlett-Packard closed its $11.7 billion acquisition of Autonomy on Monday, some apprehension remained about the price tag. H.P. paid a 64 percent premium for the British software maker. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'H.P.’s ‘Unfavorable Precedent’ on Deals', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Autonomy Corp PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hewlett-Packard Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T13:35:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a121d298-b789-51fe-92ef-b9093096e18b', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a121d298-b789-51fe-92ef-b9093096e18b'}, {'abstract': 'JPMorgan Chase said that Hewlett-Packard’s Autonomy deal “sets an unfavorable precedent for future acquisitions to come.”', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/dealbook-h-p-s-unfavorable-precedent-on-deals/', 'snippet': 'JPMorgan Chase said that Hewlett-Packard’s Autonomy deal “sets an unfavorable precedent for future acquisitions to come.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even after Hewlett-Packard closed its $11.7 billion acquisition of Autonomy on Monday, there remains some apprehension about the price tag. H.P. paid a 64 percent premium for the British software maker.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DealBook: H.P.’s ‘Unfavorable Precedent’ on Deals', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T13:44:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a645351-0f3f-536e-a9cd-124c3cef32fa', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a645351-0f3f-536e-a9cd-124c3cef32fa'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/morning-take-out-340/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Morgan Stanley Battles Rumors, Europe Faces a Reckoning | The global markets continue to be buffeted by bank woes. After tanking for most of Tuesday, the European markets were up on reports that shaky banks might get a hand from regulators, news that lifted United States stocks at the close on Tuesday. Amid the volatility, European and American banks face a brutal fallout.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T13:52:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56a0b1eb-16d7-53a4-9bf9-945707590792', 'word_count': 1805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56a0b1eb-16d7-53a4-9bf9-945707590792'}, {'abstract': 'Along with the New York modernist landmark, 65 other sites were placed on the 2102 World Monuments Watch, a list of endangered cultural heritage sites across the globe.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/world-monuments-fund-places-manufacturers-hanover-building-on-at-risk-list/', 'snippet': 'Along with the New York modernist landmark, 65 other sites were placed on the 2102 World Monuments Watch, a list of endangered cultural heritage sites across the globe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 1954 glass box at 510 Fifth Avenue is among the cultural heritage sites at risk, according to the annual list assembled by the World Monuments Fund, which was released on Wednesday. Noting that the controversial renovation of the building at 43rd Street, a branch of what was then the Manufacturers Hanover Trust Company, has been the subject of a court dispute, the fund said the case “raises questions about the legality of recent alterations and the capacity of the New York City Landmarks Commission to enforce protective regulations.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World Monuments Fund Places Manufacturers Hanover Building on At-Risk List', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Monuments Fund', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T14:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f0efad6-1aad-5c5d-904b-cc2227fcdccc', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f0efad6-1aad-5c5d-904b-cc2227fcdccc'}, {