2-cc3afd8c4c5f'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times asked the actress Donna Lynne Champlin, who is also a new mother, to be a guest blogger as she rehearsed for “Jane Austen’s Pride and Prejudice, a Musical,” part of the New York Musical Theater Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/musicals-festival-diary-firsts-for-everything-and-an-opening-to-remember/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times asked the actress Donna Lynne Champlin, who is also a new mother, to be a guest blogger as she rehearsed for “Jane Austen’s Pride and Prejudice, a Musical,” part of the New York Musical Theater Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times asked the actress Donna Lynne Champlin, who is also a new mother, to be a guest blogger as she rehearsed for “Jane Austen’s Pride and Prejudice, a Musical,” part of the New York Musical Theater Festival. In this final installment, she describes the days before opening. A review of the show appears here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Musicals Festival Diary: Firsts for Everything and an Opening to Remember', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T16:36:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donna Lynne Champlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donna', 'middlename': 'Lynne', 'lastname': 'Champlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2e24bcd-b0e6-5908-bd63-a2d8d834da8d', 'word_count': 1178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2e24bcd-b0e6-5908-bd63-a2d8d834da8d'}, {'abstract': 'The current climate at the White House presents an awkward turn of events for William M. Daley a business-friendly banker who seems more comfortable negotiating with Republicans than excoriating them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/us/politics/brutal-budget-battle-presses-william-m-daley-into-political-combat.html', 'snippet': 'The current climate at the White House presents an awkward turn of events for William M. Daley a business-friendly banker who seems more comfortable negotiating with Republicans than excoriating them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When President Obama recruited William M. Daley, a business-friendly banker with a Democratic pedigree to be his chief of staff 10 months ago, Mr. Daley seemed like the right man for a White House determined to cut deals with resurgent Republicans in Congress.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/us/politics/06daleyspan/06daley-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/06/us/politics/06daleyspan/06daley-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/us/politics/06daleyspan/06daley-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/us/politics/06daleyspan/06daley-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/06/us/politics/06daleyspan/06daley-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Budget Presses Obama Aide Into Political Fight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Budget Presses Obama Aide Into Political Fight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daley, William M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plouffe, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T16:41:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9371774c-2008-59d9-a8e4-6d2e2c48143d', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9371774c-2008-59d9-a8e4-6d2e2c48143d'}, {'abstract': 'The Tigers claim to be unruffled by losing the potential series game-winner and having to travel to the Bronx to beat the Yankees.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/tigers-take-the-tough-road/', 'snippet': 'The Tigers claim to be unruffled by losing the potential series game-winner and having to travel to the Bronx to beat the Yankees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT – It could have been neat and simple for the Detroit Tigers. Win Tuesday’s Game 4, against the Yankees at Comerica Park, and their American League division series is clinched. But the plans for a celebration at home blew up in spectacular fashion, as the Yankees pounded the Tigers, 10-1, and forced a decisive Game 5 at Yankee Stadium on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tigers Take the Tough Road', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leyland, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T16:43:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'sectio