be forgotten just the same.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steve Bartman went to a ball game. He tried to do what millions of baseball fans would love to do and catch a ball. No more, no less. But he interfered with play and was vilified because of it. He ceased being human and became a verb, a figure of hatred and of fun. The fact that he was a man of honor really meant nothing. What he did that night defined his life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tévez’s Shrug Heard Round the World', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T18:15:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Clancy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clancy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c663e93-9f76-5aa0-8557-76a161163e37', 'word_count': 1010, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c663e93-9f76-5aa0-8557-76a161163e37'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge ruled that a court-appointed authority would be installed to ensure that more minority candidates are hired at the New York Fire Department.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/nyregion/monitor-must-oversee-ny-fire-dept-hiring-judge-rules.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge ruled that a court-appointed authority would be installed to ensure that more minority candidates are hired at the New York Fire Department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a lacerating decision that accused Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg of willfully ignoring the racial imbalance in the New York Fire Department, a federal judge ruled on Wednesday that a court-appointed monitor would be installed to oversee the department’s recruitment efforts and ensure that more minority candidates are hired.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monitor Must Oversee Fire Dept. Hiring Practices, Judge Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Citing Racial Inequities, Judge Says Fire Dept. Hiring Must Be Monitored', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fire Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garaufis, Nicholas G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T18:19:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61ef6f97-954a-51e3-9fd0-d661cd47ad6b', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61ef6f97-954a-51e3-9fd0-d661cd47ad6b'}, {'abstract': 'Samantha Stosur, Li Na, and Petra Kvitova have had notable struggles after big victories.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/recent-slam-champions-find-encores-a-challenge/', 'snippet': 'Samantha Stosur, Li Na, and Petra Kvitova have had notable struggles after big victories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the scrutiny and criticism that contenders like Caroline Wozniacki and Andy Murray have received fo