how', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ccefabed-d7d5-5778-9ab8-60dbc6198a4c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ccefabed-d7d5-5778-9ab8-60dbc6198a4c'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from Paris Fashion Week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/05/fashion/1005OFFTHERUNWAYPARIS_fw.html', 'snippet': 'Scenes from Paris Fashion Week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from Paris Fashion Week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/fashion/20111005OFFTHERUNWAYPARIS-slide-BRDB/20111005OFFTHERUNWAYPARIS-slide-BRDB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/fashion/20111005OFFTHERUNWAYPARIS-slide-BRDB/20111005OFFTHERUNWAYPARIS-slide-BRDB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/fashion/20111005OFFTHERUNWAYPARIS-slide-BRDB/20111005OFFTHERUNWAYPARIS-slide-BRDB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Runway: Paris Fashion Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T18:27:57+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/b0800cd0-4064-51c4-a0be-4c682f72f4ed', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b0800cd0-4064-51c4-a0be-4c682f72f4ed'}, {'abstract': 'The brightly colored, impossibly upbeat prints of Marimekko now have a home on Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/prints-charming-marimekkos-new-york-city-flagship/', 'snippet': 'The brightly colored, impossibly upbeat prints of Marimekko now have a home on Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If your retail therapist is counseling you to find a happy place, somewhere good to start might be the northwest corner of Broadway and 23rd Street, where a Marimekko flagship store opens its doors for business this week. The airy, industrial space in the former Toy Building has been whitewashed and minimally outfitted, allowing the brightly colored, impossibly upbeat prints for which the 60-year-old company is famous, to shine. The founders, Armi Ratia and her husband, Viljo, always envisioned Marimekko not just as a lifestyle brand, but as a way of life, and over the years their graphic sensibility touched everything from textiles to teapots, all of which are available for purchase. There is even an on-site seamstress, to whip up, say, a set of napkins in Unikko, the signature poppy print, or a pillow cover in the artist Astrid Sylwan’s brush strokey Vattenblänk. The folks at Marimekko hope New Yorkers will embrace the store as a meeting point; the trick, it seems, will be getting them to leave.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prints Charming | Marimekko’s New York City Flagship', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T18:38:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0b5976b-68db-5a07-a315-09cb0f24bbea', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0b5976b-68db-5a07-a315-09cb0f24bbea'}, {'abstract': 'Weapons in the passing game have never been more important. It’s not just that potent wideouts produce big plays – it’s that they also compel defenses to be conservative with their safeties.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/the-importance-of-a-true-no-1-receiver-in-the-n-f-l/', 'snippet': 'Weapons in the passing game have never been more important. It’s not just that potent wideouts produce big plays – it’s that they also compel defenses to be conservative with their safeties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Something that has really stood out on film this season is the significance of wide receivers. With the N.F.L. seemingly entirely pass-oriented these days – the four most productive weeks in league history in terms of passing yards have been Weeks 1, 2, 3 and 4 of the 2011 season – weapons in the passing game have never been more important.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Importance of a True No. 1 Receiver in the N.F.L.', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T18:38:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32308354-91f5-5a01-bc32-b8ec6a5e46ea', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32308354-91f5-5a01-bc32-b8ec6a5e46ea'}, {'abstract': 'A gathering, now in its third week, has become a magnet for New Yorkers who say they have rarely if ever attended a protest before.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/nyregion/wall-st-protest-lures-many-new-to-this-sort-of-thing.html', 'snippet': 'A gathering, now in its third week, has become a magnet for New Yorkers who say they have rarely if ever attended a protest before.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dan Aymar-Blair — age 36, suit wearer, resident of Crown Heights, Brooklyn — never expected to find himself at a protest. Neither did Sean Aiken, a 35-year-old D.J. from Greenpoint, Brooklyn, whose interest in politics had mostly involved grumbling with his friends. The last time Peter Linard, 71, a retired waiter who lives on the Upper East Side, went to a protest, he was living in Greece, where he marched for peace — in 1961.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/nyregion/05Cityroom-Newbies1/05Cityroom-Newbies1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/06/nyregion/05Cityroom-Newbies1/05Cityroom-Newbies1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/nyregion/05Cityroom-Newbies1/05Cityroom-Newbies1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/nyregion/05Cityroom-Newbies1/05Cityroom-Newbies1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/06/nyregion/05Cityroom-Newbies1/05Cityroom-Newbies1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall St. Protest Attracts Many New to This Sort of Thing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New to This Sort of 