', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9893625-66ce-51a5-9000-836951736a78', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9893625-66ce-51a5-9000-836951736a78'}, {'abstract': 'Speculation about potential deals for Yahoo, Akamai Technologies and Research in Motion were enough to spur their share prices to big gains.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/the-markets-love-some-good-deal-speculation/', 'snippet': 'Speculation about potential deals for Yahoo, Akamai Technologies and Research in Motion were enough to spur their share prices to big gains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three of the biggest movers among technology stocks on Wednesday were Yahoo, Akamai Technologies and Research in Motion. What do they have in common?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Markets Love Some Good Deal Speculation', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AKAMAI TECHNOLOGIES INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Research In Motion Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vodafone Group Plc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T20:10:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a8f3495-31a3-552c-b46d-f71323a58176', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a8f3495-31a3-552c-b46d-f71323a58176'}, {'abstract': 'In suing federal agencies, three environmental groups argue that TransCanada has already started to prepare the route for the 1,700-mile Ketsyone XL pipeline even through environmental reviews are not complete.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/on-our-radar-a-pipeline-lawsuit/', 'snippet': 'In suing federal agencies, three environmental groups argue that TransCanada has already started to prepare the route for the 1,700-mile Ketsyone XL pipeline even through environmental reviews are not complete.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Environmental groups sue the State Department and the Department of Interior in federal court in Nebraska to block the construction of the controversial Keystone XL pipeline. They say that TransCanada has already started to prepare the route for the 1,700-mile pipeline, even through federal environmental reviews are not complete. [Bloomberg News]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: A Pipeline Lawsuit', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T20:11:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1475a812-7703-527b-ac2b-cf8e8896521a', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1475a812-7703-527b-ac2b-cf8e8896521a'}, {'abstract': 'The officer in Brooklyn is accused of federal civil rights violations that stem from a confrontation outside a bar, in which the officer is said to have used pepper spray against patrons.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/police-officer-faces-charges-that-he-abused-his-authority/', 'snippet': 'The officer in Brooklyn is accused of federal civil rights violations that stem from a confrontation outside a bar, in which the officer is said to have used pepper spray against patrons.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:23 p.m. | Updated It was the Fourth of July weekend in 2008 at the Living Room Lounge in Bensonhurst, Brooklyn, when a uniformed New York police officer issued a threat: No one, he said, “messes with my cousin’s place.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officer Faces Charges He Abused His Authority', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T20:11:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e6df75e-0571-536f-a725-67bb250e3b24', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e6df75e-0571-536f-a725-67bb250e3b24'}, {'abstract': 'I. M. Pei’s Terminal 6, originally the National Airlines “Sundrome,” is only weeks away from demolition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/06/blogs/20111006Terminal.html', 'snippet': 'I. M. Pei’s Terminal 6, originally the National Airlines “Sundrome,” is only weeks away from demolition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I. M. Pei’s Terminal 6, originally the National Airlines “Sundrome,” is only weeks away from demolition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/blogs/20111006Terminal-slide-D10C/20111006Terminal-slide-D10C-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Modernist Masterpiece Is About to Disappear at Kennedy Airport', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy International Airport (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pei, I M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JetBlue Airways', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T20:12:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/20c51ff7-d403-59fb-bbb8-1de1f9b7f98a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/20c51ff7-d403-59fb-bbb8-1de1f9b7f98a'}, {'abstract': 'Sean Avery cleared waivers Wednesday and was assigned by the Rangers to their American League team.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/avery-clears-waivers/', 'snippet': 'Sean Avery cleared waivers Wednesday and was assigned by the Rangers to their American League team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Rangers agitator Sean Avery cleared N.H.L. waivers on Wednesday, 24 hours after the Rangers placed him there. He was assigned to the team’s American Hockey League affiliate in Hartford, the Connecticut Whale.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Avery Clears Waivers', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Avery, Sean', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staal, Marc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T20:15:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30bae3aa-ad52-5b74-a438-09a8807614bf', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30bae3aa-ad52-5b74-a438-09a8807614bf'}, {'abstract': 'Wrecked in Reykjavík.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/theres-a-fjord-in-my-future/', 'snippet': 'Wrecked in Reykjavík.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This conference should be interesting. They say it will be webcast live; I’ll post information when the event approaches.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'There’s A Fjord In My Future', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T20:16:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdcdf4ee-5d5d-5c19-b07a-fae28e023693', 'word_count': 19, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdcdf4ee-5d5d-5c19-b07a-fae28e023693'}, {'abstract': 'The N.H.L. will end a miserable off-season by starting anew on Thursday with three games, in Boston, Toronto and Vancouver.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/sports/hockey/2011-12-nhl-season-brings-questions-and-relief.html', 'snippet': 'The N.H.L. will end a miserable off-season by starting anew on Thursday with three games, in Boston, Toronto and Vancouver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was another in a succession of strong years for the N.H.L.: exciting play, soaring television ratings, record revenue and the fourth straight Stanley Cup finals between traditional hockey cities. But even as the Boston Bruins were raising the silver chalice on June 15, the riot was on outside in the streets of Vancouver, a four-hour orgy of destruction that injured scores of people and caused millions of dollars in damage.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions and Relief at Season’s Start', 'kicker': 'On Hockey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Questions and Relief at Season’s Start', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaborik, Marian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staal, Marc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lundqvist, Henrik', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brodeur, Martin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parise, Zach', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T20:20:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ff240f1-ce01-546f-a23f-416ae44de60b', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ff240f1-ce01-546f-a23f-416ae44de60b'}, {'abstract': 'That sitcom is leading the way in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic among broadcast networks on Tuesday nights.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/new-girl-on-fox-keeps-drawing-viewers/', 'snippet': 'That sitcom is leading the way in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic among broadcast networks on Tuesday nights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may be just the third week of the fall TV season, but the Tuesday night programming slate has already settled into a ratings groove. Once a wild card, “New Girl” on Fox is now a mainstay thanks to a full-season pickup last week and its continued perch atop the 18-to-49-year-old demographic ratings. The comedy, which stars Zooey Deschanel, lifted Fox to another overall Tuesday night win in that category. “NCIS,” meanwhile, fulfilled the same role it has for the last nine seasons on CBS, gathering the largest possible audience (18.9 million total viewers) while posting respectable numbers in the 18-to-49 category. The one question mark: Sarah Michelle Gellar may have to go back to vampire-slaying: her new show “Ringer” on CW dropped another 33 percent in what was already a dismal 18-to-49 rating. It averaged 1.5 million viewers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘New Girl’ on Fox Keeps Drawing Viewers', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T20:20:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/096b91ce-4ffa-5290-883b-ff3716064d56', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/096b91ce-4ffa-5290-883b-ff3716064d56'}, {'abstract': 'Judicial authorities in Bahrain nullified the convictions and prison terms given to 20 medical workers last week by a court prosecuting cases arising from civil unrest in the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/world/middleeast/bahrain-orders-retrials-for-medical-workers.html', 'snippet': 'Judicial authorities in Bahrain nullified the convictions and prison terms given to 20 medical workers last week by a court prosecuting cases arising from civil unrest in the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bahraini judicial authorities on Wednesday nullified the convictions and harsh prison terms given to 20 medical workers last week by a special security court prosecuting cases arising from civil unrest in the country. The medical workers were ordered released from custody, with new trials scheduled in a civilian court. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bahrain Orders Retrials for Medical Workers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bahrain Voids Health Workers’ Penalties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Physicians for Human Rights', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T20:23:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7559c109-4d03-5d66-b3bf-eaeb6b89dded', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7559c109-4d03-5d66-b3bf-eaeb6b89dded'}, {'abstract': 'The agreement, involving a $73 million payment to the city for a playground, paves the way for waterfront access along the East River. It needs the approval of the U.N., but that is expected.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/land-swap-is-announced-to-allow-new-u-n-tower-and-esplanade/', 'snippet': 'The agreement, involving a $73 million payment to the city for a playground, paves the way for waterfront access along the East River. It needs the approval of the U.N., but that is expected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'City and state officials on Wednesday agreed to a $73 million plan that would unlock an underutilized chunk of the Manhattan waterfront between East 38th and East 60th Streets, paving the way for a new United Nations office tower and esplanade along the East River.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Land Deal Is Announced to Allow New U.N. Tower and Esplanade', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East River (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T20:27:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b45f8e56-528d-524f-972a-0094a24252f8', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b45f8e56-528d-524f-972a-0094a24252f8'}, {'abstract': 'Microsoft will allow Xbox 360 owners to watch programming they are paying for separately through Comcast, Verizon or another TV service provider.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/xbox-is-now-a-tv-box/', 'snippet': 'Microsoft will allow Xbox 360 owners to watch programming they are paying for separately through Comcast, Verizon or another TV service provider.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Microsoft on Wednesday announced the dawning of a “new era” of television. The actual announcement doesn’t amount to nearly that much, but it is worth noting for what it says about our TV habits.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Xbox Is Now a TV Box', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Xbox 360 (Video Game System)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T20:28:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Richtel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richtel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98e52ad5-702b-5ffe-b99d-59223f9a0e09', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98e52ad5-702b-5ffe-b99d-59223f9a0e09'}, {'abstract': 'The television critic Neil Genzlinger is taking your questions on “Terra Nova,” “The Playboy Club” and all things television.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/tv-chat-ask-the-critic/', 'snippet': 'The television critic Neil Genzlinger is taking your questions on “Terra Nova,” “The Playboy Club” and all things television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Neil Genzling