l', 'snippet': 'The cellist Yehuda Hanani brings to light works by Eduard Franck and Moritz Moszkowski, two neglected composers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cellist Yehuda Hanani has been fascinated in recent years with the music of Eduard Franck, a German composer who studied with Mendelssohn and was highly regarded by Schumann. During the Mendelssohn bicentenary in 2009 Mr. Hanani saw an opportunity to bring Franck’s music to light by programming works of both composers in the series he directs, Close Encounters With Music. Mr. Hanani revived and expanded on that idea at the Frick Collection on Tuesday evening in a program that included not only Mendelssohn and Franck scores but also a piece by Moritz Moszkowski, the turn-of-the-last-century virtuoso pianist who, it turns out, studied composition with Franck. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rescuing Neglected Composers', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rescuing Neglected Composers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Frick Collection', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T21:19:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6c8ae47-cef2-50fc-a433-a5bb5eec94c9', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6c8ae47-cef2-50fc-a433-a5bb5eec94c9'}, {'abstract': 'A new work by the dancer-choreographer Norwood Pennewell had its premiere during the Garth Fagan Dance engagement at the Joyce Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2