her mass-worthy raiment stripped down, and softened, for a modern eye.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/in-paris-piety-and-purity/', 'snippet': 'The twin themes resulted in collections bathed in incandescent white and highlighted by wimples, veils, cassocks and other mass-worthy raiment stripped down, and softened, for a modern eye.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FELLINI would have been spinning (cartwheels) in his grave had he witnessed the church-y proceedings on the runways of Paris this week. Taking in those shows, you might have suspected that some designers were reprising “Roma,” the director’s 1972 cinematic tour of the Eternal City complete with a fashion show including priests on roller skates, robotic bishops in miters and stoles, and nuns in habits made of blinking Christmas lights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Paris, Piety and Purity', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T22:05:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth La Ferla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Ferla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00ba55d9-86f9-5344-9b44-247e3fd3370a', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00ba55d9-86f9-5344-9b44-247e3fd3370a'}, {'abstract': '“The Nine Muses,” by the British director John Akomfrah, documents in severe winter landscapes the English immigrant experience in the decades after World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/movies/the-nine-muses-by-john-akomfrah-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Nine Muses,” by the British director John Akomfrah, documents in severe winter landscapes the English immigrant experience in the decades after World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British director John Akomfrah’s “Nine Muses” is an unclassifiable collage of archival footage, canonical literature and severe winter landscapes. Conceptually ambitious and oblique in the extreme, it’s an experimental work that is difficult to unpack critically but impossible to engage without context.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/arts/NINE/NINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/06/arts/NINE/NINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/arts/NINE/NINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 484, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/arts/NINE/NINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/06/arts/NINE/NINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cold and White: Immigrants’ Landscape', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Nine Muses'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cold and White: Immigrants’ Landscape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T22:07:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', '