agraph': 'ABOUT two years ago, Toby Salzman bought two hand-held gadgets that promised, if not the fountain of youth, at least a spigot: LightStim for Wrinkles ($299), which supposedly increases collagen and reduces lines by using red, amber and infrared light; and the Clarisonic Skin Cleansing System ($225), which claims to remove six times more dirt from your face than regular cleansing does.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/fashion/06SKIN1_SPAN/06SKIN1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/06/fashion/06SKIN1_SPAN/06SKIN1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/fashion/06SKIN1_SPAN/06SKIN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/fashion/06SKIN1_SPAN/06SKIN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/06/fashion/06SKIN1_SPAN/06SKIN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking Home the Lasers, Pulsers and Sonic Care', 'kicker': 'Skin Deep', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking Home the Lasers, Pulsers and Sonic Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ultraviolet Light', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laser (Light Amplification by Stimulated Emission of Radiation)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_