0 years, Fred Wesley, Pee Wee Ellis and Maceo Parker, former mainstays of James Brown’s band, will play together at Town Hall on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks to James Brown, even casual followers of rhythm and blues are on a first-name basis with the three core members of his old horn section. In one hit song after another, from the mid-1960s through the early 1970s, Brown, known as the Godfather of Soul, would address them directly, urging them on with interjections like, “Hit me, Fred!” or “Pee Wee, take it on out!” or “Maceo, all right, bring your lickin’ stick!”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/arts/Horn-1/Horn-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/arts/Horn-1/Horn-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/06/arts/Horn-1/Horn-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Godsons of Soul Reunite to Toot Their Horns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Godsons of Soul Reunite to Toot Their Horns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellis, Pee Wee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Maceo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-05T23:10:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role':