graph': 'When Eric Cantor, the House Republican leader, predictably said that President Obama’s jobs bill was dead on arrival in his chamber, and would not even be debated, the president — in a break from his usual forbearance — lashed right back at him. “Does he not believe in rebuilding America’s roads and bridges?” Mr. Obama asked on Tuesday. Does Mr. Cantor oppose rehiring teachers or construction workers, he continued, or giving tax breaks to businesses that hire?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where’s the Jobs Bill?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where’s the Jobs Bill? Congressional Democrats need to stop cowering and fight for it', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cantor, Eric', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T01:17:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d09b01c-3df1-5261-b8c1-e56b4e34b587', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d09b01c-3df1-5261-b8c1-e56b4e34b587'}, {'abstract': 'Jimi Hendrix was among several artists discussed in a case on whether Congress acted constitutionally by restoring copyright protection to works that had been in the public domain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/business/jimi-hendrix-is-cited-during-supreme-court-arguments.html', 'snippet': 'Jimi Hendrix was among several artists discussed in a case on whether Congress acted constitutionally by restoring copyright protection to works that had been in the public domain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Jimi Hendrix made an appearance at the Supreme Court on Wednesday in an argument over whether Congress acted constitutionally in 1994 by restoring copyright protection to foreign works that had once been in the public domain. The affected works included films by Alfred Hitchcock and Federico Fellini, books by C. S. Lewis and Virginia Woolf, symphonies by Prokofiev and Stravinsky and paintings by Picasso.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/business/Copyright/Copyright-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 614, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/business/Copyright/Copyright-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/06/business/Copyright/Copyright-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Supreme Court Argument, a Rock Legend Plays a Role', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Supreme Court Argument, A Rock Legend Plays a Role', 'name': None, 'seo': Non