{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yom Kippur', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich (Conn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T01:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Gelfand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gelfand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7a9ed8a-77e5-5cc9-9b2b-d22e09793369', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7a9ed8a-77e5-5cc9-9b2b-d22e09793369'}, {'abstract': 'Returning to the PGA Tour with a new caddie after a 54-day layoff from competition, Tiger Woods has a far greater goal than making the cut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/sports/golf/tiger-woods-beginning-return-to-tour-at-fryscom-open.html', 'snippet': 'Returning to the PGA Tour with a new caddie after a 54-day layoff from competition, Tiger Woods has a far greater goal than making the cut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN MARTIN, Calif. — After a 54-day layoff from competitive golf, Tiger Woods stepped to the first tee at CordeValle Golf Club on Wednesday morning and hit his first drive left of the fairway.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/sports/Y-JP-GOLF/Y-JP-GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/06/sports/Y-JP-GOLF/Y-JP-GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/sports/Y-JP-GOLF/Y-JP-GOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/sports/Y-JP-GOLF/Y-JP-GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/06/sports/Y-JP-GOLF/Y-JP-GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Woods Looks at His Return as a Chance at Much More', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Woods, Back on Tour, Has Sights Set High', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Professional Golfers Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T01:34:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75b6508a-5e70-55da-a83f-9890bed45b68', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75b6508a-5e70-55da-a83f-9890bed45b68'}, {'abstract': 'The latest breakdown of the Long Island Rail Road, part of the cash-starved M.T.A., is another reason why the state government needs to spend more money to keep it healthy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/opinion/hell-on-rails.html', 'snippet': 'The latest breakdown of the Long Island Rail Road, part of the cash-starved M.T.A., is another reason why the state government needs to spend more money to keep it healthy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few things say “urban mass misery” more vividly than a breakdown on the Long Island Rail Road, the nation’s oldest, largest and, lately, most trouble-prone commuter railroad. Last Thursday, lightning fried the signal system at the Jamaica Station hub in Queens, shutting service out of Penn Station at the height of rush hour. Soon after, a still-unexplained signal failure stopped all trains going east of Jamaica. Workers with mallets and spikes trudged out to the tracks to hammer stuck signals into place, a 19th-century response to a 21st-century debacle. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hell on Rails', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hell on Rails', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Long Island Rail Road Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T01:36:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ce12446-b70e-5cd7-b6df-117886a6988f', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ce12446-b70e-5cd7-b6df-117886a6988f'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Jobs earned a place on Disney’s board when he sold Pixar to the company in 2006. The deal also made him Disney’s biggest shareholder.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/jobs-frequently-consulted-with-disney-chief/', 'snippet': 'Steve Jobs earned a place on Disney’s board when he sold Pixar to the company in 2006. The deal also made him Disney’s biggest shareholder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steve Jobs’s death leaves an open seat on the board of the Walt Disney Company, which he joined in 2006 when he sold Pixar Animation Studio to Disney for $7.4 billion. The deal also made Mr. Jobs Disney’s biggest shareholder. Although he frequently consulted with Robert A. Iger, Disney’s chief executive, Mr. Jobs was not a frequent presence at board meetings, a fact that drew some criticism from people concerned with corporate governance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jobs Frequently Consulted With Disney Chief', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T01:36:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bbc70b2-585c-5c1a-b4de-078343efa9b0', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bbc70b2-585c-5c1a-b4de-078343efa9b0'}, {'abstract': 'After winning a recent straw poll in Florida, it would seem that it is Herman Cain’s moment, but his public appearances have focused on his newly released book.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/us/politics/gop-hopeful-herman-cain-on-book-tour-not-campaign-trail.html', 'snippet': 'After winning a recent straw poll in Florida, it would seem that it is Herman Cain’s moment, but his public appearances have focused on his newly released book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a whirlwind trip through New York City this week that marked the beginning of a nearly monthlong book tour, Herman Cain chatted with the hosts of ABC’s “The View,” promoted his new memoir on Fox News, met local titans like Donald Trump, shared ideas with former Mayor Edward I. Koch and enjoyed po