ract': 'As the founder of Apple, Steven P. Jobs transformed the personal computer and created a series of revolutionary products that extended computing into every nook and cranny of our culture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000001094732/the-legacy-of-steve-jobs.html', 'snippet': 'As the founder of Apple, Steven P. Jobs transformed the personal computer and created a series of revolutionary products that extended computing into every nook and cranny of our culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the founder of Apple, Steven P. Jobs transformed the personal computer and created a series of revolutionary products that extended computing into every nook and cranny of our culture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/multimedia/video-stevejobsdeath/video-stevejobsdeath-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/05/multimedia/video-stevejobsdeath/video-stevejobsdeath-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/multimedia/video-stevejobsdeath/video-stevejobsdeath-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/multimedia/video-stevejobsdeath/video-stevejobsdeath-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Legacy of Steve Jobs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T03:22:34+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Shayla Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shayla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/5c9b1838-7453-5cd2-a15e-f77cb16263b5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/5c9b1838-7453-5cd2-a15e-f77cb16263b5'}, {'abstract': 'Israel dismissed its deputy ambassador to Washington over allegations that he leaked top-secret information to an Israeli journalist, a Foreign Ministry spokeswoman said Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/world/middleeast/israel-envoy-to-washington-fired-over-leak-to-a-newspaper.html', 'snippet': 'Israel dismissed its deputy ambassador to Washington over allegations that he leaked top-secret information to an Israeli journalist, a Foreign Ministry spokeswoman said Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Israel dismissed its deputy ambassador to Washington over allegations that he leaked top-secret information to an Israeli journalist, a Foreign Ministry spokeswoman said Wednesday. The diplomat, Dan Arbel, a senior civil servant, faces a disciplinary procedure in Jerusalem. The alleged leak occurred more than two years ago, before he arrived in Washington. The case involves information related to Iran that apparently angered the United States. In December 2009, a top ministry official, Alon Bar, was suspended on suspicion of having given the information to a reporter for the newspaper Haaretz. Mr. Bar was exonerated and is now the ambassador to Spain. The investigation continued and led to Mr. Arbel, the ministry said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel: Envoy to Washington Fired Over Leak to a Newspaper', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | MIDDLE EAST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: Envoy to Washington Fired Over Leak to a Newspaper', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Haaretz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T03:31:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/85f9f4f8-dfc6-543d-98a6-db23d0760f49', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85f9f4f8-dfc6-543d-98a6-db23d0760f49'}, {'abstract': 'Uncertainty hanging over Liberia’s imminent presidential election ended Wednesday when the Supreme Court threw out a challenge to the incumbent, Ellen Johnson Sirleaf.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/world/africa/liberia-ruling-favors-president.html', 'snippet': 'Uncertainty hanging over Liberia’s imminent presidential election ended Wednesday when the Supreme Court threw out a challenge to the incumbent, Ellen Johnson Sirleaf.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Uncertainty hanging over Liberia’s imminent presidential election ended Wednesday when the Supreme Court threw out a challenge to the incumbent, Africa’s first woman to be elected as head of state, Ellen Johnson Sirleaf, left, along with her principal rivals. The civil war here, lasting more than a decade, had scattered the country’s political class, and a small opposition party said that Mrs. Johnson Sirleaf violated a constitutional clause requiring candidates be residents for 10 years before the election, which is next Tuesday. But the court said the Constitution’s authors could not have foreseen the extended conflict into which the country plunged. “We considered the suit frivolous from the beginning,” a spokesman for the president’s party said; the opposition politician who filed it, Simeon Freeman, criticized the decision as “political.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/world/06briefs-sirleaf/06briefs-sirleaf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/06/world/06briefs-sirleaf/06briefs-sirleaf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Liberia: Ruling Favors President', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | AFRICA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Liberia: Ruling Favors President', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson Sirleaf, Ellen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T03:31:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/df1fb619-ddb2-5d07-ae36-836a1febe966', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df1fb619-ddb2-5d07-ae36-836a1febe966'}, {'abstract': 'With the hashtag #SteveJobsLegacy, people on Twitter assessed the contributions of Steve Jobs to their own lives.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/on-twitter-reflecting-on-the-legacy-of-steve-jobs/', 'snippet': 'With the hashtag #SteveJobsLegacy, people on Twitter assessed the contributions of Steve Jobs to their own lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We asked our Twitter followers on @nytimes to discuss the impact of Steve Jobs’ work using the hashtag #SteveJobsLegacy. Below is a selection of the response we received. Please continue to share your thoughts by tweeting to us at @nytimes using #SteveJobsLegacy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Twitter, Reflecting on the Legacy of Steve Jobs', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T03:32:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Mainland and Liz Heron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mainland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e652116-c734-5680-9620-c4217f8f2863', 'word_count': 45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e652116-c734-5680-9620-c4217f8f2863'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Jobs broke through institutional resistance in the music business and helped change the way people get their songs.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/he-pushed-a-reluctant-industry-toward-digital-music/', 'snippet': 'Steve Jobs broke through institutional resistance in the music business and helped change the way people get their songs.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:44 p.m. | Updated Digital music is now perhaps the biggest priority in the music industry. It is the future model looked to by struggling record labels and the foundation of big-thinking start-up companies that, by at least one count, have raised more than $400 million in investment so far this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'He Pushed a Reluctant Industry Toward Digital Music', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beatles, The', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T03:39:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e629b25-4b3d-5917-bfc5-834e01c12dc7', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e629b25-4b3d-5917-bfc5-834e01c12dc7'}, {'abstract': 'President Sebastián Piñera sent a bill to Congress Tuesday calling for a strengthening of Chile’s penal code, a move aimed at further repressing large student protests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/world/americas/chile-proposal-to-curb-protesters.html', 'snippet': 'President Sebastián Piñera sent a bill to Congress Tuesday calling for a strengthening of Chile’s penal code, a move aimed at further repressing large student protests.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Sebastián Piñera sent a bill to Congress Tuesday night calling for a strengthening of Chile’s penal code, a move aimed at further repressing large student protests that have led his government’s popularity to plummet. The bill, which is expected to face a stiff challenge from the opposition Concertación coalition, would set prison sentences of up to three years for anyone who occupied public or private institutions like schools or universities, and it would also penalize other forms of demonstration. Since May, students have occupied more than 200 institutions of learning. They are demanding a range of reforms, chief among them a return to widely available free public college education that existed before the 17-year dictatorship of Gen. Augusto Pinochet. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chile: Proposal to Curb Protesters', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | THE AMERICAS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chile: Proposal to Curb Protesters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinera, Sebastian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Secondary)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T03:41:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexei Barrionuevo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barrionuevo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0e850bd-6c31-568a-bf6a-4ccb9c61193e', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0e850bd-6c31-568a-bf6a-4ccb9c61193e'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on October 6, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/pageoneplus/corrections-october-5.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on October 6, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: October 6', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T03:43:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/79497b51-24dd-5ff0-b0a1-f36d1fbdbc7d', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79497b51-24dd-5ff0-b0a1-f36d1fbdbc7d'}, {'abstract': 'Fans reacted to the death of Steven P. Jobs by using their Apple laptops, leaving flowers at Apple stores and flooding Twitter with messages — a veritable technology 21-gun salute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/technology/jobss-death-prompts-grief-and-tributes.html', 'snippet': 'Fans reacted to the death of Steven P. Jobs by using their Apple laptops, leaving flowers at Apple stores and flooding Twitter with messages — a veritable technology 21-gun salute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Artist, role model, innovator, life-changer. Those words popped up repeatedly on Wednesday in the outpouring of emotional responses to the death of Steve Jobs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/business/REACT/REACT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/06/business/REACT/REACT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/business/REACT/REACT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/business/REACT/REACT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/06/business/REACT/REACT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jobs’s Death Draws Outpouring of Grief and Tributes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jobs’s Death Draws Outpouring of Grief and Tributes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T03:45:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Richtel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richtel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eae62b9b-8f29-56f9-a790-d2f8c0c76405', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eae62b9b-8f29-56f9-a790-d2f8c0c76405'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Jansch, a founder of the progressive British folk group Pentangle, became an immediate sensation in 1965 with his self-titled debut album.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/arts/music/bert-jansch-influential-guitarist-is-dead-at-67.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Jansch, a founder of the progressive British folk group Pentangle, became an immediate sensation in 1965 with his self-titled debut album.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bert Jansch, a guitarist whose blend of classical, jazz, blues and traditional British folk music inspired a long list of folk and rock guitarists in the 1960s and ’70s, including Donovan, Jimmy Page, Neil Young and Paul Simon, died on Wednesday in London. He was 67.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/arts/subJANSCH-obit/subJANSCH-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/arts/subJANSCH-obit/subJANSCH-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/06/arts/subJANSCH-obit/subJANSCH-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bert Jansch, an Influential Folk Guitarist, Is Dead at 67', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bert Jansch, 67, Idiosyncratic Folk Guitarist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jansch, Bert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guitars', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T03:47:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d65edd4-0d1e-5cea-9e2b-f1d2edf01d70', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d65edd4-0d1e-5cea-9e2b-f1d2edf01d70'}, {'abstract': 'The top stories across India on Thursday are reported and interpreted by the Indian press.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/05/newswallah-in-the-english-language-press-thursday-3/', 'snippet': 'The top stories across India on Thursday are reported and interpreted by the Indian press.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Top leaders of the Congress Party are questioning one of the United Progressive Alliance government’s most significant achievements of its last term, the Right to Information Act.\xa0Salman Kurshid, India’s law minister, advocates amending the popular RTI act to prevent it from misuse that is affecting “institutional efficacy and efficiency.” The law, which allows citizen scrutiny of almost all government functions, has often been the target of efforts to limit its authority. (Indian Express)India’s army chief sounded the alarm over 4,000 Chinese construction workers, including some combat engineers from the People’s Liberation Army, in the portion of Kashmir controlled by Pakistan. India has asked China to stop working on infrastructure projects inside Pakistan-controlled Kashmir, the Times of India reports. The warm relationship between Pakistan and China worries India, which fears being encircled by China and its allies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: In the English-Language Press Thursday', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T03:57:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1de4dfe2-080b-53b8-b4bb-b65bd7c37551', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1de4dfe2-080b-53b8-b4bb-b65bd7c37551'}, {'abstract': 'Cooking an apple can turn this stalwart fruit into a culinary star.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/10/09/magazine/09-apples-matrix.html', 'snippet': 'Cooking an apple can turn this stalwart fruit into a culinary star.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cooking an apple can turn this stalwart fruit into a culinary star.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recipes: Baked, Sautéed, Fried or Roasted Apples', 'kicker': 'Eat | Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPLES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T03:58:00+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/564829c9-4a97-5de7-bf70-edd485c44d67', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/564829c9-4a97-5de7-bf70-edd485c44d67'}, {'abstract': 'Cooking this stalwart fruit can turn it into a culinary star.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/magazine/mark-bittman-how-you-like-them-cooked-apples.html', 'snippet': 'Cooking this stalwart fruit can turn it into a culinary star.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you transform an apple by cooking, you may make it soft, fluffy, chewy, savory, sweet or creamy — the potential is enormous. Yes, an apple loses some juiciness and freshness when you cook it, but as an ingredient it’s just as versatile as a potato. (You probably know that in French the potato is called pomme de terre, or “apple of the earth.”) The surprise from a raw apple comes from the variety and the season, whereas the surprise from a cooked apple comes from what you do with it.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '52', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/magazine/09eat_span/mag-09Eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/09/magazine/09eat_span/mag-09Eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/magazine/09eat_span/mag-09Eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/magazine/09eat_span/mag-09Eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/magazine/09eat_span/mag-09Eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How You Like Them (Cooked) Apples?', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Old Temptation, New Twist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fruit', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPLES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T04:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5b9dad9-47c0-501e-aee3-2e124705a0aa', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5b9dad9-47c0-501e-aee3-2e124705a0aa'}, {'abstract': 'A decision limits the enforcement options of Finra, an important Wall Street regulator, just as it is under pressure to impose greater accountability on brokers and firms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/business/court-rules-against-finra-on-enforcement-actions.html', 'snippet': 'A decision limits the enforcement options of Finra, an important Wall Street regulator, just as it is under pressure to impose greater accountability on brokers and firms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal appeals court in Manhattan ruled on Wednesday that Finra, an important regulator of Wall Street for more than 70 years, does not have the right to take its members to court to enforce its disciplinary actions.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Says Regulator Exceeded Its Power', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Says Regulator Exceeded Its Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Industry Regulatory Authority', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NASD', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T04:08:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diana B. Henriques', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c30f937d-7799-57ed-936b-44af7a76e011', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c30f937d-7799-57ed-936b-44af7a76e011'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 437 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/word-of-the-day-meditation/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 437 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'meditation •\\ˌme-də-ˈta-shən\\• noun', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | meditation', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T04:09:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef5d1f67-9931-5b6f-9f33-052c2a1209bb', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef5d1f67-9931-5b6f-9f33-052c2a1209bb'}, {'abstract': 'The rally in global stocks continued Thursday, but Wall Street’s gains were more moderate than Europe’s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/business/daily-stock-market-activity.html', 'snippet': 'The rally in global stocks continued Thursday, but Wall Street’s gains were more moderate than Europe’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wall Street registered gains for the third consecutive day on Thursday, following European stocks higher after central banks in Europe took action to increase liquidity. Economic data, including retail sales, also showed an American economy that is performing better than expected. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strong Retail Sales Send Issues Higher for 3rd Day', 'kicker': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strong Retail Sales Send Issues Higher for 3rd Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nikkei Stock Average', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T04:16:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Brustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf673a79-27aa-5f7b-be97-de945bafd51c', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf673a79-27aa-5f7b-be97-de945bafd51c'}, {'abstract': 'An inquiry concerning an evaluation of the Keystone XL pipeline proposal now includes lobbyists, who once held senior positions for Secretary of State Hillary Rodham and President Obama during their respective campaigns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/science/earth/06brfs-Pipeline.html', 'snippet': 'An inquiry concerning an evaluation of the Keystone XL pipeline proposal now includes lobbyists, who once held senior positions for Secretary of State Hillary Rodham and President Obama during their respective campaigns.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Friends of the Earth, an environmental group, expanded its Freedom of Information Act request concerning the State Department’s evaluation of the Keystone XL pipeline proposal, which involves the construction of a new pipeline to carry crude from Canadian oil sands to the Gulf Coast. The environmental group’s original request had centered on communication between the State Department and Paul Elliott, the chief Washington lobbyist for TransCanada, the pipeline company. Mr. Elliott was a senior official in Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton’s 2008 presidential bid. On Wednesday, the group expanded its request to cover several other lobbyists now working for TransCanada who held senior positions for Mrs. Clinton and President Obama during their campaigns. These include Jeff Berman of Bryan Cave LLC, who was national delegate director for the Obama presidential campaign. Environmental groups say the administration has shown a bias toward approving the pipeline as a result of such ties. ELISABETH ROSENTHAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Group Opposed to Pipeline Seeks More Documents on Lobbyists', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Group Opposed to Pipeline Seeks More Documents on Lobbyists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Sands', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Information Act', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Friends of the Earth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TransCanada Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T04:18:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d44fedc7-9c07-53ef-8f96-7944305a37f9', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d44fedc7-9c07-53ef-8f96-7944305a37f9'}, {'abstract': 'Embedding messages of social change in movies and documentaries was discussed by advertising executives as part of the third day of Advertising Week 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/business/media/movies-and-messages-of-social-change.html', 'snippet': 'Embedding messages of social change in movies and documentaries was discussed by advertising executives as part of the third day of Advertising Week 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE widespread changes in consumer behavior and technology that are prompting marketers to rethink how they sell products are much on the minds of Madison Avenue. That was underlined on Wednesday by spirited discussions during the third day of Advertising Week 2011.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 31