'word_count': 982, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb1a56a6-a09c-5e73-9092-ca7a7a582509'}, {'abstract': 'House Democrats released documents showing discussions between a Solyndra lobbyist and the Obama administration about a possible “phase 2 loan guarantee application.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/us/politics/2nd-us-loan-to-solyndra-said-to-have-been-considered.html', 'snippet': 'House Democrats released documents showing discussions between a Solyndra lobbyist and the Obama administration about a possible “phase 2 loan guarantee application.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Early last year, the Obama administration was so optimistic about the business prospects of Solyndra, the solar equipment manufacturer that declared bankruptcy last month after receiving a $528 million government loan, that officials entertained the possibility of giving the California company a second loan of almost half a billion dollars, according to internal e-mails.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E-Mails Suggest White House Weighed a 2nd Solyndra Loan Worth Almost Half a Billion Dollars', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'E-Mails Suggest White House Weighed a 2nd Solyndra Loan Worth Almost Half a Billion Dollars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Solyndra Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T04:38:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2930dd92-ab13-5721-aa87-a7e3280a6bc3', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2930dd92-ab13-5721-aa87-a7e3280a6bc3'}, {'abstract': 'A pioneer of “critical race theory,” Mr. Bell was the first tenured black professor at Harvard Law School before moving to New York University.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/us/derrick-bell-pioneering-harvard-law-professor-dies-at-80.html', 'snippet': 'A pioneer of “critical race theory,” Mr. Bell was the first tenured black professor at Harvard Law School before moving to New York University.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Derrick Bell, a legal scholar who saw persistent racism in America and sought to expose it through books, articles and provocative career moves — he gave up a Harvard Law School professorship to protest the school’s hiring practices — died on Wednesday in Manhattan. He was 80 and lived on the Upper West Side.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07bell/07bell-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07bell/07bell-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07bell/07bell-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07bell/07bell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07bell/07bell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Derrick Bell, Law Professor and Rights Advocate, Dies at 80', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Derrick Bell, Pioneering Law Professor And Civil Rights Advocate, Dies at 80', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bell, Derrick A Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn for the Advancement of Colored People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T05:24:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred A. Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7b962a8-8b17-509b-8267-20f4f1fdca72', 'word_count': 1354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7b962a8-8b17-509b-8267-20f4f1fdca72'}, {'abstract': 'For the second straight game, the Diamondbacks hit a grand slam against Brewers pitching, and they forced a deciding Game 5.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/sports/baseball/diamondbacks-force-game-5-against-brewers.html', 'snippet': 'For the second straight game, the Diamondbacks hit a grand slam against Brewers pitching, and they forced a deciding Game 5.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — The scenario was frozen in time from the previous night as Ryan Roberts stood in the on-deck circle. The bases again were loaded with Arizona Diamondbacks, this time in the first inning, and Roberts watched intently as Paul Goldschmidt stared at the possibility of belting a grand slam in consecutive playoff games.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/sports/06dbacks-1/06dbacks-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/06/sports/06dbacks-1/06dbacks-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/sports/06dbacks-1/06dbacks-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/sports/06dbacks-1/06dbacks-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/06/sports/06dbacks-1/06dbacks-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Once Again, Thunder in the Desert', 'kicker': 'Diamondbacks 10, Brewers 6', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Once Again, Thunder in the Desert', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Brewers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA DIAMONDBACKS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Chris', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolf, Randy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T05:34:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Spousta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spousta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04431457-3d14-54aa-8427-de8f6cf9e55d', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04431457-3d14-54aa-8427-de8f6cf9e55d'}, {'abstract': 'A group gathers in San Francisco and expresses their feelings about Steve Jobs.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/a-tribute-with-iphones/', 'snippet': 'A group gathers in San Francisco and expresses their feelings about Steve Jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 9 p.m. on Wednesday in San Francisco, a few dozen start-up entrepreneurs, Apple employees and iPhone fans gathered in Dolores Park, the four-square-block park in the middle of the city’s Mission district, home to hipsters and artists tethered to their MacBooks and iPhones. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tribute, With iPhones', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T06:39:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 