None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68ab2783-73b9-5fa0-8b1f-ee341cfaba2c', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68ab2783-73b9-5fa0-8b1f-ee341cfaba2c'}, {'abstract': 'On Oct. 6, 1981, President Anwar Sadat of Egypt was shot to death by Islamic militants during a military parade.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/oct-6-1981-egypt-president-anwar-sadat-is-killed/', 'snippet': 'On Oct. 6, 1981, President Anwar Sadat of Egypt was shot to death by Islamic militants during a military parade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Oct. 6, 1981, President Anwar Sadat of Egypt was shot to death by Islamic militants during a military parade. The assassination occurred when a truck carrying the Army officer Khalid Islambouli stopped in front of the president’s reviewing stand; Mr. Islambouli began hurling grenades toward Mr. Sadat, and three other extremists fired indiscriminately into the crowd, killing Mr. Sadat and 11 others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oct. 6, 1981 | Egypt’s Anwar Sadat Is Killed', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T08:07:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/361499aa-05cf-5c20-ace3-fed7f7bbbf93', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/361499aa-05cf-5c20-ace3-fed7f7bbbf93'}, {'abstract': 'The archbishop of Canterbury begins his visit to Africa by meeting with President Robert G. Mugabe of Zimbabwe and seeking to heal a rift within the country’s Anglican congregation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/world/africa/anglican-leader-to-seek-meeting-with-mugabe.html', 'snippet': 'The archbishop of Canterbury begins his visit to Africa by meeting with President Robert G. Mugabe of Zimbabwe and seeking to heal a rift within the country’s Anglican congregation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The Most Rev. Rowan Williams, archbishop of Canterbury, will travel to Zimbabwe this weekend as part of an African tour and will seek to persuade President Robert G. Mugabe to help end a rift among the country’s Anglicans, according to the archbishop’s office here.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anglican Leader to Seek Meeting With Mugabe', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Talks on Anglican Rift', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Rowan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mugabe, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANGLICAN CHURCHES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zimbabwe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zimbabwe African National Union-Patriotic Front (ZANU-PF)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kunonga, Nolbert', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T08:13:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/000168fd-f783-5e59-a744-f2a2cef96a7e', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/000168fd-f783-5e59-a744-f2a2cef96a7e'}, {'abstract': 'Bold talk is one thing, but Europe’s leaders have so far failed to come to grips with the depths of their economic problems, two economists write.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/the-4-trillion-euro-fantasy/', 'snippet': 'Bold talk is one thing, but Europe’s leaders have so far failed to come to grips with the depths of their economic problems, two economists write.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Boone is chairman of the charity Effective Intervention and a research associate at the Center for Economic Performance at the London School of Economics. He is also a principal in Salute Capital Management Ltd. Simon Johnson, the former chief economist at the International Monetary Fund, is the co-author of “13 Bankers.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 4-Trillion-Euro Fantasy', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T09:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Boone and Simon Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25d4748d-b0ea-5f6d-bf76-ae29cfb65766', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25d4748d-b0ea-5f6d-bf76-ae29cfb65766'}, {'abstract': 'Justice Stephen G. Breyer has never studied architecture, but he has been appointed to the jury that awards the Pritzker Prize.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/arts/design/stephen-breyer-pritzker-prize-jury-architecture.html', 'snippet': 'Justice Stephen G. Breyer has never studied architecture, but he has been appointed to the jury that awards the Pritzker Prize.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — True, he helped devise a suitable design for the federal courthouse in Boston several years ago. And he did write the foreword to a book called “Celebrating the Courthouse: A Guide for Architects, Their Clients, and the Public.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/us/JUSTICE/JUSTICE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 614, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/us/JUSTICE/JUSTICE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/06/us/JUSTICE/JUSTICE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Breyer Invited to Make a Case for Architecture', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Breyer Invited to Make a Case for Architecture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breyer, Stephen G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pritzker Prize', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T09:02:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename'