s Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c3a1974-81c5-55a8-b74b-cc45073daf61', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c3a1974-81c5-55a8-b74b-cc45073daf61'}, {'abstract': 'The reviews are in! The critics weigh in on Wednesday’s shows in Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/runway-in-review-28/', 'snippet': 'The reviews are in! The critics weigh in on Wednesday’s shows in Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elie SaabDesigner: Elie SaabDate and Location: Wednesday, Oct. 5, Espace Ephemere Tuileries, Jardin Des Tuileries, 1erPhotos: slide show', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Runway In Review', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T13:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison S. Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e921e33e-2e1b-599d-beea-bde5ff5d0971', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e921e33e-2e1b-599d-beea-bde5ff5d0971'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Corbijn, the director of “The American” and “Control” as well as videos for Nirvana’s “Heart-Shaped Box” and Depeche Mode’s “Personal Jesus,” will oversee 12 cameras at a Coldplay performance on Oct. 26 at Madrid’s Plaza de Toros de Las Ventas.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/coldplay-concert-directed-by-anton-corbijn-to-be-broadcast-live-on-the-web/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Corbijn, the director of “The American” and “Control” as well as videos for Nirvana’s “Heart-Shaped Box” and Depeche Mode’s “Personal Jesus,” will oversee 12 cameras at a Coldplay performance on Oct. 26 at Madrid’s Plaza de Toros de Las Ventas...', 'lead_paragraph': 'To add to a directorial résumé that includes films like “The American” and “Control” as well as music videos like U2’s “One” and Nirvana’s “Heart-Shaped Box,” Anton Corbijn has found an assignment that he expects will keep him on his feet. “And afterwards,” he said, “on my back, probably.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coldplay Live Concert Webcast to Be Directed by Anton Corbijn', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corbijn, Anton', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARCADE FIRE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coldplay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Depeche Mode', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duran Duran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'My Morning Jacket', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nirvana', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radiohead', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'U2', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vevo.com', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madrid (Spain)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T13:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82f74078-e5bb-5729-8886-5e66c38b203e', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82f74078-e5bb-5729-8886-5e66c38b203e'}, {'abstract': 'The potential for a calendar collision between the presidential election process and the 2011 holiday season now rests almost entirely with Billy Gardner, the secretary of state for New Hampshire.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/when-holiday-and-political-calendars-collide/', 'snippet': 'The potential for a calendar collision between the presidential election process and the 2011 holiday season now rests almost entirely with Billy Gardner, the secretary of state for New Hampshire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The potential for a calendar collision between the presidential election process and the 2011 holiday season now rests almost entirely with Billy Gardner of New Hampshire.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Holiday and Political Calendars Collide', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T13:31:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18ea100f-520e-5289-934d-83b5687ea724', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18ea100f-520e-5289-934d-83b5687ea724'}, {'abstract': 'The British Broadcasting Corporation announced on Thursday that it would eliminate 2,000 jobs, cut its sports budget, show more reruns and broadcast fewer talk shows and game shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/world/europe/new-cutbacks-announced-by-bbc.html', 'snippet': 'The British Broadcasting Corporation announced on Thursday that it would eliminate 2,000 jobs, cut its sports budget, show more reruns and broadcast fewer talk shows and game shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The British Broadcasting Corporation announced Thursday that it would eliminate 2,000 jobs, cut its sports budget, show more reruns, and broadcast fewer talk and game shows. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/world/07bbc/07bbc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/world/07bbc/07bbc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/world/07bbc/07bbc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Radically Reshaped’ BBC to Include Fewer Jobs and More Reruns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Radically Reshaped’ BBC to Include Fewer Jobs and More Reruns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservative Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T13:35:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/813431cc-ef71-50b7-bae2-33f99ca5ed10', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/813431cc-ef71-50b7-bae2-33f99ca5ed10'}, {'abstract': 'Cheers for the Wall Street protestors.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/unsavvy-people/', 'snippet': 'Cheers for the Wall Street protestors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nieman Watchdog has a very good piece by John Hanrahan about press coverage of the Occupy Wall Street demonstrations. Coverage was initially dismissive and minimal — and mea culpa, I wasn’t paying attention myself. But it’s becoming clear that there’s something important happening: finally, after three years in which Very Serious People refused to hold the financial industry accountable, there’s a real grass-roots uprising against the Masters of the Universe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unsavvy People', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T13:38:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f90ccae-44c7-51d5-80cc-81a1aadd0d6f', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f90ccae-44c7-51d5-80cc-81a1aadd0d6f'}, {'abstract': 'A brisk but dazzling 500-year shoe survey, booting the idea that foot fashion needs to be grounded.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/genie-in-a-bootie/', 'snippet': 'A brisk but dazzling 500-year shoe survey, booting the idea that foot fashion needs to be grounded.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#805", 592, 400, true, chameleonData);“100 Shoes” (The Metropolitan Museum of Art/Yale, $25) is not a collection of fashion’s most vertically daring heels, despite the Vivienne Westood platforms on the cover (and a preface by that stilt walker Sarah Jessica Parker). Instead it’s a brisk but dazzling 500-year shoe survey, booting the idea that foot fashion needs to be grounded: Moccasins were huge in Georgian England; American tango boots in the 1910s laced up like Grecian sandals; and that late-’60s prototype by Beth Levine — it kicks off the shoe slideshow above — seems to have come from a different planet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Genie in A Bootie', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T14:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edd6e2fd-803b-5c9b-9651-0e4fd4463124', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edd6e2fd-803b-5c9b-9651-0e4fd4463124'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/what-were-reading-284/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wine Review Online: Prime pinot noir from … Marin County? — Eric Asimov', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal',