'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1416755-eb3c-5207-be6f-4cceffa8bc5e', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1416755-eb3c-5207-be6f-4cceffa8bc5e'}, {'abstract': 'Missteps led to online exposure of patient data, save money by tightening your data belt, trading in your old iPhone and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/thursday-reading-missteps-exposed-patient-data-online/', 'snippet': 'Missteps led to online exposure of patient data, save money by tightening your data belt, trading in your old iPhone and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday Reading: Missteps Exposed Patient Data Online', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T14:22:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e376627-0331-54a4-a3ec-5eb71889961c', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e376627-0331-54a4-a3ec-5eb71889961c'}, {'abstract': 'Steven P. Jobs, the visionary co-founder and former chief executive of Apple, has died at 56.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/05/business/20111006_JOBS-337.html', 'snippet': 'Steven P. Jobs, the visionary co-founder and former chief executive of Apple, has died at 56.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven P. Jobs, the visionary co-founder and former chief executive of Apple, has died at 56.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/business/20111006_JOBS-slide-DNL4/20111006_JOBS-slide-DNL4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/05/business/20111006_JOBS-slide-DNL4/20111006_JOBS-slide-DNL4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/05/business/20111006_JOBS-slide-DNL4/20111006_JOBS-slide-DNL4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Steve Jobs, From Computers to Tablets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T14:23:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/dec94cdf-b157-5e0f-aad3-ef263fc83482', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/dec94cdf-b157-5e0f-aad3-ef263fc83482'}, {'abstract': 'The president of Chechnya denied a party on his birthday was a celebration of his birth. Instead, he insisted, the celebration marked a kind of rebirth for the city of Grozny, Russia.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/celebrities-attend-chechen-leaders-party/', 'snippet': 'The president of Chechnya denied a party on his birthday was a celebration of his birth. Instead, he insisted, the celebration marked a kind of rebirth for the city of Grozny, Russia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were lights and music, dancing and a huge display of fireworks. Vanessa-Mae played the violin, and even though Shakira did not attend, the actors Hilary Swank and Jean-Claude Van Damme stopped by.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrities Attend Chechen Leader’s Party', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T14:27:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a10ea729-f297-506b-bded-0144cf86b81a', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a10ea729-f297-506b-bded-0144cf86b81a'}, {'abstract': 'As his diary reveals, the man who would say anything didn’t tell us everything.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/magazine/spalding-grays-tortured-soul.html', 'snippet': 'As his diary reveals, the man who would say anything didn’t tell us everything.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spalding Gray moved to New York City in 1967, shortly after his mother’s suicide, when he was 26. He lived with his girlfriend, Elizabeth LeCompte, in an apartment on Sixth Street and Avenue D, on the Lower East Side. To make ends meet, Gray occasionally worked as a stock boy, while LeCompte sold postcards at the front desk of the Guggenheim. But mostly they were finding their places in New York’s avant-garde theater world.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/magazine/09gray/09gray-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 283, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/magazine/09gray/09gray-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/magazine/09gray/09gray-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spalding Gray’s Tortured Soul', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Dark Prince Of Downtown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, Spalding', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T14:31:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nell Casey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/c60b4366-e369-566a-8acb-eba8c93404aa', 'word_count': 4753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c60b4366-e369-566a-8acb-eba8c93404aa'}, {'abstract': 'The rule that barred athletes who had served a doping suspension of six months or longer from competing in the next Olympics was struck down as overly severe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/sports/court-overturns-olympic-ban-of-lashawn-merritt-other-doping-offenders.html', 'snippet': 'The rule that barred athletes who had served a doping suspension of six months or longer from competing in the next Olympics was struck down as overly severe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Olympic 400-meter champion LaShawn Merritt of the United States and possibly dozens of other athletes had their eligibility for the 2012 London Games restored Thursday when a doping punishment put in place by the International Olympic Committee was struck down as overly severe.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07doping-pic/07doping-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07doping-pic/07doping-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07doping-pic/07doping-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07doping-pic/07doping-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07doping-pic/07doping-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Olympic Eligibility Restored By Court', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Olympic Eligibility Restored By Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARBITRATION, CONCILIATION AND MEDIATION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Court of Arbitration for Sport', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Olympic Committee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merritt, LaShawn', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T14:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd043ab1-d91c-5337-acdf-495b89e677ef', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd043ab1-d91c-5337-acdf-495b89e677ef'}, {'abstract': 'A top official with New York City’s agency that develops affordable housing was arrested, along with six others on Thursday, and accused of scheming to obtain as much as $2 million in kickbacks from contractors and developers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/10/06/nyregion/walters-documents.html', 'snippet': 'A top official with New York City’s agency that develops affordable housing was arrested, along with six others on Thursday, and accused of scheming to obtain as much as $2 million in kickbacks from contractors and developers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A top official with New York City’s agency that develops affordable housing was arrested, along with six others on Thursday, and accused of scheming to obtain as much as $2 million in kickbacks from contractors and developers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Case of Wendell Walters et. al.', 'kicker': None, 'content