“The Human Centipede 2 (Full Sequence),” he trips over himself trying to outdo the first lurid wallow.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Human Centipede (First Sequence),” from 2010, was that rare thing: a grass-roots cult hit whose novelty — in this case a horror tableau in which three people are surgically linked mouth to anus — ignites a wildfire of notoriety. The movie was memorable (in its way), its central image underscored by a studied, clinical ambience. But it lacked subtext, the resonance of, say, George Romero’s critique of consumerism in the original “Dawn of the Dead.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/movies/human-span/human-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/06/movies/human-span/human-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/movies/human-span/human-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/movies/human-span/human-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/06/movies/human-span/human-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gore, Grime and One Creepy Guy in an Underground Garage', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Human Centipede 2 (Full Sequence)'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Six, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IFC Films', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T14:54:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8113fa8f-7d4d-57fa-9ad1-f2d2f08d4649', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8113fa8f-7d4d-57fa-9ad1-f2d2f08d4649'}, {'abstract': 'A frenzy of speculation about a teenager’s identity has gripped South Korean this week as reporters scour the Internet for clues connecting him to North Korea’s Kim Jong-il.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/web-postings-stir-interest-in-teens-relation-to-north-korean-leader/', 'snippet': 'A frenzy of speculation about a teenager’s identity has gripped South Korean this week as reporters scour the Internet for clues connecting him to North Korea’s Kim Jong-il.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sharply dressed 17-year-old might be any fashionable South Korean teenager: bleached blond hair, an earring and a necklace with a cross-shaped pendant. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Web Postings Stir Interest in Teenager’s Relation to North Korean Leader', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-nam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North