ckie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da79102e-1238-541a-9fa8-9292965adc79', 'word_count': 1296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da79102e-1238-541a-9fa8-9292965adc79'}, {'abstract': 'In Jeffrey Eugenides’s new novel, “The Marriage Plot,” a privileged English major at Brown finds herself in a Victorian mating dance during the early ’80s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/books/the-marriage-plot-by-jeffrey-eugenides-review.html', 'snippet': 'In Jeffrey Eugenides’s new novel, “The Marriage Plot,” a privileged English major at Brown finds herself in a Victorian mating dance during the early ’80s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one’s more adept at channeling teenage angst than Jeffrey Eugenides. Not even J. D. Salinger. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/BOOK/BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking for Love, by the Book', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking For Love, By the Book', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eugenides, Jeffrey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T15:34:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/32bba131-0b2c-52ef-94f5-07d3ced43b84', 'word_count': 1095, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32bba131-0b2c-52ef-94f5-07d3ced43b84'}, {'abstract': 'In spite of myself, he made my life better.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/the-influence-of-steve-jobs/', 'snippet': 'In spite of myself, he made my life better.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I bought my first computer in the spring of 1985,” Alan Jacobs writes today: “the original 128K Macintosh.” Then he lists the Mac products that he’s owned and used in the decades since: an SE30, a PowerBook 100, a Performa 6116, a Performa 7500, an original iMac (“lime green”), a later-generation iMac (“the first one with a slot CD drive”), a PowerBook G3, a PowerBook G4, an iMac G5, three MacBooks (“one each for my wife, my son, and me”), a MacBook Air, an original iPod, a third-generation iPod, a first-generation iPod Nano, the first three generations of the iPod Shuffle, the original iPhone, an iPhone 3GS, and two iPads.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Influence of Steve Jobs', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T15:35:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e93f0b4-fc39-5c51-ac22-fdf1ec48392d', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e93f0b4-fc39-5c51-ac22-fdf1ec48392d'}, {'abstract': 'Started 30 years ago partly to produce classical albums by its founder, the guitarist David Starobin, Bridge Records is a healthy survivor in a turbulent recording industry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/arts/music/bridge-records-holds-onto-its-niche-with-a-very-firm-grip.html', 'snippet': 'Started 30 years ago partly to produce classical albums by its founder, the guitarist David Starobin, Bridge Records is a healthy survivor in a turbulent recording industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Rochelle, N.Y.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09BRIDGE1_SPAN/09BRIDGE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09BRIDGE1_SPAN/09BRIDGE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09BRIDGE1_SPAN/09BRIDGE1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09BRIDGE1_SPAN/09BRIDGE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09BRIDGE1_SPAN/09BRIDGE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Holding Onto a Niche, Very Firmly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Holding Onto a Niche, Very Firmly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'su