ps://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/cordray-nomination-advances/', 'snippet': 'But the 10 Senate Republicans on the banking committee, seeking to rein in the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, all voted against Richard Cordray’s nomination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Cordray’s bid to lead the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau moved a step forward on Thursday, as a Senate committee approved his nomination along party lines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nominee to Lead Consumer Agency Clears a Hurdle', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cordray, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Banking', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T15:55:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75121be4-60de-512b-a263-33a2a9c91942', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75121be4-60de-512b-a263-33a2a9c91942'}, {'abstract': 'Some of the Republican Party’s leading donors and activists have begun to come off the sidelines and into the Romney camp.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/romney-signing-up-leading-republican-donors/', 'snippet': 'Some of the Republican Party’s leading donors and activists have begun to come off the sidelines and into the Romney camp.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the Republican presidential lineup largely settled and little prospect of new candidates entering the race, some of the Republican Party‘s leading donors and activists have begun to come off the sidelines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Signing Up Leading Republican Donors', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Callahan, Mary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, James B Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loeb, Daniel S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T15:57:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfb607c5-1bb7-5a8c-ba81-cb6b038835ef', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfb607c5-1bb7-5a8c-ba81-cb6b038835ef'}, {'abstract': 'In this undated audio clip, Mr. Transtromer discusses and reads his poem, “Schubertiana.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/a-poetry-reading-from-nobel-prize-winner-transtromer/', 'snippet': 'In this undated audio clip, Mr. Transtromer discusses and reads his poem, “Schubertiana.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Swedish poet Tomas Transtromer, who won the 2011 Nobel Prize for Literature on Thursday, is the first Swede to win the prize since 1974. Julie Bo