nate Banking Committee voted to advance Richard Cordray’s nomination to lead the new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, although Republicans have vowed to block his confirmation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate Banking Committee voted along party lines on Thursday to advance Richard Cordray’s nomination to lead the new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, although Republicans have vowed to block his confirmation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Consumer Nominee Advances, but Fight Still Looms', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cordray, Richard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cutter, Stephanie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kreuger, Alan B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shelby, Richard C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Banking', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T17:03:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c58e16af-30fc-5a33-a810-409f1e9745e5', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c58e16af-30fc-5a33-a810-409f1e9745e5'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Jobs — whose career spanned stints at Apple, NeXT and Pixar — deeply touched the lives of many executives and thought leaders, who say Apple’s visionary helped shape their professional life.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/what-i-learned-from-steve-jobs/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Jobs — whose career spanned stints at Apple, NeXT and Pixar — deeply touched the lives of many executives and thought leaders, who say Apple’s visionary helped shape their professional life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When millions of Apple devices lit up late Wednesday on the news of Steven P. Jobs’s death, the loss reverberated far beyond Silicon Valley’s famed echo chamber.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What I Learned From Steve Jobs', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benioff, Marc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Case, Stephen M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellison, Larry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meeker, Mary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuckerberg, Mark E', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T17:03:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a62a08be-becf-5a6b-9107-e8c786e8b5ef', 'word_count': 1514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a62a08be-becf-5a6b-9107-e8c786e8b5ef'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration gave the World Trade Organization a list of 200 programs, some in solar and wind power, that it said may unfairly benefit Beijing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/business/us-says-some-chinese-subsidies-violate-trade-rules.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration gave the World Trade Organization a list of 200 programs, some in solar and wind power, that it said may unfairly benefit Beijing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Under pressure from Congress to do more to confront China on economic issues, the Obama administration has notified the World Trade Organization of nearly 200 Chinese subsidy programs, saying many of them may violate free trade rules.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/business/Trade/Trade-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '200 Chinese Subsidies Violate Rules, U.S. Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '200 Chinese Subsidies Violate Rules, U.S. Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Trade Organization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T17:04:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cff09343-9c3c-5797-bd97-653bd08d311d', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cff09343-9c3c-5797-bd97-653bd08d311d'}, {'abstract': 'Although the Texas  water code exempts oil and gas drilling from some rules enacted by groundwater districts, they will apply to fracking nonetheless, some local officials decide.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/on-our-radar-fracking-vs-drought/', 'snippet': 'Although the Texas  water code exempts oil and gas drilling from some rules enacted by groundwater districts, they will apply to fracking nonetheless, some local officials decide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The long drought in Texas is prompting some local districts to impose limits on water consumption for drillers that extract natural gas through hydraulic fracturing. While so far this has not affected gas production over all, it suggests a big policy shift in a state that has exempted oil and gas companies from many pumping restrictions. [Bloomberg]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Fracking vs. Drought', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T17:08:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/858348d7-d283-5ad4-b822-fa819fdef6ff', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/858348d7-d283-5ad4-b822-fa819fdef6ff'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Heshka, a Canadian illustrator, created what he viewed as a campy cover for the 2012 product catalog issued by Cinelli, the venerable Italian bicycle and bicycle parts maker.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/for-a-bicycle-catalog-artist-its-harmony-on-the-road-mayhem-on-the-canvas/', 'snippet': 'Ryan Heshka, a Canadian illustrator, created what he viewed as a campy cover for the 2012 product catalog issued by Cinelli, the venerable Italian bicycle and bicycle parts maker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cover ar