', 'snippet': 'Two former governors call for the country’s public universities to embrace online courses as a way to make going to college easier and to increase revenue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an opinion piece Thursday on the blog Inside Higher Ed, two former governors — Jeb Bush of Florida and Jim Hunt of North Carolina — argue that America’s public universities must embrace online education.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Debate Over Online Learning', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T17:50:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca R. Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ad39f1c-3fb1-54d4-be8b-dc407c226798', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ad39f1c-3fb1-54d4-be8b-dc407c226798'}, {'abstract': 'On hearing that his female challenger did not pose nude for Cosmopolitan, as he did, Senator Scott Brown says, “Thank God.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/nudity-comments-spice-up-mass-senate-battle/', 'snippet': 'On hearing that his female challenger did not pose nude for Cosmopolitan, as he did, Senator Scott Brown says, “Thank God.”', 'lead_paragraph': '4:56 p.m. | Updated When a student at a recent United States Senate debate in Massachusetts asked Elizabeth Warren how she paid for college, pointing out that Senator Scott Brown had posed nude in Cosmopolitan magazine to help pay his law school bills, Ms. Warren said, jokingly, “I didn’t take my clothes off.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nudity Comments Spice Up Senate Battle', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'c