 all winter long.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/ravenous-preserved-unripe-figs/', 'snippet': 'With heat and a few simple ingredients, fresh figs can be enjoyed all winter long.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this new column, Monique Truong, author of “The Book of Salt” and “Bitter in the Mouth,” shares food stories and recipes from her kitchen table.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ravenous | Preserved Unripe Figs', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T18:17:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monique Truong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monique', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Truong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba346ccf-3da2-5055-8255-ac78043cafb0', 'word_count': 972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba346ccf-3da2-5055-8255-ac78043cafb0'}, {'abstract': 'The writer Stephen Karam has two productions this fall: the play “Sons of the Prophet” and the chamber opera “Dark Sisters.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/theater/stephen-karams-sons-of-the-prophet-and-dark-sisters.html', 'snippet': 'The writer Stephen Karam has two productions this fall: the play “Sons of the Prophet” and the chamber opera “Dark Sisters.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'NOT many playwrights can claim that a theater was built for them, let alone one constructed by New York City’s largest nonprofit theater organization, the Roundabout Theater Company. But in 2007 that’s what happened for Stephen Karam, whose funny, searching three-hander “Speech & Debate” became a runaway hit as the inaugural production in a 65-seat black box space called the Roundabout Underground.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09KARAM1/09KARAM1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09KARAM1/09KARAM1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09KARAM1/09KARAM1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09KARAM1/09KARAM1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09KARAM1/09KARAM1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Darkly Comic Voice Adds a Libretto to His Résumé', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Darkly Comic Voice Adds a Libretto To His Résumé', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karam, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roundabout Theater Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T18:20:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Weinert-Kendt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weinert-Kendt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8d83555-d05d-504d-b7e5-aab45e68746a', 'word_count': 1060, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8d83555-d05d-504d-b7e5-aab45e68746a'}, {'abstract': 'After passing a bill that would block regulations on cement plants, House Republicans immediately turn to a companion measure stymie rules on toxic emissions from industrial boilers and incinerators.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/house-votes-to-delay-emissions-rule/', 'snippet': 'After passing a bill that would block regulations on cement plants, House Republicans immediately turn to a companion measure stymie rules on toxic emissions from industrial boilers and incinerators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Continuing their largely symbolic attacks on the Environmental Protection Agency’s rulemaking authority, House Republicans pushed through a bill on Thursday to block the agency’s proposed effort to reduce airborne emissions of dangerous chemicals from cement manufacturing plants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Votes to Delay Emissions Rule', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T18:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6688dcb-8b41-5f0a-bde9-6cc79412da45', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6688dcb-8b41-5f0a-bde9-6cc79412da45'}, {'abstract': 'Zach Parise, the captain of the New Jersey Devils, says his knee feels good going into the N.H.L. season.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/parise-on-his-contract-status-his-knee-and-batting-practice/', 'snippet': 'Zach Parise, the captain of the New Jersey Devils, says his knee feels good going into the N.H.L. season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Zach Parise was named captain of the Devils on Wednesday; that was the easy part. In this interview, Parise discusses his comeback this season after surgery for a torn meniscus in his knee and his approach to handling questions about being in the final year of his contract.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parise on His Contract Status, His Knee and Batting Practice', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T18:36:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Botta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16cacfa4-6af8-5166-a924-4035668b8e24', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16cacfa4-6af8-5166-a924-4035668b8e24'}, {'abstract': 'A Queens woman who killed her husband in a hail of 11 bullets but claimed she had been long victimized by him was found not guilty of murder.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/sheehan-found-not-guilty/', 'snippet': 'A Queens woman who killed her husband in a hail of 11 bullets but claimed she had been long victimized by him was found not guilty of murder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 2:46 p.m. | Barbara Sheehan, a Queens woman who killed her husband, a former police sergeant, in a hail of 11 bullets while he was shaving was found not guilty on Thursday of second-degree murder. (See updated story here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sheehan Found Not Guilty', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': '