isney bought Pixar in 2006 for $7.4 billion, Mr. Jobs received a 7.4 percent stake in Disney and a seat on the board. Here are excerpts from the interview:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iger on Steve Jobs: ‘He Pushed You’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iger, Robert A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T19:11:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8373d54-1645-5b61-9a1e-68c4da430078', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8373d54-1645-5b61-9a1e-68c4da430078'}, {'abstract': 'Readers react to the death of Steven P. Jobs, the visionary co-founder of Apple.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/opinion/how-steve-jobs-transformed-our-culture.html', 'snippet': 'Readers react to the death of Steven P. Jobs, the visionary co-founder of Apple.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steve Jobs Transformed Our Culture', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Steve Jobs Transformed Our Culture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T19:13:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee5e51c9-e725-56cb-b31f-703664486e85', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee5e51c9-e725-56cb-b31f-703664486e85'}, {'abstract': 'The Revlon model on how she maintains her stunning good looks.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/face-time-anne-v/', 'snippet': 'The Revlon model on how she maintains her stunning good looks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Her full name is Anne Vyalitsyna, but she goes simply by Anne V. Based in Los Angeles, she’s the face of Revlon’s latest: the Expressionist Collection, which will be in stores Oct. 15. As we got started on a photo shoot with the photographer Cameron Krone at Manhattan’s Lambs Club, I managed to pick up some tips on how she maintains her stunning good looks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Face Time | Anne V.', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T19:15:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Turnbow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turnbow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d28e3d1a-e5a9-5e73-9b68-f86d8aa56225', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d28e3d1a-e5a9-5e73-9b68-f86d8aa56225'}, {'abstract': 'A squirrel causes Phillies pitcher Roy Oswalt problems in St. Louis, and scheduling makes watching the Arizona-Milwaukee series a challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/in-the-playoffs-spirited-squirrels-and-bad-time-slots/', 'snippet': 'A squirrel causes Phillies pitcher Roy Oswalt problems in St. Louis, and scheduling makes watching the Arizona-Milwaukee series a challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All through the baseball playoffs, Mike Tanier will provide the Bats blog with daily updates on less-than-important developments from around the league. He vows to keep Phillies homerism to a minimum.La Russa’s Acorn-Hoarding Minions. Busch Stadium has been overrun by squirrels in the last two days. On Tuesday night, a critter scurried across the field and ran around in foul territory. His reasoning: “I’m cute. I have a fluffy tail. I am totally going to get picked up by a ball girl!” On Wednesday, either the same squirrel or an accomplice dashed right in front of the plate as Roy Oswalt delivered a pitch. Umpire Angel Hernandez called it a ball, and Oswalt complained that he was distracted by the squirrel. Hernandez was probably the distracted one, as the pitch clearly caught the inside corner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Playoffs, Spirited Squirrels and Bad Time Slots', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Squirrels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Angel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keeler, Willie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manuel, Charlie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oswalt, Roy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA DIAMONDBACKS', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Brewers', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam