. 14 to 17, the 450th anniversary of St. Basil’s Cathedral in Red Square will be observed with an international choir festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 450th anniversary of St. Basil’s Cathedral in Red Square will be honored Oct. 14 to 17 with an international choir festival featuring a Russian choir from Boston and the premiere of a work for orchestra, organ and choir set to Anna Akhmatova’s poem “Requiem,” about Stalin-era suffering. “The cathedral’s silhouette is famous around the world,” said Lev Pankratov, the festival’s musical director and the composer of “Requiem.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Singing Out for St. Basil’s', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AKHMATOVA, ANNA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T20:18:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sophia Kishkovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sophia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kishkovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94c7fce2-0b6d-5c36-875f-edcc377b25a4', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94c7fce2-0b6d-5c36-875f-edcc377b25a4'}, {'abstract': 'Two deer surprisingly found on Wednesday near the base of the Verrazano-Narrows Bridge were brought back to a city animal shelter. One had died, the other was set loose on Staten Island.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/a-wayward-deer-rescued-in-brooklyn-later-died/', 'snippet': 'Two deer surprisingly found on Wednesday near the base of the Verrazano-Narrows Bridge were brought back to a city animal shelter. One had died, the other was set loose on Staten Island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the deer picked up by a police boat Wednesday in the harbor just off the Bay Ridge waterfront in Brooklyn later died.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wayward Deer Rescued in Brooklyn Later Died', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T20:23:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a53e2b5-81e1-57c8-87e0-f850f5e0e2ff', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a53e2b5-81e1-57c8-87e0-f850f5e0e2ff'}, {'abstract': 'Virtuoso Resources, a violin atelier in Manhattan, has a varied collection of instruments and a few pieces of classical music history tucked away in an Upper West Side brownstone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/09/nyregion/20111009JOINTss.html', 'snippet': 'Virtuoso Resources, a violin atelier in Manhattan, has a varied collection of instruments and a few pieces of classical music history tucked away in an Upper West Side brownstone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Virtuoso Resources, a violin atelier in Manhattan, has a varied collection of instruments and a few pieces of classical music history tucked away in an Upper West Side brownstone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/nyregion/20111009JOINTss-slide-Q5AT/20111009JOINTss-slide-Q5AT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 918, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/nyregion/20111009JOINTss-slide-Q5AT/20111009JOINTss-slide-Q5AT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/nyregion/20111009JOINTss-slide-Q5AT/20111009JOINTss-slide-Q5AT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tucked Under a Brownstone, Violins For Everyone', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Violins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Musical Instruments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T20:27:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/af2476d0-e5f7-5f42-8a9f-594f73d0f285', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/af2476d0-e5f7-5f42-8a9f-594f73d0f285'}, {'abstract': 'Harold Hagopian’s shop on the Upper West Side rents instruments, to players as young as 2, and has an alluring collection of musical mementos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/nyregion/neighborhood-joint-virtuoso-resources.html', 'snippet': 'Harold Hagopian’s shop on the Upper West Side rents instruments, to players as young as 2, and has an alluring collection of musical mementos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HAVING learned to play the violin as a boy, my husband has long harbored fantasies that our 3-year-old daughter, Meenakshi, will someday follow his footsteps into a school orchestra. While researching how she could get started, I stumbled upon Virtuoso Resources. New York has no shortage of places that stock instruments for children, but for young people eyeing the violin, viola or cello, this Upper West Side atelier offers an unusual grace note: a touch of musical history.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/nyregion/09JOINT-1/09JOINT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/09/nyregion/09JOINT-1/09JOINT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/nyregion/09JOINT-1/09JOINT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 910, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/nyregion/09JOINT-1/09JOINT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/nyregion/09JOINT-1/09JOINT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Salon for Musicians Big and Small', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Salon For Musicians Big and Small', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Musical Instruments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T20:27:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de40a4f6-b770-5b22-9eaf-dd348954b4c6', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de40a4f6-b770-5b22-9eaf-dd348954b4c6'}, {'abstract': 'The Commodity Futures Trading Commission filed a record number of enforcement cases over the last year as it moved to clean up the mess from the financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/wall-street-watchdog-finds-its-teeth/', 'snippet': 'The Commodity Futures Trading Commission filed a record number of enforcement cases over the last year as it moved to clean up the mess from the financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Commodity Futures Trading Commission, once a sleepy Wall Street watchdog, is exercising its regulatory muscle, filing a record number of enforcement cases over the last year as it moved to clean up the mess from the financial crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall Street Watchdog Finds Its Teeth', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commodity Futures Trading Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T20:28:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90886cb1-06e2-5381-a8ac-17c401206c03', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90886cb1-06e2-5381-a8ac-17c401206c03'}, {'abstract': 'The Eeyore slippers, looking innocent enough, held the secret of happiness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/fashion/fuzzy-purple-and-full-of-thorns-modern-love.html', 'snippet': 'The Eeyore slippers, looking innocent enough, held the secret of happiness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT was a snowy February day in New York City when my boyfriend of three months decided to go into his bedroom to look for his camera. I followed along to keep him company, which I was doing a fine job of until my eyes landed on something entirely out of place for a mid-30s man to have in his closet.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/09LOVE/09LOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 700, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/09LOVE/09LOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/09LOVE/09LOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fuzzy, Purple and Full of Thorns', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fuzzy, Purple and Full of Thorns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T20:29:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsee Pengal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pengal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84deb2e4-1d74-5220-a704-30d0be0aaada', 'word_count': 1487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84deb2e4-1d74-5220-a704-30d0be0aaada'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney tells a group of veterans that given the global threats to America’s interests, the nation’s defense spending should be increased instead of cut.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/romney-calls-for-more-defense-spending/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney tells a group of veterans that given the global threats to America’s interests, the nation’s defense spending should be increased instead of cut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MT. PLEASANT, S.C. — Standing among retired airplanes on the U.S.S. Yorktown, a decommissioned World War II aircraft carrier, Mitt Romney told a small group of veterans on Thursday that given the global threats to America’s interests, the nation’s defense spending should be increased instead of cut. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Calls for More Defense Spending', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T20:37:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/601c8f1c-ae3c-54c0-ab11-d23361144887', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/601c8f1c-ae3c-54c0-ab11-d23361144887'}, {'abstract': 'The chairman of the Federal Communications Commission wants to change an $8 billion fund that subsidizes telephone service in rural areas into one that will expand broadband Internet service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/business/fcc-plans-an-overhaul-of-the-universal-service-fund.html', 'snippet': 'The chairman of the Federal Communications Commission wants to change an $8 billion fund that subsidizes telephone service in rural areas into one that will expand broadband Internet service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The chairman of the Federal Communications Commission on Thursday outlined a plan to transform the Universal Service Fund, an $8 billion fund that is paid for by the nation’s telephone customers and used to subsidize basic telephone service in rural areas, into one that will help expand broadband Internet service to 18 million Americans who lack high-speed access.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/business/FCC/FCC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/business/FCC/FCC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/business/FCC/FCC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'F.C.C. Plans to Overhaul Telecom Fund to Focus on Expanding Broadband', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.C.C. Plans to Overhaul Telecom Fund to Focus on Expanding Broadband', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Genachowski, Julius', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rural Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T20:41:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f50bd5a-0f59-5d69-87b8-b6d0be73b167', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f50bd5a-0f59-5d69-87b8-b6d0be73b167'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from California,', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/06/blogs/20111006POD.html', 'snippet': 'Photographs from California,', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from California,', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/06/blogs/20111006POD-slide-IVP0/20111006POD-slide-IVP0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: California and Elsewhere', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T20:41:51+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/b22a95f9-9f4a-5027-a048-66d6b02c1f4b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b22a95f9-9f4a-5027-a048-66d6b02c1f4b'}, {'abstract': 'Fred Melamed has left Ethan Coen’s one-act play.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/a-family-breakup-in-relatively-speaking/', 'snippet': 'Fred Melamed has left Ethan Coen’s one-act play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last collaboration between the actor Fred Melamed and the filmmaker Ethan Coen yielded one of the silkiest screen villains in recent years: Sy Ableman, the gently bearish widower in “A Serious Man” (2009), who seduces the wife of the main character and then keeps explaining the logic of the cuckolding to him. (Sy: “Such a thing, such a thing – you know, Larry, the way we handle ourselves in this situation is so important.”) But their latest outing together, in the Broadway production “Relatively Speaking,” has not gone as smoothly: He left the show after the matinee on Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Family Breakup in ‘Relatively Speaking’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T20:43:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f852e6a7-9760-5fa9-ab74-e80e725d492b', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f852e6a7-9760-5fa9-ab74-e80e725d492b'}, {'abstract': 'Advice about how to tell your roommate you’re moving out, neighbors who ask you to baby-sit, and when to give a standing ovation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/fashion/stand-up-and-be-counted.html', 'snippet': 'Advice about how to tell your roommate you’re moving out, neighbors who ask you to baby-sit, and when to give a standing ovation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My girlfriend and I attended opening night at the Metropolitan Opera, featuring the world-class soprano Anna Netrebko. She was magnificent, and at the end of the evening, we gave her a standing ovation. The woman behind us called out loudly: “Sit down. I can’t see.” This led to a testy exchange with her companion: “The singers can’t see you standing.” Besides being irritated by them and with myself (for being pulled into this quarrel), I was bewildered that anyone could think of a standing ovation as rude. Your thoughts?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stand Up and Be Counted', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stand Up and Be Counted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', '