-death-will-lead-to-changes-but-not-softening-in-show/', 'snippet': 'The Public Theater’s new production of “The Agony and the Ecstasy of Steve Jobs,” a one-man show that is sharply critical of Jobs and Apple at points, will undergo changes in the aftermath of his death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Public Theater’s new production of “The Agony and the Ecstasy of Steve Jobs,” a one-man show that is sharply critical of Mr. Jobs and Apple at points, will undergo changes in the aftermath of Mr. Jobs’s death on Wednesday but begin performances as scheduled on Tuesday, Oct. 11, according to its creator, Mike Daisey.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monologist Says Jobs’s Death Will Lead to Changes, but Not Softening, in Show', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daisey, Mike', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T21:06:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e329d3c-2a1f-5404-b177-6f6148015890', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e329d3c-2a1f-5404-b177-6f6148015890'}, {'abstract': 'In the roughly three weeks after their appointments, 10 members of the bipartisan deficit panel received a total of about $83,000 for their campaign and leadership committees.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/donors-gave-83000-to-deficit-panel-members-in-august/', 'snippet': 'In the roughly three weeks after their appointments, 10 members of the bipartisan deficit panel received a total of about $83,000 for their campaign and leadership committees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Xavier Becerra of California, the senior Democrat on the House Ways and Means Subcommittee on Social Security, caused a stir in August when a supporter organizing a fund-raiser sent an invitation to donors highlighting Mr. Becerra’s appointment to the special deficit reduction committee looking for more than $1 trillion in federal spending cuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Donors Gave $83,000 to Deficit Panel Members in August', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T21:07:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0430cec0-6ae6-5a92-a514-70e3fb73d998', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0430cec0-6ae6-5a92-a514-70e3fb73d998'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to walks, talks, parades, exhibitions and other events in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/arts/spare-times-for-oct-7-13.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to walks, talks, parades, exhibitions and other events in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Around Town', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for Oct. 7-13', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Columbus Day', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T21:07:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Mancuso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/a20184f4-d349-54e5-ae5e-0e9563114080', 'word_count': 1858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a20184f4-d349-54e5-ae5e-0e9563114080'}, {'abstract': 'A traveling exhibition at the Ellis Island Museum of Immigration brings the history of “the Rock” in San Francisco to the East Coast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/arts/alcatraz-exhibition-at-ellis-island-museum.html', 'snippet': 'A traveling exhibition at the Ellis Island Museum of Immigration brings the history of “the Rock” in San Francisco to the East Coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Weideman has spent about 30 years on Alcatraz, though he hasn’t done anything illegal. He is a National Park Ranger who was assigned to supervise operations there in the early 1980s and has been devoted to the island and its many incarnations ever since. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/07MISER_SPAN/Weekend-B-Miser-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/07MISER_SPAN/Weekend-B-Miser-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/07MISER_SPAN/Weekend-B-Miser-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 7