}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a21a6005-bfd1-59cb-b39d-521906f304be', 'word_count': 2691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a21a6005-bfd1-59cb-b39d-521906f304be'}, {'abstract': 'I have innocent reasons for poking around Craigslist. A friend of mine is looking for a studio apartment. I would like to find a not-too-expensive bicycle.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/06/my-three-favorite-things-on-craigslist-today/', 'snippet': 'I have innocent reasons for poking around Craigslist. A friend of mine is looking for a studio apartment. I would like to find a not-too-expensive bicycle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have innocent reasons for poking around Craigslist. A friend of mine is looking for a studio apartment. I would like to find a not-too-expensive bicycle. But, once on the site, it is hard not to get pulled into all the strangeness that people in New York are selling, buying and generally proclaiming to the world. My three favorite items today:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Three Favorite Things on Craigslist Today', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T22:08:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cb164c9-9cef-5854-bc5e-5a816ced1567', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cb164c9-9cef-5854-bc5e-5a816ced1567'}, {'abstract': 'To encourage more black and Hispanic teachers for city schools, Wells Community Academy High School has a program that begins training aspiring teachers as soon as ninth grade.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/us/chicago-program-aims-to-create-more-black-and-hispanic-teachers.html', 'snippet': 'To encourage more black and Hispanic teachers for city schools, Wells Community Academy High School has a program that begins training aspiring teachers as soon as ninth grade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The gap between the number of minority teachers in Chicago’s public schools and minority student enrollment has widened over the last decade, but one school is working to change that by preparing the next generation of teachers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/us/07CNCTEACHERS/07CNCTEACHERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/us/07CNCTEACHERS/07CNCTEACHERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/us/07CNCTEACHERS/07CNCTEACHERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Starting Early to Create City Teachers', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Starting Early to Create City Teachers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T22:09:55+0000', 'document_type': 'artic