wl low. It was football for the new age, devoid of balance, an aerial high-wire act from the shoulder-pad set. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/Y-jp-offense/Y-jp-offense-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/Y-jp-offense/Y-jp-offense-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/Y-jp-offense/Y-jp-offense-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/Y-jp-offense/Y-jp-offense-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/Y-jp-offense/Y-jp-offense-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L.’s Shift to Pass Goes Into Higher Gear', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.F.L.’s Shift to Passing Goes Into Higher Gear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marino, Dan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brees, Drew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newton, Cameron J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodgers, Aaron', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T22:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d0db063-4732-5aab-af71-6bc360eabdc7', 'word_count': 1386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d0db063-4732-5aab-af71-6bc360eabdc7'}, {'abstract': 'Visitors to the New Museum will be able to zip down two floors on a Carsten Höller plastic slide (helmet and elbow pads included).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/arts/design/carsten-holler-is-installing-a-slide-at-new-museum.html', 'snippet': 'Visitors to the New Museum will be able to zip down two floors on a Carsten Höller plastic slide (helmet and elbow pads included).', 'lead_paragraph': 'If all goes as planned, the New Museum’s five-year-old building on the Bowery will become something of an amusement park beginning Oct. 26, with visitors hurtling through a giant plastic tube from the fourth floor to the second.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/07VOGEL_SPAN/VOGEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 776, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/07VOGEL_SPAN/07VOGEL_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/07VOGEL_SPAN/07VOGEL_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting Museumgoers on the Fast Track', 'kicker': 'Inside Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline':