meron Todd Willingham, executed by Texas — unjustly, some contend — for the murder of his children by arson.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/movies/incendiary-a-documentary-about-willingham-case-review.html', 'snippet': '“Incendiary” is a documentary about the case of Cameron Todd Willingham, executed by Texas — unjustly, some contend — for the murder of his children by arson.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Incendiary: The Willingham Case” covers a man’s execution in Texas for the murder of his children by arson. But this involving documentary, while sympathetic to opponents of the death penalty, isn’t focused on sorting out the ethical rights and wrongs of the practice. It centers instead on whether we understand or respect evolving standards of scientific evidence.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/movies/07INCENDIARY_SPAN/07INCENDIARY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/07/movies/07INCENDIARY_SPAN/07INCENDIARY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/movies/07INCENDIARY_SPAN/07INCENDIARY_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/movies/07INCENDIARY_SPAN/07INCENDIARY_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/movies/07INCENDIARY_SPAN/07INCENDIARY_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting Justice Under a Microscope', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Incendiary: The Willingham Case'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T22:57:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By David DeWitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeWitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3136d7a6-01d6-543a-9a64-406e9e3e76a3', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3136d7a6-01d6-543a-9a64-406e9e3e76a3'}, {'abstract': 'Views From the Avant-Garde, part of the New York Film Festival, has expanded its presentation of single and multiartist programs, short and long works, films and digital videos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/movies/views-from-the-avant-garde-film-series-at-lincoln-center.html', 'snippet': 'Views From the Avant-Garde, part of the New York Film Festival, has expanded its presentation of single and multiartist programs, short and long works, films and digital videos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Argh! Another year and another several dozen opportunities blown: the American avant-garde filmmaker Ken Jacobs was not anointed a “genius” by the MacArthur Foundation and given a big fat check. Again. (The most recent fellows were announced on Sept. 20.) Only 13 filmmakers have been deemed worthy of that title (Susan Sontag included) compared with at least 84 historians (in different fields), 40 or so poets and two dozen mathematicians. Clearly, at least in one respect, Mr. Jacobs picked the wrong field in which to excel. But a genius of cinema he is, though his primary tools are often light and shadow rather than film. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/07AVANT3_SPAN/Weekend-A-Cover-Reefer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 280, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/07AVANT3_SPAN/Weekend-A-Cover-Reefer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 280}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/07AVANT3_SPAN/Weekend-A-Cover-Reefer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 414, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/07AVANT3_SPAN/Weekend-A-Cover-Reefer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/07AVANT3_SPAN/Weekend-A-Cover-Reefer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Stream of Work That Defies Visual Uniformity', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Stream of Work That Defies Visual Uniformity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Film Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-06T22:58:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'm