on': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d35b570-3b02-5082-ad76-eb9c70f883d8', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d35b570-3b02-5082-ad76-eb9c70f883d8'}, {'abstract': 'The Vagos Outlaw Motorcycle Gang was dealt a major blow on Thursday, with a series of raids throughout Southern California that led to the arrests of 12 members and the seizure of more than 300 guns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/us/in-california-raid-on-gang-members-leads-to-12-arrests.html', 'snippet': 'The Vagos Outlaw Motorcycle Gang was dealt a major blow on Thursday, with a series of raids throughout Southern California that led to the arrests of 12 members and the seizure of more than 300 guns.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Vagos Outlaw Motorcycle Gang was dealt a major blow on Thursday, with a series of raids throughout Southern California that led to the arrests of 12 members and the seizure of more than 300 guns. Members are suspected of narcotics trafficking, rape and murder, including the recent killing of a rival gang member at a Nevada casino, according to the California Department of Justice, which led the crackdown. A task force had been investigating the group since last year, leading to 25 arrests and the seizure of 46 pounds of cocaine, more than $37,000 and weapons including a grenade launcher and a rocket launcher. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In California, Raid on Gang Members Leads to 12 Arrests', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WEST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Raid on Gang Members', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gangs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T02:24:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0147babb-9bf1-556a-b8fc-169d80c13501', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0147babb-9bf1-556a-b8fc-169d80c13501'}, {'abstract': 'Europe has been right to demand that Athens carry out painful reforms, but it is wrong to ask for too much austerity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/opinion/the-trouble-with-greece.html', 'snippet': 'Europe has been right to demand that Athens carry out painful reforms, but it is wrong to ask for too much austerity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Europe has been right to demand that, in exchange for bailout financing, Greece carry out painful structural reforms to make its economy more competitive and able to generate more revenue to pay down the country’s huge debts. Without that pressure, Athens would likely never be able to overcome fierce resistance from public-sector unions, professionals, the wealthy and all of the special interests determined to keep doing business as usual. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Trouble With Greece', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Trouble With Greece: Athens needs to make tough reforms, but Europe is asking for too much austerity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T02:24:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1be6fc52-c4ff-57ea-adf8-3bbb17e5890d', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1be6fc52-c4ff-57ea-adf8-3bbb17e5890d'}, {'abstract': 'Apple pioneered the big budget Super Bowl ad on TV, just one of the marketing advances led by Steven P. Jobs, executives at Advertising Week 2011 said Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/business/media/recalling-apples-influence-and-innovations-advertising.html', 'snippet': 'Apple pioneered the big budget Super Bowl ad on TV, just one of the marketing advances led by Steven P. Jobs, executives at Advertising Week 2011 said Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STEVEN P. JOBS would be an influential figure in advertising even if Apple’s sole contribution had been the “1984” commercial that introduced the Macintosh, which pioneered the idea of big-concept, big-budget spots created especially for the Super Bowl.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple Innovations Include Start of Big-Budget Super Bowl Ads', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apple Innovations Include Start Of Big-Budget Super Bowl Ads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '