berg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23a7141e-ed31-5b6e-9b15-4c3abfd097e0', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23a7141e-ed31-5b6e-9b15-4c3abfd097e0'}, {'abstract': 'The new chancellor of the Texas A&M University System is a former state comptroller. Just the latest example of what a university chancellor’s job is really about: raising money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/us/not-the-academic-type-no-problem-youre-hired.html', 'snippet': 'The new chancellor of the Texas A&M University System is a former state comptroller. Just the latest example of what a university chancellor’s job is really about: raising money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ross Ramsey, the managing editor at The Texas Tribune, writes a column for The Tribune.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not the Academic Type? No Problem. You’re Hired.', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not the Academic Type? No Problem. You’re Hired.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas A&M University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T02:59:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/917de633-d638-5796-