name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T03:11:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Hoinski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoinski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4fd95b5-a921-5e77-87c6-789912af79f8', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4fd95b5-a921-5e77-87c6-789912af79f8'}, {'abstract': 'Milwaukee’s Ryan Braun, who is half-Jewish, will not follow the example of players like Hank Greenberg and Sandy Koufax, who missed important games in observance of Yom Kippur.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/sports/baseball/2011-nl-playoffs-for-braun-stadiums-are-his-temple.html', 'snippet': 'Milwaukee’s Ryan Braun, who is half-Jewish, will not follow the example of players like Hank Greenberg and Sandy Koufax, who missed important games in observance of Yom Kippur.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If a player with Jewish heritage reaches baseball’s postseason, the inevitable question is: will he play on Yom Kippur or go to synagogue? It is not a query on the level of the Four Questions that are asked during the Passover seder. But it is one of those curious baseball inquiries — maybe on par with, Does a rising fastball really rise? — that pop up sometimes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/braun/braun-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 658, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Braun, Stadiums Remain His Temple', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Braun, Stadiums Remain His Temple', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Braun, Ryan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yom Kippur', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Brewers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenberg, Hank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koufax, Sandy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T03:19:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08658f15-4780-51c4-a604-2fdd6e67629e', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08658f15-4780-51c4-a604-2fdd6e67629e'}, {'abstract': 'The National Academy of Sciences said the cost of any new benefits that must be provided by insurance plans under the health care overhaul should be “offset by savings” elsewhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/us/politics/panel-says-us-should-weigh-cost-in-health-coverage.html', 'snippet': 'The National Academy of Sciences said the cost of any new benefits that must be provided by insurance plans under the health care overhaul should be “offset by savings” elsewhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The National Academy of Sciences said Thursday that the federal government should explicitly consider cost as a factor in deciding what health benefits must be provided by insurance plans under President Obama’s health care overhaul, and it said the cost of any new benefits should be “offset by savings” elsewhere in the health care system.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Panel Says U.S. Should Weigh Cost in Deciding ‘Essential Health Benefits’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panel Says U.S. Should Weigh Cost in Deciding ‘Essential Health Benefits’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute of Medicine', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T03:28:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a708b0c1-31cc-5ead-aee0-2ccb916f982b', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a708b0c1-31cc-5ead-aee0-2ccb916f982b'}, {'abstract': 'Big East presidents will be holding a conference call on Friday morning to discuss expansion possibilities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/sports/ncaafootball/big-east-presidents-to-discuss-possible-new-members.html', 'snippet': 'Big East presidents will be holding a conference call on Friday morning to discuss expansion possibilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The inevitable defection of Texas Christian to the Big 12 conference has left the Big East with just six members in football and a sense of uncertainly about its future in that sport. The league’s presidents will be holding a conference call on Friday morning to discuss expansion possibilities. While nothing is guaranteed, three people with knowledge of the call have indicated that invitations to new members will be discussed and could be decided on the call.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big East Presidents to Discuss Possible New Members', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big East Presidents to Discuss Possible New Members', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big East Conference', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big 12 Conference', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Christian University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T03:29:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85ec91c9-2e45-5063-92c3-2d4880be5fa3', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85ec91c9-2e45-5063-92c3-2d4880be5fa3'}, {'abstract': 'After initially denying allegations of sexual abuse at three Quebec schools it operated, a Roman Catholic order said that it had settled a class-action lawsuit by the victims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/world/americas/canada-catholic-order-settles-sexual-abuse-suit-for-17-million.html', 'snippet': 'After initially denying allegations of sexual abuse at three Quebec schools it operated, a Roman Catholic order said that it had settled a class-action lawsuit by the victims.', 'lead_paragraph': ' After initially denying allegations of sexual abuse at three Quebec schools it operated, a Roman Catholic order said Thursday that it had settled a class-action lawsuit by the victims with a $17 million payment. In addition to the payment, the Congregation of Holy Cross issued a formal apology. The settlement covers incidents from 1950 to 2001, mostly at an elite Montreal boarding school formerly run by the order, which also controls the University of Notre Dame in Indiana. A separate criminal investigation by the police is continuing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Catholic Order Settles Sexual Abuse Suit for $17 Million', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | THE AMERICAS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Catholic Order Settles Sexual Abuse Suit for $17 Million', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T03:31:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b8c8d65-5516-5fdf-a9ee-8fa8ee6e6743', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b8c8d65-5516-5fdf-a9ee-8fa8ee6e6743'}, {'abstract': 'Ranked-choice voting, being used for the first time in a competitive San Francisco mayoral race, has not proved to be a flawless system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/us/a-critical-spotlight-shines-on-ranked-choice-voting.html', 'snippet': 'Ranked-choice voting, being used for the first time in a competitive San Francisco mayoral race, has not proved to be a flawless system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven Hill is not on San Francisco’s November ballot, but few actual candidates have been as influential, or controversial, in this year’s election.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/us/07BCJAMES/07BCJAMES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/us/07BCJAMES/07BCJAMES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/us/07BCJAMES/07BCJAMES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Critical Spotlight Shines on Ranked-Choice Voting', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Critical Spotlight Shines on Ranked-Choice Voting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Steven', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quan, Jean', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T03:39:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott James', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'James', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35c7aa30-5ca0-5bec-989a-0f52aa337957', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35c7aa30-5ca0-5bec-989a-0f52aa337957'}, {'abstract': 'Revival of the seedy and crime-ridden Mid Market section of San Francisco may finally be taking off, thanks to a growing list of arts organizations that have moved in or plan to.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/us/mid-market-at-last-may-be-on-the-cusp-of-revival.html', 'snippet': 'Revival of the seedy and crime-ridden Mid Market section of San Francisco may finally be taking off, thanks to a growing list of arts organizations that have moved in or plan to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While Hal Fischer, interim director of S.F. Camerawork, pondered his organization’s move to the Mid Market district, he conducted an experiment. About three months ago, he went to an 11 p.m. event at the nearby Luggage Store gallery and intentionally parked his car on Sixth and Market, a notoriously troubled block in the midst of one of the city’s most crime-ridden areas.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/us/07BCMIDMARKET/07BCMIDMARKET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/us/07BCMIDMARKET/07BCMIDMARKET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/us/07BCMIDMARKET/07BCMIDMARKET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mid Market, at Last, May Be on the Cusp of Revival', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mid Market, at Last, May Be on the Cusp of Revival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T03:47:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reyhan Harmanci', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reyhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harmanci', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d003fd07-bcc3-5b33-abb3-8fd496fafa6b', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d003fd07-bcc3-5b33-abb3-8fd496fafa6b'}, {'abstract': 'Employees of an airport shuttle company say management solicited and reimbursed their contributions to the election campaign of the interim mayor, Edwin M. Lee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/us/contributions-to-mayor-raise-issue-of-legality.html', 'snippet': 'Employees of an airport shuttle company say management solicited and reimbursed their contributions to the election campaign of the interim mayor, Edwin M. Lee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A manager at GO Lorrie’s, one of the largest passenger shuttle companies at San Francisco International Airport, solicited and reimbursed as much as $8,000 in contributions from employees to the election campaign of interim Mayor Edwin M. Lee, employees told The Bay Citizen this week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Contributions to Mayor Raise Issue of Legality', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Contributions To Mayor Raise Issue Of Legality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Edwin M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption in Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T03:56:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Shih', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shih', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dacd3c0-7b6b-55ad-b27e-5f9d66d2b574', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dacd3c0-7b6b-55ad-b27e-5f9d66d2b574'}, {'abstract': 'The Tigers jumped out to a quick 2-0 lead after consecutive home runs off starter Ivan Nova and the Yankees stranded 11 runners on base in the 3-2 loss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/sports/baseball/yankees-october-ends-early.html', 'snippet': 'The Tigers jumped out to a quick 2-0 lead after consecutive home runs off starter Ivan Nova and the Yankees stranded 11 runners on base in the 3-2 loss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Yankees went into spring training in February, they took with them their annual goal of winning the World Series, even if many outside the team did not share that expectation. The Yankees had missed out on signing the free-agent pitcher Cliff Lee, and they carried serious concerns about their pitching rotation and the age of some of their core players.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07yankees_span/07yankees_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07yankees_span/07yankees_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07yankees_span/07yankees_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07yankees_span/07yankees_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/sports/07yankees_span/07yankees_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Exit October, as Tigers Prevail in Decisive Game 5', 'kicker': 'Tigers 3, Yankees 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exiting October', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fister, Doug', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nova, Ivan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cano, Robinson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {