est of his wife, Liu Xia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Three prominent human rights groups called on China on Friday to release the imprisoned dissident writer Liu Xiaobo, who won the Nobel Peace Prize a year ago, and to end the house arrest of his wife, Liu Xia.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3 Human Rights Groups Call for Release of Imprisoned Chinese Nobel Laureate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '3 Human Rights Groups Call for Release of Imprisoned Chinese Nobel Laureate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu Xia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu Xiaobo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T11:56:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10664369-5158-5de1-9a88-9c2f4a3f4852', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10664369-5158-5de1-9a88-9c2f4a3f4852'}, {'abstract': 'Charles Isherwood explains why he think it’s high time he stopped reviewing Adam Rapp’s plays.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/theater-talkback-for-one-critic-its-a-rapp/', 'snippet': 'Charles Isherwood explains why he think it’s high time he stopped reviewing Adam Rapp’s plays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Rapp won’t have me to kick around anymore. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: For One Critic, It’s a Rapp', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rapp, Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T12:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18d26183-cddb-51f4-9581-44f68a9f2061', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18d26183-cddb-51f4-9581-44f68a9f2061'}, {'abstract': 'A 340-ton boulder will take a very slow road to be part of an outdoor installation at the Los Angeles County Museum of Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/arts/design/los-angeles-county-museum-moves-a-340-ton-rock.html', 'snippet': 'A 340-ton boulder will take a very slow road to be part of an outdoor installation at the Los Angeles County Museum of Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIVERSIDE, Calif. — It is just under 60 miles from the Stone Valley Quarry here — an expanse of dust, boulders, roaring bulldozers and cut granite hillsides — to the lush campus of the Los Angeles County Museum of Art on Museum Mile. Behind a pile of rocks the other afternoon, out of sight from the road, workers scurried around a 340-ton, 21-foot-high solid granite boulder, trussed with red steel girders, gleaming under the desert sun. If all goes well, this boulder will be hovering over a cut in the earth on the grounds of the museum, and be open for viewing, by the end of November. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/arts/08roc