ogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/big-deal-gilded-then-gilded-now/', 'snippet': 'A castlelike five-story structure and a house with an ultramodern interior are two of the three remaining town houses on a historic block between 84th and 85th Streets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a historic moment on the block of Central Park West between 84th and 85th Streets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Deal | Gilded Then, Gilded Now', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T14:07:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Kershaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1841ec5-1bd1-5664-83f8-fdfe0d15aeb8', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1841ec5-1bd1-5664-83f8-fdfe0d15aeb8'}, {'abstract': 'Tigers rewrite the script in toppling the Yankees in the Bronx, while the National League’s two Game 5s rate differently on the panic meter and the White Sox raise more eyebrows by hiring Manager Robin Ventura.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/leading-off-that-wasnt-supposed-to-happen/', 'snippet': 'Tigers rewrite the script in toppling the Yankees in the Bronx, while the National League’s two Game 5s rate differently on the panic meter and the White Sox raise more eyebrows by hiring Manager Robin Ventura.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a while, the Tigers-as-Yankee-slayers became a plausible idea. The Tigers have the best pitcher in baseball, a shrewd manager, cool old-school uniforms. But when they botched a chance to win the American League division series at home in Game 4, a trip to the Bronx for Game 5 Thursday night was a no-hoper. You don’t let the Yankees off the mat and win. You just don’t.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: That Wasn’t Supposed to Happen', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leyland, Jim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ventura, Robin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago White Sox', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Phillies', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T14:13:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09702089-abc5-5ce9-bb44-3201c0233046', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09702089-abc5-5ce9-bb44-3201c0233046'}, {'abstract': 'With a real sense of drama, the latest episode of “The X Factor” turns this watcher into a fan.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/x-factor-watch-yes-hell-now-admit-to-being-a-fan/', 'snippet': 'With a real sense of drama, the latest episode of “The X Factor” turns this watcher into a fan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All right, now that the chaff has been separated, I’m completing my reluctant conversion into Fan of “The X Factor.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘X Factor’ Watch: Yes, He’ll Now Admit to Being a Fan', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T14:13:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21bb3f0b-05b9-5dd0-b401-3666d015c648', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21bb3f0b-05b9-5dd0-b401-3666d015c648'}, {'abstract': 'Coordinated strikes on outposts near the Pakistan border, timed apparently to mark the 10th anniversary of the start of the Afghan war, caused minimal damage, officers said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/world/asia/attacks-rock-us-outposts-near-afghanistan-pakistan-border.html', 'snippet': 'Coordinated strikes on outposts near the Pakistan border, timed apparently to mark the 10th anniversary of the start of the Afghan war, caused minimal damage, officers said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORWARD OPERATING BASE TILLMAN, Afghanistan — The sun had been up less than a half-hour on the 10th anniversary of the start of the American-led war in Afghanistan when the first rocket struck. Flying in from near the border with Pakistan, it shook this outpost with an explosion that hinted at the long day ahead.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u