I am not your president,” Mitt Romney said.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/in-foreign-policy-speech-romney-calls-for-an-american-century/', 'snippet': '“If you do not want America to be the strongest nation on Earth, I am not your president,” Mitt Romney said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLESTON, S.C. — Standing before an audience of crisply-clad, closely-shorn cadets, Mitt Romney delivered his foreign policy vision at The Citadel on Friday, calling for a strengthened military and economy to lead the country into what he called “an American Century,” while also accusing President Obama of weakening the nation’s image around the world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Foreign Policy Speech, Romney Calls for an ‘American Century’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foreign Policy (Magazine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charleston (SC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T16:27:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/645847c1-0d3e-5a55-b64f-8e6a7801f1a1', 'word_count': 941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/645847c1-0d3e-5a55-b64f-8e6a7801f1a1'}, {'abstract': 'Australia’s High Court rejects an appeal from the rock band Men at Work.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/kookaburra-sitting-pretty-in-that-old-gum-tree-as-court-upholds-copyright-ruling/', 'snippet': 'Australia’s High Court rejects an appeal from the rock band Men at Work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Men at Work, the Australian rock band, lost its final bid Friday to overturn a court ruling that it had stolen a flute riff on its 1980s hit “Down Under” from a children’s song, The Associated Press reported. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kookaburra Sitting Pretty in That Old Gum Tree as Court Upholds Copyright Ruling', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sinclair, Marion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Men at Work (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T16:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a6ef400-ef2b-5edb-8636-e92c2245aaaa', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a6ef400-ef2b-5edb-8636-e92c2245aaaa'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Ellen Marks and the Robots', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/10/t-magazine/10robots-yaeger.html', 'snippet': 'Mark Ellen Marks and the Robots', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Ellen Marks and the Robots', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'