d_count': 32, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f833206-080e-512e-8a00-82761eac26c3'}, {'abstract': 'With Italian austerity measures looming, having a nonprofit dedicated to preserving the artistic heritage of Venice seems more relevant than ever.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/venice-scrubbed-and-polished/', 'snippet': 'With Italian austerity measures looming, having a nonprofit dedicated to preserving the artistic heritage of Venice seems more relevant than ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Italian austerity measures looming and construction of the Mose Flood Barrier in full swing, little remains in Venice’s budget to protect and restore its treasures. Which is why Save Venice Inc., a nonprofit dedicated to preserving the artistic heritage of the city, seems more relevant than ever. The organization is celebrating its 40th anniversary this year with the release of the monumental book “Save Venice Inc.: Four Decades of Restoration in Venice.” The 500-page, self-published volume (hardcover edition, $200; soft cover $60; all proceeds go to Save Venice) serves as a retrospective on paper of the 400 works of art and architecture that the organization has adopted and restored.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venice Scrubbed and Polished', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Save Venice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T17:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'secti