and, the country music duo, will give a free concert in Indianapolis, where seven people were killed in August when stage rigging collapsed in high winds just before the band was to play at the Indiana State Fair. Sugarland announced on Friday that it would appear at the Conseco Fieldhouse on Oct. 28 and would collect money for survivors and relatives of victims of the accident. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sugarland to Give Free Concert in Indianapolis, Where 7 Died in Stage Accident', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State and County Fairs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sugarland (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indianapolis (Ind)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T17:14:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fadd90c2-880e-5755-9c0d-2794e0fc85a7', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fadd90c2-880e-5755-9c0d-2794e0fc85a7'}, {'abstract': 'Oct. 7, 2011 — With the economy still at the forefront, Republican candidates are focusing on foreign and defense issues. Also, Mitt Romney attracts new donors as the field settles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000001098634/the-caucus--focus-on-foreign-policy.html', 'snippet': 'Oct. 7, 2011 — With the economy still at the forefront, Republican candidates are focusing on foreign and defense issues