011/10/08/world/europe/slovakia-is-key-to-survival-of-euro-currency-zone.html', 'snippet': 'Bailouts for Greece and other European countries have touched a nerve in Slovakia, which is threatening to derail a rescue plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRATISLAVA, Slovakia — In a television advertisement for the popular Slovak beer Zlaty Bazant, a grinning man with a paunch stands on a sunny beach, nodding his head as the narrator says, “To want to borrow from everyone, that is Greek.” The ad then cuts to a skinny man, standing in a field, who shakes his head. “To not want to lend to anyone,” the narrator says, “that is Slovak.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/world/08slovakia1/08slovakia1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/08/world/08slovakia1/08slovakia1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/world/08slovakia1/08slovakia1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/world/08slovakia1/08slovakia1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/08/world/08slovakia1/08slovakia1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Slovaks Love and Hate Euro; Bailout May Lie in Between', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slovaks Love and Hate Euro; Bailout May Hang in Between', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Slovakia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Financial Stability Facility', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T18:48:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b9e2f12-fa63-58bd-8517-350f1cca403f', 'word_count': 1168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b9e2f12-fa63-58bd-8517-350f1cca403f'}, {'abstract': 'Expensive free agents and highly touted rookies have not helped the Philadelphia Eagles this season.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/eagles-are-a-dream-team-that-makes-fans-scream/', 'snippet': 'Expensive free agents and highly touted rookies have not helped the Philadelphia Eagles this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A sense of dread is creeping over Philadelphia. It is flowing through the streets, covering all of the dried-up previous layers of dread. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eagles Are a Dream Team That Makes Fans Scream', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asomugha, Nnamdi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gore, Frank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelce, Jason', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCoy,