re to Zurich that was hundreds cheaper. Trains are not cheap in Europe, but they can be cost-effective compared to car rental (and high-priced gas), and are so comfortable. And I second the cautions on the low-cost airlines within Europe. Read the fine print before you order your tickets, or you could get stuck with exorbitant luggage charges, as well as being dumped at an out-of-the-way alternative airport. Hugh S. Fullerton', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saving Money Flying to Europe', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T18:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc2415df-af46-5ec4-a80d-a5ccb2a24797', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc2415df-af46-5ec4-a80d-a5ccb2a24797'}, {'abstract': 'A chance encounter with Don Paterson’s poem, “Luing” sends a writer to the Scottish island that inspired the verse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/travel/poetry-made-me-do-it-my-trip-to-the-hebrides.html', 'snippet': 'A chance encounter with Don Paterson’s poem, “Luing” sends a writer to the Scottish island that inspired the verse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I WAS about to slide down a hill when the strangeness of my situation struck me: A poem had brought me here.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/travel/09LUING1_SPAN/09LUING1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/09/travel/09LUING1_SPAN/09LUING1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'x