ld say when they were wrong. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/business/wealth/wealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So Far, It’s Been a Half-Empty Year for Financial Forecasters', 'kicker': 'Wealth Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Far, It’s Been a Half-Empty Year for Financial Forecasters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T18:57:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c103baee-8742-5750-a659-7087eabc18a0', 'word_count': 1342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c103baee-8742-5750-a659-7087eabc18a0'}, {'abstract': 'Mondo, an Austin, Tex., offshoot of the Alamo Drafthouse theater chain, produces new posters celebrating time-honored genre favorites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/movies/movie-posters-are-the-business-of-mondo.html', 'snippet': 'Mondo, an Austin, Tex., offshoot of the Alamo Drafthouse theater chain, produces new posters celebrating time-honored genre favorites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE movie poster is dead. Long live the movie poster. Gone are the days of hand-drawn studio posters that possessed a creativity and artistry matching that of the films themselves. Think of “King Kong,” with its harrowing illustrations, or Saul Bass’s Minimalist design for “Vertigo.” The contemporary studio poster is often a literal, less adventurous affair, like the vision of Julia Roberts on the back of Tom Hanks’s scooter in the poster for “Larry Crowne,” a typical example of today’s photography-driven advertisements.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09MONDO1_SPAN/09MONDO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09MONDO1_SPAN/09MONDO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 289}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09MONDO1_SPAN/09MONDO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09MONDO1_SPAN/09MONDO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09MONDO1_SPAN/09MONDO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hand-Drawn Homage to Classic Films', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hand-Drawn Homage to Classic Films', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franchi, Rudy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Craven, Wes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Posters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fairey, Shepard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'p