 {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T19:10:39+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'Rebecca Lee Douglas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Douglas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/459a9fb5-a400-57e0-9554-b214ab73fc09', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/459a9fb5-a400-57e0-9554-b214ab73fc09'}, {'abstract': 'The transition to an at-home office can be difficult, and the most common danger is to unproductively while away the hours with nothing to show for it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/your-money/how-to-make-working-at-home-work-for-you.html', 'snippet': 'The transition to an at-home office can be difficult, and the most common danger is to unproductively while away the hours with nothing to show for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I\u2002WAS conducting an interview from my office, which doubles as my home, and was frustrated because the loud leaf blower outside was drowning out my words and thoughts. I walked from one room to another to find some quiet, stumbling at one point over a laundry basket. All the while, I was hoping I sounded professional.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/your-money/08shortcuts/08shortcuts-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/08/your-money/08shortcuts/08shortcuts-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/your-money/08shortcuts/08shortcuts-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/your-money/08shortcuts/08shortcuts-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/08/your-money/08shortcuts/08shortcuts-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Make Working at Home Work for You', 'kicker': 'Shortcuts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Make Working At Home Work for You', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freelancing, Self-Employment and Independent Contracting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telecommuting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consultants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T19:12:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alina Tugend', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tugend', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c9fda1b-aba9-5837-861f-4fb048f97689', 'word_count': 1276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c9fda1b-aba9-5837-861f-4fb048f97689'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Hall, a favorite for Sunday’s Chicago Marathon, has been coaching himself since last fall, running his own way and at his own pace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/sports/ryan-hall-sets-sights-on-chicago-marathon-without-a-coach.html', 'snippet': 'Ryan Hall, a favorite for Sunday’s Chicago Marathon, has been coaching himself since last fall, running his own way and at his own pace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ryan Hall, one of the few Americans who can compete against the best international distance runners, is going to try to win the Chicago Marathon on Sunday. And he is doing it without a coach, which is almost unheard of in elite distance running, or elite sports for that matter.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/sports/08marathon1/08marathon1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 777, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/sports/08marathon1/08marathon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/08/sports/08marathon1/08marathon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Top American Marathoner’s Success Raises Question: Is a Coach Necessary?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Top American Marathoner’s Success Raises Question: Is a Coach Necessary?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Ryan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chicago Marathon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marathon Running', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T19:14:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c19ae68-680e-5e00-b866-705caa12733c', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c19ae68-680e-5e00-b866-705caa12733c'}, {'abstract': 'When models fail.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/way-off-base-2/', 'snippet': 'When models fail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I see some commenters reacting to the failure of major inflation to break out by insisting that inflation is defined as an increase in the monetary base — that is, the bank reserves plus currency that are what increases when the Fed “prints money”. As it happens, that’s wrong: very old dictionaries defined inflation as a rise in money and/or credit, but the modern usage is, of course, a rise in prices. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Way Off Base', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T19:15:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebac06d3-2dd0-58cb-a10d-9d41faa88b66', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebac06d3-2dd0-58cb-a10d-9d41faa88b66'}, {'abstract': 'But the turn against staple-financing appears to be an overreaction — the arrangement just needs to be fully disclosed and above board.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/del-monte-settlement-highlights-risk-in-m-a-advice/', 'snippet': 'But the turn against staple-financing appears to be an overreaction — the arrangement just needs to be fully disclosed and above board.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Del Monte Foods and Barclays Capital will pay $89.4 million to settle allegations of wrongdoing in the sale of Del Monte to Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Company, Vestar Capital and Centerview Partners. The settlement is one of the largest in connection 