 a source of electricity. Here’s a news release and a pdf of the study. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Evidence of a Big Greenhouse Advantage from Gas Over Coal', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krauss, Clifford', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Worldwatch Institute', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T20:09:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23f88690-7e03-5108-a90e-d72e7a015b9d', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23f88690-7e03-5108-a90e-d72e7a015b9d'}, {'abstract': 'The muscle car offspring of the 1960s union between a Long Island auto dealer and the Motion Performance tuning shop are now sought after, rare and expensive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/automobiles/encore-for-a-muscle-car-legend.html', 'snippet': 'The muscle car offspring of the 1960s union between a Long Island auto dealer and the Motion Performance tuning shop are now sought after, rare and expensive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CORAL SPRINGS, Fla.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/automobiles/09MOTI1/09MOTI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/09/automobiles/09MOTI1/09MOTI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/automobiles/09MOTI1/09MOTI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/automobiles/09MOTI1/09MOTI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/automobiles/09MOTI1/09MOTI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Encore for a Muscle Car Legend', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Encore for a Muscle Car Legend', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T20:10:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ro McGonegal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ro', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGonegal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee09de5e-26b1-5929-a20e-5824047ffce7', 'word_count': 1522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee09de5e-26b1-5929-a20e-5824047ffce7'}, {'abstract': 'Even in this age of performance, where cars with factory-built engines of 500 horsepower are almost commonplace, there is still room for tuner shops and the extra power they provide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/automobiles/placing-a-value-on-horsepower.html', 'snippet': 'Even in this age of performance, where cars with factory-built engines of 500 horsepower are almost commonplace, there is still room for tuner shops and the extra power they provide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THOUGH the advent of pollution-control laws pulled the plug on the first wave of Detroit’s muscle cars early in the 1970s, advances in electronic management systems and exhaust treatment have since taken V-8 power to unprecedented levels. But even in this new age of performance, where cars with clean-running factory-built engines of 500 horsepower are almost commonplace, there is still room for tuner shops that dig deeper. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/automobiles/09PRIC/09PRIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/09/automobiles/09PRIC/09PRIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/automobiles/09PRIC/09PRIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non