 Twitter in the Sept. 25 issue was that on Mindy Kaling, who has more than 1.5 million followers.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/mindy-kaling-takes-the-twitter-prize/', 'snippet': 'We shouldn’t have been surprised that our most popular story on Twitter in the Sept. 25 issue was that on Mindy Kaling, who has more than 1.5 million followers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We shouldn’t have been surprised that our most popular story on Twitter in the Sept. 25 issue was that on Mindy Kaling, who has more than 1.5 million followers. “With Tweets, if you are sitting around for more than 45 seconds, it’s probably not the medium for you,” the actress/writer told Curtis Sittenfeld.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mindy Kaling Takes the Twitter Prize', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaling, Mindy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T20:56:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c8577d1-887b-5921-9a0c-239454336f87', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c8577d1-887b-5921-9a0c-239454336f87'}, {'abstract': 'Tchaikovsky’s symphonies were played by the orchestra of the Mariinsky Theater in St. Petersburg, where the Tchaikovsky operas and ballets are central to the institution’s identity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/arts/music/mariinsky-orchestra-at-carnegie-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'Tchaikovsky’s symphonies were played by the orchestra of the Mariinsky Theater in St. Petersburg, where the Tchaikovsky operas and ballets are central to the institution’s identity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a theme for a festival, Tchaikovsky in St. Petersburg, which Carnegie Hall is presenting through this month, is pretty vague. That did not matter a bit on Thursday night when Valery Gergiev conducted the Mariinsky Orchestra in the first of three programs presenting the six Tchaikovsky symphonies. The orchestra opened the Carnegie Hall season on Wednesday night with works by Shostakovich, Tchaikovsky (the “Rococo Variations,” featuring the cellist Yo-Yo Ma) and Rimsky-Korsakov.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Russia, Authentic Tchaikovsky, With Love', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Russia, Authentic Tchaikovsky, With Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tchaikovsky, Peter Ilyich', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mariinsky Theater Orchestra', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gergiev, Valery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T20:59:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd28d7f3-28b9-5a58-a03e-6174d666f98c', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd28d7f3-28b9-5a58-a03e-6174d666f98c'}, {'abstract': 'The Los Angeles Kings defeated the Rangers 3-2 in Stockholm on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/breaking-down-the-rangers-overtime-loss-to-kings/', 'snippet': 'The Los Angeles Kings defeated the Rangers 3-2 in Stockholm on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jack Johnson’s power goal wi