'nyt://article/69217063-32c4-54bd-b90e-2665e691080b', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69217063-32c4-54bd-b90e-2665e691080b'}, {'abstract': 'Rachel Griffiths, formerly of “Six Feet Under” and “Brothers & Sisters,” will make her Broadway debut in “Other Desert Cities.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/theater/rachel-griffiths-joining-other-desert-cities.html', 'snippet': 'Rachel Griffiths, formerly of “Six Feet Under” and “Brothers & Sisters,” will make her Broadway debut in “Other Desert Cities.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'ADULT children who dream of lashing out at their overbearing mothers, detached fathers and deadbeat loved ones have had a hero in Rachel Griffiths for years now.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09GRIFFITHS1/09JPGRIFFITHS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 910, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09GRIFFITHS1/09JPGRIFFITHS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/arts/09GRIFFITHS1/09JPGRIFFITHS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Playing Someone’s Fierce Sister', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Playing Someone’s Fierce Sister', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffiths, Rachel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:04:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e01bb823-6040-58b6-bc1f-c5eeb00ed565', 'word_count': 1660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e01bb823-6040-58b6-bc1f-c5eeb00ed565'}, {'abstract': 'And there were a whole lot of those books.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/my-last-play-is-one-for-the-books/', 'snippet': 'And there were a whole lot of those books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The shelves were definitely empty on Monday night when Ed Schmidt wrapped up the final performance of “My Last Play,” his one-man show about acknowledging a lifetime of failure in the theater by giving away his collection of 2,000 theater books.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘My Last Play’ Is One for the Books', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:07:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cbae72b-397f-57d0-9f93-4437d4a31e54', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cbae72b-397f-57d0-9f93-4437d4a31e54'}, {'abstract': '“The Speaker’s Progress,” an elegantly staged satire about the Arab world from the Kuwaiti playwright Sulayman al-Bassam, is at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/theater/reviews/the-speakers-progress-in-brooklyn-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Speaker’s Progress,” an elegantly staged satire about the Arab world from the Kuwaiti playwright Sulayman al-Bassam, is at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an unnamed Arab country theaters have been shut down and performance criminalized. From a lectern a former theater producer explains that what he is presenting is not a play but a reconstruction of a 1960s production based on the story of Shakespeare’s “Twelfth Night.” It’s oddly clinical: Lab coats replace costumes, and men and women remain at a distance from one another. An ominous camera sits in front of the stage. The government is watching. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Restricting Free Speech With Lab Coats in Illyria', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'The Speaker’s Progress'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Restricting Free Speech With Lab Coats in Illyria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bassam, Sulayman Al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:11:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c950096c-3d3b-52f8-9a15-19266ca307d8', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c950096c-3d3b-52f8-9a15-19266ca307d8'}, {'abstract': 'The new Nissan Quest is clearly aimed at giving customers the conventional minivan experience they seem to want: family transportation that is comfortable and versatile.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/reviewing-the-nissan-quest/', 'snippet': 'The new Nissan Quest is clearly aimed at giving customers the conventional minivan experience they seem to want: family transportation that is comfortable and versatile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Sunday’s Automobiles section, Cheryl Jensen reviews the Nissan Quest, which is redesigned for 2012. Prior generations of the minivan were trendsetters in their segment, with innovative interior features like the 2004 model’s podlike instrument panel, positioned between the driver and passenger, which housed the shift lever and other controls.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing the Nissan Quest', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler LLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:14:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4675e3f2-4536-592b-b231-366b05f00d62', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4675e3f2-4536-592b-b231-366b05f00d62'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Stewart, host of The Daily Show, and Stephen Colbert of the Colbert Report, paid tribute to Steven P. Jobs, co-founder of Apple.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/comedy-central-weighs-in-on-steve-jobs/', 'snippet': 'Jon Stewart, host of The Daily Show, and Stephen Colbert of the Colbert Report, paid tribute to Steven P. Jobs, co-founder of Apple.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jon Stewart, host of The Daily Show, and Stephen Colbert of The Colbert Report, paid tribute to Steven P. Jobs, co-founder of Apple, on Thursday night after he died on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comedy Central Weighs In on Steve Jobs', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colbert, Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Jon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:15:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13124fa7-06f9-5627-9638-7b9824a98ee4', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13124fa7-06f9-5627-9638-7b9824a98ee4'}, {'abstract': 'The presidents of the universities in the Big East Conference participated in an hour-long conference call, but no immediate decisions were made about the future of the league.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/big-east-talking-about-the-future/', 'snippet': 'The presidents of the universities in the Big East Conference participated in an hour-long conference call, but no immediate decisions were made about the future of the league.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The presidents of the universities in the Big East Conference participated in an hour-long conference call Friday morning, but no immediate decisions were made about the future of the league. A league official with direct knowledge of the call said that invitations to potential new members would be handed out soon, perhaps as early as next week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big East Talking About the Future', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big East Conference', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:17:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c985e1e-2256-5dbc-a8d1-d2fd5ebac830', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c985e1e-2256-5dbc-a8d1-d2fd5ebac830'}, {'abstract': 'October 7, 2011 — Tawakkol Karman was one of the first to lead antigovernment protests in Yemen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000001099458/timescast--yemeni-woman-wins-nobel.html', 'snippet': 'October 7, 2011 — Tawakkol Karman was one of the first to lead antigovernment protests in Yemen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'October 7, 2011 — Tawakkol Karman was one of the first to lead antigovernment protests in Yemen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/multimedia/video-tc-111007-kasinof/video-tc-111007-kasinof-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/07/multimedia/video-tc-111007-kasinof/video-tc-111007-kasinof-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/07/multimedia/video-tc-111007-kasinof/video-tc-111007-kasinof-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/07/multimedia/video-tc-111007-kasinof/video-tc-111007-kasinof-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | Yemeni Woman Wins Nobel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nobel Prizes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:17:40+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'Emily B. Hager', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/039df977-785e-5a57-bde3-a54bcaa791e8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/039df977-785e-5a57-bde3-a54bcaa791e8'}, {'abstract': 'The pared-down look and no-nonsense sensibility of “The Early Show” demonstrates how far it trails “Today” and “Good Morning America” in ratings. It’s also a sign of how weakness can become a strength.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/arts/television/the-early-show-on-cbs-is-sober-but-stronger.html', 'snippet': 'The pared-down look and no-nonsense sensibility of “The Early Show” demonstrates how far it trails “Today” and “Good Morning America” in ratings. It’s also a sign of how weakness can become a strength.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There isn’t much news you can use on “The Early Show” on CBS. It no longer offers dieting tips, barbecue recipes or audience makeovers. There are no pop concerts or “Growing Pains” cast reunions. “The Early Show” doesn’t plan weddings or even forecast rain — weather is delegated to local affiliates. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/arts/MORNING/MORNING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 237, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/08/arts/MORNING/MORNING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 237}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/arts/MORNING/MORNING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mornings Are Sober but Better at CBS', 'kicker': 'The TV Watch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mornings Are Sober But Better At CBS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:22:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b99ac767-6b52-59b3-8f5e-db84481b8cc9', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b99ac767-6b52-59b3-8f5e-db84481b8cc9'}, {'abstract': 'Teams from Harvard and Columbia debate the question, “Does reality television do more harm than good?”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/arts/television/reality-tv-debate-critics-notebook.html', 'snippet': 'Teams from Harvard and Columbia debate the question, “Does reality television do more harm than good?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'My maternal grandfather, Don Rose, was an obsessive journal-keeper when he was young. For some years beginning in his late teens, he would record his thoughts and activities in minute detail — not just that he went shopping, but also what he bought and how much it cost. (“Fare, town: .50; suit cleaned & mended, 2.05; socks, .25; collars, .25.”)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/arts/SUBREALITY/SUBREALITY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Old-Fashioned Date Can’t Beat a Night Out Debating Reality TV', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Old-Fashioned Date Can’t Beat a Night Out Debating Reality TV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:28:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/926c8ff4-5594-55cd-8f98-83f500584114', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/926c8ff4-5594-55cd-8f98-83f500584114'}, {'abstract': 'Meet Valeria S., the German-Russian model featured in our upcoming women’s issue.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/fashions-new-face-valeria-s/', 'snippet': 'Meet Valeria S., the German-Russian model featured in our upcoming women’s issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion’s New Face | Valeria S.', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:29:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f099400-409a-5843-87ab-53903210b538', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f099400-409a-5843-87ab-53903210b538'}, {'abstract': 'A recent sartorial scavenge was prompted by Céline’s resort collection and its blatantly branded top.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/label-maker/', 'snippet': 'A recent sartorial scavenge was prompted by Céline’s resort collection and its blatantly branded top.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A T-shirt?” asked the Lanvin shopgirl on the other end of the receiver when I inquired about logo tees. “We sell blouses. Have you tried calling the outlets?” My recent sartorial scavenge was prompted by Céline’s resort collection. I was already head over heels for the discreet French label, but then Phoebe Philo, its designer, showed an in-your-face Céline-tagged top, styled smartly beneath a bustier and a prim, tailored jacket. Only Philo could make blatant branding compulsively collectible so soon after we’d all stripped the initials (save our own) off our bags and sunglasses. “I’ve heard they keep them in the back,” said a saleswoman at Jeffrey when I went there looking for logos. “That’s the secret,” he added. “You have to ask.” A recent trip to Yves Saint Laurent confirmed this to be true. “We wouldn’t be YSL if we didn’t have an inscribed T-shirt, would we?” the sales associate coyly whispered to me before returning from the stockroom with a yummy stash of initialed tees in navy and magenta. “We’ll always have them.” Blouses, that is.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Label Maker', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:30:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Waldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9884f479-d1e2-5248-a91b-4c742c3ae3f4', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9884f479-d1e2-5248-a91b-4c742c3ae3f4'}, {'abstract': 'A senior Energy Department official inquired frequently about the progress of the loan even though his wife’s law firm represented the company and he promised to recuse himself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/us/politics/e-mail-shows-senior-energy-official-pushed-solyndra-loan.html', 'snippet': 'A senior Energy Department official inquired frequently about the progress of the loan even though his wife’s law firm represented the company and he promised to recuse himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A senior Energy Department official pushed hard for the government’s $535 million loan to the now-bankrupt California solar energy company Solyndra even after he had disclosed that his wife’s law firm represented the company and he had promised to recuse himself from matters related to the loan application, according to e-mails provided to Congressional investigators by the administration.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E-Mail Shows Senior Energy Official Pushed Solyndra Loan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'E-Mail Shows Official Pushed Solyndra Loan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Solyndra Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:31:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Lipton and John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4390d2fe-6caa-5e3f-9052-755565883dda', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4390d2fe-6caa-5e3f-9052-755565883dda'}, {'abstract': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural events from this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/08/arts/1008week-in-culture.html', 'snippet': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural events from this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural