s://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/world/middleeast/leading-syrian-opposition-figure-killed-another-publicly-beaten.html', 'snippet': 'A leading Kurdish political figure was shot to death in northern Syria, while a political dissident was brazenly beaten in the heart of the capital Damascus, activists said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Syrian security forces on Friday attacked two prominent opposition leaders, shooting one to death in the north and beating another in broad daylight in the heart of the capital, Damascus, activists said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Syrian Opposition Figure Killed, and Another Publicly Beaten', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria Forces Said to Kill A Dissenter In the North', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Bakri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dc1d5cd-26c9-5fa8-ba83-8bfe45d0f4ea', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dc1d5cd-26c9-5fa8-ba83-8bfe45d0f4ea'}, {'abstract': 'The two former bank executives, Sallie L. Krawcheck and Joe Price, will receive $6 million and $5 million, respectively, under agreements smoothing their departures.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/2-ousted-bank-of-america-executives-get-final-paychecks/', 'snippet': 'The two former bank executives, Sallie L. Krawcheck and Joe Price, will receive $6 million and $5 million, respectively, under agreements smoothing their departures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two ousted executives of Bank of America, Sallie L. Krawcheck and Joe Price, will receive $6 million and $5 million, respectively, under newly signed agreements smoothing their departures from the bank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 Ousted Executives of Bank of America Get Final Paychecks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krawcheck, Sallie L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:45:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Theo Francis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Theo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Francis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e8d475f-9212-577b-b07f-4996079772ac', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e8d475f-9212-577b-b07f-4996079772ac'}, {'abstract': 'The police and the Queens district attorney, Richard A. Brown, announced the sweep against the operation, which they said took in $13 million: 75 were arrested, 21 are being sought and 15 are already in jail.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/111-charged-in-elaborate-identity-theft-scheme/', 'snippet': 'The police and the Queens district attorney, Richard A. Brown, announced the sweep against the operation, which they said took in $13 million: 75 were arrested, 21 are being sought and 15 are already in jail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A total of 111 people have been indicted in an identity-theft scheme that originated largely in the back rooms of Queens restaurants, the authorities said on Friday, and then mushroomed into a worldwide network of counterfeiters, hackers, fences and thieves who made off with an estimated $13 million in fraudulent purchases.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '111 Charged in Elaborate Identity-Theft Scheme', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identity Fraud', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Richard A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T21:46:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Harris and Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6081015a-89bf-5664-9eeb-45b5b8a80a67', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6081015a-89bf-5664-9eeb-45b5b8a80a67'}, {'abstract': 'A new interactive exhi