'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hickenlooper, George', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sehring, Jonathan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Independent Film Channel', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T22:37:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43ea77cc-2fd7-53b5-b760-1ba1d5289375', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43ea77cc-2fd7-53b5-b760-1ba1d5289375'}, {'abstract': 'When I got the job as editor of this magazine almost a year ago now, it was issues like the one we are publishing this week that I hoped we would eventually be able to make.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/this-sunday-pirates-like-cookies-too/', 'snippet': 'When I got the job as editor of this magazine almost a year ago now, it was issues like the one we are publishing this week that I hoped we would eventually be able to make.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I got the job as editor of this magazine almost a year ago now, it was issues like this week’s that I wished for. I am proud of everything we’ve published in the magazine over the last several months, but like many writers and editors, I am self-critical to the point that I can look at almost anything I’ve ever done and see only the mistakes and missed opportunities therein. But that should not happen with this week’s issue. The mix of stories is the best we’ve assembled so far, starting with Jeffrey Gettleman’s epic pirates tale. It is an exciting, dramatic work of narrative journalism overflowing with memorable moments like this: “Once the pirates were in control of the Lynn Rival, they ransacked it, flinging open cupboards, eating all of the Chandlers’ cookies and stealing their money, watches, rings, electronics, their satellite phone and clothes.” Yup, those mean pirates went right for the cookies. Awesome. Adding to the flair and intensity of Jeffrey’s story are the excellent illustrations by Wesley Allsbrook, the first time she has been in the magazine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Sunday: Pirates Like Cookies, Too', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tubas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bishop, Greg', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T22:40:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Lindgren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindgren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11781c9a-2325-5e23-ae95-8eb142e7ba3a', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11781c9a-2325-5e23-ae95-8eb142e7ba3a'}, {'abstract': 'The governor’s office organized the flood of e-mail to emphasize that Republicans were united in their opposition to the proposed map, which was approved by a state commission.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/arizona-republicans-disapprove-of-draft-redistricting-map/', 'snippet': 'The governor’s office organized the flood of e-mail to emphasize that Republicans were united in their opposition to the proposed map, which was approved by a state commission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly every major Republican politician in Arizona issued a news release this week — all within an hour or so of one another on Wednesday afternoon — condemning a draft redistricting map approved by a state commission.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona Republicans Disapprove of Draft Redistricting Map', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quayle, Ben', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweikert, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scottsdale (Ariz)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T22:46:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Lacey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lacey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2087627-4ad8-5e09-a54e-b26a9ac12418', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2087627-4ad8-5e09-a54e-b26a9ac12418'}, {'abstract': 'The bookseller said that the publisher of the novels had made a deal with Amazon for exclusive e-book sales, which conflicts with a Barnes & Noble policy.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/barnes-noble-in-graphic-novel-dispu