vid Gillen and David Segal on filming food; and Richard Thaler on self-interested patriotism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/10/07/business/07weekendbiz_pod.html', 'snippet': 'This week: Jeff Sommer with John Markoff and Steve Lohr on the life of Steve Jobs; Motoko Rich on unemployment and recession; David Gillen and David Segal on filming food; and Richard Thaler on self-interested patriotism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week: Jeff Sommer with John Markoff and Steve Lohr on the life of Steve Jobs; Motoko Rich on unemployment and recession; David Gillen and David Segal on filming food; and Richard Thaler on self-interested patriotism.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The life of Steve Jobs; unemployment and recession; filming food; and self-interested patriotism.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T23:19:24+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/9590be66-b1f2-5c30-952f-ecce2cab174e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/9590be66-b1f2-5c30-952f-ecce2cab174e'}, {'abstract': 'In many ways, Apple’s co-founder emulated Polaroid’s Edwin Land, the inventor of instant photography.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/opinion/the-man-who-inspired-jobs.html', 'snippet': 'In many ways, Apple’s co-founder emulated Polaroid’s Edwin Land, the inventor of instant photography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the memorials to Steven P. Jobs this week, Apple’s co-founder was compared with the world’s great inventor-entrepreneurs: Thomas Edison, Henry Ford, Alexander Graham Bell. Yet virtually none of the obituaries mentioned the man Jobs himself considered his hero, the person on whose career he explicitly modeled his own: Edwin H. Land, the genius domus of Polaroid Corporation and inventor of instant photography.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Man Who Inspired Jobs', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Land, Edwin H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Polaroid Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-07T23:23:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Bonanos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bonanos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/80137cb6-e3ca-5a0c-b5d6-c90a7ddc9e09', 'word_count': 1250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80137cb6-e3ca-5a0c-b5d6-c90a7ddc9e09'}, {'abstract': 'President Ellen Johnson Sirleaf is not the same hero at home as she is abroad, where Liberia’s image has improved vastly under her administration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/world/africa/prize-or-not-liberian-faces-tough-race-to-keep-office.html', 'snippet': 'President Ellen Johnson Sirleaf is not the same hero at home as she is abroad, where Liberia’s image has improved vastly under her administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONROVIA, Liberia — The day began in this battered seaside capital with shouts and drumming for a leading Liberian politician — but not the one honored with a Nobel Peace Prize on Friday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/world/08nobel2/08nobel2-article