4-cbdd4350bacf', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/d15f52d0-795b-5d79-b054-cbdd4350bacf'}, {'abstract': 'Nocturnalist was at a Whitney Museum gala, a United Nations fund-raiser and a book party, and kept running into a BFF, Martha Stewart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/nyregion/a-garage-is-all-aglitter-for-arts-sake.html', 'snippet': 'Nocturnalist was at a Whitney Museum gala, a United Nations fund-raiser and a book party, and kept running into a BFF, Martha Stewart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We were in a decommissioned bus depot at Pier 57 in Hudson River Park when the artist Chuck Close buzzed past us with his girlfriend, Sienna Shields, seated in his lap on his electric wheelchair. Their lips passionately interlocked, and they never looked up as they rolled out the door. It was Wednesday night, and the Whitney Museum of American Art’s yearly gala, held this year under disco balls in an asphalt-and-steel garage, was wrapping up.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST1/NOCTURNALIST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST1/NOCTURNALIST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST1/NOCTURNALIST1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST1/NOCTURNALIST1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST1/