'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/77ee3a05-9155-5815-9fba-c9f8bbe585bf', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/77ee3a05-9155-5815-9fba-c9f8bbe585bf'}, {'abstract': 'As he left the room at the Johnson County Republican Dinner here, Mr. Perry was asked by a reporter whether he agreed with the comments of Mr. Jeffress about the Mormon Church being a cult. “No,” he replied.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/perry-disagrees-with-supporters-comment-on-mormon-church/', 'snippet': 'As he left the room at the Johnson County Republican Dinner here, Mr. Perry was asked by a reporter whether he agreed with the comments of Mr. Jeffress about the Mormon Church being a cult. “No,” he replied.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TIFFIN, Iowa — Gov. Rick Perry of Texas said Friday night that he does not believe the Mormon Church is a cult, but he declined to answer questions about a remark from a Texas pastor who criticized the religion of Mitt Romney and declared that he “is not a Christian.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perry Disagrees With Supporter’s Comment on Mormon Church', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeffress, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T01:36:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5cca8b6-2e10-54cf-bd1f-27ca3cce3101', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5cca8b6-2e10-54cf-bd1f-27ca3cce3101'}, {'abstract': 'A 2004 gang killing connected to the bus business also claimed the life of a cocktail waitress. A suspect was arrested this year in Toronto and returned to New York to face federal murder charges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/nyregion/collateral-damage-in-the-chinatown-bus-wars.html', 'snippet': 'A 2004 gang killing connected to the bus business also claimed the life of a cocktail waitress. A suspect was arrested this year in Toronto and returned to New York to face federal murder charges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2004, a seat on a bus from Chinatown to Boston cost $10, but the related costs were sometimes staggering. Indirectly, the bus business took the life of a cocktail waitress one night at work; she was killed by a stray bullet to her head. Hundreds of man-hours of police work would follow, as would the efforts of Interpol and various police agencies in the United States and Canada seven years later. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Collateral Damage in the Chinatown Bus Wars', 'kicker': 'Crime Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Collateral Damage in the Chinatown Bus Wars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chinatown (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flushing (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T01:37:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/336d91e7-8a3c-5beb-8514-012d18cbb72c', 'word_count': 820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/336d91e7-8a3c-5beb-8514-012d18cbb72c'}, {'abstract': 'An official at New York City’s housing agency put his cryptic demands to developers on little pieces of paper, court papers say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/nyregion/in-new-york-corruption-case-600000-in-scribbles-us-says.html', 'snippet': 'An official at New York City’s housing agency put his cryptic demands to developers on little pieces of paper, court papers say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent years, federal prosecutors say, Wendell B. Walters has spent a fair amount of time scribbling down numbers on little pieces of paper.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/HOUSING/HOUSING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/HOUSING/HOUSING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/HOUSING/HOUSING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Numbers Scribbled Here and There Added Up to $600,000 in Bribes, U.S. Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Numbers Scribbled Here and There Added Up to $600,000 in Bribes, U.S. Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walters, Wendell B', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Housing Preservation and Development (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racketeering and Racketeers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T01:38:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By William K. Rashbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2994387a-4a22-5c66-847c-b6dadc607e46', 'word_count': 671, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2994387a-4a22-5c66-847c-b6dadc607e46'}, {'abstract': 'In an interview with the police, Dr. Conrad Murray said he gave Michael Jackson milder drugs to help him sleep before resorting to the powerful anesthetic that killed him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/us/doctor-tells-how-michael-jackson-sought-sleep.html', 'snippet': 'In an interview with the police, Dr. Conrad Murray said he gave Michael Jackson milder drugs to help him sleep before resorting to the powerful anesthetic that killed him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an interview recorded two days after Michael Jackson’s death, Dr. Conrad Murray told the Los Angeles police that he had spent hours trying to get the singer to sleep using milder drugs before resorting to a powerful anesthetic that Jackson referred to as his “milk.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Doctor Tells How Jackson Sought Sleep', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Doctor Tells How Jackson Lacked Sleep', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Conrad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anesthesia and Anesthetics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sedatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T01:42:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By LORI MOORE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MOORE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7273b2e-0085-536b-bbf2-e35b59c82cd7', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://ar