e United States in 1998, the Cuban government immediately hailed them as heroes, with billboards, books and movies, and argued that their convictions and sentences — handed down in a Miami court — proved that the United States was an enemy, beholden to radical Cuban exiles.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/world/08cuba/08cuba-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/world/08cuba/08cuba-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/08/world/08cuba/08cuba-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One of ‘Cuban Five’ Spies Is Released on Probation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One of ‘Cuban Five’ Spies Is Released on Probation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T01:45:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damien Cave', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cave', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8db1acd-2d57-51c5-89ca-345c0652889e', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8db1acd-2d57-51c5-89ca-345c0652889e'}, {'abstract': 'For most outsiders, two years’ worth of calendar entries for Patricia E. Harris, the first deputy mayor, offer the only details of what exactly she does.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/nyregion/patricia-harris-bloomberg-deputy-has-calendars-released.html', 'snippet': 'For most outsiders, two years’ worth of calendar entries for Patricia E. Harris, the first deputy mayor, offer the only details of what exactly she does.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patricia E. Harris, the first deputy mayor, is arguably the most important unelected person in city government and may also be seen as the personification, as the head of Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s charitable foundation, of the blurred lines between the mayor’s public and private lives.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/HARRIS/HARRIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/HARRIS/HARRIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/08/nyregion/HARRIS/HARRIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Calendars Shed Light on Enigmatic Bloomberg Aide', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Calendars Shed Light on Enigmatic Aide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Patricia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freed