the weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/record/', 'snippet': 'Tim Croce welcomes us to the weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY’S PUZZLE — When The Kids were younger, I hired a teenager to babysit so I could get out of the house and have a coherent thought once a week. One evening, the teenager showed up wearing a T-shirt that had a picture of the plastic inserts we used to put into the large holes of 45 r.p.m. records so that we could play them on our turntables. Strictly out of curiosity (and not masochism, as some of you are no doubt thinking), I asked the 15-year-old if she could tell me what the object on her T-shirt was, and thoroughly enjoyed the fact that she could not. The closest she could get, being only 15, was that the picture on her shirt was “neat.” To her credit, she knew that a turntable was something on which her Dad used to play records. Whatever those were.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saturday: Sounds Like a Broken Record', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T02:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c72b55e-69ed-50f3-9d66-64d5ae1ad6f3', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c72b55e-69ed-50f3-9d66-64d5ae1ad6f3'}, {'abstract': 'The chief prosecutor in Veracruz State resigned Friday, a day after 32 bodies were discovered in a residential neighborhood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/world/mexico-prosecutor-quits-after-32-bodies-are-found.html', 'snippet': 'The chief prosecutor in Veracruz State resigned Friday, a day after 32 bodies were discovered in a residential neighborhood.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The chief prosecutor in Veracruz State resigned Friday, a day after 32 bodies were discovered in a residential neighborhood and less than three weeks after 35 bodies were dumped on a busy highway. The state prosecutor, Reynaldo Escobar Pérez, resigned for unspecified “personal reasons,” a spokeswoman said. The departure came as federal forces flooded Veracruz and arrested 20 suspects believed to be members of rival drug gangs. President Felipe Calderón hailed the arrests on Twitter as a “great blow” to criminal gangs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Prosecutor Quits After 32 Bodies Are Found', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Prosecutor Quits After 32 Bodies Are Found', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T02:01:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Zabludovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zabludovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd33b691-5f3f-5b55-8a02-8f8291ceba08', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd33b691-5f3f-5b55-8a02-8f8291ceba08'}, {'abstract': 'Eric H. Holder Jr. lashed out at members of Congress, and said that public discussion over a gun-trafficking investigation is aimed only at gaining political advantage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/us/politics/eric-holder-lashes-out-over-gun-inquiry-comments.html', 'snippet': 'Eric H. Holder Jr. lashed out at members of Congress, and said that public discussion over a gun-trafficking investigation is aimed only at gaining political advantage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. lashed out at members of Congress who are investigating Justice Department actions in a disputed gun-trafficking inquiry, saying Friday in a letter that public discussion about the issue had become “base” and “inflammatory” and was aimed solely at gaining political advantage.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/us/HOLDER/HOLDER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Holder Reacts to Criticism of Gun Inquiry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Holder Reacts to Criticism of Gun Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T02:06:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfcd9fb1-a5ef-58a1-957b-5e5da55405a4', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfcd9fb1-a5ef-58a1-957b-5e5da55405a4'}, {'abstract': 'The $5 monthly fee that banks plan to start charging for the use of a debit card may be just the start.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/opinion/nocera-revenge-of-the-gougers.html', 'snippet': 'The $5 monthly fee that banks plan to start charging for the use of a debit card may be just the start.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hardest part about writing about Bank of America’s dunderheaded plan to impose a $5-a-month fee on debit card users is deciding which of the many juicy angles to pursue. “Have Bank of America’s Managers Lost Their Minds?” asked The American Banker earlier this week. That’s one good angle.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_n