 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Of the multitudinous insults that have zinged across the Capitol this year, a taunt most brutal was leveraged by the Republican leader, Senator Mitch McConnell of Kentucky on the Senate floor on Thursday night. He accused the Democratic leader, Senator Harry Reid of Nevada, of “fundamentally turning the Senate into the House.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/us/RULES-1/RULES-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/us/RULES-1/RULES-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/08/us/RULES-1/RULES-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Like Sharks vs. Jets as Senate Wrangles Over Vote, but Without Music', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Like Sharks vs. Jets as Senate Wrangles Over Vote, but Without Music', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T02:48:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99e5ced1-6474-5432-aff5-c250ce159d87', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99e5ced1-6474-5432-aff5-c250ce159d87'}, {'abstract': 'Adrian Beltre and Victor Martinez, teammates with the Red Sox last season, followed free agency to opposing sides in this year’s American League Championship Series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/sports/baseball/alcs-martinez-and-beltre-formerly-of-boston-will-meet.html', 'snippet': 'Adrian Beltre and Victor Martinez, teammates with the Red Sox last season, followed free agency to opposing sides in this year’s American League Championship Series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The teams that will play for the American League pennant both found unlikely sources for upgrading their lineups last winter. The Texas Rangers and the Detroit Tigers signed free agents cut loose by the Boston Red Sox.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/sports/y-alcs-2/y-alcs-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Let Go by Boston, Playing on Into October', 'kicker': 'Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Let Go by Boston, Playing On Into October', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '