procedures, is being contested.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A day after a government panel said that healthy men should no longer get screened for prostate cancer, some doctors’ groups and cancer patients’ advocates began a campaign to convince the nation that the advice was misguided.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Panel’s Advice on Prostate Test Sets Up Battle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panel&#8217;s Advice On Prostate Test Sets Up Battle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostate Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostate Specific Antigen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Preventive Services Task Force', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T03:14:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ded00a22-fd07-5656-a47b-2ee5285db1dd', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ded00a22-fd07-5656-a47b-2ee5285db1dd'}, {'abstract': 'Performance of treasury bonds, stocks, and the dollar since Standard & Poor’s downgraded United States treasury debt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/10/08/business/economy/effects-of-the-standard-and-poors-downgrade.html', 'snippet': 'Performance of treasury bonds, stocks, and the dollar since Standard & Poor’s downgraded United States treasury debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Performance of treasury bonds, stocks, and the dollar since Standard & Poor’s downgraded United States treasury debt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Effects of the Standard & Poor’s Downgrade', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T03:16:35+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/688992c0-5101-5a0e-ac08-add6079be94b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/688992c0-5101-5a0e-ac08-add6079be94b'}, {'abstract': 'Since Standard & Poor’s lowered the nation’s bond rating, Treasury bonds have been one of the few investments that have produced good profits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/business/after-a-rating-downgrade-us-treasuries-turn-a-profit.html', 'snippet': 'Since Standard & Poor’s lowered the nation’s bond rating, Treasury bonds have been one of the few investments that have produced good profits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TWO months ago, Standard & Poor’s downgraded the bond rating of the United States government. So far, at least, the move has done wonders for investors in the very bonds that the rating agency disparaged.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Rating Downgrade, U.S. Treasuries Turn a Profit', 'kicker': 'Off the Charts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After a Rating Downgrade, U.S. Treasuries Turn a Profit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'US Dollar (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T03:20:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef6125f4-050a-5d0c-934a-ab7187a3974b', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef6125f4-050a-5d0c-934a-ab7187a3974b'}, {'abstract': 'The Army general who found his career stalled after a profile of Gen. Stanley A. McChrystal appeared in Rolling Stone magazine, received his third star on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/us/generals-career-is-stalled-no-more.html', 'snippet': 'The Army general who found his career stalled after a profile of Gen. Stanley A. McChrystal appeared in Rolling Stone magazine, received his third star on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Army general who served as the military’s top intelligence officer in Afghanistan, but then found his career stalled after a controversial profile of Gen. Stanley A. McChrystal appeared in Rolling Stone magazine, received his third star on Friday as he became the assistant director of national intelligence. The officer, Lt. Gen. Michael T. Flynn, was the top intelligence officer for the Joint Chiefs of Staff before he joined General McChrystal in Kabul to oversee a revamping of the American-led mission in Afghanistan. He pioneered new intelligence techniques to understand terrorist and insurgent networks, and to track and attack their leadership. However, after General McChrystal was abruptly relieved of command by President Obama following the publication of the unflattering magazine profile, General Flynn saw his promotions frozen. But two official investigations, by the Defense Department and the Army, found no proof of any wrongdoing by General McChrystal or by anyone on his command staff. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'General’s Career Is Stalled No More', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'General’s Career Is Stalled No More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McChrystal, Stanley A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T03:22:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2793c345-776a-595f-a66d-dd2c6ac51feb', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2793c345-776a-595f-a66d-dd2c6ac51feb'}, {'abstract': 'The debt crisis in Greece continued to threaten to drag down Europe, the Occupy Wall Street protests gained union support, and Steven P. Jobs, the visionary co-founder of Apple, died.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/08/business/weekly-business-photos.html', 'snippet': 'The debt crisis in Greece continued to threaten to drag down Europe, the Occupy Wall Street protests gained union support, and Steven P. Jobs, the visionary co-founder of Apple, died.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The debt crisis in Greece continued to threaten to drag down Europe, the Occupy Wall Street protests gained union support, and Steven P. Jobs, the visionary co-founder of Apple, died.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/business/bizpix-slide-ZEBW/bizpix-slide-ZEBW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 619, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/business/bizpix-slide-ZEBW/bizpix-slide-ZEBW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/08/business/bizpix-slide-ZEBW/bizpix-slide-ZEBW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week’s Business News in Pictures', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T03:27:30+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ded0b6f4-8e01-5ae1-92ab-a7cef4f03b91', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ded0b6f4-8e01-5ae1-92ab-a7cef4f03b91'}, {'abstract': 'Despite a bumpy rookie year, Joe McKnight, a 2010 draft pick, has displayed his talent on offense, defense and special teams for the Jets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/sports/football/joe-mcknight-shows-the-athleticism-the-jets-needed.html', 'snippet': 'Despite a bumpy rookie year, Joe McKnight, a 2010 draft pick, has displayed his talent on offense, defense and special teams for the Jets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. — The Jets’ special-teams coach, Mike Westhoff, has just one guideline for those who return kickoffs: they need to be moving forward when they catch the ball. There are no invisible lines in the end zone that make a kickoff too deep to return.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/sports/city----jets/city----jets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/sports/city----jets/city----jets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/08/sports/city----jets/city----jets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'McKnight Showing the Athleticism the Jets Counted On', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'McKnight Showing the Athleticism the Jets Counted On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKnight, Joe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westhoff, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T03:27:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dafda3b1-1688-558c-bc53-e4163613af95', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dafda3b1-1688-558c-bc53-e4163613af95'}, {'abstract': 'So far, the Republican presidential candidates have been prone to occasional blunders when delving into foreign policy — that is, when they have had anything to say about the topic at all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/us/politics/in-gop-race-foreign-policy-is-mainly-a-footnote.html', 'snippet': 'So far, the Republican presidential candidates have been prone to occasional blunders when delving into foreign policy — that is, when they have had anything to say about the topic at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Herman Cain suggested that Israel’s conservative prime minister would be open to allowing Palestinians right of return to the lands they fled in what is now Israel. Gov. Rick Perry suggested it was possible that American troops could be sent to Mexico if drug violence there got worse. And former Senator Rick Santorum offered that the United States should engage with the ousted Pakistani dictator Pervez Musharraf — now living in self-exile in London — to respond to the threat of Pakistan’s nuclear weapons falling into the wrong hands. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/us/JP-POLICY/JP-POLICY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/08/us/JP-POLICY/JP-POLICY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/us/JP-POLICY/JP-POLICY-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/us/JP-POLICY/JP-POLICY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/08/us/JP-POLICY/JP-POLICY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In G.O.P. Race, Foreign Policy Is a Footnote', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In G.O.P. Race, Foreign Policy Is a Footnote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T03:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper and Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/085ad762-8d44-5dbb-9cb4-e579085c56f2', 'word_count': 1128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/085ad762-8d44-5dbb-9cb4-e579085c56f2'}, {'abstract': 'The Cardinals, who led the National League in runs scored, won the fifth game of their division series on Friday because their own ace, Chris Carpenter, beat the Phillies at their own game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/sports/baseball/cardinals-advance-by-beating-phillies-in-game-five.html', 'snippet': 'The Cardinals, who led the National League in runs scored, won the fifth game of their division series on Friday because their own ace, Chris Carpenter, beat the Phillies at their own game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — The Philadelphia Phillies banked their season on baseball’s most timeless adage: good pitching stops good hitting. It led them to 102 victories, the most in the history of the franchise. It would, they hoped, carry them to their second championship in four seasons.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carpenter Finishes Off the Phillies', 'kicker': 'Cardinals 1, Phillies 0', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Excitement Central', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Phillies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carpenter, Chris', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T03:43:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/794c88db-d63d-5f36-aec1-d90d306a39e7', 'word_count': 1136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/794c88db-d63d-5f36-aec1-d90d306a39e7'}, {'abstract': 'A United States task force’s recommendation against routine prostate-specific antigen testing for prostate cancer may lead to changes in insurance and practice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/health/policy/08consumer.html', 'snippet': 'A United States task force’s recommendation against routine prostate-specific antigen testing for prostate cancer may lead to changes in insurance and practice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Insurers and clinicians scrambled on Friday to decide whether to continue to offer routine P.S.A. tests following news that an influential panel of experts no longer recommended them for healthy men.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insurers Review Whether to Still Pay for Routine Screening', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Insurers Review Whether to Still Pay for Routine Screening', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostate Specific Antigen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostate Cancer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Preventive Services Task Force', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T03:52:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Quenqua', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quenqua', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0b7d8ef-789f-5bde-b085-27cf957495ee', 'word_count': 562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0b7d8ef-789f-5bde-b085-27cf957495ee'}, {'abstract': 'Prince Amukamara, the 19th overall draft pick, has been a spectator since breaking his left foot two days after signing a four-year contract with the Giants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/sports/football/for-giants-amukamara-waiting-is-part-of-the-game.html', 'snippet': 'Prince Amukamara, the 19th overall draft pick, has been a spectator since breaking his left foot two days after signing a four-year contract with the Giants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — The arrival of the rookie Giants cornerback Prince Amukamara has been little more than a tease to this point. He has been at practices, but not practicing. He has been a part of the team, but not a part of the action.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Waiting Is Painful for Giants’ Top Pick', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Waiting Is Painful For Giants’ Top Pick', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Amukamara, Prince', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baas, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T03:54:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Viera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/560a8b75-da92-5ba3-9b07-09beb475e4f4', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/560a8b75-da92-5ba3