ediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/07/swashbuckling-times-in-los-angeles/', 'snippet': 'Perhaps it’s a yearning for better times, but the 17th century is suddenly very much in vogue in Hollywood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — On the contemporary streets of Los Angeles this past week, it became obvious, via billboards and bus posters everywhere, that Hollywood had developed a sudden fascination with the 17th Century. High and low, the symbols were there: swords, doublets and big floppy hats with a jaunty tilt. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Swashbuckling Times in Los Angeles', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Capote, Truman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ifans, Rhys', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Searchlight Pictures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T03:59:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79c9ec69-34f0-5dce-8aa9-63d9836473d8', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79c9ec69-34f0-5dce-8aa9-63d9836473d8'}, {'abstract': 'Among the many Libyans who took sides, and even took up arms, in the country’s civil war were members of its national soccer team.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/split-by-war-libyas-team-reunites-with-a-new-goal/', 'snippet': 'Among the many Libyans who took sides, and even took up arms, in the country’s civil war were members of its national soccer team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the many Libyans who took sides in the country’s civil war were members of its national soccer team. A former captain of the team called the anti-Qaddafi rebels rats and dogs, while several of his teammates took up arms against the crumbling government. James Montague visited the reconstituted team in Zambia, where on Saturday it will try to clinch a berth in next year’s African Cup of Nations. Read his article here, and come back to comment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Split by War, Libya’s Team Reunites With a New Goal', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T04:01:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40be7f2e-a5ea-5e73-9f20-7767ea4422ca', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40be7f2e-a5ea-5e73-9f20-7767ea4422ca'}, {'abstract': 'An artist who designed and maintains the grounds of Grey Gardens worked to preserve the spirit of the home’s original occupants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2009/04/16/garden/20090416-greygardens-slideshow_index.html', 'snippet': 'An artist who designed and maintains the grounds of Grey Gardens worked to preserve the spirit of the home’s original occupants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An artist who designed and maintains the grounds of Grey Gardens worked to preserve the spirit of the home’s original occupants.', 'source': 'The New 