 'uri': 'nyt://video/a40d9a68-a1eb-503c-954b-0acce7247776'}, {'abstract': 'New York Times readers sit atop the Start/Sit Accuracy Challenge  at FantasyPros.com', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/after-4-weeks-the-2011-top-fantasy-football-experts/', 'snippet': 'New York Times readers sit atop the Start/Sit Accuracy Challenge  at FantasyPros.com', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times has a reputation for having an intellectually advanced readership. Who would have thought, though, that this high I.Q. would also apply to fantasy football predictions? The readers of this blog happen to be sitting atop our Start/Sit Accuracy Challenge, which tracks how accurate several communities are at making our most difficult “Who should I start?” decisions. Congratulations on the strong showing thus far.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After 4 Weeks, the 2011 Top Fantasy Football Experts', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T04:20:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Kim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f48bf57-8e0e-59a2-8731-f1f12e10b0a4', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f48bf57-8e0e-59a2-8731-f1f12e10b0a4'}, {'abstract': 'The five-stage Tour of Beijing, which ends Sunday, is the first major attempt by professional cycling to establish itself in China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/sports/cycling/tour-of-beijing-establishes-professional-cycling-in-china.html', 'snippet': 'The five-stage Tour of Beijing, which ends Sunday, is the first major attempt by professional cycling to establish itself in China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago, the roads in and around Beijing were clogged by bicycles. Last week, however, the cars, trucks and buses that are the city’s new source of congestion were cleared away to make room for cyclists. But cyclists of an elite variety.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/sports/cycling-1/cycling-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/08/sports/cycling-1/cycling-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/sports/cycling-1/cycling-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/08/sports/cycling-1/cycling-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/08/sports/cycling-1/cycling-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Contentious Ride Into Beijing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Contentious Ride Into Beijing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Cycling Union', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HTC-Highroad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles a