6e2d'}, {'abstract': 'Top news from the regional press this week.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/newswallah-bharat-edition-5/', 'snippet': 'Top news from the regional press this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jammu and Kashmir: An uncensored video clip of two senior leaders hurling abuses at each other in the Jammu and Kashmir Assembly on Monday has gone viral in the Valley.\xa0 The 141-second long clip, in Kasmiri, of the bitter exchange between Assembly Speaker Mohammad Akbar Lone and members of the opposition party MLA, has been featured on hundreds of Facebook pages. (Kashmir Live)Haryana: The local administration in the Karnal district of Haryana launched a Facebook campaign to protect females. The impetus behind the drive is to raise youth awareness about the social fallout of a skewed sex ratio. (The Tribune)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Bharat Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singh, Manmohan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ganges River', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T07:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8b6dd62-62f6-5a44-b1ec-b0e7437d2c37', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8b6dd62-62f6-5a44-b1ec-b0e7437d2c37'}, {'abstract': 'Looking back at Friday’s results in Euro 2012 and World Cup qualifying.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/all-the-colors-of-fridays-qualifiers/', 'snippet': 'Looking back at Friday’s results in Euro 2012 and World Cup qualifying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s tough to wrap up 24 qualifying games in a comprehensive way, so let’s hit the highlights with a spin around the color wheel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All the Colors of Friday’s Qualifiers', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T08:20:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0f1fa76-5d46-5d94-b71c-9c96fec14b11', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0f1fa76-5d46-5d94-b71c-9c96fec14b11'}, {'abstract': 'An exciting qualifying session with a mixture of action at the front and some cars taking a break, there was also a controversy between Lewis Hamilton and two other drivers.', 'web_url': 'https://formulaone.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/sweet-and-sour-suzuka-qualifying-session/', 'snippet': 'An exciting qualifying session with a mixture of action at the front and some cars taking a break, there was also a controversy between Lewis Hamilton and two other drivers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUZUKA, Japan – We finally we had an interesting qualifying session for the front-runners. Never mind that Sebastian Vettel took the pole position again, his 12th in the 15 possible this season. The last laps of the session were worth the wait to watch the suspense as the leading drivers crossed the line probably the thickness of a sheet of paper apart: Jenson Button, who was fastest in every one of the three practice sessions this weekend, lost the pole position to Vettel by a few thousandths of a second.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sweet and Sour Suzuka Qualifying Session', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Button, Jenson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Lewis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vettel, Sebastian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T08:54:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d68d9af-a42b-5bf3-b414-d8f8e5cce1d7', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d68d9af-a42b-5bf3-b414-d8f8e5cce1d7'}, {'abstract': 'An exciting qualifying session with a mixture of action at the front and some cars taking a break, there was also a controversy between Lewis Hamilton and two other drivers.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/sweet-and-sour-suzuka-qualifying-session/', 'snippet': 'An exciting qualifying session with a mixture of action at the front and some cars taking a break, there was also a controversy between Lewis Hamilton and two other drivers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUZUKA, Japan – We finally we had an interesting qualifying session for the front-runners. Never mind that Sebastian Vettel took the pole position again, his 12th in the 15 possible this season. The last laps of the session were worth the wait to watch the suspense as the leading drivers crossed the line probably the thickness of a sheet of paper apart: Jenson Button, who was fastest in every one of the three practice sessions this weekend, lost the pole position to Vettel by a few thousandths of a second.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sweet and Sour Suzuka Qualifying Session', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Button, Jenson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Lewis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vettel, Sebastian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T08:54:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48d51b37-c7a5-53ca-bb2e-bca1d1b0b103', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48d51b37-c7a5-53ca-bb2e-bca1d1b0b103'}, {'abstract': 'The deaths of Thomas Edison and Steve Jobs brought outpourings of public grief, but while both were celebrated for their genius, Mr. Jobs was also remembered for his humanity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/business/an-analogy-of-thomas-edison-and-steve-jobs.html', 'snippet': 'The deaths of Thomas Edison and Steve Jobs brought outpourings of public grief, but while both were celebrated for their genius, Mr. Jobs was also remembered for his humanity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN August 1931, Thomas Alva Edison, age 84, became gravely ill with kidney problems. He recovered a little, then suffered a setback and was confined to bed at home, drifting in and out of consciousness. Newspapers issued multiple bulletins each day, reporting on signs of improvement or decline. The end came in the early morning of Oct. 18, 1931, with his family at his bedside.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/business/digi/digi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 820, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/business/digi/digi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/business/digi/digi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wizard and the Mortal: Two Sides of Genius', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Power of Taking the Big Chance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edison, Thomas A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T12:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randall Stross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randall', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c279bd00-6d5e-506f-8f6c-83a2