ups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JAKARTA, Indonesia — The Indonesian police arrested three men on Saturday and accused them of plotting two suicide attacks in the last six months that injured scores of people.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3 in Indonesia Charged With Plotting Suicide Attacks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Three Held Over Attacks In Indonesia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bashir, Abu Bakar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jemaah Islamiyah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T13:35:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Schonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d450e021-2cc4-51f5-80d4-35e029eb1579', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d450e021-2cc4-51f5-80d4-35e029eb1579'}, {'abstract': 'On walking AND chewing gum.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/ah-yes-lm-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'On walking AND chewing gum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brad DeLong, Mark Thoma, Matt Rognlie, and others are debating the usefulness of the textbook IS-LM model. So, my inflation-adjusted two cents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ah Yes, LM (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T13:37:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdd6c045-e4b0-5fad-85dd-8f10dc783e6b', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdd6c045-e4b0-5fad-85dd-8f10dc783e6b'}, {'abstract': 'Clark Gillies, 57, was a key player when the Islanders won four consecutive Stanley Cups from 1980 to 1983.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/30-seconds-with-clark-gillies-ex-star-hopes-isles-shine/', 'snippet': 'Clark Gillies, 57, was a key player when the Islanders won four consecutive Stanley Cups from 1980 to 1983.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Clark Gillies, a former Islanders star, rang the Nasdaq closing bell recently, and the bell survived. In fact, the market jumped after Gillies, a rare player who could fight as well as shoot and skate skillfully, performed the honors. Gillies, 57, was a key player when the Islanders won four consecutive Stanley Cups from 1980 to 1983. A member of the Hockey Hall of Fame, he was recently honored at the 26th Annual Great Sports Legends Dinner to benefit The Buoniconti Fund to Cure Paralysis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '30 Seconds With Clark Gillies: Ex-Star Hopes Isles Shine', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillies, Clark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Islanders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T13:59:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Brescia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brescia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/939118d0-93c8-567e-965e-5352ab1acebc', 'word_count': 1077, 'uri': 'nyt://article/939118d0-93c8-567e-965e-5352ab1acebc'}, {'abstract': 'The director behind the Christian-themed “Courageous” talks about moviemaking as ministry.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/praying-then-producing-a-hit/', 'snippet': 'The director behind the Christian-themed “Courageous” talks about moviemaking as ministry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many directors think of their work as a kind of religion, but few actually refer to their production company as “a moviemaking ministry” — unless of course they are the people behind Sherwood Pictures. The Georgia-based Sherwood Baptist Church has released four films, and its latest, “Courageous,” has shown once again that it has a way with Christian audiences. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Praying, Then Producing a Hit', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T14:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/243fe30d-9711-5201-a2f1-8f57a4a6e97d', 'word_count': 1438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/243fe30d-9711-5201-a2f1-8f57a4a6e97d'}, {'abstract': 'Justice David H. Souter, the 105th justice to be appointed to the Supreme Court, plans to retire in June after more than 18 years on the court, people informed about the decision said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/s