ork Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/sports/winnepeg-1/winnepeg-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/09/sports/winnepeg-1/winnepeg-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/sports/winnepeg-1/winnepeg-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/sports/winnepeg-1/winnepeg-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/sports/winnepeg-1/winnepeg-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giddy Winnipeg Reclaims Lost Prairie Companion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giddy Winnipeg Reclaims Lost Prairie Companion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Winnipeg Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T17:38:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/803bc778-6260-548b-a46f-b577b0452953', 'word_count': 1431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/803bc778-6260-548b-a46f-b577b0452953'}, {'abstract': 'Dozens of Afghan lawmakers ended their boycott on Saturday, with no resolution to their grievances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/world/asia/lawmakers-end-boycott-of-parliament-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Dozens of Afghan lawmakers ended their boycott on Saturday, with no resolution to their grievances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Near the white tent where an ousted Afghan lawmaker lay moaning in bed, slowly starving herself in political protest, her onetime colleagues in Parliament congratulated themselves Saturday on their decision to return to work.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/world/09afghanistan/09afghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/09/world/09afghanistan/09afghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/world/09afghanistan/09afghanistan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/world/09afghanistan/09afghanistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/world/09afghanistan/09afghanistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawmakers End Boycott of Parliament in Afghanistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawmakers End Boycott Of the Afghan Parliament', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T17:40:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e630c72-f7fa-57bd-90cb-81266685db45', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e630c72-f7fa-57bd-90cb-81266685db45'}, {'abstract': 'They are used to getting fired, but caddie Joe LaCava left the fifth-ranked Dustin Johnson to take the bag for Tiger Woods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/sports/golf/job-security-not-for-pgas-caddies.html', 'snippet': 'They are used to getting fired, but caddie Joe LaCava left the fifth-ranked Dustin Johnson to take the bag for Tiger Woods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN MARTIN, Calif. — The caddie Joe LaCava was standing outside the scoring trailer waiting for postround instructions from his new boss, Tiger Woods. Scattered showers, which were in the forecast, and sprayed shots, which were not, had dampened LaCava’s debut with Woods at the Frys.com Open. Cutting through the postround gloom, Woods’s agent, Mark Steinberg, approached LaCava and wryly congratulated him on his first round. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/sports/cad