e deal.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/08/sony-is-said-to-buy-film-rights-to-jobs-biography/', 'snippet': 'Sony Pictures Entertainment has concluded a deal to buy film  rights to the authorized biography “Steve Jobs,” from Walter Isaacson, according to a person who was briefed on the deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Sony Pictures Entertainment, the studio that the produced high-speed and high-profile movies “This Is It,” with Michael Jackson, and “The Social Network,” about Mark Zuckerberg, could do it again with the Apple co-founder Steven P. Jobs. The studio late this week concluded a deal to buy film rights to the authorized biography “Steve Jobs,” from Walter Isaacson, according to a person who was briefed on the deal and spoke on the condition of anonymity because the studio had not authorized a public statement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sony Is Said to Buy Film Rights to Jobs Biography', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Steve Jobs (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isaacson, Walter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Pictures Entertainment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T19:34:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/464e9d4a-233d-5cdf-a0b6-e018f4326efc', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/464e9d4a-233d-5cdf-a0b6-e018f4326efc'}, {'abstract': 'Freezing in the glare of the nation’s economic problems is understandable, but it’s seldom the most effective strategy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/business/economy/too-much-caution-hinders-a-turnaround.html', 'snippet': 'Freezing in the glare of the nation’s economic problems is understandable, but it’s seldom the most effective strategy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BY any measure, the global economy is facing unusually high levels of uncertainty and volatility. But human nature may be impeding our ability to turn the economy around. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/business/09-VIEW/09-VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 731, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/business/09-VIEW/09-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/business/09-VIEW/09-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Deer in the Headlights, Financially Speaking', 'kicker': 'Economic View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deer in the Headlights, Financially Speaking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of R