ck Market', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clamping Down On Rapid Trades In Stock Market', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Frequency and Flash Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T21:49:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f06caff-fba1-5458-88a4-e29abb54f869', 'word_count': 1223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f06caff-fba1-5458-88a4-e29abb54f869'}, {'abstract': 'In the last year, Oakland schools have introduced and expanded a host of programs, some federally subsidized, to feed students at school and home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/us/oakland-schools-expanding-free-meal-programs.html', 'snippet': 'In the last year, Oakland schools have introduced and expanded a host of programs, some federally subsidized, to feed students at school and home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent Saturday morning, some 60 teachers and nurses from the Oakland Unified School District gathered at Tilden Education Complex for a daylong seminar on nutrition education.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/us/09BCBREAKFAST2/09BCBREAKFAST2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 607, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/us/09BCBREAKFAST2/09BCBREAKFAST2-thumbSta