 New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Irascible and Influential Al Davis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Raiders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T22:07:32+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/3ec00afa-93cb-5e6d-b0c7-e8a2717b082f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/3ec00afa-93cb-5e6d-b0c7-e8a2717b082f'}, {'abstract': 'One court program to help keep offenders from returning to prison has had a 100 percent success rate; another, 88 percent. Both are being eliminated because of budget cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/us/parole-and-probation-courts-in-san-francisco-are-closing-after-budget-cuts.html', 'snippet': 'One court program to help keep offenders from returning to prison has had a 100 percent success rate; another, 88 percent. Both are being eliminated because of budget cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Judge Jeffrey Tauber stood in his San Francisco courtroom late last month and addressed more than 25 felons. “I’m truly apologizing that I’ve not been able to fulfill my commitment and promise to you,” he said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/us/sub09BCPAROLE/sub09BCPAROLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Parole and Probation Courts in San Francisco Are Closing After Budget Cuts', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Parole and Probation Courts Are Closing After Budget Cuts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Probation and Parole', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tauber, Jeffrey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-08T22:15:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trey Bundy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bundy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98cfebcf-0c2d-5b30-9da5-84b514d67907', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98cfebcf-0c2d-5b30-9da5-84b514d67907'}, {'abstract': 'The protests that began on Wall Street have struck a chord, and on Monday a coalition of Chicago groups will demonstrate outside meetings held by the Mortgage Bankers and Futures Industry Associations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/us/in-chicago-banking-and-futures-industry-protests-planned.html', 'snippet': 'The protests that began on Wall Street have struck a chord, and on Monday a coalition of Chicago groups will demonstrate outside meetings held by the Mortgage Bankers and Futures Industry Associations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At an August training session for Action Now, an advocacy group for the poor, Madeline Talbott, the lead organizer, handed out a copy of the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.’s “Letter From Birmingham Jail,” an impassioned plea for “people of good will” to join the fight for freedom and human rights.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url