ir-stocks.html', 'snippet': 'In the last economic slowdown, stock markets of countries like China, India and Brazil fared worse than their generally healthy economies. Could that change in the next downturn?', 'lead_paragraph': 'IDEAS that come into vogue and fail to pan out may not be wrong, just early. Is “decoupling” one of those ideas, and has its time come at last?', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/business/09-MF-EMERGE1/09-MF-EMERGE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/09/business/09-MF-EMERGE1/09-MF-EMERGE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/business/09-MF-EMERGE1/09-MF-EMERGE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/business/09-MF-EMERGE1/09-MF-EMERGE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/business/09-MF-EMERGE1/09-MF-EMERGE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Surging Economies, in Search of Surging Stocks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surging Economies, In Search Of Surging Stocks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations',