5c4115fb-1fea-5b39-a905-77356858f388', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c4115fb-1fea-5b39-a905-77356858f388'}, {'abstract': '“Cheerful Insanity” is a repertory production of two confessional plays, “Callous Cad” by Tom X. Chao and “Penetrating the Space” by Kim Katzberg.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/theater/reviews/cheerful-insanity-here-arts-center-review.html', 'snippet': '“Cheerful Insanity” is a repertory production of two confessional plays, “Callous Cad” by Tom X. Chao and “Penetrating the Space” by Kim Katzberg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Romantic and sexual trauma pervade “Cheerful Insanity: Chao and Katzberg in Repertory,” two plays of contrasting sensibilities at the Here Arts Center. Each barely an hour and running on different dates, they are both confessional in nature and intriguing.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/arts/Cheer/Cheer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Support From a Love Sprite and Some Fractured Friends', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Cheerful Insanity'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Support From a Love Sprite And Some Fractured Friends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-09T19:02:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2362db9d-f288-5f29-8d5f-5ddc7d2836f1', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2362db9d-f288-5f29-8d5f-5ddc7d2836f1'}, {'abstract': 'Sir Paul McCartney married Nancy Shevell in a small civil ceremony on Sunday at Marylebone Town Hall in London.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/paul-mccartney-marries-again/', 'snippet': 'Sir Paul McCartney married Nancy Shevell in a small civil ceremony on Sunday at Marylebone Town Hall in London.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Beatles fans now have two reasons to toast to their favorite band each Oct. 9: On what would have been John Lennon’s 71st birthday, Sir Paul McCartney married Nancy Shevell in a small civil ceremony on Sunday at Marylebone Town Hall in London, The Associated Press reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul McCartney Marries Again', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCartney, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shevell, Nancy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-09T19:05:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65cec455-fa00-5373-ae5a-3465b27f25ac', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65cec455-fa00-5373-ae5a-3465b27f25ac'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a good thing.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/is-lmentary/', 'snippet': 'It’s a good thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A number of readers, both at this blog and other places, have been asking for an explanation of what IS-LM is all about. Fair enough – this blogosphere conversation has been an exchange among insiders, and probably a bit baffling to normal human beings (which is why I have been labeling my posts “wonkish”).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'IS-LMentary', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-09T19:14:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6014ab51-6f65-5431-81ea-1a5c4a321cd7', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6014ab51-6f65-5431-81ea-1a5c4a321cd7'}, {'abstract': 'Charting the win probability in Sunday’s Jets-Patriots game.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/week-5-live-jets-patriots-win-probability/', 'snippet': 'Charting the win probability in Sunday’s Jets-Patriots game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Fifth Down has done several times already this season, we will be using a Web feature from Advanced NFL Stats that charts win probability live during today’s Jets-Patriots game. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week 5 Live: Jets-Patriots Win Probability', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-09T19:30:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13156b58-e8d7-561e-8384-6c9c2d7a4d40', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13156b58-e8d7-561e-8384-6c9c2d7a4d40'}, {'abstract': 'Maybe, but trying couldn’t and can’t hurt.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/was-failure-inevitable/', 'snippet': 'Maybe, but trying couldn’t and can’t hurt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ezra Klein has a generally reasonable analysis of the Obama administration’s failure to respond with sufficient force to the economic crisis. Broadly speaking, he’s saying that the eurovenn applied: an economically adequate response lay beyond the bounds of the politically feasible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Was Failure Inevitable?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-09T19:36:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/541ef262-4b35-5fe1-950c-792191c70646', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/541ef262-4b35-5fe1-950c-792191c70646'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands packed into a stadium in Mogadishu to denounce the Shabab Islamist group for the suicide bombing last week that killed scores of people, many of them students.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/world/africa/in-rare-rally-somalis-protest-shabab.html', 'snippet': 'Thousands packed into a stadium in Mogadishu to denounce the Shabab Islamist group for the suicide bombing last week that killed scores of people, many of them students.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOGADISHU, Somalia — Thousands of residents of this bullet-scarred city packed into a stadium on Sunday to denounce the Shabab Islamist group for the suicide bombing last week that killed scores of people, many of them students.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Rare Rally, Somalis Aim at Militants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Rare Rally, Somalis Aim At Militants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mogadishu (Somalia)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-09T19:39:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By MOHAMED IBRAHIM and JEFFREY GETTLEMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mohamed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'IBRAHIM', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'GETTLEMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19132aca-aa94-598a-9696-d2992ef3e7d7', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19132aca-aa94-598a-9696-d2992ef3e7d7'}, {'abstract': 'Syria warned foreign countries on Sunday not to recognize a newly formed opposition group, the Syrian National Council, and threatened to take “strict measures” against any country that does.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/world/middleeast/syria-warns-countries-not-to-recognize-opposition.html', 'snippet': 'Syria warned foreign countries on Sunday not to recognize a newly formed opposition group, the Syrian National Council, and threatened to take “strict measures” against any country that does.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Syria warned countries on Sunday not to recognize a new opposition group, the Syrian National Council, and threatened to take “strict measures” against any that did.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/world/10syria-image/10syria-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/world/10syria-image/10syria-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/10/world/10syria-image/10syria-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria Demands That Nations Reject Opposition Council and Protect Its Embassies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria Demands That Nations Reject Opposition Council and Protect Its Embassies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-09T20:03:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Bakri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a57a4d4-c1bd-50ec-9e06-9326512cdb64', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a57a4d4-c1bd-50ec-9e06-9326512cdb64'}, {'abstract': 'Game 2 of the A.L.C.S. is postponed because of rain.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/a-l-c-s-game-2-postponed/', 'snippet': 'Game 2 of the A.L.C.S. is postponed because of rain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After two rain delays interrupted Game 1 of the American League Championship Series on Saturday night, Major League Baseball did not take any chances on Sunday. With more rain expected Sunday night, Game 2 of the series between the Texas Rangers and the Detroit Tigers was postponed Sunday afternoon, about seven hours before the scheduled first pitch. It was rescheduled for Monday afternoon at 4:19 Eastern. Tigers Manager Jim Leyland also announced that right fielder Magglio Ordonez injured his right ankle in Game 1 and is out for the rest of the postseason. More details are available here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A.L.C.S. Game 2 Postponed', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN LEAGUE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-09T20:07:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccb30f31-d1af-538a-a8c1-f3098a5b3dc3', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccb30f31-d1af-538a-a8c1-f3098a5b3dc3'}, {'abstract': 'In most respects Christopher Hitchens is undiminished, preferring to see himself as living with cancer, not dying from it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/books/christopher-hitchens-on-writing-mortality-and-cancer.html', 'snippet': 'In most respects Christopher Hitchens is undiminished, preferring to see himself as living with cancer, not dying from it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — Christopher Hitchens, probably the country’s most famous unbeliever, received the Freethinker of the Year Award at the annual convention of the Atheist Alliance of America here on Saturday. Mr. Hitchens was flattered by the honor, he said a few days beforehand, but also a little abashed. “I think being an atheist is something you are, not something you do,” he explained, adding: “I’m not sure we need to be honored. We don’t need positive reinforcement. On the other hand, we do need to stick up for ourselves, especially in a place like Texas, where they have laws, I think, that if you don’t believe in Jesus Christ you can’t run for sheriff.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/arts/10hitchens-337/10hitchens-337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/arts/10hitchens-337/10hitchens-337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/10/arts/10hitchens-337/10hitchens-337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Voice, Still Vibrant, Reflects on Mortality', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Voice, Still Vibrant, Reflects on Mortality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitchens, Christopher', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-09T20:12:21+0000', 'document_t