onal publisher, has financed free international trips for education commissioners whose states do business with the company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/education/10winerip.html', 'snippet': 'The Pearson Foundation, the nonprofit arm of a major educational publisher, has financed free international trips for education commissioners whose states do business with the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since 2008, the Pearson Foundation, the nonprofit arm of one of the nation’s largest educational publishers, has financed free international trips — some have called them junkets — for education commissioners whose states do business with the company. When the state commissioners are asked about these trips — to Rio de Janeiro; London; Singapore; and Helsinki, Finland — they emphasize the time they spend with educators from around the world to get ideas for improving American public schools.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Free Trips Raise Issues for Officials in Education', 'kicker': 'On Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Free Trips Raise Issues For Officials In Education', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pearson Foundation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pearson PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Procurement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council of Chief State School Officers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-09T23:26:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wineri