particularly the young, the poor, the elderly, and minorities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/opinion/the-myth-of-voter-fraud.html', 'snippet': 'New restrictions on voting are really intended to keep people who vote Democratic from the polls, particularly the young, the poor, the elderly, and minorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been a record year for new legislation designed to make it harder for Democrats to vote — 19 laws and two executive actions in 14 states dominated by Republicans, according to a new study by the Brennan Center for Justice. As a result, more than five million eligible voters will have a harder time participating in the 2012 election.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Myth of Voter Fraud', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Myth of Voter Fraud: New restrictions on voting are really intended to keep Democrats from the polls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T01:35:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9c9631f-e11a-50ce-a0e2-2de7c154ee2e', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9c9631f-e11a-50ce-a0e2-2de7c154ee2e'}, {'abstract': 'The state of New York spends an average of $18,126 annually a student, and a group is seeking an additional $4,750 annually for every poor student.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/education/10equity.html', 'snippet': 'The state of New York spends an average of $18,126 annually a student, and a group is seeking an additional $4,750 annually for every poor student.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York State already outspends the rest of the nation on education, and a group of education experts at Teachers College at Columbia University is calling for it to spend even more.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Group Urges More Money to Aid Poor in School', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Group Urges More Money To Aid Poor In School', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Teachers College of Columbia University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rebell, Michael A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T01:37:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d524bb4d-218d-5ab8-8964-bd1a6b5b6f67', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d524bb4d-218d-5ab8-8964-bd1a6b5b6f67'}, {'abstract': 'The cable news channel, given little chance of succeeding in 1996, is celebrating its anniversary this month with a national tour.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/business/media/fox-news-and-hannity-at-the-top-after-15-years.html', 'snippet': 'The cable news channel, given little chance of succeeding in 1996, is celebrating its anniversary this month with a national tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — When the Fox News host Sean Hannity arrived at Centennial Olympic Park here on Thursday night, some of the hundreds of fans who had been waiting for him since sunset rushed to the rope line for handshakes and autographs. He obliged, then bounded onto a temporary stage two blocks from the CNN Center and asked them mischievously, “Do you think it’s any coincidence that the CNN logo is in the background?”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/business/FOX/FOX-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/10/business/FOX/FOX-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/business/FOX/FOX-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/business/FOX/FOX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/10/business/FOX/FOX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Victory Lap for Fox and Hannity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Victory Lap for Fox and Hannity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hannity, Sean', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T01:37:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cf04612-43ad-564e-977f-2554593e1ecb', 'word_count': 1360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cf04612-43ad-564e-977f-2554593e1ecb'}, {'abstract': 'Expanding trade agreements with South Korea, Colombia and Panama and helping displaced workers are both good for the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/opinion/a-deal-for-the-trade-deals.html', 'snippet': 'Expanding trade agreements with South Korea, Colombia and Panama and helping displaced workers are both good for the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trade is good for the economy and for employment. It opens new markets for businesses and allows access to cheaper, often better products from abroad. But it also has a dark side for workers displaced by foreign competition. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Deal for the Deals', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Deal for the Deals: Expanding trade and helping displaced workers are both good for the country', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panama', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T01:41:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce7b7030-8f30-5eb4-9ce9-70d31567d737', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce7b7030-8f30-5eb4-9ce9-70d31567d737'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Santo Domingo’s $8.5 billion fortune made him one of Latin America’s richest and most influential men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/world/americas/julio-mario-santo-domingo-colombian-billionaire-dies-at-87.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Santo Domingo’s $8.5 billion fortune made him one of Latin America’s richest and most influential men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIO DE JANEIRO — Julio Mario Santo Domingo, the Colombian magnate whose $8.5 billion fortune made him one of Latin America’s richest and most influential men, died on Friday in New York. He was 87. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/world/americas/domingo-obit/domingo-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 571, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/world/americas/domingo-obit/domingo-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/10/world/americas/domingo-obit/domingo-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Julio Mario Santo Domingo, Colombian Billionaire, Dies at 87', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Julio Mario Santo Domingo, 87, Colombian Billionaire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T01:43:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8526976-0039-5082-aee9-3b9605a7a972', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8526976-0039-5082-aee9-3b9605a7a972'}, {'abstract': 'The ruling by the Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia to ban possession of assault weapons was careful and convincing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/opinion/no-right-to-bear-assault-weapons.html', 'snippet': 'The ruling by the Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia to ban possession of assault weapons was careful and convincing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia last week persuasively  ruled that the Constitution allows the District to ban possession of assault weapons and high-capacity magazines of bullets and to require citizens to meet sensible standards for registering guns.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Right to Bear Assault Weapons', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Right to Bear Assault Weapons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': '