tandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Navigating the City Without Sight, but With a Cane and a Teacher', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eyes and Eyesight', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lighthouse International', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kramer, Karen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T01:50:33+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/bb125a59-73d6-53eb-9828-28444aba492a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/bb125a59-73d6-53eb-9828-28444aba492a'}, {'abstract': 'From about 1905 until the 1950s, West 98th and 99th Streets constituted something of a miniature Harlem, with its own Renaissance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/nyregion/reunion-for-a-vanished-neighborhood.html', 'snippet': 'From about 1905 until the 1950s, West 98th and 99th Streets constituted something of a miniature Harlem, with its own Renaissance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The reunion at the Frederick Douglass Center in Manhattan on Saturday had all the trappings of a block party. About 75 people turned out, greeting one another with smiles, hugs and questions about neighbors and family. They ate chicken, macaroni and cheese and cake while a man blew soulful melodies on an alto saxophone.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/nyregion/nabe1/nabe1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/10/nyregion/nabe1/nabe1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/nyregion/nabe1/nabe1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Community Erased by Slum Clearance Is Reunited', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Community Erased by Slum Clearance Is Reunited', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moses, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T01:51:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Schweber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c9c71f5-95e4-5287-86ca-7a178faf28a8', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c9c71f5-95e4-5287-86ca-7a178faf28a8'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Belack was a stage and television actress best known for her roles as a “Law & Order” judge and as a soap opera producer in “Tootsie” with Dustin Hoffman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/arts/television/doris-belack-judge-on-tvs-law-order-dies-at-85.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Belack was a stage and television actress best known for her roles as a “Law & Order” judge and as a soap opera producer in “Tootsie” with Dustin Hoffman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Doris Belack, a veteran stage, television and screen actress best known for her roles as a no-nonsense judge on “Law & Order” and as the peeved soap opera producer in “Tootsie,” died on Tuesday in New York. She was 85. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/arts/belack-obit/belack-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/arts/belack-obit/belack-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/10/arts/belack-obit/belack-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Doris Belack, Judge on TV’s ‘Law & Order,’ Dies at 85', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Doris Belack, 85, Actress in Theater and on TV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T01:56:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Vitello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vitello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/545fb6d5-381e-537d-b57b-dfa3be3a50c3', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/545fb6d5-381e-537d-b57b-dfa3be3a50c3'}, {'abstract': 'Ernie Els, who hasn’t won a tournament this year, saw progress at the Frys.com Open, which was won in a playoff by Bryce Molder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/sports/golf/els-sees-a-lot-of-life-left-in-his-game.html', 'snippet': 'Ernie Els, who hasn’t won a tournament this year, saw progress at the Frys.com Open, which was won in a playoff by Bryce Molder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN MARTIN, Calif. — All the attention was on Tiger Woods at the Frys.com Open, which suited Ernie Els fine. Like Woods, Els came to CordeValle Golf Club looking for his lost game, and he preferred not to be accompanied by an unwieldy search party of fans and pundits.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/sports/golf-1/golf-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 953, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/sports/golf-1/golf-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/10/sports/golf-1/golf-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Els Sees a Lot of Life Left in His Game', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Els Sees a Lot of Life Left in His Game', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PGA Tour Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Els, Ernie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Molder, Bryce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baird, Briny', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T01:56:17+0000', 'document_type':