pps for Children', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Club Penguin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T13:48:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Warren Buckleitner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Warren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckleitner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a8a8294-b8af-5ea7-9259-343e0ba45dd6', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a8a8294-b8af-5ea7-9259-343e0ba45dd6'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not centrist when Democrats do it.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/the-invisible-center/', 'snippet': 'It’s not centrist when Democrats do it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A question to which I think I know the answer: A number of my colleagues in the commentariat write longingly about the need for a “centrist” who will propose doing what needs to be done — combine short-run stimulus with long-term measures that will reduce the deficit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Invisible Center', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T13:51:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54e8cea8-0dc9-530e-93bb-aa0160e5c396', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54e8cea8-0dc9-530e-93bb-aa0160e5c396'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not the most exciting product category, but label printers are the unsung heroes of home organization. Epson has some new models out.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/new-label-printer-hotness/', 'snippet': 'It’s not the most exciting product category, but label printers are the unsung heroes of home organization. Epson has some new models out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s no glory in writing about label printers. Yet today will end and tomorrow the sun will rise and millions will look at the unlabeled boxes and cartons in their junk closet and say “I wish I had some way of labeling those.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Label-Printer Hotness!', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Printers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Epson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T14:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Biggs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Biggs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccf48417-2e5f-54a8-9214-6abfa052ff61', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccf48417-2e5f-54a8-9214-6abfa052ff61'}, {'abstract': 'When I heard there was a kind man in Midtown who erase my fine lines (without toxins or fillers) in under an hour, I snagged the first available appointment.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/stick-it-to-me/', 'snippet': 'When I heard there was a kind man in Midtown who erase my fine lines (without toxins or fillers) in under an hour, I snagged the first available appointment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I didn’t think I was a good candidate for facial acupuncture. For one thing, the only time I’m perfectly still is when I’m asleep (or getting an expensive haircut). And quite frankly, if I’m going to be stuck with needles, I would like them to deliver the kind of instant gratification that only Botox can provide. That said, when I heard there was a kind man in Midtown who would listen to my problems (but not judge me), calm me down (without meds) and erase my fine lines (without toxins or fillers), all in under an hour, I snagged the first available appointment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stick It to Me', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T14:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01b6123f-6158-5c3b-b91f-ddd0cf2dfd8b', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01b6123f-6158-5c3b-b91f-ddd0cf2dfd8b'}, {'abstract': 'Lost in the excitement over the Detroit Lions’ 4-0 start is this shocking news item out of Chicago: the Bears have a fullback.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/monday-matchup-bears-at-lions/', 'snippet': 'Lost in the excitement over the Detroit Lions’ 4-0 start is this shocking news item out of Chicago: the Bears have a fullback.', 'lead_paragraph': '