t recognized soccer nation, population 30,000, victories are as rare as the coins and stamps that make San Marino a collector’s haven.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/sports/soccer/san-marino-soccer-team-plays-on-despite-little-shot-at-winning-or-scoring.html', 'snippet': 'In Europe’s smallest recognized soccer nation, population 30,000, victories are as rare as the coins and stamps that make San Marino a collector’s haven.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN MARINO — This is Europe’s smallest recognized soccer nation, population 30,000, and victories in the tiny, mountaintop republic are as rare as the coins and stamps that make it a collector’s haven.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/11sanmarino1_cnd/11sanmarino1_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/11sanmarino1_cnd/11sanmarino1_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/11sanmarino1_cnd/11sanmarino1_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/11sanmarino1_cnd/11sanmarino1_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/11sanmarino1_cnd/11sanmarino1_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Win, 106 Losses, No Traffic Lights', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Traffic Lights: 0. Victories: 1.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Marino, Republic of', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T15:01:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By JER&Eacute; LONGMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eacute', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2676b13-43f1-5bfb-99cc-396b2d61ca8a', 'word_count': 1511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2676b13-43f1-5bfb-99cc-396b2d61ca8a'}, {'abstract': 'By finishing in third place at Suzuka, Japan, Vettel became the youngest driver to win back-to-back drivers’ championships in the series.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/monday-motorsports-sebastian-vettel-is-youngest-repeat-champion-in-formula-one-history/', 'snippet': 'By finishing in third place at Suzuka, Japan, Vettel became the youngest driver to win back-to-back drivers’ championships in the series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the Abu Dhabi Grand Prix last year, Sebastian Vettel, then 23, simultaneously won a race and a season championship. At the Japanese Grand Prix on Sunday, Vettel finished third at more than two seconds off the winning pace, yet with four races left on the Formula One calendar, Vettel, now 24, has drained the 2011 season of most, if not all of its drama by clinching his second championship in a row.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Motorsports: Sebastian Vettel Is Youngest Repeat Champion in Formula One History', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank