en biographies of Louis Armstrong, Charlie Parker and Bing Crosby. Now he will help other writers recreate the lives of their chosen subjects as the new acting executive director of the Leon Levy Center for Biography at the CUNY Graduate Center. Among his many trophies Mr. Giddins can count a Guggenheim Fellowship, a National Book Critics Circle Award, a Lifetime Achievement Award from the Jazz Journalists Association, and a Grammy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jazzy New Leader for CUNY Biography Center', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALCOTT, LOUISA MAY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARMSTRONG, LOUIS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crosby, Bing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Margaret', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giddins, Gary', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levy, Leon', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Charlie', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wineapple, Brenda', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Book Critics Circle', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T15:22:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bbcf60a-2cfc-591b-9189-6e55d5341fea', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bbcf60a-2cfc-591b-9189-6e55d5341fea'}, {'abstract': 'Bank of America will begin reimbursing employees with same-sex partners for the extra taxes they pay on domestic partner health insurance.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/bank-of-america-equalizes-health-costs-for-gay-employees/', 'snippet': 'Bank of America will begin reimbursing employees with same-sex partners for the extra taxes they pay on domestic partner health insurance.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Bank of America’s new monthly debit card fee has been roundly criticized in recent weeks. But a new change in corporate policy change is likely to receive a much warmer reception.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bank of America Equalizes Health Costs for Gay Employees', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T15:29:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/026f2116-6c02-5690-9425-91c145d18bee', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/026f2116-6c02-5690-9425-91c145d18bee'}, {'abstract': 'A collector’s personal booty becomes a fantasy hotel in Fez.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/pasha-fierce/', 'snippet': 'A collector’s personal booty becomes a fantasy hotel in Fez.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pasha Fierce', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T15:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Petkanas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Petkanas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9993cb37-5df9-5807-8b80-9fa42f207497', 'word_count': 1134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9993cb37-5df9-5807-8b80-9fa42f207497'}, {'abstract': 'Witnesses in Cairo on Sunday claimed in accounts posted on social media Web sites that the military had used excessive force, fired live ammunition at the protesters and drove armored personnel carriers into the crowds.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/social-media-accounts-of-violence-in-cairo-challenge-official-narrative/', 'snippet': 'Witnesses in Cairo on Sunday claimed in accounts posted on social media Web sites that the military had used excessive force, fired live ammunition at the protesters and drove armored personnel carriers into the crowds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague David Kirkpatrick reported from Cairo, at least 24 people were killed and more than 200 wounded on Sunday night in Cairo when a demonstration by Christians angry about a recent attack on a church in Upper Egypt devolved into violent clashes with the military.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Social Media Accounts of Violence in Cairo Challenge Official Narrative', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharaf, Essam Adbel-Aziz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coptic Orthodox Church of Alexandria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T15:33:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a1cfa32-e534-55a0-a0f1-591df054e197', 'word_count': 973, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a1cfa32-e534-55a0-a0f1-591df054e197'}, {'abstract': 'China’s plan to churn out millions of electric cars will not blunt its greenhouse impact.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/scant-co2-benefit-from-chinas-coal-powered-electric-cars/', 'snippet': 'China’s plan to churn out millions of electric cars will not blunt its greenhouse impact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much has been made of China’s big push to build and deploy 1 million electric vehicles a year by 2015. The move will help cut smog and oil imports. Less has been made of the scant impact this is likely to have on the country’s emissions of carbon dioxide, given its enduring reliance on coal for most of its electricity. Here’s a “Your Dot” contribution describing the situation from Lucia Green-Weiskel, who has worked in China for the Innovation Center for Energy and Transportation and co-authored a report on electric vehicles there for the United Nations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scant CO2 Benefit from China’s Coal-Powered Electric Cars', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T15:44:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af26dc1a-4032-518f-a408-badeefbe810a', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af26dc1a-4032-518f-a408-badeefbe810a'}, {'abstract': 'Off the Rails: Charlton Street, a West Village lane that had been included on previous subway maps, has vanished from the current version.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/a-village-street-slips-quietly-off-the-subway-map/', 'snippet': 'Off the Rails: Charlton Street, a West Village lane that had been included on previous subway maps, has vanished from the current version.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charlton Street, a sleepy three-block lane in the southern end of the West Village, is not exactly the most famous roadway in New York. Its achievements, by this city’s standards, are average stuff: a row of landmark 19th-century town 