 will be based in Chicago. The fourth, Andrew Freedman, regional sales director for the eastern region, will be based in New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Ad Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Webdenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T18:10:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed9f8dc3-41a9-52b4-8013-10d459d46289', 'word_count': 1146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed9f8dc3-41a9-52b4-8013-10d459d46289'}, {'abstract': 'Jomar, a Philadelphia-based chain, uses a new campaign to cultivate younger customers for its mostly one-of-a-kind items.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/business/media/a-search-for-bargains-goes-social.html', 'snippet': 'Jomar, a Philadelphia-based chain, uses a new campaign to cultivate younger customers for its mostly one-of-a-kind items.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Decades ago, Macy’s proclaimed, “It’s smart to be thrifty.” Now, consumers who are concerned about the economy have elevated thriftiness to a lifestyle, as evidenced by everything from TV shows about “extreme couponing” to retailers that try to turn shopping into a quest for values.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/business/media/10adnewsletter-inline/10adnewsletter-online-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 795, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Search for Bargains Goes Social', 'kicker': 'Campaign Spotlight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Search for Bargains Goes Social', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coupons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T18:14:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68b23cdf-5602-5e1e-9513-b004c405aebe', 'word_count': 1288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68b23cdf-5602-5e1e-9513-b004c405aebe'}, {'abstract': 'Spotify saw its revenue more than quintuple last year, but the company says it still lost more than $40 million.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/spotify-loss-widens-despite-higher-revenue/', 'snippet': 'Spotify saw its revenue more than quintuple last year, but the company says it still lost more than $40 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spotify, the streaming digital music service that was just given a big boost through a partnership with Facebook, saw its revenue more than quintuple last year, but the company still lost more than $40 million, it reported on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spotify Loss Widens Despite Higher Revenue', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', '