1/10/10/apple-breaks-pre-sale-records-with-iphone-4s/', 'snippet': 'Apple announced Monday that the iPhone 4S broke previous sales records for iPhones, saying it processed more than one million orders in the first 24 hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has the repetition of a Hollywood movie script: Apple releases a new product. Some in the media and analysts quickly bemoan the new product, saying it didn’t live up to the hype they created. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Disappointment? Apple’s iPhone 4S Breaks Sales Records', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T18:36:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63d55093-c75b-5537-bc1a-d67b2e71dcce', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63d55093-c75b-5537-bc1a-d67b2e71dcce'}, {'abstract': 'A philosophy student turned businessman turned politician, Janusz Palikot leads a socially libertarian-style party that made an unexpectedly strong electoral showing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/world/europe/polands-palikot-movement-signals-a-changing-society.html', 'snippet': 'A philosophy student turned businessman turned politician, Janusz Palikot leads a socially libertarian-style party that made an unexpectedly strong electoral showing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WARSAW — Waving a gun and a sex toy at a news conference may have branded Janusz Palikot as an extreme politician, but the ensuing notoriety had its benefits. Just a few years later, one out of 10 Polish voters cast a ballot for the socially libertarian-style party that bears the provocateur’s name.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/world/WARSAW/WARSAW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/11/world/WARSAW/WARSAW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 320}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/world/WARSAW/WARSAW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Provocateur’s Strong Showing Is a Sign of a Changing Poland', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Provocateur’s Strong Showing Is a Sign of a Changing Poland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tusk, Donald', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Law and Justice (Poland)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T18:39:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2124b68-0aca-59b5-84d8-9d51743cc7ae', 'word_count': 1166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2124b68-0aca-59b5-84d8-9d51743cc7ae'}, {'abstract': 'The Hazelden network of rehab centers bought a failing project on West Broadway to open a residence that treats substance abuse among young people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/nyregion/tribeca-condo-revives-as-rehab-center-for-college-students.html', 'snippet': 'The Hazelden network of rehab centers bought a failing project on West Broadway to open a residence that treats substance abuse among young people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With buffed hardwood floors, a fireplace in the living room, marble in the bathrooms and Silestone in the kitchen, the 2,200-square-foot, full-floor apartment on West Broadway looks exactly like the luxury condo it was meant to be. The furniture is plush and neutral, original artwork hangs on the walls, there is a Wii console hooked up to the flat-screen television and, when the sights of TriBeCa’s bustle from the second-floor windows are not enough, there is a planted, furnished roof deck upstairs, with views stretching from the Empire State Building to ground zero.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/nyregion/appraisal1-1318268160117/appraisal1-1318268160117-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/11/nyregion/appraisal1-1318268160117/appraisal1-1318268160117-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/nyregion/appraisal1-1318268160117/appraisal1-1318268160117-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/nyregion/appraisal1-1318268160117/appraisal1-1318268160117-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/11/nyregion/appraisal1-1318268160117/appraisal1-1318268160117-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shiny Failure, Reborn as a Rehab Center', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Shiny Failure, Reborn as a Rehab Center', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'TriBeCa (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T18:42:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane Cardwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cardwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ba02e25-c7de-5457-bbda-cb3245e571df', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ba02e25-c7de-5457-bbda-cb3245e571df'}, {'abstract': 'Bank of New York Mellon has been accused of defrauding customers of its foreign exchange services. But the cases raise the sticky questions about marketing claims.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/the-difference-between-puffery-and-fraud/', 'snippet': 'Bank of New York Mellon has been accused of defrauding customers of its foreign exchange services. But the cases raise the sticky questions about marketing claims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department and the New York attorney general, Eric T. Schneiderman, filed separate civil charges last week against Bank of New York Mellon, accusing it of defrauding customers of its foreign exchange services. The cases raise sticky questions about when marketing claims cross the imperceptible line from puffery to fraud. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Difference Between Puffery and Fraud', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of New York Mellon Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T18:43:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d812d45c-4d87-552d-936f-8006fe004024', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d812d45c-4d87-552d-936f-8006fe004024'}, {'abstract': 'Social scientists are trying to mine a world of Internet data to predict political crises, revolutions and other forms of economic and social instability.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/science/11predict.html', 'snippet': 'Social scientists are trying to mine a world of Internet data to predict political crises, revolutions and other forms of economic and social instability.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 60 years ago, in his “Foundation” series, the science fiction novelist Isaac Asimov invented a new science — psychohistory — that combined mathematics and psychology to predict the future.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/science/11PRED/11PRED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/science/11PRED/11PRED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/11/science/11PRED/11PRED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Government Aims to Build a ‘Data Eye in the Sky’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Government Aims to Build A ‘Data Eye In the Sky’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sociology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T18:47:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Markoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Markoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c555b86e-3723-5213-8054-5ab1d7f22307', 'word_count': 1258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c555b86e-3723-5213-8054-5ab1d7f22307'}, {'abstract': 'At a campaign stop in New Hampshire, Mitt Romney accuses President Obama of fostering divisiveness in America.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/romney-turns-again-to-the-economy/', 'snippet': 'At a campaign stop in New Hampshire, Mitt Romney accuses President Obama of fostering divisiveness in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILFORD, N.H. — Mitt Romney on Monday accused President Obama of fostering divisiveness in America and said the protests against Wall Street were unfairly criticizing an entire sector of the country’s economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Turns Again to the Economy', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T18:52:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker and Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2c74574-1236-5ad8-ac1e-0778caeebf24', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2c74574-1236-5ad8-ac1e-0778caeebf24'}, {'abstract': 'After years of criticism that it has fallen behind the curve in its methods for calculating global hunger, the Food and Agriculture Organization is revising its techniques.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/revisiting-the-global-food-crisis/', 'snippet': 'After years of criticism that it has fallen behind the curve in its methods for calculating global hunger, the Food and Agriculture Organization is revising its techniques.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Another new report has just become available on the subject of world hunger, and it may frustrate some readers. The new edition of State of Food Insecurity in the World, an annual report from the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations, does not actually estimate the number of hungry people across the globe. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Revisiting the Global Food Crisis', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T18:53:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5eca354d-2d76-5488-b5b0-ad7dec0be434', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5eca354d-2d76-5488-b5b0-ad7dec0be434'}, {'abstract': 'A view of the day in sports included wheelchair fencing and the world’s least stressed security guard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/10/sports/20111010-photoreplay.html', 'snippet': 'A view of the day in sports included wheelchair fencing and the world’s least stressed security guard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A view of the day in sports included wheelchair fencing and the world’s least stressed security guard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/10/sports/20111010-photoreplay-slide-JLI6/2