so rejected affirmative action in admissions.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/dream-act/', 'snippet': 'Over the weekend, Governor Brown signed a law that will help illegal immigrants pay for college, and he also rejected affirmative action in admissions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In California, illegal immigrants enrolling in college will be eligible for state scholarships and financial aid beginning next July.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dream Act Becomes Law in California', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T20:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca R. Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0cc6f29-4fba-5e7f-b388-24d40ce0ccfc', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0cc6f29-4fba-5e7f-b388-24d40ce0ccfc'}, {'abstract': 'Fractional reserve is here to stay.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/if-banks-are-outlawed-only-outlaws-will-have-banks/', 'snippet': 'Fractional reserve is here to stay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yglesias tells us that some Occupy Wall Street protesters have picked up Ron Paulish monetary ideas — although some know better. I thought I’d say a word about one particular idea that sounds plausible to some people but is actually quite wrong: banning fractional reserve banking.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'If Banks Are Outlawed, Only Outlaws Will Have Banks', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-10T20:02:58+0000', '