ia Quintet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/arts/music/scotty-mccreery-lauren-alaina-claudia-quintet-new-albums.html', 'snippet': 'New albums by Scotty McCreery, Lauren Alaina, James Carter Organ Trio and Claudia Quintet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scotty McCreery started out the most recent season of “American Idol” as a scrawny stick with a deep and hollow voice and an Alfred E. Neuman grin. By the time the show ended, he’d become a Nashville slickster would-be, with exaggerated gestures and bulging swagger. Lauren Alaina arrived at the show a savant, a flexible singer with preternatural confidence and a gift for interpretation. But with each week, she seemed to grow younger and younger, losing the boom in her voice, her confidence, her grip on the show’s narrative. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/arts/NEWMUSIC1/NEWMUSIC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/arts/NEWMUSIC1/NEWMUSIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/11/arts/NEWMUSIC1/NEWMUSIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Idol’ Singers’ Morning-After Moment', 'kicker': 'New Music', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Idol’ Singers’ Morning-After Moment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCreery, Scotty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T00:13:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica, Nate Chinen and Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c553a4a6-27b6-5506-9d5f-6c349e523e17', 'word_count': 1639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c553a4a6-27b6-5506-9d5f-6c349e523e17'}, {'abstract': 'Sheriff Lee Baca announced a number of new investigations and changes in Los Angeles County jails, saying he would appoint a special task force to examine dozens of allegations of inmate abuse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/us/pressed-sheriff-agrees-to-abuse-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'Sheriff Lee Baca announced a number of new investigations and changes in Los Angeles County jails, saying he would appoint a special task force to examine dozens of allegations of inmate abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Accusations of inmate abuse in the country’s largest jail system have piled up over the last several days and weeks, with tales of volunteers witnessing beatings of prisoners. And when news broke of a federal investigation into the conduct of several guards, the Los Angeles County sheriff, Lee Baca, reacted angrily, saying the inquiry overstepped its authority. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/us/SHERIFF/SHERIFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 673, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption