nd “Hawaii Five-0.” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/11/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marketers Work Around the Gore to Reach a Zombie Show’s Audience', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marketers Work Around the Gore To Reach a Zombie Show’s Audience', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Product Placement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T00:16:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Adam Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Adam', 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f95a0f14-6110-5c19-82ee-e69849a34ba7', 'word_count': 976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f95a0f14-6110-5c19-82ee-e69849a34ba7'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Singh was a popular singer in South Asia who helped revive and popularize ghazals, a form of Persian poetry set to music expressing the writer’s feelings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/arts/music/jagjit-singh-dies-at-70-popularized-persian-ghazal-singing.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Singh was a popular singer in South Asia who helped revive and popularize ghazals, a form of Persian poetry set to music expressing the writer’s feelings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jagjit Singh, a singer of wide popularity in South Asia who helped revive and popularize ghazals — a venerable form of Persian poetry set to music expressing the writer’s feelings, especially about love — died on Monday in Mumbai. He was 70. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/sports/singh1/singh1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 661, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/sports/singh1/singh1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/12/sports/singh1/singh1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jagjit Singh, Reviver of Persian Ghazal Singing, Dies at 70', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jagjit Singh, 70; Revived Persian Ghazal Songs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T00:17:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Haresh Pandya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Haresh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pandya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/c38040ee-8454-5b29-a9bc-ee69e97bddf3', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c38040ee-8454-5b29-a9bc-ee69e97bddf3'}, {'abstract': 'The Facebook iPad app is a drastic improvement over the Web site because it is designed to make use of the touch screen and offers new features like locating friends on a map.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/facebook-ipad-app-is-a-vast-improvement-on-web-site/', 'snippet': 'The Facebook iPad app is a drastic improvement over the Web site because it is designed to make use of the touch screen and offers new features like locating friends on a map.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until now, navigating Facebook.com on an iPad felt like trying to write an e-mail on a calculator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook iPad App Improves on Web Site', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T00:20:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9388f7c4-580b-5291-bc92-aae2c6a0cfb0', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9388f7c4-580b-5291-bc92-aae2c6a0cfb0'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Aceti was known for unorthodox camera shots, and his work included the Olympics, the World Series and the Ali-Frazier “Thrilla in Manila.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/sports/joe-aceti-director-who-shaped-tv-sports-dies-at-76.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Aceti was known for unorthodox camera shots, and his work included the Olympics, the World Series and the Ali-Frazier “Thrilla in Manila.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joe Aceti, an innovative television director who for three decades helped shape network coverage of major sports events, including the Olympics, the World Series and the Ali-Frazier “Thrilla in Manila,” died on Oct. 4 in Kirkland, Wash. He was 76.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/ACETI-obit/ACETI-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/ACETI-obit/ACETI-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/ACETI-obit/ACETI-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe Aceti, Director Who Shaped TV Sports, Dies at 76', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Joe Aceti, 76, Innovative TV Sports Director', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}