Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Omar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Al-Jawoshy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a190e8f-459d-585b-beaf-469281d8f990', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a190e8f-459d-585b-beaf-469281d8f990'}, {'abstract': 'Some investors like Douglas A. Kass, the founder and president of Seabreeze Partners Management, attribute late-day market swings to leveraged exchange-traded funds.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/volatility-thy-name-is-e-t-f/', 'snippet': 'Some investors like Douglas A. Kass, the founder and president of Seabreeze Partners Management, attribute late-day market swings to leveraged exchange-traded funds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Did you watch the markets on Monday? In the last 18 minutes of trading, the Standard & Poor’s 500-stock index jumped more than 10 points with no news to account for the rally. If you were left scratching your head, you were not alone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Volatility, Thy Name Is E.T.F.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exchange Traded Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Standard & Poor's 500-Stock Index", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T01:09:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f53c2037-caf8-5fee-91b9-997e65eb9560', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f53c2037-caf8-5fee-91b9-997e65eb9560'}, {'abstract': 'A sobering analysis of our country’s deep economic problems deserves some attention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/opinion/this-time-it-really-is-different.html', 'snippet': 'A sobering analysis of our country’s deep economic problems deserves some attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title of the white paper is, admittedly, a mouthful: “The Way Forward: Moving From the Post-Bubble, Post-Bust Economy to Renewed Growth and Competitiveness.” It was commissioned by the New America Foundation, which hoped that it might “re-center the political debate to better reflect the country’s deep economic problems,” according to Sherle Schwenninger, the director of the foundation’s Economic Growth Program. Its authors are Daniel Alpert, a managing partner of Westwood Capital; Robert Hockett, a professor of financial law at Cornell and a consultant to the New York Federal Reserve; and Nouriel Roubini, who is, well, Nouriel Roubini, whose consistently bearish views have been consistently right. It is scheduled to be released on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Time, It Really Is Different', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Time, It Really Is Different', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roubini, Nouriel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New America Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deflation (Economics)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T01:10:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/882a3480-13a6-55ad-bd4f-9b48619bdac2', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/882a3480-13a6-55ad-bd4f-9b48619bdac2'}, {'abstract': 'John Carlos, who with fellow runner Tommie Smith staged a memorable podium demonstration at the 1968 Summer Games, has published an autobiography.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/sports/john-carlos-of-68-olympics-protest-maintains-his-passion.html', 'snippet': 'John Carlos, who with fellow runner Tommie Smith staged a memorable podium demonstration at the 1968 Summer Games, has published an autobiography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 40 years after Tommie Smith and John Carlos ignited the sports world with their black-gloved fists raised on the victory stand at the 1968 Mexico City Olympics, Carlos says, “I still feel the fire.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/CARLOS/CARLOS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/CARLOS/CARLOS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/CARLOS/CARLOS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Olympic Protester Maintains Passion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Olympic Protester Maintains Passion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carlos, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Tommie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T01:11:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Amdur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amdur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6427b91e-f647-537a-b951-80258e06ab56', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6427b91e-f647-537a-b951-80258e06ab56'}, {'abstract': 'Leading Democratic figures are embracing the spread of the anti-Wall Street protests as a way to align disenchanted Americans with their party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/us/politics/wall-street-protests-gain-support-from-leading-democrats.html', 'snippet': 'Leading Democratic figures are embracing the spread of the anti-Wall Street protests as a way to align disenchanted Americans with their party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Leading Democratic figures, including party fund-raisers and a top ally of President Obama, are embracing the spread of the anti-Wall Street protests in a clear sign that members of the Democratic establishment see the movement as a way to align disenchanted Americans with their party.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/us/jp-PROTEST/jp-PROTEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/11/us/jp-PROTEST/jp-PROTEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/us/jp-PROTEST/jp-PROTEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/us/jp-PROTEST/jp-PROTEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/11/us/jp-PROTEST/jp-PROTEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Try Wary Embrace of the Protests', 'kicker': None, 'content_k