ame': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wainwright, Adam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mozeliak, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carpenter, Chris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T01:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02c3e846-f062-5f5d-8ea1-15b4824297ff', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02c3e846-f062-5f5d-8ea1-15b4824297ff'}, {'abstract': 'Linn State Technical College is the first public college in the country to institute a mandatory drug test, according to the A.C.LU., which sued and has won a temporary injunction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/us/at-linn-state-technical-a-fight-over-required-drug-tests.html', 'snippet': 'Linn State Technical College is the first public college in the country to institute a mandatory drug test, according to the A.C.LU., which sued and has won a temporary injunction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Linn State Technical College in Linn, Mo., informed students this semester that they would be required to submit to a urine test that would be checked for illegal drugs as a condition of studying at the college. Almost immediately, the American Civil Liberties Union and other groups sued on behalf of several dissenting Linn State students and have won a temporary injunction. The A.C.L.U. says Linn State is the first public college in the country to require all adult students to submit to mandatory drug tests. Linn State officials however, say the policy is legal and was developed in the interest of their 1,200 students. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At One College, a Fight Over Required Drug Tests', 'kicker': 'Asked and Answered', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At One College, a Fight Over Required Drug Tests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Drug Use)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T01:47:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4fe5c70-1b78-5c61-839d-dd1ef85f53d6', 'word_count': 1045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4fe5c70-1b78-5c61-839d-dd1ef85f53d6'}, {'abstract': 'The Patriots ran on 11 of 13 plays on the clinching 78-yard drive in their victory over the Jets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/sports/football/jets-defense-falters-with-a-chance-to-rally.html', 'snippet': 'The Patriots ran on 11 of 13 plays on the clinching 78-yard drive in their victory over the Jets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. — It was an ideal situation for the Jets. In spite of themselves, they trailed New England by 6 points Sunday midway through the fourth quarter. The Patriots had the ball at their 22. The Jets had all three timeouts. All they needed was a stop, and an improbable victory seemed possible. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/JETS/JETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/JETS/JETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/JETS/JETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 924, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/JETS/JETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/JETS/JETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Late Patriots Drive Chips at the Jets’ Foundation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Late Patriots Drive Chips at the Jets’ Foundation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T01:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19ae0ddc-a590-5c9b-aae4-23219167f42d', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19ae0ddc-a590-5c9b-aae4-23219167f42d'}, {'abstract': 'Ed Sessa rolls out a smooth Tuesday puzzle for us. Oh, and I have a cold.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/10/sore/', 'snippet': 'Ed Sessa rolls out a smooth Tuesday puzzle for us. Oh, and I have a cold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY’S PUZZLE — I have a cold. I’m not sure why I’m telling you this, except that I hope you’ll understand if there are mistakes, as I’m currently typing this with my head on my desk. Seeing the entries FEVER and ACHY in the northern part of the grid made me want to nod and say, “Yup”, but nodding and saying “Yup” would be too painful, so you’ll just have to believe me when I say that they’re there. I need to conserve my energy for the rest of the post.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday: Sore All Over', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T02:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d34646ee-a222-5964-aeba-fd2b1d895966', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d34646ee-a222-5964-aeba-fd2b1d895966'}, {'abstract': 'An oil industry strike last month has snowballed into public-sector actions by bank, health care and industrial workers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/world/middleeast/customs-officers-strike-in-kuwait-halting-oil-shipments.html', 'snippet': 'An oil industry strike last month has snowballed into public-sector actions by bank, health care and industrial workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three thousand striking customs officers disrupted oil shipments from Kuwait on Monday, escalating the labor unrest that has been gaining momentum in recent weeks in the emirate