uggling-to-find-running-game-theyve-become-known-for.html', 'snippet': 'Despite the perception of the Giants as a hard-nosed, pounding franchise, through five weeks they are averaging 3.2 yards per carry, 30th out of 32 teams through Sunday’s games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Conceptually, the Giants still believe they are a dominant running team. They talk about running the ball. They scheme so they can run the ball. Establishing the run is something Coach Tom Coughlin has preached for years and is a significant element in the amorphous (yet often-invoked) notion of Giants football.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/11/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Struggle to Find the Running Game They’ve Become Known For', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giants Struggle to Find the Rushing Attack They’ve Been Known For', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Brandon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradshaw, Ahmad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T02:25:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2346d640-4838-5611-8428-ec90eeff272f', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2346d640-4838-5611-8428-ec90eeff272f'}, {'abstract': 'Scurrying to revive a football conference dwindling in programs and in relevancy, the Big East said it was considering moving to a model that consisted of 12 football-playing universities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/sports/ncaafootball/big-east-considering-move-to-12-football-members.html', 'snippet': 'Scurrying to revive a football conference dwindling in programs and in relevancy, the Big East said it was considering moving to a model that consisted of 12 football-playing universities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scurrying to revive a football conference dwindling in programs and in relevancy, the Big East said Monday that it was considering moving to a model that consisted of 12 football-playing universities. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big East Is Considering a Move to 12 Members in Football', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big East Is Considering a Move to 12 Members in Football', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'na