roducts from the wealth of free government information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Big data, the term for scanning loads of information for possibly profitable patterns, is a growing sector of corporate technology. Mostly people think in terms of online behavior, like mouse clicks, LinkedIn affiliations and Amazon shopping choices. But other big databases in the real world, lying around for years, are there to exploit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Data in the Dirt (and the Cloud)', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T04:01:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d8efe0c-0961-57e5-b826-b6036566e2fb', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d8efe0c-0961-57e5-b826-b6036566e2fb'}, {'abstract': 'A detailed examination of Web filtering and blocking in Iran and China offers information on how to combat the techniques.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/business/media/battling-internet-censorship-must-evolve-study-says.html', 'snippet': 'A detailed examination of Web filtering and blocking in Iran and China offers information on how to combat the techniques.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A detailed study of Internet censorship in China and Iran shows that blocking techniques are changing rapidly and are becoming significant new obstacles for news organizations, governments and businesses.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Internet Censorship Growth Hampers News, Study Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Internet Censorship Growth Hampers News, Study Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T04:01:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Markoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Markoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07e52f5e-d382-54ff-a412-6829dfabf868', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07e52f5e-d382-54ff-a412-6829dfabf868'}, {'abstract': 'Scouring flea markets and thrift stores for discarded furnishings, Mr. Loughlin helped spark a market for sleek midcentury modern design.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/arts/design/robert-loughlin-artist-and-design-expert-dies-at-62.html', 'snippet': 'Scouring flea markets and thrift stores for discarded furnishings, Mr. Loughlin helped spark a market for sleek midcentury modern design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert Loughlin, an artist and quirky sage of Modernist design whose work as a “picker” and dealer in 20th-century furnishings infl