com/2011/10/12/world/asia/myanmar-reportedly-prepares-to-free-thousands-of-prisoners.html', 'snippet': 'State-run media in Myanmar said 6,300 prisoners would be released, and a new human rights body urged the country’s president to free what it called “prisoners of conscience.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — Myanmar freed a prominent dissident on Wednesday at the start of what state media said would be the release of 6,300 prisoners in a general amnesty that was expected to include a number of political prisoners.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Myanmar Frees Prominent Dissident; More Political Prisoners Expected to Follow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Myanmar Frees Prominent Dissident; More Political Prisoners Expected to Follow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T09:06:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Mydans', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mydans', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b554f5e-458f-5fac-8b9f-cb3dc19ad4a3', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b554f5e-458f-5fac-8b9f-cb3dc19ad4a3'}, {'abstract': 'Tell us what you think about the locker-decorating trend described in this article. How do you put your personal stamp on the things you’re required to have at school?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/how-do-you-personalize-the-things-youre-required-to-have-at-school/', 'snippet': 'Tell us what you think about the locker-decorating trend described in this article. How do you put your personal stamp on the things you’re required to have at school?', 'lead_paragraph': 'According to this article, middle school students across the country are creating elaborately decorated lockers featuring items like $25 mini chandeliers and motion-sensor-equipped lamps. Is this an innocent trend that simply allows students to create an individualized space at school, or does it make students who can’t afford decorations feel inferior? How do you personalize the things you bring to, or have at, school — whether a locker, uniform, backpack, binder, or desk?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Do You Personalize the Things You’re Required to Have at School?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T09:32:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susannah L. Griffee and Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susannah', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Griffee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b848d10-7dbb-5668-b4aa-177dc9edea0d', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b848d10-7dbb-5668-b4aa-177dc9edea0d'}, {'abstract': 'The Bay Area should be used to Jim Harbaugh working football miracles by now. He just wasn’t expected to do it this quickly.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/harbaugh-and-how-the-49ers-were-built/', 'snippet': 'The Bay Area should be used to Jim Harbaugh working football miracles by now. He just wasn’t expected to do it this quickly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From 1983 to 1998, the San Francisco 49ers won at least 10 games each season. They made the playoffs 15 times in those 16 years, and again earned playoff berths in 2001 and 2002.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harbaugh and How the 49ers Were Built', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harbaugh, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T10:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chase Stuart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chase', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stuart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9c8452b-9de8-5ade-9f90-c36d44b36140', 'word_count': 1687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9c8452b-9de8-5ade-9f90-c36d44b36140'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/the-early-word-alliances-2/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s Times', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Alliances', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T10:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {