helped design the space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there’s something familiar about the brand-new Silencio, a subterranean club in Paris (142 rue Montmartre; www.silencio-club.com), it may be because you are a fan of the director David Lynch. A cross between Studio 54 and a 20th-century Parisian salon, the club takes its name from Mr. Lynch’s 2001 film “Mulholland Drive” — but that’s not where the connection ends. He also helped design it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Director Lynch Turns Attention to Paris Night Club', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NIGHTCLUBS AND CABARETS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T10:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerie Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8754dd18-fc69-5bed-b264-98f4577a2ddd', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8754dd18-fc69-5bed-b264-98f4577a2ddd'}, {'abstract': 'Between 1 and 5 p.m. E.S.T. today, October 11, you can discuss the following letter with the Ethicist, Ariel Kaminer. Post your comments below, and check back later to see what the Ethicist has to say.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/armchair-ethicist-voter-edition/', 'snippet': 'Between 1 and 5 p.m. E.S.T. today, October 11, you can discuss the following letter with the Ethicist, Ariel Kaminer. Post your comments below, and check back later to see what the Ethicist has to say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Between 1 and 5 p.m. E.S.T. today, October 11, you can discuss the following letter with the Ethicist, Ariel Kaminer. Post your comments below, and check back later to see what the Ethicist has to say.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Armchair Ethicist, Voter Edition', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T10:25:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c78d76f-0585-5281-98a2-7463ab8e2c56', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c78d76f-0585-5281-98a2-7463ab8e2c56'}, {'abstract': 'The sentence was the maximum demanded by prosecutors on charges that Yulia V. Tymoshenko had harmed Ukraine’s interests as prime minister.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/world/europe/yulia-tymoshenko-sentenced-to-seven-years-in-prison.html', 'snippet': 'The sentence was the maximum demanded by prosecutors on charges that Yulia V. Tymoshenko had harmed Ukraine’s interests as prime minister.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIEV, Ukraine — From the moment President Viktor F. Yanukovich took office last year, a central question was whether he would lead Ukraine west, toward Europe, or into a tight symbiosis with the country’s Soviet-era masters in Moscow. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/world/UKRAINE-1/UKRAINE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'cr