 the Queens-Midtown Tunnel for a charity that helps needy Cuban children.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/a-familiar-figure-begs-on-the-street-but-not-for-himself/', 'snippet': 'At 97, the legendary comic Professor Irwin Corey regularly panhandles near the Queens-Midtown Tunnel for a charity that helps needy Cuban children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He is a familiar sight, the old man who solicits change from drivers stopped at a red light on East 35th Street in Midtown Manhattan every day near Third Avenue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Familiar Figure Begs on the Street, but Not for Himself', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beggars', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T11:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04e2c2ea-4511-5922-b66b-49d797cfe3aa', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04e2c2ea-4511-5922-b66b-49d797cfe3aa'}, {'abstract': 'A new recommendation that healthy men need not be screened for prostate cancer is sending a message that many doctors and patients do not want to hear: that early detection does not necessarily save lives.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/the-shortfalls-of-early-cancer-detection/', 'snippet': 'A new recommendation that healthy men need not be screened for prostate cancer is sending a message that many doctors and patients do not want to hear: that early detection does not necessarily save lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The outcry among many physicians and patients over a government panel’s recent announcement that healthy men should no longer receive P.S.A. blood testing to detect prostate cancer is rooted in a long and impassioned history among cancer screening advocates that early detection must always save lives. But as science has taught us, that’s not always the case.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Shortfalls of Early Cancer Detection', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostate Cancer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T11:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barron H. Lerner, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barron', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Lerner', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5aced8d-b411-53a2-b211-0d7ac8e3a547', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5aced8d-b411-53a2-b211-0d7ac8e3a547'}, {'abstract': 'A business owner confronts the specter of layoffs, and then everything changes.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/what-happened-next/', 'snippet': 'A business owner confronts the specter of layoffs, and then everything changes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my last post I imagined an exchange between myself and two tiny visitors. Three weeks without a sale, an extremely unusual event, had forced me to take a hard look at the numbers and explore what to do next.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happened Next', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T11:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87bded1e-238a-5557-b0ca-ef475f19d210', 'word_count': 1428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87bded1e-238a-5557-b0ca-ef475f19d210'}, {'abstract': 'China’s currency and free-trade agreements will come up for votes. But President Obama’s jobs bill is unlikely to move forward.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/congress-the-week-ahead-2/', 'snippet': 'China’s currency and free-trade agreements will come up for votes. But President Obama’s jobs bill is unlikely to move forward.', 'lead_paragraph': ' After a bit of unpleasantness on the Senate floor last week, members are expected to come together Tuesday to pass a bill to impose tariffs on some Chinese goods to punish Beijing for keeping its currency artificially depressed. The bill has a slim chance of ever being taken up in the House, where Democrats are pushing Republicans to consider the measure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mu