s.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/the-n-b-a-s-money-games/', 'snippet': 'The Day: With unemployment at 9 percent and with people camped out near Wall Street calling attention to the chasms in wealth distribution, you have to ask yourself what planet the basketball crowd is on. Also, what City Room is reading in other p...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Knickerbockers are about to enjoy one the best starts to a new season that they have had in a decade. That’s because there won’t be a start to the new season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The N.B.A.’s Money Games', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T12:55:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e055fc4b-70e2-52f0-81d1-8fee4d07ff44', 'word_count': 1180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e055fc4b-70e2-52f0-81d1-8fee4d07ff44'}, {'abstract': 'There’s something very sexy-cool about a glossy, nude lip.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/a-nude-awakening/', 'snippet': 'There’s something very sexy-cool about a glossy, nude lip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s something very sexy-cool about a glossy, nude lip. It says, “I’m hot, but I didn’t try too hard,” and it works for almost everyone. (And for almost every designer, judging by how many copped the bare-lip look for their resort and spring shows.) It’s also super-low-maintenance. “You don’t have to be concerned that your color will bleed,” says Lisa Houghton, who did the makeup on the previous page. The only caveat: you need a well-prepped pucker. Houghton exfoliated our model’s lips by dabbing on a bit of Elizabeth Arden Eight Hour Cream and rubbing it off with a tissue. Then she applied a mixture of Arden’s Crystal Clear Lip Gloss and a touch of High Shine Lip Gloss in Tropicoral for the right pinkish tone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Nude Awakening', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T13:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3731cd23-c85d-5f03-86af-22e7371b2a6f', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3731cd23-c85d-5f03-86af-22e7371b2a6f'}, {'abstract': 'Ares Management and the Canadian Pension Plan Investment Board will pay $22 a share, while the founding family will roll over its 33 percent stake.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/99-cents-only-chain-in-1-6-billion-buyout/', 'snippet': 'Ares Management and the Canadian Pension Plan Investment Board will pay $22 a share, while the founding family will roll over its 33 percent stake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The low-cost retailer 99 Cents Only Stores agreed on Tuesday to sell itself to a group of investors that includes its founding family for $1.6 billion in cash, ending a months-long sales process.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '99 Cen