, 'snippet': 'Assessing the play of the Rangers, Devils and Islanders in the first week of the N.H.L. season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Rangers did not win a game. The Islanders and Devils did, but not after enduring the embarrassment of getting shut out before capacity crowds at their home openers. What was learned from the first six games of the season for the Rangers, Devils and Islanders? Not much in the 82-game big picture. But for the faithful who couldn’t wait for the second weekend in October, hockey provides plenty to analyze.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Metro Pucks: Report Cards, Awards and Analysis', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carolina Hurricanes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Red Wings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida Panthers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Kings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nassau Coliseum', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Islanders', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Flyers', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Jose Sharks', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Lightning', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T14:40:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Botta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/590ce1ce-afa7-5519-898c-25b648fba061', 'word_count': 1065, 'uri': 'nyt://article/590ce1ce-afa7-5519-898c-25b648fba061'}, {'abstract': 'Sony’s new SLT A77 camera claims to be the world’s fastest autofocusing camera.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/sony-debuts-a-camera-for-speed-demons/', 'snippet': 'Sony’s new SLT A77 camera claims to be the world’s fastest autofocusing camera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seems like camera makers are bragging less about how many megapixels are on their sensors – which\xa0 is nearly useless as a measure of quality anyway — but are taking up a new selling point: speed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sony Unveils a Camera for Speed Demons', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sensors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T14:53:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97278d00-637f-5eb1-8517-ebfb1078130f', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97278d00-637f-5eb1-8517-ebfb1078130f'}, {'abstract': 'The truck would be based on the global Colorado seen at auto shows this year, while the convertible is the most powerful ever offered by the automaker.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/chevrolet-confirms-colorado-pickup-and-camaro-zl1-convertible/', 'snippet': 'The truck would be based on the global Colorado seen at auto shows this year, while the convertible is the most powerful ever offered by the automaker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WARREN, Mich. — During a media event marking Chevrolet’s 100th anniversary, held at the General Motors Design Center here, G.M. announced that a new version of the Chevrolet Colorado midsize pickup truck would be offered to American buyers. The automaker also unveiled a convertible model of its ultra high-performance Camaro ZL1.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chevrolet Confirms Colorado Pickup and Camaro ZL1 Convertible', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Convertibles (Autos)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T14:53:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62c9a8ce-7538-5647-90fd-fcf2c6c3ef8a', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62c9a8ce-7538-5647-90fd-fcf2c6c3ef8a'}, {'abstract': 'A few hundred people crowded an empty loft space recently to celebrate the 12th anniversary of WNYU’s show, “Beats in Space.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/notes-from-the-underground-kimann-foxman/', 'snippet': 'A few hundred people crowded an empty loft space recently to celebrate the 12th anniversary of WNYU’s show, “Beats in Space.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a curious scene, walking up lower Broadway in broad daylight and hearing the heavy beats pumping from a window above. A freight elevator ride and hefty door charge later, you’d never guess it was midafternoon, as a few hundred people crowded an empty loft space and danced to music played by an all-star roster of D.J.’s. The nine-hour event was in celebration of the 12th anniversary of Tim Sweeney’s weekly radio show “Beats in Space,” which has been broadcast every Tuesday night on WNYU (89.1) since 1999. The lineup included Rub N Tug, Kimann Foxman (of Hercules and Love Affair fame, pictured here), Matthew Dear and Sweeney himself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From the Underground | Kimann Foxman', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T15:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By IO Tillett Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Io', 'middlename': 'Tillett', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4d60b54-5bf5-53bb-8f72-d37303531111', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4d60b54-5bf5-53bb-8f72-d37303531111'}, {'abstract': 'Sean Durkin, the director of “Martha Marcy May Marlene,” discusses a scene from his film, which plays in the New York Film Festival this week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/anatomy-of-a-scene-martha-marcy-may-marlene/', 'snippet': 'Sean Durkin, the director of “Martha Marcy May Marlene,” discusses a scene from his film, which plays in the New York Film Festival this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cults, paranoia and a breakdown of trust are among the central topics explored in the psychological drama “Martha Marcy May Marlene,” written and directed by Sean Durkin. The film, which plays this week at the New York Film Festival before opening in theaters on Oct. 21, follows one young woman (Elizabeth Olsen) after she has escaped from a cult and has gone to stay with her sister (Sarah Paulson) and her sister’s husband. In this video, Mr. Durkin narrates a scene from the film that illustrates the haziness of Martha’s psychological state after her escape.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anatomy of a Scene: ‘Martha Marcy May Marlene’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Film Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olsen, Elizabeth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulson, Sarah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T15:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35870804-dc5b-597b-b489-86f0bc8b4b51', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35870804-dc5b-597b-b489-86f0bc8b4b51'}, {'abstract': 'The F.D.I.C. has approved a draft, but other federal agencies must still vote on the proposal, which will be open for public comment until January.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/regulators-advance-volcker-rule/', 'snippet': 'The F.D.I.C. has approved a draft, but other federal agencies must still vote on the proposal, which will be open for public comment until January.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal regulators on Tuesday took a much-anticipated step toward reining in risky trading on Wall Street, introducing a proposal that would prohibit federally insured banks from making certain types of bets with their own money.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regulators Advance Volcker Rule', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T15:05:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN PROTESS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'PROTESS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7730ea01-55af-5829-a1ff-689faa61655f', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7730ea01-55af-5829-a1ff-689faa61655f'}, {'abstract': 'The Detroit Lions remain undefeated. The Tigers are playing in the league championship series. And no one will have to watch the Pistons for a while.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/sports/detroit-lions-undefeated-tigers-still-in-playoffs-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'The Detroit Lions remain undefeated. The Tigers are playing in the league championship series. And no one will have to watch the Pistons for a while.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard not to root for Detroit. The city, that is. It has been dealt a pretty brutal hand by recent history, enduring the crippling combination of economic freefall, Canadian winters and Matt Millen. And no matter what you think of the place, gosh, nobody deserves Matt Millen. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/sports/12leadingoff-pic/12leadingoff-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/12/sports/12leadingoff-pic/12leadingoff-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/sports/12leadingoff-pic/12leadingoff-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/sports/12leadingoff-pic/12leadingoff-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/12/sports/12leadingoff-pic/12leadingoff-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Detroit Gets Its Motor Running', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Detroit Gets Its Motor Running', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Lions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T15:11:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '