l': 'By Jorge Castillo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castillo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71ef2b60-7997-5938-bebb-52e0952f5efc', 'word_count': 2963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71ef2b60-7997-5938-bebb-52e0952f5efc'}, {'abstract': 'Some pet owners will go to extreme lengths to preserve their pets long after they are dead, and Amy Finkel is working on a documentary of their efforts.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/preserving-memories-of-pets-and-then-some/', 'snippet': 'Some pet owners will go to extreme lengths to preserve their pets long after they are dead, and Amy Finkel is working on a documentary of their efforts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amy Finkel lives in an apartment in Boerum Hill, Brooklyn, that does not allow pets. But she does have a groundhog (Chompers), an armadillo (Fleischesser) and a boar (Angel). They are all, however, dead and stuffed — and in the case of the boar, it is just the head.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Preserving Memories of Pets, and Then Some', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxidermy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T15:34:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Jane Grossman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': 'Jane', 'lastname': 'Grossman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fc648d1-75a8-5678-a5eb-0e5374ff4b67', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fc648d1-75a8-5678-a5eb-0e5374ff4b67'}, {'abstract': 'Mel Rosenthal, a photojournalist and teacher, is retiring from Empire State College after 36 years, and our colleagues on Lens are giving him a sendoff, including a slide show of his work.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/a-passion-for-pictures-and-for-social-justice/', 'snippet': 'Mel Rosenthal, a photojournalist and teacher, is retiring from Empire State College after 36 years, and our colleagues on Lens are giving him a sendoff, including a slide show of his work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mel Rosenthal, a photojournalist and teacher with a passion for social justice and the South Bronx neighborhood where he grew up, is retiring from Empire State College after 36 years. Our colleagues on Lens are giving him a sendoff including a slide show of his work and a Q. and A. about how he earned the trust of his subjects. “I was walking down street one day, some gang members saw me,” Mr. Rosenthal recalls. “They said, ‘What the hell you doing here?’ One lifted up his pants. He had two Berettas strapped to his ankles. I said, ‘Do you really need two guns?’ ” Read more on Lens »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Passion for Pictures, and for Social Justice', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T15:43:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bab4342a-4506-5705-aa3b-4112694cf26e', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bab4342a-4506-5705-aa3b-4112694cf26e'}, {'abstract': 'Techniques used to treat traumatic brain injuries, the wounds suffered by many troops in Iraq and Afghanistan, lack rigorous scientific support, a government-appointed panel found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/health/12brain.html', 'snippet': 'Techniques used to treat traumatic brain injuries, the wounds suffered by many troops in Iraq and Afghanistan, lack rigorous scientific support, a government-appointed panel found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Techniques being used to treat psychological lapses from traumatic brain injuries, the signature wounds suffered by troops in Iraq and Afghanistan, appear to be helpful, but lack rigorous scientific support, a government-appointed panel reported Tuesday after completing the most comprehensive analysis of the evidence to date.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treatment of Trauma to Brain Is Studied', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treatment Of Trauma To Brain Is Studied', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traumatic Brain Injury', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T15:46:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benedict Carey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benedict', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3729ec2-c731-55cb-940e-cf18d0b2a86f', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3729ec2-c731-55cb-940e-cf18d0b2a86f'}, {'abstract': 'The Raine Group, an investment boutique focused on the media and entertainment industries, made a top hire and closed on its first private equity fund.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/raine-group-ramps-up/', 'snippet': 'The Raine Group, an investment boutique focused on the media and entertainment industries, made a top hire and closed on its first private equity fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Raine Group, an investment boutique focused on the media and entertainment industries, said Tuesday that it had made a major hire and closed on its first private equity fund.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raine Group Ramps Up', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T15:47:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c862d17f-48f3-5646-b21f-616fca5e8640', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c862d17f-48f3-5646-b21f-616fca5e8640'}, {'abstract': 'The White House and Congressional Democrats are developing plans to revive elements of what had been portrayed as the centerpiece of Mr. Obama’s push to revive a listless economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/us/politics/obamas-jobs-bill-senate-vote.html', 'snippet': 'The White House and Congressional Democrats are developing plans to revive elements of what had been portrayed as the centerpiece of Mr. Obama’s push to revive a listless economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In a major setback for President Obama, the Senate on Tuesday blocked consideration of his $447 billion jobs bill, forcing the White House and Congressional Democrats to scramble to salvage parts of the plan, the centerpiece of Mr. Obama’s push to revive a listless economy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/us/SUB-SUB-JOBS-1/SUB-SUB-JOBS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/12/us/SUB-SUB-JOBS-1/SUB-SUB-JOBS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/us/SUB-SUB-JOBS-1/SUB-SUB-JOBS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/us/SUB-SUB-JOBS-1/SUB-SUB-JOBS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/12/us/SUB-SUB-JOBS-1/SUB-SUB-JOBS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'President’s Jobs Measure Is Turned Back in Key Senate Test', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President’s Jobs Measure Is Defeated in Key Test in the Senate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T15:53:34+0000', 'docume