[], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T16:29:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcc515dd-0527-5086-a0a3-6f42ecee8c2e', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcc515dd-0527-5086-a0a3-6f42ecee8c2e'}, {'abstract': 'Americans have given their economy a vote of no confidence.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/worsening-attitudes/', 'snippet': 'Americans have given their economy a vote of no confidence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans have given their economy a vote of no confidence. Or at least, very little confidence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Worsening Attitudes', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T16:33:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56efb927-f2a6-5dc7-b469-e6c8dca47c7e', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56efb927-f2a6-5dc7-b469-e6c8dca47c7e'}, {'abstract': 'Responding to readers’ comments on my column and the question of whether the Tea Party will transform itself from the Party of Against into a force that can make things happen.', 'web_url': 'https://keller.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/the-republican-scramble-continued/', 'snippet': 'Responding to readers’ comments on my column and the question of whether the Tea Party will transform itself from the Party of Against into a force that can make things happen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The comment stream in response to my Monday column – “Is the Tea Party Over?” – was divided for the most part into one camp of readers proclaiming the inevitable triumph of the Tea Party, and another, larger camp praying for its demise. There’s no point quarreling with faith (in the first case) or hope (in the second). To my mind the question is whether the Tea Party will transform itself from a backlash – the Party of Against – into a force that can make things happen. The movement’s best hope of making that leap any time soon, which you can view with approval or alarm, is Rick Perry. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Republican Scramble, Continued', 'kicker': 'Bill Keller', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T16:36:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/160fd62c-0141-500c-8205-f7aaabb39dbc', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/160fd62c-0141-500c-8205-f7aaabb39dbc'}, {'abstract': 'In a document filed with the Securities Exchange Commission, the media giant pushed back against the assessment of an investor advisory company, which said its board had shown a “striking lack of stewardship” related to the phone-hacking scandal in Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/news-corp-filing-rebuts-criticism-of-board/', 'snippet': 'In a document filed with the Securities Exchange Commission, the media giant pushed back against the assessment of an investor advisory company, which said its board had shown a “striking lack of stewardship” related to the phone-hacking scandal i...', 'lead_paragraph': 'News Corporation went on the defensive Tuesday morning after an investor advisory firm urged shareholders to vote against reinstating several key members of the media giant’s board of directors, including the chairman and chief executive, Rupert Murdoch, and his son James Murdoch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Corp. Filing Rebuts Criticism of Board', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carey, Chase', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, James R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walid bin Talal', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institutional Shareholder Services', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T16:44:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8dc8370-c389-532d-8a74-5e9233a43a06', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8dc8370-c389-532d-8a74-5e9233a43a06'}, {'abstract': 'Quotes from Coach Jurgen Klinsmann and his players before the U.S. men’s national team faces Ecuador at Red Bull Arena Tuesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/some-pregame-comments-u-s-vs-ecuador/', 'snippet': 'Quotes from Coach Jurgen Klinsmann and his players before the U.S. men’s national team faces Ecuador at Red Bull Arena Tuesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARRISON, N.J. — The United States men’s national team plays Ecuador in an international friendly at Red Bull Arena on Tuesday night in the fifth game of the Jurgen Klinsmann era. Though additional matches for the rest of the year have not been announced, it is expected that the U.S. will play in Europe next month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Pregame Comments: U.S. vs. Ecuador', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Clint', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinsmann, Jurgen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T16:44:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b84903a2-e4fe-5374-a37f-8b5b0a3c1114', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b84903a2-e4fe-5374-a37f-8b5b0a3c1114'}, {'abstract': 'Minimalist sculpture meets aerodynamics in a new show at London’s Haunch of Venison.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/less-is-more-edward-barber-and-jay-osgerby/', 'snippet': 'Minimalist sculpture meets aerodynamics in a new show at London’s Haunch of Venison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the last several months, the British designers Edward Barber and Jay Osgerby of BarberOsgerby have once gain proven their impressive versatility. They’ve produced an inexpensive, wildly practical plastic chair for Vitra and directed a group of students from the ECAL in Lausanne, Switzerland, to create a playfully luxe group of objects based on a traditional Baccarat goblet. And they’ve been on fire — pardon the pun — since they were named in June as the designers of the 2012 Olympic torch, a sleek, triangular form with 8,000 perforated circles that represent each of the people who will carry the torches. (Yes, 8,000 torches — one for each torchbearer — will be produced.) But their latest effort is not about design in the expected sense.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Less Is More | Edward Barber and Jay Osgerby', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T16:45:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d39eeb2-52a7-5c3a-9de1-538621312cb5', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d39eeb2-52a7-5c3a-9de1-538621312cb5'}, {'abstract': 'A platform collapse on the set of the latest installment in the “Resident Evil” franchise has resulted in injuries to 16 actors portraying zombies.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/no-major-zombie-injuries-after-accident-on-horror-film-shoot/', 'snippet': 'A platform collapse on the set of the latest installment in the “Resident Evil” franchise has resulted in injuries to 16 actors portraying zombies.', 'lead_paragraph': ' It’s apparently a bad week to be producing a motion picture about the living dead. After what may or may not have been a weapons raid on the Brad Pitt zombie movie, “World War Z,” a platform collapse in Canada on the set of the latest installment in the “Resident Evil” series has resulted in injuries to 16 actors portraying zombies, The Associated Press reported. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Major Zombie Injuries After Accident on Film Shoot', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jovovich, Milla', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pitt, Brad', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T16:53:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcab18e6-401c-582a-bc26-a411322c87ad', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcab18e6-401c-582a-bc26-a411322c87ad'}, {'abstract': 'An attempt at citizen justice became an actual bout with the law for one self-styled citizen superhero.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/seattle-superhero-arrested-in-pepper-spraying-episode/', 'snippet': 'An attempt at citizen justice became an actual bout with the law for one self-styled citizen superhero.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maybe now he’ll go by Pepper Man. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seattle ‘Superhero’ Arrested in Pepper-Spraying Episode', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vigilantes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T16:55:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/baff384d-c413-59c8-a8d1-b25d14ccf4c6', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baff384d-c413-59c8-a8d1-b25d14ccf4c6'}, {'abstract': 'Amber Miller, a veteran marathon runner, did not have much time to celebrate after finishing the Chicago Marathon on Sunday: She had a baby to deliver.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/a-marathon-runner-delivers-a-baby/', 'snippet': 'Amber Miller, a veteran marathon runner, did not have much time to celebrate after finishing the Chicago Marathon on Sunday: She had a baby to deliver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amber Miller, a veteran marathon runner, did not have much time to celebrate after finishing the Chicago Marathon on Sunday: She had a baby to deliver.', 'source': 'The New York