hletic program remains the biggest mystery in college sports, though a conference call Tuesday morning provided some clarity. The Big 12’s interim commissioner, Chuck Neinas, said Missouri would play in the league for the 2012-13 season, giving the university time to decide whether to stay in the league or attempt to join the Southeastern Conference. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missouri to Play in the Big 12 Next Season, and Then Decide', 'kicker': 'College Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Missouri to Play in the Big 12 Next Season, and Then Decide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Colonial Athletic Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southeastern Conference', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Missouri', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlantic 10 Conference', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big East Conference', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big 12 Conference', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-11T18:20:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/736a37b0-de1c-5417-9e50-196e18de8eb0', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/736a37b0-de1c-5417-9e50-196e18de8eb0'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the dwellings of Cabo Poloni