tters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stuttering', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T00:20:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/d93b061a-8352-5b42-917b-e11feae547fb', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d93b061a-8352-5b42-917b-e11feae547fb'}, {'abstract': 'A New York State decision to release health insurers’ justifications of their proposed increases has reversed a “trade secret” exemption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/nyregion/health-insurers-ask-to-keep-rate-increase-data-secret.html', 'snippet': 'A New York State decision to release health insurers’ justifications of their proposed increases has reversed a “trade secret” exemption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Major health insurance companies seeking steep premium increases in New York have submitted memos to state officials to justify the higher rates. Now they are fighting to keep the memos from the public, saying they include trade secrets that competitors could use against them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/nyregion/INSURE/INSURE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 467, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Seeking Rate Increases in New York, Health Insurers Fight to Keep Secrets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Seeking Rate Increases in New York, Health Insurers Fight to Keep Secrets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value':