ultures and alternative systems can be nurturing, educational, illuminating, inspiring — and these are not small things — but they do not bring about fundamental change. Food co-ops, for example, make a difference, but they won’t much alter the way Big Food operates. Historically, the route to fixing broken systems goes through struggle, confrontation and even revolution.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finally Making Sense on Wall Street', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T00:30:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09c9a516-354f-5e9d-9cdd-c266373b5633', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09c9a516-354f-5e9d-9cdd-c266373b5633'}, {'abstract': 'An economics debate from hell.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/newt-gingrich-defender-of-your-prostate/', 'snippet': 'An economics debate from hell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My alleged true love insists on watching the Republican debate. I have fled upstairs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newt Gingrich, Defender Of Your Prostate', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T00:34:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9cad545-0723-5ed4-971e-a57fe534e7f1', 'word_count': 41, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9cad545-0723-5ed4-971e-a57fe534e7f1'}, {'abstract': 'The Bloomberg administration says that requiring food stamp applicants to be fingerprinted reduces fraud, but the City Council speaker, Christine C. Quinn, said it was punitive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/nyregion/christine-c-quinn-urges-city-to-drop-rule-on-fingerprinting-food-stamp-seekers.html', 'snippet': 'The Bloomberg administration says that requiring food stamp applicants to be fingerprinted reduces fraud, but the City Council speaker, Christine C. Quinn, said it was punitive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Taking aim at a practice she called unnecessary, costly and punitive, the speaker of the City Council, Christine C. Quinn, is asking the Bloomberg administration to justify requiring applicants for food stamps to be electronically fingerprinted.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fingerprinting Those Seeking Food Stamps Is Denounced', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fingerprinting Those Seeking Food Stamps Is Denounced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Resources Administration (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T00:40:00+0000', 'document_type