1-56e1-9431-081d428bfb3a', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef085694-3021-56e1-9431-081d428bfb3a'}, {'abstract': 'By helping at risk children early in their lives, a long-term mentoring program pays society back many times over.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/11/forging-a-life-changing-bond/', 'snippet': 'By helping at risk children early in their lives, a long-term mentoring program pays society back many times over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday, I reported on an organization called Friends of the Children, which identifies children in kindergarten growing up in poverty and facing multiple risk factors at home and in their neighborhood — and then connects them with adult mentors for 12 years. The idea is to guarantee that these children have a consistent relationship with a caring and responsible adult whom they see at least four hours each week, from kindergarten until high school graduation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Forging a Life-Changing Bond', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mentors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Friends of the Children', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institute of Child Health and Human Development', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T01:10:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a765a78e-aa78-5b06-943f-26ff0c6e1ebc', 'word_count': 1809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a765a78e-aa78-5b06-943f-26ff0c6e1ebc'}, {'abstract': 'Growing demand and sinking rents have contributed to the rise in high-end coffee shops in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/realestate/commercial/fresh-local-and-upscale-coffee-spots-multiply-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Growing demand and sinking rents have contributed to the rise in high-end coffee shops in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Small coffee chains, benefiting from lower retail rents and a seemingly bottomless thirst for high-end coffee even in a weak economy, are seizing the opportunity to expand in New York City.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/business/2SubCoffee/2SubCoffee-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/12/business/2SubCoffee/2SubCoffee-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/business/2SubCoffee/2SubCoffee-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/business/2SubCoffee/2SubCoffee-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/12/business/2SubCoffee/2SubCoffee-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fuel for the City That Never Sleeps', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fuel for the City That Never Sleeps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'},