hey would have more access to social services, instead of continuing to prosecute them as adults in criminal courts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Reform for Teenage Offenders', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Reform for Teenage Offenders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lippman, Jonathan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Courts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T01:45:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b51bf8e0-4d90-5411-9a51-fc6d38d2140f', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b51bf8e0-4d90-5411-9a51-fc6d38d2140f'}, {'abstract': 'Schools Chancellor Dennis M. Walcott faced the harshest criticism of his tenure as he was chastised by the City Council over the layoffs of 672 school support workers in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/nyregion/dennis-m-walcott-grilled-by-city-council.html', 'snippet': 'Schools Chancellor Dennis M. Walcott faced the harshest criticism of his tenure as he was chastised by the City Council over the layoffs of 672 school support workers in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Schools Chancellor Dennis M. Walcott on Tuesday faced the harshest criticism in the six months since he took the job, as he was chastised at a City Council hearing o