069-044bce3d5bfa'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on October 12, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/pageoneplus/corrections-october-12.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on October 12, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: October 12', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T04:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a84fd09d-98b7-5f5b-bcc1-54c231b47f0a', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a84fd09d-98b7-5f5b-bcc1-54c231b47f0a'}, {'abstract': 'Forced exercise eases symptoms in patients with Parkinson’s disease and is raising intriguing questions about how intense exercise affects the brain in healthy people.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/what-parkinsons-teaches-us-about-the-brain/', 'snippet': 'Forced exercise eases symptoms in patients with Parkinson’s disease and is raising intriguing questions about how intense exercise affects the brain in healthy people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scientific discoveries can be serendipitous, and so it was when Jay L. Alberts, then a Parkinson’s disease researcher at Emory University in Atlanta, mounted a tandem bike with Cathy Frazier, a Parkinson’s patient. The two were riding the 2003 RAGBRAI bicycle tour across Iowa, hoping to raise awareness of the neurodegenerative disease and “show people with Parkinson’s that you don’t have to sit back and let the disease take over your life,” Dr. Alberts said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Parkinson’s Teaches Us About the Brain', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muscles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Parkinson's Disease", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T04:01:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99df54a9-a69c-5fd0-980d-ef10ace5d64a', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99df54a9-a69c-5fd0-980d-ef10ace5d64a'}, {'abstract': 'The document, known as the “Inter Caetera” bull, is well known to scholars but perhaps less so to the general public, which will be able to peruse a fragment online at luxinarcana.org on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/arts/design/a-vatican-secret-for-columbus-day.html', 'snippet': 'The document, known as the “Inter Caetera” bull, is well known to scholars but perhaps less so to the general public, which will be able to peruse a fragment online at luxinarcana.org on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a post-Dan Brown world the mere mention of the Secret Vatican Archives conjures up nefarious mystery and intrigue. In fact, the “Secret” in the archives’ name refers to the private nature of the thousands of documents that line more than 50 miles’ of shelves in a two-story bunker beneath the Vatican Museums. Many of the documents have unique historical importance, like the 1493 papal bull granting to Spain lands recently discovered by Christopher Columbus. The document, known as the “Inter Caetera” bull, is well known to scholars but perhaps less so to the general public, which will be able to peruse a fragment online at luxinarcana.org on Wednesday, the day denoting Columbus’s arrival in the Americas in 1492. It is one of 100 documents that will go on a rare public viewing at the Capitoline Museum in Rome in February as part of an exhibition celebrating the 400th anniversary of the foundation of the archives. Drafted by Pope Alexander VI, the papal bull not only granted Spain certain rights in the newly discovered lands but also called for the evangelization of the indigenous people there. “It is part of the history of the colonization of the Americas that gave rise to a series of problems whose consequences would be felt over time,” said Luca Carboni, secretary general of the archives.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Vatican ‘Secret’ For Columbus Day', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Vatican ‘Secret’ For Columbus Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T04:02:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/faf76636-4993-57c4-8a80-a2ca8d10fc1c', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faf76636-4993-57c4-8a80-a2ca8d10fc1c'}, {'abstract': 'A year after a dramatic rescue from underground, many of the 33 Chilean miners are unemployed, traumatized by their experience, and poorer than before.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slide