le', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a461ef4d-e835-5942-bd71-e26f285930eb', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a461ef4d-e835-5942-bd71-e26f285930eb'}, {'abstract': 'A year after the globally televised rescue of 33 miners in Chile, most are unemployed, many are poorer than before and some are experiencing post-traumatic stress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/world/americas/chiles-rescued-miners-face-major-struggles-a-year-later.html', 'snippet': 'A year after the globally televised rescue of 33 miners in Chile, most are unemployed, many are poorer than before and some are experiencing post-traumatic stress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COPIAPÓ, Chile — After his dramatic rescue from a mine last year, Jimmy Sánchez traveled the world, cruising the Greek islands, visiting Britain, Israel, Los Angeles, Disney World — all paid for by people who were moved by the Chilean miners’ story of courage and perseverance.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Year Out of the Dark in Chile, but Still Trapped', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Year Out of the Dark in Chile, but Still Trapped', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Copiapo (Chile)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T06:07:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexei Barrionuevo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barrionuevo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64bc7e1f-c51e-5e57-be52-fffbae3ff839', 'word_count': 1476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64bc7e1f-c51e-5e57-be52-fffbae3ff839'}, {'abstract': 'In less than three years, 13,570 children have been reported missing in Delhi.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/where-are-the-children/', 'snippet': 'In less than three years, 13,570 children have been reported missing in Delhi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rajkumar Mahto of Kirari village in West Delhi lives in a single room by an open gutter with his wife, Hema Devi, and two daughters. Contact with the sewage appears to be the cause of the sores on the children’s faces and bodies. But Mahto says they have broken out because they are worried. The children, he explains, haven’t seen their 8-year-old sister, Kajal, since April 21, 2010.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Other India: Where Are the Children?', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Labor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T06:23:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'sub