': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c919883-6152-58bd-bb77-44bbfdba8f21', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c919883-6152-58bd-bb77-44bbfdba8f21'}, {'abstract': 'A report from the Joint Economic Committee of Congress finds that the American workers most likely to be hurt by free-trade agreements are also those likeliest to have a hard time finding new jobs.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/whose-jobs-are-at-risk-in-free-trade/', 'snippet': 'A report from the Joint Economic Committee of Congress finds that the American workers most likely to be hurt by free-trade agreements are also those likeliest to have a hard time finding new jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Congress expected on Wednesday to take up trade agreements with South Korea, Colombia and Panama as well as a benefits package for workers who lose their jobs to foreign competition, the Joint Economic Committee of Congress has released a report showing that the workers most likely to be hurt by free trade are the same groups that will have the most difficult time getting new jobs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whose Jobs Are at Risk in Free Trade', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T12:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d82a641f-2526-5f58-97c3-99829ab2a387', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d82a641f-2526-5f58-97c3-99829ab2a387'}, {'abstract': 'The smallest of the Detroit automakers early Wednesday tentatively agreed with the U.A.W. on a contract that would add 2,100 jobs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/business/chrysler-is-last-to-reach-deal-with-union.html', 'snippet': 'The smallest of the Detroit automakers early Wednesday tentatively agreed with the U.A.W. on a contract that would add 2,100 jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WARREN, Mich. — Chrysler will add 2,100 jobs in the United States, while paying smaller bonuses to hourly workers than its cross-town competitors, under a tentative labor agreement aimed at helping Chrysler pay off its debt and keep labor costs flat, the United Automobile Workers union said on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/business/Auto/Auto-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/business/Auto/Auto-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/13/business/Auto/Auto-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chrysler Is Last to Reach Deal With Union', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chrysler Is Last to Reach Deal With Autoworkers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'org