line': {'main': 'Two Guns, 11 Bullets and a Jury Threading a Needle', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheehan, Barbara', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T12:20:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af4dcf9e-17c2-5ab1-86a1-8b89a3163b33', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af4dcf9e-17c2-5ab1-86a1-8b89a3163b33'}, {'abstract': 'An app that lets its users broadcast anonymous messages to those nearby has become an organizing tool of the Occupy Wall Street activists.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/anonymous-messaging-app-vibe-gets-boost-from-occupy-wall-street/', 'snippet': 'An app that lets its users broadcast anonymous messages to those nearby has become an organizing tool of the Occupy Wall Street activists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Occupy Wall Street activists are no strangers to social media.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Messaging App Grows With Wall Street Protests', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T12:22:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ad2aabd-375f-5fd8-87b2-64b182ebec86', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ad2aabd-375f-5fd8-87b2-64b182ebec86'}, {'abstract': 'Where are all the gay vampires, werewolves, witches and just plain ordinary kids-in-a-story (as opposed to kids-with-a-story)?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/why-so-few-gay-characters-in-teen-fiction/', 'snippet': 'Where are all the gay vampires, werewolves, witches and just plain ordinary kids-in-a-story (as opposed to kids-with-a-story)?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are a gay teenage reader, you can find a relative abundance of books on coming out, coming to terms with a gay identity, questioning your sexuality or wrestling with prejudice. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why So Few Gay Characters in Teen Fiction?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T12:24:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Karin Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf0fdf39-2129-5bda-b554-37316886f375', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf0fdf39-2129-5bda-b554-37316886f375'}, {'abstract': 'The bar for success, lowered.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/pyrrhic-adjustment/', 'snippet': 'The bar for success, lowered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martin Wolf is, as usual, right on point today. As he says, simply providi