', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Chance for a Pitching Duel', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gallardo, Yovani', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Brewers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T14:38:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e779167c-9cfd-5d5e-b0fe-8166d6accf29', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e779167c-9cfd-5d5e-b0fe-8166d6accf29'}, {'abstract': 'Vexed by arthritis and other health issues, a 59-year-old woman rebuffs her son’s suggestion to learn how to scuba dive. But several later she discovered that in the water, nothing hurts.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/feeling-ageless-under-water/', 'snippet': 'Vexed by arthritis and other health issues, a 59-year-old woman rebuffs her son’s suggestion to learn how to scuba dive. But several later she discovered that in the water, nothing hurts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 59, I don’t feel particularly old, but sometimes my joints do. Old injuries to both knees have turned into arthritis, and a ruptured ligament and long-gone cartilage have left me a bit wobbly. Bursitis in my hips and bone spurs in my feet don’t help much.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling Ageless Under Water', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diving and Divers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Knees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T14:49:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denise Grady', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c0a1de7-6132-5416-bfd0-eb948b8693ff', 'word_count': 1096, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c0a1de7-6132-5416-bfd0-eb948b8693ff'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/what-were-reading-288/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Guardian: From the archives, the newspaper’s original (and scathing) review of French Country Cooking by Elizabeth David, published in 1951 and still a living, breathing classic. — Julia Moskin', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T14:51:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2446c5b1-f452-5f0f-b468-49bed02c5a3c', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2446c5b1-f452-5f0f-b468-49bed02c5a3c'}, {'abstract': 'A purely electric version of the four-door hatchback, which will be offered in 2012 with a gasoline engine, will be made available in low quantities to American customers in 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/chevrolet-to-sell-purely-electric-spark-hatchback-in-u-s/', 'snippet': 'A purely electric version of the four-door hatchback, which will be offered in 2012 with a gasoline engine, will be made available in low quantities to American customers in 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'General Motors introduced the 2012 Chevrolet Spark subcompact four-door hatchback in Detroit on Wednesday. The news was swiftly upstaged, however, by the subsequent announcement that a purely electric version would be available to American customers in limited quantities in 2013.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chevrolet to Sell Purely Electric Spark Hatchback in U.S.', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Cars (Compact, Subcompact and Microcars)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'A123 Systems Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T14:57:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0738cfc1-e3c8-5ec5-b8d7-9a9d684310fc', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0738cfc1-e3c8-5ec5-b8d7-9a9d684310fc'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art announced today that the spring 2012 exhibit at the Costume Institute will be “Elsa Schiaparelli and Miuccia Prada: On Fashion.”', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/prada-and-schiaparelli-at-the-met/', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art announced today that the spring 2012 exhibit at the Costume Institute will be “Elsa Schiaparelli and Miuccia Prada: On Fashion.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elsa Schiaparelli may share a birthday with Karl Lagerfeld (Sept. 10), but Miuccia Prada is unquestionably her sister in soul. Putting these two nimble minds together makes sense, and not simply because both are educated Italian women who enjoy a good fashion joke. The Metropolitan Museum of Art announced today that the spring 2012 exhibit at the Costume Institute will be “Elsa Schiaparelli and Miuccia Prada: On Fashion.” It will open May 10 and run through Aug. 19, with the gala on May 7.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prada and Schiaparelli at the Met', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T14:57:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a598f2eb-4cd5-5c10-bf50-bfea8f777fde', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a598f2eb-4cd5-5c10-bf50-bfea8f777fde'}, {'abstract': 'Dental fees vary widely even in the same geographic area, an analysis finds.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/data-reveals-wide-variation-in-dental-fees/', 'snippet': 'Dental fees vary widely even in the same geographic area, an analysis finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Consumers could save significant money on dental care by simply shopping around and asking about prices in their own communities, an analysis of health claims data shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Data Reveals Wide Variation in Dental Fees', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teeth and Dentistry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T14:59:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86fb28f8-ee43-5aab-a816-044f4bc3d29b', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86fb28f8-ee43-5aab-a816-044f4bc3d29b'}, {'abstract': 'The real surprise Tuesday was not the Tigers’ Game 3 victory, but how they continued to play through injuries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/sports/tigers-ignore-the-pain-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'The real surprise Tuesday was not the Tigers’ Game 3 victory, but how they continued to play through injuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Something far more notable happened Tuesday night in Detroit than simply a playoff baseball game. Sure, the Tigers’ 5-2 victory over the Rangers in Game 3 of the American League Championship Series was riveting enough, even if all you did was contemplate the personal expansion of the Tigers’ Miguel Cabrera — dude, Little Caesars Pizza doesn’t need another mascot — and what on earth the Rangers’ Colby Lewis was thinking by throwing the ball anywhere near Cabrera’s bat in the fifth inning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tigers Ignore the Pain', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tigers Ignore the Pain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T15:09:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20d0deb4-ddd9-5829-b711-eb5f9e499f2b', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20d0deb4-ddd9-5829-b711-eb5f9e499f2b'}, {'abstract': 'A new stop on the London food tour offers a communal locavore vibe.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/london-dispatch-maltby-street-market/', 'snippet': 'A new stop on the London food tour offers a communal locavore vibe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Borough Market has long held sway as an essential stop on the London food tour. But in the wake of disagreement over increasing rents and trading loyalties, some of Borough’s headlining purveyors left in search of new digs, setting up shop further east in and around the Victorian railway arches of Maltby, Stanworth and Druid Streets. A few years ago, Borough traders used these arches mainly for storage. But when the Monmouth Coffee Company started selling straight from its Maltby Street production site, word spread and a trickle of curious visitors began to arrive. Other vendors, encouraged, followed suit with their own stalls and the buzz got louder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Dispatch | Maltby Street Market', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T15:12:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'ori