ticle/0b0ba44f-781d-5949-b0a7-3ddb2ebde71e', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b0ba44f-781d-5949-b0a7-3ddb2ebde71e'}, {'abstract': 'In a new column for the Moment blog, Lynn Yaeger peeks at people’s terrifically odd, amusing and magnificent collections, starting with the robot menagerie of the photographer Mary Ellen Mark.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/mary-ellen-mark-and-the-robots/', 'snippet': 'In a new column for the Moment blog, Lynn Yaeger peeks at people’s terrifically odd, amusing and magnificent collections, starting with the robot menagerie of the photographer Mary Ellen Mark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a new column, Lynn Yaeger peeks at people’s terrifically odd, amusing and magnificent collections, starting with the robot menagerie of the photographer Mary Ellen Mark. “Their batteries have probably all melted. I’m a bad robot mom,” Ms. Mark said, looking with wry affection at the crowd of robots — pink fembots in frilly aprons! Mean metal guys with clock bellies! — that have taken up residence in her downtown loft, a place that has been her studio since almost before SoHo was SoHo. Read more (and view photos) on T Magazine’s Moment blog.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mary Ellen Mark and the Robots', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T16:20:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bb760bf-90aa-5e9e-a003-f985757cae99', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bb760bf-90aa-5e9e-a003-f985757cae99'}, {'abstract': 'The details laid out by the Justice Department lent greater support to claims by anti-government Syrian activists living abroad of harassment and intimidation by Syrian agents.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/u-s-accuses-virginia-man-of-espionage-at-syria-protests/', 'snippet': 'The details laid out by the Justice Department lent greater support to claims by anti-government Syrian activists living abroad of harassment and intimidation by Syrian agents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated  | A revised version of this post can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Accuses Virginia Man of Espionage at Syria Protests', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T16:22:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f6ed954-6da0-56aa-ac27-dac67d460edb', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f6ed954-6da0-56aa-ac27-dac67d460edb'}, {'abstract': 'Are the Buffalo Bills really that good? Are the Indianapolis Colts really that bad? Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer readers’ questions this week.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/have-a-question-for-n-f-l-reporter-judy-battista/', 'snippet': 'Are the Buffalo Bills really that good? Are the Indianapolis Colts really that bad? Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer readers’ questions this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are the Buffalo Bills really that good? (And what about the 49ers?) Are the Indianapolis Colts really that bad? Can Tim Tebow succeed as the starting quarterback in Denver? What will the Raiders be like without owner Al Davis? Will Los Angeles get an N.F.L. team any time soon? Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The New York Times, will answer questions from readers of The Fifth Down. Send in your questions and answers will appear on the blog on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Have a Question for N.F.L. Reporter Judy Battista?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Battista, Judy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T16:25:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/801be644-29eb-5014-9053-eeefc24bc161', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/801be644-29eb-5014-9053-eeefc24bc161'}, {'abstract': 'The number of people quitting their jobs in August also rose, which could be a good sign for the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/for-each-u-s-job-opening-4-6-unemployed/', 'snippet': 'The number of people quitting their jobs in August also rose, which could be a good sign for the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were 4.6 unemployed workers