dc67', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78ef279e-d760-57fa-94c0-a5921d56dc67'}, {'abstract': 'The New York City Ballet came closer to its dual mission of advancing music and dance in its fall season, but still the company conveyed the feeling that it was treading water.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/arts/dance/in-city-ballets-fall-season-a-need-for-surprises.html', 'snippet': 'The New York City Ballet came closer to its dual mission of advancing music and dance in its fall season, but still the company conveyed the feeling that it was treading water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than any other ballet company in the world, New York City Ballet has the marriage of music and dance written into its constitution. Elsewhere you may find dancing that’s just as musical, perhaps even more so. (Among the world’s troupes today, the Royal Ballet in London at its best is probably the most musically responsive.) But only at City Ballet is the heart of the repertory about dance making music register in space. As the company’s Balanchine Black & White Week in May demonstrated, its founder-choreographer, George Balanchine, was often prepared to strip everything else away until musicality was virtually all that remained. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/arts/NYCB2/NYCB2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 778, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/arts/NYCB2/NYCB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/13/arts/NYCB2/NYCB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At City Ballet, a Need for Surprises', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At City Ballet, a Need for Surprises', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martins, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T16:46:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/578eed9d-ad20-5dbd-a171-5743c5acf6cb', 'word_count': 1058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/578eed9d-ad20-5dbd-a171-5743c5acf6cb'}, {'abstract': 'The 1918 Strand Theater will be renovated for a 61,000-square-foot complex.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/groundbreaking-set-for-new-arts-center-in-brooklyn/', 'snippet': 'The 1918 Strand Theater will be renovated for a 61,000-square-foot complex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg on Thursday will break ground for a renovation of the 1918 Strand Theater in Brooklyn’s BAM Cultural District, to be shared by BRIC Arts/Media House, a multidisciplinary arts and media complex, and the UrbanGlass reNEWal Project, a center dedicated to artistic glass.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Groundbreaking Set for New Arts Center in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leeser, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Markowitz, Marty', 'rank': 3, 'majo