t the Republicans after Newt Gingrich said he should be in jail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Barney Frank will not go quietly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Frank Fires Back at Gingrich', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T16:56:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bbed601-9125-5e79-a5e3-028e814d3aff', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bbed601-9125-5e79-a5e3-028e814d3aff'}, {'abstract': 'Gauging the mix of disruption and transformation under way at a turbulent, and exciting, juncture in human history.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/disruption-on-the-path-to-transformation/', 'snippet': 'Gauging the mix of disruption and transformation under way at a turbulent, and exciting, juncture in human history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tom Friedman has posted a column that considers two views of world events — one seeing a great disruption, the other an exciting transformation. He ends the piece, not with a conclusion, but by asking readers which narrative they believe. (There’s more on the thinkers behind these views below.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Disruption on the Path to Transformation', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T16:57:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'pers