 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mattei, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T18:06:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0cc8bd4-37d7-581c-ab0a-d107c360a5d2', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0cc8bd4-37d7-581c-ab0a-d107c360a5d2'}, {'abstract': 'Americans have more devices sucking down data. And the carriers couldn’t be happier about that. Revenue from data services rose 21.2 percent from a year earlier.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/the-u-s-has-more-wireless-devices-than-people/', 'snippet': 'Americans have more devices sucking down data. And the carriers couldn’t be happier about that. Revenue from data services rose 21.2 percent from a year earlier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — Watching all those people juggling phones and tablets and e-readers in stores, subways and coffee shops, not to mention the many small shops continually offering new models of phones, you could think that there are more wireless devices than people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Wireless Devices Than People', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CTIA - The Wireless Association', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T18:07:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96938642-a440-5a6b-86c9-7351f821ed75', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96938642-a440-5a6b-86c9-7351f821ed75'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Kimelman, whom the government placed at the outer edge of Raj Rajaratnam’s insider-trading circle, was sentenced to two and a half years in prison.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/caught-in-a-wide-web-a-trader-faces-prison/', 'snippet': 'Michael Kimelman, whom the government placed at the outer edge of Raj Rajaratnam’s insider-trading circle, was sentenced to two and a half years in prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Friday, on a crystalline autumn afternoon, Michael A. Kimelman sat in the backyard of his home in Larchmont, N.Y. His toddler son was perched on his lap, sucking on a pacifier. His older boy played baseball with a friend, while his wife and daughter gawked at 10 egg-producing hens housed in their new chicken coop.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caught in a Wide Web, a Trader Faces Prison', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goffer, Emanuel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goffer, Zvi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T18:09:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a1833f7-7879-5b70-b7d2-1bdeab9847c0', 'word_count': 1406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a1833f7-7879-5b70-b7d2-1bdeab9847c0'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican debates have turned into a kind of spring training for the frontrunner.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/romney-the-inexorable/', 'snippet': 'The Republican debates have turned into a kind of spring training for the frontrunner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I spent last night’s Republican debate trying to imagine scenarios where Mitt Romney loses the G.O.P. nomination for president. Rick Perry gets bitten by a radioactive Lincoln-Douglas debate champion and develops a sudden facility for public argument? A long-lost codicil to the Constitution is discovered, in which the Founding Fathers endorse the 9-9-9 tax plan? Utah renames itself the Republic of Deseret and secedes from the Union, forcing Romney to make a tragic choice between his religion and his country? Or, perhaps most unlikely of all — Jon Huntsman is embraced by the Tea Party and pulls off a surprise upset in Iowa?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney the Inexorable', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T18:14:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/527509d9-0a7a-5634-964a-d3d2652e39ec', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/527509d9-0a7a-5634-964a-d3d2652e39ec'}, {'abstract': 'Left to their own devices, corporations can pose serious threats to human values.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/corporations-people-and-truth/', 'snippet': 'Left to their own devices, corporations can pose serious threats to human values.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Stone is featuring occasional posts by Gary Gutting, a professor of philosophy at the University of Notre Dame, that apply critical thinking to information and events that have appeared in the news.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corporations, People and Truth', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T18:19:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Gutting', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gutting', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f27ae0b-1ed9-5923-bdb2-03a03b3520ea', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f27ae0b-1ed9-5923-bdb2-03a03b3520ea'}, {'abstract': 'One result of the deal could be a more confrontational, Hamas-imbued Palestinian movement that could reshape regional relationships and pose a challenge to the Palestinian Authority in the West Bank.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/world/middleeast/israeli-palestinian-prisoner-swap-rattles-regional-politics.html', 'snippet': 'One result of the deal could be a more confrontational, Hamas-imbued Palestinian movement that could reshape regional relationships and pose a challenge to the Palestinian Authority in the West Bank.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — The prisoner exchange between Hamas and Israel that is expected to begin next week could reshape regional relationships, strengthening Egypt, Hamas and Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel while posing an acute challenge to the Palestinian Authority in the West Bank.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/world/13mideast/13mideast-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/world/13mideast/13mideast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/13/world/13mideast/13mideast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israeli-Hamas Agreement to Trade Prisoners May Reshape Politics in Region', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israeli-Hamas Agreement to Trade Prisoners May Reshape Politics in Region', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shalit, Gilad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barghouti, Marwan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fatah, Al', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABBAS, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T18:25:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed48cce9-8ea3-5e90-be50-2addbb8c167a', 'word_count': 1324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed48cce9-8ea3-5e90-be50-2addbb8c167a'}, {'abstract': 'The actresses Scarlett Johansson and Mila Kunis were among the victims of a hacker who stole personal information from celebrities, an F.B.I. source said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/us/florida-man-indicted-in-celebrity-phone-hacking.html', 'snippet': 'The actresses Scarlett Johansson and Mila Kunis were among the victims of a hacker who stole personal information from celebrities, an F.B.I. source said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — A Florida man was arrested Wednesday and charged with breaking into and commandeering the e-mail accounts of at least 50 celebrities — including the actresses Scarlett Johansson and Mila Kunis and the pop singer Christina Aguilera — to steal photographs, financial data and personal correspondence, the F.B.I. said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/us/HACKER/HACKER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/us/HACKER/HACKER-thumbSt