 and social trends in both countries as well as their interaction with each other. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asia Society to Host China-India Program', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chaudhuri, Amit', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deb, Siddhartha', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghosh, Amitav', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jin, Ha', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schell, Orville', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yu Hua', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Asia Society', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T19:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71dd9afe-76ca-5015-9bb8-cff58478f415', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71dd9afe-76ca-5015-9bb8-cff58478f415'}, {'abstract': 'What’s worth giving up to balance the budget and get the U.S. economy moving again?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/to-the-barricades/', 'snippet': 'What’s worth giving up to balance the budget and get the U.S. economy moving again?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gail Collins: David, I was sorry to see you didn’t have a little bit of sympathy for the Occupy Wall Street protesters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To the Barricades', 'kicker': 'The Conversation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T19:31:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks and Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78200462-3039-59d0-818c-cdffee8e289d', 'word_count': 1219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78200462-3039-59d0-818c-cdffee8e289d'}, {'abstract': 'Research in Motion’s BlackBerry outage spread to the United States late on Tuesday, leaving Wall Street bankers without their usual e-mail and messaging fix.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/wall-streets-crackberry-withdrawal/', 'snippet': 'Research in Motion’s BlackBerry outage spread to the United States late on Tuesday, leaving Wall Street bankers without their usual e-mail and messaging fix.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wednesday had the makings of a relatively good day for Wall Street. The stock market was edging toward positive territory for the year. Europe was hashing out a deal to recapitalize its banks. And enraged protestors remained encamped at Zuccotti Park, letting bank chieftains breath easy in their Park Avenue palaces.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall Street’s ‘CrackBerry’ Withdrawal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BlackBerry (Handheld Device)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Research In Motion Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T19:32:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a39a8437-e237-592f-b446-134f2015af0c', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a39a8437-e237-592f-b446-134f2015af0c'}, {'abstract': 'Creating research projects to be conducted on the International Space Station.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/a-matter-of-gravity-developing-space-based-experiments/', 'snippet': 'Creating research projects to be conducted on the International Space Station.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | In this lesson, students read about a new contest seeking student science experiments to be conducted on the International Space Station. They learn more about space-based research, design experiments they would like to see carried out in microgravity and develop scripts for video pitches to promote their ideas. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Matter of Gravity: Developing Space-Based Experiments', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Space Station', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T19:38:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Cutraro and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cutraro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00ee00e1-43a0-5edb-8ac9-3c2a8dc05391', 'word_count': 1399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00ee00e1-43a0-5edb-8ac9-3c2a8dc05391'}, {'abstract': 'Celebrations spread quickly in Gaza City as details of the prisoner swap agreement became clearer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/world/middleeast/gazans-credit-hamas-in-prisoner-swap-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Celebrations spread quickly in Gaza City as details of the prisoner swap agreement became clearer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GAZA CITY — Palestinian joy erupted quickly in this isolated enclave at the first word of the Israeli-Palestinian prisoner swap agreement announced late Tuesday. And through the hours of Wednesday as the agreement’s details became clearer, the celebrations spread and Hamas, the governing authority here that rejects Israel’s legitimacy, claimed much of the credit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinians in Gaza Celebrate Prisoner Swap Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gazans Credit Hamas in Prisoner Swap Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shalit, Gilad', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mazen, Abu', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABBAS, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T19:40:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5f6740d-d2eb-5177-95cc-e4af98c2a016', 'word_count': 1263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5f6740d-d2eb-5177-95cc-e4af98c2a016'}, {'abstract': 'A 1932 house in Oak Grove, Ore.; a bungalow in Los Angeles; and a circa 1800 cabin with a modern addition in Hillsborough, N.C.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/greathomesanddestinations/real-estate-for-599000.html', 'snippet': 'A 1932 house in Oak Grove, Ore.; a bungalow in Los Angeles; and a circa 1800 cabin with a modern addition in Hillsborough, N.C.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OAK GROVE, ORE. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/realestate/13gh-wyg1/13gh-wyg1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/13/realestate/13gh-wyg1/13gh-wyg1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/realestate/13gh-wyg1/13gh-wyg1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,