stract': 'The reading list from our winter women’s fashion issue: “Chicks With Guns,” by Lindsay McCrum, “Adam and Evelyn,” by Ingo Schulze and “White Truffles in Winter,” by N. M. Kelby.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/bookshelf-11/', 'snippet': 'The reading list from our winter women’s fashion issue: “Chicks With Guns,” by Lindsay McCrum, “Adam and Evelyn,” by Ingo Schulze and “White Truffles in Winter,” by N. M. Kelby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Ingo Schulze’s cheery novel “Adam and Evelyn” (Knopf, $28), a lecherous East German dressmaker gets a bit too cozy with his comrade clientele, inciting his girlfriend to go on a sex-charged romp through newly democratic Hungary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bookshelf', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelby, N M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schulze, Ingo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knopf, Alfred A, Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T20:21:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/691cc112-8f5a-565e-ad80-fc8c946521da', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/691cc112-8f5a-565e-ad80-fc8c946521da'}, {'abstract': 'Facing condemnation from the West following the jailing of Yulia V. Tymoshenko, the Ukrainian government could decriminalize the law under which the opposition leader was prosecuted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/world/europe/tymoshenko-to-be-freed-from-jail-in-ukraine-soon-daughter-says.html', 'snippet': 'Facing condemnation from the West following the jailing of Yulia V. Tymoshenko, the Ukrainian government could decriminalize the law under which the opposition leader was prosecuted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIEV, Ukraine — For the last few months, the people who visited Yulia V. Tymoshenko in Detention Center No. 13 have been slipping something into the stacks of documents they bring her to read — the handwritten notes known in prison slang as “malyava,” exchanged by generations of Soviet inmates, who would crumple them into pea-sized balls or roll them into narrow cones and shoot them out of blowpipes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/world/13ukraine/13ukraine-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/world/13ukraine/13ukraine-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/13/world/13ukraine/13ukraine-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ukrainian Opposition Leader to Be Freed Soon, Daughter Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ukrainian Opposition Leader to Be Freed Soon, Daughter Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tymoshenko, Yulia V', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yanukovich, Viktor F', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T20:22:31+0000', 'd