 Tip of the Week explores Apple’s built-in Lion Recovery feature.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/10/12/technology/12techtalk_pod.html', 'snippet': 'The Times technology reporter Jenna Wortham discusses new free messaging services that let users text over a Wi-Fi connection without having to pay SMS fees to wireless carriers. Tiffany Shlain, the founder of the Webby Awards and the director of ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times technology reporter Jenna Wortham discusses new free messaging services that let users text over a Wi-Fi connection without having to pay SMS fees to wireless carriers. Tiffany Shlain, the founder of the Webby Awards and the director of the documentary, “Connected,” talks about making the film and her observations on the social impact of modern technology. Pedro Rafael Rosado gets a look at Pioneer AppRadio and the tech news roundup includes Facebook’s new iPad app, declining traffic to Google+ and the recent business U-turn by Netflix. Sam Grobart, the Personal Technology editor at The Times, previews his new article on life with a high-tech toilet. For Mac users wondering how to use repair utilities without a system DVD on Mac OS X 10.7, the Tip of the Week explores Apple’s built-in Lion Recovery feature.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Free text messages; Pioneer AppRadio; the documentary film “Connected”; tech news.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'