y solvent but thriving (revenue is racing ahead of last year by 16 percent), Sarah McNally has a limitless supply of small tricks up her sleeve. And a whirring, wheezing behemoth at her side.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/fashion/13UPCLOSE_SPAN/13UPCLOSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/13/fashion/13UPCLOSE_SPAN/13UPCLOSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/fashion/13UPCLOSE_SPAN/13UPCLOSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/fashion/13UPCLOSE_SPAN/13UPCLOSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/13/fashion/13UPCLOSE_SPAN/13UPCLOSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Her Life Is a Real Page-Turner', 'kicker': 'Up Close', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Her Life Is a Real Page-Turner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McNally Jackson Books', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'NoLIta (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-12T22:41:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jan Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bde95e64-a374-5d79-8625-151e354a3129', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bde95e64-a374-5d79-8625-151e354a3129'}, {'abstract': 'Events are scheduled to raise money to preserve the architect’s Brick House, across the lawn from his famous Glass House in New Canaan, Conn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/garden/saving-philip-johnsons-brick-house.html', 'snippet': 'Events are scheduled to raise money to preserve the architect’s Brick House, across the lawn from his famous Glass House in New Canaan, Conn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever wonder how Philip Johnson managed to live in a fishbowl? If he needed a nap, he sometimes walked across the lawn from his famous Glass House in New Canaan, Conn., to the lesser-known Brick House, where an upholstered bedroom, like something from the Arabian Nights, awaited. Perhaps to maintain the illusion that he needed nothing more than his house of windows, the Brick House was rarely shown in photos of its more-famous neighbor. Now the National Trust for Historic Preservation has begun to raise money to preserve the Brick House, which was completed in 1949 and has been closed to the public since 2008 because of problems that include leaks resulting in mold on silk wall coverings, furniture and books.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/garden/13EVENTS_SPAN/13EVENTS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/13/garden/13EVENTS_SPAN/13EVENTS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': 