ned in stages.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protesters Told to Vacate Park, for Its Cleaning', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protesters Told To Vacate Park, For Its Cleaning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookfield Properties Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T01:45:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f99309f-b9a1-56d3-b43f-f02f00785e38', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f99309f-b9a1-56d3-b43f-f02f00785e38'}, {'abstract': 'An alleged murder-for-hire plot is only the latest outrage from Tehran and another reminder of why the U.S. and its allies must use diplomatic and economic sanctions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/opinion/the-charges-against-iran.html', 'snippet': 'An alleged murder-for-hire plot is only the latest outrage from Tehran and another reminder of why the U.S. and its allies must use diplomatic and economic sanctions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charges that Iranian officials ordered the assassination of Saudi Arabia’s ambassador to the United States are chilling and bizarre. If true — and American officials insist they have strong evidence — this is only the latest reminder of why the United States and its allies must use all possible diplomatic and economic pressures to isolate Tehran and block its nuclear ambitions. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Charges Against Iran', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Charges Against Iran: An alleged murder-for-hire plot is only the latest outrage from Tehran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic Revolutionary Guards Corps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arbabsiar, Mansour J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jubeir, Adel al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suleimani, Qassim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zetas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T01:46:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6ec4410-c451-5371-a60f-b1a33e6fa7c9', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6ec4410-c451-5371-a60f-b1a33e6fa7c9'}, {'abstract': 'Three witnesses testified on Wednesday they had not worked as poll watchers for John F. Haggerty Jr., who is accused of stealing more than $1 million from the mayor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/nyregion/in-haggerty-trial-3-witnesses-rebut-consultants-claims.html', 'snippet': 'Three witnesses testified on Wednesday they had not worked as poll watchers for John F. Haggerty Jr., who is accused of stealing more than $1 million from the mayor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long after the 2009 mayoral election, a lawyer for Michael R. Bloomberg’s re-election campaign heard that a reporter was trying to track $1.2 million that Mr. Bloomberg had given to the Independence Party so that a political operative named John F. Haggerty Jr. could provide ballot security.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3 Witnesses Rebut Claim by Consultant on Poll Work', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '3 Witnesses Rebut Claim By Consultant On Poll Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haggerty, John F Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Witnesses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Special Election Operations LLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T01:48:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/273f4c6c-d97c-5c56-b51a-0aa0bd5e0eef', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/273f4c6c-d97c-5c56-b51a-0aa0bd5e0eef'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bloomberg supports a bill that would place sensible limits on the city’s efforts to help the federal government detain and deport illegal immigrants who pose no threat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/opinion/a-smart-immigration-move-at-rikers-island.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bloomberg supports a bill that would place sensible limits on the city’s efforts to help the federal government detain and deport illegal immigrants who pose no threat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Michael Bloomberg speaks often about the need for smart and humane immigration reform. He has now rightly thrown his support behind a City Council bill that would place sensible limits on how far New York City goes to help the federal government detain and deport illegal immigrants who pose no threat to the community.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Smart Immigration Move at Rikers', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Smart Immigration Move at Rikers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rikers Island Prison Complex', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value'