 Molesworth’s “Uncanny Tales” or C. Schweigger’s “Schweigger on Squint.” Perhaps you missed “How to Be Happy Though Married” or the Farmers’ Bulletin devoted to “House Rats and Mice.” No worries. They are available in 24 digital formats, including versions to suit just about any e-book reader you own. These titles, and millions more, are all out of copyright and part of the accelerating effort to digitize the public domain contents of the world’s libraries. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Curious Contents of the Digital Library', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Curious Contents of the Digital Library', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Books and Readers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T02:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/923e4261-b354-5613-b183-0c1f1762f547', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/923e4261-b354-5613-b183-0c1f1762f547'}, {'abstract': 'John Farmer demonstrates thematic elegance.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/12/proceeding/', 'snippet': 'John Farmer demonstrates thematic elegance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Administrivial Exciting New York Times Crossword Puzzle Contest Alert! Heads up, my friends: Will Shortz and one of our top constructors will hold a forehead-slapping puzzle contest involving next week’s puzzles that you will definitely want to get in on. Exact instructions will follow at the top of each day’s pu