to bomb a Detroit-bound airplane in 2009 abruptly pleads guilty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000001108679/timescast--plane-bomber-pleas-guilty.html', 'snippet': 'October 12, 2011 - In a surprising turn, the Nigerian man who tried to bomb a Detroit-bound airplane in 2009 abruptly pleads guilty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'October 12, 2011 - In a surprising turn, the Nigerian man who tried to bomb a Detroit-bound airplane in 2009 abruptly pleads guilty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/us/video-tc-111012-davey/video-tc-111012-davey-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/12/us/video-tc-111012-davey/video-tc-111012-davey-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/us/video-tc-111012-davey/video-tc-111012-davey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/12/us/video-tc-111012-davey/video-tc-111012-davey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | Plane Bomber Pleads Guilty', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abdulmutallab, Umar Farouk', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T03:40:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barakat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/3f32cf29-0a2d-5b1f-acaf-2161a6b9f405', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/3f32cf29-0a2d-5b1f-acaf-2161a6b9f405'}, {'abstract': 'A subpoena went to Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. for Justice Department documents related to the law enforcement program, called Fast and Furious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/us/politics/house-panel-issues-subpoena-for-records-on-fast-and-furious.html', 'snippet': 'A subpoena went to Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. for Justice Department documents related to the law enforcement program, called Fast and Furious.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A House committee subpoenaed the Obama administration on Wednesday over a law enforcement program that allowed illegal gun purchases in the United States in an effort to link the weapons to Mexican drug cartels. Representative Darrell Issa, Republican of California and chairman of the House Oversight and Government Reform Committee, said a subpoena went to Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. for Justice Department documents related to the program, called Fast and Furious. Mr. Issa has said that Mr. Holder provided misleading testimony to Congress on May 3 about when he first learned of Fast and Furious, which was overseen by the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives. A Justice Department spokeswoman, Tracy Schmaler, said that the department had already provided thousands of documents and made many officials available for interviews and testimony. “So any notion that the department isn’t working with the committee is simply wrong,” she said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Panel Issues Subpoena for Records on Gun Program', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Panel Issues Subpoena For Records on Gun Program', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Cartels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Oversight and Government Reform Committee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Issa, Darrell E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T03:45:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/517bee52-862f-516b-bbb4-35e99492bfab', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/517bee52-862f-516b-bbb4-35e99492bfab'}, {'abstract': 'Anti-Qaddafi forces said they were almost in control of Surt, the hometown of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/world/africa/libya-fighters-say-they-are-on-verge-of-capturing-surt.html', 'snippet': 'Anti-Qaddafi forces said they were almost in control of Surt, the hometown of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MISURATA, Libya — Anti-Qaddafi fighters said they had edged closer to capturing the coastal city of Surt on Wednesday, and commanders and journalists inside the city said the fighting appeared to be confined to just two areas of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi’s hometown. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/world/africa/Libya/Libya-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/13/world/africa/Libya/Libya-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/world/africa/Libya/Libya-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/world/africa/Libya/Libya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/13/world/africa/Libya/Libya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Libya Fighters Say Capture of Surt Is Near', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Libya Fighters Say Capture Of Surt Is Near', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Surt (Libya)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T03:46:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1db3e72f-7501-5e14-a3d0-bf7e70d843c5', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1db3e72f-7501-5e14-a3d0-bf7e70d843c5'}, {'abstract': 'As cities like Tampa, Fla., have joined in the protests begun in New York, news organizations across the country have also begun to take notice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/us/occupy-wall-street-protests-a-growing-news-story.html', 'snippet': 'As cities like Tampa, Fla., have joined in the protests begun in New York, news organizations across the country have also begun to take notice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. — Splashed across the front page of the local newspaper here on Tuesday was the story of a 24-year-old Occupy protester named Keith Cuesta. He was not in New York, where some have been living in a park near Wall Street for nearly four weeks, but about 1,000 miles away in Tampa, where a small group of self-described “99 percenters” have decided to camp out in solidarity.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/us/COVERAGE/COVERAGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/13/us/COVERAGE/COVERAGE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/13/us/COVERAGE/COVERAGE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A News Story Is Growing With ‘Occupy’ Protests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A News Story Is Growing With ‘Occupy’ Protests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T03:56:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlena