to Cure for Hepatitis', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hepatitis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liver', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:01:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d7c739e-0ed5-59f6-a7ce-ede3a34547af', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d7c739e-0ed5-59f6-a7ce-ede3a34547af'}, {'abstract': 'The fourth game of the A.L.C.S. was filled with intriguing decisions.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/the-strategies-of-game-4/', 'snippet': 'The fourth game of the A.L.C.S. was filled with intriguing decisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT – The fourth game of the American League Championship Series started more than two hours late, and it stretched across 4 hours and 11 innings. But it was all worth it — for the Texas Rangers, who beat the Detroit Tigers, 7-3, and for people who are fascinated by baseball strategy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Strategies of Game 4', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43d09b6e-9fdd-5c4e-b678-bb831455d18a', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43d09b6e-9fdd-5c4e-b678-bb831455d18a'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 96 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/word-of-the-day-gory/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 96 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'gory •\\ˈgȯr-e\\• adjective', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | gory', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7948b30f-8676-5427-9fcf-3196c17ef750', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7948b30f-8676-5427-9fcf-3196c17ef750'}, {'abstract': 'Ratings issued by the Insurance Institute for Highway Safety reflected significant improvements in the availability of top-rated seat models at all price points.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/booster-seats-continue-to-improve-i-i-h-s-finds/', 'snippet': 'Ratings issued by the Insurance Institute for Highway Safety reflected significant improvements in the availability of top-rated seat models at all price points.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Insurance Institute for Highway Safety, a nonprofit financed by the insurance industry, has issued a new round of booster-seat ratings in which the organization named a record 31 seats as Best Bets, the top grade offered in the survey. Another five seats were named Good Bets; more than 40 seats received the second-lowest rating, Check Fit; while six were rated Not Recommended.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Booster Seats Continue to Improve, I.I.H.S. Finds', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Insurance Institute for Highway Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:01:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90c6a742-cece-56c4-a996-7f53f7f94d1a', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90c6a742-cece-56c4-a996-7f53f7f94d1a'}, {'abstract': 'A healthy dose of peppers bring exactly the right amount of autumn heat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/magazine/roasted-chilies-bring-the-heat.html', 'snippet': 'A healthy dose of peppers bring exactly the right amount of autumn heat.', 'lead_paragraph': "The chili harvest of West Texas, southern New Mexico and Chihuahua, Mexico, begins in late summer and lasts through the first hard frost. You can encounter the smell of chilies roasting anywhere, with the frequency and randomness I associate with leaves burning in New England. I didn’t know this until I went to New Mexico, where I'd traveled for the Hatch Chile Festival, an event every native or long-termer politely advised me to avoid. (“Well, it’s a nice drive,” they’d say, and they were right about that.)", 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '64', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/magazine/16eat_span/mag-16Eat-t-000_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/16/magazine/16eat_span/mag-16Eat-t-000_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/magazine/16eat_span/mag-16Eat-t-000_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 780, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/magazine/16eat_span/mag-16Eat-t-000_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/magazine/16eat_span/mag-16Eat-t-000_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Roasted Chilies Bring the Heat', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Burn After Eating', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Peppers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chili (Food)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:03:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45d07ba0-bd7c-5de5-9170-98d2c3ff2c77', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45d07ba0-bd7c-5de5-9170-98d2c3ff2c77'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on October 13, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/pageoneplus/corrections-october-13.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on October 13, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: October 13', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:05:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/a77dd18a-26a4-5387-8d0d-59bccfa50182', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a77dd18a-26a4-5387-8d0d-59bccfa50182'}, {'abstract': 'A Virginia resident, Mohamad Anas Haitham Soueid, is accused of collecting information about people protesting in the United States against the Assad government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/us/syrian-american-is-accused-of-spying-for-syrian-government.html', 'snippet': 'A Virginia resident, Mohamad Anas Haitham Soueid, is accused of collecting information about people protesting in the United States against the Assad government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Justice Department on Wednesday accused a Syrian-American man of secretly working for a Syrian intelligence service. It said he collected information about people in the United States who were protesting the Syrian government’s crackdown on the country’s pro-democracy movement, as part of a scheme to “silence, intimidate and potentially harm the protesters.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian-American Is Arrested on Charges of Spying for Damascus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syrian-American Is Arrested on Charges of Spying for Damascus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:06:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage and J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7aadab41-6490-573d-940a-50f124f14779', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7aadab41-6490-573d-940a-50f124f14779'}, {'abstract': 'The government said Wednesday that it would reopen its investigation into the involvement of British forces in the 1989 killing of Patrick Finucane, a lawyer who had represented Irish Republic Army activists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/world/europe/ulster-inquiry-to-reopen-in-britain.html', 'snippet': 'The government said Wednesday that it would reopen its investigation into the involvement of British forces in the 1989 killing of Patrick Finucane, a lawyer who had represented Irish Republic Army activists.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The British government said Wednesday that it would reopen its investigation into the involvement of British forces in one of the most high-profile killings in Northern Ireland during the 30 years of violence known as the Troubles. But the decision to appoint a prominent British human rights lawyer to prepare a report on the extent of police and army “collusion” in the 1989 killing of Patrick Finucane, a lawyer who had represented Irish Republic Army activists, angered his family. They had demanded a full judicial inquiry similar to the one that was completed last year into the “Bloody Sunday” killings of 1972, when British troops shot and killed 13 unarmed Catholic protesters, with another protester dying later of his wounds. The $300 million cost of that inquiry, and the 12 years it took to complete, were cited by the government as reasons for not appointing a similar inquiry in the Finucane case. A previous inquiry had shown that Mr. Finucane was shot 14 times by Protestant gunmen as he ate a meal at his home with his wife and children. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: Ulster Inquiry to Reopen', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Ulster Inquiry to Reopen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finucane, Patrick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northern Ireland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:15:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe3c8342-6992-513c-b3a9-d17c8f579ab2', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe3c8342-6992-513c-b3a9-d17c8f579ab2'}, {'abstract': 'A report issued Wednesday by the European Union criticized Turkey’s reaction to recent gas drilling conducted by Cyprus. The EU also granted Serbia candidate status on Wednesday but refused to set a date to begin formal talks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/world/europe/european-report-criticizes-turkey-serbia-is-now-candidate-for-bloc.html', 'snippet': 'A report issued Wednesday by the European Union criticized Turkey’s reaction to recent gas drilling conducted by Cyprus. The EU also granted Serbia candidate status on Wednesday but refused to set a date to begin formal talks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A report issued Wednesday by the European Union enlargement office criticized Turkey’s reaction to recent gas drilling conducted by Cyprus in the Mediterranean, suggesting continued troubles with Turkey’s longstanding bid to join the bloc. Turkey refuses to recognize the Greek Cypriot government — itself a member of the bloc — as the sole representative of the disputed island and calls for the reunification of Turkish Cypriots in the north and Greek Cypriots in the south. Turkey has called the gas exploration by the Greek Cypriots an act of provocation and started its own seismic exploration program in the sea, escorted by the Turkish Navy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'European Report Criticizes Turkey; Serbia Is Now Candidate for Bloc', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'European Report Criticizes Turkey; Serbia Is Now Candidate for Bloc', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:24:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sebnem Arsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sebnem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b0bcc0d-ab8d-51f3-9ad6-fd96cebea4e5', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b0bcc0d-ab8d-51f3-9ad6-fd96cebea4e5'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister David Cameron has taken the first formal step toward a constitutional change that would allow girls and women to ascend to the British throne before their younger brothers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/world/europe/britain-first-steps-on-change-for-women-ascending-to-throne.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister David Cameron has taken the first formal step toward a constitutional change that would allow girls and women to ascend to the British throne before their younger brothers.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Prime Minister David Cameron has taken the first formal step toward a constitutional change that would allow girls and women to ascend to the British throne before their younger brothers. Mr. Cameron told the House of Commons on Wednesday that he had written to the governments of 15 other Commonwealth nations that recognize Queen Elizabeth as head of state urging their acceptance of a change in the succession rules set by the Act of Settlement, adopted in 1701, which stipulates that male children have precedence over their older sisters in succession to the throne. Mr. Cameron also urged that the law be changed to eliminate a prohibition on the accession of any monarch who is married to a Roman Catholic, calling the ban an “historical anomaly.” The changes are said to have broad support in the other Commonwealth nations, though some are said to have reservations about opening a discussion out of concern that it might reopen potentially acrimonious debate on whether the monarchy should be abolished. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: First Steps on Change for Women Ascending to Throne', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: First Steps on Change For Women Ascending to Throne', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:25:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/de25f77f-2de1-599b-aaa9-df3033f55519', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de25f77f-2de1-599b-aaa9-df3033f55519'}, {'abstract': 'Free text messages, the documentary film “Connected,” a high-tech toilet and the Pioneer AppRadio are the topics on this week’s podcast.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/tech-talk-podcast-texting-for-free/', 'snippet': 'Free text messages, the documentary film “Connected,” a high-tech toilet and the Pioneer AppRadio are the topics on this week’s podcast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Text-messaging plans and fees can add quite a bit of revenue to the coffers of the wireless carriers, but newer services for sending messages free over Wi-Fi networks may soon take a bite out of those profits. On this week’s Bits Tech Talk podcast, Jenna Wortham, a technology reporter at The Times, discusses her recent article about how free text apps like iMessage make cellphone users happy and carriers nervous.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tech Talk Podcast: Free Texting', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bathrooms and Toilets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:38:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81d7a666-cbf3-5d6e-98b0-8f1d5ed20d8f', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81d7a666-cbf3-5d6e-98b0-8f1d5ed20d8f'}, {'abstract': 'The original newspaper article on the laying of the cornerstone for St. Patrick’s Cathedral in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/10/13/nyregion/20111013-cornerstorn-document.html', 'snippet': 'The original newspaper article on the laying of the cornerstone for St. Patrick’s Cathedral in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The original newspaper article on the laying of the cornerstone for St. Patrick’s Cathedral in New York City.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New York Times, August 16, 1858', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:48:30+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/d3fb6877-e5b1-518a-9fe5-fdcf7a28aaf8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/d3fb6877-e5b1-518a-9fe5-fdcf7a28aaf8'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oct. 12, 2011', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:51:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/b52045a3-899d-52f7-ae49-37c269b2d16c', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b52045a3-899d-52f7-ae49-37c269b2d16c'}, {'abstract': 'A review of today’s issues in the press across India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/newswallah-in-the-english-language-press-thursday-4/', 'snippet': 'A review of today’s issues in the press across India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Industrial production slowed to 4.1 percent in August, raising fears that India’s economic growth could fall faster and further than analysts previously thought. Data showed a sharp decline in mining activity combined with slower growth in manufacturing. (Financial Express) One large Indian technology outsourcing company, Infosys, however, reported stronger growth in the three months ending in September, thanks in part to the declining rupee. (Mint)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: In the English-Language Press Thursday', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:52:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4086f06-ddf1-5c8f-956e-ccb52c89e691', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4086f06-ddf1-5c8f-956e-ccb52c89e691'}, {'abstract': 'Data showed that the schools were violating requirements on bilingual education, and that in 2010 those students had an on-time-graduation rate of only 7 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/education/13ell.html', 'snippet': 'Data showed that the schools were violating requirements on bilingual education, and that in 2010 those students had an on-time-graduation rate of only 7 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City schools are broadly failing to meet the needs of many of their thousands of students who are still learning English, and they must improve or they may face sanctions, state education officials announced Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State Puts Pressure on City Schools Over English Language Learners', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State Puts Pressure on City Schools Over English Language Learners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bilingual Education', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:54:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a213739b-0741-5a13-a935-13d4b42049fd', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a213739b-0741-5a13-a935-13d4b42049fd'}, {'abstract': 'Alternate-side street-cleaning regulations will be suspended in New York City on Thursday and Friday, because of Sukkot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/nyregion/parking-rules.html', 'snippet': 'Alternate-side street-cleaning regulations will be suspended in New York City on Thursday and Friday, because of Sukkot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alternate-side street-cleaning regulations will be suspended in New York City on Thursday and Friday, because of Sukkot. Other regulations will remain in effect.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parking Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Parking Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T04:56:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0bde9c5-96d1-5761-a3e1-94a04bf58f8f', 'word_count': 23, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0bde9c5-96d1-5761-a3e1-94a04bf58f8f'}, {'abstract': 'In an effort to secure financial security, a group of day laborers started their own cleaning company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/nyregion/cleaning-together-to-escape-day-labor.html', 'snippet': 'In an effort to secure financial security, a group of day laborers started their own cleaning company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After years of waiting on a Brooklyn street corner trying to land jobs cleaning houses, Teresa Bucio decided there had to be a better way to earn a living.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cleaning Together to Escape Day Labor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cleaning Together to Escape Day Labor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migrant and Foreign Workers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T05:03:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nadia Sussman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nadia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sussman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5227482f-21db-5364-8d65-06f8dd214625', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5227482f-21db-5364-8d65-06f8dd214625'}, {'abstract': 'Videos have begun to surface of oil leaking from the cargo ship Rena, which ran aground last week off the coast of New Zealand, as it makes landfall on nearby beaches.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/spilled-oil-makes-landfall-after-new-zealand-cargo-ship-accident/', 'snippet': 'Videos have begun to surface of oil leaking from the cargo ship Rena, which ran aground last week off the coast of New Zealand, as it makes landfall on nearby beaches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Videos of the cargo ship that became stuck on a reef off the coast of New Zealand a week ago were broadcast almost immediately, as the ship began spilling oil and debris. Now more have begun to surface, documenting the sludge-covered beaches as the leaked oil makes landfall. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spilled Oil Makes Landfall After New Zealand Cargo Ship Accident', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Zealand', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T05:04:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b4494ee-6f99-5122-ab1f-73798c6c440a',