aggoner were married Friday afternoon. Msgr. Lawrence Connaughton, a Roman Catholic priest, performed the ceremony at the Chapel of the Sacred Hearts of Jesus and Mary in New York, where he is the pastor.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/09MAZZAGETTIjpg/09MAZZAGETTIjpg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/09MAZZAGETTIjpg/09MAZZAGETTIjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/09MAZZAGETTIjpg/09MAZZAGETTIjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Elizabeth Mazzagetti, Keith Waggoner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Elizabeth Mazzagetti, Keith Waggoner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T16:11:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c6f8fed-864e-5724-9496-f1dc3baa2206', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c6f8fed-864e-5724-9496-f1dc3baa2206'}, {'abstract': '“Death Comes to Pemberley” involves Elizabeth Bennet in a murder investigation.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/p-d-james-writes-a-pride-and-prejudice-sequel-but-no-zombies/', 'snippet': '“Death Comes to Pemberley” involves Elizabeth Bennet in a murder investigation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In one of the more recent sequels to “Pride and Prejudice,” Elizabeth Bennet does battle with zombies, so it’s no great stretch to imagine her as a Regency-era crime sleuth. But the author who has done so is, of all people, P. D. James, the 91-year-old monarch of British crime fiction, better known for her novels about Adam Dalgleish, the brainy Scotland Yard detective who writes poetry on the side.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'P. D. James Writes a ‘Pride and Prejudice’ Sequel (but No Zombies)', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Jane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, P D', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knopf, Alfred A, Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T16:11:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88a2881a-c7de-5613-9633-19c6bbc7c0d3', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88a2881a-c7de-5613-9633-19c6bbc7c0d3'}, {'abstract': 'A wedding at Wellesley College in Massachusetts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/aniella-gonzalez-joseph-mccart-vi-weddings.html', 'snippet': 'A wedding at Wellesley College in Massachusetts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aniella Gonzalez and Joseph Donald McCart VI were married Saturday evening. The Rev. Sammy Chong, a Roman Catholic priest, performed the ceremony in Houghton Memorial Chapel at Wellesley College in Massachusetts. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/09GONZALEZjpg/09GONZALEZjpg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/09GONZALEZjpg/09GONZALEZjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/09GONZALEZjpg/09GONZALEZjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Aniella Gonzalez, Joseph McCart VI', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aniella Gonzalez, Joseph McCart VI', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T16:12:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57fc2e56-8931-5345-ae23-b444420d8f84', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57fc2e56-8931-5345-ae23-b444420d8f84'}, {'abstract': 'The couple spent two years commuting between Houston and New York; the decision to buy a ring came on vacation in Puerto Rico.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/leslie-mays-antonio-martin-weddings.html', 'snippet': 'The couple spent two years commuting between Houston and New York; the decision to buy a ring came on vacation in Puerto Rico.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leslie Ann Mays and Antonio Daniel Martin were married Friday in Houston. The Rev. Jude E. Ezuma, a Roman Catholic priest, performed the ceremony at the Co-Cathedral of the Sacred Heart. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/09MAYSjpg/09MAYSjpg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/09MAYSjpg/09MAYSjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/09MAYSjpg/09MAYSjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leslie Mays, Antonio Martin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leslie Mays, Antonio Martin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T16:14:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c636bef-2330-59c3-b171-9705c0f58b40', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c636bef-2330-59c3-b171-9705c0f58b40'}, {'abstract': 'Elle Muliarchyk’s latest project: a series of mesmerizing close-up video portraits of models delivering tongue twisters in their native tongues.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/read-their-lips/', 'snippet': 'Elle Muliarchyk’s latest project: a series of mesmerizing close-up video portraits of models delivering tongue twisters in their native tongues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Elle Muliarchyk grew up speaking half a dozen languages, from Czech to Vietnamese (her father was a diplomat and her mother was a journalist and a linguist), and during a brief career as a model she picked up some French and Italian. Her experience in the global village of fashion and her interest in languages come together in “Lips of Babel,” a series of mesmerizing close-up video portraits of models delivering tongue twisters in their native tongues. “Tongue twisters are something we all have from childhood,” Muliarchyk says, adding that they often say a lot about their culture of origin. One from Nigeria translates as “Lady Seamstress, why are you so sad? Did a hen lay an egg on the dress you just made?” while another, from India, says, “A husband slapped his wife for no apparent reason.” News of the project spread quickly through the modeling world — entirely by word of mouth — and Muliarchyk has captured 50 and counting. The first 24 are on view next week at Motilo.com, and one segment is available, above.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Read Their Lips', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T16:15:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92de5850-3301-5306-a45f-da8376cc9efe', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92de5850-3301-5306-a45f-da8376cc9efe'}, {'abstract': 'The bride, a broadcast journalist, and the bridegroom, a publishing executive, are to be married in Rome.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/faith-salie-john-semel-weddings.html', 'snippet': 'The bride, a broadcast journalist, and the bridegroom, a publishing executive, are to be married in Rome.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Faith Coley Salie and John Winston Semel are to be married Sunday in Rome. Giulio Mambrini, a friend of the couple who was deputized by the office of the mayor of Rome, is to officiate in the Campidoglio Wedding Hall. Later in the day, Robert Weiss, another friend of the couple, is to lead a separate ceremony with a reading from the Bible and from works of literature in front of family and friends at Casina Valadier, a restaurant in the Villa Borghese park in Rome. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/09SALIEjpg/09SALIEjpg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/09SALIEjpg/09SALIEjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/09/fashion/weddings/09SALIEjpg/09SALIEjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Faith Salie, John Semel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Faith Salie, John Semel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T16:18:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b945ea5d-1f80-58fd-80f3-3c6b04cded0c', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b945ea5d-1f80-58fd-80f3-3c6b04cded0c'}, {'abstract': 'An interactive timeline of Michele Bachmann’s life and career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/10/09/us/politics/20111009_BACHMANN_TIMELINE.html', 'snippet': 'An interactive timeline of Michele Bachmann’s life and career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An interactive timeline of Michele Bachmann’s life and career.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milestones: Michele Bachmann', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T16:19:34+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/3b9d5b6c-d4c0-58e5-8446-7b6952214c9b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/3b9d5b6c-d4c0-58e5-8446-7b6952214c9b'}, {'abstract': 'A recently released report highlights the spending patterns of public and private colleges and universities over the last decade.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/delta-project/', 'snippet': 'A recently released report highlights the spending patterns of public and private colleges and universities over the last decade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Delta Project, an independent research organization focused on college affordability, released a report last month that charts trends in university spending from 1999 to 2009.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline'