blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/at-some-indian-hotels-floors-for-women-only/', 'snippet': 'A chance for some girly pampering and an extra measure of security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For women, traveling alone can be challenging. But some hotels, like the ITC group of luxury hotels in India (the ITC Gardenia in Bengaluru is shown at right), are helping to make it more appealing by offering floors exclusively for female guests.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Some Indian Hotels, Floors for Women Only', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T16:40:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fd188c6-f472-51a5-a930-8f8a7a01a19f', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fd188c6-f472-51a5-a930-8f8a7a01a19f'}, {'abstract': 'The way we eat and the way we feed our children has more of an influence than we realize.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/changing-what-your-children-choose-to-eat/', 'snippet': 'The way we eat and the way we feed our children has more of an influence than we realize.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last spring, Allison Robicelli wrote an essay titled “Chicken Nuggets and French Fries: Confessions of a Mother and a Chef,” on Nona Brooklyn, and Lisa Belkin linked to it here on Motherlode. I read it; many of you did. We sympathized with the chef whose kid loved French fries best, and we had ideas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Changing What Your Children Choose to Eat', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T16:49:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Karin Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c271cc8-dd2a-5e19-b7f9-c07307a18dc8', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c271cc8-dd2a-5e19-b7f9-c07307a18dc8'}, {'abstract': 'In Florida, Gov. Rick Scott has suggested redirecting college funds from departments like anthropology to what he considers more practical disciplines like technology and math.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/rick-scott/', 'snippet': 'In Florida, Gov. Rick Scott has suggested redirecting college funds from departments like anthropology to what he considers more practical disciplines like technology and math.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those students interested in studying anthropology in college may want to do their homework before choosing to do so at a public institution in Florida.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida Governor Wants Funds to Go to Practical Degrees', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T16:50:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca R. Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '',