': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beneath Pedro Almodóvar’s ‘Skin’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Film Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALMODOVAR, PEDRO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banderas, Antonio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T18:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/622c14e3-b0dc-5187-9d09-032c932a4528', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/622c14e3-b0dc-5187-9d09-032c932a4528'}, {'abstract': 'A look at false equivalence and false inequivalence in the fight over climate change.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/on-false-equivalence-and-false-inequivalence/', 'snippet': 'A look at false equivalence and false inequivalence in the fight over climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just over a week ago, I wrote a quick post on a new sociological analysis of organized efforts to sow doubt about global warming. The analysis was illustrated by a flow chart of what the researchers called the “climate change denial machine.” I added an update a day later describing a chart of the “climate alarmism machine” created in response by an Australian blogger.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On False Equivalence and False Inequivalence', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value':