s.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/looking-inside-the-iphone-4s/', 'snippet': 'What’s inside an iPhone 4S? The team over at ifixit, a popular free repair Web site, dissected the new phone to see Apple’s latest chips and sensors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The team over at ifixit, a popular free repair manual Web site, has been busy dissecting Apple’s iPhone 4S like a frog in a science classroom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking Inside the iPhone 4S', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Chips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T19:51:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39f25ae6-f681-5d25-a0b4-e1670c977814', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39f25ae6-f681-5d25-a0b4-e1670c977814'}, {'abstract': 'Arguing in favor of just a little screen time for your very little one.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/is-a-little-tv-really-that-bad-for-babies/', 'snippet': 'Arguing in favor of just a little screen time for your very little one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Should babies watch TV? Of course, the American Academy of Pediatrics says no. But does “no” really mean no watching the Republican presidential debate while you nurse the baby, or locking the toddler out of the room while the kindergartner watches “Dora the Explorer”?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is a Little TV Really That Bad for Babies?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T19:54:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Karin Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/caf48388-592c-5baf-bd5b-7c3b62fc40e5', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caf48388-592c-5baf-bd5b-7c3b62fc40e5'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Dubin, an architect, became fascinated by trains as a child and went on to write two of the best-known works on American passenger railroads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/us/arthur-dubin-historian-of-railroads-golden-era-dies-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Dubin, an architect, became fascinated by trains as a child and went on to write two of the best-known works on American passenger railroads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arthur Dubin, a leading historian of the golden age of American passenger railroads, when trains bore names like ocean liners and Champagne glasses were filled by elegantly attired servers, died on Oct. 3 at a nursing home in Riverwoods, Ill. He was 88.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/us/14dubin/14dubin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 823, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/us/14dubin/14dubin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 