o-tc-111013/video-tc-111013-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | October 13, 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T20:06:57+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat|Emily B. Hager|Nadia Sussman|Adam B. Ellick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': 'Barakat', 'lastname': 'Emily', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/dd7eb6b0-dd23-5726-8819-ac500751b103', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/dd7eb6b0-dd23-5726-8819-ac500751b103'}, {'abstract': 'It keeps on hacking.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/hackitude/', 'snippet': 'It keeps on hacking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It really is hard having a conversation about, well, anything when the other side just rolls out the talking points instead of discussing the issues. And while I should be used to it, having it happen face to face still gets me. If you want to know what I’m talking about, watch Fareed Zakaria this weekend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hackitude', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T20:08:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e598cfea-6628-5e32-93cc-d57660ac9f60', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e598cfea-6628-5e32-93cc-d57660ac9f60'}, {'abstract': 'He is the first to hold the post since Riccardo Muti left six years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/la-scala-names-barenboim-music-director/', 'snippet': 'He is the first to hold the post since Riccardo Muti left six years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Teatro Alla Scala in Milan has appointed Daniel Barenboim as its music director, the first person to hold the title since Riccardo Muti left amid acrimony six years ago. Mr. Barenboim, who is also music director of the Staatsoper in Berlin, will take up the post on Dec. 1, on a five-year contract. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'La Scala Names Barenboim Music Director', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barenboim, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muti, Riccardo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'La Scala', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T20:08:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbf96545-3716-5005-b7d3-2e911d0022b6', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbf96545-3716-5005-b7d3-2e911d0022b6'}, {'abstract': 'The state’s Blue Shield said it had pledged to cap profits at 2 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/california-health-insurer-will-issue-refunds/', 'snippet': 'The state’s Blue Shield said it had pledged to cap profits at 2 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blue Shield of California, a large nonprofit health insurer based in San Francisco, said on Thursday that it planned to return an additional $295 million to its customers as part of the pledge it made earlier this year to cap its earnings to 2 percent of its revenue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California Health Insurer Will Issue Refunds', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'REFUNDS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Shield of California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T20:09:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30ac92fc-44bd-51e8-804a-592a2a012834', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30ac92fc-44bd-51e8-804a-592a2a012834'}, {'abstract': 'The competition is fierce at an antiques store in Bedford-Stuyvesant, Brooklyn that specializes in midcentury-modern furniture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/16/nyregion/20111116_JOINTss.html', 'snippet': 'The competition is fierce at an antiques store in Bedford-Stuyvesant, Brooklyn that specializes in midcentury-modern furniture.', 'lead_paragraph':