Queens that is being converted into an oasis of wetlands, plantings and nice benches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Feeling inspired? New York City is holding a naming contest for a soon-to-be-unveiled green space in Queens. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Name That Green Space in Queens', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Geographical', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island City (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'QUEENS PLAZA (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T20:12:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d77bf719-004f-5a74-90b8-05aac945d9b0', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d77bf719-004f-5a74-90b8-05aac945d9b0'}, {'abstract': 'Tabaimo, whose third New York solo show, “danDAN,” runs through Oct. 28 at James Cohan Gallery in Chelsea, seems unblemished by success.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/arts/design/tabaimo-video-show-at-james-cohan-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'Tabaimo, whose third New York solo show, “danDAN,” runs through Oct. 28 at James Cohan Gallery in Chelsea, seems unblemished by success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE thing is certain about the artist known as Tabaimo: her animated videos have never followed the fashion for kawaii, or cuteness, that has ruled Japanese contemporary art for years. Instead, they focus on the anxieties bubbling beneath the surface of everyday life. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16TABAIMO1_SPAN/16TABAIMO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16TABAIMO1_SPAN/16TABAIMO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16TABAIMO1_SPAN/16TABAIMO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16TABAIMO1_SPAN/16TABAIMO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16TABAIMO1_SPAN/16TABAIMO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cutting Through Cute to the Real Japan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cutting Through Cute To the Real Japan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cohan, James, Gallery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T20:12:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Kino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8f81792-f60b-572d-b75e-ed86526fa3e8', 'word_count': 1403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8f81792-f60b-572d-b75e-ed86526fa3e8'}, {'abstract': 'The Wall Street protests represent a refusal to engage the worn-out ideologies rooted in the Cold War.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/occupy-wall-streets-political-disobedience/', 'snippet': 'The Wall Street protests represent a refusal to engage the worn-out ideologies rooted in the Cold War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our language has not yet caught up with the political phenomenon that is emerging in Zuccotti Park and spreading across the nation, though it is clear that a political paradigm shift is taking place before our very eyes. It’s time to begin to name and in naming, to better understand this moment. So let me propose some words: “political disobedience.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Occupy Wall Street’s ‘Political Disobedience’', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cold War Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T20:15:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bernard E. Harcourt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bernard', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Harcourt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fd88e9b-0852-54c7-9f4e-0f9f8b66435e', 'word_count': 1530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fd88e9b-0852-54c7-9f4e-0f9f8b66435e'}, {'abstract': 'The police released surveillance video of a woman who they say has walked off with four purses hanging on the back of chairs at Katz’s and at Clinton Street Baking Company nearby.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/police-release-video-of-suspected-purse-stealer/', 'snippet': 'The police released surveillance video of a woman who they say has walked off with four purses hanging on the back of chairs at Katz’s and at Clinton Street Baking Company nearby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If she had simply had her hand in the pickle jar at one place — or if she had stuck a finger in the maple-butter dish at the other — this would be a different story, and probably more delectable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Someone Is Stealing Purses at Katz’s Deli', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delicatessens', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Katz's Delicatessen", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T20:16:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaa86744-8ce5-5add-86d5-eb3755d58e33', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaa86744-8ce5-5add-86d5-eb3755d58e33'}, {'abstract': 'Vernon Boulevard in Long Island City has resisted change. But now, it is an urban developer’s dream slowly coming true.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/realestate/vernon-boulevard-queens-block-by-block.html', 'snippet': 'Vernon Boulevard in Long Island City has resisted change. But now, it is an urban developer’s dream slowly coming true.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT 3:30 p.m. on a Tuesday in late September, three men were sitting at the sidewalk tables in front of Tournesol on Vernon Boulevard. Pascal Escriout, the Frenchman who owns the bistro, was sharing a bottle of Bordeaux with a couple of friends — Robert Gonçalves, his partner in Domaine Wine Bar a few doors down, and one of the guys from Sweetleaf, the coffee house over on Jackson Avenue.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/realestate/SUB-cover-block/SUB-cover-block-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/16/realestate/SUB-cover-block/SUB-cover-block-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/realestate/SUB-cover-block/SUB-cover-block-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 838, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/realestate/SUB-cover-block/SUB-cover-block-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/realestate/SUB-cover-block/SUB-cover-block-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Grit’s Days Are Numbered', 'kicker': 'Block by Block', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Grit’s Days Are Numbered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island City (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T20:17:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christian L. Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christian', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/153327e8-3f60-5042-a085-20c106929e85', 'word_count': 1127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/153327e8-3f60-5042-a085-20c106929e85'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama will push for what he calls the “toughest sanctions” to punish Iranian officials whom he accused of complicity in a suspected plot to kill the Saudi ambassador to the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/us/obama-calls-for-iran-sanctions-following-alleged-plot.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama will push for what he calls the “toughest sanctions” to punish Iranian officials whom he accused of complicity in a suspected plot to kill the Saudi ambassador to the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama vowed on Thursday to push for what he called the “toughest sanctions” against Iran, saying that the United States had strong evidence that Iranian officials were complicit in an alleged plot to kill the Saudi ambassador to the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'ju