'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/2cdc7ce3-9b2b-5042-9ec6-e81eafb0b1ca', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/2cdc7ce3-9b2b-5042-9ec6-e81eafb0b1ca'}, {'abstract': 'The Cloud Gate Dance Theater of Taiwan, performing “Water Stains on the Wall” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music through Saturday, shows its love of dynamic contrasts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/arts/dance/cloud-gate-dance-theater-of-taiwan-at-bam-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Cloud Gate Dance Theater of Taiwan, performing “Water Stains on the Wall” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music through Saturday, shows its love of dynamic contrasts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a political even-handedness that deserves a place in the annals of diplomacy, the Brooklyn Academy of Music is presenting the Cloud Gate Dance Theater of Taiwan this week and the Beijing Dance Theater next week. If I too were diplomatic, I would confine my response to Cloud Gate’s “Water Stains on the Wall” — choreographed by the company’s founder and artistic director, Lin Hwai-min, with its first New York performance on Wednesday evening — to describing the many respects in which it is truly admirable. Instead, however, I start by saying that it left me cold throughout its almost 75 minutes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14water/WATER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1017, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14water/14water-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14water/14wate