y cars, the designer Jason Castriota is hoping to begin a new era at the struggling carmaker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/automobiles/saabs-new-visionary-hopes-for-salvation.html', 'snippet': 'With a pedigree chock-full of legendary cars, the designer Jason Castriota is hoping to begin a new era at the struggling carmaker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT last spring’s New York auto show, Jason Castriota worked hard. Hour after hour, he stood explaining to group after group of visitors the idea behind his futuristic Saab PhoeniX concept car.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/automobiles/PATTONDESIGN/PATTONDESIGN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 895, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Vision for Saab, Perhaps Too Late to Save It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Vision for Saab, Perhaps Too Late to Save It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saab Automobile AB', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T22:41:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e193eaf0-fe33-59a9-b3c6-cc868a352d3b', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e193eaf0-fe33-59a9-b3c6-cc868a352d3b'}, {'abstract': 'The car, a coal-black 1909 Alco-6 Racer, was one of the most famous of its era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/automobiles/mechanical-wonder-from-an-age-gone-by.html', 'snippet': 'The car, a coal-black 1909 Alco-6 Racer, was one of the most famous of its era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONG, strong and dangerous, like a gun barrel mounted on spoke wheels, the coal-black 1909 Alco-6 Racer gleams in the late summer sunlight.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/automobiles/PARKWAY1/PARKWAY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/14/automobiles/PARKWAY1/PARKWAY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/automobiles/PARKWAY1/PARKWAY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/automobiles/PARKWAY1/PARKWAY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/14/automobiles/PARKWAY1/PARKWAY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mechanical Wonder From an Age Gone By', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mechanical Wonder From an Age Gone By', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T22:41:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Hanc', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hanc', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/595de1dd-bbe3-5f08-a832-f7583c1617d8', 'word_count': 934, 'uri': 'nyt://article/595de1dd-bbe3-5f08-a832-f7583c1617d8'}, {'abstract': 'Despite doubts about an alleged Iranian plot, an adviser to the Saudi government seemed to up the ante by claiming that one of the accused plotters was also involved in a conspiracy to incite protests in Bahrain earlier this year.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/saudi-ties-alleged-iranian-plot-to-claims-bahrian-unrest-was-orchestrated-from-iran/', 'snippet': 'Despite doubts about an alleged Iranian plot, an adviser to the Saudi government seemed to up the ante by claiming that one of the accused plotters was also involved in a conspiracy to incite protests in Bahrain earlier this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | Friday | 11:37 a.m. While a number of prominent experts on Iran are not convinced that the Iranian government really did authorize a plot to assassinate Saudi Arabia’s ambassador in Washington — with the help of a Mexican drug cartel and a used-car salesman — one well-connected Saudi commentator insists that the scheme was real, and part of a much broader conspiracy against his nation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saudi Claims Alleged Iranian Plotter Also Orchestrated Bahrain Unrest', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Faisal, Turki al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakuri, Gholam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 4, 'major':