ared in power or zaniness with the family of Joseph Medill at its height. Born in 1823, Medill was a fervent abolitionist, one of the founders of the Republican Party, and is perhaps most notable for having helped put Abraham Lincoln over as his party’s candidate in the 1860 presidential election. In 1855 Medill bought a one-third ownership of The Chicago Daily Trib\xadune, and eventually controlled the majority stock in the paper, which he took great care before his death in 1899 to make certain stayed in his family.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/books/review/epsteininside1/epsteininside1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 832, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/books/review/epsteininside1/epsteininside1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/12/books/review/epsteininside1/epsteininside1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dynasts of the Daily Press', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dynasts of the Daily Press', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Amanda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKinney, Megan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T22:42:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Epstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Epstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e4c2154-c524-5861-bf28-3d83e3659067', 'word_count': 1276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e4c2154-c524-5861-bf28-3d83e3659067'}, {'abstract': 'Their politics differ, but the Occupy Wall Street and Tea Party movements agree on one thing.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/protesting-the-establishment/', 'snippet': 'Their politics differ, but the Occupy Wall Street and Tea Party movements agree on one thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Their politics differ, but the Occupy Wall Street and Tea Party movements agree on one thing. Kate Zernike reports from Atlanta. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protesting the Establishment', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T22:45:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81463f89-cd95-5921-86aa-a996803e1eb8', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81463f89-cd95-5921-86aa-a996803e1eb8'}, {'abstract': 'The president called to congratulate him, but had said something that Speaker John A. Boehner said he had to respond to.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/obamas-call-to-boehner-goes-off-message/', 'snippet': 'The president called to congratulate him, but had said something that Speaker John A. Boehner said he had to respond to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama called Speaker John A. Boehner on Thursday to congratulate him on the passage of long-stalled free trade agreements with South Korea, Colombia and Panama. But something else the president said rang in Mr. Boehner’s ears — that Republicans had offered no real alternative to Mr. Obama’s $447 billion job creation plan — and the speaker then tried to set the record straight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Call to Boehner Goes Off Message', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T22:52:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f39ec5f9-acc9-5f5b-9ef8-4f63acc7a6d0', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f39ec5f9-acc9-5f5b-9ef8-4f63acc7a6d0'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the work of the artist known as Tabaimo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/16/arts/design/20111016-TABAIMO.html', 'snippet': 'A look at the work of the artist known as Tabaimo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look at the work of the artist known as Tabaimo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/20111016-TABAIMO-slide-LT34/20111016-TABAIMO-slide-LT34-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/20111016-TABAIM