 Beach,” a documentary about an abandoned California wonderland that still holds wonder for some of its residents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/movies/bombay-beach-documenting-faded-glory-review.html', 'snippet': '“Bombay Beach,” a documentary about an abandoned California wonderland that still holds wonder for some of its residents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Palm Springs-by-the-Sea it is not. That slogan belonged to a vintage advertising campaign, glimpsed in “Bombay Beach,” for a waterside paradise on the edge of the Salton Sea in the southern California desert. In the 1950s and ’60s, this 385-square-mile body of water, created in 1905 when the rampaging Colorado River spilled over its banks, became a celebrity magnet and tourist destination. But its vogue quickly faded.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14BOMBAY_SPAN/BOMBAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14BOMBAY_SPAN/BOMBAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14BOMBAY_SPAN/BOMBAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14BOMBAY_SPAN/BOMBAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14BOMBAY_SPAN/BOMBAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Last Resort Remains an Oasis of Dreams', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Bombay Beach'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_hea