ovements according to its maker.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Prepare for iOS 5', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPod', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iCloud', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T23:33:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Boutin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boutin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ca05359-abcf-578e-bf79-a83ab04eced5', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ca05359-abcf-578e-bf79-a83ab04eced5'}, {'abstract': 'Speculation season is officially under way, as the Academy of Motion Picture Arts & Sciences announced 63 films that will be in the running for an Oscar in February.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/academy-unveils-entrants-for-best-foreign-language-film/', 'snippet': 'Speculation season is officially under way, as the Academy of Motion Picture Arts & Sciences announced 63 films that will be in the running for an Oscar in February.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Academy of Motion Picture Arts & Sciences on Thursday announced the 63 films that will be in the running in February for the Oscar for best foreign-language film, so the speculation season is now officially under way. New Zealand, which submitted “The Orator,” by the Maori director Tusi Tamasese, will be competing in the category for the first time, but the list of nominees, down by two countries compared with last year, includes many familiar names.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Academy Unveils Entrants for Best Foreign-Language Film', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T23:33:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/100ebbf8-5ba4-5140-a1ec-8e2ec7db6a85', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/100ebbf8-5ba4-5140-a1ec-8e2ec7db6a85'}, {'abstract': '“Fireflies in the Garden” toggles between a family’s present-tense strained relationships and a writer’s memories of his unhappy childhood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/movies/fireflies-in-the-garden-with-ryan-reynolds-review.html', 'snippet': '“Fireflies in the Garden” toggles between a family’s present-tense strained relationships and a writer’s memories of his unhappy childhood.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Fireflies in the Garden,” a family melodrama about coming to terms with your parents (they’re people too, as it turns out), weighs in as such an innocuous appeal to the heart that it hardly seems deserving of the critical lash. The familiarity of its milieu, its characters and their hurts and grievances, recall any number of other movies. What’s striking about this one, though, is how its predictability can seem like a hedge or maybe a defense against the very possibility of surprise.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14FIRE_SPAN/14FIRE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14FIRE_SPAN/14FIRE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14FIRE_SPAN/FIRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14FIRE_SPAN/14FIRE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14FIRE_SPAN/14FIRE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hometown Visit, en Route to the Past', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Fireflies in the Garden'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Hometown Visit, En Route to the Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Dennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dafoe, Willem', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reynolds, Ryan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Emily', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moss, Carrie-Anne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, Julia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T23:39:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b6d1f0d-7029-5200-bbc0-801e6abb37e2', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b6d1f0d-7029-5200-bbc0-801e6abb37e2'}, {'abstract': 'In Bedford-Stuyvesant, casaBAN has set out to offer fresh, distinctive antiques in an area filled with historic, heavily ornamented brownstones.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/casaban/', 'snippet': 'In Bedford-Stuyvesant, casaBAN has set out to offer fresh, distinctive antiques in an area filled with historic, heavily ornamented brownstones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I walk by the shop occasionally, and its window display has come to seem like a cruel magic trick. One day, an Indonesian stool stood front and center, begging for a privileged spot in my apartment; the next day, when I returned for a second look, it was gone. I was also obsessed with an edgy rocking chair: printed velvety cushions on a low-slung white frame with clean Danish lines. I had steeled myself to resist, but last week it was still reclining in the window, almost mockingly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Antiques That Offer a Taste of the Modern', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bedford-Stuyvesant (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T23:45:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Okeowo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Okeowo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf4b411b-615f-5b8d-8821-ea04505271d0', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf4b411b-615f-5b8d-8821-ea04505271d0'}, {'abstract': 'In “Trespass,” directed by Joel Schumacher, a band of ragtag blue-collar types take over the glamorous house of Kyle Miller, a diamond trader up to his eyeballs in debt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/movies/trespass-with-nicolas-cage-and-nicole-kidman-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Trespass,” directed by Joel Schumacher, a band of ragtag blue-collar types take over the glamorous house of Kyle Miller, a diamond trader up to his eyeballs in debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the addled mind of the home-invasion thriller “Trespass” are a few half-baked notions about class warfare in America. Kyle Miller (Nicolas Cage), a loudmouthed wheeler-dealer whose glamorous house is taken over by thieves disguised as policemen, is a shady, fast-talking diamond trader up to his bulging eyeballs in debt. So much for privilege.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14TRESPASS_SPAN/TRESPASS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14TRESPASS_SPAN/TRESPASS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/arts/14TRESPASS_SPAN/TRESPASS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/