preacher who had been detained for 12 days by the Afghan intelligence service arrived at a hospital badly beaten, suffering from kidney failure, and slipping in and out of consciousness, said doctors at the hospital and local health clinic where he was treated Thursday. They said they were not sure he would survive. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Preacher Held by Afghan Spy Agency Is Near Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Preacher Held By Spy Agency In Afghanistan Is Near Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-13T23:50:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/440eaad7-dca0-54d6-91cf-50fa24d829e0', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/440eaad7-dca0-54d6-91cf-50fa24d829e0'}, {'abstract': 'Video game makers are addicted to sequels.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/return-of-the-video-game-sequel-part-12/', 'snippet': 'Video game makers are addicted to sequels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There may not be an entertainment category that is so predictable as video games. The latest video game sales figures came out Thursday from NPD, which measures sales of consumer products. And the list of best-selling games looks very famil