ian chalet of a rich family (Brooke Shields, Bill Nighy and Ed Westwick). There she parlays her skills as a former skateboarding champ into snowboarding, becoming an ace while battling class prejudice and catching the eye of the family’s son, Jonny (Mr. Westwick).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/movies/14RDP_CHALETSPAN/14RDP_CHALETSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/14/movies/14RDP_CHALETSPAN/14RDP_CHALETSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/movies/14RDP_CHALETSPAN/14RDP_CHALETSPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/movies/14RDP_CHALETSPAN/14RDP_CHALETSPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/14/movies/14RDP_CHALETSPAN/14RDP_CHALETSPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Multitasking on the Slopes', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Chalet Girl'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Felicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T00:26:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/41cf938f-f394-51e8-b0b5-62b66a36aa35', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41cf938f-f394-51e8-b0b5-62b66a36aa35'}, {'abstract': 'Herman Cain’s 9-9-9 tax plan is a truly terrible idea.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/cold-pizza-from-herm-cain/', 'snippet': 'Herman Cain’s 9-9-9 tax plan is a truly terrible idea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By almost any measure — social, political, economic, logical — Herman Cain’s 9-9-9 tax plan is nuts, nuts, nuts. Go ahead and jack up the price of nearly everything that moves in the United States with a 9 percent national sales tax on all new purchases and services. Talk about instant branding: every time you buy something, you’ll be hit with the Herm Cain tax at the checkout line. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cold Pizza from Herm Cain', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T00:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59a6e646-c13c-5daa-a397-8d2ec2fd850e', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59a6e646-c13c-5daa-a397-8d2ec2fd850e'}, {'abstract': 'Youth courts help keep minor offenders out of the juvenile justice system and offer more chances for a better future.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/13/for-teen-offenders-hope-in-a-jury-of-their-peers/', 'snippet': 'Youth courts help keep minor offenders out of the juvenile justice system and offer more chances for a better future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Juvenile justice is a field where the cure aggravates the disease.\xa0 Take a kid of 15 or who shoplifts, gets into a fight, is caught with marijuana or is out at night spray-painting graffiti with a gang.\xa0 He’s no hardened criminal — yet.\xa0 After a tour through the juvenile justice system, however, he may well be.\xa0 He’ll be mixed in with real criminals, in an environment where violence is the only path to respect.\xa0 He’ll understand what society expects of him:\xa0 more crime.\xa0\xa0 Perhaps most important, he’ll have a criminal record — a major deterrent to getting a job.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Young Offenders, Hope in a Jury of Their Peers', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T00:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbc9d00e-6513-54a2-861b-ac2a27dcac3c', 'word_count': 1576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbc9d00e-6513-54a2-861b-ac2a27dcac3c'}, {'abstract': 'A police officer testified about how rules were broken so that narcotics officers could make their monthly quotas of arrests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/nyregion/those-drugs-they-came-from-the-police.html', 'snippet': 'A police officer testified about how rules were broken so that narcotics officers could make their monthly quotas of arrests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time he saw the chewing-tobacco can, Steve Anderson, a former undercover police officer, testified, it was in a book bag on the floor of a car that he and other undercover officers were using in a buy-and-bust operation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Drugs? They Came From the Police', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Drugs? They Came From the Police', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption in Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T00:31:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/526c0e11-9d57-558c-bdca-6066cf0822d4', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/526c0e11-9d57-558c-bdca-6066cf0822d4'}, {'abstract': 'Ford’s unionized workers, who haven’t received a raise in years, are upset with the big payouts to the company’s senior management.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/business/autoworkers-early-vote-on-ford-contract-is-negative.html', 'snippet': 'Ford’s unionized workers, who haven’t received a raise in years, are upset with the big payouts to the company’s senior management.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Voting by Ford’s unionized workers on a new contract has been unexpectedly negative, signaling a rejection of its hold-the-line pay provisions and raising at least the possibility that Detroit’s fragile labor peace could be disrupted by a strike.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/business/Auto1/Auto1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/14/business/Auto1/Auto1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/business/Auto1/Auto1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/business/Auto1/Auto1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/14/business/Auto1/Auto1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Resistance From Union in Ford Vote', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Resistance From Union In Ford Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Automobile Workers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'na