far beyond the legal issues in the case: unraveling workers’ rights that have been part of the fabric of our social contract since the Great Depression.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Labor Rights, Under Republican Attack', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Labor Rights, Under Republican Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Labor Relations Board', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T00:51:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Barenberg, James Brudney and Karl Klare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brudney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Karl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4feb5037-c170-5e45-8dfb-eb25c401042e', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4feb5037-c170-5e45-8dfb-eb25c401042e'}, {'abstract': 'The N.L.C.S. between the St. Louis Cardinals and the Milwaukee Brewers calls to mind the Budweiser and Miller beer rivalry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/sports/baseball/budweiser-miller-rivalry-part-of-brewers-cardinals-nlcs.html', 'snippet': 'The N.L.C.S. between the St. Louis Cardinals and the Milwaukee Brewers calls to mind the Budweiser and Miller beer rivalry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly 30 years on, Tony Ponturo still remembers how exciting it was to be recruited for the job of a lifetime. An advertising executive at the agency that handled the Anheuser-Busch account, Ponturo was flown to St. Louis during the 1982 World Series, in which the hometown Cardinals were playing the Milwaukee Brewers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/sports/y-breweries/y-breweries-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/sports/y-breweries/y-breweries-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/14/sports/y-breweries/y-breweries-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind a Baseball Rivalry, a Battle of Beer Companies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Behind a Baseball Rivalry, a Battle of Beer Companies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miller Brewing Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milwaukee (Wis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Louis (Mo)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anheuser-Busch InBev N.V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Brewers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T00:54:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36f02f0e-45b4-53cb-8603-14c9907de824', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36f02f0e-45b4-53cb-8603-14c9907de824'}, {'abstract': 'Surging global demand for natural gas may make the billions in infrastructure investments needed to export it make sense.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/business/outlook-brightens-for-us-gas-exports.html', 'snippet': 'Surging global demand for natural gas may make the billions in infrastructure investments needed to export it make sense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s enough to make aspiring American natural gas exporters salivate. In Asia, the “clean” hydrocarbon now fetches four times its price at home. But such a price gap must last decades to justify the infrastructure investments required to make exports possible. Still, surging global demand and booming drilling in the United States mean such outlays might now make sense.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 799, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None