 to enlist the services of a professional installer to get some of these devices working.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/automobiles/14tech/14tech-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 699, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/automobiles/14tech/14tech-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/14/automobiles/14tech/14tech-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Gadgets, Without the New Car', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Gadgets, Without the New Car', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Audiovox Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'OnStar Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T01:01:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By John R. Quain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Quain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/162ce944-2c07-5273-9aae-2cf375cf5218', 'word_count': 1116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/162ce944-2c07-5273-9aae-2cf375cf5218'}, {'abstract': 'Zuccotti Park was created by the developers of 1 Liberty Plaza in exchange for the relaxation of some zoning rules.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/nyregion/zuccotti-park-is-privately-owned-but-open-to-the-public.html', 'snippet': 'Zuccotti Park was created by the developers of 1 Liberty Plaza in exchange for the relaxation of some zoning rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Zuccotti Park, the half-acre plaza in Lower Manhattan now synonymous with Occupy Wall Street, exists in a strange category of New York parkland, identified by a seeming oxymoron: a privately owned public space.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/nyregion/JP-PARKS/JP-PARKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/nyregion/JP-PARKS/JP-PARKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/14/nyregion/JP-PARKS/JP-PARKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Privately Owned Park, Open to the Public, May Make Its Own Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Privately Owned Park, Open to the Public, May Make Its Own Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookfield Office Properties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Financial District (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T01:04:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa W. Foderaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Foderaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organiza