 report suggests results from its peers could be worse. That gloomy outlook reflects the economy and the failures of the banks themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the first of the major banks to report its earnings each quarter, JPMorgan Chase is a barometer of conditions in the financial industry. The mercury is falling. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Banks Falter', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Banks Falter: A gloomy outlook on profits reflects the economy, but also bankers’ own failures', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welch, Peter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T01:24:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ac0c918-9ef5-5751-9c46-d2d4a296d57e', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ac0c918-9ef5-5751-9c46-d2d4a296d57e'}, {'abstract': 'The guilty plea by the so-called Underwear Bomber and charges in an assassination plot linked to Iran have people arguing again about whether terrorism cases are better handled in the criminal justice system or by the military.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/us/debate-is-renewed-over-approach-for-terrorism-suspects.html', 'snippet': 'The guilty plea by the so-called Underwear Bomber and charges in an assassination plot linked to Iran have people arguing again about whether terrorism cases are better handled in the criminal justice system or by the military.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The guilty plea by the so-called Underwear Bomber and charges in an assassination plot linked to Iran have added new fuel this week to the simmering debate over whether terrorism cases are better handled in the criminal justice system or by the military. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/14/world/14interrogate1/14interrogate1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Developments Rekindle Debate Over Best Approach for Terrorism Suspects', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Developments Rekindle Debate Over Best Approach for Terrorism Suspects', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interrogations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Miranda v Arizona (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arbabsiar, Mansour J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abdulmutallab, Umar Farouk', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brennan, John O', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Armed Services', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'va