gan to tame strongly rising prices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/business/global/inflation-in-china-eases-but-food-prices-up-sharply.html', 'snippet': 'Inflation slowed slightly for consumers last month in China as stringent controls on bank lending and a gradually strengthening currency began to tame strongly rising prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Inflation slowed slightly for consumers last month in China and slowed a little more at factories, as stringent controls on bank lending and a gradually strengthening currency began to tame strongly rising prices, data released by the Chinese government on Friday showed.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inflation in China Eases, but Food Prices Up Sharply', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inflation in China Eases, but Food Prices Up Sharply', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T03:38:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc121e97-4d7c-52ec-b21a-21fd871aa309', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc121e97-4d7c-52ec-b21a-21fd871aa309'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi said Thursday that his government was the only “credible alternative” capable of leading Italy through the economic crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/world/europe/italy-prime-minister-faces-confidence-vote.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi said Thursday that his government was the only “credible alternative” capable of leading Italy through the economic crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi said Thursday that his government was the only “credible alternative” capable of leading Italy through the economic crisis. His government faces a confidence vote in Parliament on Friday. If he loses it, he will be forced to step down. On Tuesday, the government unexpectedly failed to pass routine legislation, prompting the call for the confidence vote. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy: Premier Faces Confidence Vote', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Premier Faces Confidence Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T03:38:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5138955-01ce-55f5-8b35-90710eaf78a7', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5138955-01ce-55f5-8b35-90710eaf78a7'}, {