w about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/news-quiz-oct-14-2011/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | Oct. 14, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T08:30:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Frasier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frasier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b356738-5960-5b69-b83c-d93698a65f60', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b356738-5960-5b69-b83c-d93698a65f60'}, {'abstract': '6 Q’s About the News | Why is there tension surrounding mixed race relationships?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/racial-tensions-for-mixed-families/', 'snippet': '6 Q’s About the News | Why is there tension surrounding mixed race relationships?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHO is Heather Greenwood?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Racial Tensions for Mixed Families', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T08:45:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98d2324d-6db9-53ff-b318-cdd7276d795d', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98d2324d-6db9-53ff-b318-cdd7276d795d'}, {'abstract': 'Jules Allen went to Gleason’s Gym to train. He stayed to make pictures of a smoke-filled world where boxing champs duked it out daily amid dreamers and hustlers, the up and coming and the down and out.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/the-sweet-science-of-body-and-soul/', 'snippet': 'Jules Allen went to Gleason’s Gym to train. He stayed to make pictures of a smoke-filled world where boxing champs duked it out daily amid dreamers and hustlers, the up and coming and the down and out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It wasn’t exactly a sucker punch, but Jules Allen was struck by what he found upon entering into Gleason’s Gym: sweat-soaked champs and punch-drunk pugs. Gangsters and posers. Men with hats, stogies and secrets. The leonine and the louche. Wiry trainers possessed of supreme cool and confidence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sweet Science of Body and Soul', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T09:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20a2f4bb-0d7b-5753-9184-91dcd483e63e', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20a2f4bb-0d7b-5753-9184-91dcd483e63e'}, {'abstract': 'Was the person synonymous with multiple-personality disorder nothing more than an invention?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/magazine/a-girl-not-named-sybil.html', 'snippet': 'Was the person synonymous with multiple-personality disorder nothing more than an invention?', 'lead_paragraph': '“What about Mama?” the psychiatrist asks her patient. “What’s Mama been doing to you, dear? . . . I know she gave you the enemas. And I know she filled your bladder up with cold water, and I know she used the flashlight on you, and I know she stuck the washcloth in your mouth, cotton in your nose so you couldn’t breathe. . . . What else did she do to you? It’s all right to talk about it now. . . . ”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '56', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/magazine/16sybil1/mag-16sybil-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 786, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/magazine/16sybil1/16sybil1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/magazine/16sybil1/16sybil1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Girl Not Named Sybil', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Girl Not Named Sybil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Multiple Personalities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T09:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Debbie Nathan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Debbie', 'middlenam