International Contemporary Art Fair, or FIAC, one of the world’s grandest such events, which will be held this year from Oct. 20 to 23.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Always an art lover’s paradise, Paris outdoes itself during the sprawling International Contemporary Art Fair, or FIAC, one of the world’s grandest such events, which will be held this year from Oct. 20 to 23. Centered in the glorious — and recently renovated — Grand Palais, it also extends to the Jardin des Tuileries, Jardin des Plantes, the Museum of Natural History and other institutions throughout the city. Altogether 168 galleries from 21 countries will show paintings, sculptures, installations and more ephemeral works of art. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Annual Art Fair Sprawls Across Paris', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grand Palais', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Musee d'Art Moderne de la Ville de Paris", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pompidou Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tuileries Gardens', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T10:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerie Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f7f2ac8-5d9d-5e5b-a7e2-4655e48deeca', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f7f2ac8-5d9d-5e5b-a7e2-4655e48deeca'}, {'abstract': 'Though now working for a luxury car dealership in Greenwich, Conn., Evan M. Cygler is still very much the 15-year-old who turned his fascination with collector cars into a concours.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/founder-of-scarsdale-concours-retains-a-soft-spot-for-classics/', 'snippet': 'Though now working for a luxury car dealership in Greenwich, Conn., Evan M. Cygler is still very much the 15-year-old who turned his fascination with collector cars into a concours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Evan M. Cygler and his fellow Scarsdale High School classmate Denis O’Leary III decided in 2003 to put together the first Scarsdale Concours d’Élégance, Mr. Cygler figured that if it was successful, it might come back for a couple years, raise a little money for Westchester County charities and provide some entertainment for the two car enthusiasts — who at the time were 15-year-old sophomores — before they left for college.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Founder of Scarsdale Concours Retains a Soft Spot for Classics', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Automobili Lamborghini SpA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scarsdale High School', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich (Conn)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scarsdale (NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T10:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carla Baranauckas', 'person': [{'firstname': 