le, San Francisco and 9 other locations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/16/magazine/20111016pricecheck_ss.html', 'snippet': 'Listings for New York, Seattle, San Francisco and 9 other locations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Listings for New York, Seattle, San Francisco and 9 other locations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/magazine/20111016pricecheck_ss-slide-YE40/20111016pricecheck_ss-slide-YE40-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What You Get for $300,000 in....', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T10:01:52+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/f37b47f3-eaeb-590f-8e56-2eef5bfef787', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/f37b47f3-eaeb-590f-8e56-2eef5bfef787'}, {'abstract': 'Taking cuts; short fiction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/magazine/the-ethicist-joint-venture.html', 'snippet': 'Taking cuts; short fiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I smoke a fair amount of marijuana. Sometimes I ask my friends if they want me to pick up weed for them as well, in which case they give me the money upfront. As with any other commodity, prices are usually cheaper when buying in bulk. I will often not give the change to my friends and instead use those few dollars to further my own discount. Is this unethical? I’m the one going through the effort of gathering buyers and conducting the illegal transaction. Or does that just make me a drug dealer? NAME WITHHELD', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 610, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Joint Venture', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Joint Venture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lying', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T10:01:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e161214-9922-5ae3-a2b5-c3236001619f', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e161214-9922-5ae3-a2b5-c3236001619f'}, {'abstract': 'What every white guy like me owes to Michael Stipe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/magazine/lives-the-right-moves.html', 'snippet': 'What every white guy like me owes to Michael Stipe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the video for “Losing My Religion” — the song that would finally make R.E.M. a household name, even in my own rural Midwestern house — Michael Stipe spends the first couple of minutes slouched in a chair and pacing the rough wooden floor of a big, empty room. While he sings, he flaps his arms a little at the elbows. Occasionally, his bandmates appear, all wearing white shirts like Stipe, accessorized with a jacket, pants with pleats or vests. It was the early ’90s. In the video, it’s raining outside. For some reason, there’s a pitcher of milk on the windowsill.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '106', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/magazine/16lives/mag-16Lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 943, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/magazine/16lives/mag-16Lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/magazine/16lives/mag-16Lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Right Moves', 'kicker': 'Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Right Moves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'REM', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stipe, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T10:01:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Korb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Korb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98ae320d-41b1-51a5-acd0-51b6cd9f5770', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98ae320d-41b1-51a5-acd0-51b6cd9f5770'}, {'abstract': 'Gertrude Legendre bequeathed her magnificent South Carolina plantation to her daughter. But she kept her grip on the property from beyond the grave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/magazine/key-gerties-ghost.html', 'snippet': 'Gertrude Legendre bequeathed her magnificent South Carolina plantation to her daughter. But she kept her grip on the property from beyond the grave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2000, Bokara Legendre, an artist and a stage performer, inherited her family’s plantation in the Lowcountry of South Carolina. She promptly set about making the place her own, redecorating the antebellum mansion with abstract paintings and a pastel color scheme. But this seemed to unsettle the house. The first night Legendre spent in her redone bedroom, there was a problem with the fireplace, and the chamber filled with thick black smoke. As a member of the plantation staff put out the fire, he glimpsed an apparition: the late mistress of the house, Legendre’s mother, Gertie. She was not pleased with the changes.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '70', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/magazine/16plantation1/mag-16Plantation-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 795, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 