nergy costs for the district.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/from-oil-and-gas-leases-the-greenest-of-schools/', 'snippet': 'A new K-to-12 school in rural Mosca, Colo., offers plenty of natural daylight and other design features intended to create a better learning environment while reducing energy costs for the district.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When students returned to school this fall in rural Mosca, Colo., they had plenty to cheer about besides the Thunderbirds, their football team. In August, the school district completed construction of the new Sangre de Cristo K-12 school, replacing an old metal building that more closely resembled a potato cellar, according to some students, referring to the low, dark warehouses for storing one of the region’s primary crops.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Oil and Gas Revenue, the Greenest of Schools', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building (Construction)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design (LEED)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Green Building Council', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T11:23:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Witkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witkin', 'qualifier': None,