years after her retirement and a decade after her death, she remains\xa0an often polarizing figure. On Oct. 27, the Library of America will publish “The Age of Movies: Selected Writings of Pauline Kael,” followed four days later by the publication of\xa0“Pauline Kael: A Life in the Dark,” a sometimes\xa0surprising\xa0biography by Brian Kellow, from Viking. A. O. Scott and Manohla Dargis discuss her work and its legacy. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16CRITICS-SUB_span/16CRITICS-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16CRITICS-SUB_span/16CRITICS-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16CRITICS-SUB_span/16CRITICS-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1008, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16CRITICS-SUB_span/16CRITICS-SUB_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16CRITICS-SUB_span/16CRITICS-SUB_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mad About Her: Pauline Kael, Loved and Loathed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mad About Her: Pauline Kael, Loved and Loathed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kael, Pauline', 'rank