}, {'abstract': 'The Australia and New Zealand coaches have been eager to downplay their rivalry in the buildup to the match, but it is clear that defeat to the other would be an unpalatable experience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/sports/rugby/15iht-RUGBY15.html', 'snippet': 'The Australia and New Zealand coaches have been eager to downplay their rivalry in the buildup to the match, but it is clear that defeat to the other would be an unpalatable experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUCKLAND — Four years ago, Robbie Deans and Graham Henry were going head to head for the job of New Zealand coach.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/sports/15rugby_337/15rugby_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Semifinal Is Grudge Match of Coaches', 'kicker': 'Rugby World Cup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Cup Semifinal a Grudge Match', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Zealand', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Auckland (New Zealand)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rugby (Game)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T13:07:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Rugby', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Stoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b46274a2-b996-59dc-9919-36efb7f81cb6', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b46274a2-b996-59dc-9919-36efb7f81cb6'}, {'abstract': 'The dirty secret of debates is that, for all the reporters who descend on each town for each verbal sparring match, they really can be covered just well as on television.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/debate-analysis-from-the-filing-center/', 'snippet': 'The dirty secret of debates is that, for all the reporters who descend on each town for each verbal sparring match, they really can be covered just well as on television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The list of great moments in political debates is long and well-trod — Ronald Reagan bellowing “I’m paying for this microphone,” Lloyd Bentsen putting down Dan Quayle with his “Senator, you’re no Jack Kennedy” line and, more recently, Barack Obama informing Hillary Rodham Clinton that she was “likable enough.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Look at the Debates, Beyond the Big Moments', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Simi Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T13:09:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1c954d3-cc7e-5aa7-a453-cc21dfbab774', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1c954d3-cc7e-5aa7-a453-cc21dfbab774'}, {'abstract': 'The Murdoch empire, once again.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/patterns-of-misconduct/', 'snippet': 'The Murdoch empire, once again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Via Charlie Stross, I see that the Murdoch empire has another scandal — this time involving misleading advertisers rather than readers, by inflating circulation numbers. Wow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Patterns Of Misconduct', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T13:15:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54e3b2dd-8e4f-5c2e-87ea-eb810346680e', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54e3b2dd-8e4f-5c2e-87ea-eb810346680e'}, {'abstract': 'The former Galleon head gets the toughest sentence yet for insider trading.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/record-prison-time-for-rajaratnam/', 'snippet': 'The former Galleon head gets the toughest sentence yet for insider trading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Raj Rajaratnam, the Galleon Group chief at the center of the United States’ massive insider trading investigation, was sentenced to eleven years in prison. His sentence is the longest ever for insider-trading in the United States, and follows a ten-year term for Zvi Goffer, a hedge fund manager at Galleon. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Record Prison Time for Rajaratnam', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keyw