'abstract': '“You All Are Captains” is a sort of metafiction that evolves from documentary as the filmmaker is ejected from the project.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/movies/oliver-laxes-morocco-film-you-all-are-captains.html', 'snippet': '“You All Are Captains” is a sort of metafiction that evolves from documentary as the filmmaker is ejected from the project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR the last five years the Spanish filmmaker Oliver Laxe has lived mainly in the northern Moroccan city of Tangier, where he developed a film workshop at a shelter for disadvantaged children. At first glance, Mr. Laxe’s debut feature, “You All Are Captains,” looks to be a straightforward reflection of this experience: he appears as himself, lecturing on photographic optics and showing his young charges, all preadolescent and adolescent boys, how to operate a 16-millimeter camera. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16CAPTAINS_SPAN/16CAPTAINS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16CAPTAINS_SPAN/16CAPTAINS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16CAPTAINS_SPAN/16CAPTAINS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16CAPTAINS_SPAN/16CAPTAINS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/arts/16CAPTAINS_SPAN/16CAPTAINS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 