, 'snippet': 'Third base saves the Tigers in the American League Championship Series while the Brewers grab some momentum in the N.L.C.S. and more dust flies around the Red Sox.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With all the nutty, quirky things that happen in baseball, it’s hard to manage something truly stupefying. Once you’ve seen a squirrel influence the outcome of a playoff game, a moth lodge in a pitcher’s ear and not come out, gnats take out a dynasty and, of course, Bartman, well, what can truly surprise you?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: The Base That Roared', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beltre, Adrian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Braun, Ryan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Epstein, Theo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fielder, Prince', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marshall, Brandon', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verlander, Justin', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolf, Randy', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Delmon', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN LEAGUE', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Cubs', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Free Press', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Brewers', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National League', 'rank': 22, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 23, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Raiders', 'rank': 24, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Phillies', 'rank': 25, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T15:11:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfe81130-81da-592f-9eeb-9f3cbb51f628', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfe81130-81da-592f-9eeb-9f3cbb51f628'}, {'abstract': 'Patti Smith’s photographs are an elegy to the dead, memento mori of her heroes’ worldly effects.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/requiem-lass/', 'snippet': 'Patti Smith’s photographs are an elegy to the dead, memento mori of her heroes’ worldly effects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I met Patti Smith at the Electric Lady recording studios on West Eighth Street in Manhattan on a sunny August afternoon. Both the place and the date have a special significance in Smith’s personal mythos and in the broader mythology of rock ’n’ roll. The facility, which you enter through a nondescript storefront on a once famously scruffy block now given over to discount shoe stores and student-friendly eating places, was Jimi Hendrix’s brainchild, and it stands as an enduring part of his legacy. A rack in the reception area is stocked with foldout LP sleeves of some of the legendary records that were cut here — Stevie Wonder’s “Talking Book,” AC/DC’s “Back in Black,” David Bowie’s “Young Americans” — and the psychedelic murals that Hendrix commissioned line the subterranean hallways leading to Studio A. There, his portrait hangs in the lounge, a benevolent godhead gazing down at the latter-day strivings of his fellow musicians.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Requiem Lass', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hendrix, Jimi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mapplethorpe, Robert', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Patti', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T15:15:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a46df45-1007-53fb-9f56-b79ca261ac4b', 'word_count': 2778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a46df45-1007-53fb-9f56-b79ca261ac4b'}, {'abstract': 'The German automaker’s volume leader is fitted for 2012 with the twin-scroll turbocharged 4-cylinder that appears currently in the Z4 sDrive28i, as well as a new 8-speed automatic transmission.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/wider-wedgier-bmw-3-series-gets-a-4-cylinder-engine-for-2012/', 'snippet': 'The German automaker’s volume leader is fitted for 2012 with the twin-scroll turbocharged 4-cylinder that appears currently in the Z4 sDrive28i, as well as a new 8-speed automatic transmission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sixth iteration of the BMW 3 Series sedan, arriving at United States dealers in February, has grown bigger in terms of wheelbase and overall length, smaller in terms of the engine bay and more efficient all around. It remains, however, thoroughly recognizable as the brand’s volume-leading saloon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wider, Wedgier BMW 3 Series Gets a 4-Cylinder Engine for 2012', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T15:16:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/638dfbb5-7997-50b5-8a66-422db65558ad', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/638dfbb5-7997-50b5-8a66-422db65558ad'}, {'abstract': 'The location services reward the businesses with the most check-ins by ranking them higher in their search results. Have they worked for your business?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/location-based-services-can-put-businesses-on-the-map/', 'snippet': 'The location services reward the businesses with the most check-ins by ranking them higher in their search results. Have they worked for your business?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although Starkville, Miss., is home to Mississippi State University and the fighting Bulldogs, it’s not a large city with a dense urban epicenter — the typical playground for those who use location-based marketing services such as Gowalla and Foursquare.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Location-Based Services Can Put Businesses on the Map', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foursquare', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gowalla', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T15:17:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By MP Mueller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mp', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mueller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8fcd04a-bb59-59b5-96d0-bb96a76de717', 'word_count': 1039, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8fcd04a-bb59-59b5-96d0-bb96a76de717'}, {'abstract': 'U.S.C defeated Cal to go to 5-1, but didn’t look impressive in doing so.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/for-u-s-c-injuries-and-inconsistency/', 'snippet': 'U.S.C defeated Cal to go to 5-1, but didn’t look impressive in doing so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO – As showcase games go, the tussle between U.S.C. and Cal on Thursday night functioned more as a display of the middling Pac-12. With Stanford and Oregon legitimate top 10 teams and Arizona State lingering in the top 25, the rest of the Pac-12 has looked fairly lackluster this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For U.S.C., Injuries and Inconsistency', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barkley, Matt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kiffin, Lane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacific-12 Conference', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Southern California', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T15:20:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dbfb1e1-1c10-5d16-bd68-d268b5f92749', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dbfb1e1-1c10-5d16-bd68-d268b5f92749'}, {'abstract': 'A new study from Johns Hopkins University says headaches have been a leading cause of attrition in units deployed to Iraq and Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/a-war-injury-with-a-big-impact-the-plain-old-headache/', 'snippet': 'A new study from Johns Hopkins University says headaches have been a leading cause of attrition in units deployed to Iraq and Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ask anyone about the signature wounds of the current wars and the list is likely to include lost limbs, traumatic brain injury, post-traumatic stress, back strains and knee pains. But a new study from Johns Hopkins University says the plain old headache has been a leading cause of attrition in units deployed to Iraq and Afghanistan. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A War Injury With a Big Impact: The Plain Old Headache', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T15:24:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a265c58-015c-5a7e-8868-9c38b8ea47a2', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a265c58-015c-5a7e-8868-9c38b8ea47a2'}, {'abstract': 'Michelle Obama has not been entirely consistent when it comes to dressing for state dinners.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/a-white-house-debut-for-doo-ri/', 'snippet': 'Michelle Obama has not been entirely consistent when it comes to dressing for state dinners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michelle Obama has not been entirely consistent when it comes to dressing for state dinners. Since the considered choice of a gold gown by Naeem Khan, a designer with Indian roots who is based in America, for the first dinner for the prime minister of India in November of 2009, she has mixed things up, wearing Peter Soronen to a dinner for the Mexican president, and that controversial Alexander McQueen dress for the president of China. She wore another dress by Mr. Khan to a dinner for the chancellor of Germany. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A White House Debut for Doo.Ri', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T15:28:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1908227c-55b0-54b0-8237-442795bd5019', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1908227c-55b0-54b0-8237-442795bd5019'}, {'abstract': 'The artistic director is a former principal dancer at New York City Ballet.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/hubbe-signs-on-for-five-more-years-at-royal-danish-ballet/', 'snippet': 'The artistic director is a former principal dancer at New York City Ballet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nikolaj Hübbe, 43, the popular former principal dancer at the New York City Ballet, has extended his term as artistic director at the Royal Danish Ballet for another five years, the company said on Friday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hübbe Signs On for Five More Years at Royal Danish Ballet', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hubbe, Nikolaj', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, 