ain': 'More of a Gehry-Designed Museum in Minneapolis', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gehry, Frank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Minnesota', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minneapolis (Minn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T16:20:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By STEPHANIE DAVILA', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DAVILA', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/006730ef-d0ca-53fb-839d-81d9e260ec0e', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/006730ef-d0ca-53fb-839d-81d9e260ec0e'}, {'abstract': 'A coroner has agreed to open an inquest into the radiation poisoning of former K.G.B. officer Alexander V. Litvinenko, potentially bringing the case before a British legal forum for the first time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/world/europe/britain-agrees-to-new-probe-in-the-radiation-poisoning-of-alexander-litvinenko.html', 'snippet': 'A coroner has agreed to open an inquest into the radiation poisoning of former K.G.B. officer Alexander V. Litvinenko, potentially bringing the case before a British legal forum for the first time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A coroner has agreed to open a full inquest into the radiation poisoning of the former K.G.B. officer Alexander V. Litvinenko, potentially bringing the case before a British legal forum for the first time, opening new seams of information about his death and possibly stirring new tensions with Moscow.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain Agrees to New Inquiry Into Poisoning Death of a Former K.G.B. Officer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain Agrees to New Inquiry Into Poisoning Death of a Former K.G.B. Officer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poisoning and Poisons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Litvinenko, Alexander V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T16:23:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90b8c4b9-5263-5c60-9daa-403893d3cf58', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90b8c4b9-5263-5c60-9daa-403893d3cf58'}, {'abstract': 'A reporter’s mission: navigate the new 89,000-square-foot Uniqlo flagship on Fifth Avenue at 54th Street and find 10 items for $200.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/the-uniqlo-flagship-challenge/', 'snippet': 'A reporter’s mission: navigate the new 89,000-square-foot Uniqlo flagship on Fifth Avenue at 54th Street and find 10 items for $200.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With its 300 L.E.D. screens, 100 fitting rooms and three floors stocked top to bottom with basics beyond, the new 89,000-square-foot Uniqlo flagship on Fifth Avenue at 54th Street in Manhattan, which opens today, is just a tad overwhelming. And since vast shopping opportunities often end in devastating splurges, I arrived to test-shop the store with a plan: 10 items, $200 (which meant that the +J section on the second floor was off-limits). I started at the beginning, the bottom floor, where walls of cashmere V-neck sweaters bragged grand-opening price tags ($89.90 marked down to $49.90). So as not to throw the entirety of my allowance at four candy-colored sweaters, I jumped on the theme-park-style escalators and went straight up to the third floor. It was there that I did a double take: Japanese engineered denim for $9.90! With $190 left, I grabbed a men’s flannel shirt ($29.90), a fluffy down vest ($49.90), a two-for-one Breton-striped lounge set ($24.90) and a pair of very holiday slippers ($12.90; if I don’t wear them, someone in my family will come Christmastime); $72.50 to go and my winter shopping was almost done. Then I turned a corner and found myself staring into an aquarium-like tube filled with the company’s famous (and effective!) Heattech pieces. I chose a knit cap ($12.90) and matching gloves ($12.90), a pack of socks ($9.90) and a camisole ($12.90). I had $23.90 left, enough for a pink umbrella ($12.90). Who knew Uniqlo sold umbrellas? Chic ones! Had I just $2 more — $11 was all that was left — I’d have bought two.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Uniqlo Flagship Challenge', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T16:23:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bd1b0b9-c5c4-525c-8d25-42dc3b2f417d', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bd1b0b9-c5c4-525c-8d25-42dc3b2f417d'}, {'abstract': 'Jules Allen, photographer, captured the sweat-soaked denizens of Gleason’s Gym.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/beauty-amid-the-bruises/', 'snippet': 'Jules Allen, photographer, captured the sweat-soaked denizens of Gleason’s Gym.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After moving to New York from California in 1978, Jules Allen went to the legendary Gleason’s Gym to learn to box. But he stayed to make the sweat-soaked photographs that populate a just-published book, “Double Up.” On Lens, David Gonzalez interviews Mr. Allen and presents a slide show. Check it out ringside on Lens »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beauty Amid the Bruises', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T16:26:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d7ab494-ae41-5526-aee1-504780beada0', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d7ab494-ae41-5526-aee1-504780beada0'}, {'abstract': 'Virgin Atlantic confirmed that it was in deal talks for the troubled airline BMI, following a report that British Airways’ owner was also in preliminary discussions.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/virgin-atlantic-and-british-airways-compete-over-bmi/', 'snippet': 'Virgin Atlantic confirmed that it was in deal talks for the troubled airline BMI, following a report that British Airways’ owner was also in preliminary discussions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rivalry between British Airways and Virgin Atlantic continues, this time over the midsize European carrier BMI.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'mai