'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CREATE DANGEROUSLY: The Immigrant Artist at Work,  by Edwidge Danticat (Vintage, $14.95.) Danticat, whose books include the story collection “Krik? Krak!” and the novel “Breath, Eyes, Memory,” grew up in Haiti in the 1970s, under the Duvalier dictatorships (she has lived in the United States since the age of 12). These essays reflect on the Haitian diaspora and artists who create despite the horrors that drove them from their homelands.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T17:52:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ihsan Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ihsan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/336b6cc9-e494-5748-827f-b3234f6a1254', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/336b6cc9-e494-5748-827f-b3234f6a1254'}, {'abstract': 'Embracing semiotics came with certain costs, but it left an intoxicating sense that the everyday world contained a secret layer of meaning that could be deciphered with the right key.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/books/review/i-was-an-under-age-semiotician.html', 'snippet': 'Embracing semiotics came with certain costs, but it left an intoxicating sense that the everyday world contained a secret layer of meaning that could be deciphered with the right key.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is an occupational hazard of being a writer to be appalled by the prose style you deployed in your youth. Most of the time the flaws reflect unchecked enthusiasm, or literary clichés that have not yet worn away, or a certain inability to settle on a defined voice. But reading my own college juvenilia, I have a strange and almost total sense of disconnection. This is from a paper I wrote at the age of 19:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/books/review/16johnson/16johnson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/books/review/16johnson/16johnson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/books/review/16johnson/16johnson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Was an Under-Age Semiotician', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Was an Under-Age Semiotician', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brown University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eugenides, Jeffrey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lipsyte, Sam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T17:52:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://art