uri': 'nyt://article/756af323-1e7c-5b9c-a8de-e4ae7108ca17'}, {'abstract': 'Irredeemable, a series written by Mark Waid and illustrated by Peter Krause.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/graphic-books-best-sellers-double-dipping/', 'snippet': 'Irredeemable, a series written by Mark Waid and illustrated by Peter Krause.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What happens when a super-hero goes bad? That’s the premise behind Irredeemable, a series written by Mark Waid and illustrated by Peter Krause. The former hero in question is the Plutonian and in his path are his former allies, the Paradigm, who try to impede his quest for mayhem. Plutonian’s turn to the dark side may be bad for the people he used to protect, but it’s good for Boom! Studios, which publishes the series as two collected editions hit our lists this week. On the hardcover list, at No. 7, is The Definitive Irredeemable, a deluxe reprint of the first three volumes of the series. On the softcover list, at No. 2, is volume seven, which finds the ex-hero in exile at an alien asylum. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: Double Dipping', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T18:02:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64a7cf7e-9550-5b69-968e-6867d9924e86', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64a7cf7e-9550-5b69-968e-6867d9924e86'}, {'abstract': 'The neighborhood in East Jerusalem is on the southern flank of the area projected as the capital of a future state of Palestine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/world/middleeast/new-jewish-housing-planned-in-east-jerusalem.html', 'snippet': 'The neighborhood in East Jerusalem is on the southern flank of the area projected as the capital of a future state of Palestine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Israeli government has submitted formal plans to build a new neighborhood of Jewish housing in a part of Jerusalem beyond the 1967 lines close to the West Bank city of Bethlehem, the anti-settlement Israeli group Peace Now reported Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Plans to Build More Housing in East Jerusalem', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Plans to Build More Housing in East Jerusalem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Peace Now', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABBAS, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erekat, Saeb', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T18:02:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af225ff3-060d-594a-b400-abe4af734529', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af225ff3-060d-594a-b400-abe4af734529'}, {'abstract': 'Some tips for filling out the federal financial aid form for children of same-sex parents or for applicants with same-sex partners.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/how-to-file-for-financial-aid-if-your-parents-are-gay/', 'snippet': 'Some tips for filling out the federal financial aid form for children of same-sex parents or for applicants with same-sex partners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Filling out the federal form for student financial aid is an arduous task for most applicants. But if you have two mothers or two fathers, or if you happen to be married to a same-sex partner, it can quickly escalate into an even more complicated exercise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to File for Financial Aid if Your Parents Are Gay', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Scholarships and Fellowships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T18:04:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ef14694-2c43-56c7