 among the designers who participated in the competition. Jury leaders have included Martin Margiela, Azzedine Alaia, Raf Simons and Hussein Chalayan. The Hyeres Festival is an excellent way for emerging designers and photographers to get some recognition. The deadline for applications for the spring 2012 festival is Dec. 5. So apply! For details, go to villanoailles-hyeres.com/hyeres2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hyeres Competition', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T18:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9063d14-8090-5b1b-bc72-70023d7e049e', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9063d14-8090-5b1b-bc72-70023d7e049e'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Bittman demonstrates an easy, forgiving way to cook fish in a new Minimalist video.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/the-minimalist-striped-bass-poached-in-spicy-soy-sauce/', 'snippet': 'Mark Bittman demonstrates an easy, forgiving way to cook fish in a new Minimalist video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Poaching — cooking in simmering liquid — is a fairly forgiving way to cook fish, since it’s not likely to dry out. (It also virtually eliminates the likelihood of anything sticking to the bottom of the pan, which is often in the back of your mind when you sauté.) I love using this method with striped bass, which has the added bonus of being a local fish, but you can use any firm white fillets or steaks. It’s also a great way to cook mackerel or bluefish, other locals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Minimalist: Striped Bass Poached in Spicy Soy Sauce', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bass (Fish)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T18:36:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/598c1a61-48df-5541-8113-c65a70b83782', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/598c1a61-48df-5541-8113-c65a70b83782'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Woodford lost his job after six months because his management style did not mesh with the Japanese camera maker’s executive team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/business/global/in-rare-move-olympus-fires-its-chief.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Woodford lost his job after six months because his management style did not mesh with the Japanese camera maker’s executive team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — The struggling Japanese camera maker Olympus wanted a change agent. Just not this much change, evidently. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Culture Clash, Olympus Ousts Its British Chief', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Culture Clash, Olympus Ousts Its British Chief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Olympus Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Susp