lodging options.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/travel/vibrant-lower-village-neighborhood-of-kennebunk-me.html', 'snippet': 'A world away from its better-known neighbor, the Lower Village in Kennebunk is a close-knit community with unusual restaurants, shops and lodging options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KENNEBUNKPORT, Me., is probably best known as a summer playground for the wealthy, most notably the former president, George H. W. Bush. The old money is plenty visible: confident young men stride around town in freshly pressed khakis and preppy haircuts, vintage sailboats glide into port, and straight-backed seniors sip cocktails in Adirondack chairs. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/travel/16HEADSUP_SPAN/16-HEADS-UP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/16/travel/16HEADSUP_SPAN/16-HEADS-UP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/travel/16HEADSUP_SPAN/16-HEADS-UP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/travel/16HEADSUP_SPAN/16-HEADS-UP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/travel/16HEADSUP_SPAN/16-HEADS-UP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Detour Near Kennebunkport, Me.', 'kicker': 'Heads Up', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Detour Near Kennebunkport', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kennebunkport (Me)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T18:55:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Vatner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vatner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45e95457-9405-5078-9ad7-1af2ba8bb998', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45e95457-9405-5078-9ad7-1af2ba8bb998'}, {'abstract': 'A chauffeured exploration of the driest place on earth — a vast land of contrasts in the shadow of the Andes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/travel/luxury-in-chiles-ancient-atacama-desert.html', 'snippet': 'A chauffeured exploration of the driest place on earth — a vast land of contrasts in the shadow of the Andes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF you’ve heard of the Atacama Desert in northern Chile at all, you’re likely to know one thing: it’s the driest desert on earth. That’s all I knew going in, though it triggered my reflexive mistrust of superlatives.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/travel/16EXPLORER2/16EXPLORER2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/travel/16EXPLORER2/16EXPLORER2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/travel/16EXPLORER2/16EXPLORER2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A High-End Tri