d packages, takes into account the student’s household size, family income and assets, and the number of students in college, among other factors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Same-Sex Parents and Paying for College', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Secondary)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T18:57:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/c6102a0f-d2aa-55de-a78e-7edba376d86c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/c6102a0f-d2aa-55de-a78e-7edba376d86c'}, {'abstract': 'Online organizers set Saturday as the date to spread the Occupy Wall Street to cities around the world. In Italy, protesters started early by storming into the offices of Goldman Sachs.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/as-calls-for-protests-go-global-italy-jumps-the-gun/', 'snippet': 'Online organizers set Saturday as the date to spread the Occupy Wall Street to cities around the world. In Italy, protesters started early by storming into the offices of Goldman Sachs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Online organizers have set Saturday as the date to spread the Occupy Wall Street protests to cities around the world. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Calls for Protests Go Global, Italy Jumps the Gun', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T19:03:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81337b69-b76d-5550-b9f6-a3c2efdda08d', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81337b69-b76d-5550-b9f6-a3c2efdda08d'}, {'abstract': 'Financial advisers point out that the rate of return on permanent life insurance is 3 to 5 percent and the money passes to beneficiaries free of income tax.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/your-money/life-and-disability-insurance/in-a-volatile-market-some-turn-to-insurance-instead-of-bonds.html', 'snippet': 'Financial advisers point out that the rate of return on permanent life insurance is 3 to 5 percent and the money passes to beneficiaries free of income tax.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIFE insurance, it’s fair to say, is a subject that provokes  strong opinions. People who like insurance see it as a way to leave money to heirs tax-free or to make sure there is money for a rainy day. Those who don’t like it see a product that generates huge fees for the seller and a diminishing benefit for buyers who probably don’t understand it. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/your-money/15wealth/15wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/15/your-money/15wealth/15wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/your-money/15wealth/15wealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Volatile Market, Some Turn to Insurance Instead of Bonds', 'kicker': 'Wealth Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Volatile Market, Some Turn to Insurance Instead of Bonds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Planners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Life Insurance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T19:03:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'subsection_name': 'Life and Disability Insurance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84eb60ec-8fa7-5633-b6df-fc32fbdd87a8', 'word_count': 1256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84eb60ec-8fa7-5633-b6df-fc32fbdd87a8'}, {'abstract': 'The country’s largest employer of certified financial planners is accused of putting its own employees’ 401(k) money into underperforming funds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/your-money/turning-a-lens-on-ameriprise-financial.html', 'snippet': 'The country’s largest employer of certified financial planners is accused of putting its own employees’ 401(k) money into underperforming funds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re a company trying to persuade Americans to trust you with their money, the last thing you want is former employees accusing you of cheating them out of theirs. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/business/MONEY/MONEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 834, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/business/MONEY/MONEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/15/business/MONEY/MONEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Financial Planner’s Red Flags', 'kicker': 'Your Money', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Financial Planner’s Red Flags', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '401(k), 403(b) and 457 Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ameriprise Financial Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T19:11:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15374143-430e-59b0-9361-76d50530d2f7', 'word_count': 1392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15374143-430e-59b0-9361-76d50530d2f7'}, {'abstract': 'A lawsuit brought by participants in Ameriprise’s 401(k) plan raises questions about how it treats its customers’ money.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/ameriprise-and-the-meaning-of-its-401k-lawsuit/', 'snippet': 'A lawsuit brought by participants in Ameriprise’s 401(k) plan raises questions about how it treats its customers’ money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My column this week is about Ameriprise, a company rich with history, though not always the good kind. It deserves a ton of credit for making financial planning central to its work with customers, but it has also run into plenty of trouble with regulators over the years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ameriprise and the Meaning of Its 401(k) Lawsuit', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ameriprise Financial Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T19:14:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a0172e7-f9de-5407-ae86-a3aee06ead2c', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a0172e7-f9de-5407-ae86-a3aee06ead2c'}, {'abstract': 'A congressman asks Amazon some questions about the Kindle Fire and privacy.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/questions-for-amazon-on-privacy-and-the-kindle-fire/', 'snippet': 'A congressman asks Amazon some questions about the Kindle Fire and privacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The dream of every retailer is to know exactly what its customers are thinking. Are they comparison-shopping? Just looking? Will a discount help close the deal? Or is price no object? Amazon’s coming tablet, the Kindle Fire, is equipped with a Web browser that, thanks to the wonders of cloud computing, is partly housed on Amazon’s servers. That will give the retailer opportunities to track customer behavior all over the Web, gathering data and marketing intelligence as it goes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions for Amazon on Privacy and the Kindle Fire', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amazon Kindle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bezos, Jeffrey P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Markey, Edward J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T19:19:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d17f4c6-088d-5536-9362-02e58583be94', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d17f4c6-088d-5536-9362-02e58583be94'}, {'abstract': 'The Paris-based artist and lighting director tells T how the projected image of our signature initial happened (by accident), and the kind of light he hopes women will wear this winter.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/projected-yearnings/', 'snippet': 'The Paris-based artist and lighting director tells T how the projected image of our signature initial happened (by accident), and the kind of light he hopes women will wear this winter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We asked the Paris-based artist and lighting director Thierry Dreyfus to make the T for our winter women’s issue because he lights so many of the clothes that we see on the runways. (He did 25 shows last season alone.) But it wasn’t just the halos at Comme des Garçons or the bulbed ceiling that lifted from the floor at Rag & Bone that made Dreyfus such an easy and desirable pick. All over the world — at hotels in Belgrade and Athens, in galleries in Singapore and Milan, and at design fairs in London and Miami — Dreyfus’s installations alter and electrify their surroundings and our experiences of them. Here, he tells T how the projected image of our signature initial happened (by accident), and the kind of light he hopes women will wear this winter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Projected Yearnings', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T19:22:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01c911d6-4198-529a-9ce4-ba6298063d04', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01c911d6-4198-529a-9ce4-ba6298063d04'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Kwiecien, his surgeon and manager reported in a conference call that “his recovery is progressing at a remarkable pace,” Peter Clark, the Met spokesman, wrote in an e-mail.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/mariusz-kwiecien-set-to-return-to-met-stage/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Kwiecien, his surgeon and manager reported in a conference call that “his recovery is progressing at a remarkable pace,” Peter Clark, the Met spokesman, wrote in an e-mail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just two weeks after undergoing surgery for a herniated desk, the baritone Mariusz Kwiecien will return to the stage in the title role of “Don Giovanni” at the Metropolitan Opera on Oct. 25, the company said on Friday. Mr. Kwiecien, his surgeon and manager reported in a conference call that “his recovery is progressing at a remarkable pace,” Peter Clark, the Met spokesman, wrote in an e-mail. He is expected to carry out all the stage action, with the possible exception of climbing down a ladder in the opening scene, Mr. Clark said. Mr. Kwiecien felt pain during the dress rehearsal last week and had to withdraw from early performances in the run. Doctors operated on his back on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mariusz Kwiecien Set to Return to Met Stage', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T19:23:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ff63704-c363-5cf4-9ccc-fe9edce33c8d', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ff63704-c363-5cf4-9ccc-fe9edce33c8d'}, {'abstract': 'The indictment of Robert Finn is the first of a Roman Catholic bishop in the 25 years since the scandal over sexual abuse by priests first became public in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/us/kansas-city-bishop-indicted-in-reporting-of-abuse-by-priest.html', 'snippet': 'The indictment of Robert Finn is the first of a Roman Catholic bishop in the 25 years since the scandal over sexual abuse by priests first became public in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANSAS CITY, Mo. — A bishop in the Roman Catholic Church has been indicted for failure to report suspected child abuse, the first time in the 25-year history of the church’s sex abuse scandals that the leader of an American diocese has been held criminally liable for the behavior of a priest he supervised. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/us/15bishop_inline/15bishop_inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/us/15bishop_inline/15bishop_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/15/us/15bishop_inline/15bishop_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bishop Indicted; Charge Is Failing to Report Abuse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bishop Indicted; Charge Is Failing To Report Abuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finn, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas City (Mo)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Pornography', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratigan, Shawn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T19:25:35+0000', 'docume