dential candidates’ third-quarter fund-raising reports, filed with the Federal Election Commission.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/candidates-report-third-quarter-fund-raising/', 'snippet': 'A collection of the 2012 presidential candidates’ third-quarter fund-raising reports, filed with the Federal Election Commission.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:12 p.m. | Updated The 2012 presidential candidates must file their third-quarter fund-raising reports with the Federal Election Commission by Saturday at midnight. The numbers will reveal not merely how much they are raising, but how much they are spending and where they are spending it. The chart below is a top-level breakdown of where the candidates stand, and will be updated as candidates reports become available.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Candidates Report Third-Quarter Fund-Raising', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T20:05:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f586c4e5-005c-5cd3-8bf3-68ac75b1a15e', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f586c4e5-005c-5cd3-8bf3-68ac75b1a15e'}, {'abstract': 'In a new television commercial, Ron Paul, a former obstetrician, is reminding conservative voters in Iowa of his antiabortion credentials.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/new-paul-ad-in-iowa-focuses-on-abortion/', 'snippet': 'In a new television commercial, Ron Paul, a former obstetrician, is reminding conservative voters in Iowa of his antiabortion credentials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ron Paul is best known for his antigovernment crusades and his rebukes of the Federal Reserve.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Paul Ad in Iowa Focuses on Abortion', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T20:06:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a452407-1f4e-535c-86d6-3615c075a6cc', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a452407-1f4e-535c-86d6-3615c075a6cc'}, {'abstract': 'Radiation from the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power plant may have spread to places where Japan’s government hasn’t even thought to look.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/world/asia/radioactive-hot-spots-in-tokyo-point-to-wider-problems.html', 'snippet': 'Radiation from the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power plant may have spread to places where Japan’s government hasn’t even thought to look.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Takeo Hayashida signed on with a citizens’ group to test for radiation near his son’s baseball field in Tokyo after government officials told him they had no plans to check for fallout from the devastated Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant. Like Japan’s central government, local officials said there was nothing to fear in the capital, 160 miles from the disaster zone.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/world/15radiation2/15radiation2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/15/world/15radiation2/15radiation2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 342}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/world/15radiation2/15radiation2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/world/15radiation2/15radiation2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/15/world/15radiation2/15radiation2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Citizens’ Testing Finds 20 Hot Spots Around Tokyo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Citizens’ Testing Finds 20 Radioactive Hot Spots Around Tokyo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radiation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Union of Concerned Scientists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T20:07:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'n