chmanns-money-woes-continue/', 'snippet': 'Michele Bachmann says she raised about $4 million in the last  quarter, a sign that her campaign is still having trouble attracting big donors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROCK RAPIDS, Iowa — Although candidates are not required to report their fund-raising and expenses for the financial quarter ending Sept. 30 until Saturday, Representative Michele Bachmann offered a peek here Friday into the top-line number she would report. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann’s Fund-Raising Troubles Continue', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T20:44:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea3b09d1-be01-508d-9e4a-55a39f69b771', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea3b09d1-be01-508d-9e4a-55a39f69b771'}, {'abstract': 'A vintage photo of Mitt Romney, the Republican presidential contender, the former Massachusetts governor and Bain Capital founder, could be problematic for his campaign, at a time when Wall Street is under siege from protesters angry about rising income inequality and corporate greed.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/romneys-rainmakers-where-are-they-now/', 'snippet': 'A vintage photo of Mitt Romney, the Republican presidential contender, the former Massachusetts governor and Bain Capital founder, could be problematic for his campaign, at a time when Wall Street is under siege from protesters angry about rising ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A vintage photo of Mitt Romney — the Republican presidential contender, the former Massachusetts governor and Bain Capital founder — is making the rounds on the Internet. (Due to those annoying copyright rules and the fact that Bain Capital says it doesn’t own the photo, we can’t post it, but you can see it here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Rainmakers: Where Are They Now?', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T20:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba104797-4eff-5803-8ce6-1cb358caf159', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba104797-4eff-5803-8ce6-1cb358caf159'}, {'abstract': 'After the art fair, many in the audience have ended their nights at the St. John Hotel, where the artist, who has spent most of the week in her pajamas, holds court.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/frieze-frame-sarah-lucass-bedside-manner/', 'snippet': 'After the art fair, many in the audience have ended their nights at the St. John Hotel, where the artist, who has spent most of the week in her pajamas, holds court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pretty much every art fair seems to have its own drain — the place everyone eventually winds up at the end of the night. And the one that’s emerged at Frieze this year is the lounge at the St. John Hotel, on Leicester Square in London’s Chinatown, where the artist Sarah Lucas is in bed-sidency. Inside the Maritime bar, up one flight of blue, porthole-lined stairs from the hotel’s entrance, several of Lucas’s sculptures hang from the ceiling — plastic buckets and patio chairs from which stuffed pantyhose swing like Ernesto Neto-inspired breasts, conjuring the shapes of individuals who seem ready to party. Lucas herself evidently likes to stay up late; though she’s spent most of the week in pajamas in Room 15, when I visited last night, around last call, she was holding court with a room packed with fair-weary revelers like Gavin Brown and MoMA P.S. 1’s Peter Eleey.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Frieze Frame | Sarah Lucas’s Bedside Manner', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lucas, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T20:45:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3874fecb-7ff8-5f41-9362-bbff7b983d30', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3874fecb-7ff8-5f41-9362-bbff7b983d30'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/weekend-fare-63/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This weekend is the kickoff for the first Cider Week in New York, which runs from Sunday through Oct. 23. There will be more than 85 restaurants throughout the city and Hudson Valley participating in the weeklong celebration of fermented apple juice. Consider the New Amsterdam Market, South Street (between Beekman Street and Peck Slip), which is holding a hard-cider revival on Sunday from noon to 4 p.m. with hard-cider tastings, Marlow and Sons is running a cider bar, and tapas-size snacks. Early admission is from noon to 1:30 p.m., with $45 tickets, which includes 10 tastings. General admission starts at 1:30 p.m., with five tastings for $20 and 10 for $35. Additional tastings are $5 each.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T20:48:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d46e69c-c5b4-5a18-8eb1-8a0c2dbed0bb', 'word_count': 838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d46e69c-c5b4-5a18-8eb1-8a0c2dbed0bb'}, {'abstract': 'A House subcommittee explored the agreement that put private investors ahead of the government in the event of liquidation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/us/politics/house-panel-examines-solyndras-restructuring.html', 'snippet': 'A House subcommittee explored the agreement that put private investors ahead of the government in the event of liquidation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Energy Department may have made a decision without precedent when it allowed Solyndra, the now bankrupt solar technology company, to restructure its loans so private investors — not the government — would have first call on