ng people to work; and Steve Lohr on default choices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week: Jeff Sommer with Peter Lattman on insider trading; Natasha Singer and David Gillen on Big Pink; Robert Shiller on putting people to work; and Steve Lohr on default choices.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insider trading, Big Pink, putting people to work, and default choices', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T20:57:54+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/715d5839-231b-5207-ac5a-26bf3c4c3cdf', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/715d5839-231b-5207-ac5a-26bf3c4c3cdf'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama said the deployment to Africa was meant to help regional forces combat the Lord’s Resistance Army, which has terrorized villagers in at least four countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/world/africa/barack-obama-sending-100-armed-advisers-to-africa-to-help-fight-lords-resistance-army.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama said the deployment to Africa was meant to help regional forces combat the Lord’s Resistance Army, which has terrorized villagers in at least four countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama said Friday that he had ordered the deployment of 100 armed military advisers to central Africa to help regional forces combat the Lord’s Resistance Army, a notorious renegade group that has terrorized villagers in at least four countries with marauding bands that kill, rape, maim and kidnap with impunity.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/world/14uganda_span/