e ground level into retail space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/realestate/posting-a-chelsea-building-shifts-to-condops.html', 'snippet': 'A developer first conceived of 305 West 16th Street as a rental, but decided to sell the 53 units as condos and turn the ground level into retail space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the last few years a number of new condominium projects, facing poor sales and tighter lending requirements for buyers, have chosen to become rental buildings. While rentals don’t usually generate as much initial revenue as sale properties, developers see them as a safe long-term bet, generally easy to fill and providing steady revenue.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/realestate/16POSTINGS1_SPAN/16POSTINGS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/16/realestate/16POSTINGS1_SPAN/16POSTINGS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/realestate/16POSTINGS1_SPAN/postings-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/realestate/16POSTINGS1_SPAN/16POSTINGS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/realestate/16POSTINGS1_SPAN/16POSTINGS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sales Over Rentals, Even in a Credit Crunch', 'kicker': 'Posting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sales Over Rentals, Even in a Credit Crunch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condominiums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T22:18:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a4e3e26-37b4-5b07-b348-411208eda9e6', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a4e3e26-37b4-5b07-b348-411208eda9e6'}, {'abstract': 'Most of the recent disclosures about government missteps in granting a loan guarantee to Solyndra have been e-mails, private and conversational in tone.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/another-white-house-description-of-solyndra/', 'snippet': 'Most of the recent disclosures about government missteps in granting a loan guarantee to Solyndra have been e-mails, private and conversational in tone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the insights to be drawn from the unfolding Solyndra scandal is that the flavor and texture of political scandal have changed in the digital age. The leaked  Pentagon Papers consisted of mostly dry academic prose. The written reports submitted in the Red Scare investigations of the 1950s varied in tone from sinister to bombastic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another White House Description of Solyndra', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Mail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '