e brings her big voice to an uninspiring space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martina McBride isn’t a singer given to lighthearted gesture. She’s an adult, singing about adult topics, with one of the biggest and most healing voices in Nashville. She’s best when tackling painful subjects, and while she’s capable of happiness, she could never be glib.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/arts/MARTINA/MARTINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/15/arts/MARTINA/MARTINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/arts/MARTINA/MARTINA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 784, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Life’s a Pain, and Then You Play Penn', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Life’s a Pain, and Then You Play Penn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McBride, Martina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T23:14:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d753b2a8-bc4e-51f2-9c90-da03df906c53', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d753b2a8-bc4e-51f2-9c90-da03df906c53'}, {'abstract': 'A series based on Kate Atkinson’s novels about the soft-hearted sleuth Jackson Brodie is the newest addition to the PBS catalog of programs borrowed from the BBC.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/arts/television/jackson-brodie-mysteries-on-pbs-review.html', 'snippet': 'A series based on Kate Atkinson’s novels about the soft-hearted sleuth Jackson Brodie is the newest addition to the PBS catalog of programs borrowed from the BBC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An early sign that “Case Histories” isn’t going to be a typical British mystery: the voice of Nanci Griffith singing the lovely John Prine song “Speed of the Sound of Loneliness.” Strumming guitars and Texas twangs are not the usual soundtrack for tea-fueled detection and beatings on dark Edinburgh streets.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/arts/CASE/CASE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/arts/CASE/CASE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/15/arts/CASE/CASE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Detective Is Sharp but Also Introspective', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Detective Is Sharp But Also Introspective', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isaacs, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T23:15:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name'