s the issue calmly, we end up screaming at each other. What can I do? Gillian', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Micro-Mini Mom', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Micro-Mini Mom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T23:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/190e1dbb-e04b-5696-b03f-146852650305', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/190e1dbb-e04b-5696-b03f-146852650305'}, {'abstract': 'An interactive timeline of Mitt Romney’s life and career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2007/11/14/us/politics/20071114_ROMNEY_TIMELINE.html', 'snippet': 'An interactive timeline of Mitt Romney’s life and career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An interactive timeline of Mitt Romney’s life and career.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milestones: Mitt Romney', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T23:33:30+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/bbb6bb5a-12bf-54b1-bccf-855fb4bae82d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/bbb6bb5a-12bf-54b1-bccf-855fb4bae82d'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to Maureen Dowd’s column about yoga.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/opinion/busy-moms-morning-yoga.html', 'snippet': 'A reader responds to Maureen Dowd’s column about yoga.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Busy Mom’s Morning Yoga', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Busy Mom&#8217;s Morning Yoga', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T23:34:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/11f088c8-f9d3-5a96-ab9a-5e4ea5ee9430', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11f088c8-f9d3-5a96-ab9a-5e4ea5ee9430'}, {'abstract': 'Virgin Atlantic confirmed that it was in talks with the German carrier Lufthansa, the parent company of BMI, over a deal for the troubled airline.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/business/global/virgin-atlantic-and-british-airways-compete-over-bmi.html', 'snippet': 'Virgin Atlantic confirmed that it was in talks with the German carrier Lufthansa, the parent company of BMI, over a deal for the troubled airline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rivalry between British Airways and Virgin Atlantic continues, this time over the midsize European carrier BMI. On Friday, Virgin Atlantic confirmed that it was in talks with the German carrier Lufthansa, the parent company of BMI, over a deal for the troubled airline. Britain’s Sky News reported earlier that the International Airlines Group — British Airways’ owner — was also in preliminary discussions. It was unclear whether the airlines were interested in buying BMI outright or merely adding some of its assets. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Virgin Atlantic and British Airways Compete Over BMI', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Company News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Virgin Atlantic and British Airways Compete Over BMI', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Airways PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Lufthansa AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Virgin Atlantic Airways', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T23:38:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott and Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/123f6be4-9c9c-5f60-8f7c-65d1420e5431', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/123f6be4-9c9c-5f60-8f7c-65d1420e5431'}, {'abstract': 'The Anglo-Dutch firm has agreed to buy an 82 percent stake in Concern Kalina, a Russian cosmetics brand, for $537 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/business/global/unilever-buys-russian-cosmetics-brand.html', 'snippet': 'The Anglo-Dutch firm has agreed to buy an 82 percent stake in Concern Kalina, a Russian cosmetics brand, for $537 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unilever, the Anglo-Dutch firm, has agreed to buy an 82 percent stake in Concern Kalina, a Russian cosmetics brand, for $537 million. Under the terms of the deal, Unilever will add Kalina’s portfolio to the company’s existing skin, hair and oral care brands in Russia. Consumer product companies have been looking to the emerging markets and beyond for growth. Russia’s economy is on track to grow 4.3 percent this year. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unilever Buys Russian Cosmetics Brand', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Company News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unilever Buys Russian Cosmetics Brand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Unilever N.V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Concern Kalina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-14T23:40:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7d496ff-ef49-5e55-a5f0-d1571ca95b1e', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7d496ff-ef49-5e55-a5f0-d1571ca95b1e'}, {'abstract': 'A professor of literature responds to an Op-Ed about how children’s books have become progressively darker, reflecting adult anxieties of loss and suffering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/opinion/childrens-literature.html', 'snippet': 'A professor of literature responds to an Op-Ed about how children’s books have become progressively darker, reflecting adult anxieties of loss and suffering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Children’s Literature', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Children&#8217;s Literature', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject'