': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/15/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'South Korea’s Leader Helps Obama Woo Michigan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Korea’s Leader Helps Obama Woo Michigan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee Myung-bak', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T00:50:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By HELENE COOPER&nbsp;', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61e71de1-9b41-5434-ab48-1dc6e7c86018', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61e71de1-9b41-5434-ab48-1dc6e7c86018'}, {'abstract': 'Kim Han Sol, 16, the son of Kim Jong Il’s oldest son, has started attending classes at a private English-language high school in Mostar, Bosnia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/world/europe/kim-jong-ils-grandson-attending-school-in-bosnia.html', 'snippet': 'Kim Han Sol, 16, the son of Kim Jong Il’s oldest son, has started attending classes at a private English-language high school in Mostar, Bosnia.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The grandson of the North Korean leader Kim Jong Il has started attending classes at United World College, a private English-language high school in Mostar, Bosnia, the former head of the Hong Kong branch of the school has confirmed. Stephen Codrington, currently the head of the Awty International School in Houston, Tex., interviewed the boy in Macau. Kim Han Sol, 16, is the son of Kim Jong Il’s oldest son Kim Jong Nam. “I was very impressed by his idealism,” Mr. Codrington said in a phone interview from Singapore. “He’s an intelligent, insightful boy with a maturity beyond his years. He has a real yearning for changing the situation on the Korean peninsula, which he feels very deeply about.” Mr. Codrington said that the student passed the objective criteria for admission and received no special preference. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Korean Leader’s Grandson Attending School in Bosnia', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Korean Leader’s Grandson Attending School in Bosnia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United World College', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-nam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bosnia and Herzegovina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T00:52:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Brunwasser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brunwasser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b92b05b9-f19e-5378-8ab8-fb1420c7e2b8', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b92b05b9-f19e-5378-8ab8-fb1420c7e2b8'}, {'abstract': 'The body of the former Philippine dictator Ferdinand Marcos will remain for now in its refrigerated crypt in the northern Philippines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/world/asia/ferdinand-marcos-is-denied-burial-honors.html', 'snippet': 'The body of the former Philippine dictator Ferdinand Marcos will remain for now in its refrigerated crypt in the northern Philippines.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The body of the former Philippine dictator Ferdinand Marcos will remain for now in its refrigerated crypt in the northern Philippines, as it has for most of the two decades since he died in exile in Hawaii. President Benigno Aquino III — the son of former President Corazon Aquino, who ousted Mr. Marcos in a 1986 uprising — appeared to put an end to a public spat with Mr. Marcos’s son, who was demanding that the body be buried in the national cemetery in Manila along with other dignitaries. Speaking to reporters on Wednesday, Mr. Aquino said that a state funeral would be the “height of injustice” toward the victims of Mr. Marcos’s strongman rule. Ferdinand Marcos Jr., who is now a senator, said he was offended by the surprise announcement, which appeared to ignore the recommendation of a presidential commission to bury Mr. Marcos with honors. “All these talks, discussions and debates turned out to be just a stage play,” Mr. Marcos said. The president replied, “I think I will have to communicate this to the vice president, I apologize, he’s been doing the study on my behalf.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Philippines: Dictator Is Denied Burial Honors', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Philippines: Dictator Is Denied Burial Honors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aquino, Benigno S III', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marcos, Ferdinand E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marcos, Ferdinand Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T00:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Mydans', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mydans', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6a977c0-8aff-51ac-8948-f4682d4b1e0e', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6a977c0-8aff-51ac-8948-f4682d4b1e0e'}, {'abstract': 'Brandon Inge did not quit when he was sent to the minors; now he is hitting .333 in the postseason.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/sports/baseball/in-year-11-as-a-tiger-inge-finds-life-after-toledo.html', 'snippet': 'Brandon Inge did not quit when he was sent to the minors; now he is hitting .333 in the postseason.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would have been understandable if the veteran Tigers third baseman Brandon Inge had taken his gear and gone home for good in late July.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/sports/y-jp-tigers/y-jp-tigers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 837, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/sports/y-jp-tigers/y-jp-tigers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/15/sports/y-jp-tigers/y-jp-tigers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Year 11 as a Tiger, Finding Life After Toledo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Year 11 as a Tiger, Inge Finds Life After Toledo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Inge, Brandon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toledo Mud Hens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leyland, Jim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T00:56:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b13c1b7e-f078-57de-a16a-74220305815c', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b13c1b7e-f078-57de-a16a-74220305815c'}, {'abstract': 'Readers, readers everywhere. At this week’s meeting of the Presidential Primary Book Club, we are discussing “This Is Herman Cain!”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/opinion/collins-heres-the-herminator.html', 'snippet': 'Readers, readers everywhere. At this week’s meeting of the Presidential Primary Book Club, we are discussing “This Is Herman Cain!”', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may have heard that Herman Cain, the former chief of Godfather’s Pizza, has become the latest in a list of peculiar front-runners for the Republican president