3-4d97-54f5-82f0-7d6fe7248148', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a5e27a3-4d97-54f5-82f0-7d6fe7248148'}, {'abstract': 'Partial presidential election results announced Friday suggest that the incumbent, Ellen Johnson Sirleaf, could be headed to a runoff next month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/world/africa/liberian-president-may-face-runoff.html', 'snippet': 'Partial presidential election results announced Friday suggest that the incumbent, Ellen Johnson Sirleaf, could be headed to a runoff next month.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Partial presidential election results announced Friday suggest that the incumbent, Ellen Johnson Sirleaf, could be headed to a runoff next month. With votes counted from 2,242 out of 4,457 polling places, Mrs. Sirleaf had 45 percent of the vote, to 30 percent for the ticket led by Winston Tubman, which also includes the former international soccer star George Weah, according to the National Elections Commission. If these percentages hold up, Mrs. Sirleaf would have less than the majority needed to win outright. In third place with 12 percent and the potential to be kingmaker is the former warlord Prince Johnson. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liberia: President May Face Runoff', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Liberia: President May Face Runoff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weah, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson Sirleaf, Ellen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T01:11:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8966870-a306-55d7-a3c3-a014096ae059', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8966870-a306-55d7-a3c3-a014096ae059'}, {'abstract': 'Bullying isn’t just a harmless game, it can be a deadly one, and we need to be reminded of that constantly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/opinion/blow-the-bleakness-of-the-bullied.html', 'snippet': 'Bullying isn’t just a harmless game, it can be a deadly one, and we need to be reminded of that constantly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have watched with a heavy heart these last few years as one child after another has committed suicide because he or she was bullied.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima