vestments in states like New Hampshire and Nevada for the Republican primary season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney, the former Massachusetts governor, raised just over $14 million for his presidential campaign during the three months that ended Sept. 30, according to campaign filings delivered to the Federal Election Commission on Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Raises $14 Million in 3rd Quarter, Second to Perry’s Receipts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Romney Raises $14 Million in 3rd Quarter, Second to Perry's Receipts", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T01:12:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bff7da45-57dc-5d82-95dc-a71d22e7b59e', 'word_count': 879, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bff7da45-57dc-5d82-95dc-a71d22e7b59e'}, {'abstract': 'More Americans seem to be recognizing that killing a prisoner is not the only way to make sure he is never released and that capital punishment is indefensible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/opinion/the-death-penaltys-de-facto-abolition.html', 'snippet': 'More Americans seem to be recognizing that killing a prisoner is not the only way to make sure he is never released and that capital punishment is indefensible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new Gallup poll reports that support for the death penalty is at its lowest level since 1972. In fact, though, the decline, from a high of 80 percent in 1994 to 61 percent now, masks both Americans’ ambivalence about capital punishment and the country’s de facto abolition of the penalty in most places.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Death Penalty’s De Facto Abolition', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Death Penalty&#8217;s De Facto Abolition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gallup Poll', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T01:13:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7860e952-716f-5d93-ae93-8e608f4a2a98', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7860e952-716f-5d93-ae93-8e608f4a2a98'}, {'abstract': 'As the demonstrations grow, the different worldviews of bankers show the wide chasms that have opened over who is to blame for economic malaise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/business/in-private-conversation-wall-street-is-more-critical-of-protesters.html', 'snippet': 'As the demonstrations grow, the different worldviews of bankers show the wide chasms that have opened over who is to blame for economic malaise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Publicly, bankers say they understand t