: 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de215c4b-a4e0-5a72-9bcf-d36d825ce788'}, {'abstract': 'More than 100 people, almost all of them connected to Central California gangs, were arrested this week in the latest effort to curb street gangs, Attorney General Kamala Harris announced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/us/california-gang-crackdown-leads-to-more-than-100-arrests.html', 'snippet': 'More than 100 people, almost all of them connected to Central California gangs, were arrested this week in the latest effort to curb street gangs, Attorney General Kamala Harris announced.', 'lead_paragraph': ' More than 100 people, almost all of them connected to Central California gangs, were arrested this week in the latest effort to curb street gangs, Attorney General Kamala Harris announced on Friday. The arrests resulted from an 18-month investigation by the California Department of Justice and other law enforcement agencies that began after a gang network set up operations in Gilroy. The operation also led to the seizure of 44 firearms, 81 stolen vehicles, 3 pounds of methamphetamine and other drugs. A majority of the 103 suspects arrested were gang members with felony convictions, the Department of Justice said. Suspects will face charges relating to auto theft, guns, gangs and the sale of narcotics. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Arrests in Gang Crackdown', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Arrests in Gang Crackdown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gangs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T01:43:33+0000', 'document_