s like Bay Ridge, Sunset Park and Park Slope and involved the groping and grabbing of young women near transportation hubs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The police said Friday that they had added six attacks in subway stations to a pattern of sexual assaults that have badly shaken several neighborhoods in South Brooklyn, bringing the total number of cases in that area up to 20 since March. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '6 Attacks Linked to Pattern in Brooklyn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '6 Attacks Linked to Pattern in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T01:49:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69703c1d-2aac-59cd-8e81-079535a42a6b', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69703c1d-2aac-59cd-8e81-079535a42a6b'}, {'abstract': 'On the eve of a meeting of the Central Committee of the Chinese Communist Party, a senior propaganda official said that social media need to be more tightly regulated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/world/asia/china-social-media-rules-weighed.html', 'snippet': 'On the eve of a meeting of the Central Committee of the Chinese Communist Party, a senior propaganda official said that social media need to be more tightly regulated.', 'lead_paragraph': ' With the Central Committee of the Chinese Communist Party scheduled to begin meeting Saturday, Wang Chen, a senior propaganda official, said that social media need to be more tightly regulated. The government seems likely to follow through on many hints that it would step up regulation of various Twitter-like microblogs like Weibo, said Bill Bishop, an independent analyst specializing in social media. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Social Media Rules Weighed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Social Media Rules Weighed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T01:50:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f928e493-20db-5e1c-945f-3bd8c6471509', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f928e493-20db-5e1c-945f-3bd8c6471509'}, {'abstract': 'House Republicans keep pounding at the nation’s bedrock protections, even including basic clean air and clean water laws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/opinion/the-republicans-vs-the-environment.html', 'snippet': 'House Republicans keep pounding at the nation’s bedrock protections, even including basic clean air and clean water laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As of Friday, the Republican-controlled House of Representatives had voted 168 times this year to undercut clean air and water laws while blocking efforts to limit global warming, protect public lands and guard against future oil spills. Henry Waxman, the senior Democrat on the Energy and Commerce Committee, calls this “the most anti-environmental Congress in history.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. vs. the Environment', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.O.P. vs. the Environment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Air Act', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Water Act', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T01:51:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff8f9ca1-651c-56af-ab36-9a98ff102a44', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff8f9ca1-651c-56af-ab36-9a98ff102a44'}, {'abstract': 'Deficit reduction based on fiscal austerity has led to a flat-lining economy in Britain. It is the wrong strategy for Britain, and for the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/opinion/britains-self-inflicted-misery.html', 'snippet': 'Deficit reduction based on fiscal austerity has led to a flat-lining economy in Britain. It is the wrong strategy for Britain, and for the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a year now, Britain’s economy has been stuck in a vicious cycle of low growth, high unemployment and fiscal austerity. But unlike Greece, which has been forced into induced recession by misguided European Union creditors, Britain has inflicted this harmful quack cure on itself. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain’s Self-Inflicted Misery', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain&#8217;s Self-Inflicted Misery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T01:52:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf7b0a93-a362-575c-98f7-d32ea967a07e', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf7b0a93-a362-575c-98f7-d32ea967a07e'}, {'abstract': 'The victim died after he apparently swallowed pills from a bottle of prescription drugs that his parents gave him to play with as a rattle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/nyregion/baby-boy-dies-of-suboxone-overdose.html', 'snippet': 'The victim died after he apparently swallowed pills from a bottle of prescription drugs that his parents gave him to play with as a rattle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 13-month-old boy died after he apparently swallowed pills from a bottle\xa0of prescription drugs that his parents had given him to play with as a rattle, the authorities said on Friday.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baby Boy Dies; Was Given Pills as a Toy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Given Pills as Toy, Baby Dies, Police Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perocier, Edwin Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suboxone (Drug)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T01:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72eaf23d-7177-5711-86a4-56f8bc2f45d0', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72eaf23d-7177-5711-86a4-56f8bc2f45d0'}, {'abstract': '“Jeopardy!” champ Joon Pahk is back to his old puzzle tricks.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/14/thinker/', 'snippet': '“Jeopardy!” champ Joon Pahk is back to his old puzzle tricks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY’S PUZZLE — So by now we all know that Joon Pahk ripped through Jeopardy!, won an ungodly amount of (pre-tax) money, qualified for the Tournament of Champions, and generally made us all proud, yes? Good, because today he’s back as a constructor with a tough but ultimately fair and fun puzzle that contains quite a few interesting consecutive-consonant and unique entries. Notice that I didn’t say crunchy. You’re welcome.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saturday: Rodin’s Thinker', 'kick