body would admit to feeling any for Game 6.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Both Sides Say They Don’t Feel the Pressure', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scherzer, Max', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T03:59:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Spousta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spousta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59f835e8-29ff-59f5-b62f-0c26d905f664', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59f835e8-29ff-59f5-b62f-0c26d905f664'}, {'abstract': 'Crossroads Theater Company’s production of “Ain’t Misbehavin’” largely reflects what the jazz musician and composer Fats Waller was known for.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/nyregion/review-crossroads-theater-companys-aint-misbehavin.html', 'snippet': 'Crossroads Theater Company’s production of “Ain’t Misbehavin’” largely reflects what the jazz musician and composer Fats Waller was known for.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If one musical number captures the spirit of “Ain’t Misbehavin’\xa0” (even more than the title song), it’s probably the 1938 toe-tapper “The Joint Is Jumpin.’\xa0” But in the Crossroads Theater Company’s spirited new production, it’s the out-of-character numbers that are most memorable.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/nyregion/16ARTSNJ-1/16ARTSNJ-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/nyregion/16ARTSNJ-1/16ARTSNJ-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/nyregion/16ARTSNJ-1/16ARTSNJ-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fats Waller, Reimagined', 'kicker': 'Arts | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fats Waller, Reimagined', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crossroads Theater Company', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T04:06:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3307df61-cf39-5728-aef0-0dcb13875221', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3307df61-cf39-5728-aef0-0dcb13875221'}, {'abstract': 'Carl Testa has organized the Uncertainty Music Series, held the second Saturday of every month at Never Ending Books, a bookstore-cum-community center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/nyregion/a-music-series-where-uncertainty-is-embraced.html', 'snippet': 'Carl Testa has organized the Uncertainty Music Series, held the second Saturday of every month at Never Ending Books, a bookstore-cum-community center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNCERTAINTY is getting a particularly bad rap these days, not least from politicians and pundits who blame it for the reluctance of businesses to hire and consumers to spend. But to Carl Testa, a musician for whom the act of making art is not divorced from the conditions in which it is made, the rise of uncertainty is a precursor to social transformation. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/nyregion/16MUSICCT/16MUSICCT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 875, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Following Uncertainty and Finding Music', 'kicker': 'Arts | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Following Uncertainty And Finding Music', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Haven (Conn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T04:18:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Lutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71fec146-d818-5598-bd29-1e143ab4d422', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71fec146-d818-5598-bd29-1e143ab4d422'}, {'abstract': 'Paintings by Adam Van Doren, a third-generation member of the of the Van Doren clan of New York and Cornwall, Conn., are on view at Darren Winston Books and Prints.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/nyregion/adam-van-doren-takes-on-german-expressionism.html', 'snippet': 'Paintings by Adam Van Doren, a third-generation member of the of the Van Doren clan of New York and Cornwall, Conn., are on view at Darren Winston Books and Prints.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YOU could say that Adam Van Doren was born with a silver-edged book in his hands. A third-generation member of the famous Van Doren clan of New York and Cornwall, Conn., he grew up among writers, poets, critics and academics. His grandfather, Mark, and great-uncle, Carl, were both Pulitzer Prize-winning professors at Columbia University; his uncle, Charles, also taught at Columbia until his involvement in the TV quiz show scandal of 1959 brought his career to an abrupt end. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/nyregion/16ARTSCT-1_SPAN/16ARTSCT-1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/16/nyregion/16ARTSCT-1_SPAN/16ARTSCT-1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/nyregion/16ARTSCT-1_SPAN/16ARTSCT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/nyregion/16ARTSCT-1_SPAN/16ARTSCT-1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/nyregion/16ARTSCT-1_SPAN/16ARTSCT-1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': 