fficials had not been in direct contact over the alleged plot to assassinate Saudi Arabia’s ambassador to the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American officials said Thursday that they had conveyed their concerns to the Iranian government over the alleged plot to assassinate Saudi Arabia’s ambassador to the United States. But on Friday, Iran’s official Islamic Republic News Agency insisted that American officials had not been in direct contact with Iran. Payton Knopf, a spokesman for the United States Mission to the United Nations, said, though, that “there has been direct contact with the U.S. government.” He declined to elaborate. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran: Did Plot Dialogue Take Place?', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran: Did Plot Dialogue Take Place?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T04:34:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By NYT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nyt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c1424c1-58fa-5345-ab88-3d29723b06f1', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c1424c1-58fa-5345-ab88-3d297