 city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/nyregion/vic-miles-reporter-and-anchor-on-wcbs-tv-dies-at-79.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Miles brought a no-nonsense, get-to-the-essence style to his 24 years as a reporter and anchorman for WCBS-TV/Channel 2 in New York and was among the first black television reporters in the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vic Miles, who brought a no-nonsense, get-to-the-essence style to his 24 years as a reporter and anchorman for WCBS-TV/Channel 2 in New York, died on Wednesday in Manhattan. He was 79.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/nyregion/MILES-obit/MILES-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 615, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/nyregion/MILES-obit/MILES-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/15/nyregion/MILES-obit/MILES-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vic Miles, Reporter and Anchor on WCBS-TV, Dies at 79', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vic Miles, 79, Reporter And Anchor on WCBS-TV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WCBS-TV', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T05:16:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/169698aa-b31e-5705-8d92-feabfd8b583f', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/169698aa-b31e-5705-8d92-feabfd8b583f'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Aghayan was the costume designer for stars like Judy Garland, Barbra Streisand, Diana Ross and Julie Andrews.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/arts/ray-aghayan-costume-designer-dies-at-83.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Aghayan was the costume designer for stars like Judy Garland, Barbra Streisand, Diana Ross and Julie Andrews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ray Aghayan designed his first dress, at 13, for a member of the royal court of the shah of Iran, which at the time employed his mother as a couturier, a sort of in-house designer for the personal and ceremonial needs of the Reza Pahlavi family.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/arts/AGHAYAN1-obit/AGHAYAN1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/15/arts/AGHAYAN1-obit/AGHAYAN1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/15/arts/AGHAYAN1-obit/AGHAYAN1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ray Aghayan, Costume Designer, Dies at 83', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ray Aghayan, Costume Designer, Dies at 83', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T05:41:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Vitello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vitello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/d97f9f90-1f7c-5c91-be80-20e5b55f58d4', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d97f9f90-1f7c-5c91-be80-20e5b55f58d4'}, {'abstract': 'Top stories from regional papers this week.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/newswallah-bharat-edition-6/', 'snippet': 'Top stories from regional papers this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jammu and Kashmir: India’s longest railway tunnel, through the Pir Panchal mountain range, was opened on Friday. The seven-mile long tunnel, which will “connect Kashmir with the outside world,” will be operational by 2012, Northern Railway officials said. (Greater Kashmir)Manipur: A 2-month-old blockade on arterial highways connecting Manipur is wreaking havoc in the state, the Manipur People’s Party said, causing skyrocketing prices for food, fuel and other basic amenities. (Nagaland Post) However, the chief minister of Manipur, Okram Ibobi, rubbished these reports, saying “you people sit there and report, come to Manipur tomorrow and see it is not true.” (Telegraph)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Bharat Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banerjee, Mamata', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organi