agazine-renewal-and-automated-voices.html', 'snippet': 'A reader complains to the Haggler about the way her magazine subscriptions were renewed, and about the automated system that answered her call.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVER get the sense that the junk mail you throw out every day includes an item or two that you really ought to read? Ever wonder if \xa0some ought-to-read letters have been designed to look junky on purpose? ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/business/16-HAGGLER/16-HAGGLER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 786, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/business/16-HAGGLER/16-HAGGLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/business/16-HAGGLER/16-HAGGLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Did This Become a Commitment?', 'kicker': 'The Haggler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Did This Become a Commitment?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T19:54:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Segal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Segal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b2f1a27-2efc-520f-b47f-3b9d85df718b', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b2f1a27-2efc-520f-b47f-3b9d85df718b'}, {'abstract': 'The United States and its allies need to find better ways to persuade China to change policies that are both battering the global economy and damaging its own future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/opinion/sunday/its-not-just-the-currency.html', 'snippet': 'The United States and its allies need to find better ways to persuade China to change policies that are both battering the global economy and damaging its own future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate’s vote on Tuesday to punish China for cheapening its currency is not likely to persuade Beijing to change its ways. On Thursday, the renminbi actually fell more against the dollar. If the currency bill were to become law — a long shot given opposition by Republican leaders in the House — the more likely response from China would be some form of trade policy retaliation. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Not Just the Currency', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Not Just the Currency', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renminbi (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T19:55:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a713f9ca-2e0e-57ee-ae72-b525af6017ed', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a713f9ca-2e0e-57ee-ae72-b525af6017ed'}, {'abstract': 'The police said that the victim had fought violently with his mother in the past.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/15/woman-is-questioned-in-killing-of-son-18-on-upper-west-side/', 'snippet': 'The police said that the victim had fought violently with his mother in the past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the police came to Apartment 11G at 74 West 92nd Street on Friday night, they were met at the door by a woman holding a bloody sponge. On the floor behind her was the body of her 18-year-old son, dead from a stab wound to his thigh, the police said Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woman Is Questioned in Killing of Son, 18, on Upper West Side', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T20:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f996505-f35b-5a01-a8af-549a37c3e59d', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f996505-f35b-5a01-a8af-549a37c3e59d'}, {'abstract': 'Increasing taxes on the rich is a fair and sound policy. It can help the government pay for programs to revive the economy and wrestle down the deficit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/opinion/sunday/we-thought-they-wanted-to-be-like-buffett.html', 'snippet': 'Increasing taxes on the rich is a fair and sound policy. It can help the government pay for programs to revive the economy and wrestle down the deficit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Warren Buffett pointed out that the American tax system was so egregiously rigged that he paid a smaller share of his income in taxes than his secretary, very few of his peers chimed in. It was so quiet that one might have thought Mr. Buffett’s case was a fluke. It wasn’t. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We Thought They Wanted to Be Like Buffett', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Thought They Wanted to Be Like Buffett', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buffett, Warren E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T20:08:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e672101-07d9-5f6d-8407-f7ed89d05fa8', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e672101-07d9-5f6d-8407-f7ed89d05fa8'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Michele Bachmann gave a speech Saturday about the burdens illegal immigration places on American taxpayers and signed a pledge to bui