ITY — Laura Pollán Toledo, a former high school Spanish teacher who became one of Cuba’s most public dissidents as she led other wives of political prisoners in protest every Sunday, died in a Havana hospital on Friday, her family and other dissidents said. She was 63. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/world/obit-POLLAN/obit-POLLAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/world/obit-POLLAN/obit-POLLAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/world/obit-POLLAN/obit-POLLAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Laura Pollán Toledo, Who Rallied Wives of Jailed Cuban Dissidents, Dies at 63', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laura Pollán Toledo, 63; Rallied Wives of Jailed Cuban Dissidents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ladies in White (Cuba)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollan Toledo, Laura', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-15T21:27:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byl