s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The phrase bed and breakfast often conjures images of stuffy homes filled with dusty doilies and collections of wide-eyed dolls. But the B&B industry and its standards have evolved. Say goodbye to the days of squeaky beds and frivolous throw pillows and embrace the shift toward classically elegant and strikingly modern retreats. Whether you prefer attentive or hands-off service, accommodations steeped in history or an urban atmosphere, there is a (feather-topped or custom-built) bed and a (candlelit or grab-and-go) breakfast that fits your needs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/us/16TTTRAVEL/16TTTRAVEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/16/us/16TTTRAVEL/16TTTRAVEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/16/us/16TTTRAVEL/16TTTRAVEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'B&B’s That Break the Dolls-and-Doilies Mold', 'kicker': 'Texas Monthly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'B&B’s That Break the Dolls-and-Doilies Mold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bed-and-Breakfast Lodgings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Corpus Christi (Tex)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T00:44:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'secti