000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64d86630-f9bf-51fc-94f8-7200812835f5', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64d86630-f9bf-51fc-94f8-7200812835f5'}, {'abstract': 'Sebastian Vettel won his tenth Grand Prix of the season in Korea, and his team took the 2011 constructors’ title. But the story of the weekend, and the excitement of the race, came from Lewis Hamilton of McLaren Mercedes.', 'web_url': 'https://formulaone.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/vettel-takes-10th-victory-red-bull-takes-title-but-hamilton-provides-the-story/', 'snippet': 'Sebastian Vettel won his tenth Grand Prix of the season in Korea, and his team took the 2011 constructors’ title. But the story of the weekend, and the excitement of the race, came from Lewis Hamilton of McLaren Mercedes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YEONGAM, South Korea — Sebastian Vettel may have won the Korean Grand Prix on Sunday in his usual dominating manner, taking his 10th victory of the season and the 20th of his career. And his team, Red Bull, may have won the 2011 constructors’ title thanks to that result. But all of the excitement both on track and off throughout the weekend came from another man: Lewis Hamilton.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vettel Takes 10th Victory, Red Bull Takes Title, but Hamilton Provides the Story', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Lewis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vettel, Sebastian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McLaren Racing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T10:31:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d6ed8bc-fa21-5919-b00b-3c5e141876c8', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d6ed8bc-fa21-5919-b00b-3c5e141876c8'}, {'abstract': 'Sebastian Vettel won his tenth Grand Prix of the season in Korea, and his team took the 2011 constructors’ title. But the story of the weekend, and the excitement of the race, came from Lewis Hamilton of McLaren Mercedes.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/vettel-takes-10th-victory-red-bull-takes-title-but-hamilton-provides-the-story/', 'snippet': 'Sebastian Vettel won his tenth Grand Prix of the season in Korea, and his team took the 2011 constructors’ title. But the story of the weekend, and the excitement of the race, came from Lewis Hamilton of McLaren Mercedes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YEONGAM, South Korea — Sebastian Vettel may have won the Korean Grand Prix on Sunday in his usual dominating manner, taking his 10th victory of the season and the 20th of his career. And his team, Red Bull, may have won the 2011 constructors’ title thanks to that result. But all of the excitement both on track and off throughout the weekend came from another man: Lewis Hamilton.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vettel Takes 10th Victory, Red Bull Takes Title, but Hamilton Provides the Story', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Lewis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vettel, Sebastian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McLaren Racing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T10:31:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a53694d5-1e3c-5736-adda-fe71e6f4f41a', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a53694d5-1e3c-5736-adda-fe71e6f4f41a'}, {'abstract': 'In 62 seasons of playing against each other, the 49ers and Lions have rarely had a relevant matchup. With both teams off to a strong start, this season is the exception to the rule.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/niners-lions-a-rarely-relevant-rivalry/', 'snippet': 'In 62 seasons of playing against each other, the 49ers and Lions have rarely had a relevant matchup. With both teams off to a strong start, this season is the exception to the rule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would seem unlikely that over the course of 62 seasons, two N.F.L. teams could combine for eight championships but manage to play each other in 50 largely irrelevant games. But mediocrity has been the standard when it comes to games between the Detroit Lions and San Francisco 49ers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Niners-Lions: A Rarely Relevant Rivalry', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Lions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T11:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f85d338a-b719-5a98-a669-2d48e5c31fe2', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f85d338a-b719-5a98-a669-2d48e5c31fe2'}, {'abstract': 'An inexpensive new video tool lets you shoot a moving 360-degree panorama using the iPhone.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/a-videocamera-that-captures-360-degrees-of-action/', 'snippet': 'An inexpensive new video tool lets you shoot a moving 360-degree panorama using the iPhone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Video in 3-D may be all the rage, but there is an inexpensive new video tool that I think has greater potential to change the way you shoot video.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Videocamera That Captures 360 Degrees of Action', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T11:01:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bac7a473-a881-5473-a9df-bf8ca062d0c9', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bac7a473-a881-5473-a9df-bf8ca062d0c9'}, {'abstract': 'The Martin Luther King Jr. memorial — a four-acre tract along the Tidal Basin that is anchored by an imposing granite statue of Dr. King — is the result of more than two decades of work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/us/memorial-of-martin-luther-king-jr-dedicated-in-washington.html', 'snippet': 'The Martin Luther King Jr. memorial — a four-acre tract along the Tidal Basin that is anchored by an imposing granite statue of Dr. King — is the result of more than two decades of work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — They came from across the country, some arriving before dawn, carrying folding chairs, cameras and a strong, proud sense of history. Thousands stood and sat together under a bright blue sky Sunday as a memorial to the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. — the first honoring an African-American in the area of the Mall — was dedicated at last.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/us/17king2/17king2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/us/17king2/17king2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/us/17king2/17king2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dedication to King, and the Work Yet to Do', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dedication to King, And the Work Yet to Do', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'g