ed to business after a hiatus, still using some of the same techniques Benjamin Franklin used.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first thing about Robert Warner’s print shop is it is urine-free.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Print Shop Cranks Back Up, Ancient as Ever', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franklin, Benjamin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T19:11:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f989f7b9-dfe8-5667-8fb7-213953f78870', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f989f7b9-dfe8-5667-8fb7-213953f78870'}, {'abstract': 'The Orpheus Chamber Orchestra performed a new work by Cynthia Wong, a young composer whose piece, “Memoriam,” was dedicated to her father.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/arts/music/orpheus-chamber-orchestra-at-carnegie-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Orpheus Chamber Orchestra performed a new work by Cynthia Wong, a young composer whose piece, “Memoriam,” was dedicated to her father.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The conductorless Orpheus Chamber Orchestra has long demonstrated its mettle in Baroque and classical fare. More recently it has ventured into romantic and contemporary terrain, which is invariably harder to navigate without a conductor. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/orpheus/orpheus-articleLarge.j