 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecc6b495-20ad-5b7b-8dc8-8da22b226f68', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecc6b495-20ad-5b7b-8dc8-8da22b226f68'}, {'abstract': 'Israel released the names of the first Palestinian prisoners whom it will exchange for a soldier held by Hamas. Most have been convicted of manslaughter, attempted murder or intentionally causing death.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/world/middleeast/israel-releases-names-of-477-prisoners-to-be-freed-in-trade.html', 'snippet': 'Israel released the names of the first Palestinian prisoners whom it will exchange for a soldier held by Hamas. Most have been convicted of manslaughter, attempted murder or intentionally causing death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RAMALLAH, West Bank — Israel on Sunday released the names of the first 477 Palestinian prisoners that it will exchange for a soldier held by the militant faction Hamas, and the list revealed why the country has found the trade so wrenching: a majority of the inmates were convicted of manslaughter, attempted murder or intentionally causing death.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/world/SHALIT-1/SHALIT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Releases Names of 477 Prisoners to Be Freed in Trade', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Names 477 to Go Free in Trade for Hamas-Held Soldier', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shalit, Gilad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T19:26:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner and Stephen Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae2132e0-425d-5d9e-826e-9ff45f7d05fe', 'word_count': 1226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae2132e0-425d-5d9e-826e-9ff45f7d05fe'}, {'abstract': '“Visible,” at the Harlem Stage Gatehouse, examines American history and ideas of freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/arts/dance/visible-at-harlem-stage-gatehouse-review.html', 'snippet': '“Visible,” at the Harlem Stage Gatehouse, examines American history and ideas of freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many moments in “Visible” when what seems casual is likely to be painstakingly drawn, when multiple layers of sound, text and movement create a kind of symphony. The production still seems half-baked, yet when it coheres, it’s like good jazz: without being literal it finds its way back to its theme. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/visible/visible-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/visible/visible-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/visible/visible-jumbo.j