or in 2009, it was business as usual.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Polished but perfunctory music making and unadventurous programming were often the hallmarks of Lorin Maazel’s tenure as music director of the New York Philharmonic. An amiable matinee concert on Friday at Avery Fisher Hall, the first time Mr. Maazel has conducted the Philharmonic since his departure in 2009, continued that tradition. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conductor’s Homecoming', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Conductor’s Homecoming', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maazel, Lorin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T19:53:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a622c52e-b767-5cce-9e97-1c15b635390a', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a622c52e-b767-5cce-9e97-1c15b635390a'}, {'abstract': 'A day after violent youths transformed a peaceful demonstration to call attention to economic inequality into a riot, Italy fell into national soul searching and finger pointing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/world/europe/in-italy-rioting-leads-to-recriminations.html', 'snippet': 'A day after violent youths transformed a peaceful demonstration to call attention to economic inequality into a riot, Italy fell into national soul searching and finger pointing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — As the smoke cleared Sunday, a day after a peaceful, inchoate demonstration near the Colosseum turned into a riot, Italy fell into national soul-searching and finger-pointing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/world/ITALY/ITALY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/17/world/ITALY/ITALY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/world/ITALY/ITALY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/world/ITALY/ITALY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/world/ITALY/ITALY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Italy, Rioting Leads to Recriminations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Riot in Rome, Anger and Second-Guessing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T20:06:26+0000', 'do