 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8d6cfe6-c79f-59ab-9d0b-7508000c06e3'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition to open at the New-York Historical Society on Nov. 11 delves into American taste in art during a crucial period from the 1830s through the 1860s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/arts/making-american-taste-at-the-new-york-historical-society.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition to open at the New-York Historical Society on Nov. 11 delves into American taste in art during a crucial period from the 1830s through the 1860s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early on the morning of July 27, 1861, New York’s 69th (Irish) Regiment returned from the First Battle of Bull Run, landing by steamboat at what is now Battery Park.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/17RETURN/17RETURN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/17RETURN/17RETURN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/17RETURN/17RETURN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/17RETURN/17RETURN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/17RETURN/17RETURN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Applying the Paint Was Spreading the News', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Applying the Paint Was Spreading the News', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New-York Historical Society', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Williamstown Art Conservation Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T20:39:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18e0a13e-48a7-535d-9328-7ab5c14a2161', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18e0a13e-48a7-535d-9328-7ab5c14a2161'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Boyd will step down as artistic director at The Royal Shakespeare Company.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/exeunt/', 'snippet': 'Michael Boyd will step down as artistic director at The Royal Shakespeare Company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Royal Shakespeare Company has announced that Michael Boyd will step down as artistic director next year, after more than a decade in the job, the BBC News reported. The executive director, Vikki Heywood, will leave her post at the same time. Under their supervision, the company recently completed a $177 million renovation of its theaters in Stratford-Upon-Avon, England, and a successful six-week run of performances in New York at the Park Avenue Armory. Mr. Boyd is also a chief architect of the World Shakespeare Festival, a celebration set to run from April to September 2012. Mr. Boyd said in a statement that it was “time for me to pass the challenges on to a new artistic director.” The company is expected to announce a successor early next year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exeunt', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Shakespeare Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T20:59:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f5455c2-6f7b-505c-83ca-081e5a3abdfe', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f5455c2-6f7b-505c-83ca-081e5a3abdfe'}, {'abstract': 'Ahmad Bradshaw set a career high for scoring and ran 30 yards to set up Lawrence Tynes’s game-winning field goal with 1:35 left.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/sports/football/ahmad-bradshaw-helps-giants-beat-bills-27-24.html', 'snippet': 'Ahmad Bradshaw set a career high for scoring and ran 30 yards to set up Lawrence Tynes’s game-winning field goal with 1:35 left.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Near the end of every Giants practice, as the players’ shoulders are drooping and their legs are dragging, a familiar refrain can be heard from the coaching staff.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/GIANTSfloater/GIANTSfloater-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/GIANTSfloater/GIANTSfloater-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/GIANTSfloater/GIANTSfloater-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/GIANTSfloater/GIANTSfloater-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/GIANTSfloater/GIANTSfloater-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Following Coaches’ Orders, Giants Produce Closing Kick Against Bills', 'kicker': 'Giants 27, Bills 24', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Following Orders With a Closing Kick', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tynes, Lawrence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradshaw, Ahmad', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzpatrick, Ryan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buffalo Bills', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Webster, Corey', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T21:03:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f59ff08-7121-5679-8947-f5efe7199c0d', 'word_count': 1065, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f59ff08-7121-5679-8947-f5efe7199c0d'}, {'abstract': 'Stan Lee joins 1821 Comics to start a multimedia imprint for children called, “Stan Lee’s Kids Universe.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/monsters-v-kittens/', 'snippet': 'Stan Lee joins 1821 Comics to start a multimedia imprint for children called, “Stan Lee’s Kids Universe.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stan Lee, a co-creator of childhood mainstays like Spider-Man, the X-Men and the Fantastic Four, will join with 1821 Comics to start a multimedia imprint for children called “Stan Lee’s Kids Universe.” The imprint, announced at the New York Comic Con on Friday and reported on galleycat.com, is to feature five books, including “Monsters vs. Kittens,” created by Dani Jones, and “Reggie the Veggie Crocodile.” Also among their plans is a video game for iPhone and iPad. At a Comic Con panel presentation, Mr. Lee said, “Our main purpose is we feel that there aren’t enough comic books or books for kids that really hit the target, that gives them excitement and humor together and are filled with surprises. We have a whole new group of new characters that the kids can call their own, just as the teenagers called Spider-Man their own so many years ago.” Mr. Lee is also collaborating with the 1821 Comics co-founder Terry Douglas, the writer Max Work and the artist Skan Srisuwan on a graphic novel, “Romeo & Juliet: The War,” a futuristic interpretation of the play — but with superpowers. The book is to be released in November.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monsters v. Kittens', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Stan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T21:12:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69b22da2-1484-5213-bba8-e89db402520d', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69b22da2-1484-5213-bba8-e89db402520d'}, {'abstract': 'Lions Coach Jim Schwartz chased after Niners Coach Jim Harbaugh and shoved him after what he perceived to be an overexuberant celebration following the 49ers’ victory.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/was-schwartz-justified-in-being-upset-with-harbaugh/', 'snippet': 'Lions Coach Jim Schwartz chased after Niners Coach Jim Harbaugh and shoved him after what he perceived to be an overexuberant celebration following the 49ers’ victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lions Coach Jim Schwartz chased after Niners Coach Jim Harbaugh and bumped him after what he apparently felt was an overexuberant celebration by Harbaugh following the 49ers’ 25-19 victory on Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Was Schwartz Justified in Being Upset With Harbaugh?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harbaugh, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Lions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T21:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88caaf54-ffc1-5ccc-9034-967014450a88', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88caaf54-ffc1-5ccc-9034-967014450a88'}, {'abstract': 'Kenya’s military stormed into Somalia on Sunday, sending hundreds of troops to battle the Shabab militant group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/world/africa/kenyan-forces-enter-somalia-to-battle-shabab.html', 'snippet': 'Kenya’s military stormed into Somalia on Sunday, sending hundreds of troops to battle the Shabab militant group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — The Kenyan military stormed into Somalia on Sunday, sending hundreds of troops to battle the Shabab militant group and becoming the latest East African country to be dragged into Somalia’s intractable anarchy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenyan Forces Enter Somalia to Battle Militants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kenya Enters Somalia Fray To Confront Insurgents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T21:20:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2ec3948-d72d-5394-9ff4-7884f031a099', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2ec3948-d72d-5394-9ff4-7884f031a099'}, {'abstract': 'The former N.B.A. star Kenny Anderson, once a New York City basketball prodigy, has a new mission as coach at a Jewish school in Florida.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/sports/basketball/kenny-andersons-new-path-leads-him-to-hebrew-school.html', 'snippet': 'The former N.B.A. star Kenny Anderson, once a New York City basketball prodigy, has a new mission as coach at a Jewish school in Florida.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kenny Anderson is one of the most intriguing athletes I have covered. He didn’t score the most points or transform the game, but his career from 13 to 35 illustrates the dark and light spots of an industry built on the backs of children.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/basketball/17rhoden-pic/17rhoden-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/basketball/17rhoden-pic/17rhoden-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/basketball/17rhoden-pic/17rhoden-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/basketball/17rhoden-pic/17rhoden-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/basketball/17rhoden-pic/17rhoden-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Surprising Twist in a Career That Has Been Full of Them', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Surprising Twist in a Career That Has Been Full of Them', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interscholastic Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, KENNY', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T21:27:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By William C. Rhoden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Rhoden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/501639f8-f2a4-55e9-bbb5-869162544890', 'word_count': 1402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/501639f8-f2a4-55e9-bbb5-869162544890'}, {'abstract': 'The depravity in Lucky McKee’s film “The Woman,” about a family and its captive, caused people to walk out when it was shown at Sundance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/movies/The-Woman-Directed-by-Lucky-McKee-Review.html', 'snippet': 'The depravity in Lucky McKee’s film “The Woman,” about a family and its captive, caused people to walk out when it was shown at Sundance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the horror movie “The Woman” Chris Cleek is a prosperous country lawyer with oil industry contacts and a secretary he flirts with. He runs his handsome home with almost military efficiency, having trained his family — Brian, in middle school, a chip off the old block; Peggy, a wary, withdrawn teenager; Darlin’, his charming post-toddler daughter; and Belle, his docile wife — to heed his authority. He enjoys his camouflage gear, scoped rifle and solo hunting expeditions. So when he finds the fierce, feral Woman subsisting in the woods, why shouldn’t he capture her in a net, suspend her in manacles from the roof of a ground cellar and enlist his family in her “rehabilitation”?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/woman-1/woman-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/woman-1/woman-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/woman-1/woman-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/woman-1/woman-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/woman-1/woman-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Big Happy Family (and Prisoner)', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Woman'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Big Happy Family (and Prisoner)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKee, Lucky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T21:50:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/af8dcf77-4ac3-524f-860e-90acccc1a2c2', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af8dcf77-4ac3-524f-860e-90acccc1a2c2'}, {'abstract': 'The rate stuff, not.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/gross-miscalculation/', 'snippet': 'The rate stuff, not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Somehow I missed this: Joe Weisenthal informs us that Bill Gross has publicly apologized for getting the bond market so wrong, predicting a spike in interest rates when QE2 ended. As Weisenthal points out, however, Gross’s exaggerated fear of deficits was very widespread; it was, indeed, what all the Very Serious People were obsessing about, even as the real economy was falling apart.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gross Miscalculation', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T21:50:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35f8d913-1a14-5728-b97b-4b5b69430929', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35f8d913-1a14-5728-b97b-4b5b69430929'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Wheldon died after his car burst into flames in a wreck that involved 14 others at the Las Vegas Indy 300.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/sports/autoracing/Dan-Wheldon-Crash-Vegas-IndyCar.html', 'snippet': 'Dan Wheldon died after his car burst into flames in a wreck that involved 14 others at the Las Vegas Indy 300.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dan Wheldon, a popular and congenial racecar driver from England who won the Indianapolis 500 for the second time in May, died Sunday in a fiery 15-car accident early in a 300-mile IndyCar Series race at Las Vegas Motor Speedway.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/autoracing/17indycar1/17indycar1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/autoracing/17indycar1/17indycar1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/autoracing/17indycar1/17indycar1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/autoracing/17indycar1/17indycar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/sports/autoracing/17indycar1/17indycar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheldon, Indy 500 Winner, Dies After Crash', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wheldon, Indy 500 Winner, Dies After Las Vegas Crash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indy Racing League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheldon, Dan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T21:55:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Auto Racing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b8e2f4d-2481-5cf0-b848-d4daf7c8b05c', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b8e2f4d-2481-5cf0-b848-d4daf7c8b05c'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama, Representative John Lewis and the Rev. Jesse Jackson spoke at the opening ceremony for the Martin Luther King Jr. Memorial.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/a-grand-opening-for-the-martin-luther-king-jr-monument/', 'snippet': 'President Obama, Representative John Lewis and the Rev. Jesse Jackson spoke at the opening ceremony for the Martin Luther King Jr. Memorial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An expansive three-hour ceremony opened the memorial to Martin Luther King Jr. in Washington on Sunday, with speeches by President Obama and civil rights leaders like Representative John Lewis and the Rev. Jesse Jackson, and songs by performers like Aretha Franklin, my colleagues Helene Cooper and Sabrina Tavernise reported: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Grand Opening for the Martin Luther King Jr. Monument', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T21:56:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef1cc9d2-28ec-5a8c-a1ee-c1c1d48a71a7', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef1cc9d2-28ec-5a8c-a1ee-c1c1d48a71a7'}, {'abstract': 'Day 1 of the week-long crossword contest. I’m so excited I could just plotz.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/day-one-contest/', 'snippet': 'Day 1 of the week-long crossword contest. I’m so excited I could just plotz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Administrivial Contest Rules Alert! All the puzzles this week, from Monday to Saturday, have been created by one person, Patrick Berry. Have your solutions handy, because the Saturday puzzle conceals a meta-challenge involving the solution grids of all six.\xa0When you have the answer to the meta-challenge, e-mail it to: crossword@nytimes.com. Please do not post your answers here on the blog and please do not mail them to me! Only answers e-mailed to the above address will be considered.\xa0Twenty-five correct solvers, chosen at random, whose entries are received by 6 p.m. Eastern time Sunday, Oct. 23, will receive copies of “Will Shortz Picks His Favorite Puzzles: 101 of the Top Crosswords From The New York Times.” Only one entry per person, please. The answer and winners’ names will appear on Friday, Oct. 28, at nytimes.com/wordplay.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday: Welcome to Day One of the Crossword Puzzle Contest', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T22:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bb11c79-d042-522f-9433-0b15ba579e38', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bb11c79-d042-522f-9433-0b15ba579e38'}, {'abstract': 'Prateik plays Michael Pinto, a Goan innocent who meets a host of Mumbai characters, in this Bollywood comedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/movies/My-Friend-Pinto-Bollywood-Comedy-Starring-Prateik-Review.html', 'snippet': 'Prateik plays Michael Pinto, a Goan innocent who meets a host of Mumbai characters, in this Bollywood comedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Life, according to a song in the Bollywood comedy “My Friend Pinto,” is cute, and has many moods: sometimes it’s misty, sometimes it’s crispy (or so goes the translation). “My Friend Pinto” also has many moods, too many really. It’s cute, sort of, as well as crudely slapstick and sweetly picaresque, and just a bit misty and crispy.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/myfriend/myfriend-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 838, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/myfriend/myfriend-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/myfriend/myfriend-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Innocent Who’s Adrift in Mumbai', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'My Friend Pinto'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Innocent Who’s Adrift In Mumbai', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T22:02:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/277625b9-b9df-5750-b0ce-b297ee601416', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/277625b9-b9df-5750-b0ce-b297ee601416'}, {'abstract': 'The Merlin Entertainments Group has six new or coming United States attractions, sending a message to North America: We are coming after you.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/business/media/merlin-entertainment-brings-its-amusement-parks-to-america.html', 'snippet': 'The Merlin Entertainments Group has six new or coming United States attractions, sending a message to North America: We are coming after you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WINTER HAVEN, Fla. — The Merlin Entertainments Group is one of the world’s largest operators of amusement parks and tourist attractions, entertaining more than 40 million visitors annually. But the company operates almost entirely overseas, and it has no presence in central Florida, the sweaty epicenter of the theme park universe.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/business/LEGO/LEGO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/17/business/LEGO/LEGO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/business/LEGO/LEGO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/business/LEGO/LEGO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/business/LEGO/LEGO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Britain, It’s Legoland', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Britain, It’s Legoland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMUSEMENT AND THEME PARKS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lego Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Legoland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T22:05:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecbca61d-ed1e-574c-b698-317373624212', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecbca61d-ed1e-574c-b698-317373624212'}, {'abstract': 'In the choreographer Sally Silvers’s “Prize Every Time” at Roulette in Brooklyn, performers had 30 minutes to create something and enact it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/arts/dance/Sally-Silverss-Prize-Every-Time-at-Roulette-Review.html', 'snippet': 'In the choreographer Sally Silvers’s “Prize Every Time” at Roulette in Brooklyn, performers had 30 minutes to create something and enact it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Had you been at Roulette, the theater in downtown Brooklyn, on Friday night, you would have learned — or been reminded of — a few things. Performing artists are unparalleled and exciting problem solvers, for example. The creative process, on the other hand, is often quite boring. And: the saints are the sinners who keep trying. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/silvers/silvers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1002, 'width': 721, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/silvers/silvers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/silvers/silvers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Performance From Soup to Nuttiness', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Performance From Soup to Nuttiness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silvers, Sally', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T22:07:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/331296f5-812d-5ab2-8fb5-f587c67733cd', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/331296f5-812d-5ab2-8fb5-f587c67733cd'}, {'abstract': 'The new boats on the East River have carried more than twice as many riders as forecast, and their operator is pressing the city to let him expand service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/nyregion/east-river-ferry-service-exceeds-expectations.html', 'snippet': 'The new boats on the East River have carried more than twice as many riders as forecast, and their operator is pressing the city to let him expand service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After several failed attempts at encouraging the use of boats to commute across the East River, city officials have an unforeseen problem: too many ferry riders.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/nyregion/17ferry1/17ferry1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/nyregion/17ferry1/17ferry1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/nyregion/17ferry1/17ferry1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Though Others Failed, New East River Ferries Are a Hit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pleasant Surprise for East River Ferries: Crowds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ferries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commuting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Waterway', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East River (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'maj