word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c680f023-df51-589a-b08c-e72390032e6c'}, {'abstract': 'Julian Barnes’s new novel, “The Sense of an Ending,” is on the short list for the Man Booker Prize, to be announced on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/books/Julian-Barness-Sense-of-an-Ending-Review.html', 'snippet': 'Julian Barnes’s new novel, “The Sense of an Ending,” is on the short list for the Man Booker Prize, to be announced on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there is a single theme running throughout Julian Barnes’s work, from his 1985 masterpiece, “Flaubert’s Parrot,” to “A History of the World in 10 ½ Chapters” (1989), “Love, Etc.,” and recent collections like “Pulse” (2011), it’s the elusiveness of truth, the subjectivity of memory, the relativity of all knowledge. While earlier books examined our limited ability to comprehend other people and other eras, his latest novel, “The Sense of an Ending” — which was shortlisted for this year’s Man Booker Prize (the winner will be announced Tuesday) — looks at the ways in which people distort or tailor the past in an effort to mythologize their own lives. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Life in Smoke and Mirrors', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Life in Smoke And Mirrors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': No