ble at Symphony Space on Friday and Saturday nights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a grainy 1972 video online of  Eddie and Charlie Palmieri playing “Vamonos Pa’l Monte” at the old Central Park Bandshell. It is one of the most deeply New York things you will ever see, multi-ethnic and multi-generational and crazily rocking. As the onstage hand-held camera whirls around, you see the brothers Andy and Jerry Gonzalez, then in their early 20s, in the band, Andy on bass and Jerry on congas, each in his own rhythmic trance. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/latin/latin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 666, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/latin/latin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/arts/latin/latin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scholarship You Could Dance To', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scholarship You Could Dance To', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Symphony Space', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Afro Latin Jazz Orchestra', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez, Jerry (1949-2018)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-16T22:37:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 