alism and law enforcement, is about to join the well-ballasted CBS “Early Show.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/john-miller-to-join-cbs-bolstering-the-early-show/', 'snippet': 'John Miller, whose trajectory has veered between journalism and law enforcement, is about to join the well-ballasted CBS “Early Show.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every week or so comes another signal that CBS is reshaping “The Early Show,” its low-rated morning newscast. On Monday will come another: the announcement that John Miller is joining the network as a senior correspondent with a special emphasis on the morning show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'John Miller to Join CBS, Bolstering ‘The Early Show’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T01:29:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df8b309b-e580-5a85-b05a-caf8a9e4ca33', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df8b309b-e580-5a85-b05a-caf8a9e4ca33'}, {'abstract': 'How a mild-mannered Parisian professor revolutionized European attitudes about the Union.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/vive-lunion/', 'snippet': 'How a mild-mannered Parisian professor revolutionized European attitudes about the Union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soon after he arrived in Paris, in early October 1861, John Bigelow, the newly appointed American consul general to France, paid a visit to a quiet house on Rue Taitbout, about a mile north of the Louvre. The home belonged to the grandly named Édouard-René Lefèbvre de Laboulaye, a small, soft-spoken professor of history at the Collège de France, one of the country’s elite institutions of higher learning. Laboulaye was an expert on American history, and Bigelow was there to ask him for a small favor: to change the way the French thought about America’s civil war.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vive L’Union', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T01:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Don H. Doyle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Don', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Doyle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58a20a7e-b2bf-5c0b-bf95-d32d9c47a4d1', 'word_count': 1855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58a20a7e-b2bf-5c0b-bf95-d32d9c47a4d1'}, {'abstract': 'By defending the government and the middle class, the leading Democratic candidate for a Senate seat in Massachusetts, is energizing voters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/opinion/elizabeth-warrens-appeal.html', 'snippet': 'By defending the government and the middle class, the leading Democratic candidate for a Senate seat in Massachusetts, is energizing voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a few years