ew bills into law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Jerry Brown of California took a stand for immigrants’ rights and humane, sensible government when he signed several new bills into law. It is a welcome change from the intolerance and counterproductive policies being adopted in so many other states around the country. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sensible Path in California', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Sensible Path in California', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T01:42:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/370454df-3dd3-594a-9f6b-1edd2f043ef6', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/370454df-3dd3-594a-9f6b-1edd2f043ef6'}, {'abstract': 'As regulators begin a push to produce a final draft of the Volcker Rule, they face hurdles from an unexpected group: themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/16/volcker-rule-divides-regulators/', 'snippet': 'As regulators begin a push to produce a final draft of the Volcker Rule, they face hurdles from an unexpected group: themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regulators have faced a barrage of complaints from lawmakers and financial industry lobbyists in their 14-month-long quest to constrain risky trading on Wall Street, an effort known as