taple — the cellphone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/technology/fcc-and-wireless-carriers-agree-to-alerts-to-fight-bill-shock.html', 'snippet': 'Wireless carriers have been losing good will with users bitter about the sometimes exorbitant charges resulting from overuse of what has become a consumer staple — the cellphone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Users of cellphones and other wireless devices who are nearing their monthly limit for voice, text or data services will receive alerts when they are in danger of being charged extra, under an agreement reached by carriers and the Federal Communications Commission.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wireless Users Will Get Alerts on Excess Use', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wireless Users Will Get Alerts On Excess Use', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T04:01:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization