star-studded-memorial-to-steve-jobs/', 'snippet': 'Luminaries of business, politics and entertainment attended a memorial service for Steve Jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An array of figures from technology, entertainment and politics assembled on the campus of Stanford University on Sunday night to pay tribute to Steven P. Jobs, Apple‘s late chief executive and co-founder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Star-Studded Memorial to Steve Jobs', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T06:29:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed8b713d-0f18-58a1-99e7-91e3c7a46413', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed8b713d-0f18-58a1-99e7-91e3c7a46413'}, {'abstract': 'Anadarko held a 25 percent share in the Gulf of Mexico well that blew out last year, causing the largest oil spill in U.S. history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/business/bp-recovers-4-billion-from-anadarko-for-gulf-spill.html', 'snippet': 'Anadarko held a 25 percent share in the Gulf of Mexico well that blew out last year, causing the largest oil spill in U.S. history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The British oil company BP said Monday that a partner in the well that exploded last year in the Gulf of Mexico, Anadarko Petroleum, had agreed to pay $4 billion to settle claims related to the ensuing oil spill. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/business/18oil-span/18oil-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/business/18oil-span/18oil-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/business/18oil-span/18oil-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ending Dispute, Well Partner Settles With BP for $4 Billion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ending Dispute, Well Partner Settles With BP for $4 Billion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico Oil Spill (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANADARKO PETROLEUM CORP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T07:39:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/874d9783-6c5d-5d71-84f4-77021f0ccfbb', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/874d9783-6c5d-5d71-84f4-77021f0ccfbb'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/news-quiz-oct-17-2011/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | Oct. 17, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T07:43:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Frasier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frasier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/090ec9e7-9d9f-575f-9dcc-4b9fa4a9a130', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/090ec9e7-9d9f-575f-9dcc-4b9fa4a9a130'}, {'abstract': '6 Q’s About the News | Where did protests related to the Occupy Wall Street movement take place?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/from-wall-street-to-the-world/', 'snippet': '6 Q’s About the News | Where did protests related to the Occupy Wall Street movement take place?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHERE is the Occupy Wall Street encampment?WHERE did related protests occur over the weekend?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Wall Street to the World', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T08:07:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0093c14-df9b-51f7-a871-2d9e31176878', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0093c14-df9b-51f7-a871-2d9e31176878'}, {'abstract': 'On Oct. 17, 1931, the Chicago mobster Al Capone was convicted on five of 23 income tax evasion counts he faced, and which later yielded an 11-year prison sentence.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/oct-17-1931-al-capone-guilty-of-tax-evasion/', 'snippet': 'On Oct. 17, 1931, the Chicago mobster Al Capone was convicted on five of 23 income tax evasion counts he faced, and which later yielded an 11-year prison sentence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Oct. 17, 1931, the Chicago mobster Al Capone was convicted on five of 23 income tax evasion counts he faced, and which later yielded an 11-year prison sentence. During the trial, Mr. Capone’s efforts to avoid a strict sentence were thwarted by Judge James H. Wilkerson, who refused to offer a lenient sentence in exchange for a guilty plea. Wilkerson also swapped out the jury after Mr. Capone tried to bribe the people who were serving on it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oct. 17, 1931 | Al Capone Guilty of Tax Evasion', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T08:09:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3265e247-5d5e-58a6-84f2-fbaf2d45bde1', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3265e247-5d5e-58a6-84f2-fbaf2d45bde1'}, {'abstract': 'Can you find the percentage change in debit card transaction fees?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/test-yourself-math-oct-17-2011/', 'snippet': 'Can you find the percentage change in debit card transaction fees?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your math skills with this question created by Pete Diamantis at Math for America from the Op-Ed piece “Charging for Debit Cards Is Robbery.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Math, Oct. 17, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42f18c60-82b6-5cad-be9b-71b3d895ad71', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42f18c60-82b6-5cad-be9b-71b3d895ad71'}, {'abstract': 'The flash of recognition elicits a bittersweet half grin among the British. Peter Dench went back home over the course of a decade to show how and why.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/a-decade-of-winks-and-winces/', 'snippet': 'The flash of recognition elicits a bittersweet half grin among the British. Peter Dench went back home over the course of a decade to show how and why.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Look carefully at the English and you may catch a glimpse of a unique expression. It’s a bittersweet half grin, a quintessential moment when we recognize and admirably accept our most hideous traits. This smile crossed my face when I first saw Peter Dench’s photographs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Decade of Winks and Winces', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T09:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Hamblett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamblett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported'