: 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MTV’s Next Reality Star: University for the Deaf', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T10:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca R. Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b80d453-eb6c-556f-891a-86a6884fc00c', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b80d453-eb6c-556f-891a-86a6884fc00c'}, {'abstract': 'Student Opinion | How can disappointment and failure motivate someone to achieve success?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/what-motivates-you/', 'snippet': 'Student Opinion | How can disappointment and failure motivate someone to achieve success?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peggy Payne, at age 62, is “still stewing” over not being chosen to spend the summer studying at the Governor’s School of North Carolina–in 1965. However, Ms. Payne credits this early rejection with helping her successful writing career. Have you ever had a disappointment or setback that fueled later success? How common do you think it is to respond to failure not with discouragement but a renewed “I’ll show ’em” spirit?  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Motivates You?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T10:07:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bdcb1de-9029-52f6-81a6-d69fe16ed71b', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bdcb1de-9029-52f6-81a6-d69fe16ed71b'}, {'abstract': 'The fighting that broke out late Sunday night between a rebel commander’s troops and government forces escalated into explosions and mortar fire on Monday morning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/world/middleeast/18yemen.html', 'snippet': 'The fighting that broke out late Sunday night between a rebel commander’s troops and government forces escalated into explosions and mortar fire on Monday morning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANA, Yemen — Explosions rocked the Yemeni capital on Monday morning in a sharp escalation of violence between the government and opposition forces.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/world/18yemen1_cnd/18yemen1_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/18/world/18yemen1_cnd/18yemen1_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/world/18yemen1_cnd/18yemen1_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/world/18yemen1_cnd/18yemen1_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/world/18yemen1_cnd/18yemen1_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Violence in Yemen’s Capital Escalates as Clashes