geon’s management.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/business/global/air-france-klm-board-to-meet-amid-reports-of-ouster-of-chief.html', 'snippet': 'Soaring costs and scrutiny of the airline’s safety standards made investors uneasy with Pierre-Henri Gourgeon’s management.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Barely four months after appointing him to a new four-year term, the board of Air France-KLM voted Monday to dismiss its group chief executive, Pierre-Henri Gourgeon, who had grown deeply unpopular with investors as he struggled to cope with high operating costs and increasing scrutiny of the carrier’s safety culture since a crash killed more than 200 people two years ago.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/world/18airfrance-image/18airfrance-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 792, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/world/18airfrance-image/18airfrance-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/world/18airfrance-image/18airfrance-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Air France Fires Its Chief Executive', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Air France Unexpectedly Dismisses Its C.E.O.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR FRANCE-KLM', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T11:47:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c376ee1-5eda-5ad0-ac9d-e543b4b02411', 'word_count': 1059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c376ee1-5eda-5ad0-ac9d-e543b4b02411'}, {'abstract': 'Wells Fargo, the nation’s largest consumer lender, said its third-quarter earnings rose 21 percent, even as a drop in revenue indicated a disappointing sign for the bank.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/wells-fargo-earnings-rise-21-to-4-1-billion/', 'snippet': 'Wells Fargo, the nation’s largest consumer lender, said its third-quarter earnings rose 21 percent, even as a drop in revenue indicated a disappointing sign for the bank.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:18 p.m. | Updated with closing stock price.Wells Fargo, the nation’s largest consumer lender, reported Monday that its third-quarter earnings rose 21 percent, even as a drop in revenue indicated a disappointing sign for the San Francisco-based bank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wells Fargo Earnings Rise 21%, to $4.1 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo & Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T12:09:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ad11cd7-5fd2-5ea2-bffd-1b5b3832e0be', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ad11cd7-5fd2-5ea2-bffd-1b5b3832e0be'}, {'abstract': 'The mother of a terminally ill child writes that her story is not that different from the rest of ours: we are all preparing for when our children leave us, or we leave them.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/raising-children-means-letting-go/', 'snippet': 'The mother of a terminally ill child writes that her story is not that different from the rest of ours: we are all preparing for when our children leave us, or we leave them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My father has always said that raising children is a process of letting go. From the moment your children are born, your job is to prepare them to function in the world without you, and perhaps your biggest challenge is preparing yourself for that separation. I couldn’t help hearing my father’s voice this weekend, while reading Emily Rapp’s moving piece in The Times’s Sunday Review about having a son with Tay-Sachs, a rare and untreatable genetic disorder from which he will probably die before he turns 3. As Ms. Rapp writes, her story is closer to most of ours than we would like to imagine: on some level, we are all getting ready for the day when our children leave us or we leave them. Read her story, “Notes From a Dragon Mom,” and then come back here to share your thoughts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raising Children Means Letting Them Go', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T12:10:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Megan Liberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e259a263-8472-5300-a55d-02d263d9238d', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e259a263-8472-5300-a55d-02d263d9238d'}, {'abstract': 'Are they why it has gone so wrong?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/european-spillovers/', 'snippet': 'Are they why it has gone so wrong?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wolfgang Munchau suggests a reason for European misjudgements — he argues that European leaders have failed to take account of the fact that Europe, collectively, is a fairly closed economy, selling primarily to itself:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'European Spillovers', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T12:14:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c938f1a8-cf51-5003-9b1d-69270efe5bce', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c938f1a8-cf51-5003-9b1d-69270efe5bce'}, {'abstract': 'Software patents may be a mess. But Britain’s James Dyson makes the case that strong patent protection is a vital tool of economic policy.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/another-view-of-patents-from-james-dyson/', 'snippet': 'Software patents may be a mess. But Britain’s James Dyson makes the case that strong patent protection is a vital tool of economic policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The recent news about patents has all been about big technology companies loading up on them and litigating, especially in the smartphone market.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Vi