resident Obama, The New York Times reports. Goldman Sachs employees, for example, have given $350,000 to Mr. Romney and $45,000 to Mr. Obama. They donated more than $1 million to Mr. Obama in 2008. Read more »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Ahead in Race for Wall Street Cash', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T12:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/baf82e1b-9b72-576c-8400-4b8b23ca6779', 'word_count': 51, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baf82e1b-9b72-576c-8400-4b8b23ca6779'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: A band of satirists calling themselves Billionaires for the One Percent make their point in Zuccotti Park. Also, what City Room is reading in other newspapers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/noblesse-oblige-among-the-protesting-masses/', 'snippet': 'The Day: A band of satirists calling themselves Billionaires for the One Percent make their point in Zuccotti Park. Also, what City Room is reading in other newspapers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In their finest evening clothes, Meg A. Bucks, DeForest Cali and a few of their friends deigned to mingle the other day among the Occupy Wall Street protesters camped in Zuccotti Park. It wasn’t so much that they approved of the goings-on in the park as they were thrilled to be at that location, directly across from a Brooks Brothers store on Church Street. “We always like to gather by Brooks Brothers,” Ms. Bucks said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Noblesse Oblige Among the Protesting Masses', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zuccotti Park (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T12:31:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/596f85f4-ecdc-50c9-98ed-af188a488383', 'word_count': 1003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/596f85f4-ecdc-50c9-98ed-af188a488383'}, {'abstract': 'What a prize does and doesn’t do.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/nobel-lies/', 'snippet': 'What a prize does and doesn’t do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The right was quick to claim this year’s economics Nobel as an anti-Keynesian prize. Chris Sims sets the record straight:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nobel Lies', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T12:38:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f042247-a20d-5b3b-bfef-955605a1cdc9', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f042247-a20d-5b3b-bfef-955605a1cdc9'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/morning-take-out-347/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOP STORIES ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T12:43:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f95cf97-e23b-5a59-ae33-f38e00f3920a', 'word_count': 1625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f95cf97-e23b-5a59-ae33-f38e00f3920a'}, {'abstract': 'A Louisiana microchain finds its way to the Big Apple.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/naked-pizza-is-new-to-town/', 'snippet': 'A Louisiana microchain finds its way to the Big Apple.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard not to feel naughty when ordering a 10-inch pizza for lunch. Sure, it’s got three food groups on there (and up to four or five, if you include certain toppings), but that crust is awfully thick, there’s got to be added sugar in that red sauce, and ugh — can someone pass the napkins? This Day-Glo orange grease is dripping everywhere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Naked Pizza Is New to Town', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T13:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Nichols', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nichols', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d12a31b6-11a1-5500-86f6-23a27c7f70e8', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d12a31b6-11a1-5500-86f6-23a27c7f70e8'}, {'abstract': 'The start-up could be to networking what VMWare was to computer servers, a company that comes out of nowhere and with clever software sharply drops the price a hardware maker can get for a server.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/what-is-nicira-up-to/', 'snippet': 'The start-up could be to networking what VMWare was to computer servers, a company that comes out of nowhere and with clever software sharply drops the price a hardware maker can get for a server.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With $40 million in funding, an all-star bench of investors and engineers, and technology that has already drawn spies, Nicira is an unusually visible company in the supposedly secretive “stealth” stage of its early life. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is Nicira Up To?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T13:39:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b8e9db1-8854-5180-ab16-3c80c85c1ca5', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b8e9db1-8854-5180-ab16-3c80c85c1ca5'}, {'abstract': 'Some Mumbai neighborhoods have been without power for more than 24 hours.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/dark-hours-in-mumbai/', 'snippet': 'Some Mumbai neighborhoods have been without power for more than 24 hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While blackouts are common in most parts of India, South Mumbai residents have, for the most part, been protected from such inconveniences. However, since 4 am on Saturday morning, the lights have been out in the city’s financial district, Nariman Point, and parts of South Mumbai.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dark Hours in Mumbai', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blackouts and Brownouts (Electrical)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T13:39:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4c175ef-212f-518f-8c3b-5119d19f739f', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4c175ef-212f-518f-8c3b-5119d19f739f'}, {'abstract': 'What to do after a mortgage rejection, Caribbean resorts batt