ative inquiry this week. Mr. Finkel is a true lover of both math and the outdoors and is uniquely qualified to attack this puzzle from any theoretical or practical angle. It’s the classic (with a twist) What Color Was The Bear?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: What Color Was the Bear?', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polar Bears', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T15:11:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63c43409-85a3-531c-afc5-8613f68021e5', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63c43409-85a3-531c-afc5-8613f68021e5'}, {'abstract': 'The new test may reduce the need for riskier invasive procedures like amniocentesis, but it raises ethical issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/business/sequenom-test-for-down-syndrome-raises-hopes-and-questions.html', 'snippet': 'The new test may reduce the need for riskier invasive procedures like amniocentesis, but it raises ethical issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New tests are coming to market that can detect Down syndrome in a fetus using a sample of the mother’s blood, potentially reducing the need for riskier invasive tests while also stirring ethical concerns. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/bu