type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75c99b07-4ebc-5cb0-84d5-ed9a792579ea', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75c99b07-4ebc-5cb0-84d5-ed9a792579ea'}, {'abstract': 'Egypt’s parliamentary election may be nearly two months away, but the contest has already begun in the neighborhood of Imbaba, where the arc of the Egyptian revolution is on display.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/world/middleeast/in-cairo-quarter-islamists-try-to-profit-from-revolution.html', 'snippet': 'Egypt’s parliamentary election may be nearly two months away, but the contest has already begun in the neighborhood of Imbaba, where the arc of the Egyptian revolution is on display.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — In one of Cairo’s most crowded quarters, where streets are so filled with trash that bulldozers scoop it up, the Muslim Brotherhood has opened not one but two offices. Its most conservative counterpart has followed suit. An Islamist do-gooder with forearms as broad as the Nile has vowed to win a seat in Parliament.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/world/IMBABA-1/IMBABA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/18/world/IMBABA-1/IMBABA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/world/IMBABA-1/IMBABA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/world/IMBABA-1/IMBABA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/world/IMBABA-1/IMBABA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Crowded Cairo Quarter, Islamists Try to Seize Mantle of a Revolution', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Crowded Cairo Quarter, Islamists Try to Seize Mantle of a Revolution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Said, Khaled', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic Group', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T15:28:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Shadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f737c194-bd07-5a76-872d-7abfc92bf62d', 'word_count': 1480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f737c194-bd07-5a76-872d-7abfc92bf62d'}, {'abstract': 'Is the message that we should marry for passionate, soul-fulfilling love — and never settle for less — now outdated?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/is-the-good-enough-marriage-good-for-the-children/', 'snippet': 'Is the message that we should marry for passionate, soul-fulfilling love — and never settle for less — now outdated?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Atlantic’s current obsession with the alleged “decline of men” continues in the magazine’s November issue with a cover story by Kate Bolick that begins with a sad summing-up of her own relationship status (“I am 39, with too many ex-boyfriends to count and, I am told, two grim-seeming options to face down: either stay single or settle for a ‘good enough’ mate. At this point, certainly, falling in love and getting married may be less a matter of choice than a stroke of wild great luck.”) and then meanders on into a long discussion of the future of marriage in man-challenged America.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is the ‘Good Enough’ Marriage Good for the Children?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T15:29:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Warner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Warner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f538144a-2132-5485-936c-e2fb33ffa897', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f538144a-2132-5485-936c-e2fb33ffa897'}, {'abstract': 'Critiquing Pinker’s Whiggish interpretation of history.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/steven-pinkers-history-of-violence/', 'snippet': 'Critiquing Pinker’s Whiggish interpretation of history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My column yesterday took a modest jab at Steven Pinker’s “The Better Angels of Our Nature: Why Violence Has Declined,” and I thought that I would follow up with a few more comments on his thesis. I should stipulate that I am broadly convinced by the argument that our current era of relative peace reflects a longer term trend away from violence, and broadly impressed by the evidence that Pinker marshals to support this view. (I found the book’s story more persuasive than did, say, John Gray, to pick out the most hostile review I’ve seen to date.) But here are some criticisms and caveats.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steven Pinker’s History of Violence', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T15:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d63a3baf-8996-5be7-847a-f200e2c602ad', 'word_count': 1266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d63a3baf-8996-5be7-847a-f200e2c602ad'}, {'abstract': 'Iran’s foreign minister implicitly acknowledged the possibility that the suspected plot to kill the Saudi ambassador might not be pure American fantasy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/world/middleeast/iran-says-it-wants-to-see-evidence-in-saudi-plot.html', 'snippet': 'Iran’s foreign minister implicitly acknowledged the possibility that the suspected plot to kill the Saudi ambassador might not be pure American fantasy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iran’s top leaders said Monday that the American accusation of an Iranian-hatched plot to assassinate Saudi Arabia’s ambassador to Washington was partly designed to sow discord between Iran and Saudi Arabia, in what appeared to be a new Iranian counterattack to the charges announced nearly a week ago. But the foreign minister of Iran said his government was at least willing to examine the evidence that the United States claims it has in the case. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Accuses U.S. of Trying to Sow Regional Discord', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran Accuses U.S. of Trying To Sow Regional Discord', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jubeir, Adel al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T15:36:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/222c1c45-c95a-5e0c-a70f-9db69cfa01e2', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/222c1c45-c95a-5e0c-a70f-9db69cfa01e2'}, {'abstract': 'Wildfires in Australia are stymieing a University of Michigan team’s effort to become the first Americans to win the World Solar Challenge since its inaugural running in 1987.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/delayed-down-under-a-michigan-team-recharges-in-the-world-solar-challenge/', 'snippet': 'Wildfires in Australia are stymieing a University of Michigan team’s effort to become the first Americans to win the World Solar Challenge since its inaugural running in 1987.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A wildfire has introduced an unexpected variable in the World Solar Challenge, stymieing the progress of the primary American entry in the race. The University of Michigan’s car, named Quantum, sat in third place behind Japanese and Dutch entries, respectively, when the fire put a halt to the 1,800-mile caravan across the Australian outback on Monday morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Delayed Down Under, a Michigan Team Recharges in the World Solar Challenge', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Motor Speedway', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tokai University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Berkeley', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T15:43:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald Ahrens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahrens', 'qualifier':