covers the joys and disappointments of supporting a specific club — Juventus.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/no-longer-merely-a-fair-weather-fan/', 'snippet': 'Whether by osmosis or because of romantic involvement, our intrepid reporter discovers the joys and disappointments of supporting a specific club — Juventus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHAPEL HILL, N.C. — I woke up to my alarm, put on my Juventus jersey, and headed downstairs to the living room Sunday morning. It wasn’t a major championship, no one I knew personally was playing, but as I turned on Fox Soccer, I felt nervous in anticipation of the outcome.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Longer Merely a Fair-Weather Fan', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Averbuch, Yael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Del Piero, Alessandro', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barcelona (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Juventus Football Club', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T16:42:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yael Averbuch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Averbuch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2481f0c4-4ce4-52a1-bed5-cacca42a8829', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2481f0c4-4ce4-52a1-bed5-cacca42a8829'}, {'abstract': 'He will also visit P.S. 333, the Manhattan School for Children.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/saturdays-greenmarket-special-rene-redzepi-cooking/', 'snippet': 'He will also visit P.S. 333, the Manhattan School for Children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At his restaurant Noma, in Copenhagen, René Redzepi has become the chef of the moment by cooking with foraged ingredients like sea buckthorn, axel berry shoots and ramson flower buds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saturday’s Greenmarket Special: René Redzepi', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T16:45:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7712a010-2d57-55ae-a28d-d618198d26f2', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7712a010-2d57-55ae-a28d-d618198d26f2'}, {'abstract': 'Lens: Justin Timberlake', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/17/blogs/20111017-lens-justinT.html', 'snippet': 'Lens: Justin Timberlake', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lens: Justin Timberlake', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/blogs/20111017-lens-justinT-slide-HVDT/20111017-lens-justinT-slide-HVDT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 754, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lens: Justin Timberlake', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T16:56:58+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/82c0b776-99c6-5535-92ea-d8503621edad', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/82c0b776-99c6-5535-92ea-d8503621edad'}, {'abstract': 'Off the Rails: A man claiming to be a subway conductor has earned minor celebrity status for hosting an anonymous question-and-answer session with riders.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/he-says-hes-a-conductor-conducting-a-q-and-a/', 'snippet': 'Off the Rails: A man claiming to be a subway conductor has earned minor celebrity status for hosting an anonymous question-and-answer session with riders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Transportation professionals are not the type you might expect to be perusing the dense, exclamation point-laced message boards on Reddit, a popular Web site where users carry on extensive conversations on a nearly infinite range of arcane topics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'He Says He’s a Conductor, Conducting a Q. and A.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T16:59:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0582f3af-26ce-5936-8d8a-af1ab447169a', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0582f3af-26ce-5936-8d8a-af1ab447169a'}, {'abstract': 'Readers of my latest column have taken issue with my slightly snarky references to Occupy Wall Street. Okay, maybe not “slightly.”', 'web_url': 'https://keller.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/a-few-words-about-the-occupiers/', 'snippet': 'Readers of my latest column have taken issue with my slightly snarky references to Occupy Wall Street. Okay, maybe not “slightly.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aside from our enthusiastic Slovak readership, most of the reader comments and e-mails in response to Monday’s column have taken issue with my slightly snarky reference to Occupy Wall Street. Okay, maybe not “slightly.” Here’s a sample:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Few Words About the Occupiers', 'kicker': 'Bill Keller', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T17:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/988fd530-4b9a-5668-bdb8-b6753f191ec8', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/988fd530-4b9a-5668-bdb8-b6753f191ec8'}, {'abstract': 'Even if the Durbin rules withstand the latest assault, it’s unclear how much most merchants will benefit from them.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/in-battle-with-merchants-banks-still-hope-to-overturn-durbin-amendment/', 'snippet': 'Even if the Durbin rules withstand the latest assault, it’s unclear how much most merchants will benefit from them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Durbin Amendment — the legislation that limits the fees banks can earn for debit card transactions to a scale that is “reasonable and proportional” — was signed into law more than a year ago. It survived the financial sector’s strong objections to the Federal Reserve’s aggressive first swing at regulating those fees, as well as subsequent efforts in Congress to delay adoption of the new rules. Those new rules, which were eventually watered down in a compromise that left advocates fuming, took effect Oct. 1.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Battling Merchants, Banks Still Hope to Overturn Durbin Rules', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T17:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78232e57-4307-5028-bf00-2e79d03b6656', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78232e57-4307-5028-bf00-2e79d03b6656'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama kicked off a three-day tour of North Carolina and Virginia, both states he carried in 2008. This time, he faces a greater challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/us/politics/obama-hits-road-again-to-push-pieces-of-jobs-bill.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama kicked off a three-day tour of North Carolina and Virginia, both states he carried in 2008. This time, he faces a greater challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOONE, N.C. — Loading up on Halloween candy at a store in this friendly college town on Monday, President Obama could probably imagine winning North Carolina in 2012, as he did in 2008, when he became the first Democrat since Jimmy Carter to do so.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/18/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking Toward 2012, Obama Finds North Carolina Less Receptive', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking Toward 2012, Obama Finds North Carolina Less Receptive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T17:03:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82c073b0-c55e-5f44-babc-af7e1add2581', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82c073b0-c55e-5f44-babc-af7e1add2581'}, {'abstract': 'Plenty of studies have tried to determine whether taking up yoga can help lessen pain.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/really-the-claim-yoga-can-help-manage-pain/', 'snippet': 'Plenty of studies have tried to determine whether taking up yoga can help lessen pain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE FACTS', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Really? The Claim: Yoga Can Help Manage Pain', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Complementary Medicine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T17:18:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91bdc909-0f30-536a-9392-e1c5b33f69dd', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91bdc909-0f30-536a-9392-e1c5b33f69dd'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time in a dozen years, our very own Wm. (Bill) Ferguson will perform with Lotion. They’re good, but don’t take our word for it. Take Thomas Pynchon’s.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/lotion-tonight/', 'snippet': 'For the first time in a dozen years, our very own Wm. (Bill) Ferguson will perform with Lotion. They’re good, but don’t take our word for it. Take Thomas Pynchon’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time in a dozen years, our very own Wm. (Bill) Ferguson will perform with the great New York ’90s indie-rock band Lotion, in which he played bass, with his brother Jim on guitar, Rob Youngberg on drums and Tony Zajkowski on vocals. The band’s first album, ‘‘Full Isaac,’’ was voted album of the year by the Village Voice in 1994; they were one of the first recipients of Sassy magazine’s ‘‘cute band alert’’; they toured with Pavement and Throwing Muses and Mercury Rev, and Thomas Pynchon wrote the liner notes, quoted below, for their 1996 album ‘‘Nobody’s Cool’’:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lotion, Tonight', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T17:20:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0073f108-c284-5985-81fa-db662a02abac', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0073f108-c284-5985-81fa-db662a02abac'}, {'abstract': 'The Class Act is dead, Medicare doesn’t pay for what many elderly people really need and the cost of paying out of pocket is astonishing.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/long-term-care-insurance-and-our-collective-denial/', 'snippet': 'The Class Act is dead, Medicare doesn’t pay for what many elderly people really need and the cost of paying out of pocket is astonishing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This weekend brought more depressing news on the long-term care insurance front — and continued evidence that we have our heads in the sand about these issues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Long-Term Care Insurance and Our Collective Denial', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Long-Term Care Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T17:25:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6491f513-13f9-58ea-97c7-b2c321bd68fa', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6491f513-13f9-58ea-97c7-b2c321bd68fa'}, {'abstract': 'The limited selection of appealing software, however, may still leave BlackBerry customers grumbling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/technology/rim-offers-free-apps-as-apology-for-outages.html', 'snippet': 'The limited selection of appealing software, however, may still leave BlackBerry customers grumbling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BlackBerry users will soon be able to find out at no cost if there are $100 worth of apps that interest them.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'RIM Offers Free Apps in Apology', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'RIM Offers Free Apps In Apology', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BlackBerry (Handheld Device)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apologies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Research In Motion Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 