ng heart, dizziness, extreme fatigue and headaches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patrick Fox, now 14, considers himself lucky. It took only a year to find out why he was always tired, his heart raced and he ached all over, why he became overheated easily and had terrible headaches almost every day. Once a happy, active child and good student who enjoyed school, by age 12 he could hardly get out of bed. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/science/18BROD/18BROD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 658, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/science/18BROD/18BROD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/science/18BROD/18BROD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ailment Can Steal Youth From the Young', 'kicker': 'Personal Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ailment Can Steal Youth From the Young', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heart', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nerves and Nervous System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T17:53:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane E. Brody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Brody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7fbbbcb-0465-5eb4-b6ba-85042ef62526', 'word_count': 1094, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7fbbbcb-0465-5eb4-b6ba-85042ef62526'}, {'abstract': 'Oct. 17, 2011 — President Obama begins another campaign-style swing to sell his jobs bill. Also, John Harwood interviews White House Chief of Staff William M. Daley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000001116928/the-caucus--another-obama-bus-tour.html', 'snippet': 'Oct. 17, 2011 — President Obama begins another campaign-style swing to sell his jobs bill. Also, John Harwood interviews White House Chief of Staff William M. Daley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oct. 17, 2011 — President Obama begins another campaign-style swing to sell his jobs bill. Also, John Harwood interviews White House Chief of Staff William M. Daley.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/us/politics/video-caucus-101711/video-caucus-101711-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/17/us/politics/video-caucus-101711/video-caucus-101711-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/17/us/politics/video-caucus-101711/video-caucus-101711-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/17/us/politics/video-caucus-101711/video-caucus-101711-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Caucus | Another Obama Bus Tour', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daley, William M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T17:54:42+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'Ben Werschkul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werschkul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/b4dd5e2f-6725-5fc1-84d7-9fc746ff05b0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/b4dd5e2f-6725-5fc1-84d7-9fc746ff05b0'}, {'abstract': 'Invited to create a site-specific project for this year’s Frieze Art Fair, Laric chose the fair itself as his subject.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/frieze-frame-oliver-larics-not-so-original-footage/', 'snippet': 'Invited to create a site-specific project for this year’s Frieze Art Fair, Laric chose the fair itself as his subject.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oliver Laric is an artist who rarely has anything new to say. His work frames the creative potential of repetition, championing the idea of “the copy” as denser in meaning and, in this day and age, somehow more genuine, than any notion of a true “original.” A copy has simply lived more: it contains within it not just the image or idea at hand, but also the imprint of time, place or identity linked with that moment as well as the motive of duplication. “Versions,” Laric’s video treatise on this subject, features an animated slide show of contemporary copies (the infamously Photoshopped 2008 image of missile tests in Iran, in which the missiles were cloned for heightened visual impact; Internet memes like the Zidane head butt, remixed and disseminated by users around the world); and historical antecedents (recycled character animations from early Disney movies; figurative archetypes taken from classical sculpture) that trace its relevance back to far before copy and paste was a way of life. Laric updates the piece regularly, and now a handful of versions of “Versions” are circulating online with many of his other works, causing discrepancies and redundancies that surface as a digitally savvy form of authenticity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Frieze Frame | Oliver Laric’s Not So Original Footage', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frieze Art Fair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T18:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3052466f-0d02-5882-a749-f615d2bfed99', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3052466f-0d02-5882-a749-f615d2bfed99'}, {'abstract': 'Two advertising executives are marketing a line of snacks honoring the military, and a portion of the proceeds will go to help American veterans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/business/media/five-point-snacks-takes-a-stand.html', 'snippet': 'Two advertising executives are marketing a line of snacks honoring the military, and a portion of the proceeds will go to help American veterans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two longtime advertising agency executives are finding out what life is like on the other side of Madison Avenue as they bring out a line of snacks with cause marketing at its core.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 