 'Rush Limbaugh responded to Friday’s deployment of American military advisers to combat the African rebels who call themselves the Lord’s Resistance Army by defending the group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 6:02 p.m. Apparently sensing an opportunity to tarnish President Obama’s standing with listeners who were unaware of the suffering caused by the African rebels who call themselves the Lord’s Resistance Army, Rush Limbaugh responded to the president’s deployment of 100 military advisers to combat the group in central Africa on Friday in a segment of his radio show headlined, “Obama Invades Uganda, Targets Christians.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Limbaugh Defends Lord’s Resistance Army', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Lord's Resistance Army", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T18:02:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bca10663-120e-5082-8d7f-c898f5a861a3', 'word_count': 1174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bca10663-120e-5082-8d7f-c898f5a861a3'}, {'abstract': 'A man who became wealthy working on Wall Street contributed money that helped mobilize the Occupy Wall Street movement.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/he-made-it-on-wall-st-and-used-it-to-help-start-the-protests/', 'snippet': 'A man who became wealthy working on Wall Street contributed money that helped mobilize the Occupy Wall Street movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert S. Halper, a retired Wall Street trader, spends time each day in Zuccotti Park talking to protesters about politics and their thoughts on reforming the banking system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'He Made It on Wall St. and Used It to Help Start the Protests', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Adbusters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zuccotti Park (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T18:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/810b3051-dae8-539e-9b69-5b59c14eae75', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/810b3051-dae8-539e-9b69-5b59c14eae75'}, {'abstract': 'A great combination of pesto and warm potatoes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/health/nutrition/17recipehealth.html', 'snippet': 'A great combination of pesto and warm potatoes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve always loved the combination of pesto and warm potatoes. I usually just toss steamed potatoes with the sauce, but this time I sliced up some Yukon golds, tossed them with the pesto and made a gratin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/