anda-official-says.html', 'snippet': 'Most of the military advisers being sent to Uganda to help hunt down the Lord’s Resistance Army, a guerrilla group in central Africa, will stay in Uganda, which the group has not attacked in years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KAMPALA, Uganda — Most of the 100 military advisers being sent to Uganda to help hunt down the Lord’s Resistance Army, a brutal guerrilla group in central Africa, will stay in Uganda, which the group has not attacked in years, an American government official said Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Combat Role for U.S. Advisers in Uganda, Official Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Advisers Will Stay Within Uganda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Lord's Resistance Army", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T18:16:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4456fc55-6bba-5212-8aa2-0341282c78a2', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4456fc55-6bba-5212-8aa2-0341282c78a2'}, {'abstract': 'Speaking Monday, the mayor described his sympathy for the residents near the protesters in Zuccotti Park. “The Constitution doesn’t protect tents,” he said. “It protects speech and assembly.”', 'web_url': 'h