now understand some of the noises piranhas make.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/science/18piranha.html', 'snippet': 'Using a hydrophone to record underwater sounds, scientists say they now understand some of the noises piranhas make.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everyone knows that piranhas have razor-sharp teeth, but they have another distinguishing characteristic: They make noise. Until now, however, scientists have never understood why.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/science/18OBPIRANHA4/18OBOX4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/science/18OBPIRANHA4/18OBOX4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/science/18OBPIRANHA4/18OBOX4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hearing the Repertoire of a Very Fearsome Fish', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hearing the Repertoire Of a Very Fearsome Fish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of Experimental Biology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T18:51:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1449af8-44f3-5160-8a7d-3845f3068ac9', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1449af8-44f3-5160-8a7d-3845f3068ac9'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Woodford, the chief executive who was dismissed on Friday, said he gave evidence of fraud to Britain’s Serious Fraud Office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/business/global/ousted-olympus-chief-accuses-the-company-of-fraud.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Woodford, the chief executive who was dismissed on Friday, said he gave evidence of fraud to Britain’s Serious Fraud Office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — The British executive who was publicly pilloried as a bad manager when the Japanese company Olympus fired him on Friday, struck back on Monday, saying he was forced out because he was about to expose potential financial fraud at the company.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Chief Executive of Olympus Ties Ouster to His Claim of Fraud by the Company', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Chief Executive of Olympus Ties Ouster to His Claim of Fraud by the Company', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodford, Michael C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Olympus Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T18:55:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/867a0e2a-35b3-5d6e-9fc8-0aa084db61dc', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/867a0e2a-35b3-5d6e-9fc8-0aa084db61dc'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Origins of AIDS,” Dr. Jacques Pépin starts from 1900 to work out the most likely path the virus took during the years it left almost no tracks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/health/18aids.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Origins of AIDS,” Dr. Jacques Pépin starts from 1900 to work out the most likely path the virus took during the years it left almost no tracks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our story begins sometime close to 1921, somewhere between the Sanaga River in Cameroon and the Congo River in the former Belgian Congo. It involves chimps and monkeys, hunters and butchers, “free women” and prostitutes, syringes and plasma-sellers, evil colonial lawmakers and decent colonial doctors with the best of intentions. And a virus that, against all odds, appears to have made it from one ape in the central African jungle to one Haitian bureaucrat leaving Zaire for home and then to a few dozen men in California gay bars before it was even noticed — about 60 years after its journey began.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/science/18JPAIDS1/18JPAIDS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chimp to Man to History Books: The Path of AIDS', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chimp to Human To History Books: The Path of AIDS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pepin, Jacques', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T18:59:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/913fec0d-9ff2-5934-8cb2-e3d142dc8d8d', 'word_count': 2137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/913fec0d-9ff2-5934-8cb2-e3d142dc8d8d'}, {'abstract': 'Shares of the Chinese gaming and Internet giant Shanda Interactive soared early Monday after the company announced a management-led buyout that would take the Nasdaq-listed company private.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/management-looks-to-take-chinas-shanda-private/', 'snippet': 'Shares of the Chinese gaming and Internet giant Shanda Interactive soared early Monday after the company announced a management-led buyout that would take the Nasdaq-listed company private.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — Shares of the Chinese gaming and Internet giant Shanda Interactive soared early Monday after the company announced a management-led buyout that would take the Nasdaq-listed company private.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Management Looks to Take China’s Shanda Private', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T19:10:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of