eshow/b32c2a5f-c5a3-5b37-95ed-c7df698cacef'}, {'abstract': 'Supplemental calcium does not prevent preterm birth or improve bone density in pregnant women, according to a new report.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/health/research/18childbirth.html', 'snippet': 'Supplemental calcium does not prevent preterm birth or improve bone density in pregnant women, according to a new report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most doctors encourage women to increase their calcium intake during pregnancy to protect against birth complications and thinning bones caused by the loss of calcium to developing babies. But supplemental calcium does not prevent preterm birth or improve bone density in pregnant women, according to a new report, and may be helpful only in lowering the risk of hypertension.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Childbirth: Limited Gains From Supplemental Calcium', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Childbirth: Limited Gains From Supplemental Calcium', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Calcium', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Premature Babies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T19:26:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization':