 tones opened the high-fidelity music market in the 1950s to millions of everyday listeners, died on Monday at his home in Woodstock, N.Y. He was 94.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/sports/18villchur/18villchur-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/sports/18villchur/18villchur-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/sports/18villchur/18villchur-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Edgar M. Villchur, a Hi-Fi Innovator, Is Dead at 94', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Edgar M. Villchur, a Hi-Fi Innovator, Is Dead at 94', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Villchur, Edgar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speakers (Audio)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T21:42:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4d3c2cf-5a6a-570c-98c3-3fd6c6fdec35', 'word_count': 976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4d3c2cf-5a6a-570c-98c3-3fd6c6fdec35'}, {'abstract': 'If, as a culture, we haven’t graduated beyond rather sophomoric objectification, then let it be said that we have at least learned to objectify on the basis of equal opportunity.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/the-underappreciated-hunks-of-occupy-wall-street/', 'snippet': 'If, as a culture, we haven’t graduated beyond rather sophomoric objectification, then let it be said that we have at least learned to objectify on the basis of equal opportunity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one ever said the revolution would be sexy. In fact, media coverage of Occupy Wall Street suggested quite the opposite, tending to emphasize the unkempt woolliness and generally unsanitary nature of the movement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Underappreciated Hunks of Occupy Wall Street', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identification Devices', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldman, Emma', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T21:42:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clinton Cargill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clinton', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cargill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a41af76d-e5e3-5267-a16b-cfaec06b8ebb', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a41af76d-e5e3-5267-a16b-cfaec06b8ebb'}, {'abstract': 'Ron Paul on Monday announced a plan to cut $1 trillion from federal spending in a single year, drastically reducing the size and scope of government, if he is elected president.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/paul-plan-would-eliminate-cabinet-departments-to-cut-1-trillion/', 'snippet': 'Ron Paul on Monday announced a plan to cut $1 trillion from federal spending in a single year, drastically reducing the size and scope of government, if he is elected president.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:29 p.m. | Updated LAS VEGAS — Representative Ron Paul on Monday unveiled an aggressive budget plan that would greatly shrink the federal government that he is seeking to run, eliminating the agency that oversees airport security, the Departments of Energy and Education and three others, while cutting all war financing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul Plan Would Eliminate Cabinet Departments to Cut $1 Trillion', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T21:43:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36289a91-31f5-5726-9fcc-21098ca7e494', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36289a91-31f5-5726-9fcc-21098ca7e494'}, {'abstract': 'They can’t handle the truth.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/legends-of-the-rentiers/', 'snippet': 'They can’t handle the truth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I feel Dean Baker’s pain. Dean is exercised over an NPR report which says that Argentina is suffering from its 2001 default — a claim that is totally at odds with the evidence. Argentina actually did very well by thumbing its nose at creditors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Legends Of The Rentiers', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T21:44:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f853dd2c-741a-5c7f-96da-869a04483800', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f853dd2c-741a-5c7f-96da-869a04483800'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting their two-year Legacy Tour.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/drawing-dance-a-cunningham-dancer-at-rest/', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting their two-year Legacy Tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Brooklyn artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting, through a series of drawings and paintings, their two-year Legacy Tour. After 58 years the company is scheduled to disband on New Year’s Day 2012. This is the 16th in a series of graphite drawings Mr. Parris plans to create from the road, providing a front-row seat to the final weeks of the company’s journey. This week’s entry is from London.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drawing Dance: A Cunningham Dancer At Rest', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce, Dance Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-17T21:45:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70fceb9d-6399-56b1-9c56-a46bd4a41c62', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70fceb9d-6399-56b1-9c56-a46bd4a41c62'}, {'abstract': 'Dava Sobel has taken another quirky approach to science history in “A More Perfect Heaven,” her new biography of the Renaissance astronomer Nicolaus Copernicus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/science/space/18scibooks.html', 'snippet': 'Dava Sobel has taken another quirky approach to science history in “A More Perfect Heaven,” her new biography of the Renaissance astronomer Nicolaus Copernicus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dava Sobel has long taken a quirky approach to science history. In “Galileo’s Daughter” (1999), for instance, she focused not on the standard biographical material but on the scientist’s love for his illegitimate daughter, consigned to a convent at 13 and dead of dysentery at 33.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/science/18SCIB/18SCIB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 731, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/science/18SCIB/18SCIB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/science/18SCIB/18SCIB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fiddling With a Two-Year Gap in the Busy Life of Copernicus', 'kicker': 'Books on Science', 'content_kicker': N