ree in a row on the road at Oakland, Baltimore and New England. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tracking Jets vs. Dolphins on ‘Monday Night Football’', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T00:20:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Bretherton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bretherton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76fa5859-02f6-5b1a-a7a3-558a5644811b', 'word_count': 1449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76fa5859-02f6-5b1a-a7a3-558a5644811b'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Wheldon, who died Sunday at the Las Vegas Motor Speedway, was a star in IndyCar Racing who drew little attention in his native Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/sports/autoracing/wheldon-soared-above-britains-sporting-medicority.html', 'snippet': 'Dan Wheldon, who died Sunday at the Las Vegas Motor Speedway, was a star in IndyCar Racing who drew little attention in his native Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — When the Englishman Dan Wheldon won his second Indianapolis 500 in May, taking the lead for the first time when another driver hit the wall in sight of the checkered flag, it barely rated a mention in Britain’s sports sections — and then, commonly, only in the fine print of the “who won what” summaries at the foot of the page.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/sports/WHELDON/WHELDON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/18/sports/WHELDON/WHELDON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/sports/WHELDON/WHELDON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/sports/WHELDON/WHELDON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/sports/WHELDON/WHELDON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Back Home, Known for a Tragedy, Not Successes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back Home, Known For a Tragedy, Not Successes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indianapolis 500 (Auto Race)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheldon, Dan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Las Vegas Motor Speedway', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indy Racing League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T00:23:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Auto Racing', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00631630-25e5-5eaa-a0a3-aa5d8632bf63', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00631630-25e5-5eaa-a0a3-aa5d8632bf63'}, {'abstract': 'Behind the noise of our activist protest movements hums a quiet engine of determined Americans trying to repair our economic values.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/opinion/the-great-restoration.html', 'snippet': 'Behind the noise of our activist protest movements hums a quiet engine of determined Americans trying to repair our economic values.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If, in the 1960s, you had tried to judge America by looking at the sit-ins and Woodstock, you would have had a very distorted picture of where the country was heading. You wouldn’t have been able to predict that Richard Nixon would win the youth vote in 1972, which he did. You wouldn’t have been able to predict that Republicans would go on to win four out of the next five presidential elections, a streak only interrupted by Jimmy Carter, who ran as a conservative Democrat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'