enew-millionaires-tax.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, who campaigned on the promise that he would not raise taxes, said an income tax surcharge would place New York at a competitive disadvantage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — Even as Occupy Wall Street stokes debate over income inequality, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo dug in his heels on Monday against extending a so-called millionaires’ tax on high-earning New Yorkers, saying the income tax surcharge would place New York at a competitive disadvantage with neighboring states.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Protests, Cuomo Says He Will Not Extend a Tax Surcharge on Top Earners', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Protests, Cuomo Says He Will Not Extend a Tax Surcharge on Top Earners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:05:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/294bbb28-5b73-57e8-a90f-cd0bf3c88ab6', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/294bbb28-5b73-57e8-a90f-cd0bf3c88ab6'}, {'abstract': 'After a silence from the Republican presidential candidates on national security, they are now offering largely bad analysis and worse solutions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/opinion/republicans-and-foreign-policy.html', 'snippet': 'After a silence from the Republican presidential candidates on national security, they are now offering largely bad analysis and worse solutions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a while, we were concerned that the candidates for the Republican presidential nomination were not saying much about national security and foreign affairs. Now that a few have started, maybe they were better off before.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans and Foreign Policy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans and Foreign Policy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uzbekistan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karimov, Islam', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:06:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/74a40f31-4e25-59c4-8f8a-446ab77e21df', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74a40f31-4e25-59c4-8f8a-446ab77e21df'}, {'abstract': 'On Sunday, the mix of a fast track packed with drivers with millions of dollars on the line led to one of Indy car’s worst crashes and the death of the driver Dan Wheldon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/sports/autoracing/worries-circled-las-vegas-track-before-a-pileup.html', 'snippet': 'On Sunday, the mix of a fast track packed with drivers with millions of dollars on the line led to one of Indy car’s worst crashes and the death of the driver Dan Wheldon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — The recipe for disaster in auto racing is hardly a secret. Start with a problematic racing layout, mix in a field of expert drivers with rookies and rusty ones, put millions of dollars on the line and then add speed. Lots of speed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/sports/JPINDY/JPINDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/18/sports/JPINDY/JPINDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/sports/JPINDY/JPINDY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 584, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/sport