Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:18:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f482387-3184-5354-85be-d4a12d0ee187', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f482387-3184-5354-85be-d4a12d0ee187'}, {'abstract': 'A Canadian company has drawn criticism for threatening to take property from landowners in the United States for a pipeline that has not been approved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/us/transcanada-in-eminent-domain-fight-over-pipeline.html', 'snippet': 'A Canadian company has drawn criticism for threatening to take property from landowners in the United States for a pipeline that has not been approved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Canadian company has been threatening to confiscate private land from South Dakota to the Gulf of Mexico, and is already suing many who have refused to allow the Keystone XL pipeline\xa0on their property even though the controversial project has yet to receive federal approval.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/us/PIPELINE/PIPELINE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/18/us/PIPELINE/PIPELINE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'c