8-c2de59d840f1'}, {'abstract': 'A different approach to providing housing is having success at convincing the chronic homeless to move inside.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/nyregion/nyc-makes-progress-helping-bronxs-chronic-homeless-adults.html', 'snippet': 'A different approach to providing housing is having success at convincing the chronic homeless to move inside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not far from the Major Deegan Expressway in the South Bronx is an abandoned subway platform where someone placed a plastic chair, a flimsy mattress and a nightstand. Nearby, in an old construction site, a truck trailer is lined with enough discarded furniture that it looks like a makeshift bedroom.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/nyregion/yhomeless/yhomeless-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/18/nyregion/yhomeless/yhomeless-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/nyregion/yhomeless/yhomeless-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/nyregion/yhomeless/yhomeless-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/nyregion/yhomeless/yhomeless-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Smaller Shelters and Persuasion Coax Homeless Off Bronx Streets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smaller Shelters and Persuasion Coax Homeless Off Bronx Streets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeless Services Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:22:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mosi Secret', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mosi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Secret', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a759272-6b79-5693-8d87-2f365669331a', 'word_count': 1301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a759272-6b79-5693-8d87-2f365669331a'}, {'abstract': 'A $3.4 billion settlement was reached after Ms. Cobell, as the lead plaintiff, filed a lawsuit alleging federal mismanagement of Indian trust funds since the late 1800s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/us/elouise-cobell-65-dies-sued-us-over-indian-trust-funds.html', 'snippet': 'A $3.4 billion settlement was reached after Ms. Cobell, as the lead plaintiff, filed a lawsuit alleging federal mismanagement of Indian trust funds since the late 1800s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elouise Cobell, a heroine to American Indians for leading a 15-year legal battle that ended with the federal government’s agreeing to pay $3.4 billion in compensation for mismanagement of Indian trust funds since the late 1800s, died on Sunday in Great Falls, Mont. She was 65 and lived on the Blackfeet reservation near Browning, Mont.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/us/COBELL-obit/COBELL-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/18/us/COBELL-obit/COBELL-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/us/COBELL-obit/COBELL-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/us/COBELL-obit/COBELL-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/us/COBELL-obit/COBELL-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Elouise Cobell, 65, Dies; Sued U.S. Over Indian Trust Funds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Elouise Cobell, 65; Sued for Indian Funds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cobell, Elouise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:28:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/36a9059c-3b59-57aa-925a-afb9e88d6a55', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36a9059c-3b59-57aa-925a-afb9e88d6a55'}, {'abstract': 'If a report from the anti-Qaddafi fighters about taking control of Bani Walid proves accurate, only a small district of Surt will remain as a stronghold for loyalists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/world/middleeast/bani-walid-seized-anti-qaddafi-fighters-say.html', 'snippet': 'If a report from the anti-Qaddafi fighters about taking control of Bani Walid proves accurate, only a small district of Surt will remain as a stronghold for loyalists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Libyan forces fighting the vestiges of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi’s toppled government said Monday that anti-Qaddafi fighters were in complete control of Bani Walid, a loyalist desert enclave south of Tripoli, the capital, but had yet to proclaim total victory in his Mediterranean hometown of Surt. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/world/JP-LIBYA/JP-LIBYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/18/world/JP-LIBYA/JP-LIBYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/world/JP-LIBYA/JP-LIBYA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/world/JP-LIBYA/JP-LIBYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/world/JP-LIBYA/JP-LIBYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pro-Qaddafi Enclave in Desert Is Said to Fall After a Battle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pro-Qaddafi Enclave in Desert Is Said to Fall After a Battle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tripoli (Libya)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transitional National Council (Libya)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Surt (Libya)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:32:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68d242c7-c07d-5b8b-8689-113d14893ffc', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68d242c7-c07d-5b8b-8689-113d14893ffc'}, {'abstract': 'Paul W. Bergrin, a federal prosecutor turned freewheeling defense lawyer, is charged with orchestrating the 2004 murder of a witness who was to testify against one of his clients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/nyregion/newark-lawyer-paul-bergrin-defends-himself-in-murder-trial.html', 'snippet': 'Paul W. Bergrin, a federal prosecutor turned freewheeling defense lawyer, is charged with orchestrating the 2004 murder of a witness who was to testify against one of his clients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — With his pinstripe suit and cobalt tie, the defense lawyer, Paul W. Bergrin, looked the part as he addressed the jury for the first time. The prosecution’s witnesses are liars, he said, as defense lawyers do. “They will say and they will do anything,” he said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/nyregion/bergrin/bergrin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/nyregion/bergrin/bergrin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/nyregion/bergrin/bergrin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawyer Defends Himself on Charges He Orchestrated Murder of a Witness', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawyer Defends Himself on Charges He Orchestrated Murder of a Witness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergrin, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martini, William J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Witnesses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:33:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Glaberson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glaberson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d3a8089-a25a-5b62-823a-7dea75676b3c', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d3a8089-a25a-5b62-823a-7dea75676b3c'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg announced a program meant to reduce repeated road work with coordination among utilities, contractors and city agencies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/nyregion/digital-system-in-new-york-is-meant-to-coordinate-road-work.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg announced a program meant to reduce repeated road work with coordination among utilities, contractors and city agencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many New Yorkers, the process is all too familiar: A utility company arrives, lays waste to a roadway and paves it over — just in time for private contractors to turn up and gut the street anew.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Aims for Teamwork to End Dig-Pave-Dig Cycle on Roads', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Aims for Teamwork to End Dig-Pave-Dig Cycle on Roads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:34:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4c58c4d-c368-529d-a2b8-1c479a0bea2d', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4c58c4d-c368-529d-a2b8-1c479a0bea2d'}, {'abstract': 'The underwriters of the public offering of Groupon shares, the hottest of the year, seemed to have overlooked signs of problems at the start-up.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/the-missed-red-flags-on-groupon/', 'snippet': 'The underwriters of the public offering of Groupon shares, the hottest of the year, seemed to have overlooked signs of problems at the start-up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This summer, Lloyd Blankfein, the chief executive of Goldman Sachs, flew to Chicago to personally pitch his firm to underwrite what was supposed to be the hottest initial public offering of the year: Groupon, the fledgling online coupon company that was being valued at around $30 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Missed Red Flags on Groupon', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mason, Andrew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Credit Suisse Group AG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Groupon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:35:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f795c6ed-5824-57b2-ac75-7a16264512d2', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f795c6ed-5824-57b2-ac75-7a16264512d2'}, {'abstract': 'Renee Nicole Doucuer, who was managing a research station at the South Pole when she suffered a stroke on Aug. 27, was airlifted from the isolated base on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/us/stroke-victim-is-flown-from-south-pole.html', 'snippet': 'Renee Nicole Doucuer, who was managing a research station at the South Pole when she suffered a stroke on Aug. 27, was airlifted from the isolated base on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Renee Nicole Doucuer, who was serving as winter manager at the Amundsen-Scott research station at the South Pole when she suffered a stroke on Aug. 27, was airlifted from the isolated base on Monday. Ms. Doucuer was resting in New Zealand on Monday. She is expected to undergo tests on Tuesday to determine the severity of her stroke, and the results will determine when she flies home to Seabrook, N.H. Ms. Doucuer, 58, had been trying to leave the South Pole since her stroke. But Raytheon, which operates the station under contract from the National Science Foundation, determined that any rescue during Antarctica’s winter would unnecessarily put other lives at risk. Ms. Doucuer and her family pressured Raytheon and the National Science Foundation to have a plane on standby should the weather improve. The flight that ultimately retrieved Ms. Doucuer was the first scheduled one of the spring season. A C-17 cargo plane, which was not intended to carry passengers, made room for Ms. Doucuer and a doctor from the station. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stroke Victim Is Flown From South Pole', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Science', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stroke Victim Is Flown From South Pole', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Science Foundation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Raytheon Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Pole', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doucuer, Renee Nicole', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stroke', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:36:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Quenqua', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quenqua', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9410a0fd-7468-5643-9f3c-1b75a816e505', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9410a0fd-7468-5643-9f3c-1b75a816e505'}, {'abstract': 'The hedge fund manager David Einhorn’s withering assessment of Green Mountain Coffee Roasters sent the stock plunging on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/an-investor-creates-a-tempest-in-a-coffee-cup/', 'snippet': 'The hedge fund manager David Einhorn’s withering assessment of Green Mountain Coffee Roasters sent the stock plunging on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When shares of Green Mountain Coffee Roasters began trading on Monday morning, they held the distinction of being the best-performing stock on a major exchange over the last five years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Investor Creates a Tempest in a Coffee Cup', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Einhorn, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:39:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3044c4f4-5d29-5bac-af7d-e995ec33e752', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3044c4f4-5d29-5bac-af7d-e995ec33e752'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oct. 17, 2011', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:40:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/8231e155-d339-53bf-bddc-786d4f6d2a9d', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8231e155-d339-53bf-bddc-786d4f6d2a9d'}, {'abstract': 'Security forces fired rubber bullets and tear gas at stone-wielding protesters Kampala on Monday as an activist group tried to reignite street demonstrations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/world/africa/in-uganda-security-forces-clash-with-protesters.html', 'snippet': 'Security forces fired rubber bullets and tear gas at stone-wielding protesters Kampala on Monday as an activist group tried to reignite street demonstrations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Security forces fired rubber bullets and tear gas at stone-wielding protesters Kampala on Monday as an activist group tried to reignite street demonstrations against high commodity prices and corruption. Protest organizers were arrested in Kampala, the capital, and in the southern cities of Mbarara and Masaka. In Kampala, rioting broke out in the downtown Kiseka market, with traders throwing stones as columns of police officers and armored vehicles swept the area. A tear gas canister landed in a nearby secondary school where students were taking national exams. Opposition politicians and activists called for a resumption of the protests this week. During the initial protests last spring, at least nine people were killed and hundreds were arrested.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uganda: Security Forces Clash With Protesters', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:43:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/987423f6-8a95-5231-9696-483e9d850fd0', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/987423f6-8a95-5231-9696-483e9d850fd0'}, {'abstract': 'Map shows routes once impassable by the Arctic ice cap that have opened up into new shipping lanes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/10/18/business/the-northeast-passage-opens-up.html', 'snippet': 'Map shows routes once impassable by the Arctic ice cap that have opened up into new shipping lanes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Map shows routes once impassable by the Arctic ice cap that have opened up into new shipping lanes.', 'source': 'The New Yo