raph': 'Despite all the bleak economic news, a funny thing has been happening in the financial industry over the last few months: the banks have quietly turned on the lending spigot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banks Start to Make More Loans', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo & Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T01:58:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Dash and Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2362d729-236e-5f98-8f45-076c0ea17011', 'word_count': 1210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2362d729-236e-5f98-8f45-076c0ea17011'}, {'abstract': 'Day 2 of our week-long puzzle contest.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/day-two-contest/', 'snippet': 'Day 2 of our week-long puzzle contest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Administrivial Tournament Reminder! It’s not too late to sign up for the Westchester Crossword Puzzle Tournament, held this year on Friday, October 21 at Will Shortz’s Westchester Table Tennis Club.\xa0New York Times crossword puzzles, mouth-watering desserts, and additional puzzles by our puzzle master make for an evening of fun that raises money for a great cause, the Pleasantville Fund For Learning.\xa0You can even pay at the door, so if you will be in the area, stop by and say hello. I’ll be there to greet you, but I’m just warning you: the brownies are mine. All mine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday: Day Two of the Crossword Contest', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T02:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47798e6e-5e79-5203-9af2-2b62255d7cfb', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47798e6e-5e79-5203-9af2-2b62255d7cfb'}, {'abstract': 'Mike Daisey delves into the lives of the workers in China, and the grim conditions there, as he raises questions about our support of products made in such conditions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/theater/reviews/the-agony-and-the-ecstasy-of-steve-jobs-review.html', 'snippet': 'Mike Daisey delves into the lives of the workers in China, and the grim conditions there, as he raises questions about our support of products made in such conditions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I hate to tell you this, but your best friend has a dark secret in his past, the kind of shameful history that might just have you looking at him (or her?) a little sheepishly, with a furtive, sidelong glance instead of the former adoring 