untry are marked by each city’s stew of circumstances and grievances, but the protesters seem united in feeling that the system is stacked against them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/us/the-occupy-movements-common-thread-is-anger.html', 'snippet': 'The Occupy protests across the country are marked by each city’s stew of circumstances and grievances, but the protesters seem united in feeling that the system is stacked against them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — Ken Alandt’s guitar, which he covered with bumper stickers and waved in the air at the Occupy Phoenix protest on Monday, is a symbol of the movement itself — a mélange of disparate causes, all of which prompt his blood to boil.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/us/18anger_span/18anger_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/18/us/18anger_span/18anger_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/us/18anger_span/18anger_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/us/18anger_span/18anger_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/us/18anger_span/18anger_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Countless Grievances, One Thread: We’re Angry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Countless Grievances, One Thread: We’re Angry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T02:32:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Lacey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lacey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebd61a56-5eac-5fee-9d3b-d1d9a7f1d227', 'word_count': 1168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebd61a56-5eac-5fee-9d3b-d1d9a7f1d227'}, {'abstract': 'The contagion, which does not affect people but is a scourge of fish farms, was reported by researchers in British Columbia, stirring concern that it could spread there, as it has elsewhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/science/18salmon.html', 'snippet': 'The contagion, which does not affect people but is a scourge of fish farms, was reported by researchers in British Columbia, stirring concern that it could spread there, as it has elsewhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lethal and highly contagious marine virus has been detected for the first time in wild salmon in the Pacific Northwest, researchers in British Columbia said on Monday, stirring concern that it could spread there, as it has in Chile, Scotland and elsewhere.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/us/SALMON/SALMON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 523, 'width': 949, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/us/SALMON/SALMON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/us/SALMON/SALMON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Salmon-Killing Virus Seen for First Time in the Wild on the Pacific Coast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Salmon-Killing Virus Seen for First Time in the Wild on the Pacific Coast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salmon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'British Columbia (Canada)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pacific Northwestern States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Simon Fraser University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Viruses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish Farming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T02:46:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cornelia Dean and Rachel Nuwer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cornelia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dean', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nuwer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf466521-e5bb-5077-b9e6-2f303d5a38d5', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf466521-e5bb-5077-b9e6-2f303d5a38d5'}, {'abstract': 'Donald Trump took questions from listeners in a conference call with Michele Bachmann that she said drew 200,000 people.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/17/trump-joins-bachmann-on-call-with-supporters/', 'snippet': 'Donald Trump took questions from listeners in a conference call with Michele Bachmann that she said drew 200,000 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He has had pizza in Times Square with Sarah Palin. He has dined at the swank Jean Georges restaurant on Central Park with Gov. Rick Perry of Texas. And on Monday night, Donald Trump joined Representative Michele Bachmann on a telephone conference call, the latest evidence for his strange king-making role in the Republican nominating race. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Joins Bachmann on Call With Supporters', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T02:46:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/176d1632-1d38-5b18-bf8d-5d3300183c41', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/176d1632-1d38-5b18-bf8d-5d3300183c41'}, {'abstract': 'A federal mediator met separately with officials from the N.B.A. and its players union in hopes of bringing an end to the league’s four-month long lockout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/sports/basketball/nba-and-union-meet-with-mediator.html', 'snippet': 'A federal mediator met separately with officials from the N.B.A. and its players union in hopes of bringing an end to the league’s four-month long lockout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal mediator met separately with officials from the N.B.A. and its players union in hopes of bringing an end to the league’s four-month long lockout. In the meetings, which lasted a few hours each, the mediator, George H. Cohen, heard arguments from both sides and asked questions of the representatives from the league and the union. He will meet the two sides together on Tuesday. Cohen’s suggestions are nonbinding, so he will have to use his powers of persuasion to get the league and the players to move closer to a deal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.B.A. and Union Meet With Mediator', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.B.A. and Union Meet With Mediator', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T02:48:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1d70e73-18b2-5f45-ad6d-3d0eb722a4a3', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1d70e73-18b2-5f45-ad6d-3d0eb722a4a3'}, {'abstract': 'Italian police searched for suspects on Monday in the riot that caused millions of dollars of damage and injured 135 people in downtown Rome during the weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/world/europe/hundreds-of-raids-but-no-arrests-in-italy.html', 'snippet': 'Italian police searched for suspects on Monday in the riot that caused millions of dollars of damage and injured 135 people in downtown Rome during the weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The police conducted hundreds of raids across the country on Monday against people Deputy Interior Minister Alfredo Mantovano described as far-left anarchists. The police were searching for suspects in the riot that caused millions of dollars of damage and injured 135 people in downtown Rome during a demonstration over the weekend. The police made no arrests, however, beyond the 12 people arrested Saturday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy: Hundreds of Raids, but No Arrests', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Hundreds of Raids, but No Arrests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T02:49:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1f9d63f-a9cf-51bd-a7d5-7aa5ecf11bfc', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1f9d63f-a9cf-51bd-a7d5-7aa5ecf11bfc'}, {'abstract': 'The head of the state counterespionage agency faces further investigation on charges that he broke press freedom laws by obtaining records of a reporter’s calls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/world/europe/head-of-french-spy-agency-faces-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'The head of the state counterespionage agency faces further investigation on charges that he broke press freedom laws by obtaining records of a reporter’s calls.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Bernard Squarcini, head of the state counterespionage agency, faces further investigation on charges that he broke press freedom laws by obtaining records of a reporter’s calls in order to unmask a government mole, his lawyer said Monday. The lawyer said that the preliminary charges include violating secret correspondence and unlawfully collecting data. President Nicolas Sarkozy has denied asking the agency, the Central Directorate of Internal Intelligence, to investigate the source of information published in the newspaper Le Monde about political contributions made by the L’Oreal heiress Liliane Bettencourt. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Spy Agency Chief Faces Inquiry', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Spy Agency Chief Faces Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Squarcini, Bernard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T03:02:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad70c563-7b8a-5ef2-b7a7-db0b87d7b01b', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad70c563-7b8a-5ef2-b7a7-db0b87d7b01b'}, {'abstract': 'Teachers in New York State will soon be banned from grading their own students’ state standardized tests, a Board of Regents committee decided on Monday, part of an effort to curtail cheating.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/nyregion/regents-set-to-alter-rules-for-grading-state-exams.html', 'snippet': 'Teachers in New York State will soon be banned from grading their own students’ state standardized tests, a Board of Regents committee decided on Monday, part of an effort to curtail cheating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Teachers in New York State will soon be banned from grading their own students’ state standardized tests, a Board of Regents committee decided on Monday, part of an effort to curtail cheating on the high-stakes exams. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regents Set to Alter Rules for Grading State Exams', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Regents Set To Alter Rules For Grading State Exams', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Board of Regents (NYS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'No Child Left Behind Act', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, John B Jr', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T03:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Education', 'section_name': 'New York', '