value': 'Chennai (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T06:48:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charukesi Ramadurai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charukesi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramadurai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ff4ff71-d0ef-5d2e-a744-6f2baa753429', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ff4ff71-d0ef-5d2e-a744-6f2baa753429'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/news-quiz-oct-18-2011/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | Oct. 18, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T07:28:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Frasier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frasier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd1b2129-e821-5ddc-af49-d2c42a6dc557', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd1b2129-e821-5ddc-af49-d2c42a6dc557'}, {'abstract': 'On Oct. 18, 1968, the United States Olympic Committee suspended the medal-winning sprinters Tommie Smith and John Carlos and barred them from the Olympic Village for their conduct during the playing of “The Star-Spangled Banner” in Mexico City.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/oct-18-1968-american-olympic-medal-winners-suspended-for-black-power-salutes/', 'snippet': 'On Oct. 18, 1968, the United States Olympic Committee suspended the medal-winning sprinters Tommie Smith and John Carlos and barred them from the Olympic Village for their conduct during the playing of “The Star-Spangled Banner” in Mexico City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Oct. 18, 1968, the United States Olympic Committee suspended the medal-winning sprinters Tommie Smith and John Carlos from the American national team and barred them from the Olympic Village for their conduct during the playing of “The Star-Spangled Banner” at a medal ceremony at the Summer Olympics in Mexico City. Mr. Smith, who won the gold medal, and Mr. Carlos, who took bronze in the 200-meter event, wore black gloves on the podium. As the American national anthem played, the two raised their fists in a gesture of support for the black power movement. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oct. 18, 1968 | American Olympic Medal Winners Suspended for Black Power Salutes', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T08:04:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bae6d53-5f80-571c-94ce-c42cf5e5c754', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bae6d53-5f80-571c-94ce-c42cf5e5c754'}, {'abstract': 'From erosion to withering crops to destroyed dwellings, climate change is affecting the people of Tuvalu in myriad ways.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/as-danger-laps-at-its-shores-tuvalu-pleads-for-action/', 'snippet': 'From erosion to withering crops to destroyed dwellings, climate change is affecting the people of Tuvalu in myriad ways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tuvalu, a tiny archipelago of nine South Pacific islands threatened by rising seas, is on the front lines of the planet’s climate change debate. Current projections indicate that it will\xa0 become unlivable within 50 years, resulting in an exodus and the erasure of a rich 3,000-year-old culture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Danger Laps at Its Shores, Tuvalu Pleads for Action', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Development Program', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tuvalu', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T09:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amelia Holowaty Krales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amelia', 'middlename': 'Holowaty', 'lastname': 'Krales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6e99037-ea1a-5ada-8b39-d64b1c534697', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6e99037-ea1a-5ada-8b39-d64b1c534697'}, {'abstract': 'Amelia Holowaty Krales spent 10 months on a disappearing island in the South Pacific. What she found was a tight-knit community that refuses to give up on its land.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/no-place/', 'snippet': 'Amelia Holowaty Krales spent 10 months on a disappearing island in the South Pacific. What she found was a tight-knit community that refuses to give up on its land.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amelia Holowaty Krales had been anxious the morning she photographed a boy in pink shorts floating in a shallow pool of coastal water, eyes closed, toes pointed up. [Slide 1.] It was the “king tide” in Tuvalu, a small archipelago in the South Pacific that is threatened by rising sea levels.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Water Rises, There’s No Place Like (or for) Home', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T09:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3a8c8ef-13cf-573c-9215-dbc335b0f382', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3a8c8ef-13cf-573c-9215-dbc335b0f382'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the best antonym for an adjective used in context?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/test-yourself-english-oct-18-2011/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the best antonym for an adjective used in context?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the article, “Park Cleanup Is Canceled, and Showdown Averted.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Oct. 18, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T09:01:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fcb2d02-6f42-5dd6-b7b0-04a28a213354', 'word_count': 46, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fcb2d02-6f42-5dd6-b7b0-04a28a213354'}, {'abstract': 'Ambitious attempts to overhaul the entire tax code often founder on small exceptions made, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/the-tax-reform-act-of-1986-should-we-do-it-again/', 'snippet': 'Ambitious attempts to overhaul the entire tax code often founder on small exceptions made, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul. He is the author of the forthcoming book “The Benefit and the Burden.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tax Reform Act of 1986: Should We Do It Again?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T10:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role'