ne-on-one-jeff-jarvis-author-of-public-parts/', 'snippet': 'Jeff Jarvis’s latest book, “Public Parts,” argues that people should embrace publicness, rather than fear the Internet and its potential erosion of privacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeff Jarvis‘s latest book, “Public Parts,” aims to defend society’s move to public displays of personal information in an age of the Internet, social media and blogging. In the book, Mr. Jarvis argues that people should embrace what he calls publicness, rather than fear the Internet and its\xa0potential\xa0erosion of privacy.\xa0The following is an edited interview with Mr. Jarvis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One on One: Jeff Jarvis, Author of ‘Public Parts’', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jarvis, Jeff', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T11:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c403db70-852c-5050-b08b-66b6ecc8a317', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c403db70-852c-5050-b08b-66b6ecc8a317'}, {'abstract': 'Bank of America reported a $6.2 billion profit for the third quarter as gains from assets sales and positive accounting changes outweighed weaker results in its trading business and continued losses in its huge mortgage portfolio.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/bank-of-america-notches-6-2-billion-profit/', 'snippet': 'Bank of America reported a $6.2 billion profit for the third quarter as gains from assets sales and positive accounting changes outweighed weaker results in its trading business and continued losses in its huge mortgage portfolio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Buoyed by one-time gains from accounting changes and the sale of assets, Bank of America reported a $6.23 billion profit for the third-quarter Tuesday, even as weakness on Wall Street hammered underlying results and the firm surrendered its position as the country’s largest bank by assets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bank of America Notches $6.2 Billion Profit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T11:37:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb12c6b4-d739-5d91-8b9d-a94795022142', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb12c6b4-d739-5d91-8b9d-a94795022142'}, {'abstract': 'Goldman Sachs, weighed down by problems in its private equity portfolio and the broader global economic woes, reported a loss of $428 million.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/goldman-sachs-reports-428-million-loss/', 'snippet': 'Goldman Sachs, weighed down by problems in its private equity portfolio and the broader global economic woes, reported a loss of $428 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Goldman Sachs, weighed down by problems in its private equity portfolio and the broader global economic woes, reported a loss of $428 million, compared with a $1.7 billion profit a year ago. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldman Sachs Reports $428 Million Loss', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T11:48:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e37fcb76-ffe5-5ead-ab31-e9b68e992876', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e37fcb76-ffe5-5ead-ab31-e9b68e992876'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama arrives in Virginia today, at a time when some Democratic candidates there are running away from him.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/virginia-reveals-challenges-ahead-for-obama/', 'snippet': 'President Obama arrives in Virginia today, at a time when some Democratic candidates there are running away from him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama arrives in Virginia on his bus tour today, just as some Democratic candidates for the state legislature are running away from him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Virginia Reveals Challenges Ahead for Obama', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': '