s': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Investors Service Inc", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T12:46:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffefb564-0cc7-51f7-a3a7-009822eb4d16', 'word_count': 1012, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffefb564-0cc7-51f7-a3a7-009822eb4d16'}, {'abstract': 'Images of the prisoner swap began spreading on Tuesday as Israelis celebrated the return of Gilad Shalit and Palestinians welcomed hundreds of freed prisoners home.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/video-and-photos-of-the-israeli-palestinian-prisoner-swap/', 'snippet': 'Images of the prisoner swap began spreading on Tuesday as Israelis celebrated the return of Gilad Shalit and Palestinians welcomed hundreds of freed prisoners home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The prisoner swap between Israel and Hamas began on Tuesday with the exchange of an Israeli soldier, held captive for more than five years, for hundreds of Palestinian prisoners in Israeli jails, as our colleagues Ethan Bronner and Stephen Farrell report. The Lede provided updates on the release of prisoners. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Updates on the Israeli-Palestinian Prisoner Swap', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shalit, Gilad', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T12:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey and J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d85a065b-8940-522f-9364-23a601d23094', 'word_count': 1739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d85a065b-8940-522f-9364-23a601d23094'}, {'abstract': 'Lookout, which makes mobile phone security apps, plans to introduce one for the iPhone, even though it has so far been less vulnerable to attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/lookout-introduces-a-security-app-for-iphones/', 'snippet': 'Lookout, which makes mobile phone security apps, plans to introduce one for the iPhone, even though it has so far been less vulnerable to attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most iPhone users blithely believe that their phones are safe from hackers. Unlike Android phones, which have been the target of a few malicious attacks, iPhones have so far been less vulnerable because Android is growing faster and because, unlike Apple, it does not screens all apps before allowing them in its app store.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lookout Introduces a Security App for iPhones', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T13:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd26c63a-1981-5a56-943c-b1fc941a5895', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd26c63a-1981-5a56-943c-b1fc941a5895'}, {'abstract': 'Reflections on parental loss and the isolation that can come with having a special-needs child.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/watching-an-autistic-child-regress/', 'snippet': 'Reflections on parental loss and the isolation that can come with having a special-needs child.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Terrible pain too often accompanies mother love (and father love, for that matter). I could not let Megan Liberman’s post from Monday on Emily Rapp’s “Notes From a Dragon Mom” inch down the screen without flagging another — admittedly far less hopeless — reflection on maternal loss that I read some days ago in The Chronicle of Higher Education.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watching an Autistic Child Regress', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 