on': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c81adc6-352a-5a61-8fc4-2c3ecb958a72', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c81adc6-352a-5a61-8fc4-2c3ecb958a72'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/morning-take-out-348/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Goldman Sachs Reports $428 Million Loss \xa0|\xa0 Goldman Sachs, weighed down by problems in its private equity portfolio and the broader global economic woes, reported a loss of $428 million, only the second quarterly loss since the investment bank went public in 1999.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T13:50:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc95a370-2f71-5749-ba08-b781862d6f03', 'word_count': 1799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc95a370-2f71-5749-ba08-b781862d6f03'}, {'abstract': 'Bankers for stimulus.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/surprise-anti-austerians/', 'snippet': 'Bankers for stimulus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is indeed a mixed-up, muddled-up, shook-up world. Right now, the two most prominent institutions calling for an end to the disastrous turn to short-run austerity are … Goldman Sachs and the International Monetary Fund.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surprise Anti-Austerians', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T13:55:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f86d02b6-2334-59e1-bdbc-f81b49006684', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f86d02b6-2334-59e1-bdbc-f81b49006684'}, {'abstract': 'Americans who identify with Occupy Wall Street say income inequality, eroding standards of living and corporate greed drive their support.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/views-of-the-99-percent-corporate-power-is-up-while-living-standards-are-down/', 'snippet': 'Americans who identify with Occupy Wall Street say income inequality, eroding standards of living and corporate greed drive their support.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Offshoots of the Occupy Wall Street movement have spread across the United States with organized protests coming to life in dozens of cities throughout the country. But are the demonstrations resonating with the general public?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "Views of the ’99 Percent': Corporate Power Is Up While Living Standards are Down", 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T14:10:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lori Moore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/746685f4-cf7c-5dc7-ba6a-2ea44e54771d', 'word_count': 1418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/746685f4-cf7c-5dc7-ba6a-2ea44e54771d'}, {'abstract': 'Misinformation from Investors Business Daily.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/levels-and-changes/', 'snippet': 'Misinformation from Investors Business Daily.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jared Bernstein is annoyed at an Investor’s Business Daily piece that totally misinforms readers about how to think about the effects of stimulus and austerity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Levels And Changes', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T14:22:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41476807-372a-5981-89c0-d02c0b35cce1', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41476807-372a-5981-89c0-d02c0b35cce1'}, {'abstract': 'The Löyly spa in Portland, Ore., is about communal shvitzing rather than solitary pampering.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/steam-punks/', 'snippet': 'The Löyly spa in Portland, Ore., is about communal shvitzing rather than solitary pampering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was perhaps only a matter of time before the D.I.Y. ethos touched the spa world, and it has done so with style in Portland, Ore., with Löyly, a handsome, minimalist sauna in the southeast quadrant of the city. The owner, Jessica Kelso, was inspired by traditional Scandinavian bathhouses —\xa0“löyly” is Finnish for the steam produced when water is poured over sauna rocks — and wanted to bring their sense of accessibility to Stumptown. “I felt like your choices in Oregon were a hippie hot springs experience or really spendy, overly attentive spa experiences, neither of which had ever appealed to me,” she says. The Löyly vibe is one of communal shvitzing rather than solitary pampering. A $15 fee gets you access to an elegantly designed cedar sauna, wet steam room and lounge; though massages and facials are available by appointment, scrubs, salts, masks and foot soaks are do-it-yourself. The place has become as popular with corporate types as it is with the city’s artists, musicians and restaurant servers. “Everyone looks the same wrapped in a white towel,” Kelso says, “although we do see a lot of tattoos in Portland.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steam Punks', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T14:35:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mari Brookshire', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brookshire', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a10eb96-34ac-57ea-b017-7da983137a44', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a10eb96-34ac-57ea-b017-7da983137a44'}, {'abstract': 'It’s all good.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/our-blogs-ourselves/', 'snippet': 'It’s all good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ryan Avent and I have been corresponding about the role of the economics blogosphere, for the Christmas issue of The Economist. I don’t know what parts of our conversation will actually show up there, but having assembled my thoughts I might as well put some of them up here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Blogs, Ourselves', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T14:37:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dd003e0-58b6-57ff-82b2-7d13238c71da', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dd003e0-58b6-57ff-82b2-7d13238c71da'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/what-were-reading-292/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wine Review Online: Get to know assyrtiko, the great white wine of Santorini. Ed McCarthy takes us on tour. — Eric Asimov', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T14:52:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/492f34dc-9ea6-5c32-98d3-7aa56fa3e844', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/492f34dc-9ea6-5c32-98d3-7aa56fa3e844'}, {'abstract': 'A victory over the Dolphins, who fell to 0-5, gave the Jets a platform to claim their problems are over, at least for a week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/sports/dolphins-make-jets-problems-go-away-for-a-day-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'A victory over the Dolphins, who fell to 0-5, gave the Jets a platform to claim their problems are over, at least for a week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to what can officially be described as the N.F.L.’s season of dysfunction, the final requirement for that distinction being reached sometime in the Jets’ 24-6 victory over Miami on Monday night. One team looked barely motivated to get off its own bench, managed 5 whole passing yards in the first quarter, and expended far less energy on offense than its players did squawking at one another all week. And that was the team that won. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just What the Jets Ordered', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Just What the Jets Ordered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Rams', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Dolphins', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Revis, Darrelle', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheldon, Dan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Nelson', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harbaugh, Jim', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Josh', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Jim (1966- )', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T14:52:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/660dda06-5157-5e46-ac43-14ee75907b41', 'word_count': 735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/660dda06-5157-5e46-ac43-14ee75907b41'}, {'abstract': 'While he served time in Huntsville, Tex., Brian Price cooked special last meals for 218 prisoners on death row. He opposes the state’s decision to end the custom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/us/former-inmate-shares-tricks-of-the-trade-of-a-death-row-chef.html', 'snippet': 'While he served time in Huntsville, Tex., Brian Price cooked special last meals for 218 prisoners on death row. He opposes the state’s decision to end the custom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, Texas prison officials decided to end the tradition of special meals for inmates facing execution after Lawrence Russell Brewer, 44, requested a large dinner before his Sept. 21 lethal injection. Mr. Brewer, a white supremacist gang member, had been convicted of chaining James Byrd, Jr., a 49-year-old black man, to a pickup truck and dragging him along a road until he died. As his final meal, Mr. Brewer had requested a pound of barbecue with half a loaf of white bread; three fajitas “with fixings”; a cheese omelet with “ground beef, tomatoes, onions, bell peppers and jalapenos”; two chicken fried steaks “smothered in gravy with sliced onions”; a “triple meat” bacon cheeseburger with “fixings on the side”; a “large bowl” of fried okra; a “meat lovers” pizza; a pint of vanilla ice cream; a “slab” of peanut butter fudge with crushed peanuts; and three root beers. He was given some of the items, in smaller portions, but ate nothing. After the state’s decision, Brian D. Price, 60, a former inmate who as jailhouse chef cooked last meals for 218 prisoners on death row in Huntsville, Tex., offered to prepare meals for the condemned for free. Texas said thanks but no thanks. Mr. Price discusses:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/us/20111018questionsinline/20111018questionsinline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 938, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Inmate Shares Stories of Stint as a Death Row Chef', 'kicker': 'Asked and Answered: Brian Price', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Inmate Shares Stories of Stint as a Death Row Chef', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T14:55:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce6bd8c8-5802-5284-b3ec-73e637e16504', 'word_count': 1264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce6bd8c8-5802-5284-b3ec-73e637e16504'}, {'abstract': 'Meb Keflezighi plans to run both the New York City Marathon on Nov. 6 and the United States Olympic trials 10 weeks later, but many other top Americans will run only the trials.', 'web_url': 'htt