nformed them of the miscalculation. Kiplinger says the error has been fixed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Do You Rank Among the 99 (or 1) Percent?', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T15:29:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5c75685-4084-5cdd-ade7-41cca5f9c3d6', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5c75685-4084-5cdd-ade7-41cca5f9c3d6'}, {'abstract': 'A judge in Britain rules that assets can be seized to pay off debts.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/despite-millions-of-record-sales-ub40-members-are-bankrupt/', 'snippet': 'A judge in Britain rules that assets can be seized to pay off debts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four original members of UB40, the British reggae band that sold more than 70 million records, have been declared bankrupt by a judge in Britain, the BBC and Billboard reported. A judge in the Birmingham County court said government tax officers could seize the band’s assets and property to pay off outstanding debts in a ruling against the saxophonist Brian Travers, the drummer Jimmy Brown, the trumpeter Terence Oswald and the percussionist Norman Hassan. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Millions of Record Sales, UB40 Members Are Bankrupt', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker':