2011/10/18/second-suspect-arrested-in-sex-attack-pattern/', 'snippet': 'The man is accused of sexually assaulting a woman in May; additional police lineups are being conducted.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:18 p.m. | Updated A Queens man was charged on Tuesday in connection with at least one in a string of 20 sexual assaults in Brooklyn since March, the police said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Second Suspect Charged in Sex-Attack Pattern', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T17:35:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c81e0105-ac5f-53c7-9958-b38cd13268d9', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c81e0105-ac5f-53c7-9958-b38cd13268d9'}, {'abstract': 'A. O. Scott looks back at Robert Bresson’s portrait of suffering and grace.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/critics-picks-video-au-hasard-balthazar/', 'snippet': 'A. O. Scott looks back at Robert Bresson’s portrait of suffering and grace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s Critics’ Picks, A. O. Scott looks back at Robert Bresson’s 1966 drama “Au Hasard Balthazar,” which tells the story of a donkey in rural France and the girl who loves him. Mr. Scott points out that the film isn’t a fairy tale about an animal with human qualities, but rather “an unsettling and tragic examination of some of the deepest mysteries of existence.” Balthazar is the name of the donkey who is adopted by a family and befriended by Marie (Anne Wiazemsky).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Critics’ Picks Video: ‘Au Hasard Balthazar’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T17:41:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b74a90c-fbda-5fca-a81f-4d29499ba565', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b74a90c-fbda-5fca-a81f-4d29499ba565'}, {'abstract': 'I could fill a whole separate Twitter account with things I read on fliers during the five days I spent recently in Oregon.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/sentence-of-the-weeks-oregon-edition/', 'snippet': 'I could fill a whole separate Twitter account with things I read on fliers during the five days I spent recently in Oregon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A. What we know from the physics of morphogenetic fields is that each family is beholden to one governing energy field. (A flier on a college campus in Oregon)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sentence of the Weeks, Oregon Edition', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Batuman, Elif', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'pe