Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Backe, Hans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soler, Erik', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T21:11:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b088574-d3b0-5b90-b18e-2f4fc30d2e29', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b088574-d3b0-5b90-b18e-2f4fc30d2e29'}, {'abstract': 'Before studying corals in Fiji, scientists meet with district chiefs and village leaders in ceremonies that often involve extensive socializing and drinking of kava root.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/drinking-kava-on-fiji-time/', 'snippet': 'Before studying corals in Fiji, scientists meet with district chiefs and village leaders in ceremonies that often involve extensive socializing and drinking of kava root.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Hay, a biology professor at Georgia Tech, writes from Fiji, where he is investigating coral-seaweed competition in the coral reefs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drinking Kava on ‘Fiji Time’', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coral', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reefs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Georgia Institute of Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fiji', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T21:12:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Hay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e269c53f-1370-55de-9a46-e3733f990f2e', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e269c53f-1370-55de-9a46-e3733f990f2e'}, {'abstract': 'The research firm Gartner predicts which technologies will arrive in the workplace in 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/a-shopping-list-for-corporate-buyers/', 'snippet': 'The research firm Gartner predicts which technologies will arrive in the workplace in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gartner Inc., a research firm that advises top executives on information technology, sells peace of mind as much as insight. Buy this, says a Gartner endorsement, and you’ll be moving with the rest of our forward-looking clientele. That is a big deal; even though $3.6 trillion is spent on information technology a year, few executives want to feel as if they are moving too fast or too slow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shopping List for Corporate Buyers', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gartner Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T21:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe2857e0-04ce-5827-9482-a40f3edb335f', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe2857e0-04ce-5827-9482-a40f3edb335f'}, {'abstract': 'Adbusters, which lighted the fire that became Occupy Wall Street, is organizing a worldwide protest on Oct. 29 with a goal: a “Robin Hood” tax of 1 percent of all financial transactions.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/after-igniting-wall-st-protests-magazine-proposes-one-clear-demand/', 'snippet': 'Adbusters, which lighted the fire that became Occupy Wall Street, is organizing a worldwide protest on Oct. 29 with a goal: a “Robin Hood” tax of 1 percent of all financial transactions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three months ago, the Canadian magazine Adbusters called for a protest on Wall Street, providing the spark that began a wildfire of protest across the country and, over the weekend, in an increasing number of cities around the world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Igniting Wall St. Protests, Magazine Proposes One Clear Demand', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Adbusters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wall Street (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T21:17:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7fd2783-1be7-5f74-8fe4-eb4d2fb33296', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7fd2783-1be7-5f74-8fe4-eb4d2fb33296'}, {'abstract': 'What happens when the data won’t cooperate.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/calibration-and-all-that-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'What happens when the data won’t cooperate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brad DeLong sends us to Roman Frydman sending us to an interview of Tom Sargent that touches on the shift of freshwater schools to “calibration” — which basically means tweaking the parameters of your model until it fits some aspects of the data, rather than flat-out estimating the model.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calibration And All That (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T21:17:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85298293-5124-5805-976c-d000b401bcc8', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85298293-5124-5805-976c-d000b401bcc8'}, {'abstract': '“Paul Goodman Changed My Life” is Jonathan Lee’s documentary portrait of the ’60s poet, teacher and social critic, whose name was once a household word.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/movies/paul-goodman-changed-my-life-directed-by-jonathan-lee-review.html', 'snippet': '“Paul Goodman Changed My Life” is Jonathan Lee’s documentary portrait of the ’60s poet, teacher and social critic, whose name was once a household word.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Paul Goodman Changed My Life” pays tribute to a man — poet, teacher, social critic, guru without portfolio — whose name was once a household word and whose books were talismans of intellectual seriousness and social concern. His current obscurity is something this documentary, directed by Jonathan Lee and including eloquent testimony from friends, family and admirers, is determined to overcome.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/movies/paul-span/paul-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/18/movies/paul-span/paul-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/movies/paul-span/paul-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/movies/paul-span/paul-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/movies/paul-span/paul-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gadfly of the ’60s, Getting His Due', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Paul Goodman Changed My Life'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gadfly of the ’60s, Getting His Due', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodman, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Jonathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_d