'lead_paragraph': 'With a decision expected by the end of the year from the Obama administration on the proposed Keystone XL pipeline, members of Congress have sent two letters to Secretary of State Hillary Clinton raising concerns over the State Department’s handling of a critical environmental review of the project. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '36 Lawmakers Berate State Dept. on Pipeline', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Keystone Pipeline System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blumenauer, Earl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leahy, Patrick J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyden, Ron', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T21:57:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Frosch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frosch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62c86f98-3325-52e3-b555-6282e9198e06', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62c86f98-3325-52e3-b555-6282e9198e06'}, {'abstract': 'The company said iPhone sales fell in the quarter because of widespread rumors that a new phone would be released, delaying consumer purchases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/technology/apple-disappoints-analysts-despite-54-rise-in-profit.html', 'snippet': 'The company said iPhone sales fell in the quarter because of widespread rumors that a new phone would be released, delaying consumer purchases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For any other big company, a 54 percent increase in profit and a 39 percent jump in revenue would be enviable. For Apple though, weak sales of its star product — the iPhone — were enough to overshadow everything else when it reported fourth-quarter results on Tuesday, sending the company’s shares tumbling nearly 7 percent in after-hours trading.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple’s Profit Gains 54%, but iPhone Sales Fall Short of Expectations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apple’s Profit Gains 54%, but iPhone Sales Fall Short of Expectations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T21:57:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a43b847b-84c1-5e31-88c7-bc2cf09c6433', 'word_count': 1036, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a43b847b-84c1-5e31-88c7-bc2cf09c6433'}, {'abstract': 'Wealthy investors fall into three categories right now: the bargain hunters, the natural resource crowd and the bettors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/business/opportunities-abound-even-for-the-risk-averse.html', 'snippet': 'Wealthy investors fall into three categories right now: the bargain hunters, the natural resource crowd and the bettors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nicolas Berggruen is passionate about investing. A compact, handsome billionaire, Mr. Berggruen is often talked about for his eccentricities — he does not own a home, preferring to jet around the world and live out of hotels — but his ability to find, invest in and turn around neglected companies points to a hardened and savvy approach.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19RISK/19RISK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19RISK/19RISK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19RISK/19RISK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19RISK/19RISK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19RISK/19RISK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chasing Opportunity in an Age of Upheaval', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Wealth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chasing Opportunity In an Age of Upheaval a', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T22:01:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70afaa38-3e5f-5b99-8598-aa5a2415b41d', 'word_count': 1973, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70afaa38-3e5f-5b99-8598-aa5a2415b41d'}, {'abstract': 'For the high-end security firms that protect the moneyed elite, Occupy Wall Street has been a stimulus package all its own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/business/protests-are-a-payday-for-security-firms.html', 'snippet': 'For the high-end security firms that protect the moneyed elite, Occupy Wall Street has been a stimulus package all its own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They call when they make the Forbes 400 list. They call when annual hedge fund rankings appear, when their names are mentioned on CNBC and when their children travel abroad. And, these days, they call when protesters camped in Lower Manhattan grow uncomfortable with the idea of their existence.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19JPSECURE2/19JPSECURE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 959, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19JPSECURE2/19JPSECURE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19JPSECURE2/19JPSECURE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Protests Are a Payday for Security Firms', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Wealth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protests Are a Payday for Security Firms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T22:01:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/143d2080-292d-5427-84a2-7f0b8a6bb500', 'word_count': 1469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/143d2080-292d-5427-84a2-7f0b8a6bb500'}, {'abstract': 'New exchange-traded funds and mutual funds may lower portfolio volatility, but their lack of history suggests investors should be cautious, advisers say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/business/niche-etfs-offer-portfolio-alternative-but-also-pose-risks.html', 'snippet': 'New exchange-traded funds and mutual funds may lower portfolio volatility, but their lack of history suggests investors should be cautious, advisers say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stocks are scary these days and too risky for many investors. Cash instruments and government bonds have yields close to their lowest levels ever. That combination could heighten interest in the myriad funds that focus on exotic, none-of-the-above assets.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/business/NEWfund/NEWfund-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 327, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/18/business/NEWfund/NEWfund-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 327}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/business/NEWfund/NEWfund-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 559, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/18/business/NEWfund/NEWfund-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/18/business/NEWfund/NEWfund-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Exotic Investments That Offer Gains, but Also Pose Risks', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Wealth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exotic Investments That Offer Gains, but Also Pose Risks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renminbi (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exchange Traded Funds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T22:02:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Conrad De Aenlle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Conrad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'De Aenlle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/419c3038-69c6-5ae4-a4b1-b87748c55221', 'word_count': 1052, 'uri': 'nyt://article/419c3038-69c6-5ae4-a4b1-b87748c55221'}, {'abstract': 'While the widespread defaults predicted for 2011 have not happened, it still pays an investor to carefully research a bond issue. A Web site makes this easier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/business/buying-municipal-bonds-calls-for-caution.html', 'snippet': 'While the widespread defaults predicted for 2011 have not happened, it still pays an investor to carefully research a bond issue. A Web site makes this easier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the prominent banking analyst Meredith Whitney predicted late last year that “hundreds of billions of dollars” of municipal bond defaults would occur in 2011, it rattled the nearly $3 trillion market.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19MUNI/19MUNI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19MUNI/19MUNI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19MUNI/19MUNI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19MUNI/19MUNI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19MUNI/19MUNI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Uncertain Times, Municipal Bonds Call for Caution', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Wealth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline'