ial Section: Wealth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Take Advantage of Tax Breaks Now, Experts Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T22:02:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jan M. Rosen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56f40ef2-9a0c-5538-9efe-c9659be23596', 'word_count': 1108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56f40ef2-9a0c-5538-9efe-c9659be23596'}, {'abstract': 'There are some important questions to ask, and documents to check, before you make a change to a new wealth manager.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/business/how-to-check-out-a-financial-adviser.html', 'snippet': 'There are some important questions to ask, and documents to check, before you make a change to a new wealth manager.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What do you do when your financial adviser becomes damaged goods?', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19FIRM/19FIRM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19FIRM/19FIRM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19FIRM/19FIRM-thum