, 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19APPRAISE2/19APPRAISE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 919, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19APPRAISE2/19APPRAISE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19APPRAISE2/19APPRAISE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Specialized Art of the Appraisal', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Wealth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Specialized Art Of the Appraisal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPRAISALS AND VALUATION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T22:03:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/964b3779-4bca-5ad7-b8e3-351284e73b9c', 'word_count': 1362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/964b3779-4bca-5ad7-b8e3-351284e73b9c'}, {'abstract': 'A hug from Jennifer Lopez may be worth a lot of money at a charity auction, with the cause fading to a secondary consideration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/business/charity-auctions-turn-to-what-cannot-be-bought.html', 'snippet': 'A hug from Jennifer Lopez may be worth a lot of money at a charity auction, with the cause fading to a secondary consideration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A\u2002few months ago, the restaurateur Jimmy John Liautaud had a private tour of the guitar collection of David Howell Evans (stage name the Edge) of U2. Then Mr. Liautaud and his wife, Leslie, sat down with the musician to chat about “kids, family, being on the road,” Mr. Liautaud recalled.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19AUCTION1/19AUCTION1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19AUCTION1/19AUCTION1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19AUCTION1/19AUCTION1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19AUCTION1/19AUCTION1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19AUCTION1/19AUCTION1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Charity, Bidding for Access to Stars — Even a Hug', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Wealth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Charity, Bidding for Access to Stars — Even a Hug', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T22:03:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fran Hawthorne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fran', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hawthorne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5f3e118-3ccb-5ebb-b731-d8e78e21caba', 'word_count': 1162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5f3e118-3ccb-5ebb-b731-d8e78e21caba'}, {'abstract': 'Funds that invest in commodities, real estate and currencies can provide a buffer against the volatility of stocks and bonds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/business/a-world-of-alternatives-that-goes-beyond-stocks-and-bonds.html', 'snippet': 'Funds that invest in commodities, real estate and currencies can provide a buffer against the volatility of stocks and bonds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the stock market continues to roil with no sign of abating, many investors have turned to alternative investments in hedging strategies.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19FUND/19FUND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19FUND/19FUND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/business/19FUND/19FUND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A World of Alternatives That Goes Beyond Stocks and Bonds', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Wealth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A World of Alternatives That Goes Beyond Stocks and Bonds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Standard & Poor's 500-Stock Index", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T22:03:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Wasik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Wasik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70f8dc9d-0f5f-5d94-bc8e-3b75f414ef96', 'word_count': 1009, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70f8dc9d-0f5f-5d94-bc8e-3b75f414ef96'}, {'abstract': 'One of the most recognizable faces at the base camp for Occupy Wall Street works for the New York Police Department.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/in-a-sea-of-protesters-one-mysterious-and-well-dressed-officer/', 'snippet': 'One of the most recognizable faces at the base camp for Occupy Wall Street works for the New York Police Department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many unknowns about the Occupy Wall Street protest in downtown Manhattan: Where is the next march? Who are its leaders? What do they really want? When will it end? But an even bigger question, perhaps, has emerged: Who is the Hipster Cop?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Revealed: The Officer Behind the Skinny Tie', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zuccotti Park (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T22:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acb57f72-6ddf-5eab-9c71-b4abeca75775', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acb57f72-6ddf-5eab-9c71-b4abeca75775'}, {'abstract': 'A post-debate process that once was an organic effort, the “spin room” is now an expected and well-orchestrated part of a debate. After seeing the previous action, it is not hard to guess what will be said if patterns hold.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/spin-recycle-what-the-post-debate-debate-might-be/', 'snippet': 'A post-debate process that once was an organic effort, the “spin room” is now an expected and well-orchestrated part of a debate. After seeing the previous action, it is not hard to guess what will be said if patterns hold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If a presidential campaign is a test of a candidate’s ability to govern, the moments immediately after a presidential debate measure a campaign’s ability to twist, manipulate, cajole and spin members of the press.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spin Recycle: What the Post-Debate Debate Might Be', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T22:13:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section