1/10/18/reviewing-prime-beyond/', 'snippet': 'More photos of the East Village steakhouse, reviewed by Julia Moskin, that offers Korean barbecue made with USDA prime meat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prime & Beyond serves great steaks, but it also offers a rare opportunity to taste what Korean barbecue is like when made with USDA prime meat. Bulgogi (thin-sliced steak) and kalbi (short ribs) have a rich, succulent depth that you don’t often taste at the DIY BBQ joints on 32nd Street. And the burger, although plain — not a “bulgogi burger” marinated with garlic, sesame, and sugar — is fantastic, served Korean-style, with rice, kimchi, and a softly fried egg to bind all together. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing Prime & Beyond', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Korean Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T23:26:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70b1c4a1-80ef-564f-a1aa-33cbb7d691e1', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70b1c4a1-80ef-564f-a1aa-33cbb7d691e1'}, {'abstract': 'Market influences should be putting wind in deal makers’ sails, but the Deal Professor says the overall trend is that of M.&A. rushing toward a cliff.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/as-economy-goes-so-go-takeovers-even-as-bargains-abound/', 'snippet': 'Market influences should be putting wind in deal makers’ 