ntertaining/', 'snippet': 'Post the vegetarian or vegan dishes that you serve to guests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Melissa Clark offers a full vegetarian menu for a dinner party, with recipes for farro and fresh tomato soup, a harvest tart with pumpkin, roasted red peppers and olives, dandelion salad with garlic confit dressing, and other dishes. (A slide show with more vegetarian recipes for entertaining is here.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Your Favorite Vegetarian Dish for Entertaining?', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T23:53:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/736a7ab2-6c7e-5a9c-95dd-9fe87f9ced35', 'word_count': 64, 'uri': 'nyt://article/736a7ab2-6c7e-5a9c-95dd-9fe87f9ced35'}, {'abstract': 'Amid the activity overnight at Zuccotti Park, weary protesters seek rest beneath tarpaulins or wherever they can.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/nyregion/overnight-at-zuccotti-park-protesters-seek-sleep.html', 'snippet': 'Amid the activity overnight at Zuccotti Park, weary protesters seek rest beneath tarpaulins or wherever they can.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was 4:30 a.m. when Nocturnalist awoke to a kneecap hitting our shin. Mired in sleep, we were disoriented — where were we? The necrotic chill of the slab of pavement we lay on suddenly registered and we snapped awake: It was Monday at Zuccotti Park, Occupy Wall Street’s de facto headquarters. With hundreds of people flocking to the park, a half-acre plaza in the financial district where the protest movement has made its encampment for the past month, it seemed incumbent upon Nocturnalist to check out what has arguably become a hot new nightspot. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST/NOCTURNALIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST/NOCTURNALIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST/NOCTURNALIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Protest Central, Sleep, if You Can', 'kicker': 'Nocturnalist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Protest Central, Sleep, if You Can', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zuccotti Park (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-18T23:58:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b7277ea-4343-59dc-924c-ea42a2971f67', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b7277ea-4343-59dc-924c-ea42a2971f67'}, {'abstract': 'The Web 2.0 conference and the Research in Motion developers conference were a study in contrasts.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/caught-between-tw