': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:05:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ed15efb-3cda-5314-bd5b-562b2db5d8af', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ed15efb-3cda-5314-bd5b-562b2db5d8af'}, {'abstract': 'After reporting its earnings, the Bank of America gives up its place as the biggest bank in the United States by assets to JPMorgan Chase.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/bank-of-america-gives-up-its-title-as-biggest-in-u-s/', 'snippet': 'After reporting its earnings, the Bank of America gives up its place as the biggest bank in the United States by assets to JPMorgan Chase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Bank of America, it is the end of an era.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bank of America Loses Title as Biggest in U.S.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moynihan, Brian T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:07:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson D. Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96e23775-b748-55ee-b283-3105a28e17fc', 'word_count': 988, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96e23775-b748-55ee-b283-3105a28e17fc'}, {'abstract': 'In the most contentious of the debates so far, Mitt Romney came under attack from the other Republican presidential candidates, signaling the start of a tough new phase of the campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/us/politics/republican-presidential-candidates-debate-in-las-vegas.html', 'snippet': 'In the most contentious of the debates so far, Mitt Romney came under attack from the other Republican presidential candidates, signaling the start of a tough new phase of the campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Mitt Romney came under intensive attack from his rivals for the Republican presidential nomination at a debate here Tuesday night, with a newly assertive Rick Perry leading a sometimes personal barrage against him on conservative consistency, health care policy and even the immigration status of yard workers at his home.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/us/DEBATE/DEBATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/19/us/DEBATE/DEBATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/us/DEBATE/DEBATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/us/DEBATE/DEBATE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/us/DEBATE/DEBATE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fierce Clash for Romney and Perry as Republican Candidates Debate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fierce Clash for Romney and Perry as Republican Candidates Debate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:10:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg and Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad1ac075-104f-577a-bce9-99d645d16ea1', 'word_count': 1289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad1ac075-104f-577a-bce9-99d645d16ea1'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Morello, of Rage Against the Machine and The Nightwatchman, has always written protest music. It is his aesthetic, his raison d’etre his trademark.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/q-and-a-tom-morello-offers-a-record-of-rousing-hopelessness/', 'snippet': 'Tom Morello, of Rage Against the Machine and The Nightwatchman, has always written protest music. It is his aesthetic, his raison d’etre his trademark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tom Morello has always written protest music. It is his aesthetic, his raison d’etre, his trademark. His politics are famously far left and incendiary. In the 1990s, he was the guitarist and one of the ideological forces behind Rage Against the Machine, the hard rock band that did social commentary during a period in American history when few were protesting. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Tom Morello Offers ‘a Record of Rousing Hopelessness’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morello, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rage Against the Machine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:15:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41642586-a733-5bd7-a643-0cfd3d34b022', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41642586-a733-5bd7-a643-0cfd3d34b022'}, {'abstract': 'Everlast, whose real name is Erik Schrody, has a new album that presents an angry, bleak view of America on the brink of a crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/q-and-a-everlast-sees-the-ungrateful-living-all-around-him/', 'snippet': 'Everlast, whose real name is Erik Schrody, has a new album that presents an angry, bleak view of America on the brink of a crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some events change a man’s perspective. In the last three years, Everlast says, he toured Iraq to play for the troops and watched with increasing rage as old friends and family members struggled financially after the mortgage crisis and stock market crash. He also married, and he and his wife had a daughter who they learned has cystic fibrosis. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Everlast Sees the ‘Ungrateful Living’ All Around Him', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:15:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eddddeea-2348-5ff8-a836-bb96ce0466e5', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eddddeea-2348-5ff8-a836-bb96ce0466e5'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for Oct. 18, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for Oct. 18, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oct. 18, 2011', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:16:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb444fed-1817-5bf2-aaa0-c7828c1d026e', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb444fed-1817-5bf2-aaa0-c7828c1d026e'}, {'abstract': 'Ry Cooder spoke by telephone recently from his home in Santa Monica, Calif., about his new album and how it came about.  Here are edited excerpts of the conversation.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/q-and-a-ry-cooder-on-woody-guthrie-politics-and-a-new-album/', 'snippet': 'Ry Cooder spoke by telephone recently from his home in Santa Monica, Calif., about his new album and how it came about.  Here are edited excerpts of the conversation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ry Cooder’s been called a lot of things: a “musician’s musician” and a “musical archeologist”; a virtuoso of rock and blues guitar; and an explorer of international styles. But no one has ever labeled Mr. Cooder, 64, a folksinger. No one has accused him of singing protest songs and serving up social commentaries in the tradition of Woody Guthrie, Pete Seeger, Phil Ochs or Bob Dylan. Mr. Cooder’s most recent album, “Pull Up Some Dust and Sit Down” (Nonesuch), may change that perception.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Ry Cooder on Woody Guthrie, Politics and a New Album', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:16:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/601876dc-6e01-58e5-b85c-d355c873386c', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/601876dc-6e01-58e5-b85c-d355c873386c'}, {'abstract': 'The battle for Surt underscores the problem Libya’s weak transitional government faces as it tries to stitch together a country divided by the war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/world/africa/battle-for-surt-threatens-libyas-healing-process.html', 'snippet': 'The battle for Surt underscores the problem Libya’s weak transitional government faces as it tries to stitch together a country divided by the war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SURT, Libya — The commander, defying a shower of bullets, urged his men to train their heavy weapons on a nest of pro-Qaddafi snipers in a school down the street. But then someone said that the loyalists had asked to surrender, and he told his men to hold their fire. It was a hopeful moment. After weeks of violence, the fighters were exhausted, the city was destroyed and hundreds of civilians were trapped in their homes in the area.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/world/JP-SURT/JP-SURT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/19/world/JP-SURT/JP-SURT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/world/JP-SURT/JP-SURT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/world/JP-SURT/JP-SURT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/world/JP-SURT/JP-SURT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Battle for a Holdout City Stalls Healing in Libya', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Battle for a Holdout City Stalls Healing in Libya', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tripoli (Libya)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Surt (Libya)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:16:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/176f7e3e-c6e0-5008-920c-38aacd00b0be', 'word_count': 1377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/176f7e3e-c6e0-5008-920c-38aacd00b0be'}, {'abstract': 'While Mr. Leppo was the president of the department store, the company grew from 19 stores in one region to 46 stores nationwide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/business/harold-leppo-who-guided-lord-taylors-expansion-dies-at-74.html', 'snippet': 'While Mr. Leppo was the president of the department store, the company grew from 19 stores in one region to 46 stores nationwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harold Leppo, who oversaw Lord & Taylor’s expansion into a national department store chain as its president during the 1970s and ’80s, died on Friday in Stamford, Conn. He was 74. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harold Leppo, a President of Lord & Taylor, Dies at 74', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Harold Leppo, 74, a President of Lord & Taylor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lord & Taylor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:19:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/cddd156e-c7d4-504d-93c3-b1b0bc34e544', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cddd156e-c7d4-504d-93c3-b1b0bc34e544'}, {'abstract': 'Albert Pujols has been the best player in baseball since his rookie year of 2001. He will be a free agent after the season, but first there’s the World Series to attend to.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/sports/baseball/still-great-still-albert-pujols.html', 'snippet': 'Albert Pujols has been the best player in baseball since his rookie year of 2001. He will be a free agent after the season, but first there’s the World Series to attend to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — Ty Cobb hit .240 as a rookie. Willie Mays started 1 for 26. With Albert Pujols, there was no progression. From the moment he arrived in the major leagues, on opening day 2001, he was the best player in the game. Three Most Valuable Player awards and three World Series into his career, he still is.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/sports/YPUJOLS/YPUJOLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/19/sports/YPUJOLS/YPUJOLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/sports/YPUJOLS/YPUJOLS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/sports/YPUJOLS/YPUJOLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/sports/YPUJOLS/YPUJOLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Great From Day 1, Pujols Draws Superlatives On and Off the Field', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pujols, on the Cusp of Free Agency, Draws Nothing but Admiration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pujols, Albert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:21:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 