he grounds that “there is nobody in this country who got rich on his own.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/us/WARREN/WARREN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/us/WARREN/WARREN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/us/WARREN/WARREN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Candidate’s Fighting Words Draw G.O.P.’s Fire', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Candidate’s Fighting Words Draw G.O.P.’s Fire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Scott P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:33:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f40ea26e-ab08-5f2f-8b09-58abfda5e6ab', 'word_count': 987, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f40ea26e-ab08-5f2f-8b09-58abfda5e6ab'}, {'abstract': 'A new kitchen trash bag from Glad is being marketed as an easy step for consumers — it uses less plastic, but it’s stronger and costs the same as the old bag.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/business/media/glad-cuts-the-hyperbole-for-its-new-green-trash-bag.html', 'snippet': 'A new kitchen trash bag from Glad is being marketed as an easy step for consumers — it uses less plastic, but it’s stronger and costs the same as the old bag.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOW much are marketers of green products scaling back ambitious efforts to sell eco-friendlier brands as life-changers and planet-savers? Well, a line of recycled paper products, introduced by Marcal in 2009, bears the name Small Steps rather than something grander like Giant Leaps.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Glad Cuts the Hyperbole for Its New Green Trash Bag', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Glad Cuts the Hyperbole for Its New Green Trash Bag', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:34:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20392dc8-7365-5edd-996d-985081c4c74c', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20392dc8-7365-5edd-996d-985081c4c74c'}, {'abstract': 'The four major bells atop the northern towers of the Cathedral of Notre-Dame will be melted down and replaced by nine new ones. The plans have caused a small but very Parisian ruckus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/world/europe/in-paris-bells-at-notre-dame-will-be-replaced.html', 'snippet': 'The four major bells atop the northern towers of the Cathedral of Notre-Dame will be melted down and replaced by nine new ones. The plans have caused a small but very Parisian ruckus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Since 1856, the four major bells atop the northern towers of the Cathedral of Notre-Dame have rung every 15 minutes, without fail. They rang for the end of World War I and the liberation of Paris in 1944. Most recently, they chimed in honor of the victims of 9/11.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/world/PARIS-1/PARIS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/19/world/PARIS-1/PARIS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/world/PARIS-1/PARIS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/world/PARIS-1/PARIS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/world/PARIS-1/PARIS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Melodic Emblem Falls Out of Tune', 'kicker': 'Paris Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Melodic Emblem Falls Out of Tune', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Notre Dame Cathedral (Paris)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bells', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:39:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maïa de la Baume', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maïa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de la Baume', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70ad26ff-3140-59b6-a7a7-726f6f7a72dc', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70ad26ff-3140-59b6-a7a7-726f6f7a72dc'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate moved to block an Obama administration proposal to limit the amount of potatoes and other starchy vegetables that can be served in school lunches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/us/politics/potatoes-get-senate-protection-on-school-lunch-menus.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate moved to block an Obama administration proposal to limit the amount of potatoes and other starchy vegetables that can be served in school lunches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Senate stood up Tuesday for the humble white potato and rebuffed an effort by President Obama to limit its consumption by millions of schoolchildren around the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Saves the Potato on School Lunch Menus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senate Saves the Potato On School Lunch Menus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 