able in a conservative, majority Muslim country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Rev. Boon Lin Ngeo, a Malaysian Protestant pastor whose message of tolerance for homosexuals has drawn fire in his country, sat with his male partner on a lime-green sofa inside the Office of the City Clerk in New York on a late summer day, where they waited their turn to be married. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gay Pastor in New York Urges Change in Malaysia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gay Pastor in New York Urges Change in Malaysia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ngeo, Boon Lin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kuala Lumpur (Malaysia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malaysia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:56:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman and Liz Gooch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gooch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a31d958e-5ea7-53ed-b624-3fa850ae669c', 'word_count': 1088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a31d958e-5ea7-53ed-b624-3fa850ae669c'}, {'abstract': 'In his closing argument, John F. Haggerty Jr.’s lawyer tried to link Michael R. Bloomberg’s ambition to the charges against his client.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/nyregion/closing-arguments-in-theft-trial-of-john-haggerty.html', 'snippet': 'In his closing argument, John F. Haggerty Jr.’s lawyer tried to link Michael R. Bloomberg’s ambition to the charges against his client.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his closing argument on Tuesday, Dennis C. Vacco took aim at Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg, his voice rising with each sentence as he insisted that the mayor’s cohort was desperate for him to win re-election in 2009 and as he questioned the credibility of the mayor himself. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Competing Theories in Bloomberg Consultant’s Trial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Competing Theories in Bloomberg Consultant&#8217;s Trial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haggerty, John F Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:56:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71c9c89c-efd2-5d89-95fd-14ff48380e4a', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71c9c89c-efd2-5d89-95fd-14ff48380e4a'}, {'abstract': 'A witness described being framed in one of the latest round of corruption cases involving police officers and drugs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/nyregion/witness-narrates-frame-up-in-police-corruption-trial.html', 'snippet': 'A witness described being framed in one of the latest round of corruption cases involving police officers and drugs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because Yvelisse DeLeon of Coney Island was due at an interview for a bartending job on the evening of Jan. 25, 2007, she spent part of the afternoon getting herself ready. That process included a trip to Downtown Brooklyn.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Story of Drugs and the Police', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Story Of Drugs And the Police', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption in Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T01:59:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/891c727e-f47e-541c-a5b1-40d87d2d9769', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/891c727e-f47e-541c-a5b1-40d87d2d9769'}, {'abstract': 'Day 3, in which I present you all with a useful gift.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/day-three-contest/', 'snippet': 'Day 3, in which I present you all with a useful gift.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Administrivial Heads Up For Friday! The Friday, October 21 crossword puzzle will be available at the normal time and place, but will have a format that will not be available in Across Lite.\xa0However, we will be offering a PDF version that you will need to print out to solve. That version will be available here on the blog and the Premium Puzzle Page on Thursday, October 20 at 10 p.m. Eastern time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday: Day Three of the Crossword Contest', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T02:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22c2ee6f-49f1-5324-83fb-934782a8c108', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22c2ee6f-49f1-5324-83fb-934782a8c108'}, {'abstract': 'A petition meant to protest cuts in school aid was revised to seek the end of job protection based on teacher seniority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/nyregion/revision-of-new-yorkers-petition-for-teachers-jobs-is-criticized.html', 'snippet': 'A petition meant to protest cuts in school aid was revised to seek the end of job protection based on teacher seniority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It all began with a parent’s suggestion: Why not draft a petition for parents and students to sign and send to Albany protesting cuts in state aid to city schools?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inquiry Faults Cit