ty Council speaker, said that she was not “anti-Wall Street” but that the anger of the Occupy Wall Street protesters should not be ignored.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/nyregion/christine-quinn-wants-balanced-response-to-occupy-wall-street.html', 'snippet': 'Christine C. Quinn, the City Council speaker, said that she was not “anti-Wall Street” but that the anger of the Occupy Wall Street protesters should not be ignored.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Speaking on Tuesday before an audience composed largely of business leaders, Christine C. Quinn, the City Council speaker, said that she was not “anti-Wall Street” but that the anger of the Occupy Wall Street protesters should not be ignored.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quinn Says City Must Find Balance in Response to Protests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quinn Says City Must Find Balance in Response to Protests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T02:04:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe5970aa-a632-51b0-bf0b-7c26cd4ab41c', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe5970aa-a632-51b0-bf0b-7c26cd4ab41c'}, {'abstract': 'In Munster, Ind., a school system turned to laptops and interactive computer programs in a million-dollar digital makeover that included a rental laptop for every student.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/education/19textbooks.html', 'snippet': 'In Munster, Ind., a school system turned to laptops and interactive computer programs in a million-dollar digital makeover that included a rental laptop for every student.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUNSTER, Ind. — Laura Norman used to ask her seventh-grade scientists to take out their textbooks and flip to Page Such-and-Such. Now, she tells them to take out their laptops.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/us/TEXTBOOK/TEXTBOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/19/us/TEXTBOOK/TEXTBOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/us/TEXTBOOK/TEXTBOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/us/TEXTBOOK/TEXTBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/us/TEXTBOOK/TEXTBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Out With Textbooks, in With Laptops for an Indiana School District', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Out With Textbooks, In With Laptops for an Indiana School District', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laptop Computers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T02:07:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Schwarz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwarz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03b51e35-d61b-5e6d-bfa8-06a13b121cc9', 'word_count': 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03b51e35-d61b-5e6d-bfa8-06a13b121cc9'}, {'abstract': 'We know we are descended from somewhere, but who would have suspected it was by way of a fish that used electrical currents to hunt and communicate?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/opinion/an-electrifying-ancestor.html', 'snippet': 'We know we are descended from somewhere, but who would have suspected it was by way of a fish that used electrical currents to hunt and communicate?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Evolutionary biologists at Cornell University have found that most land vertebrates — including humans — are descended from a predatory fish that lived hundreds of millions of years ago and could sense electrical fields in its environment. Soon, in evolutionary terms, the lineage of that fish split in two. One line led to fish that still retain a sophisticated electro-sensing apparatus, like the North American paddlefish. The other line led to land vertebrates — including us — that have lost the ability to detect weak electrical currents without calling the electrician.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Electrifying Ancestor', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Electrifying Ancestor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evolution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornell University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T02:07:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/33a10376-c8f5-5d69-a0df-e21bae5cf69e', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33a10376-c8f5-5d69-a0df-e21bae5cf69e'}, {'abstract': 'As investment banks pull back from a volatile commercial mortgage market, life insurance companies are moving in, expanding their lending.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/realestate/commercial/insurers-see-an-opening-in-commercial-mortgages.html', 'snippet': 'As investment banks pull back from a volatile commercial mortgage market, life insurance companies are moving in, expanding their lending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past several months, the commercial mortgage market has been volatile, plagued by weak investor appetite, wary lenders and warnings by ratings agencies of increasing risk. But one bright spot is emerging, as life insurance companies have taken advantage of the lull to become major lenders. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/Insure/Insure-articleLarge.jpg',