o shops, but New York City officials say they have made progress on a $3 billion revitalization proposal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/realestate/commercial/willets-point-redevelopment-takes-a-step-forward.html', 'snippet': 'Willets Point has long been home to an unsightly jumble of auto shops, but New York City officials say they have made progress on a $3 billion revitalization proposal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Willets Point, the unsightly jumble of auto shops in northeastern Queens, looks pretty much as it did in May 2007, when Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg announced plans for a $3 billion mixed-use development on the site — with the notable exception that Citi Field, the new home of the New York Mets, now looms over it. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/Willets/Willets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/19/business/Willets/Willets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/Willets/Willets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/Willets/Willets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/business/Willets/Willets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Queens, Neglected Sector Attracts Big Developers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Queens, Neglected Sector Attracts Big Developers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Willets Point (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T02:09:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terry Pristin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pristin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6156f7c1-b5c8-50b9-956b-612623be6edf', 'word_count': 1254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6156f7c1-b5c8-50b9-956b-612623be6edf'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Mullen, a lawyer, drove the law firm of Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom from a small, specialized firm to a fixture in the top tier of the corporate bar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/business/peter-mullen-a-force-behind-skadden-arps-dies-at-83.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Mullen, a lawyer, drove the law firm of Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom from a small, specialized firm to a fixture in the top tier of the corporate bar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter P. Mullen joined the Manhattan law firm of Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom in 1961, when it consisted of just 10 lawyers; when he stepped down as its de facto chief executive in 1994, it had more than 1,000, and was one of the world’s richest and most prominent firms.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/MULLEN-obit/MULLEN-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/MULLEN-obit/MULLEN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/business/MULLEN-obit/MULLEN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Mullen, Power at a Leading Law Firm, Dies at 83', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peter Mullen, Power at a Leading Law Firm, Dies at 83', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skadden Arps Slate Meagher & Flom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T02:16:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Williams Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Williams', 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/0812cf23-3034-58a3-8952-8c8d626cab18', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0812cf23-3034-58a3-8952-8c8d626cab18'}, {'abstract': 'What drives a young Brooklyn writer to don a Civil War-era uniform, musket and all?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/18/confessions-of-a-rookie-re-enactor/', 'snippet': 'What drives a young Brooklyn writer to don a Civil War-era uniform, musket and all?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The First Battle of Bull Run, like freshman year of college, was a time for earning reputations — and nicknames. On that same afternoon when Confederate Gen. Thomas Jonathan Jackson won his moniker, “Stonewall,” he bestowed an equally flattering reputation on a Union regiment called the 14th Brooklyn, which wore red wool trousers as part of their local militia uniform modeled after the French chasseurs. The 14th Brooklyn — the only regiment in the Union Army called by a city’s name rather than a state — was giving Jackson and his troops quite a time on Henry House Hill, and at some point Stonewall braced his soldiers for yet another charge by shouting “Hold on Boys! Here come those red-legged devils again!” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Confessions of a Rookie Re-Enactor', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camps and Camping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T02:28:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Dellinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dellinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bca7e7a5-badd-5529-8887-5dda540adff4', 'word_count': 1680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bca7e7a5-badd-5529-8887-5dda540adff4'}, {'abstract': 'Rupert Murdoch reached his boiling point last winter, a former official said, and delivered a blunt ultimatum to his son James: “You’re coming back to New York, or you’re out.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/business/media/murdochs-infighting-clouds-future-of-news-corp.html', 'snippet': 'Rupert Murdoch reached his boiling point last winter, a former official said, and delivered a blunt ultimatum to his son James: “You’re coming back to New York, or you’re out.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — It was a striking display of unity: Rupert and James Murdoch, father and son, walking side by side through central London as they faced a crisis that had laid siege to their company. Pushing through a crush of paparazzi on a street not far from Buckingham Palace, James reached out to place a reassuring hand on his father’s back. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/media/MURDOCH/MURDOCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/19/business/media/MURDOCH/MURDOCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/media/MURDOCH/MURDOCH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 585, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/business/media/MURDOCH/MURDOCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/business/media/MURDOCH/MURDOCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Rift Between Murdochs, Heir Becomes Less Apparent', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Rift Between Murdochs, Heir Becomes Less Apparent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Lachlan'