 on Mitt Romney concerning illegal immigration, and analysts contested Herman Cain’s conclusion about his tax plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rick Perry’s most pointed attack against Mitt Romney in Tuesday night’s debate concerned an immigration matter that came to light when Mr. Romney was campaigning for president four years ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Lawn Care History and the Fight Over Immigration', 'kicker': 'Check Point', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romney’s Lawn Care and the Fight Over Immigration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T02:43:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston, Binyamin Appelbaum and Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b42e4d7d-98c5-5c8f-9f12-45c9acf4752f', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b42e4d7d-98c5-5c8f-9f12-45c9acf4752f'}, {'abstract': 'Chart shows the ratio of total mortgage debt to property value in major metropolitan areas of the U.S.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/10/19/business/more-mortgage-debt-than-property-value.html', 'snippet': 'Chart shows the ratio of total mortgage debt to property value in major metropolitan areas of the U.S.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chart shows the ratio of total mortgage debt to property value in major metropolitan areas of the U.S.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Mortgage Debt Than Property Value', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T03:01:04+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/8ad62a84-faae-5576-ab3b-022d1aca919f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/8ad62a84-faae-5576-ab3b-022d1aca919f'}, {'abstract': 'Two airliners landed in error in March after the lone tower controller on a midnight shift fell asleep and regional officials reacted incorrectly, a federal investigation concluded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/us/report-faults-sleeping-and-awake-controllers.html', 'snippet': 'Two airliners landed in error in March after the lone tower controller on a midnight shift fell asleep and regional officials reacted incorrectly, a federal investigation concluded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two airliners landed in error at Reagan National Airport on March 23 after the lone tower controller on a midnight shift fell asleep and regional officials reacted incorrectly, a federal investigation concluded. As air traffic managers tried to figure out why the tower was not responding, a regional controller left the pilots of the incoming flights with the erroneous impression that they could land using rules for airports with unmanned towers, the National Transportation Safety Board said in a report Tuesday. The planes landed safely. The board blamed the tower controller’s fatigue and the Federal Aviation Administration’s scheduling practices for the incident. The F.A.A. has since revamped scheduling, assigned at least two controllers to every tower overnight and revised the guidelines for when a tower does not respond. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Faults Sleeping and Awake Controllers', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Faults Sleeping and Awake Controllers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fatigue', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Aviation Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald, Washington National Airport', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Transportation Safety Board', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T03:01:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'orga