s-what-passes-for-an-inspirational-supergroup-at-cmj/', 'snippet': 'On Tuesday night, that act vacuuming up all the attention at CMJ was Wild Flag, a new band comprised of members of old bands, that also sounds like many recent bands who have looked to those old bands for inspiration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year’s CMJ Music Marathon feels light in established acts, those midlevel bands who are used to the grind of this festival and make it an essential part of their tour schedule. What’s left is an agglomeration of small acts, and smaller acts, with the occasional boldface name screaming loudly from beneath the pile.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wild Flag Is What Passes for an Inspirational Supergroup at CMJ', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'CMJ Music Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brownstein, Carrie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiss, Janet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bowery Ballroom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dum Dum Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sleater-Kinney', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wild Flag (Music Group)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T11:45:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0532e338-8b9c-545c-9f20-1172861fe121', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0532e338-8b9c-545c-9f20-1172861fe121'}, {'abstract': 'Led by a pair of filmmakers from Brooklyn, more than 50 people from more than a dozen American cities are pooling material for a feature-length film about the nascent movement.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/coming-attractions-occupy-wall-st-the-documentary/', 'snippet': 'Led by a pair of filmmakers from Brooklyn, more than 50 people from more than a dozen American cities are pooling material for a feature-length film about the nascent movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Occupy Wall Street, the protest movement that began in Lower Manhattan and quickly spread across the country and around the world, might be coming to a theater near you.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coming Attractions: Occupy Wall St., the Documentary', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kickstarter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T11:45:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Wall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b82e87dd-ece7-51d2-bec6-fdba68f60419', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b82e87dd-ece7-51d2-bec6-fdba68f60419'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Lopez will help his “Book of Mormon” collaborators Trey Parker and Matt Stone write an episode of their animated series “South Park” that is planned for next week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/south-park-provides-the-stage-for-a-book-of-mormon-reunion/', 'snippet': 'Robert Lopez will help his “Book of Mormon” collaborators Trey Parker and Matt Stone write an episode of their animated series “South Park” that is planned for next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’d like to see what happens when Trey Parker, Matt Stone and Robert Lopez combine their comic talents but can’t get your hands on tickets for their bawdy, blaspheming Broadway hit, “The Book of Mormon,” cable television will soon provide a more easily accessible alternative.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘South Park’ Provides the Stage for a ‘Book of Mormon’ Reunion', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Trey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stone, Matt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T12:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50916a03-ad6e-5c19-b664-0a9d9fe3206a', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50916a03-ad6e-5c19-b664-0a9d9fe3206a'}, {'abstract': 'Marie Dedieu, a disabled Frenchwoman kidnapped by Somali gunmen in Kenya this month, has died in captivity, the French government announced Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/world/africa/french-woman-abducted-in-kenya-dies.html', 'snippet': 'Marie Dedieu, a disabled Frenchwoman kidnapped by Somali gunmen in Kenya this month, has died in captivity, the French government announced Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — A disabled Frenchwoman kidnapped by Somali gunmen in Kenya this month has died in captivity, the French government announced Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/world/20kenya/20kenya-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/world/20kenya/20kenya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/world/20kenya/20kenya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Frenchwoman Abducted in Kenya Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Frenchwoman Abducted in Kenya Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ali, Abdiweli Mohamed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dedieu, Marie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T12:04:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization'