nomination fight between Rick Perry and Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/debate-suggests-brutish-campaign-to-come/', 'snippet': 'Tuesday night’s debate raised the prospect of a nasty, brutish and potentially long nomination fight between Rick Perry and Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:55 p.m. | Updated Rick Perry and Mitt Romney braced Wednesday for a new, more aggressive phase in their presidential rivalry after a debate Tuesday night in which both men made clear how deep the personal animosity between them goes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debate Suggests Brutish Campaign to Come', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T12:07:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear and Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8ccdb61-7e58-535a-b457-44e6c89b80f1', 'word_count': 1318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8ccdb61-7e58-535a-b457-44e6c89b80f1'}, {'abstract': 'By breaking off its research pharmaceutical business, Abbott Laboratories will follow others that have turned to corporate breakups to bolster shareholder value.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/abbott-to-split-into-two/', 'snippet': 'By breaking off its research pharmaceutical business, Abbott Laboratories will follow others that have turned to corporate breakups to bolster shareholder value.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:01 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abbott Labs to Split Into 2 Companies', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Abbott Laboratories', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T12:12:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced and Bruce Japsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Japsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4a60c52-fae2-5202-8e9e-99eb0617a63d', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4a60c52-fae2-5202-8e9e-99eb0617a63d'}, {'abstract': 'Olympus acknowledged paying advisory fees totaling $687 million, partly confirming claims made by its former chief.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/business/global/olympus-backtracks-on-payments.html', 'snippet': 'Olympus acknowledged paying advisory fees totaling $687 million, partly confirming claims made by its former chief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — The Japanese camera maker Olympus acknowledged Wednesday that it had paid $687 million in advisory fees for its acquisition of a British medical equipment company. In doing so, the company seemed to back off statements it had made a day earlier and to partly confirm claims made by its former chief executive. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Olympus in Apparent Reversal on Payments to Advisers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Olympus in Apparent Reversal on Payments to Advisers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Olympus Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T12:19:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f35e5101-a03b-5c0a-add3-22a3d25bfaae', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f35e5101-a03b-5c0a-add3-22a3d25bfaae'}, {'abstract': 'What to ask a prospective wealth adviser, home prices feed consumer gloom, a security app for iPhones and other consumer focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/wednesday-reading-what-to-ask-a-financial-adviser/', 'snippet': 'What to ask a prospective wealth adviser, home prices feed consumer gloom, a security app for iPhones and other consumer focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday Reading: What to Ask a Financial Adviser', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T12:22:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cf78391-1e77-5b30-9668-efe0b53d08da', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cf78391-1e77-5b30-9668-efe0b53d08da'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: In the course of an average day, all too many of my fellow 99 percenters are not keeping faith with their own kind. Also, what City Room is reading in other newspapers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/solidarity-99-percent-elusive/', 'snippet': 'The Day: In the course of an average day, all too many of my fellow 99 percenters are not keeping faith with their own kind. Also, what City Room is reading in other newspapers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a lifelong member of the group now known as the 99 percent, and also as someone who hasn’t a prayer of ever breaking into the 1 percent, I know that I should feel a bond with every 99 percenter out there. I know the troubles created by that 1 percent. I’ve been to Zuccotti Park. I get it: 99 = good, 1 = bad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Solidarity: 99 Percent Elusive', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zuccotti Park (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T12:36:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dbc9da7-767f-5c76-8078-66d28475b2af', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dbc9da7-767f-5c76-8078-66d28475b2af'}, {'abstract': 'In the United States an “American Idol”-style competition reality series from Jennifer Lopez and Marc Anthony will premiere next year on Univision.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/jennifer-lopezs-talent-show-finds-u-s-home-on-univision/', 'snippet': 'In the United States an “American Idol”-style competition reality series from Jennifer Lopez and Marc Anthony will premiere next year on Univision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The marriage may be ending but the show goes on for Jennifer Lopez and Marc Anthony. The duo has sold their television series “¡Q’Viva! The Chosen” to 21 broadcast networks internationally. On Wednesday, the first three broadcast network deals were announced by the show’s producer, XIX Entertainment, the company of Simon Fuller, the creator of “American Idol.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jennifer Lopez’s Talent Show Finds U.S. Home on Univision', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, MARC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Jennifer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Univision', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T12:47:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', '