ll-settles-in-for-world-series-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'With the World Series set to begin, writers suggest how to speed up baseball, report on the contrasting styles of the two managers and ponder Albert Pujols’s next move.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Considering we live in the era of 700 television channels, iPhone movie-watching, countless hours stolen by Facebook and video games and, well, you get the picture, it is hardly stunning that the World Series has tumbled down the entertainment ladder and now looks up enviously at episodes of “Dancing With the Stars.” And considering the World Series, which begins on Wednesday night — you did know that, right? — will feature St. Louis Manager Tony La Russa spending at least 47 minutes pondering pitching changes and double switches, baseball might consider staging a few dance numbers to keep its loyal watchers from lapsing into comas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baseball’s Place in a Fast-Moving World', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Baseball’s Place in a Fast-Moving World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Raiders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Stars', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Flyers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Bengals', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Carson', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'la Russa, Tony', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'