uccotti Park, where the Chock Full o’ Nuts chain held out 13 years and delayed the completion of the privately built park.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/holding-out-at-zuccotti-park-is-a-44-year-old-tradition/', 'snippet': 'A history of resistance underlies Zuccotti Park, where the Chock Full o’ Nuts chain held out 13 years and delayed the completion of the privately built park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Resistance runs deep at Zuccotti Park. You might even say it’s in the ground. The protesters clinging tenaciously to that little parcel in Lower Manhattan owe a big spiritual debt to Chock Full o’ Nuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holding Out at Zuccotti Park Is a 44-Year-Old Tradition', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALPERN, ANDREW', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Black, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Chock Full o'Nuts", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Durst Organization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zuccotti Park (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T16:01:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/687024a5-68ff-5af2-b6ea-bb27c8fcb08a', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/687024a5-68ff-5af2-b6ea-bb27c8fcb08a'}, {'abstract': 'The Pew Environment Group issued a series of often-graphic photographs taken in Taiwan, which along with Indonesia, India and Spain, are among the world’s most active participants in mutilating sharks.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/a-snapshot-of-shark-finning/', 'snippet': 'The Pew Environment Group issued a series of often-graphic photographs taken in Taiwan, which along with Indonesia, India and Spain, are among the world’s most active participants in mutilating sharks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The global campaign in defense of sharks has picked up considerably in the last two or three years. What was once a niche issue — a sharp decline in shark populations because of soaring demand for their fins in parts of Asia — has gone mainstream. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Snapshot of Shark Finning', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sharks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Environment Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T16:06:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bettina Wassener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f9496a7-146f-5740-b00b-4b367b827ebb', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f9496a7-146f-5740-b00b-4b367b827ebb'}, {'abstract': 'Larry Rohter discusses the horror films of José Mojica Marins, otherwise known as Coffin Joe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/100000001122080/coffin-joe-lives-on.html', 'snippet': 'Larry Rohter discusses the horror films of José Mojica Marins, otherwise known as Coffin Joe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Larry Rohter discusses the horror films of José Mojica Marins, otherwise known as Coffin Joe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/multimedia/video-ab-coffinjoe/video-ab-coffinjoe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/19/multimedia/video-ab-coffinjoe/video-ab-coffinjoe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/19/multimedia/video-ab-coffinjoe/video-ab-coffinjoe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/19/multimedia/video-ab-coffinjoe/video-ab-coffinjoe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Coffin Joe Lives On', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T16:08:26+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Gabe Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/921a1e12-60b3-56a5-b02b-6b9e5c896347', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/921a1e12-60b3-56a5-b02b-6b9e5c896347'}, {'abstract': 'A teacher who had been at the prestigious New York City private school for 11 years was fired for comments to students that he said were perceived by some as racist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/nyregion/firing-at-ethical-culture-fieldston-school-prompts-outcry.html', 'snippet': 'A teacher who had been at the prestigious New York City private school for 11 years was fired for comments to students that he said were perceived by some as racist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are perhaps few schools in the nation with as progressive a pedigree as Ethical Culture Fieldston School, where students are not only expected to live the values of tolerance and inclusion, but also to make the world more tolerant and inclusive. Half those in the school’s kindergarten classes this year are minority students, with Fieldston leading a push for diversity among New York’s elite private schools. The new head of school, Damian Fernandez, an openly gay Latino, began the year promising a deeper commitment to the school’s liberal roots in ethical learning. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Fieldston School, Division Over the Dismissal of a Popular but Polarizing Teacher', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Fieldston School, Division Over the Dismissal of a Popular but Polarizing Teacher', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ETHICAL CULTURE FIELDSTON SCHOOL', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sirmon, Barry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T16:11:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenny Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92da5482-f97b-5474-ac33-a7c203a5a160', 'word_count': 1139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92da5482-f97b-5474-ac33-a7c203a5a160'}, {'abstract': 'The company agreed to settle a complaint by the S.E.C. that it had defrauded buyers in a $1 billion portfolio of mortgage-related investments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/business/citigroup-to-pay-285-million-to-settle-sec-charges.html', 'snippet': 'The company agreed to settle a complaint by the S.E.C. that it had defrauded buyers in a $1 billion portfolio of mortgage-related investments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As the housing market began its collapse, Wall Street firms and sophisticated investors searched for ways to profit. Some of them found an easy method: Stuff a portfolio with risky mortgage-related investments, sell it to unsuspecting customers and bet against it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/us/20citi-pic/20citi-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/us/20citi-pic/20citi-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/us/20citi-pic/20citi-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Citigroup to Pay Millions to Close Fraud Complaint', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Citigroup to Pay Millions to End Fraud Complaint', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Credit Suisse Group AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T16:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9148ee33-bc8d-5f59-90f6-54e9a59a41d4', 'word_count': 1099, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9148ee33-bc8d-5f59-90f6-54e9a59a41d4'}, {'abstract': 'A master of gore, the filmmaker José Mojica Marins is known for his alter ego, Coffin Joe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/movies/jose-mojica-marins-brazilian-filmmaker-conjures-macabre.html', 'snippet': 'A master of gore, the filmmaker José Mojica Marins is known for his alter ego, Coffin Joe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SÃO PAULO, Brazil —\xa0 SEATED on a sofa in the living room of his modest apartment here, dressed in shorts and flip-flops, José Mojica Marins seems inoffensive. He is mild mannered and soft-spoken, and nothing suggests he has made a career of writing, acting in and directing provocative horror movies with titles like “Hallucinations of a Deranged Mind.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cult Figure Conjures the Macabre', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Cult Figure Conjures the Macabre', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T16:13:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a6a40e7-cf97-5d84-b716-5a5b26a7ee51', 'word_count': 1632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a6a40e7-cf97-5d84-b716-5a5b26a7ee51'}, {'abstract': 'With the unemployment rate around 9 percent, many small businesses struggle to understand the jobless benefits system, which is complex and varies by state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/business/smallbusiness/managing-unemployment-premiums-in-a-time-of-joblessness.html', 'snippet': 'With the unemployment rate around 9 percent, many small businesses struggle to understand the jobless benefits system, which is complex and varies by state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mary White opened her unemployment insurance statement in August and saw that her account had been docked for a claim from an employee who had quit more than a year before, she was baffled.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/business/smallbusiness/20sbiz-span/20siz-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/business/smallbusiness/20sbiz-span/20sbiz-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/business/smallbusiness/20sbiz-span/20sbiz-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Jobless Claims Rise, Businesses Try to Manage the Burden of Benefits', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Jobless Claims Rise, Businesses Try to Manage The Burden of Benefits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T16:22:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Mount', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mount', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e59dc7f9-6359-5269-881e-c1267d6447d8', 'word_count': 1234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e59dc7f9-6359-5269-881e-c1267d6447d8'}, {'abstract': 'The United States will resume stalled talks with North Korea and has appointed an envoy with a background in nuclear issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/world/asia/united-states-looks-ready-to-re-engage-north-korea.html', 'snippet': 'The United States will resume stalled talks with North Korea and has appointed an envoy with a background in nuclear issues.', 'lead_