id': 'nyt://article/bb56ca79-c3ae-53f5-8390-19bed8475fb2', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb56ca79-c3ae-53f5-8390-19bed8475fb2'}, {'abstract': 'Cuckoo Chaos and Gauntlet Hair exceed a critic’s first-night expectations at the CMJ Music Marathon.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/a-couple-of-good-bands-buoy-cmjs-opening-night/', 'snippet': 'Cuckoo Chaos and Gauntlet Hair exceed a critic’s first-night expectations at the CMJ Music Marathon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first day of the CMJ Music Marathon is for lowering expectations. I’m spoiled because most of the shows I hear during the year are by bands that have already gotten somewhere — even if it’s only to an opening-act slot with some indie-label pals — and are playing clubs that expect people to listen. The beauty and aggravation of CMJ is that it’s a plunge into the lower echelons, the ones triaged out of my usual schedule. This is the province of peculiar club layouts, blaringly murky sound systems and disheveled guys in yesterday’s T-shirt poking at their keyboard and mixer, wishing they were Erasure circa 1989. I start to wonder if the next five days are going to be like that. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Couple of Good Bands Buoy CMJ’s Opening Night', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'CMJ Music Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANIMAL COLLECTIVE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Erasure', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vampire Weekend', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T19:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', '