le headquarters on Wednesday was, like so many of the Apple product introductions that Mr. Jobs presided over, a musical affair.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coldplay and Norah Jones Play at Memorial for Jobs', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Norah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newman, Randy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T20:19:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/157d87b1-de1e-5d14-8be3-6d037dfffc61', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/157d87b1-de1e-5d14-8be3-6d037dfffc61'}, {'abstract': 'The first stage of the three-part renovation of Madison Square Garden included new concourse areas and some improvements few fans will see.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/touring-the-renovated-garden-to-be-continued/', 'snippet': 'The first stage of the three-part renovation of Madison Square Garden included new concourse areas and some improvements few fans will see.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The oddest part of seeing the first part of the three-part renovation of Madison Square Garden is traveling from the familiar lobby (which will not be done until Year 3), up the same old escalators (untouched until at least next year) and through the doors into the new main concourse, and feeling as if you’ve stepped into another building entirely.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Touring the Renovated Madison Square Garden (to Be Continued)', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T20:23:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bef974d-433d-56d5-83f7-f48949312853', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bef974d-433d-56d5-83f7-f48949312853'}, {'abstract': 'The daily deal site is preparing for an investor road show for its planned initial public offering, with a valuation sharply below initial expectations.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/groupon-seeks-12-billion-valuation/', 'snippet': 'The daily deal site is preparing for an investor road show for its planned initial public offering, with a valuation sharply below initial expectations.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:05 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Groupon May Value Itself in I.P.O. at Close to $12 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mason, Andrew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Groupon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T20:28:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli and Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a58a2e05-febe-530b-a846-167eaa4572c8', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a58a2e05-febe-530b-a846-167eaa4572c8'}, {'abstract': 'Ekblad’s creations — crude and polished, blithe and bold — offer perspectives on modern art and culture, with and without a capital M.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/frieze-frame-ida-ekblads-ruckus/', 'snippet': 'Ekblad’s creations — crude and polished, blithe and bold — offer perspectives on modern art and culture, with and without a capital M.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ida Ekblad is at once a sculptor, painter, video maker and poet. Her motley creations — crude and polished, blithe and bold — offer perspectives on modern art and culture, with and without a capital M. Her sculpture reaches back to beatific tropes of postwar art history, which she solders together with the harsh trash of today’s world: industrial materials (scrap metal is a favorite) collected from streets and junkyards. Her paintings marry similar sentiments, committing the intangible debris of brutish shapes and colors to canvas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Frieze Frame | Ida Ekblad’s Ruckus', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T20:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1ae4894-b019-557d-aea0-64637102df72', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1ae4894-b019-557d-aea0-64637102df72'}, {'abstract': 'At a news conference, State Senator Eric Adams said that he and other city leaders had asked Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. to investigate the police three months ago, and hadn’t heard back.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/officials-renew-call-for-u-s-review-of-stop-and-frisk-policy/', 'snippet': 'At a news conference, State Senator Eric Adams said that he and other city leaders had asked Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. to investigate the police three months ago, and hadn’t heard back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The case against a New York City police officer charged with falsely arresting a black man on Staten Island in April has given new attention to the call for a federal civil rights inquiry into the Police Department’s controversial stop, question and frisk policy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officials Renew Call for U.S. Review of Stop and Frisk Policy', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T20:33:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e59c24e-2b45-5a14-a41d-b82eaff21962', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e59c24e-2b45-5a14-a41d-b82eaff21962'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Greece, Libya, Britain and Egypt.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/pictures-of-the-day-greece-and-elsewhere-7/', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Greece, Libya,