s of the World, said he knew the company’s claim that the practice was limited to one “rogue reporter” was untrue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — News International, Rupert Murdoch’s British newspaper company, knew the practice of phone hacking was widespread at the News of the World newspaper as early as 2008, a lawyer who acted for the company told lawmakers here Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News International Knew of Broader Hacking in 2008, Lawmakers Are Told', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Company Knew of More Hacking, Lawyer Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News International Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pike, Julian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T21:02:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e7a9186-a778-57fb-b1d7-69f4f59d788b', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e7a9186-a778-57fb-b1d7-69f4f59d788b'}, {'abstract': 'Too much information.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/more-uk-inflation/', 'snippet': 'Too much information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Too much information, I know. B