aragraph': 'ASADABAD, Afghanistan — American and Afghan troops have killed at least 115 insurgents as part of a tough fight to gain control of a critical corridor and resupply route to a key American base in northeastern Afghanistan, according to Afghan and American military officers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/world/asia/20afghanistan-map/20afghanistan-map-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 198, 'width': 408, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. and Afghan Troops Battle to Control Key Route', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. and Afghan Troops Battle to Control Crucial Route', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T21:33:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin and Sharifullah Sahak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sharifullah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sahak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c202786-7de1-51da-92b1-cf7eabe1391d', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c202786-7de1-51da-92b1-cf7eabe1391d'}, {'abstract': 'Eve Ashcraft, an architectural color consultant, likes to paint, and repaint, her East Village apartment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/10/20/garden/220111020-COLOR.html', 'snippet': 'Eve Ashcraft, an architectural color consultant, likes to paint, and repaint, her East Village apartment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eve Ashcraft, an architectural color consultant, likes to paint, and repaint, her East Village apartment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Paint Whisperer at Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paint', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T21:35:54+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Home & Garden', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/718faf99-9f61-5a3f-bcb0-3f5041d33d92', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/718faf99-9f61-5a3f-bcb0-3f5041d33d92'}, {'abstract': 'Ask the critics about cast changes, “The X Factor” and anything else in the television universe.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/tv-chat-ask-the-critics-4/', 'snippet': 'Ask the critics about cast changes, “The X Factor” and anything else in the television universe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, the critic Mike Hale took a look at a spate of major cast changes in prime time and came up with a report card on how the shows — “Two and a Half Men,” “CSI,” “The Office,” “Law & Order: SVU” and “House” — are handling the new characters. Only “CSI” got an A, while “Two and a Half Men” received a cringe-worthy D. But the critic Neil Genzlinger says he actually enjoys the Ashton Kutcher version of “Men.” How would you grade the shifts? Then there’s “The X Factor,” which is doing well with the 18-to-49 demographic but not with Mr. Genzlinger, who has some issues. Is there any “reality” in that reality competition or is Simon Cowell orchestrating everything? And what to make of the American Academy of Pediatrics warning, yet again, that parents should limit the amount of time infants and toddlers spend in front of the television screen? Are you suffering the effects of too much TV watching as a baby? You asked and the critics answered your questions:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TV Chat: Ask the Critics', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T21:44:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcc071eb-9e18-5748-8c73-466bf8b9501a', 'word_count': 1842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcc071eb-9e18-5748-8c73-466bf8b9501a'}, {'abstract': 'An especially focused palette of whites and creams permeated a lot of the shows.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/spring-ahead-white/', 'snippet': 'An especially focused palette of whites and creams permeated a lot of the shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A snapshot of spring’s best trends and a hint at what you’ll want to wear next year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spring Ahead | White', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T21:46:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Miesmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miesmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organizati