ening of June 24, in Paris, men’s fashion writers sat down for the spring Givenchy show at the Pompidou Center. Chairs had been arranged in the street-level lobby, and by the time the show began — an arrow of scowling men in bird of paradise prints — an audience had formed outside the windows as well.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/fashion/20GROOMS_SPAN/20GROOMS_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/20/fashion/20GROOMS_SPAN/20GROOMS_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/fashion/20GROOMS_SPAN/20GROOMS_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/fashion/20GROOMS_SPAN/20GROOMS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/fashion/20GROOMS_SPAN/20GROOMS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Here Come the (Stylish) Grooms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Here Come the (Stylish) Grooms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T21:57:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn and Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f045541f-1664-533a-bf2b-b1b90fef9e1a', 'word_count': 1479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f045541f-1664-533a-bf2b-b1b90fef9e1a'}, {'abstract': 'Obama administration officials on Wednesday denied Iranian news reports that Gholam Shakuri is an agent of Mujahedeen Khalq, a group Iran regards as a terrorist organization.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/world/middleeast/obama-administration-denies-iran-claims-that-saudi-plot-defendant-gholam-shakuri-belongs-to-exile-group.html', 'snippet': 'Obama administration officials on Wednesday denied Iranian news reports that Gholam Shakuri is an agent of Mujahedeen Khalq, a group Iran regards as a terrorist organization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Obama administration officials on Wednesday denied Iranian news reports that a man charged in a plot to assassinate the Saudi ambassador to the United States is actually an agent of an exiled Iranian opposition group.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Denies Iran Claims That Saudi Plot Defendant Belongs to Exile Group', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Denies Iran Claims About Suspect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mujahedeen Khalq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakuri, Gholam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Quds Force', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic Revolutionary Guards Corps', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T21:58:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35f64b1d-96df-5b17-ab52-e094d111b472', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35f64b1d-96df-5b17-ab52-e094d111b472'}, {'abstract': 'Nika Roza Danilova, who performs as Zola Jesus, showed a powerful voice that’s rare for pop at the Knitting Factory on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/arts/music/zola-jesus-at-the-knitting-factory-review.html', 'snippet': 'Nika Roza Danilova, who performs as Zola Jesus, showed a powerful voice that’s rare for pop at the Knitting Factory on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nika Roza Danilova, the singer who performs as Zola Jesus, seems single-minded, and her show on Tuesday night at the Knitting Factory was a unity. She had written the songs and programmed the synthesizers, played by three musicians, which blended thickly together over a drummer’s dry tribal rhythms. Her body language, except for basic bobbing, was arm and hand movements to signify her voice’s rising tones and crescendos. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mul