izes in what your average HGTV design-show host calls “pops of color.” How about a big flower arrangement, hand-painted, erupting all over your dress? Some blue and black tiger-striped bedsheets? Bright lunchboxes for your wee ones with elephants on them?', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/fashion/20CRITIC1_SPAN/20CRITIC1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/20/fashion/20CRITIC1_SPAN/20CRITIC1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/fashion/20CRITIC1_SPAN/20CRITIC1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/fashion/20CRITIC1_SPAN/20CRITIC1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/fashion/20CRITIC1_SPAN/20CRITIC1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Outspoken Elder, Very Now', 'kicker': 'Critical Shopper', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Outspoken Elder, Very Now', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marimekko', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T22:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3040008c-3a10-511a-a229-335bc21b53cf', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3040008c-3a10-511a-a229-335bc21b53cf'}, {'abstract': 'Fox hung posters across the country printed with Mr. Hill’s image, the message “Need a Sitter?” and phone numbers on tear-off tab.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/movies/phone-stunt-seeks-box-office-numbers.html', 'snippet': 'Fox hung posters across the country printed with Mr. Hill’s image, the message “Need a Sitter?” and phone numbers on tear-off tab.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to publicizing movies, a lot of stars do as little as possible: a perfunctory wave from a red carpet, a chat with Jay Leno. Then there is what Jonah Hill is doing to promote “The Sitter,” an R-rated comedy set for release on Dec. 9. Mr. Hill, last seen as a statistics nerd in “Moneyball,” is so eager to make “The Sitter” a success — it’s his first film as a solo headliner — that he agreed to an unusual request from Fox’s marketing team. Fox hung posters across the country printed with Mr. Hill’s image, the message “Need a Sitter?” and phone numbers on tear-off tabs, above. About 250,000 people called, and nearly half left messages. Here comes the unusual part: Mr. Hill agreed to carry around the phone belonging to that number and randomly answer calls himself. A Fox spokesman said Mr. Hill had answered a few dozen times. On Wednesday he began returning calls. Mr. Hill, who plays an unprepared baby sitter, also recorded messages for robo-returned calls. “Your voice sounds like a cat that was strangled with a pack of menthols,” one version says in part. “Call me back.” What did Mr. Hill have to say about the gimmick? Fox said he was unavailable to come to the phone.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Phone Stunt Seeks Box-Office Numbers', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Phone Stunt Seeks Box-Office Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Entertainment Group Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Jonah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T22:16:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa0f5b66-b78c-5ed6-99af-81e2769d0269', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa0f5b66-b78c-5ed6-99af-81e2769d0269'}, {'abstract': 'Leather skirts, derby boots, and a peppy new boutique.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/20/fashion/20111020-BROWSING.html', 'snippet': 'Leather skirts, derby boots, and a peppy new boutique.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leather skirts, derby boots, and a peppy new boutique.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/fashion/20111020-BROWSING-slide-VOCF/20111020-BROWSING-slide-VOCF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shopping Snapshots: Oct. 20', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T22:20:52+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERICA M. BLUMENTHAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/70cfdd3c-55a1-5662-8073-fa01ac74421b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/70cfdd3c-55a1-5662-8073-fa01ac74421b'}, {'abstract': 'Five of network TV’s most established shows have undergone major cast changes since last season, spurred by contract disputes, growing movie careers and creative crises.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/arts/television/for-csi-house-law-order-svu-risky-transitions.html', 'snippet': 'Five of network TV’s most established shows have undergone major cast changes since last season, spurred by contract disputes, growing movie careers and creative crises.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the season’s new television shows battle for survival, like baby turtles scurrying across the beach — five of them are gone already, picked off by the bad-ratings bird — there’s an equally important but more quiet drama going on in prime time.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/arts/Replacement/Replacement-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 999, 'width': 659, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',