igners in Milan went head-to-head with designers in New York and London?', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Month, Too Much Fashion', 'kicker': 'Front Row', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Month, Too Much Fashion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T22:25:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3b3e62d-05ec-5c1b-a074-f03150863149', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3b3e62d-05ec-5c1b-a074-f03150863149'}, {'abstract': 'The English pianist Paul Lewis, who performed on Tuesday at the 92nd Street Y, has shifted his focus to Schubert from Beethoven.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/arts/music/paul-lewis-shows-schuberts-depth-at-92nd-street-y-review.html', 'snippet': 'The English pianist Paul Lewis, who performed on Tuesday at the 92nd Street Y, has shifted his focus to Schubert from Beethoven.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a musician programs a composer’s late works, it’s hard to imagine that those pieces were mostly written while the composer was still in his 20s. But the autumnal masterpieces of Schubert, who died at 31, are indeed the efforts of a young man. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Schubert Shouts Softly', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Schubert Shouts Softly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schubert, Franz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T22:27:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dd938f9-d628-5280-8434-c54fb1f98b35', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dd938f9-d628-5280-8434-c54fb1f98b35'}, {'abstract': 'Claire Cain Miller of The Times discusses the emerging market for mobile search services and how people tend to use search engines differently on their phones compared to sitting in front of a computer. Miguel Penella, the chief executive of the Acorn Media Group, explains how his company’s Acorn TV video-streaming service is bringing in a new American audience for British television shows. The weekly news roundup notes the memorial for Apple co-founder Steve Jobs, as well as the passing of audio pioneer Edgar Villchur; Research in Motion’s free-apps apology to its customers; and the return of a few iconic product designs. The Tip of the Week looks at ways to post to social-media sites by using text messages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/10/19/technology/19techtalk_pod.html', 'snippet': 'Claire Cain Miller of The Times discusses the emerging market for mobile search services and how people tend to use search engines differently on their phones compared to sitting in front of a computer. Miguel Penella, the chief executive of the A...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Claire Cain Miller of The Times discusses the emerging market for mobile search services and how people tend to use search engines differently on their phones compared to sitting in front of a computer. Miguel Penella, the chief executive of the Acorn Media Group, explains how his company’s Acorn TV video-streaming service is bringing in a new American audience for British television shows. The weekly news roundup notes the memorial for Apple co-founder Steve Jobs, as well as the passing of audio pioneer Edgar Villchur; Research in Motion’s free-apps apology to its customers; and the return of a few iconic product designs. The Tip of the Week looks at ways to post to social-media sites by using text messages.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The mobile-search market; a streaming service for British TV shows; tech news.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T22:29:44+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/20f6e50c-5128-56c0-9e4e-52b9d82f4e2b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/20f6e50c-5128-56c0-9e4e-52b9d82f4e2b'}, {'abstract': 'Jean-Michel Cazabat opens a store; sales by Jil Sander and Elie Tahari; and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/fashion/scouting-report.html', 'snippet': 'Jean-Michel Cazabat opens a store; sales by Jil Sander and Elie Tahari; and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OPENINGS', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scouting Report', 'kicker': 'Browsing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scouting Report', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub':