duled to appear after the election.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/release-date-of-bin-laden-film-may-change/', 'snippet': 'Originally scheduled for release about three weeks before next year’s election — potentially helping President Obama — the film is now said to be scheduled to appear after the election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The fuss over whether Sony Pictures and the filmmakers Mark Boal and Kathryn Bigelow were playing politics when they scheduled their hunt-for-Bin Laden film for release on Oct. 12, shortly before next year’s presidential election, may soon be irrelevant. Sony is planning to move the as-yet untitled film until after the election, according to two people who were briefed on the studio’s plans. Both said the picture is now virtually certain to appear after the election, and might not be released until early in 2013. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Release Date of Bin Laden Film May Change', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bigelow, Kathryn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boal, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T22:44:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/446bcd01-2d44-57ac-be29-d7661605426a', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/446bcd01-2d44-57ac-be29-d7661605426a'}, {'abstract': '“Damned” is a book full of tastelessly hilarious gallows humor about a teenage girl in hell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/books/damned-by-chuck-palahniuk-review.html', 'snippet': '“Damned” is a book full of tastelessly hilarious gallows humor about a teenage girl in hell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By any definition of the word “decency” it’s been a long time since Chuck Palahniuk wrote a decent book. His lurid recent efforts, from “Snuff” (pornography) to “Tell-All” (movie-star gossip) to “Pygmy” (broken English from teenage foreign terrorists), have tried the patience of even his most die-hard fans. These books have been skimpy and tired enough to suggest that this “Fight Club” author has had all the fight drained out of him. But he shows new signs of life in “Damned,” a book full of tastelessly hilarious gallows humor about a teenage girl in hell. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/arts/jp-book/jp-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 826, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/arts/jp-book/jp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/arts/jp-book/jp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Road to Hell, Paved With Telemarketers', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Road to Hell, Paved With Telemarketers', 'name': None, 'seo': 