al': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c10907b8-6e4f-5217-924b-6b13a0e0b323', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c10907b8-6e4f-5217-924b-6b13a0e0b323'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time, furniture by the Dutch designer, who is known for using recycled materials, will be available in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/garden/piet-hein-eek-designs-at-the-future-perfect-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'For the first time, furniture by the Dutch designer, who is known for using recycled materials, will be available in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was nearly a decade ago that the Dutch designer Piet Hein Eek flashed onto the scene, one in a line of stellar graduates of the Design Academy Eindhoven. For his thesis project, Mr. Eek had retooled the environmentally friendly ethos of “reduce, reuse, recycle,” using fine cabinetmaking techniques to transform wood scrap into high-style designs.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20FURNITURE/20CURR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 660, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20FURNITURE/20CURR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20FURNITURE/20CURR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Piet Hein Eek Designs at the Future Perfect', 'kicker': 'Currents | Furniture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dutch Recycling Master Arrives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eek, Piet Hein', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Future Perfect', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T23:13:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b9a2292-c24d-5006-972e-f20604a49bdd', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b9a2292-c24d-5006-972e-f20604a49bdd'}, {'abstract': 'Astier de Villatte, the French company known for white ceramic tableware, is adding color and graphics to its dishes, a result of a collaboration with John Derian.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/garden/bored-with-white-tableware-call-john-derian.html', 'snippet': 'Astier de Villatte, the French company known for white ceramic tableware, is adding color and graphics to its dishes, a result of a collaboration with John Derian.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Astier de Villatte, the French company known for delightfully imperfect white ceramic tableware, is adding color and graphics to its dishes, a result of a collaboration with John Derian. “After almost 15 years, we were doing almost only white ceramics,” said Ivan Pericoli, one of the founders of Astier de Villatte in 1996. “It seemed natural to us, when we wanted to add images, to ask John, because he has a sensibility about color that is really close to ours.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20GOODS1/20CURR7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1016, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/g