a03-665d-5021-81a7-0509dbb6e5a2'}, {'abstract': 'At the author’s home in Maine, visitors arrive bearing watermelon and tales of marriage No. 5.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/garden/ann-beattie-with-open-doors-and-weary-ears.html', 'snippet': 'At the author’s home in Maine, visitors arrive bearing watermelon and tales of marriage No. 5.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUILD it, and they will come. Someone built it long before we were born, around 1900. All we did was buy this house in southern Maine, but we soon found: they will come. At the halfway mark from New York City to Mount Desert, which draws them like Chaucer’s Canterbury Cathedral, they will be excited that half their journey is behind them.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20DOMESTIC1/13DOMESTIC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 678, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20DOMESTIC1/13DOMESTIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20DOMESTIC1/13DOMESTIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Open Doors, and Weary Ears', 'kicker': 'Domestic Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Open Doors, And Weary Ears', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T23:13:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Beattie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename