n-symphonic-architect-qa.html', 'snippet': 'Now 86, the Atlanta architect is the focus of a new documentary that premieres tomorrow at the Architecture & Design Film Festival in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1960s, the architect John Portman began transforming the Atlanta skyline, first with his Merchandise Mart and then, in 1967, with the famed Hyatt Regency Hotel. Considered the first modern atrium-style hotel, it had glass elevators, lighted columns and cascading fountains that created a fizzy extravaganza of space and light, or what the former New York Times architecture critic Herbert Muschamp called “architecture at happy hour.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20QNA2_SPAN/20QNA2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20QNA2_SPAN/20QNA2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20QNA2_SPAN/20QNA2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20QNA2_SPAN/20QNA2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20QNA2_SPAN/20QNA2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'John Portman, Symphonic Architect', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'John Portman, Symphonic Architect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'ma