ot the idea from “Betsy-Tacy and Tib,” a wholesome (read: deviant) children’s book from the 1940s. As copycat barbering accidents go, I suppose, it could have been worse. I’m keeping my girl away from “Sweeney Todd.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20TREE1/20TREE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 969, 'width': 644, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20TREE1/20TREE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/garden/20TREE1/20TREE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Indoor Tree: A Tall, Green Slip of Summer', 'kicker': 'In the Garden', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tall, Green Slip of Summer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-19T23:57:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Tortorello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tortorello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e2cf2c0-0946-579b-b90b-3195d6e69683', 'word_count': 2024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e2cf2c0-0946-579b-b90b-3195d6e69683'}, {'abstract': 'Vancouver Canucks goalie Roberto Luongo is finding himself as a favorite target of fans, but hopes they still like him enough to play poker.', 'web_url': 'https://sla