g East Conference', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boeheim, Jim', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syracuse University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T00:06:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6224e2e-8967-5418-b44b-92fe9314c81e', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6224e2e-8967-5418-b44b-92fe9314c81e'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Kent was a silent-film star who transitioned easily into the talkies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/movies/barbara-kent-silent-film-star-dies-at-103.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Kent was a silent-film star who transitioned easily into the talkies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barbara Kent, one of the last surviving stars of silent films, who performed alongside Gloria Swanson, Greta Garbo and Harold Lloyd, died last Thursday in Palm Desert, Calif. She was 103. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/arts/KENT-obit/KENT-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/arts/KENT-obit/KENT-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/arts/KENT-obit/KENT-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Barbara Kent, Star of Silent Movies, Dies at 103', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Barbara Kent, 103, Star of Silent Movies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T00:07:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/98b4148b-f1ef-5b04-b754-e1031bf8d6c8', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98b4148b-f1ef-5b04-b754-e1031bf8d6c8'}, {'abstract': 'Bingham Ray has been named executive director of the San Francisco Film Society.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/movies/film-executive-to-head-san-francisco-society.html', 'snippet': 'Bingham Ray has been named executive director of the San Francisco Film Society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bingham Ray, a veteran indie film executive who helped get movies like “Hotel Rwanda” and “Bowling for Columbine” on the screen, has been named executive director of the San Francisco Film Society, the society said on Wednesday. The appointment puts Mr. Ray in charge of an organization that, among other things, runs the San Francisco International Film Festival. And it fills a post that has been vacant since Graham Leggat, the previous director, died in August. Recently Mr. Ray had been working with Lincoln Center as a consultant to its film program; with SnagFilms, for which he was scouting movies; and with New York University’s Tisch School of the Arts, where he has been an adjunct professor. “Too good to be true” is how Mr. Ray described his appointment in a statement.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Film Executive to Head San Francisco Society', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Film Executive to Head San Francisco Society', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ray, Bingham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Film Society', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T00:10:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/da3266f1-5ee3-5633-b023-1ea61a1f9519', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da3266f1-5ee3-5633-b023-1ea61a1f9519'}, {'abstract': 'The Carson Palmer era in Oakland was just hours old when the speculation began as to how soon the quarterback would make his first appearance in silver and black.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/sports/football/carson-palmer-gets-going-with-raiders.html', 'snippet': 'The Carson Palmer era in Oakland was just hours old when the speculation began as to how soon the quarterback would make his first appearance in silver and black.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Carson Palmer era in Oakland was just hours old when the speculation began as to how soon he would make his first appearance in silver and black. Coach Hue Jackson has delighted in stonewalling the news media, and Palmer himself, while saying all the right things — “Come Sunday, I’m going to do whatever they ask me to do”— could not help but look overwhelmed. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/sports/PALMER/PALMER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hurry-Up Offense: Palmer Gets Going With Raiders', 'kicker': 'N.F.L. Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hurry-Up Offense: Ready or Not, Palmer Gets Going With the Raiders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Carson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Raiders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T00:13:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Turbow and Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turbow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7240fc0-7ad2-5645-99aa-beafa620e22a', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7240fc0-7ad2-5645-99aa-beafa620e22a'}, {'abstract': 'To attract American investors, the Man Group is expanding its product lineup, building up its local sales force and striking distribution deals with firms like Morgan Stanley.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/big-british-hedge-fund-takes-aim-at-the-states/', 'snippet': 'To attract American investors, the Man Group is expanding its product lineup, building up its local sales force and striking distribution deals with firms like Morgan Stanley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Founded 230 years ago near the banks of the Thames, the Man Group has transformed itself from a British barrel maker to a rum merchant to a $70 billion money manager dominant in Europe and Asia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big British Hedge Fund Takes Aim at the States', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Man Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T00:24:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cea4868-9ac2-5e51-95c7-6b470fe6f948', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cea4868-9ac2-5e51-95c7-6b470fe6f948'}, {'abstract': 'Democracy and Islam can coexist in Tunisia, Rachid al-Ghannouchi believes, and his ideas may be tested if his party succeeds in Sunday’s voting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/world/africa/rachid-al-ghannouchi-imagines-democratic-future-for-tunisia.html', 'snippet': 'Democracy and Islam can coexist in Tunisia, Rachid al-Ghannouchi believes, and his ideas may be tested if his party succeeds in Sunday’s voting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — For more than three decades, Rachid al-Ghannouchi has preached that pluralism, democracy and Islam are harmonious. As his country, Tunisia, heads toward the first elections after the Arab revolts on Sunday, Mr. Ghannouchi, a renowned Islamic thinker, faces a reckoning between his principles and intentions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/world/20ghanouchi/20ghanouchi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/world/20ghanouchi/20ghanouchi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/world/20ghanouchi/20ghanouchi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Islamist Imagines a Democratic Future for Tunisia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Veteran Islamist Imagines a Democratic Future for the New Tunisia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghannouchi, Rachid al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T00:24:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Shadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bb00a0f-28a7-52f8-8690-cb6404ce55b4', 'word_count': 1262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bb00a0f-28a7-52f8-8690-cb6404ce55b4'}, {'abstract': 'After firing its chief executive and effectively paying two advisers a 35 percent commission for a British acquisition in 2008, Olympus could be forced to take big write-downs or even delist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/business/olympus-faces-credibility-gap.html', 'snippet': 'After firing its chief executive and effectively paying two advisers a 35 percent commission for a British acquisition in 2008, Olympus could be forced to take big write-downs or even delist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Olympus shares will probably languish until it comes up with some answers. The Japanese manufacturer fired its chief executive, Michael Woodford, last week and has since acknowledged effectively paying two advisers a 35 percent commission for a British acquisition in 2008. While its core business looks sound, the fear is that Olympus could be forced to take big write-downs or even delist.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/business/Views/Views-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/business/Views/Views-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Olympus Faces Credibility Gap', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Olympus Faces Credibility Gap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Temasek Holdings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodford, Michael C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Olympus Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'n