tions” that followed New York City’s deep budget cuts in 1975 and 1976. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Bleak ’70s, Salvo of Protest', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Bleak ’70s, Salvo Of Protest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Seventies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beame, Abraham D', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T00:41:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Phillips-Fein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Phillips-Fein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ace44953-5b2b-58a3-ad04-83d390f4a2da', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ace44953-5b2b-58a3-ad04-83d390f4a2da'}, {'abstract': 'Barbara Sheehan, a Queens woman who killed her husband but was acquitted of his murder, will be eligible for release again on $1 million bail pending her sentencing on a weapons conviction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/nyregion/bail-set-for-barbara-sheehan-acquitted-of-murder-but-guilty-of-weapons-charge.html', 'snippet': 'Barbara Sheehan, a Queens woman who killed her husband but was acquitted of his murder, will be eligible for release again on $1 million bail pending her