85-b307-5ccf-ba1a-5d71c6292a86', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58e72785-b307-5ccf-ba1a-5d71c6292a86'}, {'abstract': 'A new campaign by the law firm Jacoby & Meyers is taking an unconventional approach by eschewing lawyers and employing humor in its television commercials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/business/media/winning-is-everything-or-so-says-jacoby-meyers.html', 'snippet': 'A new campaign by the law firm Jacoby & Meyers is taking an unconventional approach by eschewing lawyers and employing humor in its television commercials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMONG the most derided commercials on television are those by law firms that represent victims of accidents, which often feature tough-talking lawyers promising vengeance, video of car accidents and assorted mayhem, and modest production values. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/business/20adco_span/20adco_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/20/business/20adco_span/20adco_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/business/20adco_span/20adco_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 597, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/business/20adco_span/20adco_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/business/20adco_span/20adco_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning Is Everything, or So Says a Law Firm', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winning Is Everything, Or So Says a Law Firm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T01:17:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Adam Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Adam', 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7930c5f-67be-5ab3-a044-602db0d03dbe', 'word_count': 964, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7930c5f-67be-5ab3-a044-602db0d03dbe'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Thomas’s 1967 memoir, “Down These Mean Streets,” became a classic portrait of ghetto life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/books/piri-thomas-author-of-down-these-mean-streets-dies.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Thomas’s 1967 memoir, “Down These Mean Streets,” became a classic portrait of ghetto life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Piri Thomas, the writer and poet whose 1967 memoir, “Down These Mean Streets,” chronicled his tough childhood in Spanish Harlem and the outlaw years that followed and became a classic portrait of ghetto life, died on Monday at his home in El Cerrito, Calif. He was 83.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/arts/THOMAS1-obit/THOMAS1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 658, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/arts/THOMAS1-obit/THOMAS1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/arts/THOMAS1-obit/THOMAS1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Piri Thomas, Spanish Harlem Author, Dies at 83', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Piri Thomas Dies at 83; Spanish Harlem Author', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Piri', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'HARLEM (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T01:21:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/64b67674-f070-5dee-982a-2a7732dbea17', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64b67674-f070-5dee-982a-2a7732dbea17'}, {'abstract': 'Conservatives are lining up not to denounce judicial activism, but to embrace it.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/engagement-as-the-new-activism/', 'snippet': 'Conservatives are lining up not to denounce judicial activism, but to embrace it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Remember judicial activism? Of course you do. Not so long ago, Republicans lined up to denounce President Obama’s two Supreme Court nominees as judicial activists before the ink was dry on their nomination papers. Writing in The Wall Street Journal right after Sonia Sotomayor’s nomination in May 2009, Karl Rove advised fellow Republicans that although Judge Sotomayor would almost certainly be confirmed, Republicans should nonetheless seek to score points by “making a clear case against the judicial activism she represents.” The next year, Sen. Orrin Hatch of Utah, undeterred by the fact that Elena Kagan, never having been a judge, was hard to describe plausibly as a judicial activist, explained his vote against her confirmation by saying that “Ms. Kagan’s record shows that she supports an activist judicial philosophy.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Actively Engaged', 'kicker': 'Linda Greenhouse', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute for Justice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T01:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e44739e-d76f-5703-8ea0-a464898848ff', 'word_count': 1214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e44739e-d76f-5703-8ea0-a464898848ff'}, {'abstract': 'I needed therapy to help me deal with writing a book with my psychotherapist.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/my-shrink-is-my-co-author/', 'snippet': 'I needed therapy to help me deal with writing a book with my psychotherapist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I decided to ghost write a book with my longtime psychotherapist, colleagues said, “You’re crazy.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Shrink Is My Co-Author', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NEW YORK CITY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T01:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Shapiro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shapiro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cb56337-3846-5401-a596-e31e747864b8', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cb56337-3846-5401-a596-e31e747864b8'}, {'abstract': 'New York City has a tentative approval from the state on a plan to introduce technologies that are expected to greatly reduce sewer overflow into area waterways.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/nyregion/new-york-city-set-to-commit-2-4-billion-on-storm-water-control-tactics.html', 'snippet': 'New York City has a tentative approval from the state on a plan to introduce technologies that are expected to greatly reduce sewer overflow into area waterways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bloomberg administration is set to commit $2.4 billion in public and private investment to applying new environmental technology to an old problem: the flow of untreated sewage and storm water into New York City’s waterways.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Tactics and Billions to Manage City Sewage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Tactics And Billions