ps://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/19/stalemate-remains-on-collecting-blood-samples-for-h-g-h-testing/', 'snippet': 'The N.F.L. sent a letter to the union saying that on Monday it was prepared to start collecting blood, which would be held until the final details of a testing plan were worked out. The union’s response was: No, not yet', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly two months after it had hoped to start blood testing for human growth hormone, and several days after two Congressmen announced there was a deal to begin collecting blood samples immediately, the N.F.L. and its players union remained at a standstill on Wednesday over the program.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stalemate Remains on Collecting Blood Samples for H.G.H. Testing', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T03:07:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f063cca-99d2-5a4f-b850-984a49d6494b', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f063cca-99d2-5a4f-b850-984a49d6494b'}, {'abstract': 'Tristane Banon, the French writer who accused Dominique Strauss-Kahn of trying to rape her eight years ago, said she would not pursue a civil case against him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/world/europe/france-writer-says-she-wont-sue-strauss-khan.html', 'snippet': 'Tristane Banon, the French writer who accused Dominique Strauss-Kahn of trying to rape her eight years ago, said she would not pursue a civil case against him.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Tristane Banon, the French writer who accused Dominique Strauss-Kahn of trying to rape her eight years ago, said she would not pursue a civil case against him, after French prosecutors recently declined to charge him with attempted rape. Last week, prosecutors said they could not bring a case against him, given a three-year statute of limitations for sexual assault, but they said there was evidence that he had sexually assaulted Ms. Banon. On Wednesday, Ms. Banon said she would not pursue a suit because the case had proved that she was not a liar. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Writer Says She Won’t Sue Strauss-Khan', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Writer Says She Won’t Sue Strauss-Khan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banon, Tristane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T03:17:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maïa de la Baume', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maïa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de la Baume', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7ffb0b5-b2a2-5d74-99f0-21e6b3ea1a96', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7ffb0b5-b2a2-5d74-99f0-21e6b3ea1a96'}, {'abstract': 'Carla Bruni, the wife of President Nicolas Sarkozy of France, gave birth to a girl on Wednesday evening while Mr. Sarkozy was retur