pot at the year-end championships  Istanbul.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/radwanska-slip-gives-bartoli-hope/', 'snippet': 'A loss by Agnieszka Radwanska  left the door open for Marion Bartoli to sneak past her and into the eighth and final spot at the year-end championships  Istanbul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having just won the two biggest titles of her career back-to-back in Tokyo and Beijing, Agnieszka Radwanska needed just one more win to qualify directly for the year-end WTA Championships for the first time in her career. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Radwanska Slip Gives Bartoli Hope', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T04:17:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd83db90-7b49-57c8-a2b2-ae07197b041e', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd83db90-7b49-57c8-a2b2-ae07197b041e'}, {'abstract': 'NYT Front Page for 10/20/2011', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/10/20/multimedia/20frontpage.html', 'snippet': 'NYT Front Page for 10/20/2011', 'lead_paragraph': 'NYT Front Page for 10/20/2011', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NYT Front Page for 10/20/2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T04:22:22+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/b1100aef-7b70-5445-9e7c-fb156b7ff92f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/b1100aef-7b70-5445-9e7c-fb156b7ff92f'}, {'abstract': 'Despite belt-tightening budgets, uncertainty still reigns in states like Washington, California, New York and New Jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/us/states-warn-that-tax-revenues-arent-rebounding.html', 'snippet': 'Despite belt-tightening budgets, uncertainty still reigns in states like Washington, California, New York and New Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The warning by the State of Washington’s economist was unusually blunt, a far cry from the kind of dry, green-eyeshade language that often cloaks such announcements: “We are in the fragile aftermath of the Great Recession, where a return to normalcy seems like a mirage in the desert — the closer we get to it, the further it moves away.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/us/TAXES/TAXES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/us/TAXES/TAXES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/us/TAXES/TAXES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Warning by States as Tax Revenues Fail to Rebound', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Warning by States as Tax Revenues Fail to Rebound', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T04:45:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c299a7ad-9baa-5e43-91c5-fe9be984b361', 'word_count': 703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c299a7ad-9baa-5e43-91c5-fe9be984b361'}, {'abstract': 'As word spread that infectious salmon anemia had been found in prized wild Pacific salmon, there remained much uncertainty about what its potential impact could be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/science/20salmon.html', 'snippet': 'As word spread that infectious salmon anemia had been found in prized wild Pacific salmon, there remained much uncertainty about what its potential impact could be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — The scientist in Canada got the results from a respected lab and held a news conference. The ice and bait man at a fish processor in Sitka, Alaska, heard the news on Facebook. Vardon Tremain read it in the newspaper while working on his trolling boat docked here in Salmon Bay.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/us/SALMON2/SALMON2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 797, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/us/SALMON2/SALMON2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/us/SALMON2/SALMON2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Knot of Worry Tightens for Fishermen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knot of Worry Tightens for Fishermen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salmon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'British Columbia (Canada)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pacific Northwestern States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Viruses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish Farming', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T04:56:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91e8f949-64e5-5135-92c2-af92cc7ba251', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91e8f949-64e5-5135-92c2-af92cc7ba251'}, {'abstract': 'Top stories on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/newswallah-in-the-english-language-press-thursday-5/', 'snippet': 'Top stories on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Finance Ministry finally admitted what every economist, stockbroker and reader of the business pages has long suspected: India’s growth rate will likely fall short of 8 percent this year. The global slowdown, rising oil and commodity prices and rising interest rates are to blame, Pranab Mukherjee, India’s finance minister, said Wednesday. The lower expectations will have a major impact on the best-case-scenario budget presented earlier this year, which assumed the treasury would overflow with the proceeds of a white-hot economy (Mint).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: In the English-Language Press Thursday', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hazare, Anna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kayani, Ashfaq Parvez', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR INDIA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Karnataka (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T05:08:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/401c90c0-2230-5db1-8aa5-eadaa88c0376', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/401c90c0-2230-5db1-8aa5-eadaa88c0376'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on October 20, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/pageoneplus/corrections-october-20.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on October 20, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: October 20', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T05:11:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/426f40a2-6621-597e-bf5f-a03072caf964', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/426f40a2-6621-597e-bf5f-a03072caf964'}, {'abstract': 'Some of the men were captured on surveillance cameras running through a hallway wearing Mexican sombreros that they took from a law library and also playing with a courtroom gavel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/us/5-held-in-break-in-at-san-antonio-courthouse.html', 'snippet': 'Some of the men were captured on surveillance cameras running through a hallway wearing Mexican sombreros that they took from a law library and also playing with a courtroom gavel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN ANTONIO — Five young men were arrested early Wednesday morning in connection with a break-in at the Bexar County Courthouse here that raised fears of a terror plot but appeared instead to be a prank. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas Courthouse Break-In Seen as Prank', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas Courthouse Break-In Seen as Prank', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hoaxes and Pranks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Antonio (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T05:17:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71ad7b3a-67b2-5a5a-bdfc-db878d365d8d', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71ad7b3a-67b2-5a5a-bdfc-db878d365d8d'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense recently confirmed the deaths of the following Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/us/us-military-deaths-in-iraq-and-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense recently confirmed the deaths of the following Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 4,471 American service members who have died since the start of the Iraq war and 1,795 who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the deaths of the following Americans on Wednesday: ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T05:20:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/831d984e-7255-5b8b-9ef0-ba68a79e3504', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/831d984e-7255-5b8b-9ef0-ba68a79e3504'}, {'abstract': 'Albert Pujols makes the defensive play of the game, and Chris Carpenter shows again why he’s the best Cardinals starter since Bob Gibson.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/pujolss-defense-and-carpenters-st-louis-legacy/', 'snippet': 'Albert Pujols makes the defensive play of the game, and Chris Carpenter shows again why he’s the best Cardinals starter since Bob Gibson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS – It didn’t quite get a star on my scoresheet because the ball was not hit all that hard. But the play Albert Pujols made on Michael Young to end the top of the sixth inning of Game 1 was impressive just the same. Pujols ranged to his left, across the first base line, and tossed to pitcher Chris Carpenter covering first for the out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pujols’s Defense and Carpenter’s St. Louis Legacy', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carpenter, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pujols, Albert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T05:20:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b73c5077-6349-532b-8ebb-556665b7568c', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b73c5077-6349-532b-8ebb-556665b7568c'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama wrapped up a three-city bus tour to states that could prove to be a struggle to hold onto