he capture of the city of Surt, Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi’s hometown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lede followed developments in Libya on Thursday, after the interim government announced that Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi had been killed in his hometown of Surt, which fell after weeks of intense fighting. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Updates on the Death of Muammar el-Qaddafi', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Surt (Libya)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T12:14:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4af6a7a8-6f5f-5594-8bcd-d05af93bdbbd', 'word_count': 3093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4af6a7a8-6f5f-5594-8bcd-d05af93bdbbd'}, {'abstract': 'A trial program will allow the authorities in four regions to issue bonds amid concerns about efforts by Beijing to tame inflation and a property bubble.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/business/global/china-to-allow-some-local-governments-to-issue-bonds.html', 'snippet': 'A trial program will allow the authorities in four regions to issue bonds amid concerns about efforts by Beijing to tame inflation and a property bubble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — Amid worries that local governments in China may be running short of cash, Beijing gave approval Thursday to a trial program that will allow the authorities in four regions to issue bonds.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China to Allow Some Local Governments to Issue Bonds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Local Cash Squeeze Leads Beijing to Allow Bond Sales', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T12:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99a0ed1d-692d-5be3-852f-a86a1c56e014', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99a0ed1d-692d-5be3-852f-a86a1c56e014'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: What are we to make of recent use of “chutzpah” by a couple of politicians who don’t have a Jewish bone in their bodies? Also, what City Room is reading in other newspapers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/romney-bachmann-and-the-oys-of-yiddish/', 'snippet': 'The Day: What are we to make of recent use of “chutzpah” by a couple of politicians who don’t have a Jewish bone in their bodies? Also, what City Room is reading in other newspapers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Here in New York, which probably has more Yiddish speakers than any other city in the world, including in Israel, what are we to make of recent uses of a certain Yiddish word by a couple of politicians who don’t have a Jewish bone in their bodies? We’re referring to the Mormon Mitt Romney and the evangelical Christian Michele Bachmann. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney, Bachmann and the Oys of Yiddish', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yiddish Language', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T12:22:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97fda8fd-0ee2-580a-bf1f-d65647a28718', 'word_count': 1144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97fda8fd-0ee2-580a-bf1f-d65647a28718'}, {'abstract': 'Security workers are protesting staff cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/strike-at-revamped-musee-dorsay-blocks-grand-reopening/', 'snippet': 'Security workers are protesting staff cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — A strike by workers at the Musée d’Orsay postponed the long-awaited reopening of the museum’s newly renovated galleries on Thursday. Some 34 employees, mostly security guards, staged the walkout to protest the fact that no additional workers had been recruited at the museum despite the addition of more than 21,000 square feet of display space, a museum spokeswoman said. That decision was made amid broad government cutbacks that see retiring civil servants – including museum workers – not replaced by new hires.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strike at Revamped Musée d’Orsay Blocks Grand Reopening', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Musee d'Orsay", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T12:37:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elvire Camus and Rachel Ramsay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elvire', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Camus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d84f13a6-fab0-58b1-b3df-b20776b9f1c7', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d84f13a6-fab0-58b1-b3df-b20776b9f1c7'}, {'abstract': 'Subscribers to its Web site helped The New York Times Company post a third-quarter profit of $15.7 million, partly offsetting falling revenue in every advertising category.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/business/media/the-new-york-times-company-reports-a-profit.html', 'snippet': 'Subscribers to its Web site helped The New York Times Company post a third-quarter profit of $15.7 million, partly offsetting falling revenue in every advertising category.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times Company continued to attract paying subscribers to its flagship Web site in the third quarter, bolstering a new revenue stream that has helped offset a decline in advertising revenue.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Times Co. Reports a Profit, Aided by Digital Subscribers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Times Co. Reports a Pr