in Flip League as you might think.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every major sports outlet seems to offer N.F.L. power rankings.\xa0I admit my site offers them, too. The game probability model I use for these weekly predictions also ranks teams. I match each team up against a notional league-average opponent at a neutral site, and rank each team according to the resulting game probabilities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Week 7 Game Probabilities: The Illusion of Power Rankings', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T13:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d28db1bd-cdf2-5ff3-8ba8-a322eb0d06a4', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d28db1bd-cdf2-5ff3-8ba8-a322eb0d06a4'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney may be in a fierce battle with Rick Perry at the moment. But he’s also got to worry about President Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/obama-groups-web-video-attacks-romney/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney may be in a fierce battle with Rick Perry at the moment. But he’s also got to worry about President Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney may be in a fierce battle with Rick Perry at the moment. But he’s also got to worry about President Obama.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Group’s Web Video Attacks Romney', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T13:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f77001e3-1cd1-53d9-bff3-cd8987a8b2f7', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f77001e3-1cd1-53d9-bff3-cd8987a8b2f7'}, {'abstract': 'When I caught up with the Ethiopian beauty, I found out there’s a whole lot more to her than meets the eye.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/face-time-liya-kebede/', 'snippet': 'When I caught up with the Ethiopian beauty, I found out there’s a whole lot more to her than meets the eye.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I always thought Liya Kebede was one of the most strikingly beautiful models in the business, so when I heard L’Oréal Paris had chosen her as its latest global brand ambassador, I wasn’t the least bit surprised. When I caught up with the Ethiopian beauty, I found out there’s a whole lot more to her than meets the eye.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Face Time | Liya Kebede', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kebede, Liya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turnbow, Tina', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T13:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Turnbow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turnbow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffcf60da-0ac1-5b06-8a5d-68bbe18c0caf', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffcf60da-0ac1-5b06-8a5d-68bbe18c0caf'}, {'abstract': 'Sergey Brin and Vic Gundotra talk about Google+, the new Android phone, far-afield projects and memos that put Mr. Brin to sleep. Though incumbent social networks like Facebook have a clear advantage because users are already there, Mr. Gundotra said, Google has a different advantage: most people visit Google every day, so Google constantly has the chance to lure them to Google+.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/google-will-get-new-features-and-new-users-executive-says/', 'snippet': 'Sergey Brin and Vic Gundotra talk about Google+, the new Android phone, far-afield projects and memos that put Mr. Brin to sleep. Though incumbent social networks like Facebook have a clear advantage because users are already there, Mr. Gundotra s...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Your friends and family might not yet be networking on Google+, making it less entertaining to use than, say, Facebook. But they will eventually show up, said Vic Gundotra, Google’s senior vice president in charge of Google+.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google+ Will Get New Features, and New Users, Executive Says', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name