d retirees in a contentious effort to reduce roughly $7 billion in unfunded obligations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Lincoln D. Chafee and the state treasurer, Gina M. Raimondo, on Tuesday proposed scaling back pension benefits for state workers and retirees in a contentious effort to reduce roughly $7 billion in unfunded obligations. The proposal would end cost-of-living increases for now, raise the retirement age and combine traditional pensions with 401(k)-type plans to shift some of the taxpayer burden to the beneficiaries. Labor unions have threatened to challenge the changes in court should they pass the Legislature. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rhode Island: Pension Rollbacks Proposed', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rhode Island: Pension Rollbacks Proposed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rhode Island', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chafee, Lincoln', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T14:23:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/110ee965-cf07-5bcd-a365-a29db3d44500', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/110ee965-cf07-5bcd-a365-a29db3d44500'}, {'abstract': 'A human rights commission judge has recommended the fine in response to a complaint from a woman who, after canceling a pre-wedding appointment, received a racially derogatory voice mail message.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/hair-stylists-racial-slurs-could-cost-her-22500/', 'snippet': 'A human rights commission judge has recommended the fine in response to a complaint from a woman who, after canceling a pre-wedding appointment, received a racially derogatory voice mail message.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tifany McIntosh said it only took a minute to ruin her wedding day, and to leave her in a months-long state of stomach-sickening distress. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hairstylist’s Racial Slurs Could Cost Her $22,500', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tutera, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "WE: Women's Entertainment", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madison Avenue (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T14:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Meredith Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Meredith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2b48dbd-b981-55ae-806b-5fd889faf9e4', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2b48dbd-b981-55ae-806b-5fd889faf9e4'}, {'abstract': 'Environmental change is just as likely to trap people as it is to make them migrate — or it can cause them to flee to even more vulnerable areas, a British government study warns.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/millions-will-be-trapped-amid-climate-change-study-warns/', 'snippet': 'Environmental change is just as likely to trap people as it is to make them migrate — or it can cause them to flee to even more vulnerable areas, a British government study warns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Millions of people are expected to become trapped in places that are extremely vulnerable to environmental change in the course of this century, according to a British government study released on Thursday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Millions Will Be Trapped Amid Climate Change, Study Warns', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caribbean Area', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T14:32:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hillary Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hillary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57b4bbeb-463c-5f0b-bf6e-43897ae67a56', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57b4bbeb-463c-5f0b-bf6e-43897ae67a56'}, {'abstract': 'Sgt. Sean Drenth was found in a lot with a shotgun on his chest. Suicide? Homicide? Evidence points both ways.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/us/phoenix-officers-2010-killing-confounds-colleagues.html', 'snippet': 'Sgt. Sean Drenth was found in a lot with a shotgun on his chest. Suicide? Homicide? Evidence points both ways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — Dozens of Phoenix police officers rushed to a dark vacant lot near the State Capitol here last October, responding to a radio call of an officer down. What they found continues to haunt them a year later: Sgt. Sean Drenth, a well-liked 12-year veteran, sprawled on his back, dead from a blast from his own police-issue shotgun.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/COPSHOT-1/COPSHOT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/21/us/COPSHOT-1/COPSHOT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/COPSHOT-1/COPSHOT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/COPSHOT-1/COPSHOT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/us/COPSHOT-1/COPSHOT-1