emocratic government have looked to British and American bands, from Metallica to Radiohead, for inspiration. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At CMJ, Taiwan Rocks the East Village', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'CMJ Music Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metallica', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radiohead', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Strokes, The', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T15:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31e35269-e1de-5464-a2da-d8fbc0cddeec', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31e35269-e1de-5464-a2da-d8fbc0cddeec'}, {'abstract': 'Ron Paul has started a multimillion dollar television ad campaign, the first serious push by a presidential candidate this year to influence primary voters.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/campaign-ad-barrage-begins-with-paul/', 'snippet': 'Ron Paul has started a multimillion dollar television ad campaign, the first serious push by a presidential candidate this year to influence primary voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The campaign ads are finally here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Campaign Ad Barrage Begins With Paul', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name