k Botanical Garden, is identifying your mystery fungi and fielding your questions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answers About Mushrooms, Part 1', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mushrooms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T15:57:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Lincoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lincoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3b9e4df-e13f-5b26-83e8-0a281c3944c7', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3b9e4df-e13f-5b26-83e8-0a281c3944c7'}, {'abstract': 'Kenya’s sudden incursion into Somalia over the weekend caught the United States by surprise, American officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/world/africa/americans-given-no-warning-of-kenyas-march-into-somalia-officials-say.html', 'snippet': 'Kenya’s sudden incursion into Somalia over the weekend caught the United States by surprise, American officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — As fierce fighting spread to new areas of Somalia on Thursday, American officials said they had been taken by surprise by Kenya’s recent march into Somalia to battle Islamist militants.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenya Reportedly Didn’t Warn U.S. of Somalia Incursion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Officials Say U.S. Had No Warning of Kenya’s Somalia Incursion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 2, 'major': '