 and TV', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T16:13:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Warner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Warner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/588b1283-1718-5af9-8a68-47b5bbf92552', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/588b1283-1718-5af9-8a68-47b5bbf92552'}, {'abstract': 'Displayed as a concept at the Frankfurt auto show last month, the S.U.V., based on the FX50, would be produced in low volume, Infiniti’s parent, Nissan, announced.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/sebatian-vettel-infiniti-fx-to-enter-limited-production/', 'snippet': 'Displayed as a concept at the Frankfurt auto show last month, the S.U.V., based on the FX50, would be produced in low volume, Infiniti’s parent, Nissan, announced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If timing is everything, Nissan and its luxury subsidiary, Infiniti, are not wasting much of it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sebatian Vettel Infiniti FX to Enter Limited Production', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frankfurt Auto Show', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Utility Vehicles and Light Trucks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vettel, Sebastian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Infiniti Division of Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Red Bull', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T16:13:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73385e4d-920b-587d-985b-66dcdcf166f5', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73385e4d-920b-587d-985b-66dcdcf166f5'}, {'abstract': '“Margin Call,” directed and written by J. C. Chandor, does a great deal to humanize the culprits — and beneficiaries — of the 2008 financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/movies/margin-call-with-zachary-quinto-review.html', 'snippet': '“Margin Call,” directed and written by J. C. Chandor, does a great deal to humanize the culprits — and beneficiaries — of the 2008 financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There have been reports of hurt feelings among the bankers and brokers who have been the focus of public ire and Occupy Wall Street protests. And it is true that those poor, hard-working souls have been demonized and caricatured. Surely the much-reviled 1 percent does not consist of plutocrats in top hats or predators in blue suits, but of human beings just like the other 99 percent of us, albeit with more money and perhaps more to answer for.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/movies/margin-span/margin-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/20/movies/margin-span/margin-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/movies/margin-span/margin-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/movies/margin-span/margin-span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/movies/margin-span/margin-span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Number Crunching at the Apocalypse', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Margin Call'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Number Crunching at the Apocalypse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tucci, Stanley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Irons, Jeremy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Badgley, Penn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spacey, Kevin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinto, Zachary', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Demi', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chandor, J C', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T16:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/671a4020-3313-5a1a-acbd-b6d221e7f719', 'word_count': 1178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/671a4020-3313-5a1a-acbd-b6d221e7f719'}, {'abstract': 'What to do about the aging mother or father who was never much of a parent?', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/the-undeserving-parent/', 'snippet': 'What to do about the aging mother or father who was never much of a parent?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maybe this incident tells you all you need to know. Wendy was 9 or 10, sitting in a Massachusetts restaurant with her mother and grandmother, and yawning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Undeserving Parent', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T16:19:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62d0bd51-bd25-57ba-a2ee-4fdd50a9da36', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62d0bd51-bd25-57ba-a2ee-4fdd50a9da36'}, {'abstract': 'Spring’s chokers, like those in the ’90s, have a bit of a bite.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/spring-ahead-the-choker/', 'snippet': 'Spring’s chokers, like those in the ’90s, have a bit of a bite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A snapshot of spring’s best trends and a hint at what you’ll want to wear next year.The last time we saw chokers with staying power was in the ’90s. And like those of the last millennium, spring’s have a bit of a bite — dog collar sorts at Jean Paul Gaultier, gold bondagelike ones at Lanvin and gothic juju pendant styles at Emilio Pucci and Delfina Delettrez all hug the neck with gripping poise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spring Ahead | The Choker', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T16:24:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e93c332-4414-52a4-a121-39d3a2431bc6', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e93c332-4414-52a4-a121-39d3a2431bc6'}, {'abstract': 'Dropbox keeps your important files everywhere at once. It is also an automatic, silent, encrypted backup of your essentials. And you can get at your computer’s files from your phone.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/dropbox-will-simplify-your-life/', 'snippet': 'Dropbox keeps your important files everywhere at once. It is also an automatic, silent, encrypted backup of your essentials. And you can get at your computer’s files from your phone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every time I’m tempted to write about some tech product that’s been around awhile, I’m torn. On one hand, I’ll be blasted by the technogeeks for being late to the party. On the other hand, it doesn’t seem right to keep something great hidden under a barrel from the rest of the world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dropbox Will Simplify Your Life', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data Storage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Application