f fierce fighting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/world/africa/20111021-LIBYA-slide-BBJ8/20111021-LIBYA-slide-BBJ8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/20/world/africa/20111021-LIBYA-slide-BBJ8/20111021-LIBYA-slide-BBJ8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/20/world/africa/20111021-LIBYA-slide-BBJ8/20111021-LIBYA-slide-BBJ8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Battle for Libya | Oct. 20, 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Surt (Libya)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T16:40:55+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/03e59998-a21e-52d5-a6a8-58f1e91cee23', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/03e59998-a21e-52d5-a6a8-58f1e91cee23'}, {'abstract': 'A new report suggests that majoring in science, technology, engineering or math might pay off after graduation.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/stem-study/', 'snippet': 'A new report suggests that majoring in science, technology, engineering or math might pay off after graduation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over at The Times’s Economix blog, Motoko Rich reports today on a new study from the Georgetown University Center on Education and the Workforce that indicates that college students might do well to study science, technology, engineering or math.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Supports the Practical Value of STEM Diplomas', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T16:41:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20a36a9a-e389-5e56-adb3-245613a18d6f', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20a36a9a-e389-5e56-adb3-245613a18d6f'}, {'abstract': 'With new hotels, a revived downtown, and miles of bike trails, New Mexico’s largest city has come into its own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/travel/36-hours-in-albuquerque.html', 'snippet': 'With new hotels, a revived downtown, and miles of bike trails, New Mexico’s largest city has come into its own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FREE association with “Albuquerque” used to yield “Bugs Bunny” and “that airport you go through to get to Santa Fe.” But New Mexico’s biggest city has come into its own in recent years. Thanks to tax breaks and great scenery, the TV and film industry is booming: Joss Whedon’s mega-budget “Avengers” wrapped here this summer, and next year, “Breaking Bad” starts shooting its fifth season with Albuquerque as a backdrop. For visitors, the sprawl can seem daunting, but it is tempered by new bike paths. On the main drag, Central Avenue, neon signs from Route 66’s heyday glow over revitalized, pedestrian-friendly neighborhoods. And along the banks of the Rio Grande, lush farmland provides a quiet oasis, not to mention heirloom beans, corn and more to feed the city’s vibrant organic movement.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/travel/23HOURS2/23HOURS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/travel/23HOURS2/23HOURS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/travel/23HOURS2/23HOURS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Albuquerque', 'kicker': '36 Hours', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Albuquerque', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBUQUERQUE (NM)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T16:43:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': "By Zora O'Neill", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zora', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Neill", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab95a9f8-71c0-5add-927b-86e96de20b66', 'word_count': 1390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab95a9f8-71c0-5add-927b-86e96de20b66'}, {'abstract': 'The death of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi is the latest in a string of successes for the Obama administration’s war strategy, which includes air power and a reliance on allies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/world/africa/qaddafis-death-is-latest-victory-for-new-us-approach-to-war.html', 'snippet': 'The death of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi is the latest in a string of successes for the Obama administration’s war strategy, which includes air power and a reliance on allies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — For President Obama, the image of a bloodied Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi offers vindication, however harrowing, of his intervention in Libya, where a reluctant commander in chief put strict limits on American military engagement and let NATO allies take the lead in backing the rebels.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/world/21assess/21assess-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 805, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/world/21assess/21assess-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/world/21assess/21assess-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Obama, Some Vindication of Approach to War', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Obama, Some Vindication of His Much-Criticized Approach to War', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T16:53:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd2e5bc3-ce56-587b-a82f-5f26849dc557', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd2e5bc3-ce56-587b-a82f-5f26849dc557'}, {'abstract': 'A confrontation at the Occupy Wall Street protests on Friday, which was captured on tape, has put a deputy inspector under the spotlight, and raised complaints that he had struck a protester in the early days of the demonstrations.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/for-commander-tied-to-punching-incident-evidence-of-a-blow-weeks-earlier/', 'snippet': 'A confrontation at the Occupy Wall Street protests on Friday, which was captured on tape, has put a deputy inspector under the spotlight, and raised complaints that he had struck a protester in the early days of the demonstrations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a few hundred protesters went on a raucous march through the financial district last Friday, several camera operators recorded a jarring image.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Commander Tied to Punching Incident, Evidence of a Blow Weeks Earlier', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T16:53:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8c2db16-3a3e-51b7-a938-79f2e1a077b0', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8c2db16-3a3e-51b7-a938-79f2e1a077b0'}, {'abstract': 'Terry Thompson, of Zanesville, Ohio, killed himself and then was apparently bitten, officials said Thursday. The wound was “consistent with a tiger bite,” the sheriff said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/us/preserve-owner-was-bitten-by-big-cat-authorities-say.html', 'snippet': 'Terry Thompson, of Zanesville, Ohio, killed himself and then was apparently bitten, officials said Thursday. The wound was “consistent with a tiger bite,” the sheriff said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The owner of the Ohio wildlife preserve who the authorities say set dozens of lions, tigers, bears and other animals free was bitten by one of his large cats, apparently after he fatally shot himself, officials said on Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21animals-span/21animals-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21animals-span/21animals-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21animals-span/21animals-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21animals-span/21animals-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21animals-span/21animals-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Preserve Owner Was Bitten by Big Cat, Authorities Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_