y, saying it wished to seize a “historical opportunity to reach a just and democratic resolution to an age-old political conflict.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Basque Separatists Halt Campaign of Violence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Separatists Halt Violence To Advance Basque Goals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basques', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ETA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T17:04:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a815200a-bd46-5cd1-ac9d-ed5e867628a4', 'word_count': 1083, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a815200a-bd46-5cd1-ac9d-ed5e867628a4'}, {'abstract': 'Melissa Clark demonstrates how to frost a cake. Plus, her recipe for butter cream frosting.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/video-how-to-frost-a-cake/', 'snippet': 'Melissa Clark demonstrates how to frost a cake. Plus, her recipe for butter cream frosting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the making of my latest video, on how to frost a cake, I went through vats of butter cream, as you can probably imagine. Here is the recipe I used. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: How to Frost a Cake', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Desserts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T17:19:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f9047c9-724e-537f-9745-39cf3809864b', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f9047c9-724e-537f-9745-39cf3809864b'}, {'abstract': 'The author pauses on a rainy day to reflect and answer readers’ questions about eating and what he carried (and what he needed).', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/100-miles-from-manhattan-feeling-both-young-and-old/', 'snippet': 'The author pauses on a rainy day to reflect and answer readers’ questions about eating and what he carried (and what he needed).', 'lead_paragraph': 'JONAS, Pa. — Rain and a gusty headwind kept me to a half day’s riding on Wednesday, slowing my progress home, though I’m not entirely bummed about that. It’s pretty here. I’m about 100 miles from Manhattan, having climbed some roller-coaster hills and wound a woodsy path through Hickory Run State Park, and I expect to cross the George Washington Bridge in the middle of the day Saturday. Yeah, it’s about time to be back in my own bed like a settled adult and in the newsroom like a reporter with a real job. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '100 Miles From Manhattan, Feeling Both Young and Old', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles 