onal calendars, 942 Occupy Wall Street arrests, and the latest in the Sean Bell case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To understand one reason Police Commissioner Raymond W. Kelly may be resisting calls that he disclose the daily schedules that pinpoint his movements, consider calendar entries revealing that one has had a hearing test, eaten lunch with the Brooklyn Democratic leader and switched to a less costly barber. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Confidential Calendars, at Least for Now', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bell, Sean', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Raymond W', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, Edward I', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T17:50:21+0000', 'documen