ng orders with a New York bartender’s consummate skill. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/arts/21MUSEUM1_SPAN/21MUSEUM1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/21/arts/21MUSEUM1_SPAN/21MUSEUM1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/arts/21MUSEUM1_SPAN/21JPMUSEUM1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/arts/21MUSEUM1_SPAN/21MUSEUM1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/arts/21MUSEUM1_SPAN/21MUSEUM1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Art Is Child’s Play', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Art Is Child’s Play', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Brooklyn Children's Museum", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lower Manhattan Development Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Children's Museum of the Arts", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T20:26:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurel Graeber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graeber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43318ca0-ac05-5f5d-9265-ae10945cfa4d', 'word_count': 1153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43318ca0-ac05-5f5d-9265-ae10945cfa4d'}, {'abstract': 'A corner of Manhattan called Hudson Heights is a route for thousands of cyclists who ride on paths along the Hudson River in Manhattan and over the George Washington Bridge to New Jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/arts/cycling-over-george-washington-bridge-to-new-jersey.html', 'snippet': 'A corner of Manhattan called Hudson Heights is a route for thousands of cyclists who ride on paths along the Hudson River in Manhattan and over the George Washington Bridge to New Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THEY are hard to miss on the weekend. Some on mountain bikes or 10-speeds weave their way through hilly streets that even cars struggle to climb. The more serious ones ride in packs, wear colorful spandex suits and sit on high-end bikes made by Trek, Cervélo, Cannondale and others. They ride three and four across in the street, all but daring drivers to honk or worse.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/arts/21URBAN1_SPAN/21URBAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/21/arts/21URBAN1_SPAN/21URBAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/arts/21URBAN1_SPAN/21URBAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ran