': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/2df533e8-540e-545d-a6da-e320294d8838', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/2df533e8-540e-545d-a6da-e320294d8838'}, {'abstract': 'Details of Ariel Sharon’s health and status have been closely guarded by the family, but his son, Gilad, agreed to discuss the matter as he prepares to publicize a biography of his father.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/world/middleeast/6-years-after-stroke-ariel-sharon-still-responsive-son-says.html', 'snippet': 'Details of Ariel Sharon’s health and status have been closely guarded by the family, but his son, Gilad, agreed to discuss the matter as he prepares to publicize a biography of his father.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Ariel Sharon, who suffered a debilitating stroke nearly six years ago while serving as prime minister of Israel and remains in a coma-like state, responds to some requests and, despite being fed intravenously, has put on weight, according to his son Gilad Sharon.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/world/21SHARON/21SHARON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/21/world/21SHARON/21SHARON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/world/21SHARON/21SHARON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/world/21SHARON/21SHARON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/world/21SHARON/21SHARON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Six Years After a Debilitating Stroke, Sharon Remains Responsive, His Son Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Six Years After a Debilitating Stroke, Sharon Remains Responsive, His Son Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharon, Ariel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T21:29:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0db14427-6d15-53c6-a1db-3a664058761f', 'word_count': 1096, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0db14427-6d15-53c6-a1db-3a664058761f'}, {'abstract': 'I first read “The Turn of the Screw” at my aunt’s creepy old house with floor-to-ceiling windows. Looking up from the book, I kept expecting to see Quint and Miss Jessel’s reflections burned into the glass panes.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/my-three-favorite-ghost-films/', 'snippet': 'I first read “The Turn of the Screw” at my aunt’s creepy old house with floor-to-ceiling windows. Looking up from the book, I kept expecting to see Quint and Miss Jessel’s reflections burned into the glass panes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a toddler, I was terrified of one of my father’s favorite movies, “The Day the Earth Stood Still,” directed by Robert Wise. I had no idea what the story was about; it was the imagery that overwhelmed me.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Three Favorite Ghost Films', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T21:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By PATTY RUSH', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patty', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'RUSH', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1189783-ea66-51cb-b9f1-37bbc8872b29', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1189783-ea66-51cb-b9f1-37bbc8872b29'}, {'abstract': 'The Red Bulls’ mission Thursday night: win and they’re in the M.L.S. playoffs.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/moment-of-truth-for-red-bulls/', 'snippet': 'The Red Bulls’ mission Thursday night: win and they’re in the M.L.S. playoffs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARRISON, N.J. — The Red Bulls have the Portland Timbers to thank for getting at least one albatross off their backs — Dwayne De Rosario — at least for now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moment of Truth for Red Bulls', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T21:30:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None,