nts for feline or canine companionship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PEOPLE beg him “a lot” to let them have pets, Gregory Dell’Aquila, the developer of a high-rent no-pet complex in Hoboken, acknowledges. “They say, ‘Oh, he or she is such a small little dog, and so well trained!’\xa0”', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/realestate/23NJ-ZONE_SPAN/23NJ-ZONE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/realestate/23NJ-ZONE_SPAN/23NJ-ZONE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/realestate/23NJ-ZONE_SPAN/23NJ-ZONE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Roommate Has Four Legs', 'kicker': 'In the Region | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Roommate Has Four Legs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T22:15:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Antoinette Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antoinette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_i