n University Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Tribune', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Illinois', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T22:57:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d624035d-97ab-57a7-8a4c-5a0dde5f722e', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d624035d-97ab-57a7-8a4c-5a0dde5f722e'}, {'abstract': 'In “Oranges and Sunshine” Emily Watson is a social worker who uncovers a terrible scheme involving British children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/movies/oranges-and-sunshine-starring-emily-watson-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Oranges and Sunshine” Emily Watson is a social worker who uncovers a terrible scheme involving British children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the quietly wrenching “Oranges and Sunshine” Emily Watson portrays Margaret Humphreys, an intrepid social worker from Nottingham, England, who exposed shameful national crimes. As recently as 1967, but especially in the 1940s and ’50s, as many as 130,000 children were removed from orphanages and group homes in Britain and deported to various locations in the Commonwealth, particularly western Australia. One deportee, now grown up, recalls being told at the age of 10 that he was being sent to a sunny paradise where he could pick oranges off trees.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/arts/21oranges-span/21oranges-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/21/arts/21oranges-span/21oranges-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/arts/21oranges-span/ORANGES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/arts/21oranges-span/21oranges-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/arts/21oranges-span/21oranges-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Promised Paradise, Then Sent to Hell', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Oranges and Sunshine'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Promised Paradise, Then Sent to Hell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Emily', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-20T23:25:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/61ecfd80-e122-5f7b-b638-e86bff68f819', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61ecfd80-e122-5f7