ocument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de2255e1-b3b9-52c0-91b3-65545bae3840', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de2255e1-b3b9-52c0-91b3-65545bae3840'}, {'abstract': 'Should we regulate or prohibit keeping apes, tigers, bears and other wildlife as household pets?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/opinion/exotic-animals-as-pets-an-unregulated-risk.html', 'snippet': 'Should we regulate or prohibit keeping apes, tigers, bears and other wildlife as household pets?', 'lead_paragraph': 'IMAGINE the panic and terror experienced by the monkeys, bears, lions and leopards that ran loose in Ohio earlier this week as they were chased and then killed by the police. Imagine the heartbreak of the police officers who were obliged to destroy the rambling menagerie. Officers are not trained to stalk big game and bring them in alive with tranquilizer darts. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exotic Animals as Pets: An Unregulated Risk', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exotic Animals as Pets: An Unregulated Risk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Terry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T00:19:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Laufer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Laufer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/58d7994c-1c1e-56e8-9fd0-e6879a9c4c50', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58d7994c-1c1e-56e8-9fd0-e6879a9c4c50'}, {'abstract': 'After months of delay, the Senate confirms President Obama’s choice for commerce secretary.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/john-bryson-confirmed-as-commerce-secretary/', 'snippet': 'After months of delay, the Senate confirms President Obama’s choice for commerce secretary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate voted 74-26 on Thursday to confirm the nomination of John Bryson to be the next commerce secretary, ending a months-long struggle over President Obama’s choice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'John Bryson Confirmed as Commerce Secretary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T00:20:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85eec305-645e-5993-b874-71959293f771', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85eec305-645e-5993-b874-71959293f771'}, {'abstract': 'Yan Vizinberg’s “Cargo” tells the story of a Russian woman being trafficked to New York, and the Muslim driver who must deliver her.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/movies/yan-vizinbergs-cargo-with-natasha-rinis-review.html', 'snippet': 'Yan Vizinberg’s “Cargo” tells the story of a Russian woman being trafficked to New York, and the Muslim driver who must deliver her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A stripped-down, socially conscious drama set in the slippery world of human trafficking, Yan Vizinberg’s “Cargo” is commendably free of cheap emotional manipulation. Instead the film leans almost exclusively on the focused performances of its two leads, who create a credibly barbed chemistry that goes a long way toward distracting us from the film’s low-budget deficiencies.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_CARGO/21RDP_CARGO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 298, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_CARGO/21RDP_CARGO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 298}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_CARGO/21RDP_CARGO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 509, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_CARGO/21RDP_CARGO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_CARGO/21RDP_CARGO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'She Was Told She’d Be a Model. Of Course.', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Cargo'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T00:23:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', '