le/9076f5bd-b75d-5e68-8345-f99c8cb79145'}, {'abstract': 'Libyans must resist reprisals and channel their passion into building a free and productive country. If not, they risk even more chaos and suffering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/opinion/colonel-qaddafis-end.html', 'snippet': 'Libyans must resist reprisals and channel their passion into building a free and productive country. If not, they risk even more chaos and suffering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi of Libya died as he lived — violently. We sympathize with the Libyans who suffered for so long at the hands of the ruthless dictator and are glad he can no longer hurt them. But a gruesome video broadcast on Al Jazeera — apparently showing him being dragged, beaten and then, perhaps, shot to death by armed men — is deeply troubling, if it is real. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colonel Qaddafi’s End', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colonel Qaddafi&#8217;s End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jibril, Mahmoud', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T01:12:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5d82ae8-085c-5264-9c28-265eb11424a9', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5d82ae8-085c-5264-9c28-265eb11424a9'}, {'abstract': 'In “Boy Wonder,” Caleb Steinmeyer plays a teenage vigilante who not only wants to find his mother’s killer but also to finish off every misogynist in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/movies/caleb-steinmeyer-in-boy-wonder-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Boy Wonder,” Caleb Steinmeyer plays a teenage vigilante who not only wants to find his mother’s killer but also to finish off every misogynist in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are an awful lot of terrorized women in “Boy Wonder” — so many, in fact, that the film feels like a constant assault. Their unlikely champion is Sean (Caleb Steinmeyer), a skulking 17-year-old vigilante driven by violent childhood memories of his mother’s death at the hands of a carjacker. But Sean is obsessed with more than just finding his mother’s killer: He’s also on a mission to finish off every misogynist in the five boroughs.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_BOY/21RDP_BOY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_BOY/21RDP_BOY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_BOY/21RDP_BOY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_BOY/21RDP_BOY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_BOY/21RDP_BOY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Protector of Women With a Chip on His Shoulder', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Boy Wonder'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T01:18:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/82018d58-334e-5c42-919e-5162b4bb447c', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82018d58-334e-5c42-919e-5162b4bb447c'}, {'abstract': 'A group called Positive Coaching Alliance is training thousands of coaches and parents to change to culture of youth sports for the better.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/20/the-power-of-positive-coaching/', 'snippet': 'A group called Positive Coaching Alliance is training thousands of coaches and parents to change to culture of youth sports for the better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine you’re coaching a big soccer game, against an undefeated team that has beaten your team in all your previous matches. Your 11-year-olds are playing well and are ahead. Then, in the closing minutes, the official makes a bad call that goes against you and, because of it, you lose. After the game, the parents of your players scream at the official. The kids are disappointed, looking up at you. What do you do?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Power of Positive Coaching', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':