ist', '_id': 'nyt://article/6332133d-e0c4-5f05-8a8a-39d827ede57e', 'word_count': 49, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6332133d-e0c4-5f05-8a8a-39d827ede57e'}, {'abstract': '“Norman” is a modest drama about a boy who creates a persona at school to keep the sadness of his home life at bay.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/movies/jonathan-segals-norman-review.html', 'snippet': '“Norman” is a modest drama about a boy who creates a persona at school to keep the sadness of his home life at bay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s something sweet about Jonathan Segal’s modest high school drama, “Norman,” despite the contrivances of its protagonist’s predicament and its stacking of the emotional deck. Norman Long (Dan Byrd of “Cougar Town” and “Easy A”) is a smart, sensitive and reflexively wisecracking teenager with a mother who died in a car accident and a father (the consistently reliable Richard Jenkins) who’s in, yes, the terminal stage of stomach cancer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_NORMAN/21RDP_NORMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_NORMAN/21RDP_NORMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_NORMAN/21RDP_NORMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_NORMAN/21RDP_NORMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/movies/21RDP_NORMAN/21RDP_NORMAN-thumbStan