type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2704fe5-653a-5f6f-83f8-8e09086778fc', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2704fe5-653a-5f6f-83f8-8e09086778fc'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors showed the courage that Catholic leaders lacked when Bishop Robert Finn was indicted for failing to report a priest suspected of child abuse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/opinion/accountability-in-the-catholic-church-in-missouri.html', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors showed the courage that Catholic leaders lacked when Bishop Robert Finn was indicted for failing to report a priest suspected of child abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been seven years since the Roman Catholic Church’s investigative board of laity warned that, beyond the 700 priests dismissed for sexually abusing children, “there must be consequences” for the diocesan leaders who recycled criminal priests through unsuspecting parishes. American church authorities have done nothing to heed this caution. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accountability in Missouri', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Accountability in Missouri', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finn, Robert William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Pornography', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T02:43:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6551ddb2-56d9-5177-b4de-2947ec420cd5', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6551ddb2-56d9-5177-b4de-2947ec420cd5'}, {'abstract': 'Christopher Nolan’s new Batman movie will shoot in New York for two weeks, with Zuccotti Park only two blocks from the weekend filming locale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/nyregion/dark-knight-rises-to-film-near-occupy-wall-street-site.html', 'snippet': 'Christopher Nolan’s new Batman movie will shoot in New York for two weeks, with Zuccotti Park only two blocks from the weekend filming locale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He is a tycoon, but he is also a crusader for justice: Bruce Wayne is coming to Wall Street, and how the 99 percent will receive him is the latest worry facing a beleaguered Lower Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/nyregion/BATMAN/BATMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 260, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/21/nyregion/BATMAN/BATMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 260}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/nyregion/BATMAN/BATMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/nyregion/BATMAN/BATMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/nyregion/BATMAN/BATMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Masked Protector of Gotham Has His Eye on Wall Street Protesters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Masked Protector of Gotham Has His Eye on Wall Street Protesters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nolan, Christopher', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zuccotti Park (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T02:52:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffa82b31-4c40-5916-bc45-92b8a416bd6a', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffa82b31-4c40-5916-bc45-92b8a416bd6a'}, {'abstract': 'The new system includes cap-and-trade market incentives to encourage polluters to clean up their plants, an approach much of the rest of the country has resisted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/business/energy-environment/california-adopts-cap-and-trade-system-to-limit-emissions.html', 'snippet': 'The new system includes cap-and-trade market incentives to encourage polluters to clean up their plants, an approach much of the rest of the country has resisted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SACRAMENTO — Fifteen months after a similar effort died in Congress, California regulators adopted a system on Thursday for combating climate change that sets limits on greenhouse gas emissions and creates market incentives to encourage oil refineries, electricity generators and other polluters to clean up their plants.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California Adopts Limits on Greenhouse Gases', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California Adopts Limits on Greenhouse Gases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T03:04:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6a6c11b-ef66-51c4-88c4-f44101960a98', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6a6c11b-ef66-51c4-88c4-f44101960a98'}, {'abstract': 'The definition, written more than 80 years ago, has been criticized as too narrow, resulting in thousands of rapes being excluded from the Federal Bureau of Investigation’s annual Uniform Crime Report.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/us/support-for-move-to-broaden-definition-of-rape.html', 'snippet': 'The definition, written more than 80 years ago, has been criticized as too narrow, resulting in thousands of rapes being excluded from the Federal Bureau of Investigation’s annual Uniform Crime Report.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Police officials and women’s groups on Thursday applauded a recommendation by a Federal Bureau of Investigation subcommittee that the definition of rape used by the agency be revised. The definition, written more than 80 years ago, has been criticized as too narrow, resulting in thousands of rapes being excluded from the F.B.I.’s annual Uniform Crime Report. The subcommittee recommends a broader definition, to include anal and oral rape, as well as rapes involving male victims. Currently, only sexual assaults that involved force and vaginal penetration are included. The proposal is subject to approval of a full advisory board, which meets in December. Women’s groups have been trying for years to get the definition changed. “What I’m happiest about is that such a clear consensus is emerging from law enforcement officials all over the country that this has to happen,” said Carol Tracy, executive director of the Women’s Law Project in Philadelphia. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Support for Move to Broaden Definition of Rape', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | LAW ENFORCEMENT', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Support for Move to Broaden Definition of Rape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T03:26:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Goode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bebdccb-e8ff-5307-b389-e31cda301528', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bebdccb-e8ff-5307-b389-e31cda301528'}, {'abstract': 'A judge in Boston ruled that a juror had not been impartial and repeatedly lied during jury selection, entitling the convict to a new sentencing trial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/us/mans-death-sentence-is-thrown-out-in-massachusetts.html', 'snippet': 'A judge in Boston ruled that a juror had not been impartial and repeatedly lied during jury selection, entitling the convict to a new sentencing trial.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A judge in Boston threw out a death sentence on Thursday in a 2003 murder case, ruling that a juror had not been impartial. Judge Mark L. Wolf of Federal District Court found that the juror had repeatedly lied during jury selection in a way that called her impartiality into question. He said the convict, Gary Lee Sampson, was entitled to a new sentencing trial to determine whether the death penalty was warranted. Mr. Sampson pleaded guilty to murdering two men who had picked him up hitchhiking. It was the first federal case in Massachusetts in which the death penalty was imposed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Man’s Death Sentence Is Thrown Out', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | NEW ENGLAND', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Man’s Death Sentence Is Thrown Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T03:31:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/55364fd0-b2ac-55aa-9cdf-b1e4f4fdfb45', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55364fd0-b2ac-55aa-9cdf-b1e4f4fdfb45'}, {'abstract': 'The Environmental Protection Agency announced Thursday that it planned to set standards by 2014 for the management of wastewater used in hydrofracking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/us/epa-to-tighten-rules-on-wastewater-disposal.html', 'snippet': 'The Environmental Protection Agency announced Thursday that it planned to set standards by 2014 for the management of wastewater used in hydrofracking.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Environmental Protection Agency announced Thursday that it would devise stricter rules for the treatment and disposal of toxic wastewater used in natural gas drilling. The agency said it planned to set standards by 2014 for the management of wastewater used in a rapidly growing drilling tactic known as hydrofracking, which involves injecting huge amounts of water to break up shale or coal bed formations and release the gas. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.P.A. to Tighten Rules on Wastewater Disposal', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'E.P.A. to Tighten Rules on Wastewater Disposal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drilling and Boring', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'