d-view-of-alcoholism.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Chafetz played an important role in changing the perception of alcoholism from social crime or personal failing to a disease requiring treatment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Morris E. Chafetz, who played an important role in changing the public perception of alcoholism from social crime or personal failing to a disease requiring treatment, died on Oct. 14 at his home in Washington. He was 87.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/CHAFETZ-obit/CHAFETZ-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/CHAFETZ-obit/CHAFETZ-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/us/CHAFETZ-obit/CHAFETZ-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Morris Chafetz, 87, Dies; Altered View of Alcoholism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Morris Chafetz, 87, Dies; Altered View of Alcoholism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chafetz, Morris E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T04:16:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0484765-b864-5a11-89c4-45bc34aa25b3', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0484765-b864-5a11-89c4-45bc34aa25b3'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Feinstein’s images were the centerpieces of albums by Bob Dylan, Janis Joplin and George Harrison, among others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/arts/music/barry-feinstein-photographer-of-defining-rock-portraits-dies-at-80.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Feinstein’s images were the centerpieces of albums by Bob Dylan, Janis Joplin and George Harrison, among others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barry Feinstein, a photographer who chronicled the lives of seminal rock ’n’ roll stars of the 1960s, and who was perhaps best known for the stark portrait of Bob Dylan on the cover of the 1964 album “The Times They Are A-Changin’,” died on Thursday in a hospital near his home in Woodstock, N.Y. He was 80.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/FEINSTEINaobit/FEINSTEINaobit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 200, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/21/us/FEINSTEINaobit/FEINSTEINaobit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 200}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/FEINSTEINaobit/FEINSTEINaobit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/FEINSTEINaobit/FEINSTEINaobit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/us/FEINSTEINaobit/FEINSTEINaobit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Barry Feinstein, Photographer of Defining Rock Portraits, Dies at 80', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Barry Feinstein, 80, Shooter Of Defining Rock Portraits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinstein, Barry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T04:28:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Vitello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vitello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c885492-c268-559c-946f-5daecb169eb8', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c885492-c268-559c-946f-5daecb169eb8'}, {'abstract': 'The government of Uganda is charging the ringleaders of street demonstrations this week with treason, officials said Thursday, an offense that can carry the death penalty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/world/africa/uganda-2-protest-leaders-are-charged-with-treason.html', 'snippet': 'The government of Uganda is charging the ringleaders of street demonstrations this week with treason, officials said Thursday, an offense that can carry the death penalty.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The government is charging the ringleaders of street demonstrations this week with treason, officials said Thursday, an offense that can carry the death penalty. The police said that about 40 people had been arrested across the country since Monday, when activists tried to resume demonstrations begun in April against rising commodity prices and government corruption. The police accuse the activists of seeking to overthrow the government. Two members of the group Activists 4 Change were arraigned on treason charges on Wednesday, said Judith Nabakooba, a police spokeswoman. One of them is an assistant to the opposition leader Kizza Besigye. At least nine people were killed and hundreds arrested during protests led by Mr. Besigye this past spring. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uganda: 2 Leaders of Protest Movement Are Charged With Treason, Police Say', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uganda: 2 Leaders of Protest Movement Are Charged With Treason, Police Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Besigye, Kizza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T04:29:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0dfbf99-f7ec-521f-b6f4-ecaeed9819b3', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0dfbf99-f7ec-521f-b6f4-ecaeed9819b3'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities reopened an investigation into the 1988 murder of Debra Masters Baker after DNA tests in another case linked the two crimes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/us/after-23-years-suspect-emerges-in-austin-murder-of-debra-masters-baker.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities reopened an investigation into the 1988 murder of Debra Masters Baker after DNA tests in another case linked the two crimes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost everything that Caitlin and Jesse Baker know about their mother, who was mysteriously murdered 23 years ago when they were small children, comes from memories shared by relatives and from fading family photos of the smiling, petite brunette.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21TTBAKER/21TTBAKER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 919, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21TTBAKER/21TTBAKER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21TTBAKER/21TTBAKER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After 23 Years, a Suspect Emerges and a Family’s Wounds Are Reopened', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After 23 Years, a Suspect Emerges and a Family’s Wounds Are Reopened', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morton, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major'