oor conference room in the Financial District. They met for an hour, rehearsing their strategy to assure that Ed Lee, the interim mayor of San Francisco, is elected to a four-year term on Nov. 8.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21BCMAYOR/21BCMAYOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21BCMAYOR/21BCMAYOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21BCMAYOR/21BCMAYOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21BCMAYOR/21BCMAYOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21BCMAYOR/21BCMAYOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor’s Political Machine Goes Into High Gear in Quest for Full Term', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mayor’s Political Machine Goes Into High Gear in Quest for Full Term', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T05:53:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Shih and Zusha Elinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shih', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Zusha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb894b32-75cd-5d0b-b8d0-a4832276dca5', 'word_count': 1175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb894b32-75cd-5d0b-b8d0-a4832276dca5'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer Richard Misrach waited 20 years to put his photographs of the Oakland-Berkeley fire on display, and they now can be seen at two Bay Area museums.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/us/richard-misrach-reveals-his-images-of-oakland-berkeley-fire.html', 'snippet': 'The photographer Richard Misrach waited 20 years to put his photographs of the Oakland-Berkeley fire on display, and they now can be seen at two Bay Area museums.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Misrach has built his reputation photographing destruction, be it in New Orleans after Hurricane Katrina or in the industrial area known as Cancer Alley along the Mississippi River in southern Louisiana. Twenty years ago, however, it was a disaster close to home that led him to take out his 8-by-10 large-format camera.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21BCCULTURE1/21BCCULTURE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 812, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21BCCULTURE1/21BCCULTURE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/21/us/21BCCULTURE1/21BCCULTURE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '20 Years After Fire, Revelation and Tribute', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '20 Years After Fire, Revelation and Tribute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Misrach, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco Bay Area (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T05:59:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tracey Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tracey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc0c94cf-659e-5521-ad4c-776d1f6c732a', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc0c94cf-659e-5521-ad4c-776d1f6c732a'}, {'abstract': 'The Renova Group of Russia has helped save Fort Ross State Historic Park from closing, and similar public-private partnerships are in the works across California.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/us/fort-ross-park-saved-from-closing-by-renova-group-of-russia.html', 'snippet': 'The Renova Group of Russia has helped save Fort Ross State Historic Park from closing, and similar public-private partnerships are in the works across California.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent weekday at Fort Ross State Historic Park, a group of schoolchildren dressed as 19th-century Russian fur traders and American Indian otter hunters gathered around the replica of a cannon at the center of the fort. As the fuse dwindled, the children covered their ears. The cannon exploded and cheers erupted.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russians Come to the Rescue of Sonoma’s Fort Ross Park', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russians Come to the Rescue Of Sonoma’s Fort Ross Park', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T06:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Gross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9136182-ea4b-59a6-ac66-ea2a445e1ee2', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9136182-ea4b-59a6-ac66-ea2a445e1ee2'}, {'abstract': 'A landlord’s legal maneuver is described as an injustice by tenant advocates, but courts have backed the action.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/us/forced-from-home-at-75-as-tenant-rules-bend.html', 'snippet': 'A landlord’s legal maneuver is described as an injustice by tenant advocates, but courts have backed the action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scott James writes a column for The Bay Citizen.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Forced From Home at 75 as Tenant Rules Bend', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Forced From Home at 75 As Tenant Rules Bend', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting