nyt://article/c5cc037c-0385-5b87-a664-1cfcb3980b8c'}, {'abstract': 'The Chicago Tribune and the University of Illinois are embroiled in a lawsuit over a federal law that prohibits the release of students’ academic records.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/urbana-champ/', 'snippet': 'The Chicago Tribune and the University of Illinois are embroiled in a lawsuit over a federal law that prohibits the release of students’ academic records.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To what extent does federal law protect the privacy of a college applicant’s personal information?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Applicants’ Privacy Is at Heart of Lawsuit in Illinois', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T16:53:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abb5887f-e09a-5949-ae6d-0c761b0d6b97', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abb5887f-e09a-5949-ae6d-0c761b0d6b97'}, {'abstract': 'On Thursday evening, about 20 members of Occupy Museums, a splinter group of the Occupy Wall Street protesters, made their way from the Museum of Modern Art to the New Museum of Contemporary Art to a downtown gallery, protesting what they say is the conflation of art and commerce, the snobbery of the art market, and high ticket prices at museums, which they called the “temples of the cultural elite.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/taking-the-protests-to-the-art-world/', 'snippet': 'On Thursday evening, about 20 members of Occupy Museums, a splinter group of the Occupy Wall Street protesters, made their way from the Museum of Modern Art to the New Museum of Contemporary Art to a downtown gallery, protesting what they say is t...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Occupy Wall Street movement took on the art world, sort of, this week, with a splinter group, Occupy Museums. Convened on Thursday evening through a Facebook, Twitter and Tumblr posts, about 20 people made their way from the Museum of Modern Art to the New Museum\xa0 to a downtown gallery, protesting what they say is the conflation of art and commerce, the snobbery of the art market and high ticket prices at museums, which they called the “temples of the cultural elite.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking the Protests to the Art World', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T16:54:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32802c95-1c48-5f5a-b9ed-4de230d6047a', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32802c95-1c48-5f5a-b9ed-4de230d6047a'}, {'abstract': 'Many people across the political spectrum do not support the Volcker Rule as it is now written — including Paul Volcker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/business/volcker-rule-grows-from-simple-to-complex.html', 'snippet': 'Many people across the political spectrum do not support the Volcker Rule as it is now written — including Paul Volcker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Paul Volcker called for new rules in 2009 to curb risk-taking by banks, and thus avoid making taxpayers liable in the future for the kind of reckless speculation that caused the financial crisis and resulting bailout, he outlined his proposal in a three-page letter to the president. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Volcker Rule, Once Simple, Now Boggles', 'kicker': 'Common Sense', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Volcker Rule, Once Simple, Now Boggles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T16:56:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By James B. Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f22d7139-8dc5-5b7c-9230-73833fee4b47', 'word_count': 1713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f22d7139-8dc5-5b7c-9230-73833fee4b47'}, {'abstract': '“Shakespeare in Love” moving ahead as a stage play.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/stage-version-of-shakespeare-in-love-moving-ahead/', 'snippet': '“Shakespeare in Love” moving ahead as a stage play.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Shakespeare in Love,” the 1998 romantic comedy that won seven Academy Awards, including best picture and acting honors for Gwyneth Paltrow and Judi Dench, is the latest film being eyed for adaptation to the stage. Two leading producers, Disney Theatrical Productions and the British impresario Sonia Friedman, have been holding meetings with the playwright Tom Stoppard – who shared an original screenplay Oscar for “Shakespeare in Love” with Marc Norman – and the director Jack O’Brien about the project, according to theater executives familiar with the creative discussions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stage Version of ‘Shakespeare in Love’ Moving Ahead', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T17:09:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6812eb57-8f63-5690-b4a8-e7cbbc114971', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6812eb57-8f63-5690-b4a8-e7cbbc114971'}, {'abstract': 'However you wrap it, the scarf is spring’s headlining headpiece.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/spring-ahead-the-head-scarf/', 'snippet': 'However you wrap it, the scarf is spring’s headlining headpiece.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A snapshot of spring’s best trends and a hint at what you’ll want to wear next year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spring Ahead | The Head Scarf', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T17:11:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61de0891-4425-56ce-827e-df90452744bd', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61de0891-4425-56ce-827e-df90452744bd'}, {'abstract': 'Mark F. Spangler, the former leader of the National Association of Personal Financial Advisors, is accused of investing his clients’ money into private companies without their knowledge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/your-money/financial-adviser-mark-spangler-accused-of-securities-fraud.html', 'snippet': 'Mark F. Spangler, the former leader of the National Association of Personal Financial Advisors, is accused of investing his clients’ money into private companies without their knowledge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALLEGATIONS of financial fraud have, unfortunately, become all too common in this economic downturn. But one of the latest seems worth particular note since it involves a former national chairman of the National Association of Personal Financial Advisors, who pushed the group to adopt a policy that requires members to act in the best interests of their clients and to disclose any conflicts of interest.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/your-money/22wealth/22wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/22/your-money/22wealth/22wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/your-money/22wealth/22wealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Risky Investment, Made Unwittingly', 'kicker': 'Wealth Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Risky Investment, Made Unwittingly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Placements (Non-Public Offerings) and Mini IPOs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name