'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30c4265f-4985-5542-93cc-2511d20b3789', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30c4265f-4985-5542-93cc-2511d20b3789'}, {'abstract': 'Criterion has released a Blu-ray edition of Erle C. Kenton’s 1932 “Island of Lost Souls,” a powerfully perverse adaptation of H. G. Wells’s novel “The Island of Dr. Moreau.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/movies/homevideo/new-on-blu-ray-erle-c-kentons-island-of-lost-souls.html', 'snippet': 'Criterion has released a Blu-ray edition of Erle C. Kenton’s 1932 “Island of Lost Souls,” a powerfully perverse adaptation of H. G. Wells’s novel “The Island of Dr. Moreau.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOST of the classic horror films of the early 1930s have been released and rereleased on home video to the point of surfeit and beyond. But one, in many ways the most disturbing, has remained elusive: Erle C. Kenton’s 1932 “Island of Lost Souls,” an adaptation of H. G. Wells’s novel “The Island of Dr. Moreau” so extreme in its effects that Wells himself denounced it. The film was banned in Britain until 1958, when the censors finally passed it with an X rating.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/23KEHR1/23KEHR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/23KEHR1/23KEHR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/23KEHR1/23KEHR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 780, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/23KEHR1/23KEHR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/23KEHR1/23KEHR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Island’s Inhabitants? Clearly Not Natives', 'kicker': 'DVD', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Island’s Inhabitants? Clearly Not Natives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wells, H G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DVD (Digital Versatile Disc)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blu-Ray Disc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T17:18:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'DVD', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Kehr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kehr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f864dee-8673-5deb-8921-ce700284a8f3', 'word_count': 1595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f864dee-8673-5deb-8921-ce700284a8f3'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Sullivan’s Wealth Matters column underlines the importance of doing research before handing over your money to a financial adviser.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/before-you-hand-over-your-money-for-investing/', 'snippet': 'Paul Sullivan’s Wealth Matters column underlines the importance of doing research before handing over your money to a financial adviser.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan, in his Wealth Matters column this week, writes about a Seattle investment adviser who is accused of committing securities fraud when he put his clients’ money into investments in private companies without their consent. One reason that Paul wrote about the case is that the adviser, Mark Spangler, is a former chairman of the National Association of Personal Financial Advisors, a group that requires its members to act in their clients’ best interests.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before You Hand Over Your Money for Investing', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Planners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Personal Financial Advisors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T17:19:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fb6bb18-526c-5a89-855e-ff09b8e70751', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fb6bb18-526c-5a89-855e-ff09b8e70751'}, {'abstract': 'A wide array of targets come under fire from Steven P. Jobs, the late Apple chief executive and co-founder, in a new biography.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/steve-jobs-biography-a-scorecard-of-put-downs/', 'snippet': 'A wide array of targets come under fire from Steven P. Jobs, the late Apple chief executive and co-founder, in a new biography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every authorized biography includes some score-settling by its subject. Steven P. Jobs, the late Apple co-founder and subject of Walter Isaacson’s new book, “Steve Jobs,” proves no different.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steve Jobs Biography: A Scorecard o