ls column; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Jennifer Schuessler has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/10/21/books/21bookreview_pod.html', 'snippet': 'This week, author Susan Orlean explores the life of a canine icon in her book, “Rin Tin Tin: The Life and the Legend”; Steven Heller talks about his latest Visuals column; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Jennifer Schuessler has best-sel...', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, author Susan Orlean explores the life of a canine icon in her book, “Rin Tin Tin: The Life and the Legend”; Steven Heller talks about his latest Visuals column; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Jennifer Schuessler has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Susan Orlean on her book, “Rin Tin Tin: The Life and the Legend”; Steven Heller discusses his latest Visuals column; best-seller news.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T17:38:42+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/780f6eb2-38f7-5223-8297-1bdf07ad748c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/780f6eb2-38f7-5223-8297-1bdf07ad748c'}, {'abstract': 'A longtime favorite with Italians, fennel is a crisp substitute for leafy greens when cold weather arrives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/dining/using-fennel-in-autumn-salads.html', 'snippet': 'A longtime favorite with Italians, fennel is a crisp substitute for leafy greens when cold weather arrives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THOUGH the colorful salads of summer (remember tomatoes, cucumbers, and peppers?) are justly loved, a salad in autumn — or any cold season — is a thrill. Leafy salads have their place, yes, but so do salads with no leaves or minimal leaves. Cooked vegetables make fine salads this time of year, bathed with oil and vinegar. Think beets, potatoes, carrots, artichokes. But raw vegetables can make salads that are fresh and crisp.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26KITCH_SPAN/26KITCH_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26KITCH_SPAN/26KITCH_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26KITCH_SPAN/26KITCH_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26KITCH_SPAN/26KITCH_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26KITCH_SPAN/26KITCH_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fennel Fills In for Salads in Fall', 'kicker': 'City Kitchen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fennel Fills In For Salads In Fall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fennel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T17:40:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c88f791f-092f-50a2-823f-e7fc5e35adaf', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c88f791f-092f-50a2-823f-e7fc5e35adaf'}, {'abstract': 'If Mitt Romney thinks Rick Perry remains his biggest threat, he might want to think twice about attacking him, because that only risks helping Mr. Perry position himself as the Republicans’ best alternative.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/romneys-premature-perry-panic/', 'snippet': 'If Mitt Romney thinks Rick Perry remains his biggest threat, he might want to think twice about attacking him, because that only risks helping Mr. Perry position himself as the Republicans’ best alternative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney has run a smooth, low-drama campaign so far, but its aggressive posture toward Rick Perry within the past week leaves me wondering about his strategic choices.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Premature Perry Panic', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T17:42:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f6fa08e-7107-5d69-a3c5-302d42785381', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f6fa08e-7107-5d69-a3c5-302d42785381'}, {'abstract': 'Fox won the American television rights to the World Cup in 2018 and 2022 by out-bidding ESPN, while Telemundo got the Spanish-language rights.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/fox-outbids-espn-f