violin are held in reverence by many musicians, including Jennifer Koh, who will play them at the American Academy of Arts and Letters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON the cover of his recent recording of Bach’s partitas and sonatas for unaccompanied violin Sergey Khachatryan is shrouded in darkness, head tilted back, eyes raised piously and hands pressed together above his instrument. The image is an apt representation of the reverence that musicians, scholars and listeners often bring to a discussion of these monumental works. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/23BACH1_SPAN/23BACH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/23BACH1_SPAN/23BACH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/23BACH1_SPAN/23BACH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/23BACH1_SPAN/23BACH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/23BACH1_SPAN/23BACH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Bach Laid Bare His Own Soul', 'kicker': 'Into the Music', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Bach Laid Bare His Own Soul', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN ACADEMY OF ARTS AND LETTERS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bach, Johann Sebastian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'o