e department’s interactions with Terry Thompson, and his wife, Marian.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Muskingum County Sheriff’s Department released police reports dating back to 2004 detailing the department’s interactions with Terry Thompson, and his wife, Marian.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Reports on Zanesville, Ohio, Reserve', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T19:25:41+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/a5ea9086-31fd-56ed-8784-dc51b5a8a773', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/a5ea9086-31fd-56ed-8784-dc51b5a8a773'}, {'abstract': 'The Deal Professor examines the unintended consequences of changes in corporate governance and the prospects for the future.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/corporate-governance-issues-grow-more-complex/', 'snippet': 'The Deal Professor examines the unintended consequences of changes in corporate governance and the prospects for the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s time to take stock of the corporate governance movement. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corporate Governance Issues Grow More Complex', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T19:30:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4c84239-8a67-556f-a0bc-d2952ae193d9', 'word_count': 1217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4c84239-8a67-556f-a0bc-d2952ae193d9'}, {'abstract': 'Since taking over in March, writing the Talk Q. and A. hasn’t been exactly what you could call a white-knuckle experience. Since the pages of The New York Times Magazine close more than a week before they hit newsstands, we can’t outrun the news.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/netflix-says-stop-the-presses/', 'snippet': 'Since taking over in March, writing the Talk Q. and A. hasn’t been exactly what you could call a white-knuckle experience. Since the pages of The New York Times Magazine close more than a week before they hit newsstands, we can’t outrun the news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since taking over in March, writing the Talk Q. and A. hasn’t been exactly what you could call a white-knuckle experience. Since the pages of The New York Times Magazine close more than a week before they hit newsstands, we can’t outrun the news. So this week’s interview with the C.E.O. of Netflix, Reed Hastings, provided some rare deadline drama. On Oct. 6, just as we were putting the finishing touches on the interview for the Oct. 16 issue, I got an e-mail from Netflix with the subject line “URGENT.” If the magazine ran the interview with Hastings as planned, The New York Times would look “foolish.” My contact refused to offer me any specifics about what was afoot, but he said I would understand early the following week. He was good on his word. The initial interview — in which Hastings provided his justification for spinning off the disc-only service of his company into Qwikster — would have made us look pretty dopey had we published almost a week after Netflix announced that it was ditching Qwikster altogether. So we quickly put moved up our Melissa McCarthy interview to run in Hastings’s place. Hastings talked to me three days after the Qwikster mercy killing and I drew the entirety of this week’s column from that one interview. But here’s one exchange from that earlier interview that’s worth rescuing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Netflix Says Stop the Presses!', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hastings, Reed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Melissa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DreamWorks Animation SKG Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hastings (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T19:31:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Goldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c4c3297-3659-5352-a9ff-02f961d0fb5d', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c4c3297-3659-5352-a9ff-02f961d0fb5d'}, {'abstract': 'Digitized landscapes, pixelated petals and thrilling kaleidoscopic creations flecked the runways for spring.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/spring-ahead-digital-prints/', 'snippet': 'Digitized landscapes, pixelated petals and thrilling kaleidoscopic creations flecked the runways for spring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A snapshot of spring’s best trends and a hint at what you’ll want to wear next year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spring Ahead | Digital Prints', '