 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Fine Arts (Boston)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T20:05:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith H. Dobrzynski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Dobrzynski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe7ccab8-48c6-57e9-bf71-d61eb8355312', 'word_count': 1348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe7ccab8-48c6-57e9-bf71-d61eb8355312'}, {'abstract': 'A handful of auctions of the most stunning jewelry in the world are held at night, and Christie’s event featuring the actress Elizabeth Taylor’s collection is one of them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/elizabeth-taylors-gems-to-be-auctioned-at-night.html', 'snippet': 'A handful of auctions of the most stunning jewelry in the world are held at night, and Christie’s event featuring the actress Elizabeth Taylor’s collection is one of them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No auction this season is likely to generate headlines like those from the sale of Elizabeth Taylor’s gems. Her own fascination with jewels and men’s fascination with the violet-eyed actress helped her assemble one of the world’s great collections, many pieces replete with romantic history, like La Pérégrina, a 500-year-old pear-shaped pearl that she had Cartier fashion into a necklace with rubies and diamonds, and the wedding bands from her two marriages to Richard Burton.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23JEWELS4/23JEWELS4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 967, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23JEWELS4/23JEWELS4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23JEWELS4/23JEWELS4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Selling the Sparkle as the Stars Twinkle', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Fine Arts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Selling the Sparkle As the Stars Twinkle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Christie's", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diamonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Elizabeth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T20:05:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geraldine Fabrikant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geraldine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabrikant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da280140-a928-51ad-87d0-53f97493488e', 'word_count': 1149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da280140-a928-51ad-87d0-53f97493488e'}, {'abstract': 'With the pressure of the holiday season approaching, gift-seekers can bypass museums and go straight to their shops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/museum-shops-offer-unusual-holiday-gifts.html', 'snippet': 'With the pressure of the holiday season approaching, gift-seekers can bypass museums and go straight to their shops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Museums are not just about learning and culture. Increasingly they are becoming shopping places for the committed consumer. As the holidays approach and New Yorkers are overwhelmed with family, friends, gift-buying and entertaining, museum gift shops are an obvious stop.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23SHOP2/23SHOP2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23SHOP2/23SHOP2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23SHOP2/23SHOP2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Art and Culture to Admire, and Wrap Up for the Holidays', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Fine Arts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art and Culture to Admire, and Wrap Up for the Holidays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T20:05:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geraldine Fabrikant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geraldine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabrikant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8084c02-6438-5fc3-84ee-be318a04fdc6', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8084c02-6438-5fc3-84ee-be318a04fdc6'}, {'abstract': 'Three weeks of 120 live performances will start Nov. 1., including interactive Russian Constructivist-inspired exercises in Times Square and a stationary hot-air balloon in Red Hook.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/performa-11-to-start-in-november.html', 'snippet': 'Three weeks of 120 live performances will start Nov. 1., including interactive Russian Constructivist-inspired exercises in Times Square and a stationary hot-air balloon in Red Hook.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Live performance will be erupting, and possibly disrupting, New York for three weeks starting Nov. 1, when Performa 11, a  performance art biennial, begins its fourth season. The events, mostly free and including a shamanistic dating show at El Museo del Barrio and a medieval-style rap joust at Marlborough Chelsea, will take place in theater, gallery and museum spaces as well as curbside.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23PERFORM4/23PERFORM4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23PERFORM4/23PERFORM4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23PERFORM4/23PERFORM4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23PERFORM4/23PERFORM4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23PERFORM4/23PERFORM4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Performance, Indoors and Out', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Fine Arts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Performance, Indoors and Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Performa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T20:05:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilarie M. Sheets', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6618ba82-64f6-5075-a40d-8fd7640472fe', 'word_count': 1507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6618ba82-64f6-5075-a40d-8fd7640472fe'}, {'abstract': 'Artur Walther, a collector and former partner at Goldman Sachs, travels the world in search of artists who are respected at home but haven’t yet achieved global recognition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/artur-walther-casts-global-net-in-search-of-photographers.html', 'snippet': 'Artur Walther, a collector and former partner at Goldman Sachs, travels the world in search of artists who are respected at home but haven’t yet achieved global recognition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Jo Ractliffe’s star has risen on the international art circuit during the last year, it is in many ways because of the support of the German collector Artur Walther.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23PHOTO/23PHOTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23PHOTO/23PHOTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23PHOTO/23PHOTO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23PHOTO/23PHOTO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23PHOTO/23PHOTO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Photos, Collector Casts a Global Net', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Fine Arts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Photos, Collector Casts a Global Net', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walther, Artur', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T20:05:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy Spears', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spears', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff1e3485-f5ba-56d0-bb9c-f6a315ecee5c', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff1e3485-f5ba-56d0-bb9c-f6a315ecee5c'}, {'abstract': 'A critic examines “Museum Mind,” the mental and spiritual exhaustion caused by artworks compelling intense contemplation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/an-exhibition-critic-examines-museum-mind.html', 'snippet': 'A critic examines “Museum Mind,” the mental and spiritual exhaustion caused by artworks compelling intense contemplation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The questions have been grievous, the moral issues weighty. How far should I be prepared to go in the pursuit of high-minded criticism of exhibitions and museums? Was I obligated to munch on the Cajun-fried crickets offered at New Orleans’s Insectarium in order to get the full flavor of the place? Were my perceptions off kilter if I was the only visitor to an exhibition about the history of tattoos in Philadelphia who didn’t have one of his own? Was I being unfair to Coca-Cola’s self-celebratory museum in Atlanta because I found the highlights were soda samples it offered from around the world? Was I overly fair to the Creation Museum in Kentucky, which treated the Bible as natural history and natural history as myth, when I marveled at its skewed alternate universe?', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23critic-slideshow-slide-4DIO/23critic-slideshow-slide-4DIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23critic-slideshow-slide-4DIO/23critic-slideshow-slide-4DIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23critic-slideshow-slide-4DIO/23critic-slideshow-slide-4DIO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23critic-slideshow-slide-4DIO/23critic-slideshow-slide-4DIO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23critic-slideshow-slide-4DIO/23critic-slideshow-slide-4DIO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Extreme Museum: The Rigors of Contemplation', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Extreme Museum: The Rigors of Contemplation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T20:05:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Rothstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fe089ce-145b-5c7e-8743-4ed834a8a71e', 'word_count': 1388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fe089ce-145b-5c7e-8743-4ed834a8a71e'}, {'abstract': 'Young arts professionals use Twitter, Facebook, and Meetup.com to track down lectures, openings and each other.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/social-networking-among-young-arts-professionals.html', 'snippet': 'Young arts professionals use Twitter, Facebook, and Meetup.com to track down lectures, openings and each other.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With so many museums, exhibits, art galleries and lectures to choose from every day, how does a busy young arts professional keep up? For Francesca Merlino and about two dozen of her colleagues who work for museums and arts groups in New York City, it’s following each other’s 140-character updates on Twitter and the hashtag, #artstech.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23MEETUP2/23MEETUP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23MEETUP2/23MEETUP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23MEETUP2/23MEETUP2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23MEETUP2/23MEETUP2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23MEETUP2/23MEETUP2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rendezvous With Art and Ardent', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Fine Arts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rendezvous With Art and Ardent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Meetup.com', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T20:05:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf2f702b-4c49-577e-bff8-a4660b3c4623', 'word_count': 1562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf2f702b-4c49-577e-bff8-a4660b3c4623'}, {'abstract': 'With cocktail parties, restaurants, and attention-getting events like the Rubin Museum of Art’s sleep-over, New York museums are grabbing for a slice of the city’s nightlife.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/museums-brave-new-turf-after-hours.html', 'snippet': 'With cocktail parties, restaurants, and attention-getting events like the Rubin Museum of Art’s sleep-over, New York museums are grabbing for a slice of the city’s nightlife.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Darcey Howard had her reasons for showing up at the Rubin Museum of Art in her pajamas. Seeing the Himalayan paintings and multilayered manuscript pages was not one of them.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cr