None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T20:05:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/a81bfab8-67f3-5dd8-bbd5-c9077693845b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/a81bfab8-67f3-5dd8-bbd5-c9077693845b'}, {'abstract': 'Next month, the Metropolitan Museum of Art will open its New Galleries for the Art of the Arab Lands, Turkey, Iran, Central Asia and Later South Asia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/islamic-treasures-at-the-metropolitan-museum-of-art.html', 'snippet': 'Next month, the Metropolitan Museum of Art will open its New Galleries for the Art of the Arab Lands, Turkey, Iran, Central Asia and Later South Asia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite the current trend for abbreviated titles and short, snappy messages, the Metropolitan Museum of Art is calling its majestic suite of 15 newly renovated spaces, which open on Nov. 1, the New Galleries for the Art of the Arab Lands, Turkey, Iran, Central Asia and Later South Asia. It’s a mouthful but an intentional one. The curators there are trying to underscore the diversity, richness and interconnectedness of the arts that reflect a melting pot of different cultures.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23islamic-slideshow-slide-UCGK/23islamic-slideshow-slide-UCGK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23islamic-slideshow-slide-UCGK/23islamic-slideshow-slide-UCGK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23islamic-slideshow-slide-UCGK/23islamic-slideshow-slide-UCGK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Islamic Objects of Desire', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Fine Arts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Islamic Objects of Desire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T20:06:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/578f6dc2-7f6d-5eef-a359-43067504cbb7', 'word_count': 1020, 'uri': 'nyt://article/578f6dc2-7f6d-5eef-a359-43067504cbb7'}, {'abstract': 'A confluence of exhibits of Latin American art starts next month in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/latin-american-art-rediscovered-again.html', 'snippet': 'A confluence of exhibits of Latin American art starts next month in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In November, the Art Dealers Association of America will start its new season of collector forums with “Latin American Art in Global Collections” at the Morgan Library and Museum. The panel will be timed to the Pinta, a Latin American Art fair now in its fifth year that coincides with Christie’s and Sotheby’s Latin American art auctions. Also next month, the Museum of Modern Art will open an exhibition devoted to Diego Rivera’s murals. Five years ago, the museum appointed its first curator of Latin American art.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23SUBLATIN1/23SUBLATIN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 807, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23SUBLATIN1/23SUBLATIN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/arts/artsspecial/23SUBLATIN1/23SUBLATIN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Latin American Art, Rediscovered Again', 'kicker': 'Special Section: Fine Arts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Latin American Art, Rediscovered Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'El Museo del Barrio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T20:06:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsec