forms his work with techniques from other disciplines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Near the end of his solo show “Out of Time,” the Irish step dancer Colin Dunne shares some old video of himself. In it he is a world champion. He is on television. He is 10. He responds awkwardly to stock questions. He holds up his chin as he dances expertly, stiff and orthodox. The moment is awfully cute, but also disturbing in context. You worry about what will happen to that boy, and what already has. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/DUNNE/DUNNE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/DUNNE/DUNNE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/DUNNE/DUNNE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 584, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/DUNNE/DUNNE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/DUNNE/DUNNE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'His Life After ‘Riverdance’ Is a Braid of Traditions', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'His Life After ‘Riverdance’ Is a Braid of Traditions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunne, Colin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Riverdance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T21:30:48