alue': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T23:24:49+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barakat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/4a0932ba-8f05-5785-9404-8ddb044eb954', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/4a0932ba-8f05-5785-9404-8ddb044eb954'}, {'abstract': 'On Thursday the Pennsylvania Ballet presented the North American premiere of Alexei Ratmansky’s “Jeu de Cartes.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/arts/dance/jeu-de-cartes-by-the-pennsylvania-ballet-review.html', 'snippet': 'On Thursday the Pennsylvania Ballet presented the North American premiere of Alexei Ratmansky’s “Jeu de Cartes.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — Does a month go by without some kind of premiere by the choreographer Alexei Ratmansky? In April the Bolshoi danced the world premiere of his three-act “Lost Illusions;” in May American Ballet Theater presented the world premiere of “Dumbarton,” and in June, its first New York performances of his full-length “Bright Stream”; in July the Mariinsky Ballet gave New York its first view of his “Anna Karenina” and “Little Humpbacked Horse”; and in September the Paris Opera Ballet gave the world premiere of “Psyché,” based on the Greek myth. On Thursday the Pennsylvania Ballet presented the North American premiere of Mr. Ratmansky’s “Jeu de Cartes.” It would be nice to think the guy took August off as a well-earned vacation, but I wouldn’t bank on it. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/GAME-SILO/GAME-SILO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 735, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/GAME-SILO/GAME-SILO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/GAME-SILO/GAME-SILO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Month, Another Premiere', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Month, Another Premiere', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania Ballet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratmansky, Alexei', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T23:29:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/079064c1-4fd1-5ca9-ad74-5eef949ac0cf', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/079064c1-4fd1-5ca9-ad74-5eef949ac0cf'}, {'abstract': 'Commiseration was on the agenda at Irving Plaza as the country-music singer Dierks Bentley was greeted by a sea of raised Bud Lights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/arts/music/dierks-bentley-at-irving-plaza-review.html', 'snippet': 'Commiseration was on the agenda at Irving Plaza as the country-music singer Dierks Bentley was greeted by a sea of raised Bud Lights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the rate Nashville is emasculating, you can practically call Dierks Bentley one of the tough guys these days. He’s not a fighter, or a self-loather, or much of a mean talker, but there’s a steady flow of insouciance running through his songs, a sense of lawlessness as experienced by someone who is very mindful of the law, and would like to dodge it just a bit, if that’s O.K. with you. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/DIERKS/DIERKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/DIERKS/DIERKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/DIERKS/DIERKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guy’s Guy, Keeping the Kegs Flowing', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guy’s Guy, Keeping The Kegs Flowing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bentley, Dierks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-21T23:29:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/199a7015-66bf-551c-94dd-92ca8b17dda6', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/199a7015-66bf-551c-94dd-92ca8b17dda6'}, {'abstract': "As NATO's mission in Libya is complete, did it meet or exceed its mandate?", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/africa