 manages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/us/wyoming-dealt-a-setback-over-roads-on-public-lands.html', 'snippet': 'The State of Wyoming was dealt a setback after a federal appeals court ruled that the Forest Service has broad jurisdiction in setting the balance of uses on the lands that it manages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — More than a decade after the Clinton administration proposed cordoning off tens of millions of acres of public lands in the West from road development, setting off a ferocious debate about wilderness and human uses of the land, a federal appeals court in Denver upheld the government’s authority on Friday in a sweeping rejection of the opposition.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ruling Backs Forest Service in Limiting Roads in the Wild', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ruling Backs Forest Service In Limiting Roads in the Wild', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Forest Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wyoming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T00:01:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/312e16bf-6c01-5464-a4cf-97f933b8360c', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/312e16bf-6c01-5464-a4cf-97f933b8360c'}, {'abstract': 'Some things happen at Trash Talk shows that don’t happen at other CMJ shows.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/at-a-polite-cmj-trash-talks-aggression-is-a-relief/', 'snippet': 'Some things happen at Trash Talk shows that don’t happen at other CMJ shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some things happen at Trash Talk shows that don’t happen at other CMJ shows. Theirs is the show most likely to start at an insanely late hour, the show where you are most likely to get punched in the head by the lead singer, the show where you are most likely to receive a flier marked #OCCUPYCMJ bemoaning the stranglehold of corporations over various aspects of the music business, from retail outlets to radio to touring.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At a Polite CMJ, Trash Talk’s Aggression Is a Relief', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T00:08:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afbdc7b2-eb19-551d-9d15-d52640417923', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afbdc7b2-eb19-551d-9d15-d52640417923'}, {'abstract': 'There is a reason candidates court big donors: The net share of their donations is far greater than from low-dollar donors.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/bachmanns-lack-of-big-donors-could-hinder-campaign/', 'snippet': 'There is a reason candidates court big donors: The net share of their donations is far greater than from low-dollar donors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a reason candidates court big donors. Yes, they have more money. But more important, the net share of their donations is far greater than from low-dollar donors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann’s Lack of Big Donors Could Hinder Campaign', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rollins, Ed', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T00:10:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4eeba1bb-b726-5a88-9ee9-43331eef9bcf', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4eeba1bb-b726-5a88-9ee9-43331eef9bcf'}, {'abstract': 'While Republicans talked tough on immigration, the Obama administration deported a record number of illegal immigrants.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/battle-of-the-borders/', 'snippet': 'While Republicans talked tough on immigration, the Obama administration deported a record number of illegal immigrants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is probably safe to bet that the tradition of heated arguments over immigration began millennia ago, when the first country drew a line in the sand. \xa0But the past week in the United States of America has been a hot one, at least by any recent comparison.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Battle of the Borders', 'kicker': 'The Thread', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T00:11:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Catapano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catapano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04b59eb6-c2ca-50dc-910a-3ac59a42aa46', 'word_count': 1367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04b59eb6-c2ca-50dc-910a-3ac59a42aa46'}, {'abstract': 'The agreement came as thousands of Turkish troops began the second day of a major offensive against Kurdish rebels in southeastern Turkey and Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/world/europe/turkey-and-iran-agree-to-cooperate-against-kurdish-rebels.html', 'snippet': 'The agreement came as thousands of Turkish troops began the second day of a major offensive against Kurdish rebels in southeastern Turkey and Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Turkey and Iran agreed Friday to cooperate against separatist Kurdish violence along their borders, while thousands of Turkish troops began the second day of a major offensive against Kurdish rebels in southeastern Turkey and Iraq. Foreign Minister Ahmet Davutoglu, speaking at a news conference with his Iranian counterpart, Ali Akbar Salehi, said Turkey and Iran would share intelligence and convene a joint security council. “We will work together in a common action plan until we entirely eradicate this threat of terrorism,” Mr. Davutoglu said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkey and Iran Agree to Cooperate Against Kurdish Rebels on Borders', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkey and Iran Agree to Cooperate Against Kurdish Rebels on Borders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T00:18:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sebnem Arsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sebnem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb5a11a4-8ffc-560b-81cd-66d31f2db863', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb5a11a4-8ffc-560b-81cd-66d31f2db863'}, {'abstract': 'Quarterback Carson Palmer, acquired in a trade with the Bengals, has not played since January, but fans are calling for him to start immediately.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/sports/football/carson-palmer-faces-obstacles-to-playing-for-raiders.html', 'snippet': 'Quarterback Carson Palmer, acquired in a trade with the Bengals, has not played since January, but fans are calling for him to start immediately.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALAMEDA, Calif. — The sound bite was fun, and that is surel