tract': 'An abundance of applause for President Dmitri A. Medvedev of Russia at an event on a college campus drew complaints from students who said the audience had been hand picked.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/world/europe/staged-event-in-moscow-criticized-in-social-media.html', 'snippet': 'An abundance of applause for President Dmitri A. Medvedev of Russia at an event on a college campus drew complaints from students who said the audience had been hand picked.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — At about 4 p.m. on Thursday, Russia’s president, Dmitri A. Medvedev, stepped into a packed lecture hall at Moscow State University’s venerable journalism department. Applause washed over him, proof that progressive, social media-savvy young people still look to him as a standard-bearer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Social Media Raise Curtain on Staged Event in Moscow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Social Media Raise Curtain On Staged Event in Moscow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moscow State University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medvedev, Dmitri A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Journalism Schools', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T00:51:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe