nytimes.com/2011/10/22/world/europe/mi5-references-emerge-in-britain-phone-hacking-suit.html', 'snippet': 'A lawsuit claims that Glenn Mulcaire, a private detective for the British tabloid The News of the World, has notes that mention a secret government file of a royal family friend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A British private detective at the center of the phone hacking scandal that has shaken Rupert Murdoch’s media empire cited the MI5 file of a close friend of Princes William and Harry in notes he kept on his work for the tabloid The News of the World, according to a suit filed in London. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MI5 References Emerge in Phone Hacking Lawsuit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'MI5 References Emerge In Phone Hacking Lawsuit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mulcaire, Glenn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detectives (Private)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T00:53:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jo Becker and Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Becker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d99b68ae-ee05-5e41-a421-87689a1f1172', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d99b68ae-ee05-5e41-a421-87689a1f1172'}, {'abstract': 'Where Occupy Wall Street and the Tea Party differ is in where they place the blame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/us/politics/wall-st-protest-isnt-like-ours-tea-party-says.html', 'snippet': 'Where Occupy Wall Street and the Tea Party differ is in where they place the blame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a Republican candidate forum outside Fort Worth last week, a Tea Party activist turned Senate candidate proclaimed the Occupy Wall Street protesters “unemployed, uneducated and uninformed.” To which the conservative radio host moderating the panel added, mirthfully, “This is the first occupation many of these people have seen in years.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/us/JP-TEAPARTY-1/JP-TEAPARTY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/22/us/JP-TEAPARTY-1/JP-TEAPARTY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/us/JP-TEAPARTY-1/JP-TEAPARTY-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/us/JP-TEAPARTY-1/JP-TEAPARTY-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/22/us/JP-TEAPARTY-1/JP-TEAPARTY-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall St. Protest Isn’t Like Ours, Tea Party Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wall St. Protest Isn’t Like Ours, Tea Party Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T00:58:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Zernike', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zernike', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bccc9cd-4db6-59ad-bafc-115ab18ac0d1', 'word_count': 1302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bccc9cd-4db6-59ad-bafc-115ab18ac0d1'}, {'abstract': 'A Quaker, a close friend to Lincoln and the only sitting senator to be killed in combat.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/senator-bakers-waveless-shore/', 'snippet': 'A Quaker, a close friend to Lincoln and the only sitting senator to be killed in combat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Edward Dickinson Baker, a close friend and sometimes political rival of Lincoln’s, had no fear of war. In 1832, he left his fledgling law practice in Illinois to participate in the Black Hawk War, and, in 1846, he resigned his Illinois Congressional seat to serve as a colonel of the Fourth Illinois Infantry in the Mexican War.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senator Baker’s Waveless Shore', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T0