 to the war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s announcement on Friday that the last American soldier will leave Iraq by year’s end signals a welcome end to a war that was started under false pretenses and went on far too long — killing more than 4,400 Americans and many more thousands of Iraqis and costing $1 trillion over nearly nine years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'End Date for Iraq', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'End Date for Iraq', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T01:04:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1141591c-85c1-5b94-8cae-d76eb3dd59e2', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1141591c-85c1-5b94-8cae-d76eb3dd59e2'}, {'abstract': 'Allen Craig has joined Dusty Rhodes of the 1954 Giants as the only players with run-scoring pinch-hits in three straight games in a postseason.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/sports/baseball/cardinals-craig-ties-a-postseason-pinch-hitting-mark.html', 'snippet': 'Allen Craig has joined Dusty Rhodes of the 1954 Giants as the only players with run-scoring pinch-hits in three straight games in a postseason.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In perhaps the most famous pinch-hitting moment in postseason history, Kirk Gibson of the Los Angeles Dodgers limped into the batter’s box against Dennis Eckersley of the Oakland A’s in Game 1 of the 1988 World Series. Despite a badly injured knee, and despite facing the game’s most dominant reliever, Gibson was able to put a charge into a 3-2 pitch, hitting a two-run homer to right field that gave the Dodgers a 5-4 victory.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/sports/y-craig-1/y-craig-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/22/sports/y-craig-1/y-craig-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/sports/y-craig-1/y-craig-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/sports/y-craig-1/y-craig-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/22/sports/y-craig-1/y-craig-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Postseason Pinch-Hit Star, Three Games Running', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Postseason Pinch-Hit Star, Three Games Running', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rhodes, Dusty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Craig, Allen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_da