New York. He lives there with his wife, Barbara Luisi, and their son, Aldo, 13; Mr. Luisi’s two other children are grown and studying abroad. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23ROUTINE-3/23ROUTINE-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23ROUTINE-3/23ROUTINE-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23ROUTINE-3/23ROUTINE-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brunch, Books and Family Time', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brunch, Books and Family Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luisi, Fabio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T01:20:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72e7214d-a0aa-5196-93dc-fdb15382871b', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72e7214d-a0aa-5196-93dc-fdb15382871b'}, {'abstract': 'Anita Hill’s courage opened the way for meaningful progress against sex discrimination in the workplace. It is a legacy worth celebrating.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/opinion/sexual-harassment-20-years-later.html', 'snippet': 'Anita Hill’s courage opened the way for meaningful progress against sex discrimination in the workplace. It is a legacy worth celebrating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty years ago this month, Anita Hill stepped into the glare of the national spotlight, testifying before the all-male Senate Judiciary Committee about the vulgar sexual advances she said she endured a decade earlier while working at two government agencies for Clarence Thomas, the nominee to the Supreme Court.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sexual Harassment 20 Years Later', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sexual Harassment 20 Years Later', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Anita', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Clarence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Equal Employment Opportunity Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T01:26:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/77e0c808-8128-5bc3-895e-e19d8cca61a3', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77e0c808-8128-5bc3-895e-e19d8cca61a3'}, {'abstract': 'With New York City far behind cities like San Francisco, there generally is nowhere to put a plastic lunch container but a wastebasket.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/nyregion/on-recycling-nyc-goes-from-leader-to-laggard.html', 'snippet': 'With New York City far behind cities like San Francisco, there generally is nowhere to put a plastic lunch container but a wastebasket.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT was warm and sunny on a recent Tuesday and the lunchtime crowd in Bryant Park was in full swarm. Hundreds of Midtown workers sat on the grass or at round outdoor tables sunbathing, talking on cellphones and typing away on laptops. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23RECYCLE_SPAN/23RECYCLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23RECYCLE_SPAN/23RECYCLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23RECYCLE_SPAN/23RECYCLE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23RECYCLE_SPAN/23RECYCLE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23RECYCLE_SPAN/23RECYCLE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lunch, Landfills and What I Tossed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lunch, Landfills And What I Tossed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Compost', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T01:28:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca8ffb1d-3250-553f-abf7-3efc0992a083', 'word_count': 2605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca8ffb1d-3250-553f-abf7-3efc0992a083'}, {'abstract': 'We hope Governor Cuomo is finally taking interest in the challenges facing the M.T.A. and the Port Authority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/opinion/governor-cuomos-appointments.html', 'snippet': 'We hope Governor Cuomo is finally taking interest in the challenges facing the M.T.A. and the Port Authority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo has shown little interest in the challenges facing the Metropolitan Transportation Authority, which runs New York City area subways, buses and commuter trains, or the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey, which manages the area’s ports, airports, bridges and tunnels. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Governor Cuomo’s Choices', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Governor Cuomo&#8217;s Choices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lhota, Joseph J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foye, Patrick J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T01:31:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a420d1c-82fe-519d-88f2-490e06883fea', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a420d1c-82fe-519d-88f2-490e06883fea'}, {'abstract': 'If Occupy Wall Street were a rock band, then Nirvana would come closest to representing its passion and angst.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/opinion/blow-occupy-apalooza-strikes-a-chord.html', 'snippet': 'If Occupy Wall Street were a rock band, then Nirvana would come closest to representing its passion and angst.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thursday night I spoke to a young woman in Brooklyn who was having dinner and planning the next day. Between a morning boot camp workout at the local Y.M.C.A. and an evening meeting with friends for drinks, she was planning her first trek to Zuccotti Park to take part in the Occupy Wall Street protests.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/201