, 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fe82f96-6483-5d78-863f-5d4f3dd41cb3', 'word_count': 1018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fe82f96-6483-5d78-863f-5d4f3dd41cb3'}, {'abstract': 'New York Times journalists who covered the war in Iraq are reflecting on their time there on the day that President Obama announced the end of a nine-year military engagement.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/correspondents-reflect-on-the-war-in-iraq/', 'snippet': 'New York Times journalists who covered the war in Iraq are reflecting on their time there on the day that President Obama announced the end of a nine-year military engagement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Correspondents who covered the war in Iraq are reflecting on their time there on the day that President Obama announced that American soldiers would leave Iraq by the end of the year, ending a nearly nine-year military engagement. The president appeared to leave open the possibility that a deal could still be negotiated to allow military trainers to work in the country, though it would likely be a limited number. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Correspondents Reflect on the War in Iraq', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T01:36:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin and Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'o