ats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/mets-to-play-yankees-in-spring-training/', 'snippet': 'After a 16-year hiatus, the crosstown rivals will resume playing each other in Florida.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a 16-year hiatus, the Mets and Yankees will resume playing spring-training games against each other next March, said a Yankees official who declined to be identified. The teams are tentatively scheduled to play games at each other’s complexes in Port St. Lucie and Tampa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets to Play Yankees in Spring Training', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinbrenner, George M 3d', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T02:07:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Coffey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coffey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efcedfaa-5d26-5141-b69a-4cb61d6fa3a1', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efcedfaa-5d26-5141-b69a-4cb61d6fa3a1'}, {'abstract': 'Friday was a day for regrouping and reassessing after negotiations between N.B.A. players and owners broke down on Thursday with no further sessions scheduled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/sports/basketball/with-nba-talks-halted-sides-predict-a-meeting-next-week.html', 'snippet': 'Friday was a day for regrouping and reassessing after negotiations between N.B.A. players and owners broke down on Thursday with no further sessions scheduled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hotel conference rooms had been vacated, perhaps turned over to a dental convention, or a cosmetics fair, or a symposium on gastroenterology. The charts devoted to “BRI” and luxury-tax thresholds had been packed up for another day, another meeting, another hotel.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Talks at a Halt, Silence Reigns', 'kicker': 'On Basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Talks At a Halt, Silence Reigns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Derek', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Adam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T02:11:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c510893-1305-53e4-ab40-f10cf8d96d2f', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c510893-1305-53e4-ab40-f10cf8d96d2f'}, {'abstract': 'Walter Isaacson’s biography of Steve Jobs is a clear, elegant and concise book of record.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/books/steve-jobs-by-walter-isaacson-review.html', 'snippet': 'Walter Isaacson’s biography of Steve Jobs is a clear, elegant and concise book of record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Steve Jobs anointed Walter Isaacson as his authorized biographer in 2009, he took Mr. Isaacson to see the Mountain View, Calif., house in which he had lived as a boy. He pointed out its “clean design” and “awesome little features.” He praised the developer, Joseph Eichler, who built more than 11,000 homes in California subdivisions, for making an affordable product on a mass-market scale. And he showed Mr. Isaacson the stockade fence built 50 years earlier by his father, Paul Jobs.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/BOOK/BOOK-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/22/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Making the iBio for Apple’s Genius', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making The iBio For Apple’s Genius', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isaacson, Walter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T02:11:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab44e70a-ce36-599b-86ae-ad6b33d2bca0', 'word_count': 1281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab44e70a-ce36-599b-86ae-ad6b33d2bca0'}, {'abstract': 'At Pranzi, on the ground floor of the Trump Tower at City Center, the décor is coolly modern and the menu hews to tradition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/nyregion/at-pranzi-authentic-italian-in-a-modern-setting.html', 'snippet': 'At Pranzi, on the ground floor of the Trump Tower at City Center, the décor is coolly modern and the menu hews to tradition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY lasting impression of Pranzi formed as I emerged from its formal ristorante, on the ground floor of the Trump Tower at City Center, to exit through its informal enoteca. In the jam-packed front room, a D.J. sporting French nautical stripes and tinted glasses was pushing his fun agenda from the keyboard of his bright orange Apple laptop, and the crowd — in fine spirits on a Thursday night — was loving it. We lingered for a minute, smiling, then a young man in a svelte suit held the door and with a little flourish of his hand, thanked us in the nicest way for coming.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23DINEWE1/23DINEWE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23DINEWE1/23DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23DINEWE1/23DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75,