experience, one that calls to mind the heat and keen light of the Mediterranean. However, the interior of this restaurant in Ewing, with a sunroom addition that makes up most of the dining room — dimly lighted in the evening — says New Jersey.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23DINENJ1/23DINENJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23DINENJ1/23DINENJ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23DINENJ1/23DINENJ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Authentic Greek Fare, but Distinctly New Jersey', 'kicker': 'New Jersey Dining | Ewing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Authentic Greek Fare, But Distinctly New Jersey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T02:49:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Cook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cook', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/68913356-9ed7-53a3-b0ee-ae64ea7b9fd6', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68913356-9ed7-53a3-b0ee-ae64ea7b9fd6'}, {'abstract': 'The nuclear reactors shut down by the Aug. 23 earthquake on the East Coast, will probably be allowed to reopen within weeks, a senior official of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/science/earth/22brfs-NUCLEARREACT_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The nuclear reactors shut down by the Aug. 23 earthquake on the East Coast, will probably be allowed to reopen within weeks, a senior official of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The North Anna nuclear reactors in Mineral, the only ones shut down by the Aug. 23 earthquake on the East Coast, will probably be allowed to reopen within weeks, a senior official of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said Friday. After a two-month, $21 million inspection, staff engineers told the commission at a two-hour briefing that the plant suffered only cosmetic damage. The limited damage led the plant’s operator, Dominion, and the commission to debate whether their standard for measuring a quake’s strength — based simply on ground motion — was the best one. That measure indicated that the ground motion on Aug. 23 exceeded what the reactors were designed for. But when engineers measured the quake by the total amount of energy it delivered, the quake was far too weak to produce significant damage. (The energy measure is based on both the shaking and its duration.) Most of the cosmetic damage found at the plant was limited to concrete, Dominion said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Virginia: Nuclear Reactors Expected to Reopen Soon', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | SOUTH', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Virginia: Nuclear Reactors Expected to Reopen Soon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mineral (Va)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T02:55:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f0d5a3d-1281-55ef-bfaa-82cc12cfae7c', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f0d5a3d-1281-55ef-bfaa-82cc12cfae7c'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense has identified 1,797 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/us/us-military-deaths-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense has identified 1,797 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 1,797 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the deaths of the following American this week: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T02:58:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': 