lents to the mound when he throws out the first pitch before Game 3.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/sports/baseball/a-rangers-fan-whos-hard-to-top.html', 'snippet': 'Dirk Nowitzki, the Dallas Mavericks’ star forward, will bring his basketball talents to the mound when he throws out the first pitch before Game 3.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARLINGTON, Tex. — At 7 feet, Dirk Nowitzki likely stands as the biggest fan of the Texas Rangers. And like any truly obsessed follower, Nowitzki refers to his favorite team in the first person plural. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/sports/nowitzki-refer/nowitzki-refer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/sports/nowitzki-refer/nowitzki-refer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/22/sports/nowitzki-refer/nowitzki-refer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rangers Fan Who’s Hard to Top', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rangers Fan Who’s Hard to Top', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nowitzki, Dirk', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T03:26:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Spousta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spousta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a244afb4-6866-5509-a1b9-a64748279d7d', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a244afb4-6866-5509-a1b9-a64748279d7d'}, {'abstract': 'Friends currently has a handful of very good suggestive dance-punk and indie-pop songs, but they seem capable of eccentricities and power down the line.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/21/in-friends-suggestive-notes-hints-of-future-power/', 'snippet': 'Friends currently has a handful of very good suggestive dance-punk and indie-pop songs, but they seem capable of eccentricities and power down the line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So much of what’s on offer at CMJ is raw material — maybe the band’s got it all figured out, more likely it doesn’t. If it doesn’t work, maybe it’ll try again next year. Maybe it’ll reinvent itself, or break up and reconfigure before trying again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Friends’ Suggestive Notes, Hints of Future Power', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T03:29:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dedcbd06-c186-551f-915a-b900e0e84e5a', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dedcbd06-c186-551f-915a-b900e0e84e5a'}, {'abstract': 'The Westport Country Playhouse’s production of Shakespeare’s “Twelfth Night” runs through Nov. 5.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/nyregion/twelfth-night-at-the-westport-country-playhouse-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Westport Country Playhouse’s production of Shakespeare’s “Twelfth Night” runs through Nov. 5.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The way things are going, William Shakespeare may soon be known as a writer of musicals. Last month, the Two River Theater Company in New Jersey opened a production of “Much Ado About Nothing” with at least three songs, accompanied by cast members on various musical instruments. Now along comes the Westport Country Playhouse’s very pretty, very funny and very lilting production of “Twelfth Night, or What You Will.”', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23ARTSCT-1/23ARTSCT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23ARTSCT-1/23ARTSCT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/nyregion/23ARTSCT-1/23ARTSCT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Changing Clothes for Love and Survival', 'kicker': 'Arts | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Changing Clothes For Love and Survival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wes