a'}, {'abstract': 'Authorities issued a temporary ban on stimulants used to make a type of street drug known as bath salts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/us/dea-bans-chemicals-used-in-bath-salts.html', 'snippet': 'Authorities issued a temporary ban on stimulants used to make a type of street drug known as bath salts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Drug Enforcement Administration took emergency action on Friday to ban three synthetic stimulants used to make products\xa0that are marketed at head shops and on the Web as “bath salts,” but are actually used as recreational drugs that mimic the effects of cocaine, LSD and methamphetamine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'D.E.A. Bans Chemicals Used in ‘Bath Salts’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bath Salts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drug Enforcement Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T04:27:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee2349ef-d218-535a-a95c-8d42ce14af22', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee2349ef-d218-535a-a95c-8d42ce14af22'}, {'abstract': 'According to an American who has lived in Iran since he assassinated a former member of the Shah’s government in the Washington suburbs in 1980, an alleged Iranian plot to kill the Saudi ambassador in Washington “just makes no sense at all.”', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/american-who-killed-for-iran-in-1980-resurfaces-to-comment-on-alleged-plot/', 'snippet': 'According to an American who has lived in Iran since he assassinated a former member of the Shah’s government in the Washington suburbs in 1980, an alleged Iranian plot to kill the Saudi ambassador in Washington “just makes no sense at all.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Justice Department announced last week that an undercover agent in Mexico had disrupted an Iranian plot to assassinate the Saudi ambassador in Washington, using members of Mexican drug cartel recruited by a used car salesman, officials in Tehran dismissed the charges as fiction, and several prominent American experts on Iran also expressed their doubts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Who Killed for Iran in 1980 Resurfaces to Comment on Alleged Plot', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salahuddin, Dawud', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T04:35:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faf611af-d3fa-5729-8638-77d814ab61bd', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faf611af-d3fa-5729-8638-77d814ab61bd'}, {'abstract': 'Top stories from around the country.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/newswallah-bharat-edition-7/', 'snippet': 'Top stories from around the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kashmir: An inquiry by an RTI activist found that the University of Kashmir has spent more than 2.16 crore Indian rupees, or 21.6 million (about $400,000), on vehicles for the university staff but has disbursed only 59 lakh rupees, or 5.9 million, towards student scholarships and fellowships in the last five years. The report said that 36 vehicles, mostly SUVs, were purchased, including a bulletproof car, which was bought for 9.25 lakh\xa0 rupees (about $20,000)(Kashmir Live).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Bharat Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T06:34:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24a24a5b-fe9e-5ef4-9a0c-3796dbd66341', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24a24a5b-fe9e-5ef4-9a0c-3796dbd66341'}, {'abstract': 'A Mumbai native returns, and starts to hate the person he becomes.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/why-i-left-india-again/', 'snippet': 'A Mumbai native returns, and starts to hate the person he becomes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Hindi movie on my “return to India” flight on Dec. 13th, 2006 was “Swades” (literally: “My country,” a story about a patriotic NASA engineer who returns to India to help improve his homeland).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why I Left India (Again)', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gladwell, Malcolm', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T06:58:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sumedh Mungee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sumedh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mungee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8aec057b-8dfd-574a-8e05-865595bad102', 'word_count': 1134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8aec057b-8dfd-574a-8e05-865595bad102'}, {'abstract': 'Charles M. Conlon has been deemed “the greatest baseball photographer.” Fred R. Conrad and Kerri MacDonald talked with Connie McCabe, a photograph conservator who worked on the second book of Mr. Conlon’s pictures.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/charles-m-conlon-baseball-photographs/', 'snippet': 'Charles M. Conlon has been deemed “the greatest baseball photographer.” Fred R. Conrad and Kerri MacDonald talked with Connie McCabe, a photograph conservator who worked on the second book of Mr. Conlon’s pictures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charles M. Conlon has been deemed — on Lens, if not elsewhere — “the greatest baseball photographer.” From 1904 to 1942, Mr. Conlon shot some 30,000 pictures of America’s pastime. In 1993, The Sporting News published “Baseball’s Golden Age,” a collection of his work. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Productive At-Bat for a 