d1cd38cbd', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15bab465-1537-5c39-9d7b-a24d1cd38cbd'}, {'abstract': 'Roy Keane, the former captain of Manchester United, handicaps Sunday’s Manchester derby against first-place City.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/the-manchester-derby-2/', 'snippet': 'Roy Keane, the former captain of Manchester United, handicaps Sunday’s Manchester derby against first-place City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roy Keane remembers his first as if it were yesterday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 161st Manchester Derby', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T13:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4f8b808-65c0-5a72-bdf8-598ba2dca0c8', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4f8b808-65c0-5a72-bdf8-598ba2dca0c8'}, {'abstract': 'Manufacturer iLuv has an audio plug that accommodates two sets of headphones with a separate volume control for each.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/sharing-audio-on-pods-pads-and-phones/', 'snippet': 'Manufacturer iLuv has an audio plug that accommodates two sets of headphones with a separate volume control for each.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The iPad is a great way to watch movies on, say, a plane trip. But if you are traveling with someone, you endanger your domestic bliss by hogging the entertainment and walling yourself off (“Sorry, dear, you’ll have to amuse yourself by re-reading the SkyMall catalog while I watch ‘Bridesmaids.’”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharing Audio on Pods, Pads and Phones', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Headphones and Headsets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T13:20:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8dbda27-173c-5ed3-8829-3e4957dadda2', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8dbda27-173c-5ed3-8829-3e4957dadda2'}, {'abstract': 'Shaquille O’Neal, an analyst on TNT, was hopeful there would soon be real N.B.A. games.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/30-seconds-with-shaquille-oneal-off-the-court-but-still-going-at-full-speed/', 'snippet': 'Shaquille O’Neal, an analyst on TNT, was hopeful there would soon be real N.B.A. games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shaquille O’Neal was in Manhattan the other day, dunking, grabbing rebounds and even making his free throws. After announcing his retirement in June, was he preparing for a comeback after the lockout? No, that was the virtual Shaq; the real O’Neal was controlling his moves on the new digital download of EA Sports NBA JAM: On Fire Edition. O’Neal, an analyst on TNT, was hopeful there would soon be real N.B.A. games.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '30 Seconds With Shaquille O’Neal: Off the Court, but Still Going at Full Speed', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neal, Shaquille", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T14:25:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Brescia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brescia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99979a71-2877-5f2e-a6c0-4a4adf2aa9d3', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99979a71-2877-5f2e-a6c0-4a4adf2aa9d3'}, {'abstract': 'Not better in the Baltics.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/european-wage-update/', 'snippet': 'Not better in the Baltics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A followup on my last Iceland post. A key point there was that nominal wages are downwardly rigid — it’s very hard to cut them even if your country clearly has costs that make it uncompetitive. That’s why “internal devaluation” is so difficult a strategy as compared with, well, devaluation devaluation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'European Wage Update', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T14:39:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98ef83ea-0409-56a7-b637-bc2a6dc0bea2', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98ef83ea-0409-56a7-b637-bc2a6dc0bea2'}, {'abstract': 'A punctilious process limited the drama as California air regulators approved a program to reduce emissions linked to climate change.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/cap-and-trade-sweating-the-small-stuff/', 'snippet': 'A punctilious process limited the drama as California air regulators approved a program to reduce emissions linked to climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One thing built into a politician’s DNA is a sense of occasion. Regulators tend to lack that gene. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cap and Trade: Sweating the Small Stuff', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'California Air Resources Board', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sacramento (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T14:58:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/806c9f99-82a9-50ea-969c-b314b1f484fe', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/806c9f99-82a9-50ea-969c-b314b1f484fe'}, {'abstract': 'Europe goes in circles.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/theres-a-hole-in-the-bucket/', 'snippet': 'Europe goes in circles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The torments of the euro would be funny if they weren’t so tragic. At this point the urgent need is for a big Panzerfaust — a bailout fund big enough to head off a self-fulfilling liquidity crisis for Italy. But such a fund would be backed by the credit of the euro area’s remaining AAA governments, basically Germany and France — yet at this point the euro situation has deteriorated sufficiently that taking on another commitment would undermine French credit. There’s a hole in the bucket, and every attempt to fix that hole ends up being stymied because, well, there’s a hole in the bucket.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'There’s A Hole In The Bucket', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T15:05:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/358bef9d-a7f0-536f-b302-976df6eed1e5', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/358bef9d-a7f0-536f-b302-976df6eed1e5'}, {'abstract': 'What your government does.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/an-insurance-company-with-an-army-2/', 'snippet': 'What your government does.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I gather, from what I’ve been reading and hearing in various places, that the right-wing line is that it’s all Solyndra — that your tax dollars are going to pay for vast numbers of wasteful projects.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Insurance Company With An Army', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T15:27:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25aeb931-97ad-587f-a761-dcc4ceecdc38', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25aeb931-97ad-587f-a761-dcc4ceecdc38'}, {'abstract': 'Russia’s Foreign Ministry responded to the United States’ adoption of a list imposing sanctions on officials who have been linked to the 2009 death of a whistleblower.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/world/europe/russia-will-bar-some-us-citizens-in-retaliatory-move.html', 'snippet': 'Russia’s Foreign Ministry responded to the United States’ adoption of a list imposing sanctions on officials who have been linked to the 2009 death of a whistleblower.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Russia’s Foreign Ministry announced Saturday that it confirmed a list of American citizens it will bar from entering Russia, in a retaliatory move against the United States’ adoption of the so-called Magnitsky list, which imposes sanctions on Russian officials who have been linked to the 2009 death of the whistleblower Sergei L. Magnitsky.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Will Bar Some U.S. Citizens in Retaliation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia Has List of Citizens Of U.S. to Bar From Entry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T15:33:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifie