ia since 2003 — shows that he is a  sly craftsman with plenty of flair.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/22/gotye-fans-turn-out-to-sing-along/', 'snippet': 'In his mini-set, Gotye — who has been releasing albums in Australia since 2003 — shows that he is a  sly craftsman with plenty of flair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A hit is a hit; a market boundary, in the digital era, is permeable. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gotye Fans Turn Out to Sing Along', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T18:35:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4209c17-fe7f-5c42-8578-d2efe50a1157', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4209c17-fe7f-5c42-8578-d2efe50a1157'}, {'abstract': 'While other schools around Silicon Valley brag about their wired classrooms, the Waldorf school is a throwback, with blackboards and colorful chalk, bookshelves with encyclopedias, and wooden desks filled with workbooks and No. 2 pencils.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/22/business/20111023-WALDORF.html', 'snippet': 'While other schools around Silicon Valley brag about their wired classrooms, the Waldorf school is a throwback, with blackboards and colorful chalk, bookshelves with encyclopedias, and wooden desks filled with workbooks and No. 2 pencils.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While other schools around Silicon Valley brag about their wired classrooms, the Waldorf school is a throwback, with blackboards and colorful chalk, bookshelves with encyclopedias, and wooden desks filled with workbooks and No. 2 pencils.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/business/20111023-WALDORF-slide-XDNF/20111023-WALDORF-slide-XDNF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/22/business/20111023-WALDORF-slide-XDNF/20111023-WALDORF-slide-XDNF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/22/business/20111023-WALDORF-slide-XDNF/20111023-WALDORF-slide-XDNF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Old-School in Silicon Valley', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Waldorf School of the Peninsula', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T18:40:36+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/73de390e-aeed-5d31-8277-72a634bd0c82', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/73de390e-aeed-5d31-8277-72a634bd0c82'}, {'abstract': 'For a baseball biographer, documenting the landscape is an essential part of holding myth accountable to history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/sports/baseball/no-true-sense-of-history-without-a-sense-of-place.html', 'snippet': 'For a baseball biographer, documenting the landscape is an essential part of holding myth accountable to history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the games people play, baseball is distinguished by the preservation of landmark numbers — 56, .367, 2,632, 4,256. But Major League Baseball does precious little to preserve the places where the game once breathed.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/sports/landmark3/landmark3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/23/sports/landmark3/landmark3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/sports/landmark3/landmark3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/sports/landmark3/landmark3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/sports/landmark3/landmark3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No True Sense of History Without a Sense of Place', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No True Sense of History Without a Sense of Place', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Howard University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Senators (Defunct Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 5, '