as L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/24d08012-14f1-5fe7-98c7-4f89357d02c4', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24d08012-14f1-5fe7-98c7-4f89357d02c4'}, {'abstract': 'When Sudan’s Nuba Mountains erupted in warfare this summer and aid workers were evacuated, a young American refused to leave. Here’s his story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/opinion/sunday/kristof-the-man-who-stayed-behind.html', 'snippet': 'When Sudan’s Nuba Mountains erupted in warfare this summer and aid workers were evacuated, a young American refused to leave. Here’s his story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the last few months, as you and I have been fretting about the economy or moaning about the weather, Ryan Boyette has been living in a mud-wall hut and dodging bombs in his underwear.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Man Who Stayed Behind', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Man Who Stayed Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Witnesses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Enough Project', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nuba Mountains (Sudan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Samaritan's Purse", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boyette, Ryan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T19:54:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb79f9cf-c292-5c9c-818b-8cd54962b916', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb79f9cf-c292-5c9c-818b-8cd54962b916'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate shouldn’t support a measure that would eliminate the only effective tool this country has to punish terrorists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/opinion/sunday/peddling-fear.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate shouldn’t support a measure that would eliminate the only effective tool this country has to punish terrorists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At one o’clock in the morning Friday, in one of its rushes to get out of work and back to fund-raising, the Senate took up a measure to strip the Justice Department of the power to charge and try any non-American terrorism suspect captured anywhere in the world.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peddling Fear', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peddling Fear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Tribunals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levin, Carl', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T19:56:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cb12b50-fd92-5899-a6ca-0fae646330ec', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cb12b50-fd92-5899-a6ca-0fae646330ec'}, {'abstract': 'America’s fiscal troubles are dictating a drastic scaling back of plans to expand diplomatic, economic and cultural programs once deemed vital to steadying Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/world/middleeast/us-scales-back-diplomacy-in-iraq-amid-fiscal-and-security-concerns.html', 'snippet': 'America’s fiscal troubles are dictating a drastic scaling back of plans to expand diplomatic, economic and cultural programs once deemed vital to steadying Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Beyond the final withdrawal of troops that President Obama announced Friday, America’s fiscal troubles are dictating a drastic scaling back of plans for diplomatic, economic and cultural programs once deemed vital to steadying Iraq, building a long-term alliance and prying the country from Iran’s tightening embrace. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/world/23baghdad/23baghdad-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/23/world/23baghdad/23baghdad-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/world/23baghdad/23baghdad-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/world/23baghdad/23baghdad-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStanda