', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/sunday-review/23INCLUSION/23INCLUSION-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/sunday-review/23INCLUSION/23INCLUSION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/sunday-review/23INCLUSION/23INCLUSION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Paradox of the New Elite', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Paradox Of the New Elite', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ivy League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T19:56:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Stille', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stille', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/21d6cebb-25fa-59a4-b974-cde861bc15a6', 'word_count': 1798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21d6cebb-25fa-59a4-b974-cde861bc15a6'}, {'abstract': 'The five-year championship run of Jimmie Johnson in Nascar’s top series is in jeopardy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/sports/autoracing/a-pack-of-nascar-drivers-is-ready-to-break-out-of-johnsons-shadow.html', 'snippet': 'The five-year championship run of Jimmie Johnson in Nascar’s top series is in jeopardy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jimmie Johnson hinted at vulnerability two races into the Chase for the Sprint Cup, as less-than-dominating finishes left him well behind the points leaders. Just as the doubts were raised, Johnson seemed to dismiss them with a second-place showing at Dover and a victory at Kansas that reminded everyone why he was nicknamed Five-Time.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pack of Nascar Drivers Is Ready to Break Out of Johnson’s Shadow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lead Pack Is Leaving Johnson Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Stock Car Auto Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jimmie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T19:57:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Auto Racing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Viv Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Viv', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b476fac2-7f21-551b-916b-4df38cc2ea87', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b476fac2-7f21-551b-916b-4df38cc2ea87'}, {'abstract': 'In the wake of Dan Wheldon’s death last Sunday, IndyCar officials have been all but silent, and after canceling their championship banquet, left Las Vegas trailing bitterness and finger-pointing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/sports/autoracing/a-drivers-death-has-raised-questions-about-indycars-leader.html', 'snippet': 'In the wake of Dan Wheldon’s death last Sunday, IndyCar officials have been all but silent, and after canceling their championship banquet, left Las Vegas trailing bitterness and finger-pointing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of Dan Wheldon’s death at a race in Las Vegas last Sunday, IndyCar officials have been all but silent. No formal statements, beyond an expression of regret and a pledge to investigate themselves. Certainly no news conferences to answer questions about the propriety of the race, which was held at a fast track not truly built to stage such an event.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/sports/dog-jp-indycar-1/dog-jp-indycar-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/23/sports/dog-jp-indycar-1/dog-jp-indycar-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/sports/dog-jp-indycar-1/dog-jp-indycar-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/sports/dog-jp-indycar-1/dog-jp-indycar-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/sports/dog-jp-indycar-1