ntributions to political candidates for federal office. In a brief to the United States Court of Appeals for the Fourth Circuit, the lawyers challenge a wrongheaded ruling by Judge James Cacheris of Virginia, arguing that the ban serves the government’s strong interest in preventing political corruption. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even Worse Than Citizens United', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Even Worse Than Citizens United', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cacheris, James C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-22T20:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e27492b-da4b-567c-bc37-fafce0abed8a', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e27492b-da4b-567c-bc37-fafce0abed8a'}, {'abstract': 'On the iPod’s birthday, reflecting on its impact on the way we listen to music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/opinion/sunday/happy-birthday-ipod.html', 'snippet': 'On the iPod’s birthday, reflecting on its impact on the way we listen to music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel J. Levitin, a neuroscientist at McGill University, is the author of “This Is Your Brain on Music: The Sci