ragraph': 'ZACH COLLAROS The senior Cincinnati quarterback threw for three touchdowns and ran for two more in the fourth quarter, helping Cincinnati come from behind in the closing minutes to stay atop the Big East standings with a 37-34 victory against host South Florida. Collaros finished 26 of 41 passing for 389 yards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Day’s Best in College Football', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Matt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Kellen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clemson University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'South Florida University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Iowa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T01:49:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f644cafe-1002-53a2-9bbb-f133200bf243', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f644cafe-1002-53a2-9bbb-f133200bf243'}, {'abstract': 'As choosing a school becomes increasingly complicated, some entrepreneurial parents have started small consulting businesses for bewildered parents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/us/school-consultants-help-parents-navigate-admissions-process.html', 'snippet': 'As choosing a school becomes increasingly complicated, some entrepreneurial parents have started small consulting businesses for bewildered parents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Armed with tote ba