o', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/19a0d5eb-57f8-5bf1-8f34-01c2e632a870', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19a0d5eb-57f8-5bf1-8f34-01c2e632a870'}, {'abstract': 'The hobby shop at San Quentin State Prison is lined with paintings and prints, and its display cases are filled with the inmates handiworks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/us/local-intelligence-san-quentin-prisons-hobby-shop.html', 'snippet': 'The hobby shop at San Quentin State Prison is lined with paintings and prints, and its display cases are filled with the inmates handiworks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The penitentiary at San Quentin opened on a rocky North Bay promontory in 1852, and rehabilitation and educational programs for inmates were introduced in the 1940s. Inside the prison hobby shop, a plain room just outside the gates, the walls are lined with paintings and prints, and the display cases are filled with jewelry, leather goods and other pieces made by the inmates. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/us/23BCINTEL1/23BCINTEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/23/us/23BCINTEL1/23BCINTEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/us/23BCINTEL1/23BCINTEL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Outlaw Art', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen | Local Intelligence', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Outlaw Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons