': 'The bride is a law librarian; the bridegroom works for a recruitment firm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elizabeth Anne Yates and Anthony Ian Keizner were married Thursday at the Manhattan Marriage Bureau. James Mitchell a member of the office of the New York City clerk, officiated. On Saturday, the couple had another ceremony at the Inn at Perry Cabin in St. Michaels, Md., where Niclas Kvarnstrom, a friend of the bridegroom who is a counselor at the Swedish Mission to the United Nations, led the couple in vows that they wrote. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/fashion/weddings/23YATESjpg/23YATESjpg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/fashion/weddings/23YATESjpg/23YATESjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/fashion/weddings/23YATESjpg/23YATESjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Elizabeth Yates, Anthony Keizner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Elizabeth Yates, Anthony Keizner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T06:46:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d6c34fa-c958-5ef7-9748-84f3e6b639b8', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d6c34fa-c958-5ef7-9748-84f3e6b639b8'}, {'abstract': 'After a brief college romance more than 45 years ago and decades of sustained friendship, the couple makes it official.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/fashion/weddings/gwendolyn-sommer-charles-heck-weddings.html', 'snippet': 'After a brief college romance more than 45 years ago and decades of sustained friendship, the couple makes it official.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gwendolyn Solmssen Sommer and Charles Bennett Heck are to be married Sunday at the Harold Pratt House, an event space in New York. Marcia Aronoff, a friend of the couple who became a Universal Life minister for the event, officiated. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/fashion/weddings/23SOMMERjpg/23SOMMERjpg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/fashion/weddings/23SOMMERjpg/23SOMMERjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/fashion/weddings/23SOMMERjpg/23SOMMERjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gwendolyn Sommer, Charles Heck', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gwendolyn Sommer, Charles Heck', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T06:46:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vincent M. Mallozzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vincent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd56e239-cdbf-582e-9063-91f26f745277', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd56e239-cdbf-582e-9063-91f26f745277'}, {'abstract': 'Stories from Outlook, Tehelka and Air & Space', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/newswallah-long-reads-edition-7/', 'snippet': 'Stories from Outlook, Tehelka and Air & Space', 'lead_paragraph': 'Outlook magazine’s issue this week is an anniversary special about India’s much discussed youth. In the lead essay, Akash Kapur, who previously wrote the International Herald Tribune’s Letter from India, says the youth’s “optimism and self-assuredness, their faith in the future, have come to sand, metonymically, for a nation that is itself regularly rates, in surveys and opinion polls, as among the most optimistic and self-assured in the world.” The special also includes interesting features about young Indian politicians, journalists, entrepreneurs and the cosmetics business.Tehelka has a story on the plight of residents of Delhi slums who have been evicted to make way for shopping malls, apartments and other new developments. Many of the evicted residents have ended up in worse conditions further away from the city, the piece argues, because local authorities have not made any provision for low-cost housing. One evicted resident tells the magazine: “For the government, we are like cattle who have strayed into their fields uninvited.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Long Reads Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR INDIA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T07:12:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08e6af6c-b5b8-5ad2-9aee-576b383b427b', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08e6af6c-b5b8-5ad2-9aee-576b383b427b'}, {'abstract': 'With several momentum-shifting plays involving him, Mike Napoli became a microcosm for how badly Game 3 turned against the Rangers in a 16-7 loss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/sports/baseball/wrong-place-wrong-timing-for-napoli-in-game-3.html', 'snippet': 'With several momentum-shifting plays involving him, Mike Napoli became a microcosm for how badly Game 3 turned against the Rangers in a 16-7 loss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARLINGTON, Tex. — Mike Napoli usually watches a game unfold from behind a catcher’s mask, but his view at first base was crystal clear when it came to the tag he applied on Matt Holliday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/baseball/24napoli_1/24napoli_1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrong Place, Wrong Timing for Napoli in Game 3', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wrong Place, Wrong Timing for Napoli in Game 3', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Napoli, Mike', 'rank':