ship in Unesco — the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization — has put both Washington and the organization into an urgent bind.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/world/UNESCO/UNESCO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/24/world/UNESCO/UNESCO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/world/UNESCO/UNESCO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/world/UNESCO/UNESCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/24/world/UNESCO/UNESCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinian Bid for Full Unesco Membership Imperils American Financing', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Palestinian Bid for Full Unesco Membership Imperils American Financing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T17:21:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/102daf71-d6ca-5642-af7b-ad83a6556763', 'word_count': 1059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/102daf71-d6ca-5642-af7b-ad83a6556763'}, {'abstract': 'The opening weekend ticket-sales total for that movie has been the biggest in history for a horror film, not accounting for inflation.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/paranormal-activity-3-has-record-opening-weekend/', 'snippet': 'The opening weekend ticket-sales total for that movie has been the biggest in history for a horror film, not accounting for inflation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'North American moviegoers were in the mood to be scared over the weekend, powering the micro-budgeted “Paranormal Activity 3” to a stronger-than-anticipated $54 million in ticket sales. That total, easily enough for No. 1, prompted Paramount Pictures, the studio behind this wildly successful horror franchise, to shriek with delight, or at least superlatives. (According to Paramount, the opening weekend total for “Paranormal Activity 3,” which cost just $5 million to make, is the biggest in history for a horror film — not accounting for inflation.) The studio partly attributed strong sales to strikingly positive reviews, which helped draw more moviegoers in their 30s and 40s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Paranormal Activity 3’ Has Record Opening Weekend', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jovovich, Milla', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paramount Pictures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Summit Entertainment Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T17:24:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e093efe9-8f3d-5e77-b6f1-1a07d0f455d7', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e093efe9-8f3d-5e77-b6f1-1a07d0f455d7'}, {'abstract': 'Joe Biden stirs speculation about his political future in 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/biden-wont-rule-out-2016-bid-for-president/', 'snippet': 'Joe Biden stirs speculation about his political future in 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the upcoming 2012 election, Joe Biden will rally around the flag of President Barack Obama, but in 2016? He just might run for president himself — again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden Won’t Rule Out 2016 Bid for President', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crowley, Candy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delaware', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T17:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b5a3237-7ab2-5b57-9eed-9c1109f6331f', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b5a3237-7ab2-5b57-9eed-9c1109f6331f'}, {'abstract': 'If Manchester City wanted to prove it has what it takes to win the English Premier League title, it could not have done it better than humiliating its most bitter rival in its own backyard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/sports/soccer/manchester-citys-makeover-continues-with-rout-of-united.html', 'snippet': 'If Manchester City wanted to prove it has what it takes to win the English Premier League title, it could not have done it better than humiliating its most bitter rival in its own backyard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, England — The sign said “Old Trafford welcomes supporters of Manchester City,” but in the stadium, it did not feel that way.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Victory Exalts a New Master of Manchester', 'kicker': 'Manchester City 6, Manchester United 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Victory Exalts a New Master of Manchester', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English Premier League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester City (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester United (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T17:52:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kabir Chibber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kabir', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chibber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/349234b0-2de1-5a6d-b219-acb617538cd2', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/349234b0-2de1-5a6d-b219-acb617538cd2'}, {'abstract': 'The leader of Libya’s transitional government declared to thousands of revelers that Libya’s revolution had ended, setting the country on the path to elections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/world/africa/revolution-won-top-libyan-official-vows-a-new-and-more-pious-state.html', 'snippet': 'The leader of Libya’s transitional government declared to thousands of revelers that Libya’s revolution had ended, setting the country on the path to elections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BENGHAZI, Libya — The leader of the transitional government declared to thousands of revelers in a sunlit square here on Sunday that Libya’s revolution had ended, setting the country on the path to elections, and he vowed that the new government would be based on Islamic tenets.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/world/africa/24libya2/24libya2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/24/world/africa/24libya2/24libya2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/world/africa/24libya2/24libya2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/world/africa/24libya2/24libya2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/24/world/africa/24libya2/24libya2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Revolution Won, Top Libyan Official Vows a New and More Pious State', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Revolution Won, Top Libyan Official Promises Elections and a More Pious State', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transitional National Council (Libya)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abdel-Jalil, Mustafa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T18:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter and Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e1aa927-5f7f-5374-9d87-6e90a1e4d28e', 'word_count': 1074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e1aa927-5f7f-5374-9d87-6e90a1e4d28e'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Caramanica’s moment-by-moment look at the last night of CMJ week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/touring-the-fringes-the-final-hours-of-cmj/', 'snippet': 'Jon Caramanica’s moment-by-moment look at the last night of CMJ week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I made the decision to spend the final day of this year’s CMJ festival on the fringes, at several of the symbiotic, or parasitic, events that pop up during CMJ week to take advantage of the sheer number of musicians stalking the city with an hour to spare. First, there was the Fader Fort, thrown by the Fader magazine and Fiat. That was followed by a Converse-sponsored showcase of hip-hop and hardcore at Santos Party House. After that, I closed the night at the New Museum, at a party organized by the Pitchfork spin-off site Altered Zones. All times are approximate. All feelings are not.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Touring the Fringes, the Final Hours of CMJ', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Action Bronson (1983- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boucher, Claire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elkann, Lapo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kylesa (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Santos Party House', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T19:30:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51cbd146-2a0d-5510-8d52-1f771083e8dd', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51cbd146-2a0d-5510-8d52-1f771083e8dd'}, {'abstract': 'Video reports poured out of Turkey on Sunday after a powerful earthquake struck the country’s eastern region, collapsing buildings and causing widespread panic.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/in-turkey-scenes-from-the-quake-zone/', 'snippet': 'Video reports poured out of Turkey on Sunday after a powerful earthquake struck the country’s eastern region, collapsing buildings and causing widespread panic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | Monday | 9:29 a.m. After a powerful earthquake struck eastern Turkey on Sunday, video posted online showed collapsed buildings and widespread panic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video From the Quake Zone in Turkey', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davutoglu, Ahmet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T19:51:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2a3b843-c3ad-5f6e-b7b7-8e37fa45b91c', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2a3b843-c3ad-5f6e-b7b7-8e37fa45b91c'}, {'abstract': 'As more buildings fall in a strong earthquake in Turkey, a fresh call for a safer, but cheap, design.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/designing-for-safety-in-turkey-and-other-earthquake-zones/', 'snippet': 'As more buildings fall in a strong earthquake in Turkey, a fresh call for a safer, but cheap, design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oct. 24, 5:32 a.m. | Updated The latest earthquake in Turkey — that country’s strongest in a decade — provides a fresh reminder of the deep vulnerability created by weak building designs in the world’s crowded seismic danger zones. There will be more horror to come there and in other places prone to powerful quakes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Designing for Safety in Turkey and Other Earthquake Zones', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engineering and Engineers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T19:59:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2fdb4b8-381c-5d48-b19f-18a47c0a0e30', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2fdb4b8-381c-5d48-b19f-18a47c0a0e30'}, {'abstract': 'Leaders hope the seriousness of their effort to solve the problems of Greek debt, weak banks and a bailout fund in need of reinforcement will ease the markets on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/business/global/24iht-euro24.html', 'snippet': 'Leaders hope the seriousness of their effort to solve the problems of Greek debt, weak banks and a bailout fund in need of reinforcement will ease the markets on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — With a new sense of urgency, the leaders of the 27 European Union nations grappled directly on Sunday with their thorniest financial and economi