fast Club” were in luck on Thursday as the Los Angeles County Museum of Art hosted a high-profile table reading of that quintessential 1985 film about teenagers and their stereotypes, Entertainment Weekly reported on its Web site. Instead of the original stars from the film, a different group of actors joined for the occasion. Jennifer Garner played the popular Claire (Molly Ringwald’s part in the movie), James Van Der Beek was Andy the jock (Emilio Estevez), Patton Oswalt was the nerdy Brian (Anthony Michael Hall), Mindy Kaling was the misunderstood Allison (Ally Sheedy), and Aaron Paul was the school-detention lifer Bender (Judd Nelson).  J. K. Simmons and Michael Chiklis were the only two (fictional) adults in the room, portraying Carl the janitor and the hard-line teacher Mr. Vernon. The event was the brainchild of the director Jason Reitman (“Juno,” “Up in the Air”). “I needed a film that was in a contained location with not too many characters, that was funny, that was populous, that had a great script that the audience would have a relationship with,” Mr. Reitman told Entertainment Weekly. He also said he would soon announce five additional readings of different movies to benefit Film Independent, an organization that supports independent film projects and artists.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fresh Reading of ‘The Breakfast Club’', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fresh Reading Of ‘The Breakfast Club’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles County Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaling, Mindy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oswalt, Patton', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van der Beek, James', 'rank': 5, 'major':