ndard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Black Coaches in the N.F.L., Still a Steep Road to the Top', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still a Steep Road for Black Coaches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Al', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Raiders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shell, Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T22:10:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By William C. Rhoden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Rhoden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee89529d-46d3-5aad-a005-6947cac7c438', 'word_count': 1161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee89529d-46d3-5aad-a005-6947cac7c438'}, {'abstract': 'Maxwell L. Anderson, who has been director of the Indianapolis Museum of Art since 2006, has been appointed director of the Dallas Museum of Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/arts/design/dallas-museum-lands-new-director.html', 'snippet': 'Maxwell L. Anderson, who has been director of the Indianapolis Museum of Art since 2006, has been appointed director of the Dallas Museum of Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maxwell L. Anderson, who has been director of the Indianapolis Museum of Art since 2006, has been appointed director of the Dallas Museum of Art. He succeeds Bonnie Pitman, who retired from the job in June. Mr. Anderson is a well-known figure, having run the Whitney Museum of American Art from 1998 to 2003, when he resigned after disagreements with its board. During his tenure at the Indianapolis museum attendance has more than doubled, to 450,000 visitors annually. Mr. Anderson introduced innovative Internet-based tools to engage the public, including a dedicated video channel for art and artists and a dashboard that provided users with real-time statistics, like the number of visitors that day. In June 2010 the Indianapolis Museum of Art opened 100 Acres: The Virginia B. Fairbanks Art & Nature Park, among the largest contemporary art parks in the country. Mr. Anderson is to begin his new job on Jan. 9.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dallas Museum Lands New Director', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dallas Museum Lands New Director', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Museum of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Museum of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, MAXWELL L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T22:11:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/844981be-b99b-5b9f-8687-05ea26206256', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/844981be-b99b-5b9f-8687-05ea26206256'}, {'abstract': 'Our weekly review of the performances of the three local N.H.L. teams.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/metro-pucks-a-week-of-underachievement-and-a-bit-of-cheating/', 'snippet': 'Our weekly review of the performances of the three local N.H.L. teams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our weekly review of the performances of the three local N.H.L. teams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Metro Pucks: A Week of Underachievement, and a Bit of Cheating', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Islanders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T22:11:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Botta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53ab53b5-4a69-523d-9a45-ef33eb65afc9', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53ab53b5-4a69-523d-9a45-ef33eb65afc9'}, {'abstract': 'The day after the premiere of “Boss,” Deadline Hollywood reported that two of the executive producers of the series, Richard Levine and Lyn Greene, were leaving.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/arts/television/suddenly-two-bosses-leave-the-show-boss.html', 'snippet': 'The day after the premiere of “Boss,” Deadline Hollywood reported that two of the executive producers of the series, Richard Levine and Lyn Greene, were leaving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Something unusual happened to the political drama “Boss” at the end of September: Starz ordered a second season before the first season had begun. Then on Saturday, the day after the premiere, Deadline Hollywood reported that two of the executive producers of the series, Richard Levine and Lyn Greene, were leaving before work started on the second season. They had shared the post of show runner for the first season. Deadline Hollywood reported that Starz and the show’s producer, Lionsgate, were seeking replacements. The creator of “Boss,” Farhad Safinia, will remain, as will four other executive producers, including Kelsey Grammer, who stars as a tyrannical Chicago mayor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suddenly Two Bosses Leave the Show ‘Boss’', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suddenly Two Bosses Leave the Show ‘Boss’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grammer, Kelsey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T22:12:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a629dc5b-daf6-53f3-93fe-074a7be0fade', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a629dc5b-daf6-53f3-93fe-074a7be0fade'}, {'abstract': 'Speaking in Jerusalem, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg said the city had no “plan of action” to stop Occupy Wall Street.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/even-in-jerusalem-thoughts-stray-to-zuccotti-park/', 'snippet': 'Speaking in Jerusalem, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg said the city had no “plan of action” to stop Occupy Wall Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg, the specter of Occupy Wall Street looms large — even in Jerusalem.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even in Jerusalem, Thoughts Stray to Zuccotti Park', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T22:15:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45e9f4dd-b6e2-5269-a373-828443156bd7', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45e9f4dd-b6e2-5269-a373-828443156bd7'}, {'abstract': 'Morgan Stanley analysts are saying Tesla may take roughly 2.5 percent of the electric vehicle market by 2025.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/business/anticipating-big-growth-at-tesla.html', 'snippet': 'Morgan Stanley analysts are saying Tesla may take roughly 2.5 percent of the electric vehicle market by 2025.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tesla Motors makes pure electric cars, but it’s valued like a hybrid. Quarterly numbers — due in the coming weeks — hint at its ability to hit manufacturing targets. But Silicon Valley-style growth is central to the story.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anticipating Big Growth at Tesla', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Growth at Tesla Could Be Extreme', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name':