onomic-reports-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Economic reports, corporate earnings and hearings this week in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ECONOMIC REPORTS Data will include S.& P./Case-Shiller Home Price Index and consumer confidence (Tuesday); durable goods orders and sales of new homes (Wednesday); third-quarter gross domestic product and weekly jobless claims (Thursday); and personal income, personal spending, the Thomson Reuters/University of Michigan consumer sentiment survey and pending home sales (Friday).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking Ahead to Economic Reports This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking Ahead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T22:30:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/dabc7d7d-c1ff-50d4-851d-d3a6d7ab7159', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dabc7d7d-c1ff-50d4-851d-d3a6d7ab7159'}, {'abstract': 'The 38th International Contemporary Art Fair in Paris has had a robust burst of sales despite the wobbly state of the euro.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/arts/design/38th-international-contemporary-art-fair-in-paris.html', 'snippet': 'The 38th International Contemporary Art Fair in Paris has had a robust burst of sales despite the wobbly state of the euro.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The mood was unexpectedly buoyant at the Grand Palais here on Thursday, the opening day of the 38th International Contemporary Art Fair, even as European leaders were desperately dashing around the Continent trying to save their common currency.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/Sub-jp-Fiac-1/Sub-jp-Fiac-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/Sub-jp-Fiac-1/Sub-jp-Fiac-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/Sub-jp-Fiac-1/Sub-jp-Fiac-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/Sub-jp-Fiac-1/Sub-jp-Fiac-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/Sub-jp-Fiac-1/Sub-jp-Fiac-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro Flails but Art Fair Flourishes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Euro Flails But Art Fair Flourishes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Contemporary Art Fair (FIAC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T22:32:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Celestine Bohlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Celestine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bohlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6708688-846e-50ca-9587-e23f14022000', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6708688-846e-50ca-9587-e23f14022000'}, {'abstract': 'The Pakistani military allowed an Indian Army helicopter to return home after it was intercepted in Pakistani airspace over Kashmir.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/world/asia/india-and-pakistan-avert-potential-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'The Pakistani military allowed an Indian Army helicopter to return home after it was intercepted in Pakistani airspace over Kashmir.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — A potential military and diplomatic crisis was averted Sunday after an Indian Army helicopter that had strayed into Pakistan’s airspace and was forced to land by its military was allowed to return home, according to Pakistani officials.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India and Pakistan Sidestep a Crisis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India and Pakistan Sidestep a Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T22:33:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ba25907-a63b-53c0-9980-90839fc4d31c', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ba25907-a63b-53c0-9980-90839fc4d31c'}, {'abstract': 'As federal officials plan to overhaul the rules that regulate research involving human subjects, critics warn that the revisions could seal off publicly available information.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/arts/rules-meant-to-protect-human-research-subjects-cause-concern.html', 'snippet': 'As federal officials plan to overhaul the rules that regulate research involving human subjects, critics warn that the revisions could seal off publicly available information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hoping to protect privacy in an age when a fingernail clipping can reveal a person’s identity, federal officials are planning to overhaul the rules that regulate research involving human subjects. But critics outside the biomedical arena warn that the proposed revisions may unintentionally create a more serious problem: sealing off vast collections of publicly available information from inspection, including census data, market research, oral histories and labor statistics.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/Public/Public-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/Public/Public-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/Public/Public-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 579, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Questioning Privacy Protections in Research', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Questioning Privacy Protections In Research', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clinical Trials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T22:37:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74e37f58-1097-5757-b594-ab4d48a2cd66', 'word_count': 1121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74e37f58-1097-5757-b594-ab4d48a2cd66'}, {'abstract': 'The Bush Theater in London is producing “Sixty-Six Books,” a collection of short plays, poems and songs, to commemorate the 400th anniversary of the King James Bible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/theater/bush-theater-celebrates-king-james-bible-with-sixty-six-books.html', 'snippet': 'The Bush Theater in London is producing “Sixty-Six Books,” a collection of short plays, poems and songs, to commemorate the 400th anniversary of the King James Bible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'God’s terse first line in the Book of Genesis — “Let there be light” — was ready-made for the Twitter generation. If only the rest was as crisp, the British novelist Jeanette Winterson recalled thinking, as she began to reckon with that first book for a new theatrical project on the King James Bible. And then it hit her: Maybe God’s wisdom would crackle for a modern audience as Twitter posts of 140 words or less.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/SIXTY/SIXTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/SIXTY/SIXTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/SIXTY/SIXTY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/SIXTY/SIXTY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/SIXTY/SIXTY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At London Theater, a Celebration of Biblical Proportions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At London Theater, a Celebration of Biblical Proportions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bible', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bush Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-23T22:44:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8912c89-dd74-57f9-82c0-f90c831a3dc6', 'word_count': 1077, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8912c89-dd74-57f9-82c0-f90c831a3dc6'}, {'abstract': 'The mezzo-soprano Rosalind Elias made her Broadway debut at 82 in the current revival of “Follies.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/theater/the-mezzo-soprano-rosalind-elias-in-follies-on-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'The mezzo-soprano Rosalind Elias made her Broadway debut at 82 in the current revival of “Follies.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ageless mezzo-soprano Rosalind Elias had never heard a note of Stephen Sondheim’s score for “Follies” when her agent first approached her about auditioning for the small, poignant role of Heidi Schiller, which she is now playing to acclaim in the popular revival at the Marquis Theater on Broadway.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/sub-Elias/sub-Elias-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 343, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/sub-Elias/sub-Elias-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 343}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/sub-Elias/sub-Elias-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/sub-Elias/sub-Elias-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/sub-Elias/sub-Elias-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Broadway Debut After a Life of Opera', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Broadway Debut After a Life of Opera', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'valu