80d63-c5ec-5dc8-a68e-b4af2a98174d'}, {'abstract': 'The B.C.S. rankings are determined by three components: the Harris Interactive poll, the USA Today coaches poll and the average of six computer rankings. Each component counts one-third toward a team’s B.C.S. score.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/bowl-championship-series-standings-2/', 'snippet': 'The B.C.S. rankings are determined by three components: the Harris Interactive poll, the USA Today coaches poll and the average of six computer rankings. Each component counts one-third toward a team’s B.C.S. score.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The losses by national title contenders Wisconsin and Oklahoma threw the Bowl Championship Series race into a tizzy. College football, after a few weeks heavy on chalk and light on thrillers, re-emerged as the unpredictable and parity-laden beast that had driven the sport’s popularity and television ratings the past few years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Top 2, Oklahoma St. Has Inside Track', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bowl Championship Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T00:31:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78c2c3e4-f840-5489-9b0b-d53f32546d54', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78c2c3e4-f840-5489-9b0b-d53f32546d54'}, {'abstract': 'At CBS News, Robert Pierpoint brought a human touch to his coverage, which included the Korean War and six American presidencies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/business/robert-pierpoint-86-dies-correspondent-for-cbs-news.html', 'snippet': 'At CBS News, Robert Pierpoint brought a human touch to his coverage, which included the Korean War and six American presidencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert Pierpoint, the CBS News correspondent who brought a human-interest touch to coverage of the Korean War and later reported on six presidents, from Dwight D. Eisenhower to Jimmy Carter, died Saturday in Santa Barbara, Calif. He was 86.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/business/pierpoint-obit/pierpoint-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 692, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/business/pierpoint-obit/pierpoint-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/24/business/pierpoint-obit/pierpoint-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert Pierpoint, 86, Dies; CBS News Correspondent', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Robert Pierpoint, 86, Dies; CBS News Correspondent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS News', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T00:34:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Goldstein'