eet protests continued to gain traction.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/12/business/media/carr-50/carr-50-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/12/business/media/carr-50/carr-50-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Not Occupy Newsrooms?', 'kicker': 'The Media Equation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Not Occupy Newsrooms?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gannett Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tribune Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zell, Samuel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dubow, Craig A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Today', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T01:10:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7356916-fa1d-5e48-9bdc-520ed5e3e1dd', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7356916-fa1d-5e48-9bdc-520ed5e3e1dd'}, {'abstract': 'As Case Keenum rewrites records, No. 18 Houston is poised to become the first Conference USA team to go undefeated in the league since 2004.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/sports/ncaafootball/special-season-unfolds-for-keenum-and-no-18-houston.html', 'snippet': 'As Case Keenum rewrites records, No. 18 Houston is poised to become the first Conference USA team to go undefeated in the league since 2004.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The off-campus garage apartment that Houston quarterback Case Keenum and his wife, Kimberly, share is so modest that it does not have a full number in its mailing address. The Keenums lovingly refer to their home as the Half, a cozy starter spot. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/YCOLLEGE/YCOLLEGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/YCOLLEGE/YCOLLEGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/YCOLLEGE/YCOLLEGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 836, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/YCOLLEGE/YCOLLEGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/YCOLLEGE/YCOLLEGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Records and Wins for Houston Quarterback', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Records And Wins For Houston Quarterback', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bowl Championship Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keenum, Case', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Houston', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T01:11:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbbb6a8a-2903-5e7d-b115-c025f28098a7', 'word_count': 1207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbbb6a8a-2903-5e7d-b115-c025f28098a7'}, {'abstract': 'A vaccine to protect children against malaria has shown promising results in a clinical trial. But there are big hurdles still to surmount.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/opinion/two-cheers-for-the-malaria-vaccine.html', 'snippet': 'A vaccine to protect children against malaria has shown promising results in a clinical trial. But there are big hurdles still to surmount.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A vaccine to protect children against malaria has been shown moderately effective in a large clinical trial — an achievement that could save millions of lives. The vaccine, known as RTS,S and made by GlaxoSmithKline, is the first ever to be shown effective against a human disease caused by parasites. When tested in 6,000 infants ages 5 to 17 months in seven sub-Saharan nations, it reduced the risk of infection with severe malaria by 47 percent during the year after the shots, far less than the 90 percent efficacy rate typically sought for other vaccines. And there are other big hurdles still to surmount. There are hints that the protection may wane over time and results from administering a booster shot won’t be known until 2014. Side effects could pose a problem; seizures and fevers were higher among children given the vaccine. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Cheers for the Malaria Vaccine', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Cheers for the Malaria Vaccine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malaria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clinical Trials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GlaxoSmithKline PLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gates, Bill and Melinda, Foundation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T01:18:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d756b63d-88e8-5e82-adcf-c18166474ec5', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d756b63d-88e8-5e82-adcf-c18166474ec5'}, {'abstract': 'Apple posted a video of a tribute to Steven P. Jobs, the company’s co-founder, that took place last week at the company’s campus in Cupertino, Calif.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/apple-posts-video-from-steve-jobs-tribute/', 'snippet': 'Apple posted a video of a tribute to Steven P. Jobs, the company’s co-founder, that took place last week at the company’s campus in Cupertino, Calif.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apple has posted a video of a tribute to Steven P. Jobs, the company’s co-founder, that took place last week at the Apple campus in Cupertino, Calif. (The video must be viewed in the Safari Web browser.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple Posts Video From Steve Jobs Tribute', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T01:21:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6edffff9-3065-583c-8cba-3f92ab8437c8', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6edffff9-3065-583c-8cba-3f92ab8437c8'}, {'abstract': 'The former Heisman winner for Florida directed the Broncos to an overtime victory, but his inconsistent play failed to clear up his team’s quandary at quarterback.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/sports/football/tim-tebow-leads-denver-broncos-over-miami-dolphins.html', 'snippet': 'The former Heisman winner for Florida directed the Broncos to an overtime victory, but his inconsistent play failed to clear up his team’s quandary at quarterback.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI GARDENS, Fla. — It seemed as if everyone in the stadium knew what play the Denver Broncos would run on the 2-point conversion that would tie the game with 17 seconds to play. For 55 minutes, Tim Tebow had barely looked like a functioning N.F.L quarterback. He took sacks and threw poorly. He was hesitant and overwhelmed. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/YJPDOLPHINS/YJPDOLPHINS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/YJPDOLPHINS/YJPDOLPHINS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/YJPDOLPHINS/YJPDOLPHINS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/YJPDOLPHINS/YJPDOLPHINS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/YJPDOLPHINS/YJPDOLPHINS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tebow Wills Broncos to Win With His Late-Game Play', 'kicker': 'Broncos 18, Dolphins 15 (OT)', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Willing a Win: Shaky Tebow Leads Denver With His Late-Game Play', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Dolphins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T01:22:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39849858-48f2-5c20-b669-149db91c8e77', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39849858-48f2-5c20-b669-149db91c8e77'}, {'abstract': 'The Oakland Raiders’ new quarterback, Carson Palmer, threw three interceptions in a 28-0 loss to Kansas City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/sports/football/an-up-and-down-first-game-for-palmer.html', 'snippet': 'The Oakland Raiders’ new quarterback, Carson Palmer, threw three interceptions in a 28-0 loss to Kansas City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OAKLAND, Calif. — The cheers from the home fans began to pick up about two minutes into the third quarter Sunday, which seemed strange only because the Kansas City Chiefs were ahead by 14 points and driving at the time. Then again, at that point, many of the Oakland Raiders’ followers were no longer watching what was happening on the field anyway.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/YRAIDERS2/YRAIDERS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/YRAIDERS2/YRAIDERS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/24/sports/YRAIDERS2/YRAIDERS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Palmer Struggles in Raiders Debut, but Provides Glimpses of Promise', 'kicker': 'Chiefs 28, Raiders 0', 'content_kicker':