nd Randy McMichael did not sound impressed with the Jets after San Diego’s 27-21 loss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. – The verbal jousting that accompanied the Jets’ game Sunday did not end at kickoff. It continued after their 27-21 victory, in the Chargers’ locker room, where tight end Randy McMichael sounded rather unimpressed with the Jets’ defense.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Charger Doesn’t Go Down Quietly', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T01:58:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28e4375a-59a4-5c5b-a6d2-c97fa507691b', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28e4375a-59a4-5c5b-a6d2-c97fa507691b'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers are studying high-functioning people with schizophrenia to learn how mental health disorders can be managed while people build full, successful lives.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/23/studying-successful-people-with-mental-illness/', 'snippet': 'Researchers are studying high-functioning people with schizophrenia to learn how mental health disorders can be managed while people build full, successful lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s long been thought that people with severe mental illness had limited opportunities for work, and many are advised to take on simple, low-stress jobs so as not to exacerbate their symptoms. But now researchers are studying high-functioning people with schizophrenia and its close cousin, 