ndia’s Ministry of External Affairs said it “greatly appreciates the manner in which Pakistan worked with us” (The Hindu). India’s gratitude for the swift return will be “expressed at the highest levels” when Prime Minister Manmohan Singh meets his counterpart Yousaf Raza Gillani in the Maldives next month, says the Times of India.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: In the English-Language Press Monday', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singh, Manmohan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Investment Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T04:51:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cc63b18-6978-551c-8700-41d0d5c77877', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cc63b18-6978-551c-8700-41d0d5c77877'}, {'abstract': 'In the latest episode of “The Good Wife,” a rival warns Alicia that Will is going to disappoint her. It looks like he already did.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/good-wife-watch-what-alicia-didnt-know/', 'snippet': 'In the latest episode of “The Good Wife,” a rival warns Alicia that Will is going to disappoint her. It looks like he already did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What at first glance looked like a storyline worthy of “Michael Clayton” or “The Insider” — a whistleblower commits suicide after testifying against an airline in a deadly crash — quickly morphed into yet another way of sabotaging Peter’s gubernatorial aspirations after the revelation that someone else knew about the plane’s problems all along. And with that, Sunday night’s episode of “The Good Wife” reintroduced Colin Sweeney, the wife killer (played by a vampy Dylan Baker) in Season 1 whose unapologetic lust for Alicia gave just about everyone the heebie jeebies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Good Wife’ Watch: What Alicia Didn’t Know', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T05:25:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dea45883-553a-51ec-a8ae-a7b7696e29e3', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dea45883-553a-51ec-a8ae-a7b7696e29e3'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on October 24, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/pageoneplus/corrections-october-24.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on October 24, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOREIGN', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: October 24', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T05:47:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bff8db0-970e-5031-be10-368352084e29', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bff8db0-970e-5031-be10-368352084e29'}, {'abstract': 'Mike Napoli’s performance behind the plate, and in the batter’s box, sparked Texas to a Game 4 victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/sports/baseball/world-series-back-at-catcher-napoli-puts-rangers-on-his-back.html', 'snippet': 'Mike Napoli’s performance behind the plate, and in the batter’s box, sparked Texas to a Game 4 victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARLINGTON, Tex. — Mike Napoli’s pregame routine includes taking a long, hard look at the lineup posted on a wall of the Texas Rangers’ clubhouse. Before Game 4 of the World Series, he had extra reason to stare at where Manager Ron Washington had put him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/baseball/25rangers_1/25rangers_1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/baseball/25rangers_1/25rangers_1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/baseball/25rangers_1/25rangers_1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Back at Catcher, Napoli Puts Rangers on His Back', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back at Catcher, Napoli Puts Rangers on His Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Napoli, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T07:06:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Spousta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spousta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c108c494-89e0-5c26-a675-fa802bf11811', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c108c494-89e0-5c26-a675-fa802bf11811'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/news-quiz-oct-24-2011/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | Oct. 24, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T08:06:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Frasier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frasier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0456a5d3-f0e6-5732-b3db-282d9506ef09', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0456a5d3-f0e6-5732-b3db-282d9506ef09'}, {'abstract': 'At least 279 people were killed and more than 1,300 were injured after a magnitude 7.2 earthquake shook eastern Turkey, close to its border with Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/world/europe/many-die-as-eastern-turkey-is-jolted-by-quake.html', 'snippet': 'At least 279 people were killed and more than 1,300 were injured after a magnitude 7.2 earthquake shook eastern Turkey, close to its border with Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — Rescue crews dug with their bare hands, used heavy machinery to remove chunks of fallen concrete and relied on cellphone calls from the missing in the search on Monday for survivors of the deadly earthquake in eastern Turkey.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/world/QUAKE/QUAKE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Turkey, Desperate Race to Find Trapped Survivors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Turkey, Desperate Race To Find Trapped Survivors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T08:22:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sebnem Arsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sebnem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/648da1b4-2e49-5d00-96dd-043e9f06b588', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/648da1b4-2e49-5d00-96dd-043e9f06b588'}, {'abstract': 'On Oct. 24, 1945, the United Nations charter took effect after being ratified by the five permanent members of the Security Council (the United States, Great Britain, France, the Soviet Union and the Republic of China) and a majority of the other 46 members.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/oct-24-1945-united-nations-is-born/', 'snippet': 'On Oct. 24, 1945, the United Nations charter took effect after being ratified by the five permanent members of the Security Council (the United States, Great Britain, France, the Soviet Union and the Republic of China) and a majority of the other ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Oct. 24, 1945, the United Nations charter took effect after being ratified by the five permanent members of the Security Council (the United States, Great Britain, France, the Soviet Union and the Republic of China) and a majority of the other 46 members.The  New York Times reported the following day, “In signing the protocol [U.S. Secretary of State James F.] Byrnes said the Charter was now a ‘part of the law of nations’ and that it was ‘a memorable day for the peace-loving peoples of all nations.’ But he warned that peace depended upon the will of the peoples for peace rather than upon documents.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oct. 24, 1945 | United Nations Is Born', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T08:35:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6efe1169-cd7e-58cb-bc90-5f3e7bc547d7', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6efe1169-cd7e-58cb-bc90-5f3e7bc547d7'}, {'abstract': 'India’s fastest track faces fanfare, farmer protests and tax questions.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/f1-races-into-india-controversy-follows/', 'snippet': 'India’s fastest track faces fanfare, farmer protests and tax questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will the Buddh International Circuit, India’s first Formula One arena, be ready on Oct. 28, when teams descend on the venue for their first practice session? Even Bernie Ecclestone had his doubts until recently.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F1 Races Into India, Controversy Follows', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T08:47:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikhila Gill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikhila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b29ae16-45ba-52e6-888a-edd78ea881b8', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b29ae16-45ba-52e6-888a-edd78ea881b8'}, {'abstract': 'Nancy McGirr went from covering civil wars in Central America to teaching photography to impoverished children. Twenty years later, she’s being honored for her dedication to her students and her art.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/from-out-of-the-dump-to-the-top-of-the-heap/', 'snippet': 'Nancy McGirr went from covering civil wars in Central America to teaching photography to impoverished children. Twenty years later, she’s being honored for her dedication to her students and her art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nancy McGirr has spent two decades in Guatemala finding value amid castoffs. The symbolism did not escape her when she started teaching photography to a handful of children whose families eked out a living scavenging through the festering, grimy heaps of the capital’s municipal dump.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Out of the Dump to the Top of the Heap', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T09:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By