', 'lead_paragraph': 'To hear Will Ferrell tell it, accepting the 14th Mark Twain Prize for American Humor was a matter of relenting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oops, There Goes the Twain Award', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferrell, Will', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy, John F, Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T14:41:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7611d3de-407c-5035-a227-3724ad00246e', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7611d3de-407c-5035-a227-3724ad00246e'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/what-were-reading-296/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Boston Globe: Almost half the fish sold at 134 restaurants, grocery stores and seafood markets in the Boston area was mislabeled, mostly as more expensive species, DNA analysis found. — Nick Fox', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T14:42:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab3ac88d-af43-5097-961c-4f34ee58dcf1', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab3ac88d-af43-5097-961c-4f34ee58dcf1'}, {'abstract': 'I accept on behalf of IS-LM.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/praise-is-always-welcome/', 'snippet': 'I accept on behalf of IS-LM.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Henry Blodget says nice things about my track record, and also points to David Frum — who has been getting ever more interesting as he wanders off the conservative reservation, saying much the same thing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Praise Is Always Welcome', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T14:43:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1029851c-20d6-51d2-97ec-afa76bd81f9c', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1029851c-20d6-51d2-97ec-afa76bd81f9c'}, {'abstract': 'Howard Greenberg brings a wealth of experience to aid in the defense of a Brooklyn man accused of kidnapping, killing and dismembering an 8-year-old boy.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/veteran-lawyer-joins-defense-team-for-trial-in-killing-of-brooklyn-boy/', 'snippet': 'Howard Greenberg brings a wealth of experience to aid in the defense of a Brooklyn man accused of kidnapping, killing and dismembering an 8-year-old boy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A veteran criminal defense lawyer signed on to defend Levi Aron, the man accused of killing 8-year-old Leiby Kletzky over the summer, strengthening a defense team that the judge presiding over the case had criticized for its inexperience.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Veteran Lawyer Joins Defense Team in Leiby Kletzky Case', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aron, Levi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Firetog, Neil J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kletzky, Leiby', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T14:49:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95c2fb05-62e9-5a9d-a270-5e053938479d', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95c2fb05-62e9-5a9d-a270-5e053938479d'}, {'abstract': 'The Lions and Raiders may need to readjust their expectations; the Jets get back on track; and just what did Tim Tebow’s winning performance prove?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/sports/a-weekend-of-disorder-in-the-nfl-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'The Lions and Raiders may need to readjust their expectations; the Jets get back on track; and just what did Tim Tebow’s winning performance prove?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just when you think you might have figured out some order amid the sports chaos, weekends like this one come along and it turns out chaos was just sitting back, waiting for another chance to turn all of your expectations into punch lines. It’s kind of like that annoying uncle who finds just the right opening to mess up your hair at family gatherings. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Disorder in the N.F.L.', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Disorder in the N.F.L.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holland, Derek', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pujols, Albert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burress, Plaxico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Carson', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodgers, Aaron', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferguson, Alex', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Napoli, Mike', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T14:50:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d75ff28a-9807-5297-bab2-abc73a38ab89', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d75ff28a-9807-5297-bab2-abc73a38ab89'}, {'abstract': 'Rising demand for its lustrous shell may end up eradicating an animal that grows slowly and needs 15 years or more to reach sexual maturity, scientists say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/science/25nautilus.html', 'snippet': 'Rising demand for its lustrous shell may end up eradicating an animal that grows slowly and needs 15 years or more to reach sexual maturity, scientists say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a living fossil whose ancestors go back a half billion years — to the early days of complex life on the planet, when the land was barren and the seas were warm.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25nautilusspan/25nautilus-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25nautilusspan/25nautilus-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25nautilusspan/25nautilus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25nautilusspan/25nautilus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25nautilusspan/25nautilus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Loving the Chambered Nautilus to Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Loving the Chambered Nautilus to Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T14:58:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By William J. Broad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Broad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e99e9c6c-26cd-59a9-9289-3af0a9e3412d', 'word_count': 1292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e99e9c6c-26cd-59a9-9289-3af0a9e3412d'}, {'abstract': 'Ray Lewis sounded almost misty-eyed last week when he talked about the glory days of the Ravens-Jaguars rivalry.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/monday-matchup-jaguars-at-ravens/', 'snippet': 'Ray Lewis sounded almost misty-eyed last week when he talked about the glory days of the Ravens-Jaguars rivalry.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Ravens at Jaguars, 8:30 p.m. Eastern, ESPNLine: Ravens by 9\uf024', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Matchup:  Ravens at Jaguars', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jacksonville Jaguars', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T15:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Tanier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a41ea59c-c426-534d-a59e-d66afd8688d9', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a41ea59c-c426-534d-a59e-d66afd8688d9'}, {'abstract': 'With his product collaborations with Nymphenburg and Steuben winding down, Ted Muehling is eager to get back to making jewelry.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/hidden-gem/', 'snippet': 'With his product collaborations with Nymphenburg and Steuben winding down, Ted Muehling is eager to get back to making jewelry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten years is the length of an average commercial lease, but it’s also, as the designer Ted Muehling has discovered, the approximate life span of a neighborhood. Back in 2001, Muehling moved his storefront workshop from a formerly desolate block on Greene Street to Howard Street — at the time SoHo’s final frontier. But when a Mondrian hotel went up nearby, so did Muehling’s rent, and the designer moved on once again. His new store, on White Street in TriBeCa, is grander in proportion and there is more selling space, but also more space for Muehling to display the many things he collects and that inspire him, from natural wonders like seashells or insects to the work of his partner, the artist Mats Gustafson, or that of his friend Jan Baracz, who carves bellybuttons into large stones. And while his workrooms are smaller, for the first time Muehling has a little studio all his own — an “attic” tucked into a mezzanine under a skylight in the back. The timing could not have been better. With his product collaborations with Nymphenburg and Steuben winding down, Muehling is eager to get back to making jewelry. On a recent morning, a pair of canaries twittered joyfully, and an installation of monarch butterflies on a dried mullein stem was magically animated by a breeze from the air-conditioner. As with his previous store, this one is livened by sounds from behind the scenes — the bang of metal on metal, the murmur of NPR — evidence that this is a place where things are made and not just sold. It’s the kind of neighborhood place, Muehling points out, where you can walk in and they’ll make a new wire for your earring if you don’t mind waiting 20 minutes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hidden Gem', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muehling, Ted', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T15:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dc6da8e-7b18-52ae-bd85-060867b9000a', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dc6da8e-7b18-52ae-bd85-060867b9000a'}, {'abstract': 'Several companies announced acquisitions that lifted shares along with a hint of more Fed stimulus and hope for a solution to Europe’s debt crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/business/daily-stock-market-activity.html', 'snippet': 'Several companies announced acquisitions that lifted shares along with a hint of more Fed stimulus and hope for a solution to Europe’s debt crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stocks in the United States closed higher Monday, extending the trend in global markets on the announcement of some strong corporate results, mergers and hope for an agreement on resolving Europe’s debt problems.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Doldrums Continue to Fade', 'kicker': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Summer Doldrums Continue to Fade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T15:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 