he head, her Congressional staff said in a statement.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giffords Arrives in North Carolina for More Treatment', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Carolina: More Therapy for Giffords', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T16:48:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b48b9a6c-fc5b-56e4-ae33-175c341e01e0', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b48b9a6c-fc5b-56e4-ae33-175c341e01e0'}, {'abstract': 'The BIS does the honors.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/the-worst-institution-in-the-world/', 'snippet': 'The BIS does the honors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ryan Avent sends us to the Bank for International Settlements, which has decided to throw everything we’ve learned from 80 years of hard thought about macroeconomics out the window, and to embrace full-frontal liquidationism. The BIS is now advocating a position indistinguishable from that of Schumpeter in the 1930s, opposing any monetary expansion because that would leave “the work of depressions undone”.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Worst Institution In The World', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T16:53:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45cf691b-5fe7-5dcd-991b-8955017f0792', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45cf691b-5fe7-5dcd-991b-8955017f0792'}, {'abstract': 'Occupy Wall Street demonstrators may lack many comforts, but one thing they do not lack is reading material.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/for-quiet-moments-between-protests-a-growing-library/', 'snippet': 'Occupy Wall Street demonstrators may lack many comforts, but one thing they do not lack is reading material.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the rain poured down over Lower Manhattan on a recent weeknight, a patchwork of umbrellas and tarps in the northeast corner of Zuccotti Park was preventing something very precious from getting wet: the books of Occupy Wall Street’s self-run People’s Library.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Quiet Moments Between Protests, a Growing Library', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zuccotti Park (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T16:55:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ritchie S. King', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ritchie', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'King', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b6b27e6-fe3e-5013-953f-719feeec94e1', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b6b27e6-fe3e-5013-953f-719feeec94e1'}, {'abstract': 'After the Obama campaign’s skillful use of social media in 2008, House Republicans have adopted Twitter as their karaoke microphone against the White House bullhorn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/us/politics/after-being-burned-in-08-republicans-embrace-twitter-hard-for-12.html', 'snippet': 'After the Obama campaign’s skillful use of social media in 2008, House Republicans have adopted Twitter as their karaoke microphone against the White House bullhorn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama’s image projected from one of the many television screens that hang in Representative Eric Cantor’s office suite, where the president could be seen telling a crowd in North Carolina that he was open to “any serious idea” Republicans offered on jobs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/us/SOCIAL/SOCIAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/25/us/SOCIAL/SOCIAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/us/SOCIAL/SOCIAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/us/SOCIAL/SOCIAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/us/SOCIAL/SOCIAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The G.O.P.’s Very Rapid Response Team', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The G.O.P.’s Very Rapid Response Team', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T16:57:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e33b6def-b249-5ec7-bc0a-5b8df18976b1', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e33b6def-b249-5ec7-bc0a-5b8df18976b1'}, {'abstract': 'Cooks cook. Hostesses host. Bartenders tend. What do owners do after a fine staff has been assembled and the handbooks have all been written?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/southfork-kitchen-and-its-owner-have-survived-a-year/', 'snippet': 'Cooks cook. Hostesses host. Bartenders tend. What do owners do after a fine staff has been assembled and the handbooks have all been written?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I promised myself (and staff) (and wife) that I would dedicate every waking (and sleeping) hour to the operation of the restaurant for exactly one year. And then, crash tutorial completed, I would back off from the day-to-day obligations, trusting that the right staff had been marshaled and the right culture inculcated, that my personal stamp would not be erased without leaving some readable palimpsest. Detachment would be healthy for all concerned — no one likes the boss hanging around all the time, and the boss could concentrate on neglected parts of his restaurant (and his life).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Southfork Kitchen (and Its Owner) Have Survived a Year', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T17:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By BRUCE BUSCHEL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BUSCHEL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b71db2d-d50a-5a02-acac-0e5ca3a5673b', 'word_count': 1141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b71db2d-d50a-5a02-acac-0e5ca3a5673b'}, {'abstract': 'Citing the need for democratic and ethical principles in the marketplace, officials from the Roman Catholic Church suggested the creation of a supranational economic authority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/world/europe/vatican-calls-for-global-oversight-of-the-economy.html', 'snippet': 'Citing the need for democratic and ethical principles in the marketplace, officials from the Roman Catholic Church suggested the creation of a supranational economic authority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VATICAN CITY — The Vatican called on Monday for an overhaul of the world’s financial systems, and again proposed establishment of a supranational authority to oversee the global economy, calling it necessary to bring more democratic and ethical principles to a marketplace run amok.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vatican Calls for Oversight 