', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Krupp and Rachel Stuart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krupp', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stuart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad4111dd-7057-5db4-a18e-80ab798b69dc', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad4111dd-7057-5db4-a18e-80ab798b69dc'}, {'abstract': 'Among the six new N.F.L. quarterbacks who started on Sunday, the Broncos’ Tim Tebow had the only win and the Vikings’ Christian Ponder had the most promising debut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/sports/football/developing-tim-tebow-christian-ponder-after-positive-starts-nfl-fast-forward.html', 'snippet': 'Among the six new N.F.L. quarterbacks who started on Sunday, the Broncos’ Tim Tebow had the only win and the Vikings’ Christian Ponder had the most promising debut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just two weeks ago the N.F.L. was enjoying a period of remarkable stability at quarterback, which surely helped inflate the early-season scoring and passing figures that generated the hand-wringing over whether the fundamental essence of football was being lost to the spread offense. Through Week 5, 30 teams started the same person at quarterback in every game, the most ever. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/25forward-pic2/25forward-pic2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/25forward-pic2/25forward-pic2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/25forward-pic2/25forward-pic2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/25forward-pic2/25forward-pic2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/25forward-pic2/25forward-pic2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Developing Tebow and Ponder After Positive Starts', 'kicker': 'N.F.L. Fast Forward', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Problems and Promise Of Tebow and Ponder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ponder, Christian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Vikings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T17:06:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/433a6533-cf29-5988-a9fa-cf2e1e43b712', 'word_count': 1639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/433a6533-cf29-5988-a9fa-cf2e1e43b712'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Bhaktipada, a charismatic spiritual leader, served eight years on charges connected to racketeering and murder for hire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/us/swami-bhaktipada-ex-hare-krishna-leader-dies-at-74.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bhaktipada, a charismatic spiritual leader, served eight years on charges connected to racketeering and murder for hire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Swami Bhaktipada, a former leader of the American Hare Krishna movement who built a sprawling golden paradise for his followers in the hills of Appalachia but who later pleaded guilty to federal racketeering charges that included conspiracy to commit the murders-for-hire of two devotees, died on Monday in a hospital near Mumbai, India. He was 74. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/swami2/swami2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 810, 'width': 823, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/swami2/swami2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/swami2/swami2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Swami Bhaktipada, Ex-Hare Krishna Leader, Dies at 74', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Swami Bhaktipada Dies at Age 74; Ex-Hare Krishna Leader and Felon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bhaktipada, Kirtanananda Swami', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hare Krishna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T17:08:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d2e7e67-48a9-52f8-95b3-879f6740ae77', 'word_count': 1334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d2e7e67-48a9-52f8-95b3-879f6740ae77'}, {'abstract': 'Once one of the few makeup options for women of color, Fashion Fair is finding increased competition from major brands and revamping its image.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/fashion/fashion-fair-deepens-its-coverage.html', 'snippet': 'Once one of the few makeup options for women of color, Fashion Fair is finding increased competition from major brands and revamping its image.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON a recent rainy evening, Rose Estime, a 35-year-old accountant who lives in Manhattan, left the Macy’s Herald Square store with a small bag containing a cleanser by Fashion Fair that she was eager to try. Ms. Estime has been a loyal customer of the cosmetics line, which is meant for black women, for more than a decade. “It matches my skin color, and I have itchy, sensitive skin and it helps me,” she said. “They’re the only products I can use without issues.” ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27SKIN1/27SKIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27SKIN1/27SKIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27SKIN1/27SKIN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':