92bfff1c4e5'}, {'abstract': 'The artist formerly known as Lauren Zettler celebrated the release of her new EP with an intimate performance at Flux Studios.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/notes-from-the-underground-lightyear/', 'snippet': 'The artist formerly known as Lauren Zettler celebrated the release of her new EP with an intimate performance at Flux Studios.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lightyear, the artist formerly known as Lauren Zettler, celebrated the release of her new EP, “All of the Miles,” with an intimate performance at Flux Studios. Zettler alternated between the piano and acoustic guitar, leading a small band and two backup vocalists through a string of airtight pop-folk numbers. Well produced and thoroughly rehearsed, Lightyear is a solidly professional act from an accomplished songwriter who should soon be mentioned in the same breath with the likes of Meiko, Feist and Regina Spektor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From the Underground | Lightyear', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T18:55:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By IO Tillett Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Io', 'middlename': 'Tillett', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/724e7022-297a-5175-a767-2ae3e322f960', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/724e7022-297a-5175-a767-2ae3e322f960'}, {'abstract': 'Maybe it’s because appetizers are a tease. Or maybe it’s because you’re at your hungriest when you eat them.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/my-three-favorite-appetizers-i-think/', 'snippet': 'Maybe it’s because appetizers are a tease. Or maybe it’s because you’re at your hungriest when you eat them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My three favorite appetizers vary by day, by week — even by moment. I like too many of them. Maybe it’s because appetizers are a tease. Or maybe it’s because you’re at your hungriest when you eat them. It seems like there are an awful lot of good ones out there. All the better to experiment. If they don’t turn out perfect, so what? They’re not the main course.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Three Favorite Appetizers, I Think', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Martha', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pepperidge Farm Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Galicia (Spain)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T18:57:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lia Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5f1ef7b-c9c0-5494-8359-f41005ec79d0', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5f1ef7b-c9c0-5494-8359-f41005ec79d0'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Thailand, Turkey, Libya and Cuba.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/24/blogs/20111024POD.html', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Thailand, Turkey, Libya and Cuba.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Thailand, Turkey, Libya and Cuba.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/blogs/20111024POD-slide-9OZD/20111024POD-slide-9OZD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/blogs/20111024POD-slide-9OZD/20111024POD-slide-9OZD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/24/blogs/20111024POD-slide-9OZD/20111024POD-slide-9OZD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Thailand and Elsewhere', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T19:02:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/2c50f90a-0d11-5ee6-b80f-f78168ec22d6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/2c50f90a-0d11-5ee6-b80f-f78168ec22d6'}, {'abstract': 'Two books examine the dangers of drunken driving and concussions on the playing field.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/health/25zuger.html', 'snippet': 'Two books examine the dangers of drunken driving and concussions on the playing field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A sports arena is a symbol of rousing good times; so is an open bar. Both are also reliable harbingers of medical disaster. And as two new books make clear, when one man’s sport is another’s undoing (or merely his own), decades may be lost in bitter disagreement over what is to be done.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25ZUGE1/25ZUGE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 610, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype