itical streak who praised the Upper West Side for its down-to-earthness makes an $11.7 million  move skyward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oct. 28, 5:21 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Deal | Alec Baldwin Buys a Penthouse in the Village', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, Alec', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T19:14:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a193ee3e-07c7-5750-9ac7-dd7b2668090f', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a193ee3e-07c7-5750-9ac7-dd7b2668090f'}, {'abstract': 'Preliminary estimates show that the World Series attracted more viewers than an N.F.L. game on Sunday night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/for-a-night-baseball-beats-football-in-the-ratings/', 'snippet': 'Preliminary estimates show that the World Series attracted more viewers than an N.F.L. game on Sunday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps it was the 62-7 score, or the increased competition from other networks or an overall lack of interest in a match-up – a rematch of Super Bowl XLIV – between the New Orleans Saints and a Peyton Manning-less Indianapolis Colts team. Whatever the reason, preliminary estimates from Nielsen suggest that “Sunday Night Football” on NBC posted its lowest rating in nearly three years. It was not the No. 1 program of the night in total viewers or in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic. That claim goes to Game 4 of the World Series, in which the Texas Rangers defeated the St. Louis Cardinals, 4-0. That baseball game averaged 15.2 million total viewers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Night, Baseball Beats Football in the Ratings', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T19:15:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b9aa63e-1a5b-5248-952d-4b99152f02f1', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b9aa63e-1a5b-5248-952d-4b99152f02f1'}, {'abstract': 'The best of readers’ street fashion photos for the week of Oct. 17.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/24/fashion/20111024-streetstyle-user.html', 'snippet': 'The best of readers’ street fashion photos for the week of Oct. 17.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best of readers’ street fashion photos for the week of Oct. 17.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/fashion/20111024-streetstyle-user-slide-FREE/20111024-streetstyle-user-slide-FREE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/fashion/20111024-streetstyle-user-slide-FREE/20111024-streetstyle-user-slide-FREE-thumbStanda