t six months.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/district-attorney-wont-drop-charges-against-protesters/', 'snippet': 'Under an offer from the district attorney’s office, some 300 Occupy Wall Street protesters could have charges against them dismissed as long as they do not get arrested again in the next six months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Manhattan district attorney’s office will not summarily dismiss the charges against some 300 Occupy Wall Street protesters who were arrested and charged with disorderly conduct during rallies on the Brooklyn Bridge and at Union Square, a lawyer for the protesters said Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'District Attorney Won’t Drop Charges Against Protesters', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T20:34:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df3b6073-0669-5d5c-a536-96867849e387', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df3b6073-0669-5d5c-a536-96867849e387'}, {'abstract': 'Israel reached an agreement with Egypt for the release of Ilan Grapel of Queens, who also holds Israeli citizenship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/world/middleeast/deal-for-release-of-american-held-in-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'Israel reached an agreement with Egypt for the release of Ilan Grapel of Queens, who also holds Israeli citizenship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Israel announced Monday that it had reached an agreement with Egypt, with American assistance, for the release of Ilan Grapel, an American law student from Queens who also holds Israeli citizenship. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/world/MIDEAST/MIDEAST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 725, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/world/MIDEAST/MIDEAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/world/MIDEAST/MIDEAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Reaches Deal for Release of an American Held in Egypt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Reaches Deal for Release Of an American Held in Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grapel, Ilan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T20:34:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_o