rought to assembling their fabulous collections of art.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25BEEC/25BEEC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25BEEC/25BEEC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25BEEC/25BEEC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25BEEC/25BEEC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25BEEC/25BEEC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Next for Newport Preservation: Gilded-Age Beeches', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Next for Newport Preservation: Gilded-Age Beeches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newport (RI)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T20:35:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cornelia Dean', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cornelia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dean', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef75e017-2901-53c9-affa-cfffdeca9e1c', 'word_count': 1161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef75e017-2901-53c9-affa-cfffdeca9e1c'}, {'abstract': 'The Washington art band Bluebrain’s new iPhone app is a grand orchestral guide to the streams, forests and rock faces of Central Park.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/for-iphones-a-central-park-soundtrack/', 'snippet': 'The Washington art band Bluebrain’s new iPhone app is a grand orchestral guide to the streams, forests and rock faces of Central Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When that great emerald and hilly patch at the center of Manhattan first opened, music was limited to brief concerts under the Naumberg Bandshell. Today, of course, Central Park is fixed in sonic history — landmark rock shows, global benefits, swanky midsummer soirees — so diverse that any attempt to fuse the park’s streams, forests and rock faces into a single musical experience seems almost futile.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For iPhones, a Central Park Soundtrack', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T20:37:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin R. Freed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Freed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71693d13-a695-5765-80e3-f55f52ec945f', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71693d13-a695-5765-80e3-f55f52ec945f'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers are working to incorporate communications devices into the clothes we wear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/science/25shirt.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers are working to incorporate communications devices into the clothes we wear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Volakis wants to make the world hands-free. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New Yor