ideo/e12a664e-0a63-581f-9567-42ed22e27bb4'}, {'abstract': 'A veteran of the Obama and Clinton administrations, Neera Tanden, will lead the Center for American Progress, whose progressive viewpoint reflects a disaffected element of President Obama’s base.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/new-leader-for-liberal-research-group/', 'snippet': 'A veteran of the Obama and Clinton administrations, Neera Tanden, will lead the Center for American Progress, whose progressive viewpoint reflects a disaffected element of President Obama’s base.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A veteran of the Obama and Clinton administrations, Neera Tanden, will be taking over as president of the Center for American Progress, a research organization that represents the views of the president’s more liberal, and somewhat disaffected, base.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Leader for Liberal Research Group', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tanden, Neera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for American Progress', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T21:44:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2618c91-9596-5f41-9cf7-20ff109ec48c', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2618c91-9596-5f41-9cf7-20ff109ec48c'}, {'abstract': 'As part of the White Light Festival, the London Symphony Orchestra performed Beethoven’s seldom heard “Missa Solemnis,” on Friday, and Britten’s “War Requiem,” on Sunday afternoon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/arts/music/london-symphony-orchestra-at-avery-fisher-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'As part of the White Light Festival, the London Symphony Orchestra performed Beethoven’s seldom heard “Missa Solemnis,” on Friday, and Britten’s “War Requiem,” on Sunday afternoon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lincoln Center’s monthlong White Light Festival is back for its second year. As before, the focus of the event is a little blurry. In the words of Lincoln Center’s artistic director, Jane Moss, White Light is an exploration of music and art’s power to reveal “dimensions of our interior lives.” The programs offer “a spectrum of artistic expression that moves us inward and expands our spirit.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/requiem/requiem-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/requiem/requiem-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/requiem/requiem-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/requiem/requiem-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/requiem/requiem-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading the March to a Mystical Place', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leading the March to a