dvertising', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodhouse, Brad', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic National Committee', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T21:59:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae2a442b-a074-5741-bb56-98f4c1666fb2', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae2a442b-a074-5741-bb56-98f4c1666fb2'}, {'abstract': '“Radio and Juliet” interprets Shakespeare’s story of star-crossed lovers with Radiohead songs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/arts/dance/radio-and-juliet-at-skirball-center-review.html', 'snippet': '“Radio and Juliet” interprets Shakespeare’s story of star-crossed lovers with Radiohead songs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s the pitch: a ballet of Romeo and Juliet. Sure, that’s been done before, but this is contemporary, set to songs by Radiohead, sure to appeal to a youthful demographic. And get this: Juliet doesn’t kill herself. The whole love story comes through her flashbacks. This thing is stripped-down, chic, just Juliet in a corset and six men in suits without shirts. It doesn’t take up your whole evening, either. An hour and you’re out.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/radiohead/radiohead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Romeo Meets Radiohead in a Love Story of Twitches', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romeo Meets Radiohead In a Love Story of Twitches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radiohead', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:02:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c435f1e-d955-5aec-bf31-6b2a0756ae64', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c435f1e-d955-5aec-bf31-6b2a0756ae64'}, {'abstract': 'Kansas City Ballet inaugurates its new home by adapting Twain’s classic in a new all-American work, “Tom Sawyer.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/arts/dance/tom-sawyer-by-kansas-city-ballet-review.html', 'snippet': 'Kansas City Ballet inaugurates its new home by adapting Twain’s classic in a new all-American work, “Tom Sawyer.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANSAS CITY, Mo. — On Thursday I was exploring America’s oldest grand opera house still used for its original purpose, the Academy of Music in Philadelphia. Over the weekend I was discovering its newest auditorium for opera and ballet, the Kauffman Center for the Performing Arts here in Kansas City. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/SAWYER/SAWYER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/SAWYER/SAWYER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/SAWYER/SAWYER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yes, Those Are Tom, Becky and Huck Leaping', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yes, Those Are Tom, Becky and Huck Leaping', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Ballet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:03:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8d68634-ec9a-5546-a432-30f379f4eab1', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8d68634-ec9a-5546-a432-30f379f4eab1'}, {'abstract': 'A. O. Scott looks back at Spike Lee’s 2002 film that takes place in the aftermath of the 9/11 attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/critics-picks-video-25th-hour/', 'snippet': 'A. O. Scott looks back at Spike Lee’s 2002 film that takes place in the aftermath of the 9/11 attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s Critics’ Picks, A. O. Scott looks back at Spike Lee‘s 2002 film “25th Hour.” It stars Edward Norton as Monty Brogan, a man experiencing his last day of freedom before going to serve a long prison sentence. It tracks him as he says his goodbyes and takes care of some unfinished business. “25th Hour” features a strong ensemble cast, including Brian Cox, Barry Pepper, Philip Seymour Hoffman, Anna Paquin and Rosario Dawson as Monty’s girlfriend. “But the real love interest,” Mr. Scott says, “is New York City itself.” The film takes in the aftermath of the September 11 attacks and “it captures, better than any other movie, the mood of raw shock and grief that blanketed the city in those months.” Have you seen “25th Hour?” Please share your thoughts in the comments area below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Critics’ Picks Video: ’25th Hour’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dawson, Rosario', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Philip Seymour', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Spike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norton, Edward', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paquin, Anna', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:04:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d769710-0300-5484-aeb7-301a70a25cad', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d769710-0300-5484-aeb7-301a70a25cad'}, {'abstract': 'The group occupied Artists Space, a gallery in SoHo with heat and indoor plumbing, on Saturday and left when asked on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/nyregion/occupy-wall-street-splinter-group-occupies-art-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'The group occupied Artists Space, a gallery in SoHo with heat and indoor plumbing, on Saturday and left when asked on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The boundaries of Occupy Wall Street expanded beyond Zuccotti Park over the weekend, as a splinter group briefly took over an art gallery in SoHo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protesters Briefly Take Over a Gallery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protesters Briefly Take Over a Gallery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARTISTS SPACE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:04:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/812ddfc0-eada-53fb-b3fd-de470f535f88', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/812ddfc0-eada-53fb-b3fd-de470f535f88'}, {'abstract': 'Many members of the middle class have to look after their disabled relatives themselves, or pay someone to do it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/health/25seniors.html', 'snippet': 'Many members of the middle class have to look after their disabled relatives themselves, or pay someone to do it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The law that many Americans had hoped would transform the nation’s dysfunctional system of long-term care for the swelling ranks of people with disabilities and dementia quietly died this month, a victim of its own weaknesses, a toxic political environment and President Obama’s re-election campaign focus on jobs.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25JPSENI2/25JPSENI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 868, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25JPSENI2/25JPSENI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/science/25JPSENI2/25JPSENI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Still No Relief in Sight for Long-Term Needs', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still No Relief in Sight For Long-Term Needs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Health Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Long-Term Care Insurance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 9, 'majo