k': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02afa58d-7d04-5ae7-abe6-0a91c8012214', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02afa58d-7d04-5ae7-abe6-0a91c8012214'}, {'abstract': 'A recipe for tagliolini with chicken livers and fennel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/dining/tagliolini-with-chicken-livers-and-fennel-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'A recipe for tagliolini with chicken livers and fennel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Rosso di Montalcino wines, my appetite turns to chicken livers. Their edge of bitterness tamed by salt seems to be on the same wavelength as the wines. In Tuscany, chicken liver crostini, often seasoned with anchovies, are a typical palate awakener. I gave my chicken livers a bit more heft, with a flat noodle pasta, using black olive paste for salty bite. This dish can be a dinner party first course — the primi, as they say in Italy — to be followed by a more substantial main dish, perhaps served with a Brunello. Or the pasta and the Rosso can stand on their own for a simpler dinner in the American style.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26PAIR_SPAN/Pairings-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26PAIR_SPAN/Pairings-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26PAIR_SPAN/Pairings-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26PAIR_SPAN/Pairings-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26PAIR_SPAN/Pairings-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tagliolini With Chicken Livers and Fennel', 'kicker': 'Recipe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pairings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chickens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pasta', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:10:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55902d38-a48f-5ecf-852b-c2ca2fbd6318', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55902d38-a48f-5ecf-852b-c2ca2fbd6318'}, {'abstract': 'The wine panel tasted 20 bottles of Rosso di Montalcino, with its unmistakable earthy, dusty flavors of pure sangiovese grapes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/dining/reviews/rosso-di-montalcino-wine-review.html', 'snippet': 'The wine panel tasted 20 bottles of Rosso di Montalcino, with its unmistakable earthy, dusty flavors of pure sangiovese grapes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN retrospect, what was all the fuss about? Here sat the wine panel, having tasted 20 bottles of Rosso di Montalcino, reveling in the unmistakable earthy, dusty flavors of pure sangiovese. With their winsomely bitter, citrus-tinged cherry flavors, these wines were soulful and elemental, like good trattoria food. They wanted less talking and more drinking.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26WINE/Wine-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26WINE/Wine-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26WINE/Wine-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pure Montalcino, Minus the Wait', 'kicker': 'Wines of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pure Montalcino, Minus the Wait', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:11:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Dining & Wine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fd2f249-d0cb-52e0-9224-5311bdb3d3bc', 'word_count': 1294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fd2f249-d0cb-52e0-9224-5311bdb3d3bc'}, {'abstract': 'My parents surprised my three sisters and me with a “bonding” vacation and carte blanche to travel anywhere to do so. We are 27 to 21, with varied interests and are looking for quality down time, but also activities. Does such a place even exist?', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/qa-for-sisters-hawaii-may-beckon/', 'snippet': 'My parents surprised my three sisters and me with a “bonding” vacation and carte blanche to travel anywhere to do so. We are 27 to 21, with varied interests and are looking for quality down time, but also activities. Does such a place even exist?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: For Sisters, Hawaii May Beckon', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glaciers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surfing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oahu (Hawaii)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Patagonia (Argentina)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:14:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13c1f763-28e4-594a-b81b-962fab34476b', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13c1f763-28e4-594a-b81b-962fab34476b'}, {'abstract': 'Lens: Turning Point — John Minchillo', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/24/blogs/20111024-lens-tp-johnm.html', 'snippet': 'Lens: Turning Point — John Minchillo', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lens: Turning Point — John Minchillo', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/blogs/20111024-lens-tp-johnm-slide-E4TX/20111024-lens-tp-johnm-slide-E4TX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lens: Turning Point — John Minchillo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:24:04+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/0ecb4a09-7d63-56fe-8cab-aab4606356a9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/0ecb4a09-7d63-56fe-8cab-aab4606356a9'}, {'abstract': 'Claire Tomalin’s “Charles Dickens” and Robert Douglas-Fairhurst’s “Becoming Dickens” explore a complicated author.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/books/charles-dickens-by-claire-tomalin-becoming-dickens.html', 'snippet': 'Claire Tomalin’s “Charles Dickens” and Robert Douglas-Fairhurst’s “Becoming Dickens” explore a complicated author.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a remarkable account of a meeting he had with Charles Dickens in 1862, Dostoyevsky recalled that the British novelist told him: “All the good simple people in his novels, Little Nell, even the holy simpletons like Barnaby Rudge, are what he wanted to have been, and his villains were what he was (or rather, what he found in himself), his cruelty, his attacks of causeless enmity toward those who were helpless and looked to him for comfort, his shrinking from those whom he ought to love, being used up in what he wrote. There were two people in him, he told me: one who feels as he ought to feel and one who feels the opposite. From the one who feels the opposite I make my evil characters, from the one who feels as a man ought to feel I try to live my life. ‘Only two people?’ I asked.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/jp-book-2/jp-book-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 861, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/jp-book-2/jp-book-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/jp-book-2/jp-book-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two-Sided Man Gets Two New Biographies', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two-Sided Man Gets Two New Biographies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tomalin, Claire', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douglas-Fairhurst, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickens, Charles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/136dba71-5dc2-5434-ba33-654cc8c74587', 'word_count': 1401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/136dba71-5dc2-5434-ba33-654cc8c74587'}, {'abstract': 'Young South Korean pop bands, and plenty of them, packed them in at Madison Square Garden on Sunday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/arts/music/shinee-and-south-korean-k-pop-groups-at-madison-square-garden-review.html', 'snippet': 'Young South Korean pop bands, and plenty of them, packed them in at Madison Square Garden on Sunday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Think of the work required to make just one Justin Bieber. The production, the management, the vocal training, the choreography, the swagger coaching — all that effort to create one teen-pop star in a country that’s still starving for them. South Korea has no such drought, thanks to several companies that specialize in manufacturing a steady stream of teenage idols, in groups of various configurations. One of the longest-running of these companies is SM Entertainment, which on Sunday night hosted SM Town Live, a sold-out showcase at Madison Square Garden for several of its acts, any one of which any American reality-TV talent show or major-label A&R department worth its salt would be thrilled to have discovered.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/kpop_span/kpop-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/kpop_span/kpop-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/kpop_span/kpop-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/kpop_span/kpop-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/kpop_span/kpop-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Korean Pop Machine, Running on Innocence and Hair Gel', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Korean Pop Machine, Running on Innocence and Hair Gel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SM Entertainment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:32:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5927210-ddae-5e5d-a06d-aa28a4fb714b', 'word_count': 922, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5927210-ddae-5e5d-a06d-aa28a4fb714b'}, {'abstract': 'Metro areas where the share of poor people living in the suburbs crossed the 50 percent mark between 2000 and 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/10/23/us/poverty-in-the-suburbs.html', 'snippet': 'Metro areas where the share of poor people living in the suburbs crossed the 50 percent mark between 2000 and 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Metro areas where the share of poor people living in the suburbs crossed the 50 percent mark between 2000 and 2010.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poverty in the Suburbs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:33:55+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/b1dd7055-f967-548e-9d95-e44c57d62f9a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/b1dd7055-f967-548e-9d95-e44c57d62f9a'}, {'abstract': 'Television has lagged behind film in showing the battlefields of Iraq and Afghanistan. The latest offering, “Bomb Patrol: Afghanistan,” begins on Tuesday night on the G4 cable channel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/arts/television/television-still-struggles-to-bring-war-zones-home.html', 'snippet': 'Television has lagged behind film in showing the battlefields of Iraq and Afghanistan. The latest offering, “Bomb Patrol: Afghanistan,” begins on Tuesday night on the G4 cable channel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hollywood has brought the wars in Afghanistan and Iraq home for American filmgoers in sometimes stunning, painful detail in recent years. “Lions for Lambs” featured stars like Tom Cruise and Meryl Streep. “The Hurt Locker” won the Oscar for best picture. “Restrepo” and other documentaries wowed reviewers.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/bomb/bomb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/bomb/bomb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/bomb/bomb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 595, 'width': 328, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/bomb/bomb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/arts/bomb/bomb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TV Struggles to Bring War Zones to Americans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'TV Struggles To Bring War Zones To Americans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'G4 Network', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:39:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3b0a51d-de16-5040-ad1a-fa4e17c57571', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3b0a51d-de16-5040-ad1a-fa4e17c57571'}, {'abstract': 'Netflix says it lost 800,000 subscribers in the United States in three months, a notable decline after years of consistent growth. Its stock fell sharply after the announcement.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/netflix-loses-subscribers-despite-higher-earnings/', 'snippet': 'Netflix says it lost 800,000 subscribers in the United States in three months, a notable decline after years of consistent growth. Its stock fell sharply after the announcement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Netflix said Monday that it ended the third quarter of the year with 23.8 million subscribers in the United States, a loss of 800,000 in three months, representing a notable decline after years of consistent growth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Netflix Loses Subscribers, Though Earnings Rise', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:44:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ff2dca6-ddd7-59a7-ae67-41a0ed9c6240', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ff2dca6-ddd7-59a7-ae67-41a0ed9c6240'}, {'abstract': 'The new Samsung MV800 has a flip-up three-inch rear screen that makes it perfect for self-portraits.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/a-camera-narcissus-could-love/', 'snippet': 'The new Samsung MV800 has a flip-up three-inch rear screen that makes it perfect for self-portraits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Samsung is offering a new camera that Narcissus might love almost as much as he loved himself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Camera Narcissus Could Love', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T22:59:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1119e5a0-94e9-5c26-9171-25bd3ff11a29', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1119e5a0-94e9-5c26-9171-25bd3ff11a29'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s 2012 presidential campaign started its first Tumblr microblogging site on Monday. The account will be used to showcase submissions from supporters.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/obama-campaign-experiments-with-tumblr-for-12/', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s 2012 presidential campaign started its first Tumblr microblogging site on Monday. The account will be used to showcase submissions from supporters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s no secret that President Obama’s victory in 2008 was helped by his adoption of Twitter and other social media platforms. For 2012, Republicans and other politicians are flocking to\xa0these services too, hoping to spread the party gospel 140 characters at a time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Campaign Experiments With Tumblr for ’12', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tumblr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T23:12:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8349ea7e-77c9-5c8b-9cf7-801b4f389264', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8349ea7e-77c9-5c8b-9cf7-801b4f389264'}, {'abstract': 'The corporation’s independent shareholders voted largely against reinstating Rupert Murdoch’s sons James and Lachlan to the company board, according to a tally.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/news-corp-shareholders-slap-down-murdochs-sons/', 'snippet': 'The corporation’s independent shareholders voted largely against reinstating Rupert Murdoch’s sons James and Lachlan to the company board, according to a tally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'News Corporation‘s independent shareholders voted largely against reinstating Rupert Murdoch’s sons James and Lachlan to the company board, according to a tally the company filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission on Monday.\xa0Although the Murdoch family’s control of a large percentage of voting shares all but guaranteed that all 15 board members would be re-elected after a contentious shareholder meeting on Friday, the detailed tally showed widespread opposition to the roles of James and Lachlan Murdoch. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Murdoch’s Sons Rebuked by News Corp. Shareholders', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, James R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Lachlan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEWS CORP', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T23:17:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick and Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52180dfb-0358-578b-aaa4-0f2d9449e1c7', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52180dfb-0358-578b-aaa4-0f2d9449e1c7'}, {'abstract': '“I Want My MTV,” by Craig Marks and Rob Tannenbaum, chronicles the rise and fall of America’s first music video channel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/books/i-want-my-mtv-by-craig-marks-and-rob-tannenbaum-review.html', 'snippet': '“I Want My MTV,” by Craig Marks and Rob Tannenbaum, chronicles the rise and fall of America’s first music video channel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like almost everyone who was a teenager in the early 1980s, when the Music Television network first went live on cable, I wanted my MTV. I’d glue myself to the channel for hours, losing body mass, muscle control and self-esteem, the way my son gives himself over to video games today. MTV demanded that you linger in front of it for entire afternoons, because it tucked its few good videos amid so many horrible ones. You had to learn Zen couch potato patience.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/book1/book1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 904, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/book1/book1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/24/arts/book1/book1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Video Killed Radio Stars', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Video Killed Radio Stars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tannenbaum, Rob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T23:31:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7971093c-4954-54ba-9bac-1ba67dd3ca92', 'word_count': 1225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7971093c-4954-54ba-9bac-1ba67dd3ca92'}, {'abstract': 'A video of a Tibetan monk’s attempt to kill himself last month by self-immolation to protest Chinese policies has been released.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/world/asia/in-china-video-of-tibetan-monks-protest-released.html', 'snippet': 'A video of a Tibetan monk’s attempt to kill himself last month by self-immolation to protest Chinese policies has been released.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A video of a Tibetan monk’s attempt to kill himself last month by self-immolation to protest Chinese policies has been released. The video was given anonymously to The Associated Press and released Sunday. It shows a monk, Lobsang Konchok, lying in a street in the town of Aba, in Sichuan Province, with his robes and shoes partly burned off. Security officers and a police car are visible in the background. The monk set himself on fire on Sept. 26 but lived. Nine Tibetans have set themselves on fire this year in Sichuan, and at least five have died. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Video of Monk’s Protest Released', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Video of Monk’s Protest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immolation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monasteries and Monks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T23:31:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f087d13-4097-530d-ad5e-7f3a1934eade', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f087d13-4097-530d-ad5e-7f3a1934eade'}, {'abstract': 'A developing relationship between investors and entrepreneurs in Brazil comes as venture capital firms in the United States are starting to take notice.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/nurturing-start-ups-in-brazil-with-a-nod-to-silicon-valley/', 'snippet': 'A developing relationship between investors and entrepreneurs in Brazil comes as venture capital firms in the United States are starting to take notice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAMPINAS, Brazil — When the investment firm Monashees Capital first called Juliano Ipolito, the co-founder of an online handicrafts marketplace, he assumed that he would have to visit the firm in São Paulo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nurturing Start-Ups in Brazil, With a Nod to Silicon Valley', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Butterfield, Stewart', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palihapitiya, Chamath', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACCEL PARTNERS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T23:32:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vinod Sreeharsha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vinod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sreeharsha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19140e28-a08d-5739-a732-6031a0ec8883', 'word_count': 1091, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19140e28-a08d-5739-a732-6031a0ec8883'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge temporarily blocked a law requiring public assistance applicants to take a drug test, saying it is probably an intrusion on their Fourth Amendment rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/us/welfare-drug-test-requirement-blocked-in-florida.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge temporarily blocked a law requiring public assistance applicants to take a drug test, saying it is probably an intrusion on their Fourth Amendment rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge on Monday temporarily blocked a far-reaching Florida law that requires public assistance applicants to take a drug test, saying the law probably violates a constitutional ban on unreasonable search and seizure. The law, which took effect in July, is the only one in the country that requires people receiving cash assistance through welfare to pass a drug test. The applicants must pay for the test themselves but are reimbursed if they test negative. A similar law in Michigan was struck down as unconstitutional a decade ago. In her ruling, Judge Mary S. Scriven of Federal District Court in Orlando said that there was “no special need” for the state to require drug tests and that it should stop, at least until the court made a final determination in the case. The “court concludes that preliminarily enjoining what appears likely to be deemed an unconstitutional intrusion on the Fourth Amendment rights” of applicants “serves the public interest,” Judge Scriven said. The ruling stems from a lawsuit filed by Luis Lebron, a Navy veteran, and the American Civil Liberties Union of Florida. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida: Judge Blocks Welfare Drug Tests', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida: Judge Blocks Welfare Drug Tests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Drug Use)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T23:43:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/32ce7fe1-1ccf-5671-be6a-fe571acc1ec5', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32ce7fe1-1ccf-5671-be6a-fe571acc1ec5'}, {'abstract': 'The general prosecutor’s office in Ukraine on Monday said that it had reopened another criminal case against Yulia V. Tymoshenko.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/world/europe/ukraine-reopens-case-on-yulia-tymoshenko.html', 'snippet': 'The general prosecutor’s office in Ukraine on Monday said that it had reopened another criminal case against Yulia V. Tymoshenko.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The general prosecutor’s office on Monday said that it had reopened another criminal case against Yulia V. Tymoshenko, the opposition leader and a former prime minister. Ms. Tymoshenko is already serving a seven-year sentence on charges that have been condemned in the West as politically motivated. The reopened case, which dates back 15 years to her tenure as head of United Energy Systems of Ukraine, alleges that she embezzled about $3 million from the federal budget and evaded paying about $2.5 million in taxes. The case was closed in 2005, after Ms. Tymoshenko became prime minister. The announcement further dims hopes that she will be released and allowed to take part in 2012 parliamentary elections, which European leaders have said is a precondition for completing free trade and association agreements between Ukraine and the European Union. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ukraine: New Test for Ex-Premier', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ukraine: New Test for Ex-Premier', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tymoshenko, Yulia V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embezzlement', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-24T23:44:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0404aebe-f456-529e-af47-c2d84147ba87', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0404aebe-f456-529e-af47-c2d84147ba87'}, {'abstract': 'Regulators claimed that Pipeline Trading Systems, an alternative trading platform, failed to provide the confidentiality and liquidity it advertised to customers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/business/trading-company-will-pay-1-million-to-settle-sec-case.html', 'snippet': 'Regulators claimed that Pipeline Trading Systems, an alternative trading platform, failed to provide the confidentiality and liquidity it advertised to customers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pipeline Trading Systems, an alternative trading platform, will pay $1 million to resolve regulatory claims that it failed to provide the confidentiality and liquidity it advertised to customers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trading Company Will Pay $1 Million to Settle S.E.C. Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trading Company Will Pay $1 Million to Settle S.E.C. Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities