0 ejections in a February game, have a rematch Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNIONDALE, N.Y. — The Islanders said it would be just another game when they face the Penguins here Tuesday night — and again in Pittsburgh on Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/hockey/hockey-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/hockey/hockey-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/hockey/hockey-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/hockey/hockey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/sports/hockey/hockey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Revisiting Night of Taunts, Punches and Injuries', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Revisiting Night of Taunts, Punches and Injuries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Islanders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Penguins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dipietro, Rick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooke, Matt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T01:41:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bed988b8-283c-5310-adc0-47502b0bdd2c', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bed988b8-283c-5310-adc0-47502b0bdd2c'}, {'abstract': 'A White House meeting was convened last week to tackle the issue of what to do if the Libyan leader were captured alive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/us/politics/before-qaddafis-death-us-debated-his-future.html', 'snippet': 'A White House meeting was convened last week to tackle the issue of what to do if the Libyan leader were captured alive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Last Wednesday evening, the White House convened a 90-minute meeting to tackle a looming, delicate question: What should be done with the Libyan dictator, Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi, if he were captured alive, either in Libya or in a neighboring country?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before Qaddafi’s Death, U.S. Debated His Future', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Before Qaddafi’s Death, U.S. Debated His Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transitional National Council (Libya)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T01:41:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b66c86f4-a296-58c0-b285-1d32bebd968a', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b66c86f4-a296-58c0-b285-1d32bebd968a'}, {'abstract': 'In his biography of Steve Jobs, Walter Isaacson had difficulty getting the critical and historical distance he needed to take his subject’s true measure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/opinion/nocera-the-biographers-dilemma.html', 'snippet': 'In his biography of Steve Jobs, Walter Isaacson had difficulty getting the critical and historical distance he needed to take his subject’s true measure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was halfway through Walter Isaacson’s new biography of Steve Jobs when I suddenly went searching through my bookshelf for the book he wrote about Benjamin Franklin. I had read the latter biography when it came out in 2003, and I remembered it fondly. I was trying to figure out why “Steve Jobs,” despite being full of new information about the most compelling businessman of the modern era, was leaving me cold.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Biographer’s Dilemma', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Biographer&#8217;s Dilemma', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isaacson, Walter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T01:56:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dff598b-16d3-5990-8e55-bd41d40845b5', 'word_count': 859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dff598b-16d3-5990-8e55-bd41d40845b5'}, {'abstract': 'C. W. Stewart has the loaf of bread and the jug of wine. You do the rest.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/stocking/', 'snippet': 'C. W. Stewart has the loaf of bread and the jug of wine. You do the rest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY’S PUZZLE — It’s nice to welcome back C. W. Stewart, not just because she’s the second female constructor in a row this week, but because we haven’t had a puzzle from her since June (Across Lite, Solution, blog).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday: Bad Child’s Stocking Filler', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T02:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b126982a-153b-5825-a3e3-6eeb60add8eb', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b126982a-153b-5825-a3e3-6eeb60add8eb'}, {'abstract': 'New refinancing rules could help millions of homeowners, but more is still needed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/opinion/on-the-road-to-mortgage-relief.html', 'snippet': 'New refinancing rules could help millions of homeowners, but more is still needed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At long last, Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac, the government-run mortgage companies, have issued new rules to allow millions of underwater borrowers, who are current on their payments, to refinance their high-rate mortgages into lower-rate loans. President Obama, who pushed for the changes, rightly emphasized the benefits in a speech on Monday in Las Vegas, a city ravaged by foreclosures. Refinancings will lower monthly payments, reduce the likelihood of default and boost consumer spending. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Road to Relief', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Road to Relief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeowner Affordability and Stability Plan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Assn (Fannie Mae)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T02:07:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad9c76cf-c469-53b4-9d35-411a48952962', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad9c76cf-c469-53b4-9d35-411a48952962'}, {'abstract': 'Borough President Marty Markowitz’s network of nonprofit groups has received large donations from corporations and developers with pending Brooklyn projects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/nyregion/for-brooklyn-leader-marty-markowitz-mix-of-business-charity-and-power.html', 'snippet': 'Borough President Marty Markowitz’s network of nonprofit groups has received large donations from corporations and developers with pending Brooklyn projects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When one of the biggest real estate developments in Brooklyn was stalled two years ago, its owner turned to the city government for help, seeking $20 million in financing. Nearly 50 projects were applying for a small number of aid packages at the time, but this one, City Point, had a prominent supporter.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/nyregion/ymarty1/ymarty1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/25/nyregion/ymarty1/ymarty1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/nyregion/ymarty1/ymarty1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/nyregion/ymarty1/ymarty1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/nyregion/ymarty1/ymarty1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Brooklyn Office, Mixing Clout and Charity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Brooklyn Office, Mixing Clout and Charity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Markowitz, Marty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Forest City Ratner Companies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T02:10:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins and Alison Leigh Cowan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'Leigh', 'lastname': 'Cowan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15d3a60b-c581-57d8-8f68-34d821f07ce7', 'word_count': 1999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15d3a60b-c581-57d8-8f68-34d821f07ce7'}, {'abstract': 'Anna Fermanova was sentenced to four months in prison for trying to smuggle night-vision weapon scopes to Russia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/nyregion/anna-fermanova-sentenced-for-trying-to-smuggle-weapon-scopes-to-russia.html', 'snippet': 'Anna Fermanova was sentenced to four months in prison for trying to smuggle night-vision weapon scopes to Russia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'She would always be “the other Anna,” her alleged criminal misdeeds and her personal life not quite the measure of the Anna who came before her. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woman Sentenced in Effort to Smuggle Scopes to Russia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Woman Sentenced in Effort To Smuggle Scopes to Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smuggling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T02:11:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mosi Secret', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mosi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Secret', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0fb2d49-d09f-5eac-8dbb-33f15fca63ed', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0fb2d49-d09f-5eac-8dbb-33f15fca63ed'}, {'abstract': 'A puzzle about how ensemble action can be honed down to act on individual units – a process analogous to how our thoughts control our actions by ensemble-to-single neuron honing in the brain.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/numberplay-from-sledgehammer-to-scalpel/', 'snippet': 'A puzzle about how ensemble action can be honed down to act on individual units – a process analogous to how our thoughts control our actions by ensemble-to-single neuron honing in the brain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weeks ago, we celebrated the Rubik’s Cube. One of the things that I find fascinating about the Rubik’s Cube is that, even though a single move changes the position of 8 cubies, you can string together a series of moves such that you can change the orientations of exactly 2 cubies (the quarks and anti-quarks we mentioned), leaving the rest of the cube completely unchanged. Even though we move an ensemble of eight different cubies at a time, we are able to precisely cancel the motion of all of the other cubies we moved, and hone in with surgical precision on the two we are interested in. Using sledgehammer moves, we are able to create a scalpel!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: From Sledgehammer to Scalpel', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T02:11:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pradeep Mutalik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pradeep', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mutalik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66b401ae-d6bb-54a1-b29e-43205945feaa', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66b401ae-d6bb-54a1-b29e-43205945feaa'}, {'abstract': 'The Veterans Affairs Department has to do a lot more to meet urgent mental health needs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/opinion/while-veterans-wait.html', 'snippet': 'The Veterans Affairs Department has to do a lot more to meet urgent mental health needs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Veterans Affairs Department has devoted much effort and money to improve and expand its mental health care, especially for those coming home from Iraq and Afghanistan with post-traumatic stress disorder and brain injuries. But continuing reports of drug dependency, suicides and suicide attempts among veterans and active-duty soldiers suggest that urgent needs remain vast and unmet. So do persistent accounts from veterans who say they spend months waiting for mental health care. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'While Veterans Wait', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'While Veterans Wait', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T02:13:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3086a652-3b32-5c0b-a03e-2899f51b2dea', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3086a652-3b32-5c0b-a03e-2899f51b2dea'}, {'abstract': 'The youth, not identified by authorities, was identified in two lineups by women whose attempted rapes were said by police to be part of a pattern that began in September.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/nyregion/15-year-old-arrested-on-rape-charges-related-to-queens-attacks.html', 'snippet': 'The youth, not identified by authorities, was identified in two lineups by women whose attempted rapes were said by police to be part of a pattern that began in September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 15-year-old Queens youth has been arrested on charges that he tried to rape two women this month, part of what the authorities say is a pattern of five attacks in the borough’s southeastern section that began in late September.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '15-Year-Old Held in Rape Attempts in Queens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '15-Year-Old Held in Rape Attempts in Queens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T02:14:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/817ee51a-595b-5c2d-a07c-774f3d33ad6d', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/817ee51a-595b-5c2d-a07c-774f3d33ad6d'}, {'abstract': 'Facing increasing poverty rates, suburban communities must re-evaluate their identities and how they serve their populations.', 'w