tps://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/us/suburban-poverty-surge-challenges-communities.html', 'snippet': 'The poor population in America’s suburbs rose 53 percent last decade, double the 26 percent increase in cities, confronting communities with unaccustomed challenges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARMA HEIGHTS, Ohio — The poor population in America’s suburbs — long a symbol of a stable and prosperous American middle class — rose by more than half after 2000, forcing suburban communities across the country to re-evaluate their identities and how they serve their populations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/us/SUBURBS3/SUBURBS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/25/us/SUBURBS3/SUBURBS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/us/SUBURBS3/SUBURBS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/us/SUBURBS3/SUBURBS3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/us/SUBURBS3/SUBURBS3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Outside Cleveland, Snapshots of Poverty’s Surge in the Suburbs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Outside Cleveland, Snapshots of Poverty’s Surge in the Suburbs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suburbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cleveland (Ohio)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T02:17:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1c9b252-a7c2-5983-9a6d-e4094359ddf1', 'word_count': 1230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1c9b252-a7c2-5983-9a6d-e4094359ddf1'}, {'abstract': 'A commercial that ran only once in 1964 is still studied today in academic and political circles.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/24/revisiting-the-daisy-ad-revolution/', 'snippet': 'A commercial that ran only once in 1964 is still studied today in academic and political circles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the most negative political ad in American history. The adorable petal-picking, tow-headed tot who now approaches middle age has few regrets about her role in a commercial that revolutionized campaign politics. “It’s only been in the last few years,” says Monique Luiz, that she has “realized the importance of this iconic ad.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Revisiting the Daisy Ad Revolution', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T02:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Will Storey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Will', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Storey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'o