d expectations, but warned of more job cuts in its investment bank as Europe’s sovereign debt crisis caused trading revenue to plunge.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:39 a.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deutsche Bank Earnings Beat Expectations', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T06:36:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1c214cc-6856-5cb4-90cd-1d35bc9bc39a', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1c214cc-6856-5cb4-90cd-1d35bc9bc39a'}, {'abstract': 'A New York-based company aims to make Indian desserts more upscale.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/french-chocolate-meets-indian-mithai/', 'snippet': 'A New York-based company aims to make Indian desserts more upscale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Indian mithai, or sweets, have never been on the top of my must-eat list: the overly sugary taste of ladoos and burfis, often made with ingredients of suspect quality, do little for me.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French Chocolate Meets Indian Mithai', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Desserts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T07:10:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9095e33-c344-509d-b6b8-b197f2445bb4', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9095e33-c344-509d-b6b8-b197f2445bb4'}, {'abstract': 'Swami Bhaktipada, 74, ex-Hare Krishna leader, died in Mumbai.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/ex-hare-krishna-leader-dies-in-mumbai/', 'snippet': 'Swami Bhaktipada, 74, ex-Hare Krishna leader, died in Mumbai.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Swami Bhaktipada, 74, a former leader of the American Hare Krishna movement died on Monday in a hospital near Mumbai. He had built a sprawling golden paradise for his followers in the hills of Appalachia, but later pleaded guilty to federal racketeering charges that included conspiracy to commit the murders-for-hire of two devotees, this obituary in The New York Times says: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Hare Krishna Leader Dies in Mumbai', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T07:32:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35106e70-1c95-5db6-99eb-2e797ff3ed6b', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35106e70-1c95-5db6-99eb-2e797ff3ed6b'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the best synonym for an adjective used in context?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/test-yourself-english-oct-25-2011/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the best synonym for an adjective used in context?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the movie review, “Occupying Boston and Beyond, With Tent Libraries for All.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimed