eat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/broadway-recruits-nick-jonas-to-boost-kids-night-attendance/', 'snippet': 'To help increase ticket sales for its annual Kids’ Night on Broadway, New York theater owners and producers have recruited a former Broadway kid himself, pop idol Nick Jonas, as the 2012 spokesman for the five-day program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To help increase ticket sales for its annual Kids’ Night on Broadway, New York theater owners and producers have recruited a former Broadway kid himself, pop idol Nick Jonas, as the 2012 spokesman for the five-day program in February. The 19-year-old Mr. Jonas appeared on Broadway as a boy in “Les Misérables,” “Beauty and the Beast” and “Annie Get Your Gun” before achieving pinup status as a member of the Jonas Brothers band, and on Jan. 24 he will take over the lead role of J. Pierrepont Finch in the Broadway revival of “How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Broadway Recruits Nick Jonas to Boost Kids’ Night Attendance', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T20:11:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34c29239-6193-58d4-b2cc-eafd32603825', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34c29239-6193-58d4-b2cc-eafd32603825'}, {'abstract': 'The chief wine critic of The Times will review the weekly restaurant reviews until the paper names a permanent critic.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/eric-asimov-is-the-interim-restaurant-critic/', 'snippet': 'The chief wine critic of The Times will review the weekly restaurant reviews until the paper names a permanent critic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While we wait for the puffs of white smoke that will issue from the chimney atop 620 Eighth Avenue when The Times names its next restaurant critic, the weekly reviews will be written by Eric Asimov. This week he takes on Salinas, in Chelsea, which is worth two stars in his book.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eric Asimov Is the Interim Restaurant Critic', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T20:15:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81c47840-fe19-5ccf-b941-c62ba9b34c68', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81c47840-fe19-5ccf-b941-c62ba9b34c68'}, {'abstract': 'The restaurant Salinas in Chelsea digs deeply into the traditions of Spanish cooking rather than probing its outward boundaries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/dining/reviews/salinas-nyc-restaurant-review.html', 'snippet': 'The restaurant Salinas in Chelsea digs deeply into the traditions of Spanish cooking rather than probing its outward boundaries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVER since the center of culinary innovation shifted to Spain with the ascent of El Bulli and other like-minded restaurants, New York has been awaiting its own specimen of contemporary Spanish gastronomy. For some reason, it hasn’t happened, at least, not entirely successfully.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26SUBREST_SPAN/26SUBREST_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26SUBREST_SPAN/26SUBREST_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26SUBREST_SPAN/26SUBREST_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26SUBREST_SPAN/26SUBREST_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/dining/26SUBREST_SPAN/26SUBREST_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spain Without the Hocus-Pocus', 'kicker': 'Restaurant Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spain Without the Hocus-Pocus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T20:17:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Dining & Wine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fe42578-a7eb-552c-be87-7f26912f37fc', 'word_count': 1213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fe42578-a7eb-552c-be87-7f26912f37fc'}, {'abstract': 'Salinas, a new Spanish restaurant in Chelsea, is reviewed by Eric Asimov this week.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/reviewing-salinas/', 'snippet': 'Salinas, a new Spanish restaurant in Chelsea, is reviewed by Eric Asimov this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yes, I’ve got myself some temp work here as the process of selecting the next restaurant critic unfolds. This week, I’m reviewing Salinas, one of a series of good Spanish restaurants to have opened in recent years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing Salinas', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T20:18:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97191274-a0e7-5fad-959b-4c25c39106a2', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97191274-a0e7-5fad-959b-4c25c39106a2'}, {'abstract': 'In Thailand, a number of loose crocodiles are swimming through rising flood waters around the outskirts of Bangkok.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/flood-waters-free-crocodiles-in-thailand/', 'snippet': 'In Thailand, a number of loose crocodiles are swimming through rising flood waters around the outskirts of Bangkok.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First it was Bengal tigers in Ohio. Now it’s crocodiles in Bangkok that have broken loose and are menacing the local population.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flood Waters Free Crocodiles in Thailand', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crocodiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangkok (Thailand)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T20:18:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a8b9166-2759-5c4b-a378-f7d722553bd5', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a8b9166-2759-5c4b-a378-f7d722553bd5'}, {'abstract': 'The selection of Ms. Rometty, a senior vice president at I.B.M., will make her one of the highest-profile women executives in corporate America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/technology/ibm-names-a-new-chief.html', 'snippet': 'The selection of Ms. Rometty, a senior vice president at I.B.M., will make her one of the highest-profile women executives in corporate America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Virginia M. Rometty, a senior vice president at I.B.M., will be the company’s next chief executive, the directors announced on Tuesday. She will succeed Samuel J. Palmisano, 60, who will remain as chairman, at the start of next year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/business/26blue-pic/26blue-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/26/business/26blue-pic/26blue-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/business/26blue-pic/26blue-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop