ew under the sun, but does this excuse fashion designers’ endless plunder of the past and what the late raconteur Quentin Crisp once dismissed, with an audible curl of the lip, as “decade-ism”? This season, the 1970s are back, as they have been repeatedly since the ’90s; in the ’70s people were wild for the ’30s, so if you participate in what some are calling a ’90s revival, you are in fact piling on more than 50 years of influences and references. It seems rather ... bloated, doesn’t it?', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27JPCRITIC/27JPCRITIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27JPCRITIC/27JPCRITIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27JPCRITIC/27JPCRITIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Uniqlo Alights on Fifth Avenue', 'kicker': 'Critical Shopper ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uniqlo Alights on Fifth Avenue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uniqlo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T20:27:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/70ab528b-823b-51fc-b4b4-d6a0f9ab0ce1', 'word_count': 948, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70ab528b-823b-51fc-b4b4-d6a0f9ab0ce1'}, {'abstract': 'The ratings results for the World Series games this year have been buffeted by competition, with the latest evidence being Game 5 Monday night.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/even-against-series-viewers-flock-to-the-n-f-l/', 'snippet': 'The ratings results for the World Series games this year have been buffeted by competition, with the latest evidence being Game 5 Monday night.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:15 p.m. | Updated If Major League Baseball truly wants to make an argument about still being America’s pastime after this year’s World Series, it will need some real voodoo mathematics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even Against Series, Viewers Flock to the N.F.L.', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Saints', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T20:34:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bff5c1c6-af5c-54a0-83b0-ec51463cb47b', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bff5c1c6-af5c-54a0-83b0-ec51463cb47b'}, {'abstract': 'Kenny Wheeler was honored at the Festival of New Trumpet Music, and he showed why.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/arts/music/kenny-wheeler-at-festival-of-new-trumpet-music-review.html', 'snippet': 'Kenny Wheeler was honored at the Festival of New Trumpet Music, and he showed why.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The music of Kenny Wheeler doesn’t really clamor for attention. Mr. Wheeler, a quietly influential jazz trumpeter originally from Canada but living in Britain for nearly 60 years, favors graceful melody and intuitive harmony, avoiding the trappings of needless flourish and easy friction. His songs — for that’s usually what they are, solid and hummable — tend to be meticulous in their construction but free of visible effort, in the manner of fine haberdashery or good industrial design. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/wheeler/wheeler-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/wheeler/wheeler-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/wheeler/wheeler-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Influence And Songs That Grow On You', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_k