lip men moan about how much money they’re going to...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone who has roamed through television’s renovating/make-overing/house-flipping genre probably has been struck with the notion that the most appropriate tool for attacking some of the featured projects is a bulldozer. That is certainly a likely response to the opening episode of “Flip Men,” Tuesday night on Spike. When you have to rip as much out of a house as ends up being ripped out here, maybe you should have just torn the danged thing down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Channel Surfing: ‘Flip Men’ vs. Ratholes', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T21:25:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a71716c-e778-546b-8fbf-bee3dd8e570e', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a71716c-e778-546b-8fbf-bee3dd8e570e'}, {'abstract': 'As Republican volunteers make phone calls urging voters to support two ballot initiatives, Mitt Romney refuses to endorse their stance.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/for-mitt-romney-an-awkward-visit-at-a-republican-phone-bank/', 'snippet': 'As Republican volunteers make phone calls urging voters to support two ballot initiatives, Mitt Romney refuses to endorse their stance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Issues 2 and 3, Mitt Romney had zero to say.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Romney, an Awkward Visit', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': 