'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b43cd1e8-480c-532d-bfaf-212ae74ecf18'}, {'abstract': 'The a capella group Anonymous 4 takes on chants from a powerful group of medieval nuns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/arts/music/anonymous-4-at-corpus-christi-church-review.html', 'snippet': 'The a capella group Anonymous 4 takes on chants from a powerful group of medieval nuns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The boundless array of restrictions imposed on women over the centuries has included a ban on their singing polyphonic music in the Middle Ages. But it is thought that the nuns in Las Huelgas, a Cistercian convent for noblewomen in north-central Spain, enthusiastically flouted the rule. Indeed, the medieval abbesses at Las Huelgas could even say Mass and hear confessions, privileges revoked by the 19th century. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/26anon/26anon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/26anon/26anon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/26anon/26anon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recreating The Chants Of Feisty 1200s Nuns', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recreating The Chants Of Feisty 1200s Nuns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANONYMOUS 4', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harmonia Mundi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T22:01:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf42be58-4346-5798-9610-778166e2df4f', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf42be58-4346-5798-9610-778166e2df4f'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Perry/The New York Times At Montclair State University, a group brought traditional Hawaiian hula from Maui, in dance and narration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/arts/dance/hula-by-na-kinimakalehua-at-montclair-state-review.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Perry/The New York Times At Montclair State University, a group brought traditional Hawaiian hula from Maui, in dance and narration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTCLAIR, N.J. — Montclair State University’s Peak Performances series has a reputation for presenting avant-garde dance, frequently imported from abroad and for some reason unavailable in New York. What took the stage of the Alexander Kasser Theater on Thursday, however, was more like a holiday pageant suitable for a high school auditorium. Diorama groupings, a mismatch between mythic subject matter and amateur performances, even a skittish narrator giving a halting reading of stilted text — it was all there. Plus the hula.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/26hawaiian/26hawaiian-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawaii’s Traditions, Retold in Words and Movement', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hawaii’s Traditions, Retold in Word