': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T22:02:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81452c97-516d-5820-a99e-4dfdf7b51df8', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81452c97-516d-5820-a99e-4dfdf7b51df8'}, {'abstract': 'In “Whitechapel,” a new crime series on BBC America, gruesome murders mimic the Jack the Ripper killings of the 1880s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/arts/television/whitechapel-on-bbc-america-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Whitechapel,” a new crime series on BBC America, gruesome murders mimic the Jack the Ripper killings of the 1880s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An awful lot of copycatting is going on in “Whitechapel,” a six-part crime series starting on BBC America on Wednesday night, and only some of it is by the killer being pursued. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/26whitechapel/26whitechapel-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/26whitechapel/26whitechapel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/26whitechapel/26whitechapel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling the Long Reach of Jack the Ripper in a Series of Gruesome Killings', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Feeling the Long Reach of Jack the Ripper in a Series of Gruesome Killings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BBC America', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T22:06:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/38ccdf2d-be5a-54c2-9c02-4a55927b2fef', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38ccdf2d-be5a-54c2-9c02-4a55927b2fef'}, {'abstract': 'Wall Street banks are pushing spinoffs to compensate for declining takeover volume, but they may find themselves facing the same pressure to split up from their own investors.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/bankers-may-be-target-of-their-own-tactic-advocating-a-breakup/', 'snippet': 'Wall Street banks are pushing spinoffs to compensate for declining takeover volume, but they may find themselves facing the same pressure to split up from their own investors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps it is not Occupy Wall Street that the banks should fear, but their latest frothy financial product. Investment bankers are crisscrossing the nation peddling spinoffs. But given the weak stock prices of these banks, they may find themselves under the same pressure to split up from their own investors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banks May Be Target of Their Own Tactic: Advocating a Breakup', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T22:09:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3149c42-2d7b-5dbf-8972-4efb454b66ac', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3149c42-2d7b-5dbf-8972-4efb454b66ac'}, {'abstract': 'Jimmy Sturr brought his band and his four-plus decades of experience as a leading polka star to Brooklyn Bowl.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/arts/music/jimmy-sturr-and-his-orchestra-at-brooklyn-bowl-review.html', 'snippet': 'Jimmy Sturr brought his band and his four-plus decades of experience as a leading polka star to Brooklyn Bowl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jimmy Sturr has been at this awhile. The way he snatches the microphone from its stand and yanks it up to his mouth, the ever so slight crouch in his stance when he’s trying to communicate a point, the gleam that appears to emanate from him onstage: all products of four-plus decades of work at keeping polka alive. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/26sturr1/26sturr1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/26sturr1/26sturr1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/26sturr1/26sturr1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giving ‘Sweet Home Alabama’ a Polish Accent', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giving ‘Sweet Home Alabama’ a Polish Accent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Bowl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sturr, Jimmy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T22:11:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/75c6120b-75b6-5216-8a5a-ab88c30e5ff7', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75c6120b-75b6-5216-8a5a-ab88c30e5ff7'}, {'abstract': 'The violinist Jennifer Koh played Bach’s Unaccompanied Sonatas and Partitas in a single marathon concert presented by the Miller Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/arts/music/jennifer-koh-at-the-american-academy-of-arts-and-letters-review.html', 'snippet': 'The violinist Jennifer Koh played Bach’s Unaccompanied Sonatas and Partitas in a single marathon concert presented by the Miller Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By refusing to specialize in a particular corner of the violin repertory, and leaping freely among several, Jennifer Koh has built a following that draws on, and ideally brings together, several of the music world’s style-conscious enclaves. Some listeners know her for the hard-edged contemporary scores she has recorded and to which she has devoted full recitals. Others associate her with the six free lunchtime recitals of Bach’s Unaccompanied Sonatas and Partitas (BWV 1001-6) she gave at Columbia University two seasons ago. She is also touring with a Bach and Beyond series in which she juxtaposes the solo Bach works with 20th- and 21st-century pieces, some written for the occasion. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/26jennifer/26jennifer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/26jennifer/26jennifer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/arts/26jennifer/26jennifer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scaling Bach’s Mountains With Stamina and Skill', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scaling Bach’s Mountains With Stamina and Skill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN ACADEMY OF ARTS AND LETTERS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koh, Jennifer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miller Theater at Columbia University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-25T22:12:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'repo