 Criminal Court.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A committee on Tuesday announced its list of four final candidates to become the chief prosecutor for the International Criminal Court: Fatou Bensouda of Gambia, Andrew Cayley of Britain, Mohamed Chande Othman of Tanzania and Robert Petit of Canada. The prosecutor is expected to be chosen in December to replace Luis Moreno-Ocampo of Argentina. Mrs. Bensouda is widely considered to be the front-runner. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hague: Four Prosecutor Finalists', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hague: Four Prosecutor Finalists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bensouda, Fatou', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hague (Netherlands)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T00:39:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1478a2a-c431-5f24-9811-6db03282405c', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1478a2a-c431-5f24-9811-6db03282405c'}, {'abstract': 'An expansion of the income-based college-loan repayment program is expected on Wednesday, lowering monthly payments and allowing some loan consolidation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/education/26debt.html', 'snippet': 'An expansion of the income-based college-loan repayment program is expected on Wednesday, lowering monthly payments and allowing some loan consolidation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama will announce new programs Wednesday to lower monthly loan payments for some students graduating next year and thereafter and to let borrowers who have a mix of direct federal loans and loans under the old Federal Family Education Loan Program consolidate them at a slightly lower interest rate. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President to Ease Student Loan Burden for Low-Income Graduates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President to Ease Student Loan Burden for Low-Income Graduates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'College Board', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T00:39:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb30779f-2b54-539f-b022-cfe4beff2c00', 'word_count': 1017, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb30779f-2b54-539f-b022-cfe4beff2c00'}, {'abstract': 'Monday night’s bullpen debacle by the Cardinals has put a new spotlight on baseball’s reliance on landlines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/sports/baseball/world-series-baseballs-game-of-telephone.html', 'snippet': 'Monday night’s bullpen debacle by the Cardinals has put a new spotlight on baseball’s reliance on landlines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — In Atlanta, there are televisions in the dugouts to help the manager monitor the action in his team’s bullpen — who is warming up, and how ready a pitcher might be to enter the game.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/sports/PHONE2/PHONE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/sports/PHONE2/PHONE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/sports/PHONE2/PHONE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Baseball’s Game of Telephone', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Missed Bullpen Calls Lead to an Interesting Game of Telephone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'la Russa, Tony', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T00:40:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a945808-2681-54c8-949d-31be7f285b19', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a945808-2681-54c8-949d-31be7f285b19'}, {'abstract': 'Uganda’s Parliament has voted to reopen a debate on a bill that seeks to outlaw homosexuality and that could be expanded to include the death penalty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/world/africa/anti-gay-bill-is-revived-in-uganda.html', 'snippet': 'Uganda’s Parliament has voted to reopen a debate on a bill that seeks to outlaw homosexuality and that could be expanded to include the death penalty.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Parliament has voted to reopen a debate on a bill that seeks to outlaw homosexuality and that could be expanded to include the death penalty for gay men and lesbians. The legislation, first proposed in 2009, will be sent to a committee for consideration, Speaker Rebecca Kadaga told lawmakers. The Legal and Parliamentary Affairs Committee in the previous Parliament suggested that the penalty for “aggravated homosexuality” should be the same as for “defilement,” a crime that is punishable by death. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uganda: Anti-Gay Bill Is Revived', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uganda: Anti-Gay Bill Is Revived', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T00:46:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/00a0bd68-f9c1-56e8-b571-70c05cf03a20', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00a0bd68-f9c1-56e8-b571-70c05cf03a20'}, {'abstract': 'An unidentified gunman wounded the chief justice of the high court in the Pakistani-controlled part of the disputed Kashmir region on Tuesday, the police said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/world/asia/judge-wounded-by-gunman-in-pakistan-controlled-kashmir.html', 'snippet': 'An unidentified gunman wounded the chief justice of the high court in the Pakistani-controlled part of the disputed Kashmir region on Tuesday, the police said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An unidentified gunman wounded the chief justice of the high court in the Pakistani-controlled part of the disputed Kashmir region on Tuesday, the police said. The justice, Ghulam Mustafa Mughal, was shot in the abdomen and taken to a military hospital, where his condition was said to be stable. The gunman was not caught, and the motive for the attack was unclear. Kashmir is claimed by both India and Pakistan, and the attack occurred after death threats were made to another Pakistani judge, who had sentenced the killer of the Punjab Province governor. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan: Judge Wounded by Gunman', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Judge Wounded by Gunman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T00:49:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa590a65-c604-5612-b22a-5a46f6991157', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa590a65-c604-5612-b22a-5a46f6991157'}, {'abstract': 'Consumer debt and government spending are what really drive economic growth, not private investment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/opinion/its-consumer-spending-stupid.html', 'snippet': 'Consumer debt and government spending are what really drive economic growth, not private investment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS an economic historian who has been studying American capitalism for 35 years, I’m going to let you in on the best-kept secret of the last century: private investment — that is, using business profits to increase productivity and output — doesn’t actually drive economic growth. Consumer debt and government spending do. Private investment isn’t even necessary to promote growth. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/opinion/26OPED/26OPED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 285, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/26/opinion/26OPED/26OPED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 285}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/opinion/26OPED/26OPED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 486, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/opinion/26OPED/26OPED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/opinion/26OPED/26OPED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Consumer Spending, Stupid', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It&#8217;s Consumer Spending, Stupid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T00:49:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Livingston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Livingston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca2b274b-6904-5fce-9205-45384df4075c', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca2b274b-6904-5fce-9205-45384df4075c'}, {'abstract': 'The network is planning to show English-language subtitles in an effort to attract viewers among the skyrocketing number of second- and third-generation Hispanic-Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/business/media/telemundo-seeks-spanglish-speakers-in-aim-for-new-viewers.html', 'snippet': 'The network is planning to show English-language subtitles in an effort to attract viewers among the skyrocketing number of second- and third-generation Hispanic-Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Telemundo has long trailed its rival Univision in their competition for Hispanic television viewers in the United States. But as the number of second- and third-generation Hispanic-Americans skyrockets, the perennial runner-up is embracing a new strategy — English-language subtitles and Spanglish — to attract deep-pocketed viewers and the advertisers who covet them.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/business/TELEMUNDO/TELEMUNDO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 859, 'width': 751, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/business/TELEMUNDO/TELEMUNDO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/business/TELEMUNDO/TELEMUNDO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Telemundo Blends English Into a Mostly Spanish Lineup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Telemundo Blends English Into a Mostly Spanish Lineup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Univision', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saralegui, Cristina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spanish Language', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TELEMUNDO', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T00:51:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick'