', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T01:03:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/11530e4d-3423-5223-914c-81f9c89266ce', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11530e4d-3423-5223-914c-81f9c89266ce'}, {'abstract': 'The first lady speaks at a Walgreens on the South Side about her goal of reducing childhood obesity.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/in-chicago-michelle-obama-takes-on-food-deserts/', 'snippet': 'The first lady speaks at a Walgreens on the South Side about her goal of reducing childhood obesity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — Michelle Obama took an afternoon away from fund-raising for her husband’s re-election campaign on Tuesday to draw attention to another — and far less divisive — goal: reducing childhood obesity. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Chicago, Michelle Obama Takes On ‘Food Deserts’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walgreen Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T01:04:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaa1b0c8-2e9c-5092-b390-6cd7ec710d7e', 'word_count': 562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaa1b0c8-2e9c-5092-b390-6cd7ec710d7e'}, {'abstract': 'Coaches can have a profound effect, for better or worse, on the lives of young people.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/the-end-of-the-cold-war-coach/', 'snippet': 'Coaches can have a profound effect, for better or worse, on the lives of young people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Youth sports in the United States is a contradiction. In surveys, parents overwhelmingly say that youth sports should emphasize values like teamwork, honesty, discipline and fair play. But when adults are asked what values they think youth sports actually reinforce most, they say competitiveness and the importance of winning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moving Beyond the Cold War Coach', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T01:05:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05e3a380-b990-5e8d-ae72-cedf67643ccc', 'word_count': 2171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05e3a380-b990-5e8d-ae72-cedf67643ccc'}, {'abstract': 'Wireless companies should provide customers with transparent pricing and more choices. And the F.C.C. must establish regulations with bite.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/opinion/how-to-fix-the-wireless-market.html', 'snippet': 'Wireless companies should provide customers with transparent pricing and more choices. And the F.C.C. must establish regulations with bite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s good that wireless companies have agreed to warn customers when they are about to exceed monthly limits on voice, text or data usage or incur international roaming fees, which can result in thousands of dollars of extra charges. But consumers need more protection.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Fix the Wireless Market', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Fix the Wireless Market', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T01:07:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/df6480e7-3657-5215-9134-3dc6f5b4cfca', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df6480e7-3657-5215-9134-3dc6f5b4cfca'}, {'abstract': 'States and cities need more federal help to protect vulnerable citizens and curb homelessness. Congress should fully finance important housing programs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/opinion/a-foolish-time-to-cut-housing-aid.html', 'snippet': 'States and cities need more federal help to protect vulnerable citizens and curb homelessness. Congress should fully finance important housing programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With record numbers of families teetering on the verge of homelessness, Congress should be shoring up the precious few federal programs that provide affordable housing for the poor, the elderly and the disabled. Instead, both the House and Senate are considering cuts to the Department of Housing and Urban Development budget, which would hurt cash-strapped states and communities in sheltering the most vulnerable citizens.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Foolish Time to Cut Housing Aid', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Foolish Time to Cut Housing Aid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing and Urban Development Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public and Subsidized Housing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T01:12:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d792a48f-416f-5c18-94dc-2d29d8e1871e', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d792a48f-416f-5c18-94dc-2d29d8e1871e'}, {'abstract': 'On the eve of a European Union summit meeting, crucial financial measures were still unresolved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/world/europe/europe-faces-new-hurdles-in-debt-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'On the eve of a European Union summit meeting, crucial financial measures were still unresolved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — New fissures and disagreements emerged on Tuesday on the eve of a European Union summit meeting promoted as the moment for agreement on a comprehensive solution to the two-year-old euro crisis. Crucial financial measures were left unresolved, and Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi of Italy faced strong opposition inside his governing coalition to major changes demanded by the Europeans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/world/JP-EUROPE/JP-EUROPE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/world/JP-EUROPE/JP-EUROPE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/world/JP-EUROPE/JP-EUROPE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Faces New Hurdles in Crisis Over Debt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Hurdles For Europe In Crisis Over Debt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusc