es two basic questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Could there be a better pretext for a disaster movie? Scientists from McMaster University in Ontario and the University of Tübingen in Germany have reconstructed the genetic code of the microbe that caused the Black Death. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Has the Black Death Paled?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Has the Black Death Paled?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plague', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature (Journal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McMaster University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T01:21:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce1ddcf8-278c-59fa-a711-84c257a4b721', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce1ddcf8-278c-59fa-a711-84c257a4b721'}, {'abstract': 'Carlos Tévez was fined a month’s pay by Manchester City for refusing to enter a game in September, but rather than accept it he is vowing to sue for defamation of character.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/tevez-situation-takes-another-odd-turn/', 'snippet': 'Carlos Tévez was fined a month’s pay by Manchester City for refusing to enter a game in September, but rather than accept it he is vowing to sue for defamation of character.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news that Manchester City has fined its sulking striker Carlos Tévez a month’s pay and sentenced him, essentially, to time served as a punishment would seem to put to rest the controversy that has been a rare stain on the club’s solid start to the Premier League season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tévez Situation Takes Another Odd Turn', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester City (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T01:22:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d6ca2be-e32b-5e13-87e0-0c3383f59dbe', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d6ca2be-e32b-5e13-87e0-0c3383f59dbe'}, {'abstract': 'On Thanksgiving, Dr. Julia Chase-Brand, 69, plans to run a race in Manchester, Conn., where 50 years ago she and two other women ran in an act of civil disobedience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/sports/julia-chase-brand-a-leading-pioneer-in-womens-running.html', 'snippet': 'On Thanksgiving, Dr. Julia Chase-Brand, 69, plans to run a race in Manchester, Conn., where 50 years ago she and two other women ran in an act of civil disobedience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW LONDON, Conn. — Except for a strategic bit of elastic that may be required, the blue running tunic, circa Smith College 1961, still fits. It will be worn again a half-century later, this time in celebration and tribute rather than defiance.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/sports/YJPRUNNER1/YJPRUNNER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/26/sports/YJPRUNNER1/YJPRUNNER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/sports/YJPRUNNER1/YJPRUNNER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/sports/YJPRUNNER1/YJPRUNNER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/sports/YJPRUNNER1/YJPRUNNER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Leading Pioneer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Leading Pioneer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chase-Brand, Julia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T01:23:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34396dd2-4a24-50cd-b9e4-ba59f1f036dd', 'word_count': 2074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34396dd2-4a24-50cd-b9e4-ba59f1f036dd'}, {'abstract': 'Tony La Russa’s reputation for managerial genius took a hit on Monday. On Tuesday, the Cardinals’ manager elaborated on what went wrong in Game 5.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/sports/baseball/a-day-after-disaster-la-russa-explains-himself.html', 'snippet': 'Tony La Russa’s reputation for managerial genius took a hit on Monday. On Tuesday, the Cardinals’ manager elaborated on what went wrong in Game 5.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — He has won two World Series, been a subject of books about his managerial prowess and is considered by some as one of the best managers in baseball history. But on his way to what will undoubtedly be a Hall of Fame induction, Tony La Russa, a manager for 33 years, stumbled Monday night.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/sports/baseball/26cardinals-pic/26cardinals-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/26/sports/baseball/26cardinals-pic/26cardinals-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/sports/baseball/26cardinals-pic/26cardinals-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/26/sports/baseball/26cardinals-pic/26cardinals-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/26/sports/baseball/26cardinals-pic/26cardinals-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Day After Disaster, Manager Explains Himself', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Day After Disaster, Manager Explains Himself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'la Russa, Tony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Motte, Jason', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T01:25:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f73906d2-1097-59f8-9d37-f11793dbf281', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f73906d2-1097-59f8-9d37-f11793dbf281'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Rick Perry of Texas capped an eventful day on the campaign trail Tuesday with an interview on “The O’Reilly Factor” in which he criticized his chief rival, Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/25/perry-makes-digs-at-romney-on-fox-news/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Rick Perry of Texas capped an eventful day on the campaign trail Tuesday with an interview on “The O’Reilly Factor” in which he criticized his chief rival, Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Rick Perry of Texas capped an eventful day on the campaign trail Tuesday with an interview on “The O’Reilly Factor” on the Fox News Channel. He expressed regret for participating in campaign debates, which have largely resulted in poor reviews for him. And yet again, he came in tongue a-blazin’, this time with some cho