 portion of the wealthiest Americans based in New York, the divisions are clear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/nyregion/as-data-show-theres-a-reason-the-wall-street-protesters-chose-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'With a significant portion of the wealthiest Americans based in New York, the divisions are clear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the federal income tax was first imposed in 1913, the richest 0.1 percent of households reaped 8.6 percent of the nation’s income. In 2007, as the recession began, the share going to that sliver of megarich Americans was 12.3 percent. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As the Data Show, There’s a Reason the Wall Street Protesters Chose New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As the Data Show, There’s a Reason the Protesters Chose New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rockefeller, John D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T02:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48d5ccd2-6824-558e-939c-c752fbcc3139', 'word_count': 1015, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48d5ccd2-6824-558e-939c-c752fbcc3139'}, {'abstract': 'A constitutional amendmen