e', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44b43dd6-4a30-5c5b-9a15-97691f46235c', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44b43dd6-4a30-5c5b-9a15-97691f46235c'}, {'abstract': 'Police used tear gas on protesters at the Occupy Oakland movement on Tuesday, after clearing protesters from an area near city hall earlier in the day.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/police-said-to-fire-tear-gas-at-protesters-in-oakland-calif/', 'snippet': 'Police used tear gas on protesters at the Occupy Oakland movement on Tuesday, after clearing protesters from an area near city hall earlier in the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated 9:48 a.m. Riot police in Oakland dispersed hundreds of protesters with tear gas on Tuesday night as crowds tried to re-enter a plaza outside of City Hall that the authorities had cleared of an encampment earlier in the day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Fire Tear Gas at Occupy Protesters in Oakland', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tear Gas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oakland (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T04:22:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan, J. David Goodman and Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organ