count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31781b8a-b5f8-50df-a4f7-6d4468cd95b5'}, {'abstract': 'Explosions boomed across the capital, Sana, as mostly peaceful antigovernment protests continued.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/25/world/africa/20111026-337-YEMEN.html', 'snippet': 'Explosions boomed across the capital, Sana, as mostly peaceful antigovernment protests continued.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Explosions boomed across the capital, Sana, as mostly peaceful antigovernment protests continued.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/world/africa/20111026-YEMEN-slide-8HD1/20111026-YEMEN-slide-8HD1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/25/world/africa/20111026-YEMEN-slide-8HD1/20111026-YEMEN-slide-8HD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/25/world/africa/20111026-YEMEN-slide-8HD1/20111026-YEMEN-slide-8HD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting in Yemen Intensifies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T05:10:48+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/3fabc288-1c72-5004-b4fc-f5d3a2d23a58', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/3fabc288-1c72-5004-b4fc-f5d3a2d23a58'}, {'abstract': 'Top stories on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/newswallah-in-the-english-language-press-wednesday-6/', 'snippet': 'Top stories on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The head of the agency that manages travel for Kiran Bedi severed ties with her nongovernmental organization,\xa0 India Vision Foundation, on Tuesday. Anil Bal, proprietor of Flywell Travel, claimed that the controversy over the inflated travel invoices furnished by Ms. Bedi had unnecessarily tarnished his reputation. Mr. Bal, a founding member of the foundation, also resigned as trustee of the organization (The Indian Express).Prime Minister Manmohan Singh was skeptical of the July 2005\xa0 nuclear agreement with the United States in the run-up to the joint statement declaring the pact, a new book by former U.S. Secretary of State Condelezzaa Rice claims. Mr. Singh was wary about the impact of the deal on domestic politics, Ms. Rice writes in her upcoming memoir “In No Higher Honor.” The then-foreign minister, Natwar Singh, was far more adamant about the deal — called\xa0 the U.S.-India Civil Nuclear Cooperation — and worked with U.S. officials to persuade the prime minister it was a good idea (Hindustan Times).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: In the English-Language Press Wednesday', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T05:12:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamposh Raina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamposh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08167d23-9ada-577c-9f26-24b1f03a91e3', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08167d23-9ada-577c-9f26-24b1f03a91e3'}, {'abstract': 'In a live episode of “The X Factor,” the addition of choreography results in what look like bad Broadway numbers.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/x-factor-watch-squabbling-and-dancing-and-some-singing-all-of-it-live/', 'snippet': 'In a live episode of “The X Factor,” the addition of choreography results in what look like bad Broadway numbers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some welcome testiness finally worked its way into “The X Factor” on Tuesday night, but so did lots of unwelcome choreography, headache-inducing lighting and overorchestration. Some of the singers in this live show were more or less swallowed up by their absurdly excessive production numbers as “The X Factor” abandoned its roots as a singing competition and turned into something resembling a bad Broadway musical. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘X Factor’ Watch: Squabbling and Dancing (and Some Singing), All of It Live', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T05:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13f80190-4b21-5024-934b-5be8e4f790b7', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13f80190-4b21-5024-934b-5be8e4f790b7'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on October 26, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https