4b95e19aa'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/news-quiz-oct-26-2011/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | Oct. 26, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T08:15:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Frasier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frasier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5065c9b-025b-5101-97dc-815820581a1a', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5065c9b-025b-5101-97dc-815820581a1a'}, {'abstract': 'Are Diwali celebrations incomplete without firecrackers.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/a-firecracker-free-diwali/', 'snippet': 'Are Diwali celebrations incomplete without firecrackers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For most people, Diwali festivities are incomplete without the crackling of firecrackers. And almost everyone has a favorite, ranging from the innocuous “phooljhadi,” or sparkler, to the rocket, which usually fails to live up to its name, hissing into the sky with fierce intensity only to fall flat on the ground within minutes. And then there is the pernicious-sounding “bomb,” whose name says it all. They come in different shapes and sizes but the firecrackers have one thing in common: they unleash an ear-splitting bang when they are set ablaze.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Firecracker-Free Diwali?', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diwali (Hindu Festival)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fireworks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T08:44:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamposh Raina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamposh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af7c4bbb-a29a-5755-b70f-db220661e8f6', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af7c4bbb-a29a-5755-b70f-db220661e8f6'}, {'abstract': 'In photographing the Swiss banking industry, Mark Henley faced the challenge of documenting something no one can see. Yet the pictures — like something out of a noir film — have familiar qualities.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/casing-swiss-banking-secrets/', 'snippet': 'In photographing the Swiss banking industry, Mark Henley faced the challenge of documenting something no one can see. Yet the pictures — like something out of a noir film — have familiar qualities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With billions of dollars shrouded in secrecy — and protected by armed guards and vaults — the best Mark Henley could hope for in Switzerland was to subtly stake out his targets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Casing Swiss Banking Secrets', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T09:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Hamblett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ham