'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/the-amnesiac-economy/', 'snippet': 'Forgetting can hurt you, badly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Thoma sends us to John Cassidy on the absence of really new ideas in this crisis — largely because we didn’t need new ideas, all we needed for the most part was to remember things that we somehow forgot. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Amnesiac Economy', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T10:26:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bea6f66d-85e2-5442-aac8-4dd97db2674a', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bea6f66d-85e2-5442-aac8-4dd97db2674a'}, {'abstract': 'Fangs for the memories.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/onion/', 'snippet': 'Fangs for the memories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, for those wondering:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Onion', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T10:38:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2bd3ca9-d0a8-5cf7-a697-1c5fdb067a3c', 'word_count': 45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2bd3ca9-d0a8-5cf7-a697-1c5fdb067a3c'}, {'abstract': 'Citizens in Massachusetts are gathering signatures in hopes of placing a “death with dignity” law on the ballot.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/the-next-death-with-dignity-battleground/', 'snippet': 'Citizens in Massachusetts are gathering signatures in hopes of placing a “death with dignity” law on the ballot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most fall weekends, you can find Randee Laikind buttonholing people at the Shelburne Falls Market in western Massachusetts, or wielding her clipboard on the town common in nearby Greenfield or Amherst.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Next Death-With-Dignity Battleground', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euthanasia and Assisted Suicide', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospice Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T11:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29fbe2c3-c7ad-5adc-a561-fd09cbf8a9df', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29fbe2c3-c7ad-5adc-a561-fd09cbf8a9df'}, {'abstract': 'Motion-sensitive cameras record the behavior of predators in Arctic oilfields whose numbers have soared because of the free food and the housing afforded by development.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/arctic-predators-caught-in-the-act/', 'snippet': 'Motion-sensitive cameras record the behavior of predators in Arctic oilfields whose numbers have soared because of the free food and the housing afforded by development.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arctic Alaska is often described as our county’s last great frontier, with its bitterly cold winters, Inupiat Eskimos on the hunt and caribou roaming the open tundra. At the same time, there is the reality of change, with oil drilling advancing, polar bears imperiled and the region’s snow pack threatened by global warming. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arctic Predators, Caught in the Act', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wildlife Conservation Society', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'National Petroleum Reserve (Alaska)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T11:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Liebezeit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liebezeit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab27b52b-515d-532d-901e-07544934fb38', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab27b52b-515d-532d-901e-07544934fb38'}, {'abstract': 'The Pittsburgh-Arizona game was just another showcase of Ben Roethlisberger’s uncanny ability to extend plays.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthd