r Greek debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — European leaders, in a significant step toward resolving the euro zone financial crisis, early Thursday morning obtained an agreement from banks to take a 50 percent loss on the face value of their Greek debt.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/world/27europe2_337/27europe2_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 653, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Agrees to Basics of Plan to Resolve Euro Crisis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe In Accord On Basics Of Plan To Save The Euro', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Financial Stability Facility', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T14:11:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger and Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f24f255-0fe5-515c-82d3-2c70dfa85827', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f24f255-0fe5-515c-82d3-2c70dfa85827'}, {'abstract': 'Streams and rivers in the United States alone release almost 100 million metric tons of carbon dioxide each year — equal to a car burning 40 billion gallons of gasoline, “enough to drive back and forth to the moon 3.4 million times,” a study says.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/a-carbon-culprit-rivers-and-streams/', 'snippet': 'Streams and rivers in the United States alone release almost 100 million metric tons of carbon dioxide each year — equal to a car burning 40 billion gallons of gasoline, “enough to drive back and forth to the moon 3.4 million times,” a study says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The amount of carbon dioxide being released from streams, rivers and lakes is probably being undercounted by scientists modeling the earth’s carbon budget, a new study suggests.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Carbon Culprit: Rivers and Streams', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Geological Survey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T14:28:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifie