s.com/2011/10/26/petula-clark-heading-to-midtown/', 'snippet': 'The British singer will make her first New York appearance in decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Petula Clark, the British singer and actress best known for her hit “Downtown,” will make her first appearance at a New York City nightclub since the 1970s early next year, her publicist said. Ms. Clark, who is 78, lives in Switzerland and has not played New York for decades. She will appear at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency on Park Avenue at 61st Street from Jan. 24 to Feb. 4, performing her hits, including “I Know a Place” and “My Love,” as well as songs from musicals she appeared in, both onstage and screen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Petula Clark Heading to Midtown', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Petula', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Avenue (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T14:44:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9815fa01-831f-5814-8637-0ba85ecf4e74', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9815fa01-831f-5814-8637-0ba85ecf4e74'}, {'abstract': 'At a conference of 1,600 researchers, a participant offers a shorthand of his own: F.H.S.W.T.B.C.K.T.O.A.T.A., or “For heaven’s sake, who the bleep can keep track of all these?”', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/for-climate-scientists-a-dive-into-alphabet-soup/', 'snippet': 'At a conference of 1,600 researchers, a participant offers a shorthand of his own: F.H.S.W.T.B.C.K.T.O.A.T.A., or “For heaven’s sake, who the bleep can keep track of all these?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For journalists, climate science can be a challenge in and of itself. The uncertainties, the dueling algorithms, the long horizons involved in predicting how climate change could unfold — all of this conspires against a reporter trying to report the relevant news in a clear and accessible way. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Climate Scientists, a Dive Into Alphabet Soup', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gleick, Peter H', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T14:58:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hillary Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hillary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d60590a-0a89-5f33-893a-085cda602757', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d60590a-0a89-5f33-893a-085cda602757'}, {'abstract': 'Like this season’s mushrooms, your questions kept coming. Gary Lincoff, an expert mycologist, answers another round of reader questions.', 'w