ncoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99325a35-b502-534e-847f-9929c6518a9e', 'word_count': 1201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99325a35-b502-534e-847f-9929c6518a9e'}, {'abstract': 'Two Federal agencies team up to create a one-page sheet that might simplify families’ understanding of what various colleges might cost them.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/a-one-page-form/', 'snippet': 'Two Federal agencies team up to create a one-page sheet that might simplify families’ understanding of what various colleges might cost them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our colleagues at The Times’s Bucks blog write this morning about the efforts by the new federal Consumer Financial Protection Bureau and the Department of Education to create a one-page financial aid “shopping sheet.” As Ann Carrns writes on Bucks: “The idea here is that a single sheet of basic information would help students and their families better understand the amount of financial aid they qualify for, and compare aid packages offered by different colleges and universities before deciding which school to attend.” Be sure to take a look at a draft of the sheet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A One-Page Form to Compare Student Aid Offers', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T15:06:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bff20679-b4ef-5da1-8fb8-a1dc8744d571', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bff20679-b4ef-5da1-8fb8-a1dc8744d571'}, {'abstract': 'Nutzy, the mascot of the Richmond Flying Squirrels, will be at Busch Stadium on Wednesday night fo