xiness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RISING hemlines get all the attention, but what about necklines? They’re one of the few things on the rise lately, reaching a recent high — on shirts buttoned all the way to the chin — on spring 2012 runways at Jason Wu, Céline and Dior. It makes a kind of sense, then, as the eye moves north of the collarbone, that chokers, those much maligned neckpieces synonymous with the 1990s, would stage a comeback. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27POINTS1/27POINTS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27POINTS1/27POINTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27POINTS1/27POINTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Naughty Necklace', 'kicker': 'Fine Points', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Naughty Necklace', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T15:38:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Joy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Joy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Caption', '_id': 'nyt://article/644f9d47-b432-55de-ac85-0f9d734d0a9c', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/644f9d47-b432-55de-ac85-0f9d734d0a9c'}, {'abstract': 'The Romanian-born Mr. Ciulei was best known in the United States for leading the Guthrie Theater in Minneapolis and for productions at Arena Stage in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/arts/liviu-ciulei-daring-theater-director-dies-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'The Romanian-born Mr. Ciulei was best known in the United States for leading the Guthrie Theater in Minneapolis and for productions at Arena Stage in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Liviu Ciulei, who was voted best director at the Cannes Film Festival in 1965 and who led the Guthrie Theater in Minneapolis in the 1980s, when it won a Tony Award, died on Tuesday in Munich. He was 88.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/sports/27ciulei/27ciulei-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/sports/27ciulei/27ciulei-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/sports/27ciulei/27ciulei-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Liviu Ciulei, a Daring Theater Director, Dies at 88', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Liviu Ciulei, a Daring Theater Director, Dies at 88', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guthrie Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T15:54:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6fe9a5d-510d-5ae3-aacf-0e4d6385ec19', 'word_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6fe9a5d-510d-5ae3-aacf-0e4d6385ec19'}, {'abstract': 'This year is the 400th anniversary of the King James Bible’s publication, and the TV network affiliated with Brigham Young University is broadcasting a three-part documentary series on that Bible’s history.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/channel-surfing-fires-of-faith-on-byutv/', 'snippet': 'This year is the 400th anniversary of the King James Bible’s publication, and the TV network affiliated with Brigham Young University is broadcasting a three-part documentary series on that Bible’s history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may never have heard of BYUtv, but it’s in the midst of broadcasting a smart three-part series on the creation of the most influential book the Western world has ever seen, the King James Bible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Channel Surfing: ‘Fires of Faith’ on BYUtv', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bible', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyndale, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brigham Young University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T16:00:39+0000', 'document_type'