d_paragraph': 'Daniel B. Burke, who helped engineer the acquisition of the American Broadcasting Company by Capital Cities, one of the boldest corporate takeovers of the 1980s, and went on to become chief executive of the merged company, died on Wednesday at his home in Rye, N.Y. He was 82.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/business/BURKE-obit/BURKE-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 956, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/business/BURKE-obit/BURKE-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/business/BURKE-obit/BURKE-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daniel B. Burke, Leading Media Executive, Dies at 82', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Daniel B. Burke, Leading Media Executive, Dies at 82', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burke, James E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T16:12:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d481d00-f84a-58e9-bf2f-484b99a74104', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d481d00-f84a-58e9-bf2f-484b99a74104'}, {'abstract': 'Louisville may be the university that is admitted to the Big 12 instead of West Virginia, with one source saying it is “too close to call.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/sports/ncaafootball/big-12-may-admit-louisville-not-west-virginia.html', 'snippet': 'Louisville may be the university that is admitted to the Big 12 instead of West Virginia, with one source saying it is “too close to call.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'West Virginia University athletic officials spent most of Tuesday preparing to leave the Big East Conference for the Big 12. The Mountaineers’ athletic director, Oliver Luck, was so sure of the move that he tipped off Big East colleagues Monday night and told staff members Tuesday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big 12 Might Admit Louisville, Not West Virginia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big 12 Might Admit Louisville, Not West Virginia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'West Virginia University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Louisville', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big 12 Conference', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T16:16:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifi