'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51344d07-abf3-5c44-aefe-00df74eaf29b', 'word_count': 1934, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51344d07-abf3-5c44-aefe-00df74eaf29b'}, {'abstract': 'A new study showed success in implanting one embryo, rather than two or more.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/i-v-f-without-the-risk-of-multiple-births/', 'snippet': 'A new study showed success in implanting one embryo, rather than two or more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago, a friend, who, like many of our peers, got started late in the baby game and ended up going the\xa0 in vitro fertilization route, told me she was pregnant with twins. They’d used two embryos to maximize the chance of getting pregnant, and both had taken. But they didn’t want twins. The next time I saw her, she had one baby.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.V.F. Without the Risk of Multiple Births?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T16:19:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenny Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fef1dee9-d92c-5995-99fa-6e5f546ff5b1', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fef1dee9-d92c-5995-99fa-6e5f546ff5b1'}, {'abstract': 'In a look at about two dozen cases, when owners appealed Community Board 3’s rejection of their applications, the State Liquor Authority almost always approved them.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/state-officials-have-frequently-overruled-local-boards-rejection-of-liquor-licenses/', 'snippet': 'In a look at about two dozen cases, when owners appealed Community Board 3’s rejection of their applications, the State Liquor Authority almost always approved them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Community Board 3 is often seen as the party pooper of the downtown dining and drinking scene, regularly voting to oppose new liquor licenses for restaurants and bars in the East Village and Lower East Side. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State Officials Have Frequently Overruled Local Board’s Rejection of Liquor Licenses', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T16:26:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/634e0dc3-e0b2-5547-8743-53c38b9571c8', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/634e0dc3-e0b2-5547-8743-53c38b9571c8'}, {'abstract': 'Benjamin Millepied, a principal dancer with New York City Ballet, has retired to focus on choreography, the company announced on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/millepied-retires-from-city-ballet/', 'snippet': 'Benjamin Millepied, a principal dancer with New York City Ballet, has retired to focus on choreography, the company announced on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Benjamin Millepied, a principal dancer with New York City Ballet, has retired and plans to focus on his choreography, the company announced on Wednesday. Mr. Millepied, 34, originally from Bordeaux, France, and known to many non-balletomanes as the choreographer for the Oscar-nominated movie “Black Swan,” joined the company in 1995 after training at City Ballet’s affiliated School of American Ballet. He was promoted to principal in 2002 and originated roles in ballets by Jerome Robbins, Peter Martins, Christopher Wheeldon, Alexei Ratmansky and others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Millepied Retires From City Ballet', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Millepied, Benjamin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T16:29:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/377c501b-6406-520c-9193-ec15d3bb907f', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/377c501b-6406-520c-9193-ec15d3bb907f'}, {'abstract': 'In anticipation of Halloween: custom costumes from inspired designers.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/spooky-sketches-mandy-coon/', 'snippet': 'In anticipation of Halloween: custom costumes from inspired designers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T challenges 10 designers to turn everyday objects into killer Halloween costumes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spooky Sketches | Mandy Coon', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T16:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'orga