n the award for the past five years and was among the 10 players nominated Wednesday for this year’s award.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ladies’ Day: FIFA’s List of 10 for Women’s Player of the Year', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Solo, Hope', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wambach, Abby', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Women's Professional Soccer", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zurich (Switzerland)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T17:28:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b170bff2-88cd-5b7f-ac9d-51edb0e7708b', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b170bff2-88cd-5b7f-ac9d-51edb0e7708b'}, {'abstract': 'A new at-home hair and makeup service serves polished and professional results.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/vain-glorious-prieto-select/', 'snippet': 'A new at-home hair and makeup service serves polished and professional results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An unlikely beauty director at best, I’m the girl who — horrors — doesn’t take off her mascara at night (if I’m even wearing any) and never mastered the fine art of foundation. I do have a couple of guilty pleasures, like an occasional cat eye or a sweep of blue eye shadow, but my application skills are next to nil. What’s more, I barely know how to wield a hair dryer or flat iron. If I don’t have time to run to Orlo or Garren, I’m sunk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Prieto Select', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T17:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdce5c5a-3209-58ba-a2e6-fce32e4b7486', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdce5c5a-3209-58ba-a2e6-fce32e4b7486'}, {'abstract': 'The ECB’s radical theory, and the damage it’s doing.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/wild-eyed-theorists-in-pinstripes/', 'snippet': 'The ECB’s radical theory, and the damage it’s doing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In what amounts to a perfect followup to my post on the amnesiac economy, Paul De Grauwe takes the ECB to task for refusing to do what is necessary to save the euro, and taking refuge in a very narrow definition of its role.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wild-Eyed Theorists In Pinstripes', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T17:35:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54208253-9b8d-50f5-b6f6-b328acde0f8f', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54208253-9b8d-50f5-b6f6-b328acde0f8f'}, {'abstract': 'A bus company in Brooklyn serving a largely Hasidic and Orthodox Jewish clientele denied that it discriminates against female passengers by forcing them to sit at the rear of the bus.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/bus-operator-denies-discriminating-against-women/', 'snippet': 'A bus company in Brooklyn serving a largely Hasidic and Orthodox Jewish clientele denied that it discriminates against female passengers by forcing them to sit at the rear of the bus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bus company that transports primarily Orthodox and Hasidic Jewish passengers between Williamsburg and Borough Park in Brooklyn has denied that it discriminates against female passengers by compelling them to sit at the rear of the bus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bus Operator Denies Discriminating Against Women', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T17:38:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5afb7db-d6ec-5506-bae8-64db8090bedd', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5afb7db-d6ec-5506-bae8-64db8090bedd'}, {'abstract': 'The peace process in Ireland will be in the spotlight on Thursday as the nation holds its election for the largely ceremonial post of president of the Irish Republic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/world/europe/irish-election-portends-signs-of-reconciliation.html', 'snippet': 'The peace process in Ireland will be in the spotlight on Thursday as the nation holds its election for the largely ceremonial post of president of the Irish Republic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GALWAY, Ireland — On an autumn evening beside the storied beauty of Galway Bay, with a chilly gust blowing off the Atlantic, Martin McGuinness breezed into a popular tourist hotel that looks out across the bay with the air of a man who has found a measure of peace after a lifetime gripped by Ireland’s troubled past. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/world/27irelandspan/27ireland-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/27/world/27irelandspan/27ireland-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/world/27irelandspan/27ireland-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/world/27irelandspan/27ireland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/world/27irelandspan/27ireland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailhe