o a lucrative and truly global event.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/returning-for-a-breeders-cup-overflowing-with-story-lines/', 'snippet': 'The Rail returns to cover the 28th running of the Breeders’ Cup World Championships, an event that has turned into a lucrative and truly global event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They got money, $26 million in purses, and a record number of horses pre-entered – 193 of them were pre-entered Wednesday. We’re talking the 28th running of the Breeders’ Cup World Championships, an event that has turned into a lucrative and truly global event.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Returning for a Breeders’ Cup Overflowing With Story Lines', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Breeders' Cup (Horse Race)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Churchill Downs Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T18:03:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e48bc01e-af12-58ae-aea1-97229481de2f', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e48bc01e-af12-58ae-aea1-97229481de2f'}, {'abstract': 'Principals these days are expected to be a little bit of many different things: manager, educator, financial whiz, social worker, enforcer, data analyst, cheerleader and contortionist (figuratively, at least). They are the people with whom the buck stops. Fernanda Santos, who covers city schools for The Times, tagged along with a city school principal all day.', 'web_ur