: 'By Joel Lovell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cf33358-6a70-5b62-9d4b-00bdecdedde6', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cf33358-6a70-5b62-9d4b-00bdecdedde6'}, {'abstract': 'We took my 3-year-old’s pacifier away last weekend. We haven’t slept since.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/breaking-the-pacifier-addiction/', 'snippet': 'We took my 3-year-old’s pacifier away last weekend. We haven’t slept since.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m thrilled to be writing Motherlode this week for so many reasons. I love the topic, I love the audience and at this very moment, I need advice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking the Pacifier Addiction', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T18:47:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenny Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80f930d5-cfab-5ec3-ae4f-0c9b4bd138a9', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80f930d5-cfab-5ec3-ae4f-0c9b4bd138a9'}, {'abstract': 'The 5-year-old cat, who escaped in August, was found just about where he had been lost.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/missing-no-more-jack-the-cat-turns-up-at-j-f-k/', 'snippet': 'The 5-year-old cat, who escaped in August, was found just about where he had been lost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jack the Cat did not patronize the duty-free shops. He was never spotted near any of the drinking establishments. And if he bothered to sample the food court fare, his emaciated condition would register as a scathing critique.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missing No More: Jack the Cat Turns Up at J.F.K.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy International Airport (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T18:48:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b35435f-be23-5107-aa02-104f365cba7d', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b35435f-be23-5107-aa02-104f365cba7d'}, {'abstract': 'The trade group for insurers files a  legal brief on the health care law.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/insurers-weigh-in-on-health-care-law/', 'snippet': 'The trade group for insurers files a  legal brief on the health care law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The health insurance industry is urging the Supreme Court to decide as quickly as it can whether the federal health care law is, in fact, constitutional and to consider what other parts of the law should be struck down if the individual mandate does not pass muster.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insurers Weigh In on Health Care Law', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T18:53:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfc3c579-4526-5252-8623-1bf32d9d3eba', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfc3c579-4526-5252-8623-1bf32d9d3eba'}, {'abstract': 'A salvaged shipping container may seem an unpromising showcase for cutting-edge style.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/life-as-a-runway-african-style-glows-in-brooklyn/', 'snippet': 'A salvaged shipping container may seem an unpromising showcase for cutting-edge style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A salvaged shipping container may seem an unpromising showcase for cutting-edge style. But not to Hekima Hapa, who set up shop in one of the rectangular spaces scattered throughout the Dekalb Market in Brooklyn on Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Life as a Runway: African Style Glows in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T18:58:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth La Ferla and ELIZABETH LIPPMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Ferla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LIPPMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2039f76-1584-53fa-8e25-5f94dfd33961', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2039f76-1584-53fa-8e25-5f94dfd33961'}, {'abstract': 'A British court ruling on the pension obligations of Nortel Networks and Lehman Brothers shows the flaws in a nation-by-nation approach to resolving insolvencies.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/the-conflict-between-global-companies-and-local-laws/', 'snippet': 'A British court ruling on the pension obligations of Nortel Networks and Lehman Brothers shows the flaws in a nation-by-nation approach to resolving insolvencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the context of financial institutions, it is widely understood that the nation-by-nation approach to dealing with failing banks through laws like the Orderly Liquidation Authority of Title II of the Dodd-Frank Act really does not work. There is no such thing as a purely domestic “too big to fail” financial institution.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Conflict Between Global Companies and Local Laws', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nortel Networks Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T19:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen J. Lubben', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Lubben', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e6ccb56-6294-5695-802d-7cab772510d9', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e6ccb56-6294-5695-802d-7cab772510d9'}, {'abstract': 'Federal regulators gave BP a permit to drill a new well in the Gulf of Mexico, the first time the oil company will be allowed to drill there since the Deepwater Horizon disaster in April 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/bp-to-drill-again-in-the-gulf-of-mexico/', 'snippet': 'Federal regulators gave BP a permit to drill a new well in the Gulf of Mexico, the first time the oil company will be allowed to drill there since the Deepwater Horizon disaster in April 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration on Wednesday gave BP its first drilling permit in the Gulf of Mexico since the Deepwater Horizon rig exploded in April 2010.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BP to Drill Again in the Gulf of Mexico', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T19:05:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b1e5ac5-aae3-51b3-9991-ba78cfa0477c', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b1e5ac5-aae3-51b3-9991-ba78cfa0477c'}, {'abstract': 'An online tool helps the impaired rate the accessibility of restaurants, hotels and other sites.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/an-accessibility-map-for-the-impaired/', 'snippet': 'An online tool helps the impaired rate the accessibility of restaurants, hotels and other sites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new online rating tool to help people with disabilities evaluate the accessibility of restaurants, hotels and other sites was released this month by the Rick Hansen Foundation. The Global Accessibility Map was designed as an easy-to-use source for people with mobility, sight and hearing impairments. (Visually impaired users can access it using standard software programs that convert text into audible content.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Accessibility Map for the Impaired', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T19:13:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9409423-d81b-5bb2-8514-896196cc7956', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9409423-d81b-5bb2-8514-896196cc7956'}, {'abstract': 'A 13th week 