hsonian, and the passage of a resolution to limit the duration of drumming.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/occupywallst-roundup-day-40/', 'snippet': 'Ruminations on wandering serfs and derelicts, the harvesting of signs by the Smithsonian, and the passage of a resolution to limit the duration of drumming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are the Occupy Wall Street protesters the modern-day equivalent of wandering serfs in 14th-century Britain? Or are they a bunch of grubby lowlifes and ex-cons? [Metro Focus, New York Post]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '#OccupyWallSt Roundup, Day 40', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zuccotti Park (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T19:18:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jillian Dunham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jillian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dunham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1278411-a6b7-5ac8-8402-054ec243109e', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1278411-a6b7-5ac8-8402-054ec243109e'}, {'abstract': 'Now at P. S. 1: a compulsively watchable, feature-length digital animation that goes well beyond the whisper of sweet nothings.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/artifacts-frances-starks-best-thing/', 'snippet': 'Now at P. S. 1: a compulsively watchable, feature-length digital animation that goes well beyond the whisper of sweet nothings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some people like to talk during sex. Others get their kicks by talking about it. And then there are those who would rather just watch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Artifacts | Frances Stark’s Best Thing', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T19:21:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Yablonsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yablonsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab815be6-d8d1-5abd-b9d7-712de80c3bab', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab815be6-d8d1-5abd-b9d7-712de80c3bab'}, {'abstract': 'Complaints filed by the Federal Trade Commission claim two California-based debt collectors used abusive tactics.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/f-t-c-claims-abusive-tactics-by-two-debt-collection-firms/', 'snippet': 'Complaints filed by the Federal Trade Commission claim two California-based debt collectors used abusive tactics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In tough economic times, with many people out of work and struggling to pay their bills, it’s no surprise that debt collectors are out in force. But recently, the Federal Trade Commission moved to shut down two California-based operators that handled collections nationally, including one that is accused of using tactics so egregious that they resemble scenes from a film noir script.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.T.C. Claims Abusive Tactics by Two Debt Collection Firms', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collection Agencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federa