i (United Arab Emirates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T20:54:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24a82296-23ac-524a-a0d0-3409de585d36', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24a82296-23ac-524a-a0d0-3409de585d36'}, {'abstract': 'Ivo van Hove brings his stage adaptation of this Ingmar Bergman movie to the Brooklyn Academy of Music’s Next Wave Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/theater/reviews/cries-and-whispers-at-bam-review.html', 'snippet': 'Ivo van Hove brings his stage adaptation of this Ingmar Bergman movie to the Brooklyn Academy of Music’s Next Wave Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The blood has been drained from Ingmar Bergman’s “Cries and Whispers” in Ivo van Hove’s clinical stage adaptation of the celebrated film, at the Brooklyn Academy of Music as part of the Next Wave Festival. The saturated reds that were a stylistic hallmark — and a symbolic one — of Bergman’s movie are nowhere to be seen in Mr. van Hove’s cooler, more diffuse examination of the agonies of a woman’s death and its impact on her two sisters and the devoted maid who attends her.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/27cries/27cries-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/27cries/27cries-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/27cries/27cries-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/27cries/27cries-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/27cries/27cries-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sister Slips Away, Under Her Camera’s Gaze, in Update of Bergman', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Cries and Whispers'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sister Slips Away, Under Her Camera’s Gaze, in Update of Bergman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Next Wave Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergman, Ingmar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Hove, Ivo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T21:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a41aa465-8e52-5083-9bfe-23d53050381b', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a41aa465-8e52-5083-9bfe-23d53050381b'}, {'abstract': 'The Chevrolet Cruze is one model that, while not performing well on the publication’s annual reliability report, is selling strongly in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/some-losers-in-consumer-reports-reliability-survey-are-winners-in-showrooms/', 'snippet': 'The Chevrolet Cruze is one model that, while not performing well on the publication’s annual reliability report, is selling strongly in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Consumer Reports Annual Auto Reliability Survey, released on Tuesday afternoon, is intended to provide shoppers with a sense of the projected reliability of new models. But as the sales of some new cars indicate, a poor showing in the study does not translate to poor performance in the marketplace.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Losers in Consumer Reports Reliability Survey Are Winners in Showrooms', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler LLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jeep Division of Chrysler', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LEXUS DIVISION OF TOYOTA MOTOR SALES USA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corp', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T21:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3fc9821-dad5-569e-ab23-114b4ed3d2ef', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3fc9821-dad5-569e-ab23-114b4ed3d2ef'}, {'abstract': 'Australian researchers found that obese people who lost weight experienced metabolic and hormonal changes even a year later that increased their appetites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/health/biological-changes-thwart-weight-loss-efforts-study-finds.html', 'snippet': 'Australian researchers found that obese people who lost weight experienced metabolic and hormonal changes even a year later that increased their appetites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, studies of obesity have found that soon after fat people lost weight, their metabolism slowed and they experienced hormonal changes that increased their appetites. Scientists hypothesized that these biological changes could explain why most obese dieters quickly gained back much of what they had so painfully lost.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/us/diet/diet-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 970, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/us/diet/diet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/us/diet/diet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Shows Why It’s Hard to Keep Weight Off', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Shows Why It’s Hard To Keep Weight Off', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Journal of Medicine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hormones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank'