easy to appreciate,” he says. Brackett has gained a following with his seasonal bento — dishes include pickled plum, Dungeness crab rice and miso-cured black cod — delivered in bamboo husk boxes. Go to interactive feature >>', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edible Selby | Boon Boxes', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T21:15:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Todd Selby and Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Todd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Selby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cebcd30-6b6a-53e0-849e-6513d9f76b32', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cebcd30-6b6a-53e0-849e-6513d9f76b32'}, {'abstract': 'The Kenyan government revealed that its foray against Islamist militants was not simply a response to a wave of kidnappings, as previously claimed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/world/africa/kenya-planned-somalia-incursion-far-in-advance.html', 'snippet': 'The Kenyan government revealed that its foray against Islamist militants was not simply a response to a wave of kidnappings, as previously claimed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — The Kenyan government revealed on Wednesday that its extensive military foray into Somalia this month to battle Islamist militants was not simply a response to a wave of recent kidnappings, as previously claimed, but was actually planned far in advance, part of a covert strategy to penetrate Somalia and keep the violence in one of Africa’s most anarchic countries from spilling into one of A