imedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sentence of the Week, Hilarrifying Edition', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T21:29:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3240ec3-bfb8-5f40-8b79-dd27bcff27d5', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3240ec3-bfb8-5f40-8b79-dd27bcff27d5'}, {'abstract': 'There are several apps that help lead the way to that special cup of coffee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/technology/personaltech/for-coffee-fans-virtual-treasure-maps-app-smart.html', 'snippet': 'There are several apps that help lead the way to that special cup of coffee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rise of coffee houses has been a blessing and a curse for coffee lovers. If you’re far from your favorite spot, the search for a decent replacement can be excruciating.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/business/27-SMART2/27-SMART2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 702, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/business/27-SMART2/27-SMART2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/business/27-SMART2/27-SMART2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Coffee Fans, a Collection of Virtual Treasure Maps', 'kicker': 'App Smart', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Coffee Fans, a Collection of Virtual Treasure Maps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beverages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T21:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Tedeschi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tedeschi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6288714-85be-570b-8ba1-694db20b56e5', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6288714-85be-570b-8ba1-694db20b56e5'}, {'abstract': '“In addition to her growing dissatisfaction with the run of new movies, Pauline was not particularly happy with her situation at The New Yorker.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/books/review/pauline-kael-a-life-in-the-dark.html', 'snippet': '“In addition to her growing dissatisfaction with the run of new movies, Pauline was not particularly happy with her situation at The New Yorker.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In addition to her growing dissatisfaction with the run of new movies, Pauline was not particularly happy with her situation at The New Yorker. She continued to do battle with William Shawn over tone and language in her copy, and after more than ten years of the same arguments, she was suffering from battle fatigue. Shawn, for his part, was just as exasperated as he once had been about Pauline’s insistence on using sexual and scatological language that he deemed inappropriate for the magazine. Their arguments had lost none of their sting over the years; as always, Pauline seemed to enjoy pushing Shawn to the limits, trying to find a crack in his gentlemanly decorum. “I can remember a couple of times, at least, seeing him turn so red when they would start arguing,” remembered William Whitworth, who served as Pauline’s immediate editor for a time in the 1970s. “She would never let it go. Shawn had had a heart attack, and I thought a couple of times that he might fall over on the floor right there in the office. She was the only person in the process whodidn’t treat him the way the world of journalism did, and the way the rest of us did, as a very special little person — which he was. She treated him like one of the guys and talked to him that way, with a lot of wisecracks.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Pauline Kael: A Life in the Dark’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T21:39:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Kellow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kellow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/377b5a4e-53ea-511b-b72a-9ffb2498cdbb', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/377b5a4e-53ea-511b-b72a-9ffb2498cdbb'}, {'abstract': 'Two new alternatives to acetone and other smelly solvents are BIO remover and Priti NYC wipes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/fashion/products-for-unsmelly-removal-of-nail-polish-trial-run.html', 'snippet': 'Two new alternatives to acetone and other smelly solvents are BIO remover and Priti NYC wipes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'REMOVING nail polish, at least with solutions containing acetone or similar solvents, is a smelly business (and can be irritating to skin and lungs, according to the Environmental Working Group, a nonprofit advocacy group).', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27SKIN5/27SKIN5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 898, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27SKIN5/27SKIN5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27SKIN5/27SKIN5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trial Run', 'kicker': 'Skin Deep ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trial Run', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nails (Body Part)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T21:40:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Saint Louis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': 'Saint', 'lastname': 'Louis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d75054fb-9ca4-51dd-9e81-58ea17d706e6', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d75054fb-9ca4-51dd-9e81-58ea17d706e6'}, {'abstract': 'Two new books, Brian Kellow’s “Pauline Kael,” and a memoir by James Wolcott, “Lucking Out,” focus on the swashbuckling era of criticism when Kael’s voice boomed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/books/pauline-kael-a-life-in-the-dark-and-lucking-out-review.html', 'snippet': 'Two new books, Brian Kellow’s “Pauline Kael,” and a memoir by James Wolcott, “Lucking Out,” focus on the swashbuckling era of criticism when Kael’s voice boomed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the imperial zenith of her career, Pauline Kael labeled a film “the most virtuoso example of sophisticated kaleidoscopic farce that American moviemakers have ever come up with.” This was in the midst of the 1970s, a period that Kael’s sharpest protégé, James Wolcott, now calls “the feudal age of film criticism.” That era is due for new scrutiny with the publication of three new books about the period. Each has a lot to say, though none entirely explain Kael’s heady assessment, above, of the 1975 film “Shampoo.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/jump-book/jump-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/jump-book/jump-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/jump-book/jump-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The ’70s, as Dramatic as a Movie', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The ’70s, As Dramatic As a Movie', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kael, Pauline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kellow, Brian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolcott, James', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T21:40:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/56a047a4-8447-5407-aff3-8826c42d57f3', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56a047a4-8447-5407-aff3-8826c42d57f3'}, {'abstract': 'The city’s market has fluctuated as the government has taken steps to control runaway prices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/10/26/greathomesanddestinations/20111030ihhhongkong.html', 'snippet': 'The city’s market has fluctuated as the government has taken steps to control runaway prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The city’s market has fluctuated as the government has taken steps to control runaway prices.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Renovated Duplex Penthouse in Hong Kong', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T21:42:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/922d32f7-04d3-5141-9267-e70633d4095f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/922d32f7-04d3-5141-9267-e70633d4095f'}, {'abstract': 'The first issue of Style.com/Print, a magazine developed by the fashion news Web site Style.com, will hit newsstands next week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/fashion/stylecom-print-a-fashion-web-sites-glossy-debut.html', 'snippet': 'The first issue of Style.com/Print, a magazine developed by the fashion news Web site Style.com, will hit newsstands next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEXT week, the first issue of a glossy magazine from the editors of Style.com, with the puzzling name of Style.com/Print, will hit newsstands. The cover shows a close-up of Lindsey Wixson, the model from Kansas with the strawberry-shaped smoocher, framed by a thick lipstick-red border. There are no teasers about what’s inside, just a quote from Ms. Wixson that suggests she will never be known as the Joan Didion of her trade.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27ROW/27ROW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 728, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27ROW/27ROW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27ROW/27ROW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finally, the Web at Hand', 'kicker': 'Front Row', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finally, The Web At Hand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name'