., more than 1,000 miles to the south.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I noted in my article in Wednesday’s paper, Shell Oil has received several preliminary permits to begin drilling exploratory wells off the Arctic coast of Alaska next summer even as foes of drilling there argue that the severe conditions — ice, darkness, brutal storms — will make it impossible to properly respond to a spill or other problem. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Coast Guard Challenge: Arctic Drilling', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T22:15:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a14936b1-e3b0-552c-a87d-b97c0da2850b', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a14936b1-e3b0-552c-a87d-b97c0da2850b'}, {'abstract': 'At the opening of Carsten Höller’s funhouse exhibition at the New Museum, intensity was the rule.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/fashion/at-a-museum-carnival-exhibits-scene-city.html', 'snippet': 'At the opening of Carsten Höller’s funhouse exhibition at the New Museum, intensity was the rule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK parties, where any number of bad things can happen to a sensitive guest, often provoke as much delight as anxiety. Tuesday’s opening of Carsten Höller’s funhouse exhibition at the New Museum was no exception. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/fashion/27SCENE2/27SCENE2-articleLarg