esigned on Wednesday in response to a corruption scandal, reviving concern about President Dilma Rousseff’s unstable governing coalition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/world/americas/orlando-silva-brazils-sports-minister-resigns.html', 'snippet': 'Orlando Silva, the sports minister of Brazil, resigned on Wednesday in response to a corruption scandal, reviving concern about President Dilma Rousseff’s unstable governing coalition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — Brazil’s embattled sports minister resigned on Wednesday amid accusations of corruption. He is the sixth minister to step down in disgrace since President Dilma Rousseff took office in January. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/world/27silva-image/27silva-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/world/27silva-image/27silva-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/28/world/27silva-image/27silva-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil’s Sports Minister Steps Down', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sports Minister In Brazil Quits Under Pressure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2016)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rousseff, Dilma', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silva, Orlando', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Da Silva, Luiz Inacio Lula', 'rank':