6T23:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/16f07406-55a3-5aa9-8437-e2817856dada', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16f07406-55a3-5aa9-8437-e2817856dada'}, {'abstract': '“Mike Judge’s Beavis and Butt-Head,” a new version of the animated series, has its debut on MTV on Thursday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/arts/television/mike-judges-beavis-and-butt-head-on-mtv.html', 'snippet': '“Mike Judge’s Beavis and Butt-Head,” a new version of the animated series, has its debut on MTV on Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We find Beavis and Butt-Head where we left them — resiliently stuck to that dirty couch, watching their flickering TV, laughing with that combination of giggle and heavy pant. The products of heavy metal, collapsed family structures and inertia, they’re mischievous and susceptible, and not gumptious enough for real misbehavior.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/27beavis/27beavis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/27beavis/27beavis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/27beavis/27beavis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Look Who’s Trashing ‘Jersey Shore’ Now', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Look Who’s Trashing ‘Jersey Shore’ Now', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T23:56:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7801bebc-5aef-5362-92b7-81e25e1eaa44', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7801bebc-5aef-5362-92b7-81e25e1eaa44'}, {'abstract': 'A freshman at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology, whose father is a Nobel-winning scientist on the faculty, was found dead in his dormitory room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/us/mit-freshman-son-of-nobel-winner-is-found-dead.html', 'snippet': 'A freshman at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology, whose father is a Nobel-winning scientist on the faculty, was found dead in his dormitory room.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A freshman at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology, whose father is a Nobel-winning scientist on the faculty, was found dead in his dormitory room, the university said Wednesday. The death of the student, Satto Tonegawa, son of Susumu Tonegawa, is under routine investigation by the state police and the Middlesex County district attorney’s office. “There is no indication that there was foul play,” said Cara O’Brien, a spokeswoman for the district attorney’s office. Susumu Tonegawa, director of the Riken-M.I.T. Center for Neural Circuit Genetics, won the 1987 Nobel Prize for medicine or physiology. His son Satto, a prize-winning pianist, grew up in Chestnut Hill, Mass. Last month an M.I.T. sophomore, Nicolas E. Del Castillo, was found dead in his dorm room, a death that was ruled a suicide. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: M.I.T. Freshman Is Found Dead', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: M.I.T. Freshman Is Found Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tonegawa, Satto', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T23:58:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d7c0866-7974-52ab-8d81-4c9d32aff8ba', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d7c0866-7974-52ab-8d81-4c9d32aff8ba'}, {'abstract': 'Toronto, which has not won a Stanley Cup since 1967, is in first place in its division, raising hopes that things may finally be different.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/sports/hockey/kessel-and-maple-leafs-have-promising-start.html', 'snippet': 'Toronto, which has not won a Stanley Cup since 1967, is in first place in its division, raising hopes that things may finally be different.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is an old gag in championship-starved Toronto: “Go Leafs go ... and take the Blue Jays, Argonauts and Raptors with you.” That’s a bit harsh — the Argonauts last won a title in 2004, the Blue Jays in 1992 and ’93 — but the joke is really aimed at the team that matters most in Toronto, the Maple Leafs, who have not lifted the Stanley Cup since 1967.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maple Leafs and Their Star Player Give Toronto Fans Reason for Hope', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Maple Leafs and Their Star Player Give Toronto Fans Reason for Hope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Maple Leafs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Connolly, Tim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-26T23:59:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ca1d397-fd48-56cc-ae79-af9535c142ab', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ca1d397-fd48-56cc-ae79-af9535c142ab'}, {'abstract': 'The Rangers traveled 16,000 miles across two continents during the preseason and the early part of the regular season. Now, finally, they’re ready to play at the Garden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/sports/hockey/after-epic-trip-new-york-rangers-ready-for-first-home-game.html', 'snippet': 'The Rangers traveled 16,000 miles across two continents during the preseason and the early part of the regular season. Now, finally, they’re ready to play at the Garden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Rangers fans enter Madison Square Garden on Thursday for the first sports event at the newly renovated arena, they will find better sightlines, some upper-bowl seats seemingly cantilevered over the ice, interior corridors at least twice the width of the narrow old ones, luxury suites that look like Manhattan apartments, many more restrooms — in short, a vastly improved building. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/sports/RANGERScity/RANGERScity-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/27/sports/RANGERScity/RANGERScity-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/sports/RANGERScity/RANGERScity-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/sports/RANGERScity/RANGERScity-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/sports/RANGERScity/RANGERScity-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After 16,000 Miles, the Rangers Skate on Home Ice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After 16,000 Miles, the Rangers Skate on Home Ice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tortorella, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Road Trips', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Callahan, Ryan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T00:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07e092f6-7f60-553c-a0f3-d20a25fef7fc', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07e092f6-7f60-553c-a0f3-d20a25fef7fc'}, {'abstract': 'Nan Goldin’s “Scopophilia” is showing at the Matthew Marks Gallery in Manhattan. Randy Kennedy interviewed Ms. Goldin for Thursday’s Arts section.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/tuesdays-with-nan-goldin/', 'snippet': 'Nan Goldin’s “Scopophilia” is showing at the Matthew Marks Gallery in Manhattan. Randy Kennedy interviewed Ms. Goldin for Thursday’s Arts section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thursday’s Arts pages feature Randy Kennedy’s interview with Nan Goldin, who is known for her photographs of “life lived at full tilt, of addiction and physical abuse, of friends and lovers ravaged by AIDS and other afflictions,” as Mr. Kennedy writes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesdays With Nan Goldin', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldin, Nan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Randy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louvre', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marks, Matthew, Gallery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T00:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'f