ussa plans to see “Moneyball” on the unplanned World Series off-night. Ron Washington has already lived it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS – How to spend a rained-out night off in the World Series? Tony La Russa, the manager of the St. Louis Cardinals, said he planned to see “Moneyball,” the movie about Oakland Athletics General Manager Billy Beane.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Movie for a Rained-Out Ballgame', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'la Russa, Tony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T00:08:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70808073-9804-50bc-b7f2-0a2b317e926c', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70808073-9804-50bc-b7f2-0a2b317e926c'}, {'abstract': 'Amanda McBroom, the Los Angeles cabaret singer and composer of “The Rose,” is performing at the Metropolitan Room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/arts/music/amanda-mcbroom-at-the-metropolitan-room-review.html', 'snippet': 'Amanda McBroom, the Los Angeles cabaret singer and composer of “The Rose,” is performing at the Metropolitan Room.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A professional Pollyanna” is how Amanda McBroom, the Los Angeles cabaret singer and composer of “The Rose,” cheerfully described herself on Sunday evening at the Metropolitan Room in her new show, “Strange Days.” Ms. McBroom, accompanied on piano by her longtime songwriting collaborator, Michele Brourman, fortified that image with a sturdy 