aying field. Marathons are different: runners race past the fans who line sidewalks, only to be replaced by more runners.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Phone App to Keep Fans in Touch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Phone App to Keep Fans in Touch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Road Runners Club', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T00:16:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3772ffe4-62ce-5fcf-bd5e-589f0124241d', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3772ffe4-62ce-5fcf-bd5e-589f0124241d'}, {'abstract': 'Eight years ago, a state worker started haunted tours of New York’s Capitol, which has enough spooky back story to rival the modern-day foibles of wayward governors and law-breaking legislators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/nyregion/at-capitol-in-albany-spending-an-evening-with-ghosts.html', 'snippet': 'Eight years ago, a state worker started haunted tours of New York’s Capitol, which has enough spooky back story to rival the modern-day foibles of wayward governors and law-breaking legislators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — In a black bowler hat and flowing frock coat, Stuart Lehman stands out at the Capitol. It is just past 5 o’clock, and around him state workers hustle toward the doors.', 'print_section'