for 14 notable artists, including Meryl Streep, Yo-Yo Ma and Amy Tan, for discussions and performances beginning Nov. 14.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/arts/group-of-american-cultural-figures-to-visit-china.html', 'snippet': 'Asia Society and the Aspen Institute are sponsoring a trip to Beijing for 14 notable artists, including Meryl Streep, Yo-Yo Ma and Amy Tan, for discussions and performances beginning Nov. 14.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is not your average cultural exchange. There are no obscure acrobatic troupes and no awkward high school students.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/27exchange/27exchange-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/27exchange/27exchange-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/arts/27exchange/27exchange-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'American Cultural Group to Visit China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Cultural Group to Visit China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aspen Institute', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Asia Society', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T00:20:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Xiyun Yang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Xiyun', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06ea177e-a685-535f-b0fd-17089908e089', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06ea177e-a685-535f-b0fd-17089908e089'}, {'abstract': 'A report from the Working Mother Research Institute finds that whether working or stay-at-home, mothers feel guilty about something.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/neglected-children-messy-houses-and-guilt/', 'snippet': 'A report from the Working Mother Research Institute finds that whether working or stay-at-home, mothers feel guilty about something.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In case you missed it, the Working Mother Research Institute surveyed 3,781 women and issued a report called “What Moms Choose.” It quantifies a lot of things we know, and a few that we don’t. Here are a few statistics to throw out over dinner, if you belong to one of those families who have civilized, discussion-based dinners (I tell myself that will happen when the children are older):', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Neglected Children, Messy Houses and Guilt', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T00:23:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenny Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83c1d2b7-9221-558f-8d6a-c9882b18e3bc', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83c1d2b7-9221-558f-8d6a-c9882b18e3bc'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense recently confirmed the deaths of the following Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/us/us-military-deaths-in-iraq-and-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense recently confirmed the deaths of the following Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 4,473 American service members who have died since the start of the Iraq war and 1,805 who have died as part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the deaths of the following Americans this week: ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T00:26:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/35bd8e82-438f-5c8b-9394-448f915f8b90', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35bd8e82-438f-5c8b-9394-448f915f8b90'}, {'abstract': 'The donation, from the Diller-von Furstenberg Family Foundation, will boost the park’s endowment and help cover costs for its final segment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/nyregion/20-million-gift-to-high-line-park.html', 'snippet': 'The donation, from the Diller-von Furstenberg Family Foundation, will boost the park’s endowment and help cover costs for its final segment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many visitors to the High Line, the popular park that wends above street level on the West Side of Manhattan,