ame': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T00:35:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11dcdcdf-3997-53bf-a673-da0149529f6f', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11dcdcdf-3997-53bf-a673-da0149529f6f'}, {'abstract': 'The veteran comedy writer and author of a new book of essays, “Cool, Calm & Contentious,” has filled her Malibu, Calif., home with unusual statues, portraits and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/garden/qa-the-comedy-writer-merrill-markoe.html', 'snippet': 'The veteran comedy writer and author of a new book of essays, “Cool, Calm & Contentious,” has filled her Malibu, Calif., home with unusual statues, portraits and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Merrill Markoe, the veteran comedy writer who helped David Letterman develop the format for his late night television show in the early 1980s and who, for a time, was the show’s head writer as well as Mr. Letterman’s live-in girlfriend, has a book of essays, “Cool, Calm & Contentious,” out next week. The theme of the book, she said, may be being with crazy people in crazy situations. In fact, many of the essays are not only crazy-funny, but crazy-heartbreaking. Ms. Markoe, who grew up in Miami and San Francisco and intended to be a painter, writes about the narcissistic mother who belittled her work and a sexual attack when she was a 19-year-old art school student at the University of California, Berkeley, in the 1960s. And while she has been discreet about her relationship with Mr. Letterman, declining interviews when he was blackmailed for having an affair with a staff member a couple of years ago, she has a good deal to say about a fellow who sounds a lot like him here, although she calls the man in question Bobby.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/garden/27QNA1_SPAN/27QNA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/27/garden/27QNA1_SPAN/27QNA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/garden/27QNA1_SPAN/27QNA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/garden/27QNA1_SPAN/27QNA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/garden/27QNA1_SPAN/27QNA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Merrill Markoe on Puppets and Monkey Portraits', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Merrill Markoe on Puppets and Monkey Portraits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Markoe, Merrill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T00:35:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Wadler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wadler', 'quali