crept back into the negotiating room on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/sports/basketball/nba-negotiations-continue-into-the-night.html', 'snippet': 'Optimism, a rare visitor in N.B.A. circles in recent months, crept back into the negotiating room on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Optimism, a rare visitor in N.B.A. circles in recent months, crept back into the room on Wednesday — slowly, cautiously and with muted fanfare. The lockout is not over, and a labor deal is not yet in reach. But it may be on the horizon by the weekend.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.B.A. Negotiations Yield a Glimmer of Hope for Full Season', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.B.A. Negotiations Yield a Glimmer of Hope for Full Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter, Billy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T01:22:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/395e458e-8f60-57d1-9ea9-2880a6468fcc', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/395e458e-8f60-57d1-9ea9-2880a6468fcc'}, {'abstract': 'The flurry of visa-related bills making the rounds on Capitol Hill offers further proof that the country cannot live without immigrant labor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/opinion/so-much-for-the-nativists.html', 'snippet': 'The flurry of visa-related bills making the rounds on Capitol Hill offers further proof that the country cannot live without immigrant labor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a Capitol riddle for you: Representative Lamar Smith, one of the most reflexively anti-immigrant hard-liners in Congress, is sponsoring a bill to flood the agriculture sector with up to half-a-million visas for guest workers. Understand why and you’re well on your way to unpacking the nation’s dysfunctional relationship with undocumented immigrants.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'So Much for the Nativists', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Much for the Nativists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migrant and Foreign Workers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Lamar S', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lofgren, Zoe', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Labrador, Raul', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Charles E', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Michael S', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chaffetz, Jason', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'