': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd67a71c-d59a-57e7-bfca-f7a607d259b1', 'word_count': 2465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd67a71c-d59a-57e7-bfca-f7a607d259b1'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s redistricting issues should be resolved by serving the public’s interest instead of party majorities and incumbents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/opinion/new-yorks-redistricting-charade.html', 'snippet': 'New York’s redistricting issues should be resolved by serving the public’s interest instead of party majorities and incumbents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York’s legislative redistricting committee is holding public hearings around the state, but the exercise is a sham. The new political districts are being drawn in secret for one overriding purpose: to protect party majorities and incumbents, often for life. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Redistricting Charade', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York’s Redistricting Charade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T01:34:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e26dddc-616f-5af6-a6f2-e0b56fd7e6b9', 'word_count'