: 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/nyregion/foodfight-a-nonprofit-group-works-with-new-york-city-schools.html', 'snippet': 'A new series of courses at 15 New York City high schools is aiming to make students aware of the politics, marketing and demographics of the food industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A commercial for McDonald’s fish sandwiches played in a classroom at Park Slope Collegiate one day last month as part of a class called the Science of Food. It was clear that many students had seen the ad — several sang along with the jingle — but this was the first time they had been asked to critique it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/nyregion/FOODFIGHT/FOODFIGHT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/nyregion/FOODFIGHT/FOODFIGHT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/nyregion/FOODFIGHT/FOODFIGHT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In High Schools, a Critical Lens on Food', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In High Schools, a Critical Lens on Food', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T01:42:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hannah Wallace', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wallace', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bafbff0-55da-5cca-b60f-771d965ffe32', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bafbff0-55da-5cca-b60f-771d965ffe32'}, {'abstract': 'Stanford is a leading contender in the Bloomberg administration’s competition to create a new school of applied sciences that officials hope will spur the growth of high-tech business in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/nyregion/stanford-raises-cost-of-science-school-bid-to-2-5-billion.html', 'snippet': 'Stanford is a leading contender in the Bloomberg administration’s competition to create a new school of applied sciences that officials hope will spur the growth of high-tech business in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stanford University’s proposed graduate school of science on Roosevelt Island carries a $2.5 billion price tag, the university said Wednesday, more than double its estimate just weeks ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stanford’s Estimated Cost for Science School Doubles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stanford’s Estimated Cost For Science School Doubles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ROOSEVELT ISLAND (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornell University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduate Schools and Students', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T01:44:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline'