media': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Telling Court of a Scheme to Sell Arms to Terrorists', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Telling Court Of a Scheme To Sell Arms To Terrorists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arms Trade', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smulian, Andrew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bout, Viktor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T01:55:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noah Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e71c1ad7-a548-55ac-99b8-fd3a5cdc1639', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e71c1ad7-a548-55ac-99b8-fd3a5cdc1639'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg said the carriage industry was a part of the city’s heritage and beloved by tourists, and there was no reason to shut it down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/nyregion/bloomberg-rejects-calls-to-ban-horse-drawn-carriages.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg said the carriage industry was a part of the city’s heritage and beloved by tourists, and there was no reason to shut it down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Days after a carriage horse collapsed and died in Midtown, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg on Wednesday dismissed calls for a ban on the carriage industry, saying he could not imagine why “anybody wants to destroy something that is part of New York’s heritage and that tourists love.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Carriage Horse Dies, Mayor Rejects Calls for Ban', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Carriage Horse Dies, Mayor Rejects Calls for Ban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Horse and Carriage Assn, New York', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T01:57:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f001b2f-860c-5df4-afcd-2afea5278235', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f001b2f-860c-5df4-afcd-2afea5278235'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees are close to completing a new contract proposal for C.C. Sabathia, who can opt out of his current deal after the World Series.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/new-offer-for-sabathia-in-the-works/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees are close to completing a new contract proposal for C.C. Sabathia, who can opt out of his current deal after the World Series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — The Yankees are close to completing a new contract proposal for the left-hander C.C. Sabathia, which they intend to present to him before he can opt out of his current contract, according to a baseball executive who spoke on the condition of anonymity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Offer for Sabathia in the Works', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T01:57:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bd94e8a-32fa-5e1e-bbe2-996653a0be84', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bd94e8a-32fa-5e1e-bbe2-996653a0be84'}, {'abstract': 'A bootiful championship round grid from the Westchester Crossword Puzzle Tournament by Kurt Mueller.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/26/scared/', 'snippet': 'A bootiful championship round grid from the Westchester Crossword Puzzle Tournament by Kurt Mueller.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY’S PUZZLE — There’s a lot to like in this puzzle, but perhaps my favorite part is that it allowed me to draw little pictures of ghosts inside some of the squares of this rebus. That wasn’t a completely original idea. Jeffrey Schwartz, second place winner of the 2011 Westchester Crossword Puzzle Tournament, drew them during the championship round and I thought that was a lot more fun than trying to cram the word GHOST into each square. Congratulations as well to champion Robert Mackey and third place winner Elaine Lippman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday: Visibly Scared Out of One’s Wits', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T02:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8a3df3b-5ae6-5796-9f3b-291ff4e09313', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8a3df3b-5ae6-5796-9f3b-291ff4e09313'}, {'abstract': 'The vodka’s new campaign commemorates its efforts to reach American consumers who are gay, efforts which began in 1981 with magazine ads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/business/media/absolut-heralds-its-marketing-to-gay-consumers.html', 'snippet': 'The vodka’s new campaign commemorates its efforts to reach American consumers who are gay, efforts which began in 1981 with magazine ads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MARKETERS like to mark milestones, whether it is the 50th anniversary of the debut of “The Dick Van Dyke Show,” the 125th anniversary of the introduction of Coca-Cola or the 150th anniversary of the Brooklyn Academy of Music. Now, a brand is about to celebrate something that typically passes unnoticed: the 30th anniversary of a media placement.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 725, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheig