dernist restaurant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/magazine/recipe-eleven-madison-park-granola.html', 'snippet': 'The recipe to the ending note of a meal at the modernist restaurant.', 'lead_paragraph': '2 3⁄4 cups rolled oats 1 cup shelled pistachios 1 cup unsweetened coconut chips 1/3 cup pumpkinseeds 1 tablespoon salt 1⁄2 cup light brown sugar 1/3 cup maple syrup 1/3 cup extra virgin olive oil 3⁄4 cup dried sour cherries.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/magazine/30eat2/30eat2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 880, 'width': 976, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eleven Madison Park Granola', 'kicker': 'Recipe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T03:58:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a8a9ed7-4fe2-5c8d-a276-e594499bb26c', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a8a9ed7-4fe2-5c8d-a276-e594499bb26c'}, {'abstract': 'Goals by Joel Lindpere and Thierry Henry lifted the Red Bulls over F.C. Dallas in a one-game wild card match. The Red Bulls will play the Los Angeles Galaxy next.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/sports/soccer/red-bulls-defeat-dallas-to-advance.html', 'snippet': 'Goals by Joel Lindpere and Thierry Henry lifted the Red Bulls over F.C. Dallas in a one-game wild card match. The Red Bulls will play the Los Angeles Galaxy next.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRISCO, Tex. — The Red Bulls were riding a wave of momentum last week as they became re-energized just in time to salvage a spot in the M.L.S. playoffs. Still, their captain, Thierry Henry, had issued a warning that the team needed to play better if it expected to beat F.C. Dallas.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/sports/REDBULLS/REDBULLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 332, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/27/sports/REDBULLS/REDBULLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 332}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/sports/REDBULLS/REDBULLS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 943, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/sports/REDBULLS/REDBULLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/sports/REDBULLS/REDBULLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Bulls Cash In on Playoff Chance', 'kicker': 'Red Bulls 2, F.C. Dallas 0', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hot at the Right Time, The Red Bulls Advance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lindpere, Joel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henry, Thierry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T03:58:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Spousta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spousta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9a8f339-d61c-58f0-ad9e-996b79ac63bf', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9a8f339-d61c-58f0-ad9e-996b79ac63bf'}, {'abstract': 'In the years just after the founding of the United Nations in 1945, Mr. Sherry became known as the English-speaking voice of Andrei Y. Vishinsky, the Soviet delegate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/us/George-Sherry-Voice-at-United-Nations-Dies-at-87.html', 'snippet': 'In the years just after the founding of the United Nations in 1945, Mr. Sherry became known as the English-speaking voice of Andrei Y. Vishinsky, the Soviet delegate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George L. Sherry, a former United Nations official who helped calm crises around the world — a role that evolved from his time as the leading rapid-fire translator of speeches by Russian diplomats in the organization’s early days — died in Manhattan on Friday. He was 87.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/world/SHERRY-obit/SHERRY-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 915, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/27/world/SHERRY-obit/SHERRY-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/27/world/SHERRY-obit/SHERRY-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'George L. Sherry, Envoy and Well-Known Voice at U.N., Dies at 87', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'George L. Sherry, 87, Envoy and Well-Known Voice at U.N.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Translation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Language', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T03:59:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/26085098-41bd-5be1-bbf6-fca43173093a', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26085098-41bd-5be1-bbf6-fca43173093a'}, {'abstract': 'Modernist cuisine made – well, not simple. But doable at least.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/magazine/modernist-cuisine-for-laymen.html', 'snippet': 'Modernist cuisine made – well, not simple. But doable at least.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eleven Madison Park is a grand and airy urban palace of a restaurant in the Metropolitan Life North Building at the foot of Madison Avenue. The dining room has wide marble floors and soaring, double-height ceilings, and huge windows that overlook the leafy acres of Madison Square Park. It is among the most beautiful restaurants in the world.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '46', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/magazine/30eat_span/30eat_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/30/magazine/30eat_span/30eat_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/magazine/30eat_span/30eat_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/magazine/30eat_span/30eat_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/magazine/30eat_span/30eat_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Liquid Nitrogen Optional', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Liquid Nitrogen Optional', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eleven Madison Park (NYC Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T04:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b45c888-9243-5768-8503-376825cc0451', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b45c888-9243-5768-8503-376825cc0451'}, {'abstract': 'Mindfulness, or being fully present and attentive to the moment, not only improves the way doctors engage with patients but also mitigates the stresses of clinical practice.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/teaching-doctors-to-be-mindful/', 'snippet': 'Mindfulness, or being fully present and attentive to the moment, not only improves the way doctors engage with patients but also mitigates the stresses of clinical practice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was 6:40 in the morning and nearly all of the doctors attending the medical conference had assembled for the first session of the day. But there were no tables and chairs in sight, no lectern, no run-throughs of PowerPoint presentations. All I could make out in the early morning darkness were the unmoving forms of my colleagues, cross-legged on cushions and raised platforms, eyes closed and hands resting with palms upward in their laps.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teaching Doctors to Be Mindful', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meditation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T04:01:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01b39a37-beec-52f7-b419-708fcafe3da2', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01b39a37-beec-52f7-b419-708fcafe3da2'}, {'abstract': 'Can your romantic life be reduced to the pronouns you say (or tweet or post or text)? Sort of.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/small-talk/', 'snippet': 'Can your romantic life be reduced to the pronouns you say (or tweet or post or text)? Sort of.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Behavioral scientists have long known that humans, whether in the schoolyard or in a dimly lighted bar, have a tendency to subconsciously mimic the sounds, style and movement of others. Recent research, however, shows that this mimicry also extends to how we speak and write. Even the least important words we choose can say a lot about us.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Romance Be Reduced to Pronouns?', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T04:02:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f006729-58cc-5d0b-90e3-5f85241b3ad3', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f006729-58cc-5d0b-90e3-5f85241b3ad3'}, {'abstract': 'Has there ever been a candidate with such strong polling but such weak fundamentals? Almost certainly not.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/herman-cain-outlier/', 'snippet': 'Has there ever been a candidate with such strong polling but such weak fundamentals? Almost certainly not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Herman Cain, the Georgia businessman who has never held elected office, is tied for the lead in national polls of Republican voters — or perhaps even slightly ahead of Mitt Romney, as he was in Tuesday night’s New York Times/CBS News poll. Mr. Cain has also led in most recent polls of the Iowa caucuses and the South Carolina primary, has taken the lead in Ohio, and is close to Mr. Romney in Florida. If all you had to go on was the polls, you might think that Mr. Cain was the favorite to win the Republican nomination.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Herman Cain, Outlier', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T04:02:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a4f9e6d-1219-5a94-91b0-fd2db25f584b', 'word_count': 1175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a4f9e6d-1219-5a94-91b0-fd2db25f584b'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on October 27, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/pageoneplus/corrections-october-27.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on October 27, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: October 27', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T04:03:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person