ven as investors extended a rally in stocks, some credit markets barely budged, indicating continued doubts about a long-term fix for the debt crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/business/daily-stock-market-activity.html', 'snippet': 'Even as investors extended a rally in stocks, some credit markets barely budged, indicating continued doubts about a long-term fix for the debt crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'World financial markets powered higher on Thursday in the giddy hope that Europe’s plan to solve its sovereign debt crisis would finally lift the uncertainty over the global economy and markets. In the United States, a sharp jump in stocks continued what has become the biggest monthly rally in 37 years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shares Jump on European Deal to Solve Debt Crisis', 'kicker': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gauging the Fallout of Another Rescue: Shares Jump on Hope Fueled by Europe’s Deal to Solve Its Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T10:31:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley and Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f78c39c-7a65-5491-abc3-f661a6c21e3a', 'word_count': 1255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f78c39c-7a65-5491-abc3-f661a6c21e3a'}, {'abstract': 'Readers suggest that Dr. Jaliman use fewer words and do more to establish trust on her site.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/how-a-doctors-web-site-can-generate-more-business/', 'snippet': 'Readers suggest that Dr. Jaliman use fewer words and do more to establish trust on her site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, my post asked whether visiting a service provider’s Web site made you want to use the service.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How a Doctor’s Web Site Can Generate More Business', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jaliman, Debra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T11:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabriel Shaoolian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabriel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shaoolian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05bac737-cad6-55c5-84d0-c08fb52a34a5', 'word_count': 1347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05bac737-cad6-55c5-84d0-c08fb52a34a5'}, {'abstract': 'The report, using census data, found that immigrant households on the island made an annual income not far behind that of American-born families.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/study-finds-that-immigrants-are-central-to-long-island-economy/', 'snippet': 'The report, using census data, found that immigrant households on the island made an annual income not far behind that of American-born families.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Immigrants, those who are here legally and illegally, are important contributors to the economy on Long Island and are a relatively affluent group, according to a report to be released on Thursday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Finds That Immigrants Are Central to Long Island Economy', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levy, Steven A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lucero, Marcelo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fiscal Policy Institute', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T11:01:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Meredith Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Meredith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e24c955-0369-522f-a2dd-6278d1fec44b', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e24c955-0369-522f-a2dd-6278d1fec44b'}, {'abstract': 'Dropbox, the file-sharing service, is hoping to appease information technology departments by introducing a new service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/technology/dropbox-aims-to-solidify-its-place-with-businesses.html', 'snippet': 'Dropbox, the file-sharing service, is hoping to appease information technology departments by introducing a new service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Perhaps it should not have surprised corporate information technology departments that employees would use Dropbox, a service for easily sharing files among different devices by storing them in “the cloud.” But that did not mean they loved the idea of confidential files on a service they could not control. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dropbox Bids to Find Entry in Businesses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dropbox Bids To Find Entry In Businesses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data Storage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dropbox Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T11:36:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b09ae96-18c7-55b8-80f2-386bf6c7a96f', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b09ae96-18c7-55b8-80f2-386bf6c7a96f'}, {'abstract': 'Five years ago, the city started aggressively enforcing its 1998 ban on electronics to keep cellphones out of schools, except for students with medical conditions. Yet today, students at most schools know they can get away with carrying their phones unless they flaunt them. It is the students at schools with metal detectors who pay a price for following the rules, by using trucks and bodegas to stash their phones for a dollar a day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/10/27/ban-on-cellphones-creates-a-tale-of-two-city-schools/', 'snippet': 'Five years ago, the city started aggressively enforcing its 1998 ban on electronics to keep cellphones out of schools, except for students with medical conditions. Yet today, students at most schools know they can get away with carrying their phon...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cellphone Ban Is a Tale of Two City Schools', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T11:42:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By BETH FERTIG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Beth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'FERTIG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/228ef206-aae9-5786-bb05-a1857ae48fcb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/228ef206-aae9-5786-bb05-a1857ae48fcb'}, {'abstract': 'Alfred, a restaurant-finding app, will learn your preferences and tailor your choices.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/making-restaurant-recommendations-smarter/', 'snippet': 'Alfred, a restaurant-finding app, will learn your preferences and tailor your choices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the neat tricks of the new iPhone 4S is how Siri, its virtual assistant feature, taps into the restaurant database of Yelp to recommend local dining options. When I ask Siri, “What’s the best place to get dessert nearby,” it grabs a list of a dozen purveyors of sweetness in my area, ordered by their Yelp ratings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Restaurant Recommendations Smarter', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T11:43:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a4627e6-2383-58dc-ba15-0d646c1cdf76', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a4627e6-2383-58dc-ba15-0d646c1cdf76'}, {'abstract': 'Violators will face fines ranging from $5,000, for a first offense, to around $100,000.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/toronto-bans-shark-fin-sales/', 'snippet': 'Violators will face fines ranging from $5,000, for a first offense, to around $100,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shark fin soup will be off the menu before long in Canada’s largest city. After a frequently theatrical debate that included the flight of an inflatable shark around its chamber, the Toronto City Council voted this week to ban the consumption, possession and sale of shark fins.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toronto Bans Shark Fin Sales', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sharks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 5, 'major'