e': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T15:32:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6ba2e7e-c591-56d0-943c-34a9f6d115cf', 'word_count': 1055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6ba2e7e-c591-56d0-943c-34a9f6d115cf'}, {'abstract': 'At a news conference in London on Wednesday, he announced that he would create a new “Sleeping Beauty” for Christmas 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/a-new-sleeping-beauty-courtesy-of-matthew-bourne/', 'snippet': 'At a news conference in London on Wednesday, he announced that he would create a new “Sleeping Beauty” for Christmas 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — He has turned his hand to “Swan Lake,” “The Nutcracker,” “La Sylphide” and “Cinderella,” but Matthew Bourne isn’t done yet rethinking the ballet classics. At a news conference at Sadler’s Wells on Wednesday, he announced that he would create a new “Sleeping Beauty” for Christmas 2012 as part of a yearlong celebration of the 25th anniversary of his company, New Adventures.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New ‘Sleeping Beauty,’ Courtesy of Matthew Bourne', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T15:32:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02b1f890-53dc-5e02-a489-9d5238502a8f', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02b1f890-53dc-5e02-a489-9d5238502a8f'}, {'abstract': 'The mascot for the Richmond Flying Squirrels is making the most of his brief trip to St. Louis despite the rainout.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/someone-left-a-squirrel-out-in-the-rain/', 'snippet': 'The mascot for the Richmond Flying Squirrels is making the most of his brief trip to St. Louis despite the rainout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mike Tanier will provide Bats with updates on less than important developments from the World Series.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Someone Left a Squirrel Out in the Rain', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisk, Carlton', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgan, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Reds', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T15:35:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Tanier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0636cbd-ca14-5150-8214-8cb7334e50b0', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0636cbd-ca14-5150-8214-8cb7334e50b0'}, {'abstract': 'California’s promise to pay to clean up the Imperial Valley’s Salton Sea, once called “an environmental Chernobyl,” still faces a legal challenge. If the pledge is invalidated,  the state’s biggest water sale could also be nullified.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/did-california-overreach-in-promising-to-help-the-salton-sea/', 'snippet': 'California’s promise to pay to clean up the Imperial Valley’s Salton Sea, once called “an environmental Chernobyl,” still faces a legal challenge. If the pledge is invalidated,  the state’s biggest water sale could also be nullified.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the joys of reporting is the serendipitous encounter, the fascinating digression. It was farmers I hoped to talk to when I visited the Imperial Valley this summer for my recent article about farmers who leave fields fallow and earn money for sending the water saved to San Diego.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Did California Overreach in Promising to Help the Salton Sea?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado River', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Diego (Calif)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T15:36:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b676660-6293-5e7c-9913-94a4ac8d8027', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b676660-6293-5e7c-9913-94a4ac8d8027'}, {'abstract': 'Microsoft and Yahoo are the latest companies to join the effort to equalize the cost of health benefits for employees with same-sex partners.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/microsoft-and-yahoo-equalize-health-benefits-for-gay-employees/', 'snippet': 'Microsoft and Yahoo are the latest companies to join the effort to equalize the cost of health benefits for employees with same-sex partners.', 'lead_paragraph': ' With open enrollment season in full swing, several big companies have said that they would begin to reimburse gay employees for the extra taxes they pay on health insurance for their significant others. Now, two more technology giants, Microsoft and Yahoo, have decided to join in, starting Jan. 1.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Microsoft and Yahoo Equalize Health Benefits for Gay Employees', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T15:39:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7a96803-4e37-571e-93bc-c9a622d6511e', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7a96803-4e37-571e-93bc-c9a622d6511e'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook plans to announce creation of a nonprofit foundation to run the Open Compute Project, an effort to encourage collaboration among technology giants on building low-cost computing centers.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/facebook-led-consortium-plans-to-remake-big-computing/', 'snippet': 'Facebook plans to announce creation of a nonprofit foundation to run the Open Compute Project, an effort to encourage collaboration among technology giants on building low-cost computing centers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A consortium of technology heavyweights led by Facebook wants to fill the world with enormous low-cost computing centers, using the same collaborative techniques that created an explosion of software development over the past decade. In the process, they may also outmaneuver Google.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook-Led Consortium Plans to Remake Big Computing', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bechtolsheim, Andreas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T15:41:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0413a7c2-179b-5ee1-a96a-f4e8f3bced36', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0413a7c2-179b-5ee1-a96a-f4e8f3bced36'}, {'abstract': 'I’ve never really paid the sort of attention I suppose I should have to arguments about Shakespeare’s identity.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/theater-talkback-who-wrote-shakespeare-who-cares/', 'snippet': 'I’ve never really paid the sort of attention I suppose I should have to arguments about Shakespeare’s identity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'May I make a confession? And I realize that this may be regarded as a heresy by the members of my tribe, by which I mean those of us who were and always shall be nerdy English majors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: Who Wrote Shakespeare? Who Cares?', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shakespeare Birthplace Trust', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T15:42:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbc3c943-f69c-57f2-b75c-030e2cee5286', 'word_count': 1463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbc3c943-f69c-57f2-b75c-030e2cee5286'}, {'abstract': 'Exploring corn country, energy trends and ways to educate that foster a durable culture meshing innovation and resilience.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/exploring-corn-energ-and-humanitys-growth-spurt/', 'snippet': 'Exploring corn country, energy trends and ways to educate that foster a durable culture meshing innovation and resilience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been on the road, learning about damaging and sustainable agricultural methods (and a big corn-to-ethanol plant) in Iowa, meeting with hundreds of science-oriented high school students in Houston to discuss energy and innovation and speaking about how new opportunities for globally sharing and shaping insights and information can be a prime route toward sustaining human progress on a finite planet (and on a tight budget).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exploring Corn, Energy and Humanity’s Growth Spurt', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Secondary)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T15:43:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f300051a-4b5e-5ce8-9fcd-08e620dd5735', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f300051a-4b5e-5ce8-9fcd-08e620dd5735'}, {'abstract': 'Entering the new Buddh International Circuit outside New Delhi, scene of the F1 race this weekend, felt like coming into a different country.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/a-passage-to-the-buddh-circuit-in-india/', 'snippet': 'Entering the new Buddh International Circuit outside New Delhi, scene of the F1 race this weekend, felt like coming into a different country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI – Since Tuesday I have been on a series of airplanes, taxis, metros, commuter trains and have walked through garbage heaps and dark unknown alleys in parts of the world I never dreamed existed. On the final leg of the trip Thursday morning I took a strange, motorized rickshaw from Noida City Center to the Buddh International Circuit outside New Delhi.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Passage to the Buddh Circuit in India', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumacher, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T15:47:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d56e096-75e9-5c10-b6c5-8c00a4cd0d80', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d56e096-75e9-5c10-b6c5-8c00a4cd0d80'}, {'abstract': 'Entering the new Buddh International Circuit outside New Delhi, scene of the F1 race this weekend, felt like coming into a different country.', 'web_url': 'https://formulaone.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/a-passage-to-the-buddh-circuit-in-india/', 'snippet': 'Entering the new Buddh Internati