 in his attic after winning it in a fan appreciation lottery.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/islanders-1993-division-playoff-banner-lives-in-a-fans-attic/', 'snippet': 'Richard Vollmer, a longtime season ticket holder, keeps the Islanders’ 1993 playoff banner in his attic after winning it in a fan appreciation lottery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the second intermission of an Islanders Fan Appreciation game back in 1994, Richard Vollmer was in his seat, keeping an eye on his children while flipping through the latest issue of The Hockey News. He heard the public address announcer at Nassau Coliseum say his seat’s section, 336, as the Islanders were presenting prizes to thank fans for another season of support.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Islanders’ 1993 Division Playoff Banner Lives in a Fan’s Attic', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Islanders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T16:33:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Botta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf72f131-d1c3-5e4a-985f-8a2e667cbb06', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf72f131-d1c3-5e4a-985f-8a2e667cbb06'}, {'abstract': 'As long as movements to expand or strengthen conventional arm registers and counter-proliferation protocols lack traction or are thwarted, 107-millimeter rockets are likely to be fired at whoever tries to hold territory in Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nyt