t from a year ago.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/evercore-profit-slumps-49/', 'snippet': 'In the third quarter, the advisory firm posted a profit of $19.7 million, or 46 cents per share, up 35 percent from a year ago.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:13 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Evercore Profit Climbs 35%', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Evercore Partners Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T16:45:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a499266b-a8b6-593c-934b-76f58e07a156', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a499266b-a8b6-593c-934b-76f58e07a156'}, {'abstract': 'It’s Reaganism for the rich, Mondale-ism for the middle class.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/the-flat-tax-fantasy/', 'snippet': 'It’s Reaganism for the rich, Mondale-ism for the middle class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I agree with most everything in John Podhoretz’s dyspeptic assessment of the Republican field, but I balked at this part:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Flat Tax Fantasy', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T16:46:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b94b228-8892-57e8-9d98-560f006b80f4', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b94b228-8892-57e8-9d98-560f006b80f4'}, {'abstract': 'A new book predicts that an emphasis on efficiency and real costs will make renewable energy the inevitable replacement for fossil fuels.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/fossil-fuels-as-the-whale-oil-of-the-future/', 'snippet': 'A new book predicts that an emphasis on efficiency and real costs will make renewable energy the inevitable replacement for fossil fuels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amory B. Lovins, the longtime efficiency guru, has a new book out that analyzes the possibility of converting the nation to almost total reliance on renewable sources of energy. The conclusions may not win instant acceptance, but it is certainly in the running for the best-blurbed energy book of the year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fossil Fuels as the Whale Oil of the Future', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T16:53:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b0e7121-51e1-5032-8840-1eb3f78db8e4', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b0e7121-51e1-5032-8840-1eb3f78db8e4'}, {'abstract': '11 were charged in a massive fraud scheme in which hundreds of Long Island Rail Road workers made false disability pension claims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/10/28/nyregion/28lirr-complaint-doc.html', 'snippet': '11 were charged in a massive fraud scheme in which hundreds of Long Island Rail Road workers made false disability pension claims.', 'lead_paragraph': '11 were charged in a massive fraud scheme in which hundreds of Long Island Rail Road workers made false disability pension claims.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'L.I.R.R. Retirement Disability Fraud Complaint', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Long Island Rail Road Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T16:53:02+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/d4b8c1ad-3cea-5e6b-af1e-e42b50ab4f5e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/d4b8c1ad-3cea-5e6b-af1e-e42b50ab4f5e'}, {'abstract': 'Few understand how much we spend on health care, how much we need to spend to provide quality care, and the difference between the two.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/spending-more-doesnt-make-us-healthier/', 'snippet': 'Few understand how much we spend on health care, how much we need to spend to provide quality care, and the difference between the two.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you have heard it once, you have heard it hundreds of times. “The United States spends too much on health care.” This is not a partisan point. You can hear this from Republicans as well as Democrats. “We know that our families, our economy and our nation itself will not succeed in the 21st century if we continue to be held down by the weight of rapidly rising health care costs,” President Obama said in 2009. Representative Paul D. Ryan, Republican of Wisconsin, agrees: “There is no serious dispute — on either side of the aisle.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spending More Doesn’t Make Us Healthier', 'kicker': 'Ezekiel J. Emanuel', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T16:53:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ezekiel J. Emanuel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ezekiel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Emanuel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4876d8bc-62bd-55b0-a5ff-3a5bbad8b290', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4876d8bc-62bd-55b0-a5ff-3a5bbad8b290'}, {'abstract': 'The president of Ukraine has been accused of plagiarizing sections of his new English-language book from several sources, including a college essay.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/ukraines-president-accused-of-plagiarism/', 'snippet': 'The president of Ukraine has been accused of plagiarizing sections of his new English-language book from several sources, including a college essay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The publisher of a new English-language book on Ukraine describes it as “a practical guide for prospective investors!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ukraine’s President Accused of Plagiarism', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 