, 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T16:57:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36a9c44a-c066-5151-b0a3-9ee705fdd13d', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36a9c44a-c066-5151-b0a3-9ee705fdd13d'}, {'abstract': 'New technology has brought new challenges for parents trying to childproof their home for babies, toddlers and small children.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/new-rules-for-childproofing-a-home/', 'snippet': 'New technology has brought new challenges for parents trying to childproof their home for babies, toddlers and small children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you thought childproofing was about cabinet locks and baby monitors, think again. New technology has brought new challenges for parents trying to childproof their home for babies, toddlers and small children. The latest Home & Garden report offers practical, informative advice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Rules for Childproofing a Home', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T17:07:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6b1e41d-4c91-557e-950f-8258cd738ec5', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6b1e41d-4c91-557e-950f-8258cd738ec5'}, {'abstract': 'The estimated sale price of one cover, showing the Penguin fleeing Batman and Robin, is $300,000.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/holy-cash-cow-vintage-comics-covers-from-joker-creator-up-for-auction/', 'snippet': 'The estimated sale price of one cover, showing the Penguin fleeing Batman and Robin, is $300,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next month, Heritage Auctions will put on the block several pieces of Batman memorabilia that will entice fans with deep pockets. Collectors who are interested in original art will have their eye on three vintage covers from the collection of Jerry Robinson,  the comic book artist who created the Joker. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holy (Cash) Cow! Vintage Comics Covers From Joker Creator Up for Auction', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Novack, Ben Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Jerry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T17:10:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73a218d7-0176-5d05-b91b-9c78534691dc', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73a218d7-0176-5d05-b91b-9c78534691dc'}, {'abstract': 'The illustrator Chris Gall has blended his strangely transporting tableaus into the first cocktail book from the Manhattan speakeasy PDT.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/booze-cruise/', 'snippet': 'The illustrator Chris Gall has blended his strangely transporting tableaus into the first cocktail book from the Manhattan speakeasy PDT.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chris Gall, the Arizona illustrator most famous in New York for his flying fish posters inside M.T.A. subway cars, has blended his strangely transporting tableaus into the first cocktail book from the Manhattan speakeasy PDT. (That’s the place you enter through a phone booth inside a hot-dog joint.) Written by Jim Meehan, “The PDT Cocktail Book” (Sterling Epicure, $25) also includes contributions from the bar’s resident mixologists: Brian Shebairo’s Lake George recipe — Jameson, Glenlivet, Drambuie and lemon juice — is stiff enough to spell vacation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Booze Cruise', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T17:15:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61a2b9cb-8884-55c6-b8b4-fe8bafd043bf', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61a2b9cb-8884-55c6-b8b4-fe8bafd043bf'}, {'abstract': 'The former pastry chef at Daniel is opening a shop in SoHo.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/dominique-ansel-not-your-everyday-bakery/', 'snippet': 'The former pastry chef at Daniel is opening a shop in SoHo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dominique Ansel, who was the pastry chef at Daniel for six years and worked at Fauchon in Paris before that, is opening his own pastry shop and café on Wednesday. And in addition to croissants, macarons and éclairs, he is baking a few specialties that are not everyday indulgences in New York. Among them are a tall, fluted cake, the gâteau battu, which comes from Mr. Ansel’s native Picardy, northeast of Paris, and is halfway between brioche and pound cake but lighter than either one. He sells the whole cake and slices, excellent with soft butter and jam. He is also baking kouign amann, a flaky, crispy little Breton pastry, which a few American chefs are starting to feature on their menus. And his take on the Paris-Brest, a filled ring of cream puff pastry, is called Paris-New York and has caramel, peanuts and chocolate. His menu also includes savory items like sandwiches, quiches, soups and salads. The narrow space with an open kitchen has a few seats and a marble counter, an all-weather greenhouse for seating in the back, and a garden.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dominique Ansel, Not Your Everyday Bakery', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T17:20:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ae39710-3922-5b83-a88f-fcb386386fa7', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ae39710-3922-5b83-a88f-fcb386386fa7'}, {'abstract': 'The new app AirCassette recreates classic blank tapes on your iPhone’s display when you listen to your iTunes library.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/the-mixtape-is-back/', 'snippet': 'The new app AirCassette recreates classic blank tapes on your iPhone’s display when you listen to your iTunes library.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They say that fashion is cyclical. The same goes for technology. Sure, most cellphones are the epitome of trendiness, but just think how cool you’ll be if you hark back to the 1980s with AirCassette, an app that turns your iPhone into a cassette player.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mixtape Is Back!', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T17:21:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Biggs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Biggs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3ce68df-b399-53a2-b1ed-fbfe9b8bc803', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3ce68df-b399-53a2-b1ed-fbfe9b8bc803'}, {'abstract': 'In voting to repeal a withholding requ