n': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56c27a33-c176-55fb-a714-e938361e6050', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56c27a33-c176-55fb-a714-e938361e6050'}, {'abstract': 'This week: interviews with Dee Dee of Dum Dum Girls and Judy Collins.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/popcast-interviews-with-dum-dum-girls-and-judy-collins/', 'snippet': 'This week: interviews with Dee Dee of Dum Dum Girls and Judy Collins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week on Popcast, we hear from a young garage pop songwriter and an eminent singer from folk’s golden age, each with acclaimed new projects this fall.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Popcast: Interviews with Dum Dum Girls and Judy Collins', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T17:48:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Egner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e9690c9-281b-5269-8c35-ea25c571341c', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e9690c9-281b-5269-8c35-ea25c571341c'}, {'abstract': 'When girls ditch you as soon as your roommate walks in, it’s time to fly solo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/fashion/time-to-fly-solo-social-qs.html', 'snippet': 'When girls ditch you as soon as your roommate walks in, it’s time to fly solo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am a junior in college and have an amazing relationship with my roommate. We hang out together all the time, and I love him like a brother. Trouble is, he’s really good looking, and as soon as girls see him, they ditch me. I can be talking to a woman all night (and getting along really well), but as soon as he appears, she loses interest in me. I don’t think he’s doing it intentionally, but it’s starting to get me down. What should I do? ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Time to Fly Solo', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time to Fly Solo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T17:53:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ba8fec3-dc04-5afe-93ce-a4217a63fa90', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ba8fec3-dc04-5afe-93ce-a4217a63fa90'}, {'abstract': 'Is this year of late-blooming teams in the N.F.L.? Kansas City, Philadelphia and Jacksonville make a case for it.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/the-attack-of-the-n-f-l-s-late-bloomers/', 'snippet': 'Is this year of late-blooming teams in the N.F.L.? Kansas City, Philadelphia and Jacksonville make a case for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For some, Jacksonville’s shocking victory over Baltimore on Monday night proved the N.F.L. adage that any team can be beaten. The Jaguars had lost eight of nine games dating to last season, and the Ravens were off to one of the fastest starts in the league, with blowout victories over Pittsburgh, the Jets and Houston.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Attack of the N.F.L.’s Late Bloomers', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jacksonville Jaguars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Chiefs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 