een police officers began surrendering to the authorities in the Bronx at about midnight on Thursday to face criminal charges after a long-running grand jury investigation into the widespread practice of fixing traffic tickets for colleagues, family members and friends, people with knowledge of the matter said. A 16th officer was arrested earlier Thursday night.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/nyregion/28tickets/28tickets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 231, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/28/nyregion/28tickets/28tickets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 231}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/nyregion/28tickets/28tickets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Authorities Move to Charge 16 Officers After Widespread Ticket-Fixing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Authorities Move to Charge 16 Officers After Widespread Ticket-Fixing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T21:05:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By William K. Rashbaum and Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28250855-9d55-555e-9719-c1283b38ccd3', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28250855-9d55-555e-9719-c1283b38ccd3'}, {'abstract': 'Gela Babluani’s American remake of his prizewinning film, “13,” has its share of stars, including Sam Riley, Curtis Jackson, Mickey Rourke, Jason Statham and Michael Shannon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/movies/13-with-sam-riley-and-jason-statham-review.html', 'snippet': 'Gela Babluani’s American remake of his prizewinning film, “13,” has its share of stars, including Sam Riley, Curtis Jackson, Mickey Rourke, Jason Statham and Michael Shannon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vince Ferro (Sam Riley), the protagonist of the Georgian director Gela Babluani’s “13,” is a part-time electrician whose family may have to sell its home in Ohio to pay his father’s medical bills. While on the job, he overhears his employer discussing a mysterious get-rich-quick scheme. After his boss dies of a drug overdose, Vince picks up an envelope addressed to the dead man and, following the instructions, travels to Chicago, where he is whisked by train and car to a rural mansion. There he finds himself an involuntary player in a Russian roulette tournament from which there is no escape.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/arts/28THIRTEEN_SPAN/THIRTEEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 306, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/28/arts/28THIRTEEN_SPAN/THIRTEEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 306}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'