at least on the East Coast) it stretched into early Friday morning. The result was one of the wildest and most memorable World Series games ever played, a 10-9 extra-inning victory for the St. Louis Cardinals that will force the first Game 7 of a World Series since 2002.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World Series: Cardinals Force a Game 7', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T21:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c487829-3d4c-5ab8-bc47-c690453b32ca', 'word_count': 4007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c487829-3d4c-5ab8-bc47-c690453b32ca'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. McNally is the president and chief executive of Skanska USA, which specializes in civil, infrastructure and commercial developments, and building construction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/realestate/michael-f-mcnally.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. McNally is the president and chief executive of Skanska USA, which specializes in civil, infrastructure and commercial developments, and building construction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mr. McNally, 56, is the president and chief executive of Skanska USA, which specializes in civil, infrastructure and commercial developments, and building construction.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print