agraph': ' The moderate Islamist party Ennahda won a 41 percent plurality in Tunisia’s first free election, election officials said Thursday. Ennahda was the only Islamic or religious party competing in the vote on Sunday, the first election of the Arab Spring, meaning that a majority of Tunisians cast their votes for secular parties. Winning 90 of 217 seats in the constituent assembly, Ennahda will lead the formation of a new coalition government and name its prime minister, and it will also have the loudest voice in the assembly as it writes a new constitution. The runner-up, the liberal Congress for the Republic, founded by the veteran human rights advocate Moncef Marzouki, will have 30 seats. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tunisia: Islamist Party Wins Vote', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tunisia: Islamist Party Wins Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nahda Party, Al- (Tunisia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-27T23:35:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a703faf7-42dd-578d-9232-b5d7a8bc8b85', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a703faf7-42dd-578d-9232-b5d7a8bc8b85'}, {'abstract': 'In “God’s Land,” by Preston Miller, a commune of Taiwanese immigrants waits for a spaceship to descend and deliver it to the promised land.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/movies/gods-land-directed-by-preston-miller-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “God’s Land,” by Preston Miller, a commune of Taiwanese immigrants waits for a spaceship to descend and deliver it to the promised land.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been a season of cults and extreme religious visions: Vera Farmiga wrestles with faith in “Higher Ground,” and Elizabeth Olsen escapes a charismatic leader’s grip in “Martha Marcy May Marlene.” In Preston Miller’s dramedy “God’s Land,” a commune of Taiwanese immigrants in Garland, Tex., waits for a spaceship to descend and deliver it to the promised land. Or dimension, rather.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/movies/28RDP_GODS/28RDP_GODS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/28/movies/28RDP_GODS/28RDP_GODS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/movies/28RDP_GODS/28RDP_GODS-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/movies/28RDP_GODS/28RDP_GODS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/28/movies/28RDP_GODS/28RDP_GODS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': 