the immigration law is a first step in a larger strategy to topple a 29-year-old Supreme Court ruling that all children in the United States are guaranteed an education.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/us/alabama-immigration-laws-critics-question-target.html', 'snippet': 'The schools provision of the immigration law is a first step in a larger strategy to topple a 29-year-old Supreme Court ruling that all children in the United States are guaranteed an education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALABASTER, Ala. — The champions of Alabama’s far-reaching immigration law have said that it is intended to drive illegal immigrants from the state by making every aspect of their life difficult. But they have taken a very different tone when it comes to the part of the law concerning schools.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/us/SUB-ALABAMA-1/SUB-ALABAMA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/28/us/SUB-ALABAMA-1/SUB-ALABAMA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/us/SUB-ALABAMA-1/SUB-ALABAMA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/us/SUB-ALABAMA-1/SUB-ALABAMA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/28/us/SUB-ALABAMA-1/SUB-ALABAMA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Critics See ‘Chilling Effect’ in Alabama Immigration Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker':