sease, which has felled up to 95 percent of the cypress trees in some timber plantations and forests across the globe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/us/seiridium-fungal-killer-of-cypresses-worldwide-is-traced-to-california.html', 'snippet': 'The fungus, Seiridium, causes cypress canker disease, which has felled up to 95 percent of the cypress trees in some timber plantations and forests across the globe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the last five years, scientists have been on the trail of a fungus that has caused a deadly epidemic in the world’s forests. The fungus, Seiridium, causes cypress canker disease, which has felled up to 95 percent of the cypress trees — a family that includes junipers — growing in some timber plantations and forests across the globe.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fungal Killer of Cypresses Originated in California', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fungal Killer Of Cypresses Originated In California', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fungi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Monterey (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T00:17:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Upton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Upton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19a15dbf-122f-5c67-b255-5af97e6e94f3', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19a15dbf-122f-5c67-b255-5af97e6e94f3'}, {'abstract': 'There are 13 televised debates scheduled throug