, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T01:27:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6e450d6-d120-524a-92d6-53576fa32040', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6e450d6-d120-524a-92d6-53576fa32040'}, {'abstract': 'An extreme ballot measure in Mississippi, which would define a fertilized human egg as a “person,” would destroy women’s reproductive rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/opinion/the-personhood-initiative.html', 'snippet': 'An extreme ballot measure in Mississippi, which would define a fertilized human egg as a “person,” would destroy women’s reproductive rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A ballot measure going before voters in Mississippi on Nov. 8 would define the term “person” in the State Constitution to include fertilized human eggs and grant to fertilized eggs the legal rights and protections that apply to people. It is among the most extreme assaults in the push to end women’s reproductive rights. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The ‘Personhood’ Initiative', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The &#8216;Personhood&#8217; Initiative', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reproduction (Biological)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T01:31:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6b8c871-e987-5124-ae09-d906a5011070', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6b8c871-e987-5124-ae09-d906a5011070'}, {'abstract': 'With food aid to Somalia blocked by Islamist militants, aids groups are using vouchers to help some refugees get food to survive.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/in-famine-vouchers-can-be-tickets-to-survival/', 'snippet': 'With food aid to Somalia blocked by Islamist militants, aids groups are using vouchers to help some refugees get food to survive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The town of Dhobley, Somalia, sits at the gateway of hell.\xa0 Just west of Dhobley is the border with Kenya, and the road to Dadaab, which hosts a giant complex of refugee camps; Dhobley has become the last stop in Somalia for a growing stream of desperate, starving people in flight from famine.\xa0 In Dhobley, as well, drought has ruined crops and felled cows.\xa0\xa0 There is no government to help.\xa0 The town is a battleground; control of Dhobley has teetered between the Shabaab Islamist militant group and government forces.\xa0 Shabaab has blocked food aid from entering Dhobley and burned a food truck, but soldiers from all sides have stolen food meant for the destitute.\xa0\xa0 The usual street life of an African village — children playing, women laughing together — has vanished.\xa0\xa0 Gunshots are a constant background noise — “like birds singing,” said Tracy Stover, the emergency coordinator in Dadaab for the humanitarian group World Concern.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Famine, Vouchers Can Be Tickets to Survival', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Aid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vouchers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T01:35:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd6cbcab-ed95-5723-89c3-79b3ffd418bb', 'word_count': 1494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd6cbcab-ed95-5723-89c3-79b3ffd418bb'}, {'abstract': 'Why did the Lincoln administration embrace the suspension of habeas corpus?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/27/mr-sewards-little-bell/', 'snippet': 'Why did the Lincoln administration embrace the suspension of habeas corpus?', 'lead_paragraph': '“My Lord, I can touch a bell on my right hand, and order the arrest of a citizen in Ohio. I can touch the bell again, and order the arrest of a citizen in New York. Can the Queen of England, in her dominions, do as much?” William Henry Seward’s boast to Lord Lyons, Britain’s envoy to the United States for much of the Civil War — and a diplomat with whom Lincoln’s secretary of state enjoyed an often fractious relationship — is almost certainly an apocryphal invention of administration critics. But it nevertheless illustrates a higher truth: Seward’s early and aggressive involvement with the wartime suspension of the writ of habeas corpus, one of the most controversial actions of the Lincoln administration. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Seward’s Little Bell', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T01:35:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Beard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69b72818-b0fd-5f65-8ac1-b687f8213023', 'word_count': 1631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69b72818-b0fd-5f65-8ac1-b687f8213023'}, {'abstract': 'The conviction of a safety director at the Upper Big Branch mine should give momentum to Congress to pass a raft of needed safety reforms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/opinion/some-justice-at-upper-big-branch.html', 'snippet': 'The conviction of a safety director at the Upper Big Branch mine should give momentum to Congress to pass a raft of needed safety reforms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The safety director at the Upper Big Branch mine in West Virginia, where 29 miners were killed last year, has been convicted of lying to federal investigators and ordering the destruction of records on hazardous conditions. The verdict should add needed momentum to federal and state investigations into the mine’s owner at the time, Massey Energy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Justice at Upper Big Branch', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some Justice at Upper Big Branch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massey Energy Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Upper Big Branch Mine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T01:39:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0882e18c-27e4-53b4-89db-7530b3770de5', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0882e18c-27e4-53b4-89db-7530b3770de5'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, speaking to a gay rights group, called for legalization of same-sex marriage in every state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/nyregion/gov-andrew-m-cuomo-calls-for-same-sex-marriage-in-all-states.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, speaking to a gay rights group, called for legalization of same-sex marriage in every state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, hailed as a hero at a gala dinner for the state’s largest gay rights group, issued a passionate plea on Thursday for other states to follow New York’s lead and allow gay couples to wed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Urges States to Allow Gay Marriage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo Urges States to Allow Gay Marriage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Empire State Pri