ess Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Louise Story and Julie Creswell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Louise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Story', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Creswell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77461fab-1ac9-579e-988f-de97988cbddd', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77461fab-1ac9-579e-988f-de97988cbddd'}, {'abstract': 'Alfredo Astiz and 11 other former military and police officers in Argentina have been sentenced to life in prison for crimes committed during the 1976-83 military dictatorship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/world/americas/argentina-12-given-life-sentences-for-crimes-during-dictatorship.html', 'snippet': 'Alfredo Astiz and 11 other former military and police officers in Argentina have been sentenced to life in prison for crimes committed during the 1976-83 military dictatorship.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Alfredo Astiz and 11 other former military and police officers have been sentenced to life in prison for crimes committed during the 1976-83 military dictatorship, a court announced Wednesday. Mr. Astiz, 59, nicknamed the “Blond Angel of Death,” was convicted for his role in executing human rights activists in 1977; they were tortured at the Navy Mechanics School, known as ESMA, and then dropped from navy airplanes into the South Atlantic. His victims included several founders of the Mothers of the Plaza de Mayo human rights group and two French nuns, the court found. Four other defendants received sentences of 18 to 25 years in prison. About 5,000 detainees passed through ESMA during the dictatorship, of whom more than 90 percent were killed, according to the National Commission on the Disappearance of Persons. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentina: 12 Given Life Sentences for Crimes During Dictatorship', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Argentina: 12 Given Life Sentences For Crimes During Dictatorship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Astiz, Alfredo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Navy Mechanics School', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T02:44:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexei Barrionuevo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barrionuevo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b54bfd34-0afa-5efd-ba89-c09d1c4fa00f', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b54bfd34-0afa-5efd-ba89-c09d1c4fa00f'}, {'abstract': 'Delaware’s attorney general said Merscorp’s mortgage registry database obscured data and made it difficult for homeowners to fight foreclosures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/business/delaware-suit-accuses-merscorp-of-deception-in-mortgage-registry.html', 'snippet': 'Delaware’s attorney general said Merscorp’s mortgage registry database obscured data and made it difficult for homeowners to fight foreclosures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Delaware’s attorney general on Thursday accused Merscorp, which operates a national mortgage registry used by banks, of deceptive practices that hide information from borrowers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Merscorp Faces Deception Suit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Merscorp Faces Deception Suit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delaware', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mortgage Electronic Registration Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T02:46:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d820289d-01d6-56ec-9fcb-3be592cd5e54', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d820289d-01d6-56ec-9fcb-3be592cd5e54'}, {'abstract': 'The sheriff of Cook County, Ill., is hoping to use DNA to identify eight victims of the serial killer John Wayne Gacy, more than 30 years after their deaths.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/us/sheriff-hopes-to-identify-john-wayne-gacy-victims-using-dna.html', 'snippet': 'The sheriff of Cook County, Ill., is hoping to use DNA to identify eight victims of the serial killer John Wayne Gacy, more than 30 years after their deaths.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — Again and again, DNA evidence has emerged as a new answer to old crimes — long-awaited proof that a suspect did or, as in the most celebrated cases, did not commit a crime. But DNA matching also has a compelling role for the victims of crimes, which is why Thomas J. Dart, the sheriff of Cook County, is suddenly hopeful for revelations in the case of John Wayne Gacy, whose notorious serial killings took place more than 30 years ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/us/GACY-1/GACY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/28/us/GACY-1/GACY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/us/GACY-1/GACY-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/us/GACY-1/GACY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/28/us/GACY-1/GACY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Effort in Illinois to Use DNA to Identify a Serial Killer’s Victims', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Effort in Illinois To Use DNA to Identify A Serial Killer’s Victims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cook County (Ill)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Serial Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gacy, John Wayne Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T02:48:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e70f6e3-0891-587d-ad65-a748cf4a4b81', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e70f6e3-0891-587d-ad65-a748cf4a4b81'}, {'abstract': 'Hugues-Denver Akassy, on trial in Manhattan for charges including stalking and rape against five women, told jurors his side of the story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/nyregion/hugues-denver-akassy-charged-with-rape-testifies.html', 'snippet': 'Hugues-Denver Akassy, on trial in Manhattan for charges including stalking and rape against five women, told jurors his side of the story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While some people say “having sex,” he says “making love.” He speaks with a heavy French accent and has strong facial features. When recounting stories, he often purses his lips as if offering an air kiss, giggles and stares into the distance, then bows his head and flicks his eyebrows in a pose of seduction.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Charged With Rape Testifies About His Encounters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Charged With Rape Testifies About His Encounters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akassy, Hugues-Denver', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T02:52:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ee45b92-5eed-5f75-93f7-5b8aa00654bf', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ee45b92-5eed-5f75-93f7-5b8aa00654bf'}, {'abstract': 'Readers over 70, have you taken stock of your life so far? Well, please write it down and tell us what you’ve learned so it can be shared with younger generations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/opinion/brooks-the-life-report.html', 'snippet': 'Readers over 70, have you taken stock of your life so far? Well, please write it down and tell us what you’ve learned so it can be shared with younger generations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are over 70, I’d like to ask for a gift. I’d like you to write a brief report on your life so far, an evaluation of what you did well, of what you did not so well and what you learned along the way. You can write this as a brief essay or divide your life into categories — career, family, faith, community, and self-knowledge — and give yourself a grade in each area.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'th