ry response against North Korea if there is another provocation in the region from North Korean leaders.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/world/28military-image/28military-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/world/28military-image/28military-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/29/world/28military-image/28military-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Panetta Joins South Korea in Warning to North', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panetta Joins South Korean Defense Minister in Warning North', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Kwan-jin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T06:18:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Bumiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bumiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/197ad4bb-ff6f-5e22-8a1b-1c0c56bb721d', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/197ad4bb-ff6f-5e22-8a1b-1c0c56bb721d'}, {'abstract': 'With a guess on a changeup, the local kid from the St. Louis suburb of Wildwood earned a lasting place in Cardinals history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/sports/baseball/freese-earns-a-place-in-cardinals-history.html', 'snippet': 'With a guess on a changeup, the local kid from the St. Louis suburb of Wildwood earned a lasting place in Cardinals history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — He guessed right on a changeup, and once the ball left David Freese’s bat, he saw everything. The soaring drive deep to center field. Josh Hamilton chasing it for a few steps, then giving up. And a solitary usher in the bleachers trying to stop joyous St. Louis Cardinals fans from jumping onto the grassy batter’s eye in pursuit of Freese’s game-winning home run.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Freese Earns a Place in Cardinals History', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Freese Is Most Valuable, and Most Improbable', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freese, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T06:57:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/088686e0-9880-5e64-b2f1-2420c2691ace', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/088686e0-9880-5e64-b2f1-2420c2691ace'}, {'abstract': 'A new policy banning meat, poultry and fish products raises ire in Goa.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/goans-threaten-jet-airways-boycott/', 'snippet': 'A new policy banning meat, poultry and fish products raises ire in Goa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Goa’s ever-active Internet discussion groups have been buzzing in recent days with complaints about a new Jet Airways policy banning passengers from carrying meat, fish and poultry products on both domestic and international flights even in their checked-in luggage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goans Threaten Jet Airways Boycott', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetarianism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jet Airways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Goa (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T07:52:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Naresh Fernandes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Naresh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f772a563-ee2a-5b06-a358-1d2781c91867', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f772a563-ee2a-5b06-a358-1d2781c91867'}, {'abstract': 'On Oct. 28, 1886, President Grover Cleveland dedicated the Statue of Liberty, a gift from France, in New York Harbor.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/oct-28-1886-statue-of-liberty-unveiled/', 'snippet': 'On Oct. 28, 1886, President Grover Cleveland dedicated the Statue of Liberty, a gift from France, in New York Harbor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Oct. 28, 1886, President Grover Cleveland dedicated the Statue of Liberty, a gift from France, in New York Harbor. In that day’s edition, The New York Times described the building excitement for the ceremony: “All day yesterday people came to the city in droves to participate in to-day’s celebration. Extra heavily loaded trains, much behind schedule time, were the rule on every railroad entering the city. Every hotel was crowded to its utmost capacity last night, and there was hardly one of the better known hotels which did not have to turn away hundreds of would be guests.”The ceremony included speeches by the president and famed French engineer Ferdinand de Lesseps, among others, as well as music and gun salvo. The finale? The statue’s designer, Frederic-Auguste Bartholdi, who was perched in the statue’s torch, pulled a rope removing a large French flag from the front of the statue, revealing Lady Liberty’s face to the crowd.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oct. 28, 1886 | Statue of Liberty Is Unveiled', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T08:07:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a14c2224-43b8-5c68-9c02-9a1a92e75b4f', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a14c2224-43b8-5c68-9c02-9a1a92e75b4f'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/news-quiz-oct-28-2011/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | Oct. 28, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T08:16:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Frasier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frasier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/110a2081-11bb-536d-b976-fc032424e38f', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/110a2081-11bb-536d-b976-fc032424e38f'}, {'abstract': 'To cope with the stress of conflict photography, Guillermo Cervera dives into the surf to photograph the perfect wave. How an old hand at the sea says a farewell to arms every now and then.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/trading-war-for-waves/', 'snippet': 'To cope with the stress of conflict photography, Guillermo Cervera dives into the surf to photograph the perfect wave. How an old hand at the sea says a farewell to arms every now and then.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Guillermo Cervera knows there is a certain risk lurking behind each assignment. In Libya, it came from the attack that claimed the lives of Tim Hetherington and Chris Hondros, who were by his side when they were felled in Misurata. In Chad, it was from a brief — though harrowing — detention, where he was threatened with torture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trading War for Waves', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surfing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T09:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'perso