3'}, {'abstract': 'Two men with decades in baseball, Bud Selig, the game’s commissioner, and Bill DeWitt, the St. Louis Cardinals owner, celebrated the most thrilling contest of their lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/sports/baseball/for-dewitt-and-selig-the-most-thrilling-game-of-their-lives.html', 'snippet': 'Two men with decades in baseball, Bud Selig, the game’s commissioner, and Bill DeWitt, the St. Louis Cardinals owner, celebrated the most thrilling contest of their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS – The two men, both in their 70’s, with decades in baseball and a fortune to their names, huddled together in the runway outside the home clubhouse at Busch Stadium early Friday morning. They could have been caffeinated Little Leaguers at a pizza parlor, celebrating the most thrilling game of their lives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/29kepner-image2/29kepner-image2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/29kepner-image2/29kepner-image2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/29kepner-image2/29kepner-image2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/29kepner-image2/29kepner-image2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/29kepner-image2/29kepner-image2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For DeWitt and Selig, the Game of a Lifetime', 'kicker': 'On Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For DeWitt and Selig, the Most Thrilling Game of Their Lives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Selig, Bud', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeWitt, Bill Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T09:24:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef887b5d-626b-569a-9f71-d7bb32ac73b5', 'word_count': 1498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef887b5d-626b-569a-9f71-d7bb32ac73b5'}, {'abstract': 'Zhejiang Youngman Lotus Automobile and Pang Da Automobile Trade agreed to pay €100 million, or $140 million, just before the struggling Swedish automaker faced court action.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/business/global/chinese-carmakers-to-buy-saab-pulling-it-back-from-the-brink.html', 'snippet': 'Zhejiang Youngman Lotus Automobile and Pang Da Automobile Trade agreed to pay €100 million, or $140 million, just before the struggling Swedish automaker faced court action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Saab Automobile said Friday that it had won a reprieve from collapse after two Chinese carmakers agreed in principle to buy the ailing Swedish automaker just hours before it faced court action that could have led to its liquidation. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The