ay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shortz, Will', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T11:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Will Shortz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Will', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shortz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d960a80a-0d9c-5da8-a750-6e9ed7b58fcc', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d960a80a-0d9c-5da8-a750-6e9ed7b58fcc'}, {'abstract': 'The Pipeline fellows have decided to invest $105,000 in a for-profit, socially conscious company called PhilanTech.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/angel-investors-in-training-choose-an-investment/', 'snippet': 'The Pipeline fellows have decided to invest $105,000 in a for-profit, socially conscious company called PhilanTech.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since April, I’ve followed the progress of the first class of Pipeline Fellowship fellows, 10 women who learned how to become angel investors during a six-month program, and then chose a company to receive their pooled investment. When I last checked in with them, they had narrowed the field of possible companies to three — all of which were for-profit, woman-led, and socially conscious, as required by Pipeline.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Angel Investors-in-Training Choose an Investment', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T11:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2031c345-75f5-59ee-b2e7-00afc45731f5', 'word_count': 669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2031c345-75f5-59ee-b2e7-00afc45731f5'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney likes following the rules, explaining the rules and pointing out to others when they,  heaven forbid, break the rules.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/romney-seeks-order-in-chaos-of-campaign/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney likes following the rules, explaining the rules and pointing out to others when they,  heaven forbid, break the rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney likes rules.The former governor of Massachusetts likes following the rules, explaining the rules and pointing out to others when they, heaven forbid, break the rules. At the most recent Republican debate in Las Vegas, Mr. Romney inadvertently cast himself as the Enforcer when he tried mightily to ensure that every candidate received their allotted response time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Seeks Order in Chaos of Campaign', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T11:18:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cf8d3e9-3c3e-54ce-8b90-e9947d93f6b7', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cf8d3e9-3c3e-54ce-8b90-e9947d93f6b7'}, {'abstract': 'A house that produces more energy than it uses is a rarity in Russia, where enough energy is wasted each year to power all of France.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/active-house-upends-russian-energy-habits/', 'snippet': 'A house that produces more energy than it uses is a rarity in Russia, where enough energy is wasted each year to power all of France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent Saturday, a bus filled with local architects arrived at a field 12 miles southwest of Moscow. As a light snow began to fall, they made their way past a handful of model homes to a wooden A-frame whose spare, modern lines could be straight out of Dwell magazine. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Active House’ Upends Russian Energy Habits', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T11:22:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sally McGrane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sally', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddb26e9f-8103-5d92-8983-f6b85b42346d', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddb26e9f-8103-5d92-8983-f6b85b42346d'}, {'abstract': 'Golden Gate Capital, the West Coast private equity firm, has closed its latest fund at $3.5 billion, according to people briefed on the matter.', 'web_url': 'https: