r. Qaddafi maintains he is innocent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chief prosecutor of the International Criminal Court at The Hague said Friday that he had been in indirect contact with Seif al-Islam el-Qaddafi, the fugitive son of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi and his onetime heir apparent, about turning himself in to face trial before the court.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/world/28libya-image/28libya-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/29/world/28libya-image/28libya-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Qaddafi Son Maintains Innocence as Criminal Court Cites Indirect Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Criminal Court Cites Indirect Talks With Qaddafi Son', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Seif al-Islam el-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moreno-Ocampo, Luis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T12:59:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_