': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chalayan, Hussein', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crawford, Ilse', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parreno, Philippe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Somerset House', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T13:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ce07f74-b299-58e6-b6b9-b491b9ad8ef0', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ce07f74-b299-58e6-b6b9-b491b9ad8ef0'}, {'abstract': 'Beginning with the 2012 Breeders’ Cup, 2-year-olds will not be administered medication hours before they race for the first time in decades.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/goodbye-lasix-and-good-riddance/', 'snippet': 'Beginning with the 2012 Breeders’ Cup, 2-year-olds will not be administered medication hours before they race for the first time in decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beginning with the 2012 Breeders’ Cup, 2-year-olds will not be administered medication hours before they race for the first time in decades. The regulators of racing have seen the light from the horse and rider perspective. Extensive studies clearly indicate that drugs cause more trouble for racehorses and their riders than they alleviate. Lasix jurisdictions have significantly more breakdowns than jurisdictions where Lasix is not allowed. No prerace Lasix means no attending veterinarians with loaded syringes in the stall injecting the horses with drugs hours before they run. The dangerous and dubious charade of medicating racehorses before they compete is coming to a welcome end.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goodbye Lasix, and Good Riddance', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Breeders' Cup (Horse Race)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterinary Medicine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T13:14:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sid Gustafson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sid', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gustafson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55259b9f-a116-5804-b4bd-cb9b2889f193', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55259b9f-a116-5804-b4bd-cb9b2889f193'}, {'abstract': 'M. Michele Burns, the former chief executive of the human resource consulting firm Mercer, has been elected to Goldman’s board.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/goldman-adds-a-board-member/', 'snippet': 'M. Michele Burns, the former chief executive of the human resource consulting firm Mercer, has been elected to Goldman’s board.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The members of Goldman Sachs’s board of directors, who sit atop one of the highest perches on Wall Street, now number an even dozen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldman Adds a Board Member', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 2, 'major'