/interactive/abd0e91a-e91e-5ba2-930d-5213e101f127'}, {'abstract': 'The first in a new generation of  satellites will provide scientists with crucial data for charting climate change and warning of weather catastrophes.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/long-awaited-climate-satellite-lifts-off/', 'snippet': 'The first in a new generation of  satellites will provide scientists with crucial data for charting climate change and warning of weather catastrophes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five years after its original launch date, a new observation satellite lifted off on Friday in California with a new generation of observation tools critical to weather forecasters and climate scientists alike.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Long-Awaited Climate Satellite Lifts Off', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Satellites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Weather Service', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vandenberg Air Force Base (Calif)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T15:12:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbf5fa2e-d3d2-5972-9ea3-2e449286f9a3', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbf5fa2e-d3d2-5972-9ea3-2e449286f9a3'}, {'abstract': 'The home to the world’s largest collection of Israeli art now has a new wing, designed by Preston Scott Cohen.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/new-build-the-tel-aviv-museum-of-art/', 'snippet': 'The home to the world’s largest collection of Israeli art now has a new wing, designed by Preston Scott Cohen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It isn’t every day that Tel Aviv gets a piece of architecture worth writing home about. In fact, one of the easiest arguments to win in the Middle East might be that Tel Aviv’s urban core has not sprouted a truly remarkable structure in the more than half a century since the Bauhaus inkwell — which left its curvilinear imprint on hundreds of buildings in “The White City” — began to dry up. But with the completion of the Herta and Paul Amir Building at the Tel Aviv Museum of Art, opening on Wednesday, things are set to get noticeably whiter and brighter. The new wing, designed by the Cambridge, Mass.-based architect Preston Scott Cohen (who is also chairman of the architecture department at Harvard University), looks a bit like an elongated Rubik’s Cube doused with bleach. The gleaming white parabolas of the facade are composed of 465 flat, interlocking, precast concrete panels of different shapes and sizes. The building’s three floors are linked to two more below grade by an 87-foot-high, top-lit atrium, a “lightfall” that will shine on the world’s largest collection of Israeli art. The building’s confident yet supple geometries provide a nifty counterpoint to the museum’s main building, a 1971 Brutalist number by the Israeli architect Dan Eytan (who also designed Israel’s decidedly unfussy Dimona nuclear reactor). Next to that chunky monkey, Cohen’s creation is pure pizazz. Fittingly, in honor of the building’s inauguration later this month, the city of Tel Aviv has declared 2012 to be Art Year, culminating in a four-day blowout Art Weekend March 21-24.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Build | The Tel Aviv Museum of Art', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Preston Scott', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tel Aviv (Israel)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T15:15:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Grant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3609cf17-2992-5521-8531-adab446f44d5', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3609cf17-2992-5521-8531-adab446f44d5'}, {'abstract': 'Best known for comic characters (perhaps one in particular), Woody Harrelson adds to his impressive résumé of serious roles by playing a corrupt police officer in “Rampart.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/movies/woody-harrelson-why-everybody-knows-his-name.html', 'snippet': 'Best known for comic characters (perhaps one in particular), Woody Harrelson adds to his impressive résumé of serious roles by playing a corrupt police officer in “Rampart.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amsterdam', 'print_section': 'MT', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/arts/30CARR1_SPAN/30CARR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/30/arts/30CARR1_SPAN/30CARR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/arts/30CARR1_SPAN/30CARR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/arts/30CARR1_SPAN/30CARR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/arts/30CARR1_SPAN/30CARR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Everybody Knows His Name', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Everybody Knows His Name', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrelson, Woody', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moverman, Oren', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T15:17:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/059f9d22-7d45-5089-9190-458a24f904b3', 'word_count': 1981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/059f9d22-7d45-5089-9190-458a24f904b3'}, {'abstract': 'Thursday night was the Fashion Group’s annual blowout, at Cipriani Wall Street, a journey of 1,000 miles (it seemed).', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/a-rainy-night-of-stars-and-a-laurel/', 'snippet': 'Thursday night was the Fashion Group’s annual blowout, at Cipriani Wall Street, a journey of 1,000 miles (it seemed).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thursday night was the Fashion Group’s annual party, at Cipriani Wall Street, a journey of 1,000 miles (it seemed). Everyone was packed into the former bank, unaware that in an hour or so we were going to be served this large, brown, rectangular hunk of ground lamb with a side of scalloped potatoes. I had just come from celebrating the season with a pumpkin pie bake-off at the office, so the lamb thing was a definite freakout, a no-go. Raf Simons, one of the evening’s honorees, made a tidy joke at the podium about the gravy stain on his tie. Awards were also given to Kate and Laura Mulleavy of Rodarte, Giambattista Valli, Andrew Rosen, Daphne Guinness, Lauren Bush and Wanda Ferragamo. Steve Sadove, the chairman of Saks Fifth Avenue, and Ronald Frasch, the store’s president, were the designated “superstars,” with Mr. Frasch making a funny speech about golf, competition and why he loves his job.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rainy Night of Stars, and a Laurel', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T15:25:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62ea2dae-2fe2-54d1-980a-ecfe2019ac8c', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62ea2dae-2fe2-54d1-980a-ecfe2019ac8c'}, {'abstract': 'In “We Bought a Zoo,” the director Cameron Crowe’s first feature film since 2005, Matt Damon’s character takes over a dilapidated wildlife park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/movies/cameron-crowes-we-bought-a-zoo-with-matt-damon.html', 'snippet': 'In “We Bought a Zoo,” the director Cameron Crowe’s first feature film since 2005, Matt Damon’s character takes over a dilapidated wildlife park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES', 'print_section': 'MT', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/arts/30ROZEN1_SPAN/30ROZEN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/30/arts/30ROZEN1_SPAN/30ROZEN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/arts/30ROZEN1_SPAN/30ROZEN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/arts/30ROZEN1_SPAN/30ROZEN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/arts/30ROZEN1_SPAN/30ROZEN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cameron Crowe Gets Out of the House', 'kicker': 'Holiday Movies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cameron Crowe Gets Out of the House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Damon, Matt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crowe, Cameron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T15:32:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leah Rozen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rozen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/008e000a-04cd-5f28-a6c0-8494516431eb', 'word_count': 1822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/008e000a-04cd-5f28-a6c0-8494516431eb'}, {'abstract': 'The Rangers’ slow start has highlighted their lack of team speed.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/rangers-early-season-troubles-show-lack-of-speed/', 'snippet': 'The Rangers’ slow start has highlighted their lack of team speed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the Rangers lost their home opener, 4-2, to Toronto Thursday night, Coach John Tortorella said his team was mentally and physically lethargic. This may be true, but there could be another reason why they have spent so much of the early part of this season chasing the puck around the rink. Tortorella’s team is hardly a collection of fleet skaters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rangers’ Early Season Troubles Show Lack of Speed', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dubinsky, Brandon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaborik, Marian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lundqvist, Henrik', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T15:41:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Botta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df0e1552-3df7-5a70-8de6-0add16fe0b57', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df0e1552-3df7-5a70-8de6-0add16fe0b57'}, {'abstract': 'Federal tax credits for long-term care policies are increasing — but so are prices.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/good-news-and-bad-on-long-term-care/', 'snippet': 'Federal tax credits for long-term care policies are increasing — but so are prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Desperately searching for any crumb of good news about long-term care, now that the Class Act appears dead, I was glad to get an e-mail from Jesse Slome, executive director of the American Association for Long-Term Care Insurance, pointing out that the I.R.S. is going to allow slightly higher tax deductions in 2012 for the smattering of people who have bought private long-term care policies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Good News and Bad on Long-Term Care', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Long-Term Care Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T15:45:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d1b1df3-3cc9-598f-9166-b082654d703b', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d1b1df3-3cc9-598f-9166-b082654d703b'}, {'abstract': 'Brett Ratner directed the “Rush Hour” films and a new comedy, “Tower Heist,” with Ben Stiller and Eddie Murphy. But “X-Men” fans can’t forgive him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/movies/brett-ratner-directs-tower-heist.html', 'snippet': 'Brett Ratner directed the “Rush Hour” films and a new comedy, “Tower Heist,” with Ben Stiller and Eddie Murphy. But “X-Men” fans can’t forgive him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN you present a comedy achievement award to Brett Ratner, as the Friars Club did on a recent Saturday night in Manhattan, who shows up for the ceremony? You get the entrepreneur Russell Simmons and the billionaire Ronald O. Perelman, who roasted Mr. Ratner for his tastes in fashion models and baggy pants; Michael Barker, co-president of Sony Pictures Classics, who praised Mr. Ratner’s omnivorous cinematic appetite; and Richard Belzer, the comedian and “Law & Order: SVU” star, who briefly summoned the Friars Club abbot Jerry Lewis on his cellphone.', 'print_section': 'MT', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/arts/30ITZKOFF2_SPAN/30ITZKOFF2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/30/arts/30ITZKOFF2_SPAN/30ITZKOFF2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/arts/30ITZKOFF2_SPAN/30ITZKOFF2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 779, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20