Decision Time', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T15:54:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Godfrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Godfrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59099fd8-a79f-513f-853d-0f3ee7cea0e8', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59099fd8-a79f-513f-853d-0f3ee7cea0e8'}, {'abstract': 'Designing accurate simulators for drivers to get acquainted with the newly built Buddh International Circuit was complicated by the track’s numerous construction delays.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/on-eve-of-inaugural-formula-one-indian-gp-teams-revved-up-their-simulators/', 'snippet': 'Designing accurate simulators for drivers to get acquainted with the newly built Buddh International Circuit was complicated by the track’s numerous construction delays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Formula One series is racing in India for the first time this weekend. But long before teams arrived at the barely completed Buddh International Circuit on Thursday, they prepared for the grand prix, scheduled for Oct. 30, the same way they did for the first-ever Korean Grand Prix last year and the first-ever Abu Dhabi Grand Prix in 2009: They ran laps in the simulator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Eve of Inaugural Formula One Indian GP, Teams Revved Up Their Simulators', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ferrari SpA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McLaren Racing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WilliamsF1', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T16:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard S. Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6aef124-1569-5e3f-b184-b7d5ccd0af35', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6aef124-1569-5e3f-b184-b7d5ccd0af35'}, {'abstract': 'The farmers say that between 1981 and 1997, the Agriculture Department ignored their complaints about local officials who unfairly denied them farm loans and other aid.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/us/politics/judge-signs-off-on-settlement-for-black-farmers.html', 'snippet': 'The farmers say that between 1981 and 1997, the Agriculture Department ignored their complaints about local officials who unfairly denied them farm loans and other aid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge in Washington has granted final approval for a $1.25 billion settlement by the Agriculture Department for\xa0 African-American farmers’ longstanding claims of racial discrimination.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Signs Off on Settlement for Black Farmers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Signs Off on Settlement for Black Farmers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 