he movement.’’', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Representative Michele Bachmann, the hits keep coming. The leader of a Tea Party group has called on Mrs. Bachmann, the founder of the Tea Party Caucus in Congress, to quit the presidential race because “every day the campaign flounders, it risks hurting the credibility of the movement.’’', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tea Party Leader Tells Bachmann to Quit', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T17:24:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccf322e6-7b8b-5e13-98da-7fbf34e7ef94', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccf322e6-7b8b-5e13-98da-7fbf34e7ef94'}, {'abstract': 'Chase, which had been testing a $3 monthly fee, has decided not to introduce a monthly fee for debit card purchases.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/chase-bank-wont-impose-debit-card-fee/', 'snippet': 'Chase, which had been testing a $3 monthly fee, has decided not to introduce a monthly fee for debit card purchases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JPMorgan Chase has decided against adopting a monthly fee for account holders who use debit cards for purchases.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chase Bank Won’t Impose Debit Card Fee', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name':