in-november/', 'snippet': 'The show will have a new Mary Jane Watson and a new Arachne.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The two lead actresses in the Broadway musical “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark,” who muddled through months of backstage drama and script changes last winter, will leave the show in November when their contracts expire, the producers said on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Actresses to Bow Out of ‘Spider-Man’ in November', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carney, Reeve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Damiano, Jennifer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mendoza, Natalie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Peter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taymor, Julie', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T18:56:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94b45efe-d2db-5741-8064-cc3ddb2dab60', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94b45efe-d2db-5741-8064-cc3ddb2dab60'}, {'abstract': 'Many Greeks fear a loss of sovereignty and resent the monitoring of the economy that will continue for years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/world/europe/greeks-direct-anger-at-germany-and-european-union.html', 'snippet': 'Many Greeks fear a loss of sovereignty and resent the monitoring of the economy that will continue for years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — Every Oct. 28 Greece celebrates “Oxi Day,” or “\xa0‘No’ Day,” a national holiday commemorating Greek resistance to the Axis powers during World War II. On Friday, those celebrations took on a greater weight. As Greeks suffer from harsh austerity measures, there is growing popular sentiment here that the country has ceded key parts of its sovereignty, and its pride, to its foreign lenders. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/world/29GREECE/29GREECE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/29/world/29GREECE/29GREECE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/world/29GREECE/29GREECE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 625, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/world/29GREECE/29GREECE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/29/world/29GREECE/29GREECE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greek Anger on Debt Agreement Is Focused Especially on Germany', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greek Anger on Debt Agreement Is Focused Especially on Germany', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Papoulias, Karolos', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Papandreou, George A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T18:59:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7996e40-3659-5c7d-a624-224b3a4a361e', 'word_count': 1034, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7996e40-3659-5c7d-a624-224b3a4a361e'}, {'abstract': 'Movie releases for December.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/movies/december-movie-release-schedule.html', 'snippet': 'Movie releases for December.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DEC.', 'print_section': 'MT', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'December/January Release Schedule', 'kicker': 'Holiday Movies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T19:01:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Kehr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kehr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/163f608b-cf09-56f9-b8f1-2d1ad41e892e', 'word_count': 2006, 'uri': 'nyt://article/163f608b-cf09-56f9-b8f1-2d1ad41e892e'}, {'abstract': 'Lost because of logging and other predations, the imperial woodpecker makes a poignant reappearance in a 16-millimeter film shot in 1956.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/a-riveting-glimpse-of-a-vanished-bird/', 'snippet': 'Lost because of logging and other predations, the imperial woodpecker makes a poignant reappearance in a 16-millimeter film shot in 1956.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two feet tall, the imperial woodpecker of Mexico once reigned as the largest woodpecker in the world. But aggressive logging and even poisoning by the lumber companies in its Sierra Madre habitat is thought to have driven the bird into extinction sometime in the mid-20th century.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Riveting Glimpse of a Vanished Bird', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Logging Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Woodpeckers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornell Laboratory of Ornithology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T19:04:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d924ad68-830f-57ad-98ff-5fa686b2b7ef', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d924ad68-830f-57ad-98ff-5fa686b2b7ef'}, {'abstract': 'What we’re reading.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/lotsa-links/', 'snippet': 'What we’re reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Great graphic about menhaden (bunker) from the Pew Environmental Group. Really gets the message across: stop overfishing! ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lotsa Links', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T19:08:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34bad76f-c1df-5e5e-9ac3-d9c29c42bc66', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34bad76f-c1df-5e5e-9ac3-d9c29c42bc66'}, {'abstract': 'An artist explores the question: Can all urban-dwelling animals be accommodated in the concrete jungle?', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/london-underground-animal-estates-london-edition/', 'snippet': 'An artist explores the question: Can all urban-dwelling animals be accommodated in the concrete jungle?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Designers are used to designing for people, but what if the client was an animal? I’m not talking about designing a kennel for your dog, but rather homes for all the animals that are native to our cities, yet which are often forgotten. Can the birds and the bees, the kestrels and the beetles, all be accommodated in the concrete jungle? This is what the artist Fritz Haeg is encouraging us to think about at the “Animal Estates London HQ: Urban Wildlife Client Services.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Underground | Animal Estates, London Edition', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None,