//artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/cardinals-comeback-fuels-fox-victory/', 'snippet': 'Game 6 of the World Series cleans up in the ratings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, at least in terms of television ratings, the World Series was the only game in town. Fox easily won the night in all categories thanks to the St. Louis Cardinals’ remarkable extra-inning comeback 10-9 victory over the Texas Rangers in Game 6. CBS came in second despite seeing drops across the board, with “The Big Bang Theory” leading all other scripted programs at 14.3 million total viewers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cardinals’ Comeback Fuels Fox Victory', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T20:21:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e25e325-85ee-5785-be09-6d9e74cb43a9', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e25e325-85ee-5785-be09-6d9e74cb43a9'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Libya, Thailand, Turkey and Sri Lanka.', 'web_url': '