/10/28/another-flap-over-a-possible-flip-for-mitt-romney/', 'snippet': 'Rivals charge that Mitt Romney changed his stance on climate change, but the record may show otherwise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Just days after Mitt Romney came under attack for seeming to waver on antiunion rules in Ohio, the former governor of Massachusetts drew scrutiny yet again for alleged shape-shifting. The issue of the moment? Climate change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Flap Over an Alleged Romney Flip', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh (Pa)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T21:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/601bc3d9-876b-5d22-8c3f-58c2a580efcc', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/601bc3d9-876b-5d22-8c3f-58c2a580efcc'}, {'abstract': 'Remembering the year punk broke.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/10/30/arts/music/20111030-KUO-CHART.html', 'snippet': 'Remembering the year punk broke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Remembering the year punk broke.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reassessing the Year Punk Broke', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T21:06:03+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/c944c3dc-9966-5666-b0a3-6943a92b5041', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/c944c3dc-9966-5666-b0a3-6943a92b5041'}, {'abstract': 'Two decades after Nirvana’s “Nevermind” and the documentary “1991: The Year Punk Broke” had an imprinting effect on him as a teenager, the artist Andrew Kuo considers what it all meant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/arts/music/andrew-kuo-looks-back-at-the-punk-of-1991.html', 'snippet': 'Two decades after Nirvana’s “Nevermind” and the documentary “1991: The Year Punk Broke” had an imprinting effect on him as a teenager, the artist Andrew Kuo considers what it all meant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN 1991, the year Nirvana’s breakthrough album “Nevermind” (DGC) was released, the artist Andrew Kuo was a 13-year-old alternative rock superfan\xa0of bands like Nirvana,\xa0Fugazi and Dinosaur Jr.\xa0A year later he became obsessed with the film “1991: The Year Punk Broke,” which documented Sonic Youth’s 1991 tour of Europe and features backstage antics from\xa0the likes of Thurston Moore and\xa0Kim Gordon of Sonic Youth,\xa0Kurt Cobain and Dave Grohl of Nirvana,\xa0and Courtney Love.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sonic Tattoos, Gingerly Reconsidered', 'kicker': 'Music', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sonic Tattoos, Gingerly Reconsidered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T21:09:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Kuo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kuo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fd0adeb-bef9-534d-9b78-d0bc4886c931', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fd0adeb-bef9-534d-9b78-d0bc4886c931'}, {'abstract': 'Advances in virtual staging enable brokers to do everything from “furnishing” an empty space to “clearing away” clutter in a cramped apartment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/realestate/posting-staging-ever-more-virtual.html', 'snippet': 'Advances in virtual staging enable brokers to do everything from “furnishing” an empty space to “clearing away” clutter in a cramped apartment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR the longest time, if brokers wanted to “stage” an apartment to sell, they needed to buy or rent furnishings, wall covering, carpets and other interior decorations. Then, a few years ago, advances in computer rendering gave them a simple and cheap way to hire a virtual staging company to render those items into a photograph of an empty room.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/realestate/30POSTING2-2/30POSTING2-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/30/realestate/30POSTING2-2/30POSTING2-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/realestate/30POSTING2-2/30POSTING2-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/r