d the Tea Party movement; the New York Civil Liberties Union sets up a table in Zuccotti Park; and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With snow in the forecast and Zuccotti Park newly bereft of gas generators protesters are stocking up on Mylar sleeping bags and bike generators. [City Room, Dawn Hoag via Twitter, Young Manhattanite]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '#OccupyWallSt Roundup, Day 42', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zuccotti Park (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T22:45:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jillian Dunham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jillian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dunham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91b329f4-44d7-50e7-842f-3508d839a360', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91b329f4-44d7-50e7-842f-3508d839a360'}, {'abstract': 'The violinist Christian Tetzlaff and the pianist Lars Vogt took on Schumann, Franck and Bartok at Alice Tully Hall on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/arts/music/christian-tetzlaff-at-alice-tully-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'The violinist Christian Tetzlaff and the pianist Lars Vogt took on Schumann, Franck and Bartok at Alice Tully Hall on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With so much unaccompanied violin music of Bach on New York stages in recent days — Gidon Kremer played the Chaconne last Saturday and Jennifer Koh the six sonatas and partitas on Sunday — Christian Tetzlaff might have felt like the odd man out at Alice Tully Hall on Wednesday evening. Mr. Tetzlaff devoted his recital to sonatas by Schumann, Franck and Bartok. But when it comes to Bach, he has been there and done that: two years ago he played all the unaccompanied violin works in a stunning marathon recital at the 92nd Street Y. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/arts/christian/christian-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/arts/christian/christian-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/29/arts/christian/christian-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaving Bach in the Past, a Violinist Turns to Schumann, Franck and Bartok', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leaving Bach in the Past, a Violinist Turns to Schumann, Franck and Bartok', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumann, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tetzlaff, Christian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartok, Bela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vogt, Lars', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T22:47:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': 