fternoons, he blows off steam by boxing or playing basketball.  ROBIN FINN', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30ROUTINE-2_SPAN/30ROUTINE-2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30ROUTINE-2_SPAN/30ROUTINE-2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30ROUTINE-2_SPAN/30ROUTINE-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Little-Girl Time and Big-Boy Sports', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Little-Girl Time and Big-Boy Sports', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Children's Museum of the Arts", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-28T23:39:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5420f9f1-1357-5eb3-b7f5-bd8592767de6', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5420f9f1-1357-5eb3-b7f5-bd8592767de6'}, {'abstract': 'Despite a recommendation by the Texas Board of Pardons and Parole that Kelsey Patterson be spared due to severe mentally illness, he was executed for a double murder in 2004.', 'web_url': 'https://www.n