l-known …', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/one-nation-innumerate/', 'snippet': 'Data have a well-known …', 'lead_paragraph': 'Via Brian Beutler, Politico has part of George Will’s forthcoming attack on Romney:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Nation, Innumerate', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T00:40:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81531100-0c2e-53de-aa66-99dad647e0c7', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81531100-0c2e-53de-aa66-99dad647e0c7'}, {'abstract': 'Twenty people were killed Friday in multiple shootouts in two states, law enforcement officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/world/americas/20-killed-in-shootouts-in-mexico.html', 'snippet': 'Twenty people were killed Friday in multiple shootouts in two states, law enforcement officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty people were killed Friday in multiple shootouts in two states, law enforcement officials said. In Michoacán, 14 bodies were found in three different locations. Of these, 10 people died in the city of Pátzcuaro after a confrontation with soldiers patrolling the area. Michoacán has been beset by violence in recent years, much of it attributed to the Familia drug cartel, and recently the cartel’s turf war with a splinter group called the Knights Templar. In the state of Sinaloa, a confrontation between members of an organized crime gang on a highway left six people dead, three of them unarmed civilians.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: 20 Killed in Shootouts', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: 20 Killed in Shootouts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Cartels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T00:44:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Zabludovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zabludovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d3f14ad-f0c8-5e4a-82ed-e45ac84fb8ad', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d3f14ad-f0c8-5e4a-82ed-e45ac84fb8ad'}, {'abstract': 'La Gazzetta, the lively trattoria in the meatpacking district, offers Cinema Italiano, a weekly screening of classics, on Mondays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/nyregion/la-gazzetta-mixes-italian-food-and-old-movies.html', 'snippet': 'La Gazzetta, the lively trattoria in the meatpacking district, offers Cinema Italiano, a weekly screening of classics, on Mondays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Monday nights can feel slow in New York, as many spots take a day of rest after the busy weekend. But at La Gazzetta, the lively trattoria on the ground floor of Villa Pacri in the meatpacking district on Gansevoort Street at Ninth Avenue, it is a different story. On Mondays, it draws a crowd of regulars from the neighborhood, couples on first dates and families, for Cinema Italiano, its weekly screenings of classics like “To Kill a Mockingbird” and “The Godfather” — a hipper dinner theater for the downtown set — and for a menu offering Italian snacks, pastas and entrees. Last week, as the original “Casino Royale” with Peter Sellers and David Niven played in the background, a couple from London on their way to Buffalo and Toronto mixed business and pleasure.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30TABLE_SPAN/30TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30TABLE_SPAN/30TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30TABLE_SPAN/30TABLE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30TABLE_SPAN/30TABLE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30TABLE_SPAN/30TABLE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fresh Food and Vintage Movies', 'kicker': 'At the Table | La Gazzetta', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fresh Food and Vintage Movies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Meatpacking District (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T00:44:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane Cardwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cardwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6889c32c-bfb7-53cb-a31f-c7aa7c403bf4', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6889c32c-bfb7-53cb-a31f-c7aa7c403bf4'}, {'abstract': 'Baseball’s commissioner says he’s confident M.L.B. will get back the money it loaned to the Mets.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/seligs-not-worried-about-the-mets/', 'snippet': 'Baseball’s commissioner says he’s confident M.L.B. will get back the money it loaned to the Mets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — Commissioner Bud Selig said the Mets, who borrowed $25 million from Major League Baseball after last season, still had not paid back the loan. But Selig said he was not worried about getting the money back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Selig’s Not Worried About the Mets', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Selig, Bud', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T00:45:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc43ac16-8ab3-5e03-a5d6-660a8727caa7', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc43ac16-8ab3-5e03-a5d6-660a8727caa7'}, {'abstract': 'The Italian government declared a state of emergency on Friday in areas struck by flooding and mud slides earlier this week, and allocated $92 million to assist residents there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/world/europe/italy-declares-emergency-in-flood-zones.html', 'snippet': 'The Italian government declared a state of emergency on Friday in areas struck by flooding and mud slides earlier this week, and allocated $92 million to assist residents there.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Italian government declared a state of emergency on Friday in areas struck by flooding and mud slides earlier this week, and allocated $92 million to assist residents there. Torrential rains and flash floods on Tuesday and Wednesday killed at least seven people and left hundreds homeless in coastal areas of Tuscany and Liguria, including villages of Cinque Terre, Unesco World Heritage sites. Rescue and clean-up efforts continued Friday, but were hampered by inaccessible roads and disrupted electricity, water and gas. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy: Emergency Declared in Flood Zones', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Emergency Declared in Flood Zones', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T00:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3c5f639-6540-5215-a9eb-6b5917ab40c2', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3c5f639-6540-5215-a9eb-6b5917ab40c2'}, {'abstract': 'With the latest decline in savings, some are asking whether consumers are returning to their old spending habits, while others wonder if the new data is even true.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/business/americans-savings-rate-drops-again-puzzling-experts.html', 'snippet': 'With the latest decline in savings, some are asking whether consumers are returning to their old spending habits, while others wonder if the new data is even true.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the recession began, Americans began to save more of their money, prompting predictions that their financial habits might be changing permanently. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/business/Savings/Savings-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 615, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Savings Rate Is Dropping, and Experts Are Puzzled', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Savings Rate Is Dropping, And Experts Are Puzzled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T00:46:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shaila Dewan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shaila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dewan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organizat