byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12bd711f-da66-5a53-9864-b369baa46d65', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12bd711f-da66-5a53-9864-b369baa46d65'}, {'abstract': 'The report underscored the Obama administration’s halting progress toward fulfilling its pledge to end homelessness among veterans by 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/us/study-finds-slight-decline-in-veterans-using-shelters.html', 'snippet': 'The report underscored the Obama administration’s halting progress toward fulfilling its pledge to end homelessness among veterans by 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Homeless veterans are most likely to be middle-aged white men with a disability. Younger veterans are more than twice as likely to be homeless than nonveterans in the same age group. And California has the most homeless veterans of any state, accounting for about a quarter of the nation’s total.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Finds Slight Decline in Veterans Using Shelters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Finds Slight Decline In Veterans Using Shelters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T00:53:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d5c8eba-feb6-5fd3-b676-185a716960b0', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d5c8eba-feb6-5fd3-b676-185a716960b0'}, {'abstract': 'In this edition: Herman Cain and overly confident punditry, some crowded estimates and two more endorsed ideas about newspaper endorsements.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/reads-reactions-13/', 'snippet': 'In this edition: Herman Cain and overly confident punditry, some crowded estimates and two more endorsed ideas about newspaper endorsements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this edition: a lot of Herman Cain and overly confident punditry, some crowded estimates and two more endorsed ideas about newspaper endorsements.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reads and Reactions', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T00:55:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1a4de74-4d52-535d-83e6-ce86ac476323', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1a4de74-4d52-535d-83e6-ce86ac476323'}, {'abstract': 'The case for vaccinating boys, as well as girls, against a sexually transmitted virus associated with several cancers is getting stronger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/opinion/the-hpv-vaccine-is-for-their-own-good.html', 'snippet': 'The case for vaccinating boys, as well as girls, against a sexually transmitted virus associated with several cancers is getting stronger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The case for vaccinating all preteens against a sexually transmitted virus that causes cancer keeps getting stronger. After a thorough review of the evidence, an influential federal advisory committee recommended that boys ages 11 and 12 should routinely be vaccinated against the human papillomavirus, or HPV, echoing a 2006 recommendation for vaccinating girls of that age. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Their Own Good', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Their Own Good', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Papilloma Virus (HPV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Merck & Company Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardasil (Vaccine)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexually Transmitted Diseases', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T00:56:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8973cd6-f330-510f-bc9a-b264d914a945', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8973cd6-f330-510f-bc9a-b264d914a945'}, {'abstract': 'The facts in Pennsylvania’s death penalty cases show an abysmal failure of justice and a convincing argument to end the barbaric punishment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/opinion/pennsylvania-and-the-death-penalty.html', 'snippet': 'The facts in Pennsylvania’s death penalty cases show an abysmal failure of justice and a convincing argument to end the barbaric punishment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pennsylvania ranks high among states that impose death sentences and low among those that carry them out: 208 men and women are on death row, but no one has been executed since 1999; only three people have been executed since the penalty was reinstated in 1976. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death Row in Pennsylvania', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Death Row in Pennsylvania', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T01:01:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2945c4c9-6e86-5395-bd47-859dfc2ddf8f', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2945c4c9-6e86-5395-bd47-859dfc2ddf8f'}, {'abstract': 'O, Canada.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/28/friday-night-music-2/', 'snippet': 'O, Canada.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Still loving this album:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': []