zation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6fcacf2-a32b-5cac-89d2-b091c55597db', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6fcacf2-a32b-5cac-89d2-b091c55597db'}, {'abstract': 'The Dolphins’ improbable defeat against the Broncos and Tim Tebow was a revealing signpost in the middle of another lost season in Miami.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/sports/football/dolphins-are-in-the-middle-of-another-lost-season.html', 'snippet': 'The Dolphins’ improbable defeat against the Broncos and Tim Tebow was a revealing signpost in the middle of another lost season in Miami.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Outside the stadium where the Miami Dolphins play, a bronze statue of Don Shula shows him being carried off the field on the shoulders of his players. It is a tribute to a team of a much different era, when the Dolphins had the N.F.L.’s only perfect season and their defense was so good that it did not have to spend a week arguing about why it could not stop a goal-line run that everybody knew was coming. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/DOLPHINS1/DOLPHINS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/DOLPHINS1/DOLPHINS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/DOLPHINS1/DOLPHINS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/DOLPHINS1/DOLPHINS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'im