nded their contract with the radio station WCBS 880 to broadcast their games through the 2012 season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees have extended their contract with the radio station WCBS 880 to broadcast their games through the 2012 season, meaning that the announcers John Sterling and Suzyn Waldman will most likely come back in their same roles.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Stay With WCBS on Radio', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees Stay With WCBS on Radio', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T02:57:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ca7aa42-283e-585c-a508-86bd7d0c568f', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ca7aa42-283e-585c-a508-86bd7d0c568f'}, {'abstract': 'Two members of the House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform sent a letter about the failure to begin testing for human growth hormone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/sports/football/nfl-football-roundup.html', 'snippet': 'Two members of the House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform sent a letter about the failure to begin testing for human growth hormone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chairman and the ranking member of the House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform, in a letter about the failure to begin testing for human growth hormone sent to the N.F.L. and the players union Friday, said “it appears that the players’ union may be using stall tactics to avoid complying with the collective bargaining agreement.” ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/nfl/nfl-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 789, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Congressmen Say Union May Be Stalling on H.G.H.', 'kicker': 'N.F.L. Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congressmen Say Union May Be Stalling on H.G.H.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Drug Use)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Growth Hormone', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T03:05:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cada191d-5e20-5c92-9b30-874853c0a564', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cada191d-5e20-5c92-9b30-874853c0a564'}, {'abstract': 'The iPhone is the latest in a succession of status objects that have fostered urban crime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/nyregion/easy-to-use-or-steal-iphone-inches-out-of-reach.html', 'snippet': 'The iPhone is the latest in a succession of status objects that have fostered urban crime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among his various legacies, Steve Jobs, whose memorial continues with the arrival of the iPhone 4S, left us with a tangible and resonant symbol of our economic frictions: an easily brandished, easily taken device that in its sleek design and intuitive simplicity flaunts the relative effortlessness of affluent, knowledge-class living. The have-nots, particularly teenagers, covet and seek what, by now, the haves assume as birthright and dependency.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30bigcity-span/30SUBjpBIG-CITY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30bigcity-span/30SUBjpBIG-CITY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30bigcity-span/30SUBjpBIG-CITY-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30bigcity-span/30SUBjpBIG-CITY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30bigcity-span/30SUBjpBIG-CITY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Easy to Use, or Steal, but Inching Out of Reach', 'kicker': 'Big City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Easy to Use, or Steal, But Inching Out of Reach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, '