acked a plane.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/nyregion/george-wright-tells-story-of-hijacking-from-portugal.html', 'snippet': 'Captured in Portugal last month, George Wright recounts his odyssey since he escaped from prison and hijacked a plane.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CASAS NOVAS, Portugal — George Wright, the fugitive murderer who was captured in Portugal last month, 39 years after hijacking a jetliner and demanding a $1 million ransom, said he figured authorities in the United States had given up the chase long ago. But, he said, he never stopped worrying that they would come knocking.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/nyregion/WRIGHT3/WRIGHT3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/29/nyregion/WRIGHT3/WRIGHT3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/nyregion/WRIGHT3/WRIGHT3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/nyregion/WRIGHT3/WRIGHT3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/29/nyregion/WRIGHT3/WRIGHT3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Telling the Story of 41 Years on the Run', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Telling The Story Of 41 Years On the Run', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hijacking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prison Escapes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fugitives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portugal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, George (1943- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T03:24:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder and James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/821371d0-016a-5834-a02e-644adcf73a2b', 'word_count': 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/821371d0-016a-5834-a02e-644adcf73a2b'}, {'abstract': 'The state finance director, Ana Matosantos, was arrested early Friday and accused of driving drunk after the police saw her swerving near the Capitol.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/us/politics/california-official-arrested.html', 'snippet': 'The state finance director, Ana Matosantos, was arrested early Friday and accused of driving drunk after the police saw her swerving near the Capitol.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The state finance director, Ana Matosantos, was arrested early Friday and accused of driving drunk after the police saw her swerving near the Capitol. Ms. Matosantos offered her resignation to Gov. Jerry Brown, but he did not accept it and she reported to work. “My decision to drive last night was reckless and irresponsible,” she said in a statement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Official Arrested', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Official Arrested', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matosantos, Ana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T03:25:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e2bbeab-3aed-5e7e-b3be-e916b8ecf265', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e2bbeab-3aed-5e7e-b3be-e916b8ecf265'}, {'abstract': 'Ron Washington said that if Game 7 presented the Rangers with a save situation, he would call on Neftali Feliz, as usual.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/sports/baseball/world-series-rangers-washington-stands-by-closer-feliz-after-game-6-heartbreak.html', 'snippet': 'Ron Washington said that if Game 7 presented the Rangers with a save situation, he would call on Neftali Feliz, as usual.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — Texas Manager Ron Washington said his team seemed relaxed and normal Friday afternoon, the day after twice failing to get the final strike to finish off the World Series in Game 6. Washington described the disappointment in that 10-9 loss in 11 innings as “taking a blow to the gut.” ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/notebook/notebook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 733, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas Manager Stands By the Closer Who Let It Slip Away', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas Manager Stands By the Closer Who Let It Slip Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feliz, Neftali', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T03:34:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4375bcb-5d7c-5d1a-a853-54f78767afff', 'word_count': 976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4375bcb-5d7c-5d1a-a853-54f78767afff'}, {'abstract': 'La Bella Havana in Yonkers, formerly the French-Cuban restaurant Belle Havana, offers traditional Cuban fare in a casual, comfortable setting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/nyregion/la-bella-havana-a-cuban-restaurant-in-yonkers-review.html', 'snippet': 'La Bella Havana in Yonkers, formerly the French-Cuban restaurant Belle Havana, offers traditional Cuban fare in a casual, comfortable setting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN I first started working in Manhattan, in the 1980s, I became acquainted with the cheap but absolutely delicious Cuban food that was then ubiquitous on a strip of Ninth Avenue in Chelsea. It was an exciting culinary experience — a window into an unfamiliar culture and a taste awakening. One dish in particular satisfied me every time: picadillo, that basic beef hash made Cuban-style, with tomatoes, green olives and raisins.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30DINEWE1/30DINEWE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30DINEWE1/30DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30DINEWE1/30DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuban Food, Authentic and Light', 'kicker': 'Westchester Dining | Yonkers', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuban Food, Authentic and Light', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yonkers (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T03:37:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily DeNitto', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeNitto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc5e4344-391f-5e9d-80f6-091223fc3205', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc5e4344-391f-5e9d-80f6-091223fc3205'}, {'abstract': 'Amateurs 18 and older will be permitted to enter into deal with agents or sponsors regarding their future — as long as they do not enjoy financial gain as amateurs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/sports/golf/changes-to-golfs-amateur-rules-help-ease-financial-pressure.html', 'snippet': 'Amateurs 18 and older will be permitted to enter into deal with agents or sponsors regarding their future — as long as they do not enjoy financial gain as amateurs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the English amateur Tom Lewis burst onto the golf scene with a share of the first-round lead at the British Open in July, rumors swirled that dollar signs were dancing in his eyes and that he would jump to the professional ranks while his endorsement earnings potential was hot.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Changes to Rules Help Ease Pressure on Amateurs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Changes to Rules Help Ease Pressure on Amateurs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Golf Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal and Ancient Golf Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T03:49:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Schupak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schupak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e83d3ef-ce51-57c1-a046-fd6fa7760b70', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e83d3ef-ce51-57c1-a046-fd6fa7760b70'}, {'abstract': 'The Cardinals, who made the postseason with the fewest wins, 90, of any playoff team, won their 11th World Series title by beating the Rangers in a series that went all seven games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/sports/baseball/cardinals-win-world-series.html', 'snippet': 'The Cardinals, who made the postseason with the fewest wins, 90, of any playoff team, won their 11th World Series title by beating the Rangers in a series that went all seven games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — When the St. Louis Cardinals were down to their apparent final strike of the season, in both the ninth and 10th innings of Game 6 on Thursday night, Manager Tony La Russa told his players in the dugout not to forget to thank the fans for their support amid what was looking like a crushing season-ending loss.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/29series3_span/29series3_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/29series3_span/29series3_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/29series3_span/29series3_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/29series3_span/29series3_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/29/sports/29series3_span/29series3_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'All the Way Back, the Cardinals Win the World Series', 'kicker': 'Cardinals 6, Rangers 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ALL THE WAY BACK', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freese, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'la Russa, Tony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Josh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T04:01:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a2c89dd-d4e9-5f79-a695-9c84501ffe19', 'word_count': 1280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a2c89dd-d4e9-5f79-a695-9c84501ffe19'}, {'abstract': 'The death toll from twin bombings on Thursday in a Shiite neighborhood of Baghdad rose on Friday to 36 killed and 78 wounded, according to an official at the Ministry of Interior.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/world/middleeast/iraq-baghdad-bomb-toll-rises.html', 'snippet': 'The death toll from twin bombings on Thursday in a Shiite neighborhood of Baghdad rose on Friday to 36 killed and 78 wounded, according to an official at the Ministry of Interior.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The death toll from twin bombings on Thursday in a Shiite neighborhood of Baghdad rose on Friday to 36 killed and 78 wounded, according to an official at the Ministry of Interior. Initially, on Thursday evening, officials put the number of deaths at 12, but many who were hurt later succumbed to their wounds. Among the dead were several police officers and soldiers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: Baghdad Bomb Toll Rises', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: Baghdad Bomb Toll Rises', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T04:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arango', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a64978d2-0152-5612-b791-b6040bfd81af', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a64978d2-0152-5612-b791-b6040bfd81af'}, {'abstract': 'Weekend games in college football include Oklahoma at Kansas State and Michigan State at Nebraska.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/games-to-watch-on-saturday-8/', 'snippet': 'Weekend games in college football include Oklahoma at Kansas State and Michigan State at Nebraska.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NO. 11 OKLAHOMA AT NO. 10 KANSAS STATE3:30 p.m. Eastern, ESPN', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Games to Watch on Saturday', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas State University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Michigan State University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Nebraska', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Oklahoma', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Southern California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T04:21:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred Bierman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bierman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/555640d6-8fb2-5075-87eb-6336b5457b25', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/555640d6-8fb2-5075-87eb-6336b5457b25'}, {'abstract': 'Thatcher McGhee’s Irish Pub and Eatery in Pompton Lakes, N.J., where the menu leans heavily toward American-friendly pub food, is as Irish as you want it to be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/nyregion/channeling-ireland-at-thatcher-mcghees-pub-in-nj-review.html', 'snippet': 'Thatcher McGhee’s Irish Pub and Eatery in Pompton Lakes, N.J., where the menu leans heavily toward American-friendly pub food, is as Irish as you want it to be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S barely 7 o’clock on a Saturday evening and the throttle is wide open at Thatcher McGhee’s Irish Pub and Eatery in Pompton Lakes. The large square bar is packed two deep with knots of sports fans, young couples and off-duty mechanics talking about the day’s work. A burly patron who could easily be a finalist in a Jeff Lebowksi lookalike contest is well into a plate of bangers and mash, next to a heavily tattooed fellow picking his way through his Thatch fries, an unholy concoction featuring three cheeses, bacon and ranch dressing, which seems to be a house favorite.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30DINENJ3/30DINENJ3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30DINENJ3/30DINENJ3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/nyregion/30DINENJ3/30DINENJ3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Neighborhood Pub, Channeling Ireland', 'kicker': 'New Jersey Dining | Pompton Lakes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Neighborhood Pub, Channeling Ireland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T04:35:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Veale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Veale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a259730-825d-5ede-b3da-97468bdaf1db', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a259730-825d-5ede-b3da-97468bdaf1db'}, {'abstract': 'The St. Louis Cardinals win the World Series, beating the Texas Rangers, 6-2.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/28/sports/baseball/World-Series-Game-7.html', 'snippet': 'The St. Louis Cardinals win the World Series, beating the Texas Rangers, 6-2.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The St. Louis Cardinals win the World Series, beating the Texas Rangers, 6-2.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/sports/World-Series-Game-7-slide-MFEG/World-Series-Game-7-slide-MFEG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/sports/World-Series-Game-7-slide-MFEG/World-Series-Game-7-slide-MFEG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/28/sports/World-Series-Game-7-slide-MFEG/World-Series-Game-7-slide-MFEG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'World Series Replay: Game 7', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T04:45:16+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/68ab256b-4bae-5805-9ca1-c9d40f4b1279', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/68ab256b-4bae-5805-9ca1-c9d40f4b1279'}, {'abstract': 'The Jesuit priest moved to the San Salvador university dormitory where six priests and two women were murdered by government forces in 1989.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytim