 tree trunks around the city is called the “mushroom of immortality” in traditional Chinese medicine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s difficult these days to walk around the city without finding fungi growing in planters, on wood mulch, or at the base of trees, so I wasn’t surprised to discover a beautiful cluster of red-shellacked reishi mushrooms growing fan-like at the base of a tree at the College of Staten Island.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Urban Forager | Reishi, the Leathery Healer', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mushrooms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoff, Gary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T13:12:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ava Chin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ava', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b424a066-9553-5e62-8c12-e7c9946ddc5b', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b424a066-9553-5e62-8c12-e7c9946ddc5b'}, {'abstract': 'The singer’s power-pop hits and dismissal of criticism about her weight have fostered a distinct relationship with fans: less that of adulation than of identification and admiration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/fashion/kelly-clarkson-the-role-model-next-door.html', 'snippet': 'The singer’s power-pop hits and dismissal of criticism about her weight have fostered a distinct relationship with fans: less that of adulation than of identification and admiration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE other night, Danielle Travali, 25, was listening to Kelly Clarkson’s new album, “Stronger.” Ms. Travali has fought her brigade of demons and then some, describing herself as an eating-disorders survivor.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/fashion/30KELLY2_SPAN/30KELLY2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/30/fashion/30KELLY2_SPAN/30KELLY2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/fashion/30KELLY2_SPAN/30JPKELLY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/fashion/30KELLY2_SPAN/30KELLY2_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/fashion/30KELLY2_SPAN/30KELLY2_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kelly Clarkson, a Pop Star Proud in Her Own Skin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pop Star Proud in Her Own Skin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarkson, Kelly', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T13:24:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jan Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e67af05-36b2-59e0-bf15-cb98a92d1bdf', 'word_count': 1380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e67af05-36b2-59e0-bf15-cb98a92d1bdf'}, {'abstract': 'How to stop action on inequality, climate, and more.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/denial-in-depth/', 'snippet': 'How to stop action on inequality, climate, and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Columbia Journalism Review has a takedown of a “study” from American Enterprise Institute purporting to show that inequality hasn’t increased, after all. What’s striking is the way AEI doesn’t even resort to the usual practice of concocting misleading numbers; it just flat-out lies about what various other peoples’ research, like Robert Gordon’s work, actually says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Denial In Depth', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T13:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab26147f-4786-5ddc-84f1-df8de79c5958', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab26147f-4786-5ddc-84f1-df8de79c5958'}, {'abstract': 'Italy at 6.03.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/falling-short-in-europe-again/', 'snippet': 'Italy at 6.03.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kash Mansori is unhappy with the state of the Italian bond market just days after the supposed big rescue. Indeed, the Panzerfaust has fallen far short; Italy is having to roll over its debt at levels that are unsustainable, and the unraveling of the euro is definitely still on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Falling Short In Europe (Again)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T13:51:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f293273-4b5b-5059-9e7a-ec3044eed983', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f293273-4b5b-5059-9e7a-ec3044eed983'}, {'abstract': 'Winning the Classic has proven to deliver all the spoils that Triple Crown races do – a massive payday, Eclipse awards and lucrative breeding potential.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/a-fourth-jewel-for-the-crown-found-in-november/', 'snippet': 'Winning the Classic has proven to deliver all the spoils that Triple Crown races do – a massive payday, Eclipse awards and lucrative breeding potential.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, all those competing at the highest levels of North American racing have commenced each new year with their sights set on winning the same three races – the Kentucky Derby, the Preakness Stakes and the Belmont Stakes. Victories in these classics significantly raise the stature of horses, jockeys, trainers and owners alike and have a lasting impact on one’s legacy, often tipping the scales in one’s favor when it’s time to be considered for the Hall of Fame.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fourth Jewel for the Crown, Found in November', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Breeders' Cup (Horse Race)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baffert, Bob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pletcher, Todd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zito, Nick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T13:55:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christian Teja', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Teja', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/481208db-6c7d-5e9f-934e-3faa7df9a712', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/481208db-6c7d-5e9f-934e-3faa7df9a712'}, {'abstract': 'If a work schedules and bedtimes make family dinner impossible, can breakfast become the bedrock of family together-time?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/can-breakfast-replace-family-dinner/', 'snippet': 'If a work schedules and bedtimes make family dinner impossible, can breakfast become the bedrock of family together-time?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can the family breakfast serve the same purpose as the family dinner?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Breakfast Replace Family Dinner?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T14:28:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenny Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e7ed5a4-acb4-5177-a694-ce19d2d9d66c', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e7ed5a4-acb4-5177-a694-ce19d2d9d66c'}, {'abstract': 'Ramses Barden, the Giants’ third-year receiver, is waiting to make the kind of impact he had in college at Cal Poly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/sports/football/giants-are-waiting-for-ramses-barden.html', 'snippet': 'Ramses Barden, the Giants’ third-year receiver, is waiting to make the kind of impact he had in college at Cal Poly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Over the past two seasons, Ramses Barden has been Hakeem Nicks. He has also been Mario Manningham, Steve Smith and, on occasion, Domenik Hixon.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/sports/dog-giants/dog-giants-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/30/sports/dog-giants/dog-giants-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/sports/dog-giants/dog-giants-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 943, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/sports/dog-giants/dog-giants-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/sports/dog-giants/dog-giants-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Receiver Learns Roles, but Hasn’t Found One', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Receiver Learns Roles, But Hasn’t Found One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barden, Ramses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T14:54:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9c47952-9f42-5260-8273-aff9bb240dcd', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9c47952-9f42-5260-8273-aff9bb240dcd'}, {'abstract': 'At another time, Mayor Jean Quan might have joined the protesters. Instead, she is a focus of their wrath.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/us/Oakland-Protests-Test-Mayor-Jean-Quan-Activist-Background.html', 'snippet': 'At another time, Mayor Jean Quan might have joined the protesters. Instead, she is a focus of their wrath.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Jean Quan was an undergraduate, she once sat for 10 hours inside Sproul Hall at the University of California, Berkeley, demanding better treatment for minority students. As a community activist, she helped unionize hospital workers and organized parents in a poor neighborhood of West Oakland.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/us/30BCQUAN_span/30BCQUAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/30/us/30BCQUAN_span/30BCQUAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': No