 'With the exception of an ugly Game 3, the Texas Rangers and the St. Louis Cardinals had been so evenly matched that the differences in the two teams seemed infinitesimal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the time the last out was made, Rangers fans knew what was coming. They had felt the tide shift in the late innings of Game 6, which will surely go down as one of the most torturous losses in World Series history — not one, but two blown chances to win the championship on a single pitch. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/us/30TTSPORTS/30TTSPORTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/us/30TTSPORTS/30TTSPORTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/us/30TTSPORTS/30TTSPORTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Rangers Fans, the Promised Land Was Two Strikes and a Few Inches Away', 'kicker': 'Texas Monthly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Rangers Fans, the Promised Land Was Two Strikes and a Few Inches Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freese, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, David M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub