ource': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Free Agent Outlook: Pujols, Sabathia and Reyes Stand Above the Rest', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fielder, Prince', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ortiz, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oswalt, Roy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pujols, Albert', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T17:57:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6662537-65b8-518d-b56d-bf9b14be7604', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6662537-65b8-518d-b56d-bf9b14be7604'}, {'abstract': 'In the late 1970s and early 1980s New York as a whole resembled a haunted house. The photographer John Conn spent those years documenting the subway system — which is to say, the dungeon in the haunted house’s basement.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/when-the-city-was-a-house-of-horrors/', 'snippet': 'In the late 1970s and early 1980s New York as a whole resembled a haunted house. The photographer John Conn spent those years documenting the subway system — which is to say, the dungeon in the haunted house’s basement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The late 1970s and early 1980s — when buildings were burning, fiscal crises were raging and the Dead Boys were playing at CBGB — were a macabre time in New York City’s history, a period when it could be said that the city resembled a haunted house.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When the City Was a House of Horrors', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Eighties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Seventies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T18:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88672c69-87cc-543e-a6fc-a1c3cc98b659', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88672c69-87cc-543e-a6fc-a1c3cc98b659'}, {'abstract': 'In a foreclosure settlement with the federal government, banks would pay relatively little, proving again that accountability has been mostly A.W.O.L. in the aftermath of the 2008 crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/business/a-foreclosure-settlement-that-wouldnt-sting.html', 'snippet': 'In a foreclosure settlement with the federal government, banks would pay relatively little, proving again that accountability has been mostly A.W.O.L. in the aftermath of the 2008 crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AFTER months of back and forth, a deal that is supposed to punish large financial institutions for foreclosure misconduct may be nigh.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Deal That Wouldn’t Sting', 'kicker': 'Fair Game', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Deal That Wouldn’t Sting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attorneys General', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T18:01:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Morgenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morgenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2279a2ca-8f56-5644-bff6-ebfedbe3d6bb', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2279a2ca-8f56-5644-bff6-ebfedbe3d6bb'}, {'abstract': 'Inflation was high in 1979 when Paul Volcker introduced a new policy framework. Today, Ben Bernanke needs to stage a quiet revolution of his own to tame unemployment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/business/economy/ben-bernanke-needs-a-volcker-moment.html', 'snippet': 'Inflation was high in 1979 when Paul Volcker introduced a new policy framework. Today, Ben Bernanke needs to stage a quiet revolution of his own to tame unemployment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN October 1979, inflation was running at more than 10 percent a year, and the Federal Reserve’s gradual interest rate increases weren’t solving the problem. So Paul Volcker, the Fed chairman, dramatically changed how monetary policy was conducted. Today, an equally intractable unemployment crisis demands that Ben S. Bernanke, the current Fed chairman, stage a quiet revolution of his own.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/business/30view-pic/30view-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1007, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/business/30view-pic/30view-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/business/30view-pic/30view-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dear Ben: It’s Time for Your Volcker Moment', 'kicker': 'Economic View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dear Ben: It’s Time For a Volcker Moment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Volcker, Paul A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T18:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christina D. Romer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6cebae7-1543-54eb-9e11-4466000dd587', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6cebae7-1543-54eb-9e11-4466000dd587'}, {'abstract': 'Many Kurds are caught between guerrillas seeking minority rights and local autonomy and a central government that says it wants to make peace but fears carving up the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/world/europe/kurds-in-turkey-rended-by-war-that-haunts-country.html', 'snippet': 'Many Kurds are caught between guerrillas seeking minority rights and local autonomy and a central government that says it wants to make peace but fears carving up the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SIRNAK, Turkey — Portraits of Mevlude Gungen’s two eldest children hang just above the television, the only piece of furniture in her spare living room. On a recent day, the set was tuned to the station run by a Kurdish militant group, bringing her news of the conflict that has haunted her country — and her family — for years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/world/KURDS/KURDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/30/world/KURDS/KURDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/world/KURDS/KURDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/world/KURDS/KURDS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/world/KURDS/KURDS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Kurds in Turkey, a Country’s Conflict Rends Families', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Kurds in Turkey, a Country’s Conflict Rends Families', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kurdistan Workers Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T18:20:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/039f39b8-bb2a-5b52-a2cd-1c5600900bd4', 'word_count': 1283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/039f39b8-bb2a-5b52-a2cd-1c5600900bd4'}, {'abstract': 'What it tells us about the debate.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/29/more-thoughts-on-weaponized-keynesianism/', 'snippet': 'What it tells us about the debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let me follow up a bit on the sudden discovery by Republicans that cuts in government spending cost jobs and drive up the unemployment rate – as long as the spending is on destruction rather than construction. Oh, and thanks to commenters for reminding me of Barney Frank’s coinage, “weaponized Keynesianism.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Thoughts On Weaponized Keynesianism', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T18:20:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13273b01-6871-5d4d-bdcb-aa8ae29ff6f5', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13273b01-6871-5d4d-bdcb-aa8ae29ff6f5'}, {'abstract': 'Denied visas to the United States, Uganda’s Little League team may host a good-will baseball mission from Canada.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/sports/baseball/fund-raising-effort-to-send-canadian-team-to-face-uganda-youth-team.html', 'snippet': 'Denied visas to the United States, Uganda’s Little League team may host a good-will baseball mission from Canada.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the team from Kampala, Uganda, was denied visas and was unable to play in the Little League World Series last July, the filmmaker Jay Shapiro found himself adding a heart-rending chapter to the documentary he was filming about the team, and doing so in a sea of sympathy. All kinds of people, from children offering to donate their baseball mitts to major league players, contacted him to ask the same thing: what can I do?', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/sports/dog-uganda/dog-uganda-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/30/sports/dog-uganda/dog-uganda-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/sports/dog-uganda/dog-uganda-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/sports/dog-uganda/dog-uganda-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/sports/dog-uganda/dog-uganda-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ugandans May Get a Game Yet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ugandans May Get a Gam