: None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7aef579d-efbf-5cb4-bb99-6c62825f5134', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7aef579d-efbf-5cb4-bb99-6c62825f5134'}, {'abstract': 'Every Tuesday, Curry Without Worry distributes spicy restaurant-quality meals — what its founder calls “soul-pleasing food” — at no cost to both the hungry and the well-fed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/us/curry-without-worry-soup-kitchen-feeds-the-haves-and-the-have-nots.html', 'snippet': 'Every Tuesday, Curry Without Worry distributes spicy restaurant-quality meals — what its founder calls “soul-pleasing food” — at no cost to both the hungry and the well-fed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the evening light dimmed, Shrawan Nepali greeted each person who stood in a long line waiting for his food: a woman with her butterscotch-colored cocker spaniel, a poet poring over a mystery book, art students, commuters, a homeless woman with crimson sneakers and men wearing black hoods to guard against the cold and conversation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/us/30BCCURRY/30BCCURRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/us/30BCCURRY/30BCCURRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/us/30BCCURRY/30BCCURRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bringing the Haves and Have-Nots Together for Curry and Compassion', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bringing the Haves and Have-Nots Together for Curry and Compassion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Curry (Cuisine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soup Kitchens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FOOD BANK', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Project Open Hand', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T19:38:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Pogash', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb7a836f-0015-5fd5-8845-e860a0ef31b7', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb7a836f-0015-5fd5-8845-e860a0ef31b7'}, {'abstract': 'After his cellphone was stolen in South Africa, a T-Mobile customer wound up with a monstrous bill — and asked the Haggler to intervene.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/your-money/a-cellphone-theft-and-a-25000-phone-bill.html', 'snippet': 'After his cellphone was stolen in South Africa, a T-Mobile customer wound up with a monstrous bill — and asked the Haggler to intervene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Haggler has been traveling recently, and that can mean only one thing: a column that opens with a rant about traveling. Our subject this time is hotel doors, the kind that go ka-boom when they close.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/business/30-HAGGLER/30-HAGGLER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/business/30-HAGGLER/30-HAGGLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/business/30-HAGGLER/30-HAGGLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mystery of the $25,000 Phone Bill', 'kicker': 'The Haggler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Mystery Of the $25,000 Phone Bill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-29T19:41:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Segal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Segal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/495fe695-6e56-5874-9657-cdb8a3dad78e', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/495fe695-6e56-5874-9657-cdb8a3dad78e'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Berke, calling himself a member of the After Party, promotes his candidacy with videos in which he smokes marijuana, cavorts with models and downs vodka shots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/us/politics/miami-beach-comedians-serious-mostly-candidacy.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Berke, calling himself a member of the After Party, promotes his candidacy with videos in which he smokes marijuana, cavorts with models and downs vodka shots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI BEACH — Wearing a black suit and tie with neon-pink laces on his kicks, the man in the video struggles