cases that can be helped by early detection through widespread screening are small in number.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After decades in which cancer screening was promoted as an unmitigated good, as the best — perhaps only — way for people to protect themselves from the ravages of a frightening disease, a pronounced shift is under way.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/us/SCREENING/SCREENING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 956, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/30/us/SCREENING/SCREENING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/30/us/SCREENING/SCREENING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Considering When It Might Be Best Not to Know About Cancer', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Considering When It Might Be Best Not to Know About Cancer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Preventive Services Task Force', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breast Cancer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostate Specific Antigen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mammography', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostate Cancer', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cervical Cancer', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011