e fan at the commencement of an event that would forever alter the landscape of thoroughbred horse racing.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/breeders-cup-memories-from-the-first-break-of-the-gate/', 'snippet': 'Remembering how exciting it was to be a race fan at the commencement of an event that would forever alter the landscape of thoroughbred horse racing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was at Hollywood Park on Nov. 10, 1984, for the inaugural running of the Breeders’ Cup. My dad and I had been going to races in Southern California for just over a decade by that time, and we rarely missed a feature race on a weekend at any of the area’s major tracks, so there was no way we were missing the first Breeders’ Cup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breeders’ Cup Memories, From the First Break Out of the Gate', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Breeders' Cup (Horse Race)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T13:26:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rich Perloff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rich', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perloff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/262d300b-19f4-51ee-8ab2-865cd07ec4d2', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/262d300b-19f4-51ee-8ab2-865cd07ec4d2'}, {'abstract': 'By building a wall of sandbags to spare the low-lying Thai capital, in the delta of the country’s main river system, officials have sacrificed the provinces to the north.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/world/asia/31iht-thailand31.html', 'snippet': 'By building a wall of sandbags to spare the low-lying Thai capital, in the delta of the country’s main river system, officials have sacrificed the provinces to the north.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — Shielded by hundreds of thousands of sandbags piled shoulder high along the city’s outskirts, most of Bangkok remained dry on Sunday, allaying fears for now that the massive metropolis would be swamped by monsoon floodwaters.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/world/THAILAND/THAILAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/31/world/THAILAND/THAILAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/world/THAILAND/THAILAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/world/THAILAND/THAILAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/31/world/THAILAND/THAILAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Floodwalls Keep Bangkok Dry but Provinces Angry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Floodwalls Keep Bangkok Dry but Provinces Angry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yingluck Shinawatra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangkok (Thailand)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T13:49:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26f294b9-112d-5681-aefd-1e66040df5d5', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26f294b9-112d-5681-aefd-1e66040df5d5'}, {'abstract': 'Checking in on the documentary “Fires of Faith.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/channel-surfing-fires-of-faith-part-3/', 'snippet': 'Checking in on the documentary “Fires of Faith.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s perhaps the most beloved (and, for many, most sacred) book ever published in the West, but oh, the birth pangs. BYUtv has been exploring the creation of the King James Bible in “Fires of Faith,” a well-made three-part documentary (also viewable on the channel’s Web site) that concludes Sunday night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Channel Surfing: ‘Fires of Faith,’ Part 3', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T14:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc60250b-f0da-5863-8499-3b3cc75524ff', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc60250b-f0da-5863-8499-3b3cc75524ff'}, {'abstract': 'Think of it as a communication strategy.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/a-volcker-moment-indeed-slightly-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'Think of it as a communication strategy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christina Romer calls on Ben Bernanke to adopt a nominal GDP target, and suggests that he consider himself in a position comparable to that of Paul Volcker — where Volcker took drastic action to fight inflation, Bernanke should do likewise to fight unemployment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Volcker Moment Indeed (Slightly Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T14:33:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c562d872-a42e-5373-9c19-e90e25f25809', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c562d872-a42e-5373-9c19-e90e25f25809'}, {'abstract': 'Fallacies presented as news analysis.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/social-security-bait-and-switch-a-continuing-series/', 'snippet': 'Fallacies presented as news analysis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dean Baker is angry at the Washington Post for spreading disinformation about Social Security. He’s right, of course — and it’s shocking that a well-known fallacy is the subject of a “news analysis” that purports to inform readers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Social Security Bait And Switch, A Continuing Series', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T14:47:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/104d91ca-2262-5e77-8656-d1c41a08b115', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/104d91ca-2262-5e77-8656-d1c41a08b115'}, {'abstract': 'At a memorial service for her brother, Mona Simpson recalled his love of beauty and his family, and his final moments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/opinion/mona-simpsons-eulogy-for-steve-jobs.html', 'snippet': 'At a memorial service for her brother, Mona Simpson recalled his love of beauty and his family, and his final moments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I grew up as an only child, with a single mother. Because we were poor and because I knew my father had emigrated from Syria, I imagined he looked like Omar Sharif. I hoped he would be rich and kind and would come into our lives (and our not yet furnished apartment) and help us. Later, after I’d met my father, I tried to believe he’d changed his number and left no forwarding address because he was an idealistic revolutionary, plotting a new world for the Arab people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sister’s Eulogy for Steve Jobs', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Sister&#8217;s Eulogy for Steve Jobs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T15:11:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mona Simpson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simpson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/91f2c65a-dba1-5df2-bc38-40d4eda3932c', 'word_count': 2384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91f2c65a-dba1-5df2-bc38-40d4eda3932c'}, {'abstract': 'Rick Perry says he has the skills to debate President Obama, despite concerns about his debate performances.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/committing-to-debates-perry-plays-down-the-issue/', 'snippet': 'Rick Perry says he has the skills to debate President Obama, despite concerns about his debate performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as Rick Perry admits he has struggled during televised debates against the polished Mitt Romney and other G.O.P. candidates, the Texas governor maintains he could handle President Obama, a man he has acknowledged to be a “very good debater.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Committing to Debates, Perry Plays Down the Issue', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wallace, Chris', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T15:13:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e728251-9a39-56a1-a53d-cc3d9aea988f', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e728251-9a39-56a1-a53d-cc3d9aea988f'}, {'abstract': 'On “Face the Nation,” Bob Schieffer, who blames tobacco for his past bout with cancer, takes issue with the Cain campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/can-gets-tough-treatment-for-videos-cigarette-scene/', 'snippet': 'On “Face the Nation,” Bob Schieffer, who blames tobacco for his past bout with cancer, takes issue with the Cain campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON – Had Herman Cain known he would be running into a human buzzsaw named Bob Schieffer on Sunday, he might have had second thoughts about including a now infamous scene at the end of his new campaign video that shows his chief of staff, Mark Block, coolly smoking a cigarette.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cain Gets Tough Treatment for Video’s Cigarette Scene', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Block, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schieffer, Bob', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T16:20:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article',