sues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Plouffe, a senior adviser to President Obama and one of the chief architects of his 2008 victory, accused Mitt Romney of trimming his views for political gain and lacking the conviction needed to hold high office. The comments were unusual for their harsh assessment of Mr. Romney’s politics and his character at this early stage of the campaign and for the fact that they came from an official serving in the White House rather than in Mr. Obama’s Chicago-based re-election campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Adviser Unloads on Romney', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plouffe, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T17:23:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46cba933-9462-58e6-941f-e21a44e4b2ff', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46cba933-9462-58e6-941f-e21a44e4b2ff'}, {'abstract': 'With a surge in the polls, Herman Cain’s crowds have been standing room only, which he attributes to voters overcoming hesitations about his ability to gain the nomination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/us/cain-hopes-his-moment-in-the-sun-endures.html', 'snippet': 'With a surge in the polls, Herman Cain’s crowds have been standing room only, which he attributes to voters overcoming hesitations about his ability to gain the nomination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOMEWOOD, Ala. — For Herman Cain, these have been the sweet days. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/us/politics/31cain1/31cain1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/us/politics/31cain1/31cain1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/31/us/politics/31cain1/31cain1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tested Again and Again, Cain Takes Comfort in His Rise in the Polls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tested Again and Again, Cain Takes Comfort in His Rise in the Polls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T17:38:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material':