, affection between humans and animals is seen as a type of illness.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/the-pathology-of-dependence-on-animals/', 'snippet': 'In a nation where hunting and meat eating is idealized, affection between humans and animals is seen as a type of illness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a 1991 interview titled “Eating Well,” Jacques Derrida wonders whether a head of state (chef d’Etat) could gain office by declaring himself or herself a vegetarian.\xa0 He concludes, “The chief (chef) must be an eater of flesh.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pet Lovers, Pathologized', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T19:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kelly Oliver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kelly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oliver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47ad892f-9b8a-528a-bcbf-0fb583985f19', 'word_count': 1063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47ad892f-9b8a-528a-bcbf-0fb583985f19'}, {'abstract': 'Above the bustling street level, apartments in East Harlem are boarded up and vacant, with owners content to earn income off storefronts rather than deal with the trouble of renters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/nyregion/east-harlem-landlords-keep-apartments-sealed-up.html', 'snippet': 'Above the bustling street level, apartments in East Harlem are boarded up and vacant, with owners content to earn income off storefronts rather than deal with the trouble of renters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'East Harlem has been undergoing a resurgence for two decades, yet the neighborhood is still pockmarked with four- or five-story walk-ups where the ground-floor stores are bustling and the apartments above are devoid of life. Their windows are boarded up, blocked up or just drearily empty, torn curtains testifying to no one’s having lived there for years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/nyregion/31empty2/31empty2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/31/nyregion/31empty2/31empty2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/nyregion/31empty2/31empty2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In East Harlem, ‘Keep Out’ Signs Apply to Renters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In East Harlem, ‘Keep Out’ Signs Apply to Renters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Landlords', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Harlem (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T19:58:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66ca7721-56af-5efe-8b2b-aa95263e1f6c', 'word_count': 1079, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66ca7721-56af-5efe-8b2b-aa95263e1f6c'}, {'abstract': 'Legislators in Nebraska have been unexpectedly summoned to a special session over the Keystone XL pipeline, which would run through the states on its way from Canada to the Gulf Coast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/business/energy-environment/nebraska-legislature-to-debate-keystone-xl-oil-pipeline.html', 'snippet': 'Legislators in Nebraska have been unexpectedly summoned to a special session over the Keystone XL pipeline, which would run through the states on its way from Canada to the Gulf Coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a federal decision anticipated soon on whether an oil pipeline will be allowed to run from Canada through the nation’s midsection, lawmakers in Nebraska are being summoned on Tuesday to an unexpected legislative session over the issue, which has stirred up a level of rancor that few had predicted.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/business/energy-environment/31pipeline-map/31pipeline-map-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 468, 'width': 260, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nebraska Seeks a Say on the Route of a Pipeline', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nebraska Seeks a Say On the Route Of a Pipeline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Keystone Pipeline System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Sands', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TransCanada Corporation', 'rank':