nk': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC News', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MSNBC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T21:34:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d317bba1-9411-55b8-8a64-7838ee5d4308', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d317bba1-9411-55b8-8a64-7838ee5d4308'}, {'abstract': 'Still looping.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/european-doom-loop/', 'snippet': 'Still looping.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For once — and I almost never say this — I think Dean Baker is being a bit too hard here. The Draghi piece was mainly a profile, and I’m willing to cut a bit of slack on the macro analysis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'European Doom Loop', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T21:38:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57ac0c46-bc47-57e4-8e31-9f2dc477820e', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57ac0c46-bc47-57e4-8e31-9f2dc477820e'}, {'abstract': 'If we can learn not to freak out when they freak out, we can help them learn to regulate emotions on their own.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/seeing-tantrums-as-distress-not-defiance/', 'snippet': 'If we can learn not to freak out when they freak out, we can help them learn to regulate emotions on their own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I describe the process I went through to get my 3-year-old into preschool to non-New Yorkers, they look at me as if I was wearing an astronaut suit to a dinner party. Eight interviews? Eight tours? Eight applications? For a kid who still has trouble drinking out of a cup? Absurd. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeing Tantrums as Distress, Not Defiance', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T21:51:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenny Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad92f567-8b48-5449-8965-404c4bae3eb3', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad92f567-8b48-5449-8965-404c4bae3eb3'}, {'abstract': 'A punk rocker-turned-comedic actor-turned mayor of Reykjavik, Iceland, checks in at a local radio festival.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/for-a-free-form-radio-conference-a-kindred-spirit/', 'snippet': 'A punk rocker-turned-comedic actor-turned mayor of Reykjavik, Iceland, checks in at a local radio festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would be hard to overstate the level of preposterousness that surrounds Jon Gnarr, the punk rocker-turned-comedic actor-turned mayor of Reykjavik, Iceland. Mr. Gnarr was elected in 2010 after he formed a quasi-satirical political party, the Best Party; his campaign promises included putting a polar bear in the city zoo and offering free towels in the swimming pools — as well as a promise to break all his campaign promises.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Free-Form Radio Conference, a Kindred Spirit', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gnarr, Jon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Reykjavik (Iceland)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T21:56:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2a149e0-919a-5761-8845-493ed598486e', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2a149e0-919a-5761-8845-493ed598486e'}, {'abstract': 'Jeff Chen delivers a puzzle with bite.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/halloween/', 'snippet': 'Jeff Chen delivers a puzzle with bite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — Happy Halloween, everybody! Have you all purchased your candy to dole out to trick-or-treaters? Anyone dressing up in costume for the holiday? Here on the East Coast, we’re having a very snowy Halloween, and if I was going to dress up, it would most likely be as a Resentful Homeowner Who Is Getting Really Tired of Shoveling Her Walkway. On the other hand, I’m hoping there will be lots of chocolate left over to make it worth my while. There’s always a silver lining, am I right?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday: A Halloween Puzzle With Bite', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T22:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93e0ade3-0870-5cf4-8935-7de21e09c9eb', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93e0ade3-0870-5cf4-8935-7de21e09c9eb'}, {'abstract': 'The demand for the skills required by many new advertising jobs exceeds the number of professionals who have them, particularly in jobs requiring advanced mathematics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/business/media/ad-companies-face-a-widening-talent-gap.html', 'snippet': 'The demand for the skills required by many new advertising jobs exceeds the number of professionals who have them, particularly in jobs requiring advanced mathematics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Ad:tech advertising technology conference hits New York next week, marketers, advertising agencies and recruiters may spend less time listening to the panelists and more time working the floor to find new employees. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/business/Talent/Talent-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/business/Talent/Talent-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/31/business/Talent/Talent-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Advertising Companies Fret Over a Digital Talent Gap', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Advertising Companies Fret Over a Digital Talent Gap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T22:08:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68aea5ab-3ea0-5c8b-a8ad-768a13164ff4', 'word_count': 1171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68aea5ab-3ea0-5c8b-a8ad-768a13164ff4'}, {'abstract': 'The Red Bulls’ 1-0 loss to the Galaxy on Sunday ended with the teams’ pushing and shoving at midfield, and both teams lost a player for the second leg as a result.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/what-was-rafa-marquez-thinking/', 'snippet': 'The Red Bulls’ 1-0 loss to the Galaxy on Sunday ended with the teams’ pushing and shoving at midfield, and both teams lost a player for the second leg as a result.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Red Bulls’ 1-0 loss to the Galaxy on Sunday ended with the teams’ pushing and shoving at midfield after the Red Bulls’ Rafael Marquez threw the ball at a Galaxy player after the final whistle. Moments later, Marquez and defender Stephen Keel were flat on their backs, with Keel apparently bloodied in the melee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Was Rafa Marquez Thinking?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T22:10:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bcde8e5-2743-50ab-b662-54dc2c15173f', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bcde8e5-2743-50ab-b662-54dc2c15173f'}, {'abstract': 'Huntsman takes on Mitt Romney with a video that highlights his changing positions.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/huntsman-video-takes-on-romney-backflips/', 'snippet': 'Huntsman takes on Mitt Romney with a video that highlights his changing positions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The campaign of Jon M. Huntsman Jr. on Sunday released a Web video titled “Backflip,” which highlights what it calls some of Mitt Romney‘s flips on issues like abortion, gun control and the Ohio proposal to curb the bargaining power of unions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Huntsman Video Takes On Romney ‘Backflips’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T22:11:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Mullany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mullany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2929177d-884d-5fda-855e-83078567d138', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2929177d-884d-5fda-855e-83078567d138'}, {'abstract': 'With “Sannidhanam: The Temple and the Goddess,” the dancer Rama Vaidyanathan brought southern India’s Bharatanatyam style of movement to New York University on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/arts/dance/rama-vaidyanathan-at-skirball-center-review.html', 'snippet': 'With “Sannidhanam: The Temple and the Goddess,” the dancer Rama Vaidyanathan brought southern India’s Bharatanatyam style of movement to New York University on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do we watch dance in terms of form or expression? As shapes, rhythms and beauty or as meanings, stories and significance? Actually, there’s no either/or about it. Dancing is both/and: both a metric, spatial pattern and a profoundly human act at the same time. Yet it always takes me aback to see how drastically Indian classical dance often sets up an apparent dichotomy. That bit was about angles and meters, this bit is about character, emotion and story. But one dancer performs both. By commuting between the two aspects, she demonstrates contrasting planes of existence.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/arts/Dancing/Dancing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 831, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/arts/Dancing/Dancing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/31/arts/Dancing/Dancing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love and Eros in Motion Among the Deities', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love and Eros in Motion Among the Deities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vaidyanathan, Rama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T22:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/461ace7f-08ff-5e03-bf5e-abb3b62e8e72', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/461ace7f-08ff-5e03-bf5e-abb3b62e8e72'}, {'abstract': 'The UChicago Conference on Jersey Shore Studies on Friday attracted media-studies scholars, sociologists, humorists and philosophers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/arts/television/jersey-shore-has-its-day-at-university-of-chicago.html', 'snippet': 'The UChicago Conference on Jersey Shore Studies on Friday attracted media-studies scholars, sociologists, humorists and philosophers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — When Deena Cortese was added to the cast of “Jersey Shore” in Season 3, she was nervous that she wouldn’t be welcome, that she wouldn’t be able to forge a place for herself in a group with well-established social dynamics.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/arts/31SHORE/31SHORE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/arts/31SHORE/31SHORE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/31/arts/31SHORE/31SHORE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Jersey Shore’ Arrives in Academia. Discuss.', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Jersey Shore’ Arrives in Academia. Discuss.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Chicago', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sociology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polizzi, Nicole', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T22:32:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b71ca31-2a19-5dbd-a5fe-0357b087865d', 'word_count': 1136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b71ca31-2a19-5dbd-a5fe-0357b087865d'}, {'abstract': 'Artistic differences are cited in the fracturing of the classical music partnership of Hélène Grimaud and Claudio Abbado, ahead of the release of a recording by Ms. Grimaud.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/arts/music/helene-grimaud-and-claudio-abbado-part-ways.html', 'snippet': 'Artistic differences are cited in the fracturing of the classical music partnership of Hélène Grimaud and Claudio Abbado, ahead of the release of a recording by Ms. Grimaud.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Artistic differences.” It’s the euphemism of choice to save face and explain away unpleasant disputes among performers. The phrase pops up all the time in the arts, but in truth it describes nothing.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/arts/2d-sub-HELENE-2/2d-sub-HELENE-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/arts/2d-sub-HELENE-2/2d-sub-HELENE-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/31/arts/2d-sub-HELENE-2/2d-sub-HELENE-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Titans Clash Over a Mere Cadenza', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Titans Clash Over a Mere Cadenza', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABBADO, CLAUDIO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mozart, Wolfgang Amadeus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Busoni, Ferruccio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank'