mpanies, died Thursday in Chicago. He was 85. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/business/pritzker-obit/pritzker-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 736, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/business/pritzker-obit/pritzker-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/31/business/pritzker-obit/pritzker-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert A. Pritzker Dies at 85; Led Family Business', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Robert A. Pritzker, 85; Led Family Business', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hyatt Hotels Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pritzker, Jay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T23:38:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Williams Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Williams', 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/69af3a32-77ca-529f-9015-ff167bee3e43', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69af3a32-77ca-529f-9015-ff167bee3e43'}, {'abstract': 'At the world team championships in the Netherlands on Saturday, much to the delight of hundreds of spectators, the Bermuda Bowl was won by the host nation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/crosswords/bridge/the-dutch-are-hosts-and-winners-of-bermuda-bowl-bridge.html', 'snippet': 'At the world team championships in the Netherlands on Saturday, much to the delight of hundreds of spectators, the Bermuda Bowl was won by the host nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VELDHOVEN, the Netherlands — At the world team championships here on Saturday, much to the delight of hundreds of spectators, the Bermuda Bowl was won by the host nation. In the 128-board final Sjoert Brink, Bas Drijver, Bauke Muller, Simon de Wijs, Ricco van Prooijen and Louk Verhees Jr., with Eric Laurant the nonplaying captain, defeated U.S.A.-2: Daniel Zagorin, Kevin Bathurst, Joe Grue, Justin Lall, John Hurd and Joel Wooldridge, with Curtis Cheek the nonplaying captain. The final score was 300 international match points to 255. Italy was third.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dutch Hosts Are Winners of Bermuda Bowl', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dutch Hosts Are Winners of Bermuda Bowl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T23:46:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c61de0a-376f-5268-9d8e-16381d7