to announce the 2012 season of its American Songbook series, a typically eclectic lineup that is to feature several Tony Award winners and a group of celebrated pop composers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/theater/american-songbook-slate-lands-top-stage-talent.html', 'snippet': 'Lincoln Center is to announce the 2012 season of its American Songbook series, a typically eclectic lineup that is to feature several Tony Award winners and a group of celebrated pop composers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lincoln Center is to announce on Monday the 2012 season of its American Songbook series, a typically eclectic lineup that is to feature several Tony Award winners, a group of celebrated pop composers and a solo acoustic set by Thurston Moore, the Sonic Youth co-founder. The concert series, which is scheduled to run from Jan. 11 through Feb. 11 at the Allen Room of Frederick P. Rose Hall, is to include Mr. Moore (Feb. 2); Elaine Paige , the British musical theater actress (Feb. 10); and a performance by Lin-Manuel Miranda previewing his new work, “The Hamilton Mixtape” (Jan. 11). The lineup is also to include the Broadway stars LaChanze (Jan. 19), Michael Cerveris (Jan. 21) and Laura Benanti (Feb 11).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Songbook Slate Lands Top Stage Talent', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Songbook Slate Lands Top Stage Talent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Songbook (Music Series)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-30T23:53:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theat