ew-ad-race-but-the-vehicles-are-retreads/', 'snippet': 'The quadrennial series of presidential campaign ads that is beginning to appear for the 2012 race will largely feature stock characters, like the Humble Statesman and the Flip-Flopping Weasel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON—In Mitt Romney’s telling, Gov.Rick Perry made Texas a wasteland. Under the words “Unemployment Has Doubled,” a tumbleweed rolls across a barren highway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Ad Race, but the Vehicles Are Retreads', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T00:12:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Harwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e1a2d17-c71e-5251-8a5e-c8f51a69162b', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e1a2d17-c71e-5251-8a5e-c8f51a69162b'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time since fighting broke out in the Yemeni capital, Sana International Airport came under direct attack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/world/middleeast/airport-in-sana-yemen-is-hit-by-shells.html', 'snippet': 'For the first time since fighting broke out in the Yemeni capital, Sana International Airport came under direct attack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANA, Yemen — For the first time since fighting broke out here in the Yemeni capital, Sana International Airport came under direct attack on Sunday night, in a possible move by opposition forces to escalate the conflict with the government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Airport in Yemen Is Hit by Shells as Attacks in the Capital Widen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Airport in Yemen Is Hit by Shells As Attacks in the Capital Widen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T00:13:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Kasinof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kasinof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0e7f530-c371-5853-8eb5-45e29b929788', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0e7f530-c371-5853-8eb5-45e29b929788'}, {'abstract': 'The former head of the Democratic National Committee under President Obama, Clyde Williams has raised nearly $50,000 for a race against Charles B. Rangel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/nyregion/clyde-williams-likely-to-challenge-rangel-for-seat-in-house.html', 'snippet': 'The former head of the Democratic National Committee under President Obama, Clyde Williams has raised nearly $50,000 for a race against Charles B. Rangel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He survived an ethics investigation and a humiliating censure vote on the floor of the House. He endured a brutal re-election battle. Now Representative Charles B. Rangel may face yet another tough challenge to his dwindling power and stature.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/nyregion/rangel1/rangel1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/nyregion/rangel1/rangel1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/31/nyregion/rangel1/rangel1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Adviser to White House Is Likely to Seek Rangel’s Seat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Adviser To White House Is Likely to Seek Rangel’s Seat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Keith L T', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rangel, Charles B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'HARLEM (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T00:13:35+0000', 'document_type