6-5cf1-9f44-5379e848dc9a'}, {'abstract': 'The club that has for decades organized the New York City Marathon is unveiling a new look on Monday, the better to emphasize its broader mission as fitness promoters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/sports/new-york-road-runners-rebrands-to-emphasize-broader-mission.html', 'snippet': 'The club that has for decades organized the New York City Marathon is unveiling a new look on Monday, the better to emphasize its broader mission as fitness promoters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, most people have known the New York Road Runners as the organizer of the New York City Marathon, and rightly so. The event draws 45,000 runners from all over the world, attracts more than 2 million spectators and is broadcast internationally. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Road Runners’ Manifesto: More Than Marathoners', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Road Runners’ Manifesto: More Than Marathoners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organizations, Societies and Clubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Road Runners Club', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T00:20:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2de1058-f11b-51fc-9ef6-742784f0cb9c', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2de1058-f11b-51fc-9ef6-742784f0cb9c'}, {'abstract': 'Oyster River Middle School in Durham, N.H., is struggling to stay true to its traditions of excellence while meeting the federal standards set by the No Child Left Behind Law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/education/no-child-left-behind-catches-up-with-new-hampshire-school.html', 'snippet': 'Oyster River Middle School in Durham, N.H., is struggling to stay true to its traditions of excellence while meeting the federal standards set by the No Child Left Behind Law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURHAM, N.H. — Every spring, Linda Rief, who is in her 25th year of teaching English at Oyster River Middle School, has eighth graders do a semester-long “genre” project. They pick a subject area like mysteries, read masters like Agatha Christie, study the writer’s craftsmanship (“Explain how the author foreshadows doom”), then draft their own.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/us/WINERIP/WINERIP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/31/us/WINERIP/WINERIP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/us/WINERIP/WINERIP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/us/WINERIP/WINERIP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/31/us/WINERIP/WINERIP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Standardized Era, a Creative School Is Forced to Be More So', 'kicker': 'On Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'prin