, 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecc863e7-a5ed-5544-bbca-7712e180e436'}, {'abstract': 'A veteran Army officer’s surprising compassion for the prisoners of war in Boston.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/30/the-light-in-a-dark-harbor/', 'snippet': 'A veteran Army officer’s surprising compassion for the prisoners of war in Boston.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mid-autumn dusk of Oct. 31, 1861 cloaked Boston’s island-studded harbor as the revolving beacon atop Boston Light began to glow. The beams radiating from the lighthouse’s bold white pillar sparkled in the enfeebled eyes of the men huddled aboard the steamer the State of Maine, making its way slowly toward the military prison at Fort Warren, an island garrison near the harbor’s outer edge. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Light in a Dark Harbor', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T01:21:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55eabe8b-18d7-5f53-a4c0-e512c8a230a1', 'word_count': 1499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55eabe8b-18d7-5f53-a4c0-e512c8a230a1'}, {'abstract': 'As time runs short in the nominating contest, Gov. Rick Perry of Texas is using new advisers and a new strategy on how to better introduce a candidate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/us/politics/rick-perry-presses-for-second-look-from-early-voters.html', 'snippet': 'As time runs short in the nominating contest, Gov. Rick Perry of Texas is using new advisers and a new strategy on how to better introduce a candidate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — With time running short before the first votes are cast in the Republican presidential contest, Gov. Rick Perry of Texas is urgently trying to convince voters that his candidacy warrants a second look. He is retooling his campaign with a newly emphatic anti-Washington message and steering the race into a sharper ideological contrast with Mitt Romney.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/us/REPUBS/REPUBS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/us/REPUBS/REPUBS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/31/us/REPUBS/REPUBS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Perry Presses for Second Look From Early Voters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perry Presses for Second Look From Early Voters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T01:22:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk