nd possibly being convicted on a more serious charge with a stiffer sentence. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Duty of Effective Counsel', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Duty of Effective Counsel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plea Bargaining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T02:08:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/248de6f3-f62b-5647-8a94-e0d600787f0f', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/248de6f3-f62b-5647-8a94-e0d600787f0f'}, {'abstract': 'Intensive federal effort is needed to help vulnerable families before the homelessness situation gets worse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/opinion/ever-more-homeless-families.html', 'snippet': 'Intensive federal effort is needed to help vulnerable families before the homelessness situation gets worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An increase in poverty and rising rents produced a spike in homelessness among families in recent years. With the economy still weak and 14 million people out of work, the situation is bound to get worse. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ever More Homeless Families', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ever More Homeless Families', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing and Urban Development Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Recovery and Reinvestment Act (2009)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T02:11:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dede516-d7ac-5ac4-a1c9-b1702a99e060', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dede516-d7ac-5ac4-a1c9-b1702a99e060'}, {'abstract': 'Unnecessary horn honking might be hard to fix, but New York City drivers could use the reminder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/opinion/the-350-honk.html', 'snippet': 'Unnecessary horn honking might be hard to fix, but New York City drivers could use the reminder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, it has been illegal in New York City to use “any claxon installed on a motor vehicle” except in an emergency or, unfortunately, as one of those irritating car alarms. The fine for unnecessary horn-blowing is steep — $350 per summons — although very few tickets are given out, which may explain the din.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The $350 Honk', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The $350 Honk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'su