elping hand and a gloved fist in efforts to resolve shortages that have worsened greatly in recent years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/health/policy/medicine-shortages-addressed-in-obama-executive-order.html', 'snippet': 'An executive order by the Obama administration offers drug manufacturers and wholesalers a helping hand and a gloved fist in efforts to resolve shortages that have worsened greatly in recent years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama will issue an executive order on Monday that the administration hopes will help resolve a growing number of critical shortages of vital medicines used to treat life-threatening illnesses, among them several forms of cancer and bacterial infections.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Tries to Speed Response to Shortages in Vital Medicines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Tries to Speed Response To Shortages in Vital Medicines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shortages', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T04:14:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/302823d6-9f25-579d-aabe-2ad78a677620', 'word_count': 1025, 'uri': 'nyt://article/302823d6-9f25-579d-aabe-2ad78a677620'}, {'abstract': 'NYT Front Page for 10/31/2011', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/10/31/multimedia/31frontpage.html', 'snippet': 'NYT Front Page for 10/31/2011', 'lead_paragraph': 'NYT Front Page for 10/31/2011', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NYT Front Page for 10/31/2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T04:30:40+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/aaf79d69-2908-5ce8-bc52-a22d0a14baaa', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/aaf79d69-2908-5ce8-bc52-a22d0a14baaa'}, {'abstract': 'The owner of a seafood restaurant finds something else he can harvest locally.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/mining-salt-from-the-sea/', 'snippet': 'The owner of a seafood restaurant finds something else he can harvest locally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the magical aspects of running a business is how it eventually taps into everything you know, or thought you knew. Maybe that’s why you got into that particular business in the first place, without ever knowing about this secret synergy. Southfork Kitchen has drawn upon just about every experience or interest I have ever had, both obvious and all but forgotten, from music to design, food to entertainment, media to human interaction (oy, those human interactions!). More than a string of nouns, it is nearly a summation of a life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mining Salt From the Sea', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Buschel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buschel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b678d913-1836-5354-b1d3-552d76371e04', 'word_count': 1375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b678d913-1836-5354-b1d3-552d76371e04'}, {'abstract': 'In this episode of “The Good Wife,” the lawyers one-up each other in the connections game.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/good-wife-watch-its-all-about-connections/', 'snippet': 'In this episode of “The Good Wife,” the lawyers one-up each other in the connections game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rare occurrence on “Affairs of State,” the season’s sixth episode of “The Good Wife” on Sunday night: Alicia Florrick was unequivocally on the wrong side of the case. She and the new associate, Caitlin, defended a Taiwanese student who was a suspect in a rape and murder aboard a party boat. The story seemed to revolve around the question of diplomatic immunity (in this case, the lack thereof), but that was a MacGuffin. In the final minutes we and Alicia discovered that she had been defending the killer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Good Wife’ Watch: It’s All About Connections', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T05:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74e1a9b4-6e1a-58a0-947e-481d48c5432f', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74e1a9b4-6e1a-58a0-947e-481d48c5432f'}, {'abstract': 'Postal services in Germany and other European nations have reinvented themselves over the past decade. The United States Postal Service, facing insolvency, is now looking toward Europe for new operating models.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/10/23/world/20111023NEWPOSTAL.html', 'snippet': 'Postal services in Germany and other European nations have reinvented themselves over the past decade. The United States Postal Service, facing insolvency, is now looking toward Europe for new operating models.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Postal services in Germany and other European nations have reinvented themselves over the past decade. The United States Postal Service, facing insolvency, is now looking toward Europe for new operating models.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/world/20111023NEWPOSTAL-slide-FHGB/20111023NEWPOSTAL-slide-FHGB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/23/world/20111023NEWPOSTAL-slide-FHGB/20111023NEWPOSTAL-slide-FHGB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/23/world/20111023NEWPOSTAL-slide-FHGB/20111023NEWPOSTAL-slide-FHGB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Postal Services Adapt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post Offices and Equipment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Postal Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T05:08:44+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6aab619c-c6fe-5657-8f63-be1cbc5983b3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6aab619c-c6fe-5657-8f63-be1cbc5983b3'}, {'abstract': 'Top news on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/newswallah-in-the-english-language-press-monday-5/', 'snippet': 'Top news on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'India successfully hosted its first-ever Grand Prix on Sunday, in front of a 95,000 strong crowd at the Buddh International Circuit outside New Delhi. National dailies were united Monday in their praise for the “flawlessly executed” event (Times of India), which has “dispelled myths”\xa0(CNN-IBN) about India’s ability to host high-end sporting events after the debacle of the Commonwealth Games. “I honestly cannot wait to come back to India,” said the two-time world champion Sebastian Vettel, echoing the sentiments of other Formula One drivers whose time in India has left an “indelible mark” on them (Indian Express). “Good tracks these F1 fellows are used to but friendly, open people proved to be India’s greatest ambassadors,” according to the Hindustan Times. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: In the English-Language Press Monday', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hazare, Anna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T05:12:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikhila Gill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikhila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d40a9950-3f15-5a1f-be35-48cc5d7795a6', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d40a9950-3f15-5a1f-be35-48cc5d7795a6'}, {'abstract': 'Can a movement built on disdain for politics can survive the down-and-dirty of Indian political life?', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/will-the-middle-class-stick-by-team-anna/', 'snippet': 'Can a movement built on disdain for politics can survive the down-and-dirty of Indian political life?', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no question that any deep political engagement among India’s rapidly growing middle class is a major threat to the status quo in Indian politics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will the Middle Class Stick by Team Anna?', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'na