g Sikh security guards. The men were angry at Gandhi’s authorization of a military attack on a revered Sikh temple in Amritsar five months earlier.Gandhi, the daughter of Indian independence leader and first Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru, first acceded to prime minister in 1966. Her New York Times obituary described her as “strong-willed, autocratic and determined to govern an almost ungovernable nation that seemed always in strife” and “a decisive—some said dictatorial—leader.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oct. 31, 1984 | Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi Assassinated', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T08:25:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4b66e43-4074-5e4e-a4ea-f87e358d5580', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4b66e43-4074-5e4e-a4ea-f87e358d5580'}, {'abstract': 'On film, he has looked every bit as bad as his numbers indicate. His lateral agility is gone, as is his stop/start burst and quickness. He appears to be thinking rather than playing.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/more-than-a-slump-for-titans-chris-johnson/', 'snippet': 'On film, he has looked every bit as bad as his numbers indicate. His lateral agility is gone, as is his stop/start burst and quickness. He appears to be thinking rather than playing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Don’t mean to harp on the negative after a 17-point victory for the Titans on Sunday, but what in the world is wrong with Chris Johnson?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Than a Slump for Titans’ Chris Johnson', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline':