Colonel Qaddafi was captured and the cameras started rolling.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As News Animations Go Mainstream, Taiwanese Pioneers Try Playing It Straight', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APPLE DAILY', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Next Media Ltd', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T12:42:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Flora Lee Peir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Flora', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Peir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87195a51-a5b2-520b-8e39-db2c90046c31', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87195a51-a5b2-520b-8e39-db2c90046c31'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/morning-take-out-356/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MF Global Said to Be Preparing a Bankruptcy Filing \xa0|\xa0 Shares in MF Global Holdings were halted for trading early on Monday, as the brokerage prepared to file for bankruptcy protection and sell some of its assets to the Interactive Brokers Group, according to people briefed on the matter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T12:52:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71dc355c-3c02-5b06-9730-c6b5b7e0936c', 'word_count': 1732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71dc355c-3c02-5b06-9730-c6b5b7e0936c'}, {'abstract': 'The reading list from our design and living issue: books by Lou Beach, Blandine Vié, Allegra McEvedy and Gerhard Meier.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/bookshelf-12/', 'snippet': 'The reading list from our design and living issue: books by Lou Beach, Blandine Vié, Allegra McEvedy and Gerhard Meier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marvels of economy, the stories in Lou Beach’s first collection, “420 Characters” (Houghton Mifflin Harcourt, $22), originated as Facebook status updates (and conform to the 420-character limit). One begins: “I had never used a chain saw.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bookshelf', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T13:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/659f941e-4070-5286-8471-04a5aa3cfd0a', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/659f941e-4070-5286-8471-04a5aa3cfd0a'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets face an unusually tough scheduling challenge in a few weeks, playing New England on a Sunday night and then at Denver four days later.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/should-the-n-f-l-flex-the-jets-out-of-a-sunday-night-game/', 'snippet': 'The Jets face an unusually tough scheduling challenge in a few weeks, playing New England on a Sunday night and then at Denver four days later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Jets’ next two games –– at Buffalo (5-2) next Sunday and at home against the Patriots (5-2) on Nov. 13 — figure to be pivotal in the race for the A.F.C. East title. At 4-3, the Jets are a game behind, and if they can win both, they will be in no worse than a tie for first place in the division. The Jets would have the tiebreaker advantage over both teams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should the N.F.L. ‘Flex’  the Jets Out of a Sunday Night Game?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T13:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Bretherton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bretherton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95a845fc-83fb-5586-9c5a-1afe33ce48fa', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95a845fc-83fb-5586-9c5a-1afe33ce48fa'}, {'abstract': 'The organization defied a mandate