31/the-long-good-buy/', 'snippet': 'Reluctant to dismantle his office, Robert Trachtenberg bought himself some time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After 24 years in the same rent-controlled apartment that I had used as my office (but absolutely not as a mortuary or dental practice, which everyone knows is against code, if you’re reading this, L.A. Housing Department), I got the heave-ho when the owners informed me that they needed the place for family. Having been in this one spot for so long, I actually began to look forward to moving, exploring a new part of town, and even gave some mild thought to deaccessioning some pieces I had collected over the years. On my first day of packing, however, I found a New Yorker cartoon that helped me make up my mind. It showed an old man lying on his deathbed. Looking up at a visitor, he says, “I should have bought more crap.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Long Good Buy', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trachtenberg, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bonhams', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hermes International SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Hollywood (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T14:46:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Trachtenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trachtenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0b737d1-b260-53a0-bba9-d23c318e6f8e', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0b737d1-b260-53a0-bba9-d23c318e6f8e'}, {'abstract': 'Leading Off: Steelers and Patriots give the N.F.L. a boost of star power, with Ben Roethlisberger out-Bradying Tom Brady, but the race to the bottom is going strong between the Colts and Dolphins.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/leading-off-race-is-on-to-the-n-f-l-s-bottom-and-top/', 'snippet': 'Leading Off: Steelers and Patriots give the N.F.L. a boost of star power, with Ben Roethlisberger out-Bradying Tom Brady, but the race to the bottom is going strong between the Colts and Dolphins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most remarkable thing about the slate of N.F.L. games on Sunday is that they finally made the races at the top of the standings nearly as riveting as the one going on at the bottom. It took until Week 8, but we got a clash of powerhouses in the Patriots-Steelers game and a hint that the Eagles might be rounding into a juggernaut to remind us that A) the football gods are not just going to hand a second straight Super Bowl trophy to Green Bay, and B) not every coach dreams of penciling Andrew Luck into next year’s lineup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: Race Is On to the N.F.L.’s Bottom, and Top', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowher, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feldman, Bruce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freeman, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harbaugh, Jim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luck, Andrew', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roethlisberger, Ben', 'rank': 8, '