, 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05818a99-0634-5e1e-a8be-e0aa63c5a0e2', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05818a99-0634-5e1e-a8be-e0aa63c5a0e2'}, {'abstract': 'The Icon 4×4 Bronco, based on Ford’s renowned yet flawed proto-S.U.V., will be a highlight of the SEMA Show, running Nov. 1 to 5 in Las Vegas.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/the-birth-of-a-66-bronco-by-way-of-the-21st-century/', 'snippet': 'The Icon 4×4 Bronco, based on Ford’s renowned yet flawed proto-S.U.V., will be a highlight of the SEMA Show, running Nov. 1 to 5 in Las Vegas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the featured complete vehicles at the Specialty Equipment Manufacturers Association Show in Las Vegas will be the Icon 4×4 Bronco, featured in Sunday’s Automobiles section. Here, Jerry Garrett explains how this thoroughly modern $159,000 retromobile came to be.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Birth of a ’66 Bronco, by Way of the 21st Century', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jeep Division of Chrysler', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T17:47:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96079281-1c8a-52e1-be83-91cce55d474e', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96079281-1c8a-52e1-be83-91cce55d474e'}, {'abstract': 'A study found insufficient evidence that dust and pollution in Iraq and Afghanistan could cause long-term health problems in returning troops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/us/not-enough-data-to-link-pollution-to-ill-troops.html', 'snippet': 'A study found insufficient evidence that dust and pollution in Iraq and Afghanistan could cause long-term health problems in returning troops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A study released on Monday found that there was insufficient data to conclude that dust and pollution in the war zones of Iraq and Afghanistan, particularly from the burn pits used by the military to incinerate garbage, could cause long-term health problems in troops. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Finds Scant Data on Illnesses of Troops', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Finds Scant Data On Illnesses Of Troops', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T17:48:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f77a0c1-203b-5979-b329-ed856478440e', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f77a0c1-203b-5979-b329-ed856478440e'}, {'abstract': 'Joan Didion’s “Blue Nights” is a loving portrait of her deceased daughter and a conflicted effort to grapple with her grief through words.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/books/blue-nights-by-joan-didion-review.html', 'snippet': 'Joan Didion’s “Blue Nights” is a loving portrait of her deceased daughter and a conflicted effort to grapple with her grief through words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When she was a child, Quintana Roo Dunne — the daughter of Joan Didion and John Gregory Dunne — had a name for fear and death and the unknown: the Broken Man. She used to have nightmares that the Broken Man would come and take her away, and begged her parents to keep her safe. “I had promised her,” Ms. Didion recalled, “that we would not let the Broken Man catch her.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/Jp-book/Jp-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/Jp-book/Jp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/Jp-book/Jp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Loss, a Mother Explores Dark Questions and Bright Memories', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Loss, a Mother Explores Dark Questions and Bright Memories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Didion, Joan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T17:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/56ca70ee-bcbf-5583-819d-ad38ad01b441', 'word_count': 1248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56ca70ee-bcbf-5583-819d-ad38ad01b441'}, {'abstract': 'Ron Balasco joined Redbook, New York, part of the Hearst Magazines unit of the Hearst Corporation, as health account director, responsible for sales in the health care categories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/business/media/accounts-and-people-of-note-in-the-ad-industry.html', 'snippet': 'Ron Balasco joined Redbook, New York, part of the Hearst Magazines unit of the Hearst Corporation, as health account director, responsible for sales in the health care categories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ron Balasco joined Redbook, New York, part of the Hearst Magazines unit of the Hearst Corporation, as health account director, responsible for sales in the health care categories, including all advertising for over-the-counter and direct-to-consumer products in the New York market. He succeeds Andrew Weicker, who had been New York director and left to join WebMD as director for strategic accounts. Mr. Balasco had most recently been corporate sales director at Time Inc., New York, part of Time Warner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Ad Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Webdenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'majo