nyt://article/1c2c88f3-eea1-5233-808c-4d6daa75c44d'}, {'abstract': 'How to set up (or turn off) Apple’s new Find My Mac feature.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/qa-locating-the-mac-on-a-map/', 'snippet': 'How to set up (or turn off) Apple’s new Find My Mac feature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Locating the Mac on a Map', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iCloud', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T17:52:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6e9051a-b8ce-5d58-83fd-76370e3cb9da', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6e9051a-b8ce-5d58-83fd-76370e3cb9da'}, {'abstract': 'The Sun Valley Resort in Idaho embraces branded entertainment — content with a sponsored point of view — in a new campaign laden with online video clips.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/business/media/shining-a-light-on-sun-valley.html', 'snippet': 'The Sun Valley Resort in Idaho embraces branded entertainment — content with a sponsored point of view — in a new campaign laden with online video clips.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seventy years after Sun Valley was a star of a Hollywood movie, the resort is producing films of its own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/business/media/31adnewsletter-inline/31adnewsletter-inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/31/business/media/31adnewsletter-inline/31adnewsletter-inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/31/business/media/31adnewsletter-inline/31adnewsletter-inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shining a Light on Sun Valley', 'kicker': 'Campaign Spotlight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shining a Light on Sun Valley', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sun Valley (Idaho)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T17:54:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8355943-fea2-593c-b620-18de81a4339f', 'word_count': 1727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8355943-fea2-593c-b620-18de81a4339f'}, {'abstract': 'A study released on Monday found that there was insufficient data to conclude that dust and pollution in the war zones of Iraq and Afghanistan could cause long-term health problems in troops.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/study-on-burn-pits-cite-inadequate-evidence-of-health-effects/', 'snippet': 'A study released on Monday found that there was insufficient data to conclude that dust and pollution in the war zones of Iraq and Afghanistan could cause long-term health problems in troops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many years, troops returning from Iraq and Afghanistan have complained of breathing problems and some have been found with serious illnesses and diseases. Many doctors and researchers focused on one particular culprit: burn pits used by the military to incinerate everything from plastic water bottles to construction materials.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study on ‘Burn Pits’ Cites Inadequate Evidence of Health Effects', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Respiratory Diseases', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute of Medicine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T17:56:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4fd0cb1-107d-5567-8d09-5da8255c67dc', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4fd0cb1-107d-5567-8d09-5da8255c67dc'}, {'abstract': 'Two new shows with similar themes, one on ABC and the other on NBC, seem to be attracting attention so far.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/fairy-tale-shows-capture-viewers/', 'snippet': 'Two new shows with similar themes, one on ABC and the other on NBC, seem to be attracting attention so far.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It appears that the viewing public has fallen under the spell of not one but two fairy-tale-centric dramas. “Once Upon a Time” on ABC on Sunday night held on to its impressive premiere numbers: it fell slightly in total viewers to 11.64 million, but retained 100 percent of its premiere 18-to-49-year-old audience. Two nights earlier, despite competing against Game 7 of the World Series, the premiere of NBC’s “Grimm” was sampled by 6.5 million total viewers. It was also the highest-rated Friday nonsports telecast in the 18-to-49 category from any network since Dec. 31, 2010.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fairy-Tale Shows Capture Viewers', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T18:02:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0066c5f5-ed47-5fb8-9141-9e15e37a1c49', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0066c5f5-ed47-5fb8-9141-9e15e37a1c49'}, {'abstract': 'The Commodity Futures Trading Commission and Interactive Brokers,  a Connecticut-based brokerage firm, had raised questions about capital levels.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/regulators-had-grave-concerns-about-mf-global/', 'snippet': 'The Commodity Futures Trading Commission and Interactive Brokers,  a Connecticut-based brokerage firm, had raised questions about cap