', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Biggs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8f45143-0945-5db9-97a4-51d761355bc1', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8f45143-0945-5db9-97a4-51d761355bc1'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s Critics’ Picks, A. O. Scott looks back at “Detour,” a 1945 film noir directed by Edgar G. Ulmer.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/critics-picks-video-detour/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s Critics’ Picks, A. O. Scott looks back at “Detour,” a 1945 film noir directed by Edgar G. Ulmer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s Critics’ Picks, A. O. Scott looks back at Edgar G. Ulmer’s low-budget film “Detour” (1945). The film stars Tom Neal as a struggling musician who’s hitchhiking his way through California when he meets a femme fatale, played by Ann Savage. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Critics’ Picks Video: ‘Detour’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ulmer, Edgar G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T18:45:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36aa2865-2b6b-5ec5-ab0f-d89d5b489411', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36aa2865-2b6b-5ec5-ab0f-d89d5b489411'}, {'abstract': 'Protests in London’s financial district prompted another resignation Monday as the dean of St. Paul’s Cathedral, the Right Rev. Graeme Knowles, announced his intention to step down.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/amid-london-protests-another-church-official-resigns/', 'snippet': 'Protests in London’s financial district prompted another resignation Monday as the dean of St. Paul’s Cathedral, the Right Rev. Graeme Knowles, announced his intention to step down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Protests in London’s financial district prompted another resignation Monday as the dean of St. Paul’s Cathedral, the Right Rev. Graeme Knowles, announced his intention to step down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Protests Lead 2nd Church Official to Resign', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T18:46:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/184ecb62-f355-5532-8316-f81e3e05626e', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/184ecb62-f355-5532-8316-f81e3e05626e'}, {'abstract': 'The cable channel FX said on Halloween that it had ordered a second season of “American Horror Story,” which is on track to become the highest-rated first season of any series it has shown.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/fx-adds-another-chapter-to-american-horror-story/', 'snippet': 'The cable channel FX said on Halloween that it had ordered a second season of “American Horror Story,” which is on track to become the highest-rated first season of any series it has shown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ll chalk it up to pure coincidence and nothing more sinister that FX waited until Monday – Halloween – to announce that it is ordering a second season of its macabre series “American Horror Story” from creators Ryan Murphy and Brad Falchuk. The show, which stars Dylan McDermott and Connie Britton as a struggling married couple living in a haunted Los Angeles mansion where people can’t seem to stop dying, has been a hit for the cable network, drawing nearly 3.2 million viewers for its Oct. 5 debut and averaging about 2.8 million for each new installment. FX said that, through four episodes, “American Horror Story” was on track to become the highest-rated first season of any series it has broadcast, surpassing Mr. Murphy’s plastic-surgery drama “Nip/Tuck,” which began in 2003. The second season of “American Horror Story” will run 13 episodes; no debut was immediately announced, though it will likely run in the fall, at which point we’ll know whether it’s more or less terrifying than Charlie Sheen’s new FX series, “Anger Management.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'FX Adds Another Chapter to ‘American Horror Story’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Halloween', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Falchuk, Brad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Ryan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T18:53:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48002ccb-7344-5a97-8518-9d73de826595', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48002ccb-7344-5a97-8518-9d73de826595'}, {'abstract': 'Animations displaying the speed of different boarding strategies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/11/01/business/airline-boarding.html', 'snippet': 'Animations displaying the speed of different boarding strategies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Animations displaying the speed of different boarding strategies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comparing Airplane Boarding Methods', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T18:55:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/8b91a5a8-cc65-56a0-b568-d43b10241fa2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/8b91a5a8-cc65-56a0-b568-d43b10241fa2'}, {'abstract': 'Boarding times at airports have doubled since the 1970s, prompting airlines to try all kinds of elaborate tricks to get passengers in speedily and leave the gate on time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/business/airlines-are-trying-to-cut-boarding-times-on-planes.html', 'snippet': 'Boarding times at airports have doubled since the 1970s, prompting airlines to try all kinds of elaborate tricks to get passengers in speedily and leave the gate on time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the common tale of woe for many travelers waiting to board a plane. First the airline has to go through a long list of passengers who have priority: First- and business-class passengers, frequent fliers, elite card holders, uniformed members of the military, families with children, those who hold credit cards affiliated with the airlines, passengers who paid for priority seats.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/business/01Air_cnd/01Air_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/business/01Air_cnd/01Air_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/01/business/01Air_cnd/01Air_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Most Annoying Airline Delays Might Just Be in the Boarding', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Most Annoying Airline Delays Might Just Be in the Boarding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delays (Transportation)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luggage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T18:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jad Mouawad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9c1da59-e8ec-5794-a72b-6770d880b376', 'word_count': 1132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9c1da59-e8ec-5794-a72b-6770d880b376'}, {'abstract': 'The philosopher A.C. Grayling on meaninglessness and making meaning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/opinion/100000001141283/ac-grayling.html', 'snippet': 'The philosopher A.C. Grayling on meaninglessness and making meaning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The philosopher A.C. Grayling on meaninglessness and making meaning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/opinion/video-stone-grayling/video-stone-grayling-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/10/28/opinion/video-stone-grayling/video-stone-grayling-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/28/opinion/video-stone-grayling/video-stone-grayling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/28/opinion/video-stone-grayling/video-stone-grayling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A.C. Grayling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T18:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Opinion', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'None None', 'person': [{'firstname': 'None', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'None', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/cca751f0-21ac-562d-88c2-d0156ba61781', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/cca751f0-21ac-562d-88c2-d0156ba61781'}, {'abstract': 'Actually, I believe in mallets towards none.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/i-dont-think-thor-needs-to-worry-about-competition/', 'snippet': 'Actually, I believe in mallets towards none.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From Business Insider:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Don’t Think Thor Needs To Worry About Competition', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T18:58:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e7b0a82-5c70-59fc-a46b-f1d2e4c5e255', 'word_count': 3, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e7b0a82-5c70-59fc-a46b-f1d2e4c5e255'}, {'abstract': 'A rift seems to be growing in Zuccotti Park, and a poll finds that a majority of Americans agree or mostly agree with the protesters.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/occupywallst-roundup-day-45/', 'snippet': 'A rift seems to be growing in Zuccotti Park, and a poll finds that a majority of Americans agree or mostly agree with the protesters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even within a square block, room for tension: a look at the geographical divide within Zuccotti Park between Occupy Wall Street’s true believers on the east side and some less committed hangers-on and troublemakers on the west side. [Daily News]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '#OccupyWallSt Roundup, Day 45', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zuccotti Park (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T18:58:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jillian Dunham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jillian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dunham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32633be3-0b64-568d-a126-5ea3a8c34650', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32633be3-0b64-568d-a126-5ea3a8c34650'}, {'abstract': 'Ready for the holiday season? These clay clutches at Bergdorf Goodman should put you in the spirit of things.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/the-get-ronnie-kirsch-clutches/', 'snippet': 'Ready for the holiday season? These clay clutches at Bergdorf Goodman should put you in the spirit of things.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ronnie Kirsch’s polymer clay clutches stood out among the piles of diamonds and silk pajamas at Bergdorf Goodman’s holiday preview. It was refreshing to see such a colorful clutch after a season of so many neutral handbags. Right on time for spring’s pop fluorescents, the stripes are actually made of clay, then set in an oven like pottery. Kirsch, who holds a bachelor’s in fine arts from the Rhode Island School of Design and worked in the design departments of Cartier and the Tiffany & Company before starting her own collection, treats the bags as she would works of art. We recommend doing the same.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Ronnie Kirsch Clutches', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bergdorf Goodman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T18:59:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e241dc71-e2ea-5468-8ecb-55d0e1dc94b7', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e241dc71-e2ea-5468-8ecb-55d0e1dc94b7'}, {'abstract': 'The walls will be lowered and fences moved in in an attempt to make it easier to hit home runs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/sports/baseball/mets-to-alter-dimensions-of-citi-field.html', 'snippet': 'The walls will be lowered and fences moved in in an attempt to make it easier to hit home runs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Citi Field, the nearly $800 million stadium built by and for the Mets, was the realization of a family dream, constructed with government financial backing and the support of two mayors. The stadium, with its Ebbets Field touches, was an ode to the past. With its Shake Shack burgers and lobster rolls, it was also a bold bid to cash in on pricey ballpark amenities.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/sports/mets-slide-show-slide-X2XO/mets-slide-show-slide-X2XO-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/01/sports/mets-slide-show-slide-X2XO/mets-slide-show-slide-X2XO-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/sports/mets-slide-show-slide-X2XO/mets-slide-show-slide-X2XO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/sports/mets-slide-show-slide-X2XO/mets