rstname': 'Wm', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b5f0ce2-dd85-5adf-96da-e59ab4279f76', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b5f0ce2-dd85-5adf-96da-e59ab4279f76'}, {'abstract': 'In Britain especially, MF Global’s bankruptcy will play out pretty much like Lehman’s.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/a-lehman-brothers-in-minature/', 'snippet': 'In Britain especially, MF Global’s bankruptcy will play out pretty much like Lehman’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MF Global Holdings and one of its United States subsidiaries filed for Chapter 11 protection on Monday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lehman Brothers, in Miniature', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T19:14:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen J. Lubben', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Lubben', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6eaacae-5048-5202-a1a4-cd3c07fb0505', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6eaacae-5048-5202-a1a4-cd3c07fb0505'}, {'abstract': 'I want to let my daughter roam the way I did as a child, but when she asks for new freedoms, I balk.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/fighting-the-overprotective-impulse/', 'snippet': 'I want to let my daughter roam the way I did as a child, but when she asks for new freedoms, I balk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I don’t mean to rub it in for those of you in the Northeast (O.K., maybe a little), but Sunday was gorgeous in Berkeley, Calif.: balmy, blue sky and, touch wood, steady ground. My husband and daughter and I took advantage by indulging in a stack of pancakes at an outdoor cafe. She got itchy as Steven and I lingered over coffee and the Sunday paper (why is it that kids wolf their food down when you want to lounge and are impossibly pokey when you don’t?) and she asked me if she could go to the bookstore. The store was down the block, around the corner and across one high-traffic street that had a crosswalk but no stop sign or light.I glanced at Steven, hoping for a clue about how to respond.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting the Overprotective Impulse', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T19:15:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peggy Orenstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peggy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Orenstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b47364f5-c98f-5d92-9dc8-67df3267d9bb', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b47364f5-c98f-5d92-9dc8-67df3267d9bb'}, {'abstract': 'One of the network’s biggest stars announces her divorce, and executives on Monday were discussing whether to pull from the schedule “Kim’s Fairytale Wedding: A Kardashian Event.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/kardashian-divorce-forces-the-e-network-to-scramble/', 'snippet': 'One of the network’s biggest stars announces her divorce, and executives on Monday were discussing whether to pull from the schedule “Kim’s Fairytale Wedding: A Kardashian Event.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the biggest stars on the E! network, Kim Kardashian, said Monday that she was separating from her husband, Kris Humphries, 72 days after an extravagant, literally made-for-television wedding. Ms. Kardashian cited irreconcilable differences, but some of her fans and detractors sensed a business decision. Ms. Kardashian, after all, had earned millions of dollars by selling the television rights to her Aug. 20 wedding to E!, which has shown Kardashian family reality shows for several years. E! made the most of it, premiering “Kim’s Fairytale Wedding: A Kardashian Event” on Oct. 9 and 10 and replaying it almost every day since then. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kardashian Divorce Forces the E! Network to Scramble', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kardashian, Kim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'E! Entertainment Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T19:20:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb719981-b27b-5bd4-8509-e75323716b6f', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb719981-b27b-5bd4-8509-e75323716b6f'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister George Papandreou said that the decision on the deal, which includes fresh financial assistance but also imposes unpopular austerity measures, belonged to the Greek people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/world/europe/greece-to-hold-referendum-on-new-debt-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister George Papandreou said that the decision on the deal, which includes fresh financial assistance but also imposes unpopular austerity measures, belonged to the Greek people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — In a surprise move that jolted Europe and put his political future in play, Prime Minister George A. Papandreou announced Monday that his government would hold a referendum on a new aid package for Greece, putting austerity measures — and potentially membership in the euro zone — to a popular vote for the first time. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/world/SUB-GREECE/SUB-GREECE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/world/SUB-GREECE/SUB-GREECE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/01/world/SUB-GREECE/SUB-GREECE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anxieties Stir as Greece Plans Referendum on Latest Europe Aid Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Anxieties Stir as Greece Plans Referendum on Latest Europe Aid Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Papandreou, George A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T19:20:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis and Rachel Do