le as a way to distinguish themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/business/places-to-sleep-join-forces-with-places-to-sweat.html', 'snippet': 'Though many hotels have perfectly good fitness centers, some are pairing up with brand-name gyms like Core Performance, Exhale and SoulCycle as a way to distinguish themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rochelle Jacobs has been working out at Exhale, the mind and body spa, two to three times a week for the last nine years. She says she is so dedicated to her gym that she picks her hotels based on their fitness offerings.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/business/Gym/Gym-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/business/Gym/Gym-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/01/business/Gym/Gym-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Gym at the Inn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Gym at the Inn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Clubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T20:12:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Ellin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'mid