ering to fandom.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/it-is-designed-to-break-your-heart/', 'snippet': 'The Texas Rangers and the importance of suffering to fandom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Thursday, just before the sixth game of the World Series, ESPN’s Jayson Stark wrote a piece about the Texas Rangers’ relationship to their local sports fans, suggesting that the team’s recent success and potential title might be finally earning them a place in the hearts of Dallas’s football-mad faithful. Despite their long World Series drought, Stark noted, the Rangers had never inspired the same kind of undying passion as frustrated franchises like the Cubs or Indians or pre-2004 Red Sox: Instead of agonizing over their baseball nine’s inability to win it all, the Dallas-Fort Worth fan base mainly just ignored them. But a Rangers victory over the Saint Louis Cardinals, he suggested, might change all that: “If these Rangers find a way to win just one more time, life in Texas may never be the same all-Cowboys-all-the-time universe again.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It Is Designed to Break Your Heart', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:04:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03200215-1818-5cca-8d02-efdfa4d3d2a1', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03200215-1818-5cca-8d02-efdfa4d3d2a1'}, {'abstract': 'The Green House concept is the most comprehensive effort to reinvent the nursing home, including the way medical care is delivered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/health/shrinking-the-nursing-home-until-it-feels-like-a-home.html', 'snippet': 'The Green House concept is the most comprehensive effort to reinvent the nursing home, including the way medical care is delivered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Toni Davis spent much of her childhood roaming the corridors of a nursing home in West Orange, N.J., where her mother was the director. Even now she recalls the pleas of the residents there: “\xa0‘Please help me, please take me home with you,’ they’d beg,” Ms. Davis said. “I remember asking my mom, ‘Why can’t we take them home for dinner for just one night?’"', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/science/Home/Home-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/01/science/Home/Home-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/science/Home/Home-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 551, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/science/Home/Home-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/01/science/Home/Home-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Nursing Home Shrinks Until It Feels Like a Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Nursing Home Shrinks Until It Feels Like a Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major':