tion_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'None None', 'person': [{'firstname': 'None', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'None', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/5729f53f-2fc2-512e-ba25-4e6803b8c0c1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/5729f53f-2fc2-512e-ba25-4e6803b8c0c1'}, {'abstract': 'HarperCollins said on Monday it would acquire the Nashville-based publisher Thomas Nelson, bolstering the company’s strength in the market for inspirational and religious books.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/harpercollins-acquires-religious-book-publisher/', 'snippet': 'HarperCollins said on Monday it would acquire the Nashville-based publisher Thomas Nelson, bolstering the company’s strength in the market for inspirational and religious books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HarperCollins Publishers said on Monday that it would acquire Thomas Nelson, a publisher based in Nashville, bolstering the company’s strength in the market for inspirational and religious books.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'HarperCollins Acquires Religious Book Publisher', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HarperCollins Publishers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zondervan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nashville (Tenn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcb05691-e63c-5fe8-aa95-0beed06fb829', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcb05691-e63c-5fe8-aa95-0beed06fb829'}, {'abstract': 'Compared with current tax policy, the plan would also be likely to reduce federal tax revenues by $570 billion, or about 15 percent, according to the Tax Policy Center.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/rich-get-biggest-break-in-perry-tax-plan-study-finds/', 'snippet': 'Compared with current tax policy, the plan would also be likely to reduce federal tax revenues by $570 billion, or about 15 percent, according to the Tax Policy Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Rick Perry’s proposal for an opt-in flat tax would primarily benefit the wealthiest Americans, according to a new analysis from the Tax Policy Center, a nonpartisan research organization. Compared with current tax policy, the plan would most likely reduce federal tax revenue by $570 billion, or about 15 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rich Get Biggest Break in Perry Tax Plan, Study Finds', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tax Policy Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:32:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a37528b-d59d-5236-b2c9-fd6a5431cd21', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a37528b-d59d-5236-b2c9-fd6a5431cd21'}, {'abstract': 'In “East Meets West” at the 92nd Street Y on Thursday, the violinist Daniel Hope offered works from Ravel, Bartok and others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/arts/music/east-meets-west-with-daniel-hope-at-92nd-street-y-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “East Meets West” at the 92nd Street Y on Thursday, the violinist Daniel Hope offered works from Ravel, Bartok and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his lucid and haunting works, the composer Toru Takemitsu synthesized the sounds of his native Japan with the techniques of Western modernism. Speaking from the stage of the 92nd Street Y on Thursday evening, the English violinist Daniel Hope summed up this cosmopolitan style: “So far, and yet very near.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/Hope/Hope-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/Hope/Hope-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/Hope/Hope-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/Hope/Hope-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/Hope/Hope-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Blending of Cultures, Politics Pushed Aside', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Blending of Cultures, Politics Pushed Aside', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hope, Daniel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ninety-Second Street Y', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:34:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/596d9216-017e-5f0b-ac35-a0787c49557a', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/596d9216-017e-5f0b-ac35-a0787c49557a'}, {'abstract': 'Adrian Utley of Portishead and Will Gregory of Goldfrapp performed a score to accompany Carl Theodor Dreyer’s “Passion de Jeanne d’Arc” at Alice Tully Hall on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/arts/music/passion-de-jeanne-darc-at-alice-tully-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'Adrian Utley of Portishead and Will Gregory of Goldfrapp performed a score to accompany Carl Theodor Dreyer’s “Passion de Jeanne d’Arc” at Alice Tully Hall on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Silent films have always had a devoted constituency among history-minded cinema enthusiasts, and aficionados of the form will tell you that directors and actors cultivated an artistry in those dialogue-free movies that was lost when talkies displaced them. For more casual viewers, public screenings are relatively hard to come by. These days they are most likely to be seen as part of a musical performance. Composers, it turns out, are doing more to keep these classics in public view than film societies. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/sub-white/sub-white-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 897, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/sub-white/sub-white-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/sub-white/sub-white-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Joan of Arc’s Suffering, This Time With Sound', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Joan of Arc’s Suffering, This Time With Sound', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White Light Festival (Lincoln Center, NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dreyer, Carl Theodor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Portishead', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:35:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/afe0b6a5-f6db-5eed-a30d-66b34822e631', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afe0b6a5-f6db-5eed-a30d-66b34822e631'}, {'abstract': 'The Czech-born choreographer Dusan Tynek is presenting works old and new as part of his company’s two-week season at the TriBeCa Performing Arts Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/arts/dance/dusan-tynek-dance-at-tribeca-arts-center-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Czech-born choreographer Dusan Tynek is presenting works old and new as part of his company’s two-week season at the TriBeCa Performing Arts Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a sign of the skill, range and taste of the Czech-born choreographer Dusan Tynek that a new dance of his will often recall the work of a great choreographer, a different one each time. That same trait is what keeps Mr. Tynek from advancing out of the artistic category of promising. The first section of his new “Widow’s Walk,” performed on Friday as part of his company’s two-week season at the TriBeCa Performing Arts Center, could have been made by Martha Graham.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/tynek/tynek-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/tynek/tynek-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/tynek/tynek-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sea That Gives, and Takes Away', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sea That Gives, and Takes Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tynek, Dusan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:36:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b14eb02-8d62-54cf-8925-e8d523df2516', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b14eb02-8d62-54cf-8925-e8d523df2516'}, {'abstract': '“Unguarded,” an ESPN documentary, recounts the descent of the onetime basketball star Chris Herren into heroin and painkillers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/arts/television/unguarded-documentary-about-chris-herren-on-espn-review.html', 'snippet': '“Unguarded,” an ESPN documentary, recounts the descent of the onetime basketball star Chris Herren into heroin and painkillers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heroin and painkillers play a larger role than basketball in “Unguarded,” an ESPN documentary on Tuesday night. “I come in here and tell you my nightmare,” the onetime star Chris Herren, long past his glory days, tells a gym full of high school students, and that’s the function of the film as well. Unlike the students, we don’t have to listen to him, but it’s a pretty good story; even if sports aren’t your thing, you might find it worth hanging around the gym for an hour and a half.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/Unguarded/Unguarded-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/Unguarded/Unguarded-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/Unguarded/Unguarded-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 455, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Point Guard’s Nightmare Descent Into Drugs', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Point Guard’s Nightmare Descent Into Drugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herren, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:40:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a355d225-1381-5604-85c6-61e295b6c8c7', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a355d225-1381-5604-85c6-61e295b6c8c7'}, {'abstract': 'The post positions were drawn Monday for all 15 of the Breeders’ Cup races, which offer a combined purse of $26 million.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/uncle-mo-is-favorite-in-breeders-cup-classic/', 'snippet': 'The post positions were drawn Monday for all 15 of the Breeders’ Cup races, which offer a combined purse of $26 million.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:25 a.m. | Updated Prayer for Relief has developed a fever and will not race in the Classic, bringing the field to 12.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uncle Mo Is Favorite in Breeders’ Cup Classic', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:41:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1078985f-140e-5e98-8d64-53fd7f93b5ff', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1078985f-140e-5e98-8d64-53fd7f93b5ff'}, {'abstract': 'The German tenor Jonas Kaufmann, recently recovered from chest surgery, sang works by Mahler, Liszt and Strauss in his first New York recital at the Metropolitan Opera.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/arts/music/jonas-kaufmann-in-recital-at-the-metropolitan-opera-review.html', 'snippet': 'The German tenor Jonas Kaufmann, recently recovered from chest surgery, sang works by Mahler, Liszt and Strauss in his first New York recital at the Metropolitan Opera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Friedrich Rückert’s poem “I Am Lost to the World,” the narrator sighs that the world “has heard nothing from me for so long,/That it may very well believe that I am dead.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/JONAS/JONAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/JONAS/JONAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/JONAS/JONAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fast-Rising Opera Star in a Solo Setting', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fast-Rising Opera Star in a Solo Setting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaufmann, Jonas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:41:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbdb3fb0-1c7a-5bd2-999f-25bd1f79d2c3', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbdb3fb0-1c7a-5bd2-999f-25bd1f79d2c3'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of readers commented on Matt Bai’s article “Does Anyone Have a Grip on the G.O.P.?”', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/does-anyone-have-a-grip-on-the-democrats/', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of readers commented on Matt Bai’s article “Does Anyone Have a Grip on the G.O.P.?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hundreds of readers commented on Matt Bai’s article “Does Anyone Have a Grip on the G.O.P.?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Does Anyone Have a Grip on the Democrats?’', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bai, Matt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:45:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2e2fbf1-be75-5536-96ad-686192f680cc', 'word_count': 16, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2e2fbf1-be75-5536-96ad-686192f680cc'}, {'abstract': 'A mother looks back on her son’s decision to dress like a girl for Halloween, and the surprising national controversy it generated. But lost in the discussion, it seems, was the real message of her son’s costume choice.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/lessons-from-a-halloween-costume/', 'snippet': 'A mother looks back on her son’s decision to dress like a girl for Halloween, and the surprising national controversy it generated. But lost in the discussion, it seems, was the real message of her son’s costume choice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago I made the seemingly mundane choice to let my son choose his costume for Halloween. He chose Daphne from Scooby Doo. A few parents at his preschool disapproved, I wrote a blog post about it,  and in the blink of an eye, the post set off a national discussion about gender identity, bullying and a parent’s role in both issues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons From a Halloween Costume', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Costumes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Halloween', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:47:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Manley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0971a68f-497c-5f8d-a4b9-3628d724937b', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0971a68f-497c-5f8d-a4b9-3628d724937b'}, {'abstract': 'Is presidential greatness really enhanced by certain prior experiences?', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/prior-experience-and-presidential-greatness/', 'snippet': 'Is presidential greatness really enhanced by certain prior experiences?', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no shortage of claims about what qualifies a candidate to be president. Military service, owning a business, serving in a legislature, serving in an executive position — all of these and more are cited routinely.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prior Experience and Presidential Greatness', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:48:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Sides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2227fc6-ff5d-58ee-a8f3-7d6236e6f60b', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2227fc6-ff5d-58ee-a8f3-7d6236e6f60b'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers have discovered that reindeer use a combination of strategies to keep cool, including sometimes panting like a dog.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/science/staying-cool-after-a-slog-with-a-sleigh-isnt-easy.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers have discovered that reindeer use a combination of strategies to keep cool, including sometimes panting like a dog.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arctic reindeer have thick fur coats that help them survive frigid winters. But they also need to cool off in the winter when their bodies grow warm from running. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/science/01OBREINDEER3/01OBREINDEER3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 870, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/01/science/01OBREINDEER3/01OBREINDEER3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 870}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/science/01OBREINDEER3/01OBREINDEER3-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 706, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/science/01OBREINDEER3/01OBREINDEER3-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 706, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/science/01OBREINDEER3/01OBREINDEER3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/01/science/01OBREINDEER3/01OBREINDEER3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/science/01OBREINDEER3/01OBREINDEER3-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Staying Cool After a Slog With a Sleigh Isn’t Easy', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Staying Cool After a Slog With a Sleigh Isn’t Easy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of Experimental Biology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reindeer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:48:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6c28877-30b1-5971-8a60-ce436a671ccd', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6c28877-30b1-5971-8a60-ce436a671ccd'}, {'abstract': 'Landon Donovan says the Red Bulls play dirty. Are they the only ones?', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/the-dirty-tackle-beckham-the-dirty-team-new-york-or-is-it-just-red-bulls-vs-galaxy/', 'snippet': 'Landon Donovan says the Red Bulls play dirty. Are they the only ones?', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Sunday’s 1-0 Galaxy victory over the Red Bulls in the opener of their two-game, total-goals M.L.S. playoff series, Landon Donovan of Los Angeles ripped into the home team for their “dirty” play. Video below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dirty Tackle (Beckham)? The Dirty Team (New York)? Or Is It Just Red Bulls vs. Galaxy?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckham, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donovan, Landon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T21:49:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '