and Harpo Marx in the “I Love Lucy” show? A homage to a scene in the Marx Brothers film “Duck Soup,” it features Lucy dressed as Harpo. When she finds herself face to face with the real thing — typical Lucy — she must pretend that she is his reflection and mimics his every move. It’s comedy gold. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/arts/zaporah/zaporah-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Improviser With a Touch of ‘I Love Lucy’', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Improviser With a Touch of ‘I Love Lucy’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Danspace Project', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T22:23:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0d2b148-3356-5a4b-9ce7-8da0a3ab044a', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0d2b148-3356-5a4b-9ce7-8da0a3ab044a'}, {'abstract': 'How the Paris Ritz, the former gold standard for hotel living, has fallen from grace.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/10/31/lumiere-closin-up-the-ritz/', 'snippet': 'How the Paris Ritz, the former gold standard for hotel living, has fallen from grace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The marble fountain sang. The waiters moved with elegance and grace. The sun softened the sharp edges of the late October afternoon. The outdoor terrace at the Ritz was open for tea. It could have been perfect.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lumière | Closin’ Up the Ritz', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-10-31T22:23:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Sciolino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sciolino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ae613e2-bec9-5c82-bc6d-d02ce3c0b829', 'word_count': 1277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ae613e2-bec9-5c82-bc6d-d02ce3c0b829'}, {'abstract': 'A town house in Brooklyn was a recruitment tool for Saint Ann’s, helping it become more competitive with its peers in attracting leaders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/11/01/nyregion/for-saint-anns-using-a-town-house-to-lure-a-new-leader.html', 'snippet': 'A town house in Brooklyn was a recruitment tool for Saint Ann’s, helping it become more competitive with its peers in attracting leaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The buyer was looking for a town house in Brooklyn. It needed living space for a family of five and entertaining space for crowds in the dozens. It had to be within walking distance of Pierrepont Street — ruling out Park Slope — but outside of Brooklyn Heights, with its higher price tags.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/nyregion/appraisal/appraisal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/01/nyregion/apprai